export anchor VisualStyles:
    description:
        The style library for Brightwork. A style is one complete visual
        direction for the whole app. Every style in one run draws the same
        screen with the same content, so styles can be compared fairly. Runs 1
        to 5 and 16 to 45 show the projects dashboard, and runs 6 to 15 each
        show another screen, named by each style's screen key. Runs 46 to 85
        are dark and show the dashboard or one of the suite's other apps. Styles are numbered for good. A number is never reused,
        renumbered or deleted, even when the style is rejected.

    gallery: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/index.html

    preferences:
        likes: No products or moods named yet.
        dislikes: None named yet.
        limits:
            Runs 1 to 45 use a light base, as first agreed. From run 46 the user
            asked for dark base styles, so dark is now allowed and runs 46 to 85
            are all dark. Each style picks its own colours, with no brand
            colour to keep. All text and meaningful icons meet WCAG AA contrast.
            System font stacks only, with no web fonts. A status always shows a
            word, and its icon or symbol differs in shape, so meaning never
            depends on colour. Every style works at 375px with no sideways page
            scroll.

    direction:
        Open question. The user has not favoured, rejected or chosen any style
        yet.

    style1:
        number: 1
        run: 1
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Clean app
        idea: Calm white cards on a cool grey page, soft shadows and rounded pills that make the app feel light and friendly.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/1.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #f5f7fa, the page background
            surface: #ffffff, cards, the sidebar and fields
            text: #1b2230, body text and headings
            muted: #5b6475, labels, dates and meta text
            border: #e3e7ee, field borders, the sidebar edge and progress tracks
            accent: #2563eb, links, primary buttons, progress fill and the focus ring
            accentSoft: #e8efff, the active nav item and icon tiles
            success: #17784a text on #e4f4eb, the On track pill
            warning: #965800 text on #fdf0d9, the At risk pill
            danger: #c0282d text on #fde7e8, the Behind pill and the overdue count
        type:
            System sans, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica
            Neue, Arial, sans-serif. Sizes are 28px bold for the page title,
            18px bold for section titles, 16px semibold for project names, 15px
            regular body at 1.5 line height, 13px muted meta and 12px semibold
            pills. Key numbers are 26px bold with tabular figures.
        layout:
            A white sidebar 232px wide with the brand and nav on the left. The
            main area has a top bar with search, notifications and the New
            project button, then the greeting, a row of four summary cards, and
            a two to one grid of project cards beside the chart and activity
            cards. Below 700px the sidebar becomes a sticky top bar with icon
            nav, and everything stacks in one column.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px gaps between cards, 20px card padding, 24 to 32px between sections.
        density: Roomy. About six project cards fill a wide screen.
        corners: 12px on cards, 8px on buttons and fields, fully round pills, progress bars and avatars.
        borders: 1px #e3e7ee on fields and the sidebar edge only. Cards have no border.
        shadows: Cards use 0 1px 2px plus 0 4px 12px, both rgba(16,24,40,0.06).
        icons:
            20px rounded line icons with a 1.8 stroke. Summary icons sit in
            40px soft tinted tiles. Status pills carry a circle tick, a warning
            triangle or an octagon. Team members show as coloured initial
            avatars.
        focus: A 3px outline in rgba(37,99,235,0.35) offset 2px. A focused field gets an accent border and a 3px soft ring.
        tone: Friendly sentence case, such as Good morning, Mara, and View all.

    style2:
        number: 2
        run: 1
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Editorial guide
        idea: A printed weekly on warm paper, with serif headlines, ink rules and plain words that read the dashboard like a short report.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/2.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            paper: #faf6ee, the page
            ink: #1f1b16, text, rules, the primary button and this week's chart bars
            graphite: #6b6156, labels, captions and meta text
            hairline: #dcd2c2, thin rules between entries, progress tracks and last week's chart bars
            oxblood: #8c2a1c, links and the Behind status
            forest: #2e5b3a, the On track status
            ochre: #855400, the At risk status
            highlight: #f1eadb, the background of a focused field
        type:
            Serif for headings and body, Iowan Old Style, Palatino Linotype,
            Palatino, Book Antiqua, Georgia, serif. Labels use the system sans
            in 11px semibold capitals with 0.12em letter spacing. Sizes are a
            44px small-caps wordmark, 40px page headline, 26px section titles,
            22px project names, 17px body at 1.55 line height and 15px italic
            meta. Summary figures are 52px with old-style numerals.
        layout:
            A centred masthead with the wordmark, a date line between ink
            rules, and a centred row of capitalised nav links. A lead section
            pairs the headline and an italic standfirst with four large figures
            split by hairlines. Below it, a two to one column layout holds the
            numbered project entries beside the chart and the activity notes.
            Content is capped at 1180px. Below 640px the columns stack and the
            figures form a two by two grid.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 18px between entries, 32px section padding, 40 to 48px between columns.
        density: Medium. Few elements, long lines and generous leading.
        corners: None. Every edge is square, including buttons.
        borders: A 3px double ink rule under the masthead and above the style sheet, 1px ink under section titles, 1px hairline between entries.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            No pictogram icons. Status is a capitalised word with a
            typographic symbol, a tick for On track, an open triangle for At
            risk and a cross for Behind. Entries are numbered with italic roman
            numerals. Progress is a thin ink line on a hairline track.
        focus: A 2px ink outline offset 3px. A focused field gets a 2px underline and the highlight background.
        tone: Full sentences, a little formal, such as The week at a glance, Notes from the team and The fortnight. Small numbers are written as words in the activity notes.

    style3:
        number: 3
        run: 1
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Dense listing
        idea: A compact work tool, with tables, mono figures and terse labels that fit the whole picture on one screen.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/3.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            background: #ffffff, tables and the page
            panel: #f3f5f7, the toolbar
            paneHead: #e8ecf0, the title bar of each pane
            menuBar: #20262d, the top menu bar, with #e9edf1 and #c7cfd7 text
            text: #11161b, body text and this week's chart bars
            muted: #4a5561, column headers, meta text and last week's bars
            line: #cfd5dc, grid lines between panes and under headers, with #e3e7eb between rows
            accent: #0b6b57, links, the primary button and the OK status
            risk: #875200, the RISK status
            late: #b3261e, the LATE status and the overdue count
            select: #fff4c2, the selected row and the focus fill
            focusRing: #e0a800, the 2px focus outline and the active tab marker is #f2c94c
        type:
            System sans for words, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto,
            sans-serif, at 13px body, 12px secondary text and 11px semibold
            capitals for headers. Figures, dates, codes and user handles use
            ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas, Liberation Mono, monospace,
            with tabular figures. Summary figures are 18px semibold mono.
        layout:
            A 36px dark menu bar with a mono wordmark, tabs, a quick search
            with a slash shortcut hint, and the user handle. A grey toolbar
            holds the title, the date, an update time, Export and New project.
            A strip of five summary cells runs edge to edge. Below it, the
            projects table fills the left pane, and a 360px right pane holds a
            compact bar chart and an activity log table. Below 1000px the panes
            stack. Below 640px the table drops the Team, Tasks and Owners
            columns and the summary strip becomes two columns.
        spacing: A 4px unit. 8px cell padding and 12px pane padding.
        density: High. 28px table rows, about 20 rows visible on a laptop.
        corners: 2px on buttons, fields and status badges. Everything else is square.
        borders: 1px grid lines everywhere, in #cfd5dc between panes and under headers and #e3e7eb between rows. Even rows get a #fafbfc band.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            12px square-cap line icons, only inside buttons. Status is an
            outlined mono badge with a shape glyph and a code word, a filled
            circle with OK, a triangle with RISK and a square with LATE. A key
            under the table spells out each code. Owners show as lowercase mono
            initials.
        focus: A 2px #e0a800 outline with the #fff4c2 fill. The primary button keeps its fill and takes the outline offset 1px.
        tone: Terse and technical, with abbreviations such as Due 7d, Hrs/wk and Done/wk, codes in capitals, and arrows for links.

    style4:
        number: 4
        run: 2
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Playful pastel
        idea: A friendly toy box of candy pastel blocks, chunky round corners and soft blobs that makes project work feel light and encouraging.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/4.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            cream: #fffaf3, the page background
            plum: #2b2645, text, headings and the current nav pill
            dusk: #5a5470, hints, dates and meta text
            grape: #6a3fd4, the primary button, progress fill, this week's chart bars and the focus ring
            grapeDeep: #4b2aa3, links and the ledge under the primary button
            mint: #c8f0dc, a summary tile and the On track pill with #1d6b47 text
            peach: #ffd9c7, a summary tile, the chart block and the Marketing tag
            lilac: #e3d9ff, the greeting block and the Design tag
            butter: #fff0b8, a summary tile, the bell button and the At risk pill with #8a4b00 text
            sky: #d3ecff, a summary tile and the Engineering tag
            cherry: #b3243f, the Behind pill text on #ffd6dc, the overdue count and the bell badge
            blush: #fde4ef, the background blob behind the top right corner
        type:
            Rounded system sans for everything, ui-rounded, SF Pro Rounded,
            Arial Rounded MT Bold, system-ui, sans-serif. Sizes are 48px
            extra bold for the greeting, 56px extra bold tight summary
            numbers with tabular figures, 34px extra bold card percentages,
            26px extra bold section titles, 20px extra bold card titles, 16px
            regular body at 1.5 line height, 14px bold pills and 13px meta.
        layout:
            A top bar with the brand, search, a round bell, the user face and
            the New project button, then the nav as a white pill strip on its
            own row. A hero row pairs a big lilac greeting block with a two by
            two grid of pastel summary tiles. Below, a two to one grid holds
            six white project cards in two columns beside a peach chart block
            and a stack of activity bubbles. A pink blob peeks in at the top
            right. Below 1000px everything stacks, and below 640px the cards
            go to one column and the search takes a full row.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px between tiles and cards, 22 to 40px padding inside blocks, 40px between sections.
        density: Airy. Big blocks and big numbers, about four project cards per screen.
        corners: 20 to 48px on blocks, with one tighter 10px corner on each block so it wobbles like a blob. Buttons, fields, pills, nav and progress bars are fully round.
        borders: None on blocks. Fields carry a 3px #eadfce border. Last week's chart bars are white with a 2px plum outline.
        shadows: No blur. A flat 6 to 8px ledge straight down, #f1e8da under white cards and pills, #4b2aa3 under the grape button.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.25em with a fat 2.4 round stroke. Status pills use
            filled shapes with a white mark, a circle with a tick for On track,
            a rounded triangle with a bang for At risk and a rounded square
            with a dash for Behind. People show as pastel initial faces.
        focus: A 4px grape outline offset 3px. A focused field gets a grape border and a 4px #d6c8ff ring.
        tone: Warm and encouraging in sentence case, such as Hi Mara, nice work this week, need a little love and See them all.

    style5:
        number: 5
        run: 2
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Swiss grid
        idea: A strict twelve column grid in black Helvetica on white, where huge flush left numbers, rules and alignment carry everything and one signal red marks what needs action.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/5.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            white: #ffffff, the only background
            black: #000000, text, rules, numbers, the primary button and this week's bars
            grey: #595959, meta text, dates and axis labels
            midGrey: #8a8a8a, last week's chart bars only, never text
            hairline: #c8c8c8, row rules and progress tracks
            signalRed: #d0021b, the overdue fact, the Behind status, the peak day and the focus ring
        type:
            Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, Nimbus Sans, Liberation Sans,
            sans-serif, in weights 400 and 700 only. Summary figures are 128px
            bold at 0.9 line height with minus 0.05em tracking, the greeting
            is 72px bold with tight tracking, section titles are 28px bold,
            project names 17px bold, body 15px at 1.45 and labels 13px bold in
            lowercase.
        layout:
            A twelve column grid with 24px gutters, 40px margins and a 1320px
            cap. The head row puts the lowercase wordmark with a small red
            square in columns 1 to 3, text nav in 4 to 9 and notifications in
            10 to 12. A 2px rule opens a second row with an underlined search,
            the user name and the black New project button. The greeting sits
            in columns 4 to 12 with the date in 1 to 3. Four huge figures span
            three columns each under a 2px rule. Every section after that puts
            its title and a short note in columns 1 to 3 and content in 4 to
            12, with a ruled projects table, then a thin bar chart beside an
            activity list. Below 720px all columns stack and the figures form
            a two by two grid.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 72px between sections, 14px row padding, 24px gutters.
        density: Medium. Few elements, very large figures and generous white space.
        corners: None. Every edge is square.
        borders: No boxes at all. A 2px black rule opens each block and table head, 1px #c8c8c8 rules separate rows, and an 8px black rule opens the style sheet.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            No pictograms. Status is a 10px solid geometric mark beside the
            word, a circle for On track, a triangle for At risk and a square
            for Behind, with Behind set in bold red. Progress is a 2px track
            with a 4px black fill and the percent beside it.
        focus: A 2px signal red outline offset 2px. A focused field gets a 2px red underline.
        tone: Plain and factual, lowercase labels such as tasks due this week, sentence case headings and no exclamation marks.

    style6:
        number: 6
        run: 2
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Neo-brutalist
        idea: Raw web zine energy, with thick black borders, hard offset shadows and loud yellow, pink and cyan blocks stacked like stickers on off-white paper.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/6.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            paper: #fdf8e8, the page background
            ink: #000000, all text, borders, shadows and status shapes
            white: #ffffff, cards, fields and the chart plate
            yellow: #ffdd00, the header band, the chart block and the At risk stamp
            pink: #ff70c8, the primary button, this week's bars and the Behind stamp
            cyan: #38d9f0, the greeting block, the user tag and the On track stamp
            lime: #b6f04a, one summary block and the style sheet tags
            butter: #fff6b3, the focused field fill
        type:
            Monospace for headings, numbers, labels and buttons, ui-monospace,
            SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas, Liberation Mono, Courier New, monospace,
            mostly 800 weight in capitals. Body text is system-ui at 16px
            weight 500. Sizes are 46px caps greeting, 52px summary figures with
            minus 0.06em tracking, 40px card percentages, 30px caps section
            titles set white on a black bar, 19px caps card titles and 13px
            caps labels.
        layout:
            A full width yellow header band with a black brand block tilted
            by 2 degrees, a wide search field, a bell, a cyan user tag and a
            pink New project button. Under it, a band of nav tabs split by 3px
            black borders, with the current tab inverted. A hero row pairs a
            cyan greeting block with four summary blocks staggered at
            different heights. Projects follow as a three column grid of
            bordered cards, each with a header row, a hatched meter and a
            footer of due date and status stamp. Last comes a yellow chart
            block beside a pink activity block of numbered rows. Below 1080px
            the rows stack and projects go to two columns, and below 640px
            to one column with the stats in a two by two grid.
        spacing: An 8px unit used loosely. 20 to 28px gaps so the shadows have room and 14 to 20px padding.
        density: Medium. Big chunky blocks, about six project cards on a laptop screen.
        corners: Zero. Every corner is sharp.
        borders: 3px solid black on every box, field, button, divider and chart bar, and a 6px black rule above the style sheet.
        shadows: A hard offset of 6px 6px 0 in black with no blur. A pressed button drops into its shadow.
        icons:
            Square cap line icons with a 3px stroke. Status is a coloured
            stamp in caps with a solid black circle for On track, a solid
            black triangle for At risk and a heavy black X for Behind.
            Progress meters use black and yellow diagonal stripes. Activity
            rows carry black number tabs 01 to 06.
        focus: A 3px dashed black outline offset 4px. A focused field also takes the butter fill.
        tone: Loud and blunt with caps labels, such as 4 TASKS OVERDUE. FIX THESE FIRST. and VIEW ALL with an arrow.

    style7:
        number: 7
        run: 2
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Blueprint
        idea: The dashboard as an engineering drawing on pale blue drafting paper, with navy line work, monospace lettering, outlined boxes and dimension style annotations.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/7.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            paper: #e9f2fc, the page under the grid
            gridMinor: #d6e5f6, the 8px background grid
            gridMajor: #bcd4ee, the 40px background grid and chart guide lines
            wash: #f4f8fd, the fill inside every box
            navy: #0b2a5b, text, the sheet frame, box outlines and the primary button
            lineBlue: #1d5fa8, rules, table lines, progress fill, open chart bars and links
            cyan: #2a9fd6, decoration only and never text
            pencil: #3c5a80, captions, labels and meta text
            green: #0b6146, the On track status
            amber: #8a5300, the At risk status
            redline: #b0213a, the Behind status, the overdue count and the overdue note
            trace: #fff7d6, the focus fill
        type:
            One monospace family for everything, ui-monospace, SF Mono,
            Cascadia Mono, Menlo, Consolas, Liberation Mono, monospace. Sizes
            are 44px bold summary figures, a 30px bold greeting, 22px brand
            in caps with 0.18em tracking, 13px bold caps figure titles with
            0.14em tracking, 14px body at 1.5 and 11px caps captions with
            0.14em tracking.
        layout:
            A drawing sheet capped at 1280px with a 2px navy outer frame and a
            1px blue inner frame. At the top a title block grid lists Project
            Brightwork, Drawing Home Overview, Drawn by Mara Okafor, the date
            and Sheet 01 of 06. A tool row holds the search, the bell and New
            project, then the nav as numbered sheet tabs 01 to 06. A General
            Notes box holds the greeting as a numbered list beside a summary
            strip whose labels sit on dimension lines with end ticks. Below,
            FIG. 1 PROJECT SCHEDULE is a full width ruled table with refs P-01
            to P-06 and a key. FIG. 2 THROUGHPUT and FIG. 3 ACTIVITY LOG sit
            side by side. Every figure title is set into the top border of its
            box. Below 1000px everything stacks, the title block becomes two
            columns and the table scrolls inside its box.
        spacing: An 8px unit matching the minor grid. 24px between figures and 16 to 24px inside.
        density: Medium. 40px table rows and figures packed like a drawing sheet.
        corners: Square. Only the initial tags and the status rings are round.
        borders: A 2px navy sheet frame, a 1px blue inner frame, 1px navy figure boxes, 1px blue table cells and 1px dashed blue dividers.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            Outline drafting icons with a 1.5px stroke. Status is a ringed dot
            for On track, an open triangle with a bar for At risk and a
            crossed square for Behind, beside the word in caps. The chart uses
            open outlined bars for last week and hatched bars for this week,
            with dimension lines marking each week total and a leader to MAX
            17. People show as outlined circle initials.
        focus: A 2px dashed navy outline offset 3px with the trace fill.
        tone: Technical drawing language with caps labels, FIG. numbers, refs such as P-04, and times written as T minus 12 min.

    style8:
        number: 8
        run: 2
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Frosted glass
        idea: Light airy panels of frosted glass floating over a soft pastel haze, with thin white edges, light type weights and plenty of breathing room.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/8.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            haze: #eef0fb, the page base under a linear gradient from #fdf1f6 to #eef0fb to #ecf8f5
            roseGlow: #f9c9df, a radial blob at the top left
            periwinkleGlow: #c4d0ff, a radial blob at the top right
            aquaGlow: #bdeee0, a radial blob at the lower right
            lavenderGlow: #e3d2ff, a radial blob at the lower left
            glass: #ffffff, panels at 55 percent with a 22px blur, or 88 percent where blur is not supported
            edge: #ffffff, 1px panel borders at 85 percent and a 1px inner top highlight
            ink: #1f2340, text and headings
            slate: #4a4f6e, meta text, labels and axis text
            violet: #5b4bd6, the primary button, progress rings, this week's line and the focus ring
            violetDeep: #4636b8, links
            green: #0f6b4f, the On track status
            amber: #8a4a00, the At risk status
            raspberry: #b42347, the Behind status, its ring and the overdue fact
        type:
            Text in Segoe UI Variable Text, Segoe UI, system-ui, SF Pro Text,
            Helvetica Neue, Roboto, sans-serif, and display in Segoe UI
            Variable Display, SF Pro Display, Segoe UI, system-ui, sans-serif.
            Sizes are a 52px weight 300 greeting, 54px weight 200 summary
            figures with tabular numerals, 22px weight 400 section titles,
            16px weight 500 project names, 15px body at 1.55 and 13px meta and
            pills.
        layout:
            A floating glass pill top bar with the brand, search, a round
            bell, the user and New project. A centred hero gives the date, the
            greeting and one line on the overdue tasks, then the nav as a
            centred glass segmented control. Four glass summary panels follow
            in a row. Below, a grid puts the projects panel on the left, as
            rows with a progress ring, name, meta and status pill, and stacks
            the chart and activity panels on the right. Below 1000px the board
            stacks and the summary becomes two by two, and below 640px the
            search takes a full row and New project shrinks to its icon.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 20px between panels, 24px inside panels and 56px above the greeting.
        density: Airy. Few panels and a centred hero, about one screen for the whole dashboard.
        corners: 24px panels, 18px rows, 32px on the style sheet, and fully round pills, buttons, nav and search.
        borders: 1px white at 85 percent on every panel plus a 1px inner top highlight.
        shadows: Soft and wide, 0 10px 40px in rgba(60,50,140,0.10). The violet button glows with 0 6px 20px at 35 percent.
        icons:
            Thin rounded line icons at 18px with a 1.4 stroke. Status pills
            show a circle with a tick for On track, a diamond with a bang for
            At risk and a rounded square with a down arrow for Behind.
            Progress is a 56px ring with the percent inside. The chart is a
            dashed grey line for last week and a solid violet line with a soft
            area and dots for this week. Activity is a thin timeline with
            hollow dots.
        focus: A 2px violet outline offset 3px plus a 6px soft violet halo. A focused field gets a violet border, a 4px soft ring and a white fill.
        tone: Calm and reassuring in sentence case, such as A calm week overall and worth a look first.

    style9:
        number: 9
        run: 3
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Enterprise shell
        idea: A formal corporate suite, with a deep-blue shell bar, a collapsible tree nav, breadcrumbs and flat square tiles on light grey that frame the work like an official system of record.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/9.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            shell: #0f2a52, the shell bar and the top rule of the style sheet
            shellHover: #1d3f72, shell dividers and hover in the shell
            canvas: #edf0f4, the page behind the tiles
            tile: #ffffff, tiles, the tree nav and fields
            text: #1b2430, body text and headings
            muted: #556170, labels, meta text and chart axes
            line: #cdd3db, tile borders, with #e4e8ed between rows
            primary: #0b57b0, buttons, links, progress bars, this week's bars and the focus outline
            primaryDark: #083f80, primary hover and the current nav text
            selection: #e3edf9, the current nav item, pressed toggles and initials tiles
            positive: #1f6e3a, the On track circle
            attention: #8a5200, the At risk diamond, with the alert strip on #fff6e5
            critical: #b3241b, the Behind square and the overdue figure
        type:
            Segoe UI first, then system-ui, -apple-system, Roboto, Helvetica
            Neue, Arial, sans-serif. Sizes are 24px semibold for the page title,
            15px semibold for tile titles, 14px regular body at 1.43 line height,
            13px for table cells and meta, and 12px semibold for labels. Tree
            group headings are 12px semibold capitals with 0.06em spacing. KPI
            figures are 32px light weight with tabular figures.
        layout:
            A 48px deep-blue shell bar with an app launcher, the wordmark and a
            product label, a white search field, notifications and the user. A
            white tree nav 248px wide on the left holds three collapsible groups,
            Workspace, Organisation and Administration, with counts and a
            Collapse navigation button at the bottom. The main area has
            breadcrumbs, a toolbar with the title Portfolio overview, the
            greeting line and the Customise, Export and New project buttons, then
            an amber alert strip for the overdue tasks. A row of four KPI tiles
            follows, two with micro charts. Below, the projects table tile takes
            two thirds and a column of the Throughput chart tile and the Recent
            activity tile takes one third. Below 820px the tree becomes a
            horizontal tab row under the shell, and below 560px the search drops
            to its own row and the tiles stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 8px gaps between tiles, 16px tile padding and a 24px page gutter.
        density: Compact. 44px table rows, 36px nav rows and a 48px shell bar.
        corners: 4px on tiles and 2px on buttons, fields, avatars and segmented controls.
        borders: 1px #cdd3db around every tile, 1px #e4e8ed between rows and a 3px primary bar on the left of the current nav item.
        shadows: None. Tiles are flat and separated by the grey canvas.
        icons:
            16px line icons with a 1.5 stroke, square caps and mitred joins.
            Status uses filled 14px shapes beside the word, a circle with a tick,
            a diamond with a bar and a square with a cross, and a legend under
            the table names each shape. People show as square initials tiles.
        focus: A 2px primary outline offset 1px, white inside the shell bar. A focused field gets a primary border plus the outline, and a focused row gets the selection fill with an inset outline.
        tone: Formal and neutral, such as Portfolio overview, Throughput, Attention required and Review overdue tasks.

    style10:
        number: 10
        run: 3
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Retro desktop
        idea: A 1990s desktop, with silver bevelled windows on a teal backdrop, where each part of the dashboard opens as its own window with a title bar, sunken fields and pixel-crisp edges.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/10.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            desktop: #008080, the backdrop behind the windows, with white icon labels
            face: #c0c0c0, windows, buttons and the taskbar
            highlight: #ffffff, the top-left bevel edge and sunken field fills
            light: #dfdfdf, the inner light bevel edge
            shadow: #808080, the inner dark bevel edge and inactive title bars
            dark: #0a0a0a, the outer dark bevel edge
            text: #000000, all body text, with #3a3a3a for meta
            navy: #000080, the active title bar, the selected row, progress blocks and links
            titleEnd: #1084d0, the right end of the title bar gradient
            okGreen: #006400, the On track tick
            caution: #ffd800, the At risk triangle with a black outline
            stopRed: #b00000, the Behind square and the overdue readout
            monitor: #00ff00 on #000000, this week's chart bars, with #00a800 for last week and #005a00 grid lines
        type:
            Tahoma, MS Sans Serif, Microsoft Sans Serif, Segoe UI, Geneva,
            Verdana, sans-serif, with font smoothing off. Body is 12px at 1.35
            line height, title bars 12px bold, the greeting 14px bold, meta 11px
            and summary readouts 22px bold in right-aligned sunken boxes. Chart
            axes use Courier New at 9px.
        layout:
            A teal desktop with a column of six 32px desktop icons on the left
            as the nav, the current one with its label on navy. Beside it sit
            the windows on a grid with 16px gaps. A full-width Brightwork - Home
            window has a menu row, a toolbar with Find, New project...,
            notifications and the user, a message area with a warning icon,
            the greeting and the overdue line, and four group boxes with the
            summary readouts. Below it, a Projects folder window titled C drive Projects, a list view with
            raised column headers and a status bar sits beside a Task Monitor
            chart window and an Event Log window. A taskbar with Start, open
            window buttons and a clock tray closes the desktop. Below 1000px the
            windows stack, and below 640px the icons form a row across the top.
        spacing: A 4px unit. 8px window padding and 16px gaps between windows.
        density: Compact. 12px text, about 22px list rows and 23px buttons.
        corners: None anywhere. Every edge is square and pixel aligned.
        borders: Two-pixel bevels built from four inset lines. Raised for windows and buttons, sunken for fields, lists and readouts, and etched for group boxes.
        shadows: None outside the bevels. Depth comes only from light and dark edges.
        icons:
            16px and 32px pixel icons with black outlines and flat fills, drawn
            with crisp edges. Each title bar ends in minimise, maximise and close
            buttons with pixel glyphs. Status is a green tick, a yellow triangle
            with an exclamation mark or a red square with a white cross, always
            with the word. Progress is a sunken bar of navy blocks.
        focus: A 1px dotted black outline inset 4px inside the control. A selected row is navy with white text and a dotted white outline when focused.
        tone: System dialog speak, such as Find, New project..., 6 object(s), Event Log and a Projects folder title.

    style11:
        number: 11
        run: 3
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Notebook
        idea: A personal planner on lined paper, with a red margin, taped sticky notes, highlighter marks and handwritten headings, while the numbers and names stay in a clean sans so they read at a glance.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/11.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            desk: #e9e4d8, the surface behind the paper
            paper: #fffdf5, the notebook page
            rule: #c6dbf0, ruled lines every 32px
            margin: #e07070, the margin line and link underlines
            ink: #1f2a44, text, the primary button and this week's chart bars
            pencil: #4f5666, meta, dates and placeholders
            highlighter: #fff176, emphasis marks and the focus fill
            pinkMarker: #ffc9db, the highlight on the project that is behind
            noteYellow: #fff1a6, sticky notes
            noteBlue: #d7ecff, sticky notes and index tabs
            notePink: #ffdbe4, the overdue note and the activity card
            noteGreen: #def3c9, notes and the name tag
            greenPen: #2b6a2f, the On track tick
            brownPen: #8a4b00, the At risk triangle
            redPen: #b3261e, the Behind cross and the circle around the overdue count
        type:
            Headings, labels and status words use a hand stack, Segoe Print,
            Bradley Hand, Comic Neue, Comic Sans MS, Chalkboard SE, cursive.
            Data uses system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Arial,
            sans-serif. Sizes are a 44px hand headline, 28px hand section
            titles, 24px hand card titles, 44px bold sans figures, 16px semibold
            sans project names, 15px sans body and 14px meta, all set on a 32px
            line grid.
        layout:
            A notebook page centred on the desk, up to 1200px, with punched
            holes and a red margin line 80px from the left. Coloured index tabs
            along the top edge are the nav, the current tab merges into the
            page. The header holds the wordmark with a doodled star, an
            underlined search, the New project button, a bell and a green name
            tag. A handwritten greeting with a squiggle sits above the date and a
            highlighted overdue line with a red circled 4. Four taped sticky
            notes, each rotated a little, hold the summary. Below, the projects
            are a to-do list on the ruled lines on the left, and on the right a
            taped graph-paper card holds the chart and a pink card holds the
            activity. Below 1000px the columns stack and the notes form a two by
            two grid. Below 640px the margin moves in to 40px.
        spacing: An 8px unit tied to a 32px line grid, with 24px between notes and 48px between columns.
        density: Relaxed. Each project takes about three ruled lines.
        corners: Square paper and notes. Buttons and progress bars use a wobbly hand-drawn radius, 255px 15px 225px 15px over 15px 225px 15px 255px.
        borders: 2px ink strokes on buttons and progress bars, a 2px ink underline on fields and dashed pencil rules between activity notes.
        shadows: A soft paper lift on notes and cards, 2px 4px 8px in warm brown at 18 percent. The primary button has a 3px highlighter offset shadow.
        icons:
            Doodled line strokes with round ends, about 2px. Status is a pen
            tick, a wobbly triangle with an exclamation mark or a scribbled
            cross, with the word in the hand font. Progress bars are hatched in
            ink. Strips of translucent tape hold notes and cards.
        focus: A 2px dashed ink outline offset 3px. A focused field or row gets a highlighter stroke behind it and a thicker underline.
        tone: Personal and chatty, like notes to self, such as Morning, Mara!, do these first! and see all 6.

    style12:
        number: 12
        run: 3
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Monochrome minimal
        idea: Black, white and grey only, one weight, hairlines and a great deal of empty space, so the content itself is the only thing that carries weight.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/12.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            white: #ffffff, the page and the secondary button
            ink: #111111, text, the primary button, this week's chart marks and list top rules
            grey: #595959, labels, meta text and chart axes
            mid: #8c8c8c, last week's chart marks only
            rule: #d4d4d4, field lines, dividers and progress tracks
            hair: #ececec, row separators and section dividers
            wash: #f4f4f4, the fill of a focused row
        type:
            One family at weight 400 only, -apple-system, Helvetica Neue,
            Helvetica, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Arial, sans-serif. Sizes are
            72px summary figures with tight letter spacing, a 48px headline,
            16px names and lead text, 14px body at 1.6 line height and 12px grey
            labels. Bold is never used, and hierarchy comes from size alone.
        layout:
            A 96px header line with a lowercase wordmark, 12px nav words with a
            1px underline on the current one, an underlined search, notification
            and user words and a black New project button. The page is a run of
            full-width bands split by hairlines, each with a 12px label in a
            240px left column and the content on the right. The bands are the
            greeting, the four figures split by thin vertical rules, the
            numbered project list, and the chart beside the activity list.
            Content is capped at 1200px with 48px side gutters. Below 1100px the
            label sits above its content. Below 820px the nav moves to its own
            row, the figures form a two by two grid and each project shows its
            progress and facts under its name.
        spacing: An 8px unit used in large steps, 96px band padding, 48px gutters and 72px project rows.
        density: Very low. One idea per band, and the page scrolls rather than crowds.
        corners: None.
        borders: 1px only, #ececec between rows, #d4d4d4 for fields and dividers and #111111 to open a list.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            No pictograms. Status is a 10px geometric mark beside its word, an
            open circle for On track, an open triangle for At risk and a solid
            square for Behind. Progress is a 1px track with a 3px black fill.
            The chart is thin stems with open dots for last week and solid dots
            for this week.
        focus: A 1px ink outline offset 4px. A focused field gets a doubled ink underline, and a focused row gets the wash fill and a 1px ink outline.
        tone: Quiet and plain, with full stops and few words, such as Good morning, Mara. and Everything else is moving.

    style13:
        number: 13
        run: 3
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Bento tiles
        idea: A modern product page, where the dashboard is a bento grid of softly tinted tiles in different sizes, with big rounded corners and large heavy numbers that make the key facts land first.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/13.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #f6f5f2, the page, inner chips, fields and the nav track
            tile: #ffffff, the header bar and plain tiles
            lilac: #efeaff, the hero tile
            mint: #e2f6ec, the active projects tile
            sky: #e4efff, the due this week tile
            sun: #fff5d4, the hours tile
            peach: #ffede1, the user avatar and accents
            text: #17161c, text and the dark hero button
            muted: #57546a, tile titles and meta text
            line: #e6e3ec, progress ring tracks and activity chip borders
            violet: #5b3fd9, the primary button, this week's bars, progress rings and the focus ring
            violetDark: #4529b8, the hero figure, links and primary hover
            violetSoft: #9283d8, last week's bars
            green: #17663f, the On track check
            amber: #8a4a00, the At risk diamond
            red: #b4232a, the Behind cross and the notification badge
        type:
            System sans, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica
            Neue, Arial, sans-serif. Sizes are a 168px black weight hero figure,
            64px black weight tile figures, a 32px extra bold greeting, 16px
            extra bold project names, 15px regular body, 15px bold muted tile
            titles and 13px extra bold status words. Large type is set tight,
            from minus 0.03em to minus 0.06em.
        layout:
            A white header bar with 24px corners holds the wordmark with a four
            colour square logo, the nav as a segmented pill track, a search pill,
            the New project button, a notifications square and the avatar. Below
            it a four column bento grid with 16px gaps. A two by two lilac hero
            tile holds the greeting, the date, a giant 4 with tasks are overdue
            and a dark Review overdue tasks button. Mint, sky and sun tiles hold
            active projects, due this week and hours. A tall white chart tile
            on the right spans three rows and shows horizontal bars per day. A
            wide projects tile shows six chips in two columns, each with a
            progress ring, and a wide activity tile shows six chips in three
            columns. Below 1180px the grid has two columns, and below 860px the
            tiles stack in reading order with the small figure tiles in pairs.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px between tiles, 24px tile padding and 8px between inner chips.
        density: Medium. A few big tiles, each fact with room of its own.
        corners: 24px on tiles and the header bar, 18px on inner chips, 16px on buttons and fields, 14px on avatars and fully round chart bars.
        borders: None on tiles. Only activity chips carry a 1px #e6e3ec border.
        shadows: None, apart from a faint 1px lift on the current nav pill.
        icons:
            Rounded line icons with a 2.2 stroke, sized to the text, set in 40px
            frosted white squares on the figure tiles. Status is a bold check, a
            hollow diamond or a cross beside a bold word, with a key under the
            projects. Progress is a 52px ring with the percentage inside.
        focus: A 3px violet outline offset 3px. A focused field turns white with a violet border and a 4px soft violet halo.
        tone: Confident and short, such as Good morning, Mara, All 6 projects and See everything.

    style14:
        number: 14
        run: 4
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Terminal light
        idea: A light terminal session on warm cream, where everything is monospace, panels are drawn with box lines and progress is a row of hash marks.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/14.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            cream: #fdf6e3, the page
            bar: #eee8d5, the top status line and the bottom key bar
            ink: #2b2a26, text, box lines, the primary button fill and the cursor block
            dim: #5c5a50, meta text, column headers and the hollow cells of last week's chart
            rule: #a59f8c, dot leaders and dashed rules
            blue: #1d4f91, links and the filled cells of this week's chart
            plum: #8a2f6b, key hints in brackets, user handles and heading markers
            ok: #2f6a00, the [+] ON TRACK code and the user at host part of the prompt
            warn: #8a5200, the [!] AT RISK code
            bad: #b0221c, the [x] BEHIND code and the overdue count
            sel: #f5e7b8, the selected row and the focus fill
        type:
            One monospace stack for everything, ui-monospace, SF Mono,
            JetBrains Mono, Menlo, Consolas, DejaVu Sans Mono, Liberation Mono,
            monospace, with tabular figures. Body is 14px at 1.5 line height,
            13px on phones. Panel titles and status codes are 14px bold.
            Column headers are 14px regular capitals in the dim colour. The
            style sheet title is 20px bold. There are no other sizes.
        layout:
            A tmux style status line runs across the top with a plum square
            and the lowercase wordmark, the nav as numbered windows such as
            0 home and 1 projects with the current one bold, underlined and
            starred, and the user name on the right. Below it sits the prompt
            line mara at brightwork ~ $ dashboard with a solid block cursor,
            then a row with the search box, the new project button and the
            notify(3) button, each showing its key hint. A double lined
            greeting box holds the greeting and the overdue warning. Then a
            two column grid holds the summary box beside the chart box, and the
            projects table and the activity log each span the full width. A key
            bar of shortcuts closes the page. Content is capped at 1240px.
            Below 860px everything is one column, and the table scrolls inside
            its box.
        spacing: Character grid. A 1ch horizontal unit, an 8px vertical unit, 16px between panels and 20px top padding inside a box.
        density: Medium high. One record per line, with no cards.
        corners: None anywhere. Everything is square.
        borders:
            Every panel is a 1px ink box with its lowercase title cut into the
            top edge between box drawing tees, and an optional dim hint or
            link cut into the top right edge. The greeting box uses a 3px
            double line. Table headers sit over a dashed ink line, and the
            summary uses dotted leaders between each label and its value.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            No pictograms at all. Status is a bracket code and a capital word,
            [+] ON TRACK, [!] AT RISK and [x] BEHIND. Progress is ten
            characters of hash marks and dashes in brackets followed by the
            percent. Key hints such as [n], [/] and [o] appear in plum. The
            chart is columns of small cells, hollow for last week and filled
            blue for this week, with the value above each column and the day
            letter below.
        focus: A 2px dashed ink outline offset 2px with the sel fill. The primary button keeps its ink fill and takes the outline offset 3px.
        tone: Lowercase command words, such as tail -f activity, ls -a, notify(3) and grep. Full sentences appear only in the greeting.

    style15:
        number: 15
        run: 4
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Document workspace
        idea: The dashboard as one calm document page, with a narrow column, a big title, callouts, toggles and properties, beside a slim grey list of pages.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/15.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #ffffff, the document
            sidebar: #f6f5f2, the page list and the search field
            hover: #ecebe7, the current and hovered page in the sidebar
            text: #2a2a28, body text, titles and the progress fill
            muted: #6b6a66, property names, column names and meta text
            line: #e9e8e4, row rules, dividers and progress tracks
            linkBlue: #2f5fa7, the primary button, the focus ring, links in callouts and this week's bars
            callout: #fbf3e4 with a #ead9b5 border, the overdue callout
            onTrack: #25613a text on #e6f1e8, the On track tag
            atRisk: #8a5300 text on #fbeed5, the At risk tag
            behind: #a32b1f text on #fbe4e1, the Behind tag and the overdue count
            neutralTag: #4d5c70 text on #eef2f7, team tags
            lastWeek: #8f8d86, last week's chart bars
        type:
            System sans, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Segoe UI,
            system-ui, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial, sans-serif. Sizes are
            40px bold for the page title, 24px bold for headings, 20px
            semibold for toggle titles, 28px semibold for summary figures,
            16px body at 1.6 line height, 14px for properties, tables and the
            sidebar, and 13px for tags.
        layout:
            A light grey sidebar 240px wide lists the workspace name and the
            pages with a glyph before each, and two project pages nest under
            Projects. A slim top bar holds the breadcrumb Brightwork / Home on
            the left and the search, the notifications bell, the New project
            button and a round initials avatar on the right. The document is a
            centred column at most 760px wide with a 64px line glyph, the big
            title Home, then property rows for Signed in, Date and Needs
            attention, a divider, a greeting sentence, a warm callout for the
            overdue tasks, a This week heading over four figures split by thin
            lines, and three open toggles for Projects, Tasks completed and
            Recent activity. Projects is a database table with Name, Team,
            Status, Progress, Tasks and Due columns and a faint New project
            row under it. Activity is a plain bullet list. Below 860px the
            sidebar becomes a wrapped row of page links above the page, and
            below 560px the figures form a two by two grid and the table
            scrolls inside its toggle.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 48px above the title, 32px above headings, 16px callout padding and 8px table cell padding.
        density: Calm. One narrow column with generous line height, and toggles fold detail away.
        corners: 4px on tags, buttons, fields, callouts and sidebar rows. Avatars are round.
        borders: 1px #e9e8e4 row rules and dividers only, plus the callout border. There are no cards.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            16px thin line glyphs with a 1.6 stroke and round caps sit before
            every page in the sidebar, every property name and every column
            name, and a 64px glyph of the same kind sits above the page title.
            Toggles use a small chevron that turns down when open. Status tags
            carry a circle tick for On track, a triangle for At risk and a
            crossed square for Behind.
        focus: A 2px #2f5fa7 outline offset 2px with 4px rounding. A focused field gets a #2f5fa7 border and a 1px ring of the same colour.
        tone: Plain, personal sentence case, such as Needs attention, Recent activity and Open overdue tasks.

    style16:
        number: 16
        run: 4
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Analytics forward
        idea: Charts lead everything, with a large hero chart on top, a sparkline and a delta on every number, and progress rings for projects in deep teal and coral on white.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/16.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            background: #ffffff, the page and cards
            wash: #f2f7f7, the hero stat panel and the last week band in the chart
            ink: #10292c, text and ring labels
            muted: #4f6466, labels, axes and meta text
            grid: #dbe5e6, card borders, gridlines and ring tracks
            teal: #0f5f66, the chart line, the primary button, good deltas, On track and its ring
            tealSoft: #e8f3f3, avatars and the selected row
            coral: #c4452e, the peak marker, the focus outline, the Behind glyph and ring
            coralText: #b23a22, bad deltas, the Behind word and the overdue chip text
            coralSoft: #fbeae6, the overdue chip and the overdue card wash
            amber: #9a5b00, the At risk glyph, word and ring
        type:
            System sans, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica
            Neue, Arial, sans-serif, with tabular figures everywhere. The hero
            figure is 72px light. KPI figures are 36px light. The greeting is
            22px bold, section titles 18px bold, project names 16px bold, body
            15px, deltas 14px bold, and eyebrow labels 12px bold capitals with
            0.08em letter spacing.
        layout:
            A white top bar with a teal chart logo, the wordmark, tabs with a
            3px teal underline on the current one, the search, the New project
            button, the bell with a coral count and the avatar with the name.
            A greeting row puts the greeting and date on the left and a coral
            overdue chip on the right. The hero card comes next and spans the
            full width, a 260px stat panel with 73 tasks completed this week,
            the delta and three small facts beside a large area line chart of
            all 14 days. A row of four KPI cards follows, each with an eyebrow,
            a figure, a sparkline of eight weeks and a delta line. Projects are
            a three by two grid of cards, each with a 72px progress ring, the
            name, a meta line and the status. Activity is one bordered list
            with time, initials and the sentence. Below 1100px the KPIs and
            projects go two across, below 860px the hero stacks, and below
            600px everything is one column and the hero chart scrolls sideways
            inside its card with a hint under it.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px gaps between cards and inside them, 24px hero padding and 40px between sections.
        density: Medium. Every figure travels with a chart, a delta and a comparison line.
        corners: 6px on cards, buttons, fields and chips. Avatars and rings are round.
        borders: 1px #dbe5e6 on every card. The overdue KPI card takes a pale coral border and a coral wash fading to white.
        shadows: None. Cards are flat and outlined.
        icons:
            18px line icons with a 2px round stroke for search, bell and plus.
            Deltas use an up arrow or a flat right arrow before a signed
            number. Status glyphs are solid shapes with a white mark, a circle
            with a tick for On track, a diamond with a bar for At risk and a
            down triangle for Behind, always beside the word. The hero chart
            has white dots with teal rings and a larger coral dot labelled 17
            peak.
        focus: A 3px coral outline offset 2px. A focused field also turns its border teal.
        tone: Numeric and comparative, such as +14 · +24%, vs 59 last week, +1 worse and Best day.

    style17:
        number: 17
        run: 4
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Luxury
        idea: An ivory house style with thin, widely tracked capitals, a dark gold accent, hairline rules and a great deal of quiet space.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/17.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            ivory: #faf7f0, the page
            stone: #f3eee3, the style sheet ground
            ink: #1e1b16, text and the primary button
            taupe: #5e574b, capital labels and last week's dashed line
            darkGold: #7a5c1e, the accent, progress fills, this week's line, the focus outline and At risk
            hairline: #d9d0bd, rules between entries and sections and progress tracks
            sage: #3d5a40, On track
            oxblood: #8e2f22, Behind and the overdue figure and word
        type:
            Display face Didot, Didot LT STD, Bodoni 72, Bodoni MT, Big Caslon,
            Libre Bodoni, Hoefler Text, Garamond, Times New Roman, serif, always
            regular weight. The wordmark is 40px capitals with 0.42em tracking,
            the greeting 56px italic, summary figures 72px, section titles 22px
            capitals with 0.36em tracking and project names 24px capitals with
            0.16em tracking. Body is Avenir Next, Avenir, Gill Sans, Helvetica
            Neue, Segoe UI, system-ui, sans-serif at 15px regular and 1.7 line
            height. Labels are 11px sans capitals with 0.28em tracking in taupe.
        layout:
            One centred column 880px wide. A slim utility row shows the date on
            the left and an underlined search, Notices · 3 and Mara Okafor on
            the right, over a hairline. A centred masthead holds the spaced
            wordmark, a 40px gold rule and a centred row of spaced capital nav
            links with a gold underline on Home. The greeting is centred with
            much space around it, a capital date line, the italic greeting, one
            sentence about the four overdue tasks and two buttons. Each later
            section opens with a hairline and a centred spaced title over a
            small caption, The Week as a two by two grid of large figures split
            by hairlines, The Portfolio as one project per row with an italic
            gold No. 1, the name, the percent, a capital meta line, the status
            and a hairline progress track, The Fortnight as a thin line chart
            over a two row table of daily values, and Correspondence as rows of
            time beside a name and a sentence. Below 720px the wordmark
            shrinks, rows stack and the figure grid stays two by two.
        spacing: An 8px unit used generously. 96px between sections, 36px inside portfolio rows and 40px inside figure cells.
        density: Very sparse. One or two elements per row.
        corners: Square throughout. Only the palette swatches are round.
        borders: 1px hairline rules in #d9d0bd between entries and sections, a 1px ink rule above the style sheet and a 40px gold rule under the wordmark. Progress fills are a 3px gold line on the hairline track.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            No pictograms. Status is a 12px thin outline mark beside a tracked
            capital word, a circle for On track in sage, a lozenge for At risk
            in gold and a struck square for Behind in oxblood. Notifications
            are the word Notices with a count. The chart uses hollow taupe dots
            on a dashed line for last week and solid gold dots on a solid line
            for this week.
        focus: A 2px dark gold outline offset 4px. A focused field gets a 2px gold underline as well.
        tone: Courteous and composed, with titled sections such as The Week, The Portfolio, The Fortnight and Correspondence, and small numbers written as words in prose.

    style18:
        number: 18
        run: 4
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Bauhaus
        idea: Primary red, yellow and blue blocks locked together by thick black bars, with circles, squares and triangles as both structure and status.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/18.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            paper: #f5f1e8, the page
            white: #ffffff, fields, the chart box and the style sheet
            black: #111111, text, the header, thick bars, progress fills and the hours block
            red: #d1281f, the primary button, the overdue block, the Behind square and this week's bars
            redText: #b8211a, red text on paper when needed
            yellow: #f2c230, the date tag, the activity panel, the tasks due block and the At risk triangle
            blue: #1f4fa0, the focus outline, the active projects block, the On track circle and last week's bars
            track: #d9d4c7, the empty part of progress bars
            cream: #fff8dc, a focused field and a focused row
        type:
            Geometric sans, Futura, Futura PT, Century Gothic, Avenir Next,
            Avenir, Trebuchet MS, Gill Sans, sans-serif. Summary figures are
            80px extra bold with tight tracking, the greeting 64px extra bold
            capitals, section titles 28px extra bold capitals, project names
            18px extra bold in sentence case, body 16px medium, and labels 13
            to 14px extra bold capitals with 0.08em tracking.
        layout:
            A black header with a 12px red bar under it holds a red square logo
            with a yellow circle, the capital wordmark, capital nav links with
            a 4px yellow underline on Home, a search field with a yellow square
            icon cell, a red New project button, a blue square showing the
            notification count and a yellow initials circle. The hero is a
            seven to five split, a yellow date tag, the huge greeting and a
            white strip with a thick red left edge saying 4 tasks are overdue
            on the left, and a composition of a blue circle, a yellow square, a
            red triangle, an open black ring and crossing black bars on the
            right. A 12px black bar tops four unequal summary blocks in blue,
            yellow, red and black. Below, a seven to five split puts the
            projects list on the left and a white chart box with a yellow
            corner square above a yellow activity panel on the right. Below
            900px the splits stack and the summary goes two by two, and below
            560px the project rows stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 20px block padding, 32 to 56px between bands and a 40px column gap.
        density: Bold and medium. Few, large elements in an uneven grid.
        corners: None. Only true circles are round.
        borders: Thick black bars, 12px under the header and above the summary, 8px above each section title, 4px around boxes, fields and secondary buttons and 2px between rows.
        shadows: None. Depth comes from flat overlapping colour.
        icons:
            Solid geometric glyphs only. Status is a blue circle for On track,
            a yellow triangle with a black outline for At risk and a red square
            for Behind, always beside the capital word, and a key under the
            list spells this out. Summary labels and activity bullets use solid
            white or black circles, squares, triangles and a quarter circle.
            Progress is a 14px black bar on the track colour.
        focus: A 4px blue outline offset 3px. Controls on the black header use a 4px yellow outline, and a focused field also takes the cream fill.
        tone: Direct and declarative with capital labels, such as Good afternoon, Mara. and 4 tasks are overdue.

    style19:
        number: 19
        run: 5
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Tonal surfaces
        idea: A modern mobile-OS app feel, where layers of tinted teal-grey surfaces replace borders and a floating action button, chips and a navigation rail do the work.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/19.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            surface: #f6fafa, the page and the project items inside panels
            containerLow: #edf3f4, the rail, panels and summary tiles
            container: #e4eced, the bottom bar and the style sheet ground
            containerHigh: #d9e4e6, the search bar, unselected chips, filled fields and progress tracks
            onSurface: #161d1f, text
            onVariant: #3d494c, labels, meta text and inactive icons
            primary: #00677d, the filled button, progress fill, links, this week's bars and the focus ring
            primaryContainer: #b8eaff with #001f28 text, the floating action button
            secondaryContainer: #cde7ef with #0a2229 text, the active nav pill, the selected chip and the tonal button
            onTrack: #1b6a36 on #c4eecb, the On track chip
            atRisk: #6c5200 on #fde39f, the At risk chip
            behind: #9b2a20 on #ffdad4, the Behind chip, the overdue tile and the overdue assist chip
        type:
            Roboto Flex, Roboto, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Helvetica
            Neue, Arial, sans-serif. Display numbers are 45px regular on a 52px
            line, the greeting is 36px regular, section titles are 22px regular,
            project names are 16px medium, body is 14px on a 20px line, and
            meta and chips are 12px to 14px medium. Large text stays at regular
            weight, never bold.
        layout:
            An 88px navigation rail on the left holds a square brand mark, a
            56px floating action button for New project, and six items with an
            icon above a 12px label. The main area has a top app bar with the
            brand, a fully round search bar, a notifications icon button and an
            avatar. Then the greeting with the date and a tinted overdue chip,
            four summary tiles in a row, and a panel of projects with filter
            chips and a two column grid of items, beside a chart panel and an
            activity panel. Below 640px the rail hides, the search drops under
            the app bar, an extended floating button labelled New project sits
            at the end of the content, and a six item bottom navigation bar
            closes the dashboard in the page flow, not fixed.
        spacing: A 4px grid. 8px between project items, 12px between tiles, 16px panel padding and 24px page margins.
        density: Medium. Big display numbers, 48px touch targets and two project columns.
        corners: 16px on panels, tiles and the floating button, 12px on items and icon tiles, 8px on chips and status chips, 20px on full round buttons, 28px on the sheet top.
        borders: None. Surfaces separate by tone alone, and filled text fields keep a 1px bottom line.
        shadows: Only the floating action button, 0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,0.18) plus 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.08).
        icons:
            24px solid geometric icons. The active nav icon sits in a 56 by 32
            pill. Status chips carry a filled circle with a tick for On track,
            a filled diamond with a bar for At risk and a filled square with a
            dash for Behind. Chart bars are fully round pills.
        focus: A 3px #00677d outline offset 2px. A focused filled field gets a 3px primary bottom bar instead.
        tone: Short, friendly and plain, such as Hi, Mara, See all, and chip counts like At risk 1.

    style20:
        number: 20
        run: 5
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Organic wellness
        idea: A calm wellness-app mood in sage, cream and terracotta, with soft blob shapes, generous rounded cards, leaf-shaped progress and gentle reassuring words.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/20.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            cream: #f8f3e8, the page
            card: #fffbf3, cards, the nav pill, search and round buttons
            oat: #efe6d4, the leaf progress track and the style sheet ground
            sageTint: #dfe8d6, the On track pill, the soft button, a summary pebble and last week's chart area
            sage: #9db59a, decorative blobs and link underlines only
            sageDeep: #3f5e45, headings, numbers, the primary button, progress fill and the chart line
            terracotta: #96421f, the overdue phrase, the Behind status and the focus ring
            terracottaTint: #f3dccf, the Behind pill and the overdue pebble
            ochre: #7a5410 on #f4e4c1, the At risk pill
            text: #2e3a30, body text
            muted: #5a6559, meta text and captions
        type:
            Gill Sans, Gill Sans MT, Seravek, Optima, Candara, Trebuchet MS,
            sans-serif, at regular weight for headings. The greeting is 46px on
            a 1.1 line, summary numbers are 44px, section titles 28px, project
            names 21px, the calm lead line 20px, body 17px on a 1.6 line and
            meta 15px. Pills and buttons are 14px to 16px semibold.
        layout:
            No sidebar. A centred column capped at 1200px. The header holds a
            leaf brand mark in a blob, a floating pill of six nav links, a
            round search, a round bell and an organic avatar. A hero splits
            into the greeting, date, a calm sentence and a Start a new project
            button on the left, and four summary numbers set in irregular
            pebble shapes in a two by two grid on the right. Large pale sage
            and terracotta blobs drift behind it. Below, six project cards sit
            in three columns, then a wide chart card beside an activity card.
            Below 1000px the hero stacks and projects go to two columns, and
            below 640px everything is one column with the nav as a three by
            two grid.
        spacing: An 8px unit used generously. 24px card gaps, 28 to 32px card padding and 56px between sections.
        density: Low. Three project cards per row, large type and plenty of cream around everything.
        corners: 32px on cards, 40px on large panels, 64px on the sheet top, fully round pills and buttons, and irregular percentage radii on the pebbles and avatars.
        borders: None on cards. Fields use a soft 1.5px inset line in #cbbfa6.
        shadows: One warm soft shadow, 0 10px 30px rgba(92,72,40,0.08).
        icons:
            22px thin rounded line icons with a 1.6 stroke. Status pills use
            solid shapes, a leaf for On track, a soft rounded triangle for At
            risk and a soft rounded square for Behind. Progress is a leaf, a
            16px bar with two opposite round corners. The chart is a smooth
            curved area, pale for last week and deeper sage for this week, with
            the peak marked.
        focus: A 3px terracotta outline offset 3px. A focused field gets a 2px sage deep inner ring and turns white.
        tone: Calm and reassuring, such as A steady week, could use a little care today, projects growing and Moments from the team.

    style21:
        number: 21
        run: 5
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Gamified
        idea: Productivity as a friendly game, with XP bars, level badges, a streak counter and achievement chips in bold purple, orange and green on white.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/21.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            white: #ffffff, the page and cards
            lilac: #f3effc, the XP track, the active tab and avatar tiles
            lilac2: #e2d9f8, the XP track rim, last week's bars and the secondary button edge
            line: #e4e0ef, 3px card outlines and the quest card press edge
            purple: #6d28d9, XP fill, level badges, links and this week's bars
            purpleDark: #4c1d95, the focus halo and chart value labels
            green: #15803d, the go button and the top level badge, with a #0d5a2a press edge
            orange: #c2410c, the streak number and notification count, with #8a2e08 text on #ffedd5
            gold: #facc15 with #422006 text, the score chip and the focus ring
            red: #b91c1c on #fee2e2, the overdue cards and the Behind tag
            text: #1e1b2e, body text, with #565166 for muted text
        type:
            ui-rounded, SF Pro Rounded, Arial Rounded MT Bold, Varela Round,
            Nunito, Trebuchet MS, system-ui, sans-serif. Weights are heavy,
            900 for headings and numbers and 600 for body. The score is 44px,
            the greeting 30px, section titles 22px, quest names 18px, body
            15px, tags 13px. Buttons are 15px uppercase with 0.02em tracking.
        layout:
            A top bar with a hexagon lightning logo, six icon tabs, a search,
            a bell with a count bubble and the avatar, kept on one line on wide
            screens. Below it three columns. The left player column holds the
            greeting card, an orange streak card with a flame and 14 day
            streak, a red overdue card and a two by two grid of summary stats.
            The centre quest board shows six project cards in two columns,
            each with a hexagon level badge, an XP bar, task count and status
            tag, plus a green New project button. The right column holds the
            chart card and a team feed with achievement chips. Below 1240px the
            right column moves under the others, and below 640px all is one
            column with tabs as a three by two grid.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px between quest cards, 18 to 20px card padding and 24px page gutters.
        density: Medium. Three columns, chunky controls and every number big and bold.
        corners: 24px on cards, 16px on buttons and rows, 14px on fields and tabs, hexagons for level badges.
        borders: 3px solid #e4e0ef on every card, field and tab. Status tags use a 2px tinted rim.
        shadows: No blur. Solid offset press edges, 0 5px 0 a darker shade under buttons and 0 6px 0 #e4e0ef under quest cards.
        icons:
            22px chunky filled icons. Level badges are 52 by 58 hexagons with
            LV over the level, which is the tens digit of the percent done.
            Status tags show a star for On track, a triangle with an
            exclamation mark for At risk and a circle with a down arrow for
            Behind. Each feed item earns a small achievement chip such as Task
            done, Team player, Level up, New quests, Deep focus or Delivered.
            Chart bars are rounded with the value printed on top.
        focus: A 4px gold outline offset 2px, ringed by a 7px dark purple halo.
        tone: Upbeat and playful but plain, such as Let’s go, Mara!, Quest board, 14 day streak and +14 on last week, with uppercase buttons.

    style22:
        number: 22
        run: 5
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Signage
        idea: Wayfinding signage for work, with huge high-contrast type, black and safety-yellow bands, big pictograms and numbered sections that read from across the room.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/22.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            white: #ffffff, the page and section ground
            black: #111111, text, rules, the top band, the primary button and this week's bars
            safetyYellow: #ffcc00, the greeting band, the active nav item, At risk and the focus halo
            goGreen: #00703c with white, the On track pictogram and word
            stopRed: #c8102e with white, the Behind pictogram and word
            midGrey: #8c8c8c, last week's chart bars only
            lightGrey: #e6e6e6, the meter track
            muted: #444444, placeholder text
        type:
            Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial Nova, Arial, Liberation Sans,
            sans-serif, heavy and mostly uppercase. Summary numbers are up to
            128px at weight 900 with tight tracking, the greeting up to 96px
            uppercase, section titles up to 56px uppercase, project names up to
            40px, activity text 24px and labels 20px weight 800 uppercase with
            0.04em tracking. Sizes scale down with clamp on phones.
        layout:
            Full width stacked bands, no columns. A black top band holds a
            yellow square B mark, uppercase nav words with the current one on
            yellow, a white search block, a square bell and the avatar. A
            yellow band carries a black circle badge, the greeting, the date
            with a black 4 TASKS OVERDUE tag and a big black New project
            button. Then four giant counts split by thick black rules, with the
            overdue count reversed to yellow on black. Numbered sections follow
            like platform signs, 1 Projects as one full width row per project
            with a pictogram tile, name, status word, facts and a giant
            percent over a thick meter, 2 Tasks done with week totals beside
            large bars, and 3 Latest as a departure board of times and events.
            A hazard stripe ends the dashboard. Phones stack each row.
        spacing: An 8px unit in big steps. 24px row padding, 48px section padding and a 40px page gutter.
        density: Very low. One project per full width row and one fact per line.
        corners: Square everywhere, except 6px on pictogram tiles and section number blocks and a full circle on the badge.
        borders: Heavy black rules, 8px between bands, 4px between rows and cells and 3px in the style sheet tables.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            Big solid pictograms in 88px tiles, a ringed tick on green for On
            track, a solid triangle with an exclamation mark on yellow inside a
            black edge for At risk and a boxed cross on red for Behind. Section
            numbers sit in 72px black squares. Arrows mark links.
        focus: A 6px black outline with a 12px yellow halo. On the black band a 6px yellow outline.
        tone: Extremely direct uppercase, such as 4 OVERDUE, TASKS DONE, LATEST and ALL PROJECTS with an arrow.

    style23:
        number: 23
        run: 5
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Stationery
        idea: A tidy Japanese paper notebook, with washi and kraft tones, pale ruled lines, a red square seal and stamped circle, triangle and cross status marks in small neat type.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/23.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            desk: #ece3d2, the background behind the notebook
            washiPaper: #fbf8f1, pages, fields and cards
            kraft: #d6bf98, notebook accents
            kraftLight: #ede1c9, the index tabs
            ruleBlue: #cfdae5, the ruled lines and the graph grid
            line: #d8ccb6, row lines, the page edge and the stitch between pages
            sumiInk: #2b2721, text, heading rules and this week's chart cells
            greyInk: #615a50, labels and times, with #8f8676 for last week's cells
            sealRed: #b3262c, the seal, the overdue figure, the Behind stamp and section numbers
            indigo: #2c4a72, links, progress cells and the focus ring
            matcha: #4a6b33, the On track stamp
            amber: #855700, the At risk stamp
        type:
            A sans for text, Hiragino Sans, Hiragino Kaku Gothic ProN, Yu
            Gothic UI, Yu Gothic, Meiryo, Noto Sans CJK JP, system-ui, and a
            Mincho serif for headings and figures, Hiragino Mincho ProN, Yu
            Mincho, Noto Serif CJK JP, Georgia, serif. Body is 13px on a 24px
            line, project names 14px, labels 11px uppercase with 0.2em
            tracking, section titles 17px serif with 0.1em tracking, the
            greeting 26px serif on a 48px line and summary figures 30px serif.
        layout:
            A notebook on a desk. The cover row holds a tilted red square seal
            with B, the brand with a small Project notebook line, a search, a
            square bell and a round red hanko with the initials. Six index tabs
            in kraft and pastel tints hang above the notebook. The notebook is
            a two page spread with a dashed stitch between pages and washi tape
            strips on top. The left page has a boxed date, the greeting, a note
            with the overdue fact highlighted, section 01 This week as a ruled
            form of four figures, and section 02 Tasks completed as a graph
            paper chart. The right page has 03 Projects ledger, a numbered
            table with progress, tasks, due and stamped status, a symbol key,
            and 04 Diary of times and events. Below 980px the pages stack, and
            below 640px each ledger row becomes a three line entry.
        spacing: A strict 24px baseline. Every line, row and gap is 12, 24 or 48px, with 48px page padding.
        density: Medium-high but airy. Small type and a full ledger on one page.
        corners: 2px on buttons and fields, 3px on the seal and stamps, 4px tops on the index tabs.
        borders: 1px hairlines, ink under headings and table heads, beige between rows, a dashed stitch between pages.
        shadows: None. Depth comes from washi tape strips, tabs and the tilted seal.
        icons:
            16px thin square-cap line icons. Status stamps are tilted outlined
            boxes in the status colour with a ring for On track, an open
            triangle for At risk and a cross for Behind, after the Japanese
            circle, triangle and cross marks. Progress is a strip of ten ruled
            cells filled in indigo. The chart stacks one small cell per task.
        focus: A 2px indigo outline offset 2px. A focused field gets a 2px indigo underline and a pale blue fill.
        tone: Calm, tidy and brief, such as Projects ledger, Diary, come first today, and numbered sections 01 to 04.

    style24:
        number: 24
        run: 6
        screen: LandingPage
        name: Art deco
        idea: A gilded 1920s poster, with cream paper, black bands, deep gold sunbursts and stepped fans, and tall condensed capitals set in strict symmetry.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/24.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            cream: #f3ead6, the page
            ivory: #fbf6ea, the hero arch, feature panels, fields and the style sheet
            jet: #15120d, text, the top bar, the quote band, the footer and the primary button
            goldLeaf: #c8a14b, rules, sunburst rays, double frames and the focus halo, never text
            goldInk: #6e5212, gold text on cream such as eyebrows and the accent half of the headline
            goldOnJet: #d9b660, gold text, lines and the primary button label on black
            taupe: #5e5446, body copy, notes and captions
            emerald: #1d5c46, the On track chip with a diamond
            amber: #7a4e00, the At risk chip with a triangle
            oxblood: #8c1c1c, the Overdue chip with a crossed square
        type:
            Two stacks. Display caps use Futura Condensed, Avenir Next
            Condensed, Roboto Condensed, Helvetica Neue Condensed, Arial Narrow,
            sans-serif-condensed with font-stretch condensed, always uppercase
            and tracked 0.12 to 0.28em. Text uses Didot, Bodoni 72, Bodoni MT,
            Big Caslon, Georgia, serif. The headline is 92px bold caps at 0.98
            line height, section titles 44px caps, the quote 44px serif italic,
            feature titles 22px caps, body 17px serif at 1.6, labels and nav
            14px caps.
        layout:
            A black top bar with a fan mark, the spaced caps brand, caps nav
            links and a Start free button, edged by a doubled gold line. The
            hero is centred inside a tall ivory arch with a round top and a
            double gold frame, over gold sunburst rays fanning up from below.
            An eyebrow flanked by short double rules sits above the headline,
            whose second half is gold. Under the arch a black plaque lists three
            projects with due dates and status chips. The logo strip is one
            centred line of caps names split by gold diamonds between double
            rules. Three features are ivory panels with stepped ziggurat tops
            and black roman numeral medallions. The quote is a full black band
            with a gold fan hanging from its top edge. The closing band is a
            double framed ivory box. The footer is black with gold caps
            headings. Below 760px the nav folds into a Menu disclosure and
            panels stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit in big steps of 24, 32, 48 and 96px. Sections have 96px above and below.
        density: Sparse and ceremonial. One idea per band, everything centred on one vertical axis.
        corners: Square. The only curves are the large hero arch and arched swatch tops. Feature panels get stepped corners in 16px steps.
        borders: Double gold hairlines, a 1px line, a 4 to 6px gap, then another line. Black bars carry a doubled gold edge.
        shadows: None. Depth comes from stacked frames and black bands.
        icons:
            Geometric filled shapes in currentColor at text size, such as a
            diamond play mark and a fan logo. Status chips are ivory with a
            filled diamond for On track, a filled triangle for At risk and a
            crossed square for Overdue, always with the caps word.
        focus: A 2px jet outline offset 3px inside a 6px gold halo. On black a 2px gold outline. A focused field gets a gold underline and a cream fill.
        tone: Formal and declarative in spaced capitals, such as What Brightwork does, warmed by italic serif lines.

    style25:
        number: 25
        run: 6
        screen: LandingPage
        name: Memphis
        idea: A 1980s Memphis poster, with squiggles, confetti shapes and clashing pastel and primary blocks thrown into a playful, off-balance layout.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/25.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            paper: #fff8ec, the page and fields
            white: #ffffff, cards and the style sheet
            ink: #121212, text, every 3px outline, stripe and dot patterns
            bubblegum: #ff7eb6, highlight blocks, the quote disc and the Overdue chip
            yolk: #ffd23f, the primary button, highlights and the At risk chip
            mint: #6be3c9, blocks, underline highlights, the focused field offset and the On track chip
            cobalt: #2442d6, squiggles, the closing band with white text and the focus outline
            lilac: #c7b4ff, sticker labels, one feature card and focused rows
            graphite: #4a4a4a, notes and secondary text
        type:
            Futura, Century Gothic, Avenir Next, Trebuchet MS, Gill Sans, URW
            Gothic, sans-serif. The headline is 96px extra bold at 0.95 line
            height with minus 0.04em tracking, section titles 60px extra bold,
            the quote 54px extra bold, feature titles 24px, the lede 20px, body
            17px at 1.55 and chips 13px extra bold.
        layout:
            A light top bar with a brand mark of a pink square, a yellow circle
            and a blue squiggle, plain nav links that turn into outlined mint
            blocks on hover, and a yellow Start free button. The hero is split
            unevenly. The left holds a tilted lilac sticker saying Hey, small
            teams, a headline with on one in a tilted pink block and calm page
            underlined by a blue squiggle, an indented lede with a thick cobalt
            left bar, and the buttons. The right is a pile of shapes, a yellow
            dotted disc, a striped mint square and a cobalt triangle, with a
            tilted white card listing three projects on top. Confetti such as
            rings, zigzags and crosses floats around. The logo strip is a black
            band with zigzag edges and names in differently shaped and tilted
            colour chips. Three feature cards are staggered at different
            heights, each a different colour with one big rounded corner. The
            quote sits beside a large pink disc with a cobalt square. The
            closing band is cobalt with a yellow circle and yellow squiggle.
            The footer has a dot grid and shaped colour headings. Below 980px
            everything stacks, and below 640px the nav wraps under the brand.
        spacing: An 8px unit but placement is uneven on purpose, with 48px indents and card offsets of 24 and 72px.
        density: Loose and busy at once. Few words, many shapes in the margins.
        corners: Mixed on purpose. Square blocks, full circles, and single 26 to 64px rounded corners on one side only.
        borders: 3px solid ink on every block, 2px dashed ink between list rows, zigzag edges on the logo band.
        shadows: No blur. Each block sits on an offset patterned twin of diagonal stripes, a dot grid or a solid colour, 14 to 17px down and right.
        icons:
            Large 64px filled geometric glyphs with 3px ink outlines, such as a
            target, a ticked square and a triangle with bars. Status chips use a
            filled circle for On track on a round mint chip, a triangle for At
            risk on a square yellow chip and a cross for Overdue on a pink chip
            with two rounded corners, each with the word.
        focus: A 3px dashed cobalt outline offset 4px, yellow on cobalt. A focused field also gets a solid mint offset block.
        tone: Cheerful and chatty, such as Hey, small teams and Three things it does really well.

    style26:
        number: 26
        run: 6
        screen: LandingPage
        name: Y2K bubble
        idea: Late-90s web optimism, with bubbly chrome-silver capsules, glossy pill buttons, iridescent pastel edges and little star sparkles.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/26.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            haze: #eef0ff, the page base under faint pink, blue and mint glows
            midnight: #1c1b4d, text and headings
            dusk: #4a4880, secondary text and notes
            gelBlue: #3a5ff0 to #1b34a8, the glossy primary pill and the window title strip
            linkBlue: #2b45d4, links
            chrome: #ffffff, #c9cfe0 and #8f97b3, the top bar, capsules and secondary pills as a banded silver gradient
            iris: #ffd6f5, #d6e9ff, #d9ffef and #fff1c9, card rings and the quote bubble
            magenta: #b0207a, small headings and the focus glow, with #e0389b for sparkles
            jade: #0f6b45, the On track gem
            amber: #8a4b00, the At risk gem
            cherry: #b3123a, the Overdue gem
        type:
            Headings and labels use Arial Rounded MT Bold, Trebuchet MS,
            Verdana, Tahoma, sans-serif in bold. Body uses Verdana, Tahoma,
            Lucida Grande, sans-serif. The headline is 76px at 1.02 line height
            with minus 0.03em tracking, a white emboss shadow, and its second
            half in a dark violet to blue to plum gradient. Section titles are
            46px, the quote 36px, feature titles 21px, the lede 18px, body 15px
            at 1.65 and chips 12px.
        layout:
            A floating chrome capsule top bar with a glass orb logo, a sunken
            segmented control for the nav and a glossy blue Start free pill.
            The hero is split, with an iridescent badge, the headline, lede,
            buttons and note on the left, and on the right a chrome device
            bezel holding a white window with a glossy blue title strip and
            three project rows with status gems. Star sparkles float nearby.
            The logo strip is a centred row of soft glossy capsules. Three
            feature cards have iridescent gradient rings, a white gloss strip
            and a glossy colour sphere icon. The quote is an iridescent speech
            bubble with a tail pointing down at an orb avatar. The closing band
            is a huge chrome capsule with the line and a pill. The footer is a
            pale silver gradient. Below 960px the hero stacks, and below 720px
            the nav drops to a full width second row inside the capsule.
        spacing: An 8px unit with 24 to 28px gaps and roomy 72 to 96px section padding.
        density: Airy and toy-like. Short lines, big rounded shapes, one idea per capsule.
        corners: Everything bubbly. Pills at 999px, cards 36px, the device bezel 40px, the quote bubble 48px.
        borders: 1px silver #8f97b3 around chrome, 3px iridescent gradient rings around cards, 1px white highlights on top edges.
        shadows: Soft drops of 0 16px 40px rgba(28,27,77,0.12), inner shading at the bottom, and a white gloss strip over the top half of every pill and card.
        icons:
            Thick round 2.4 stroke white glyphs inside glossy 84px spheres with
            a light spot. Status gems sit in white pills, a round tick for On
            track, a diamond with an exclamation mark for At risk and a rounded
            square with a cross for Overdue, beside the word.
        focus: A white 3px ring, then a 3px magenta ring and a soft magenta glow.
        tone: Upbeat and bouncy, such as Everything bubbles up to one page and My projects.

    style27:
        number: 27
        run: 6
        screen: LandingPage
        name: Aurora gradient
        idea: A modern startup page, with soft aurora mesh glows on white, a huge tightly tracked headline, a floating glassy pill nav and a generous centred hero.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/27.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            white: #ffffff, the page, windows and fields
            mist: #f6f6fa, table heads and the style sheet
            ink: #0b0d17, headlines, text and the primary pill
            slate: #545a6e, body copy, labels and nav links
            hairline: #e7e8ef, borders, dividers and progress tracks
            violet: #5a3ee0, the focus ring and the start of gradient text
            aurora: #b8a6ff, #8de3d6, #ffc7a8 and #ffb3d9, blurred glows and icon rings, never behind small text
            green: #157347, the On track pill
            amber: #8a5300, the At risk pill
            red: #b42318, the Overdue pill
        type:
            System sans, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica
            Neue, Arial, sans-serif, with small labels in ui-monospace, SF Mono,
            Menlo, Consolas, monospace. The headline is 104px bold at 0.98 line
            height with minus 0.055em tracking. Section titles are 52px bold,
            the quote 48px semibold with its second half in a violet to teal
            gradient, feature titles 19px, body 16px at 1.6, and eyebrows 12px
            mono uppercase tracked 0.08em.
        layout:
            A sticky glassy pill nav floats centred at the top with a gradient
            ring logo, quiet links and a small black Start free pill. Four large
            blurred aurora blobs in violet, mint, peach and pink glow behind the
            hero and fade to white. The hero is centred, with a small New chip,
            the huge headline, the lede, a black pill with an arrow and the tour
            link with a ringed play button. Below it a glass framed product
            window shows a projects table with progress bars, avatars, due dates
            and status pills. The logo strip is a row of grey wordmarks with
            small glyphs. Three features sit in columns split by hairlines with
            gradient ringed icon tiles and no cards. The quote is big and
            centred. The closing band is a 32px rounded panel filled with a
            soft aurora wash. The footer is minimal with mono headings. Below
            900px the nav links move into a centred row under the bar and
            columns stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit with big jumps, 72 to 112px between sections and 28 to 36px around the headline.
        density: Very airy. One centred column for the hero, text capped at 520 to 640px.
        corners: Pills for nav and buttons, 32px on the closing panel, 22px outer and 14px inner on the product window, 12px on fields and icon tiles.
        borders: 1px #e7e8ef hairlines, 1px white edges on glass, 1.5px aurora gradient rings on icon tiles.
        shadows: Long soft violet tinted drops, 0 40px 80px minus 30px rgba(43,22,140,0.35) under the window, and a small violet glow under the primary pill. Glass is 55 to 62 percent white with a 10 to 16px backdrop blur.
        icons:
            20px thin 1.6 stroke line icons in white tiles with a gradient
            ring. Status is a white pill with a ringed tick for On track, an
            outlined triangle with an exclamation mark for At risk and a filled
            square with a cross for Overdue, plus the word.
        focus: A 2px violet outline offset 3px. A focused field gets a violet border and a 4px soft violet ring.
        tone: Crisp and confident with short punchy lines, such as Less tracking. More finished work.

    style28:
        number: 28
        run: 6
        screen: LandingPage
        name: Tropical resort
        idea: A sunny resort brochure, with palm-leaf silhouettes, turquoise sea and coral sand tones, wavy edges, a postcard and relaxed rounded type.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/28.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            sand: #fbf1df, the page and control panels
            shell: #fffaf1, cards, the postcard, the quote band and fields
            lagoon: #bfe9e4, the hero horizon, the logo band and the menu button
            sea: #0a7f86, links, accent words and the focused field border
            deepWater: #064e57, text, headings and the footer
            coral: #c94a2f, the primary button and the focus outline, with #a8391f for small eyebrow text
            coralSand: #ffd9cc, the Overdue chip and the flower disc, with #ffe1c2 for the closing band
            sun: #ffc857, sun discs and footer headings on deep water, never text on light
            palm: #1e5a3c, leaf silhouettes and the On track chip text
            driftwood: #5c5246, body copy, notes and tag strings
            mango: #7a5600, At risk text on #fdecc2
            rust: #9a3b22, Overdue text
        type:
            A rounded stack, ui-rounded, SF Pro Rounded, Nunito, Varela Round,
            Quicksand, Arial Rounded MT Bold, Trebuchet MS, system-ui,
            sans-serif. The headline is 80px extra bold at 1.06 line height
            with its second half in sea. Section titles are 50px, the quote
            42px, feature titles 23px, all extra bold. The lede is 20px, body
            17px at 1.65 and chips 14px extra bold.
        layout:
            A top bar over the hero with a sun and waves mark, rounded nav links
            and a coral Start free button. The hero is a sand to lagoon sky
            gradient with a soft sun disc and faint palm leaves at the corners.
            The left holds a small shell pill with a sun icon, the headline,
            the lede, the buttons and the note with a wave icon. The right holds
            a slightly tilted postcard with a dashed inner border, a stamp of an
            island and the title Greetings from this week listing three projects
            and status chips. A wavy edge leads into a lagoon band where the
            logo names hang as luggage tags from a line. Three features are
            shell cards with tall arched tops holding small beach scene
            pictures. The quote sits on shell beside a coral flower disc with a
            pale palm leaf. The closing band is a peach sunset with a wavy top
            and a half sun. The footer is deep water with sun yellow headings.
            Below 960px the hero stacks, and below 760px the nav becomes a Menu
            disclosure.
        spacing: An 8px unit, 96px sections, 32px between cards and 56px between hero columns.
        density: Relaxed brochure pace. Large type, short lines, plenty of sky.
        corners: Soft everywhere. Arched card tops of 160px, 20 to 28px card corners, 18px fields, and a leaf shaped button rounded 26px except one 8px corner.
        borders: Almost none. A 2px dashed inner line on the postcard, 2px sand rules between rows and a dotted stamp edge.
        shadows: Warm teal drops of 0 24px 40px minus 28px rgba(6,78,87,0.5), and a solid darker coral lip under the primary button.
        icons:
            Small filled scene illustrations in palette colours inside the
            arched feature pictures, such as a window, a flag with a tick and a
            sun chart. Status chips are soft tinted pills with a filled circle
            tick for On track, a filled triangle with an exclamation mark for
            At risk and a rounded square with a cross for Overdue, beside the
            word.
        focus: A 3px coral outline offset 3px, sun yellow on deep water. A focused field adds a sea border and a soft sea glow.
        tone: Warm, unhurried holiday language, such as Greetings from this week and Everything your team needs to unwind.

    style29:
        number: 29
        run: 7
        screen: SignIn
        name: Pixel 8-bit
        idea: A light 8-bit title screen where every box is drawn in 4px pixel steps, the type is chunky monospace caps, and signing in feels like pressing start.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/29.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            sky: #cfe8ff, the page background
            panel: #fffdf5, the menu panel and the style sheet
            cloud: #ffffff, fields, secondary buttons and the pixel clouds
            ink: #1a1c2c, text, every pixel outline and the 1P tag
            dim: #4a4e69, the Player 1 line and secondary text
            startRed: #b4202a, the primary button and the error text and badge
            linkBlue: #29539b, links with a 4px underline bar
            coin: #ffcd75, the hard shadow under the brand, the Show key and the focus bar
            grass: #38b764, the decorative ground strip
            soil: #8a5a2b, the decorative brick ground with #9c6a37 bricks
        type:
            Courier New, Courier, ui-monospace, DejaVu Sans Mono, Menlo,
            Consolas, monospace, always bold. The brand is 40px weight 900
            uppercase with 0.06em tracking and a hard 4px coin shadow. The
            heading is 20px uppercase. Buttons are 15px uppercase with 0.06em
            tracking. Field text is 16px, body and errors 14px, and labels 12
            to 13px uppercase with 0.1em tracking.
        layout:
            A centred title screen on a pale sky. Two pixel clouds float at the
            top corners, then a pixel sun logo beside the brand and the line
            Player 1 · ready. A single panel 440px wide holds a 1P tag with the
            heading, two full width sign-in buttons, a dashed or divider, the
            fields, the checkbox row, the red start button with a play arrow and
            the create account line. Privacy and Terms sit below the panel, and
            a grass and brick ground strip runs along the bottom. At 375px the
            clouds hide and the panel fills the width.
        spacing: A 4px pixel grid. 16 to 20px between controls and 28px panel padding.
        density: Low. One panel, big targets and lots of sky.
        corners: Notched pixel corners from four flat 4px box-shadows with no blur, so each box loses one pixel at every corner.
        borders: 4px ink pixel outlines on every box. Buttons add a 4px inner bevel, lighter top left and darker bottom right. Dividers are 8px ink dashes 4px thick.
        shadows: No soft shadows. Only the hard 4px coin shadow under the brand.
        icons:
            Pixel art drawn in SVG with crisp edges. A pixel sun logo, square
            letter keys G and M on the sign-in buttons, a square badge with an
            exclamation mark on the error, an X in the square checkbox, and a
            play arrow on the start button and on a focused list row.
        focus: A 4px dashed ink outline offset 8px. Buttons and rows also get a 4px coin bar along the bottom, and a focused field gets an 8px coin halo outside its pixel outline.
        tone: Game menu words, short and upbeat, such as Player 1 · ready and a 1P tag. Labels and buttons are uppercase.

    style30:
        number: 30
        run: 7
        screen: SignIn
        name: Leather skeuomorphic
        idea: A 2010-era desk object, a stitched tan leather folio holding a cream ruled paper card, with embossed labels and glossy buttons you want to press.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/30.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            desk: #e9dfcc, the page behind the folio with a fine noise grain
            tanLeather: #c99c6b, the folio cover and the section tabs, with grain
            deepLeather: #a97a4b, the debossed badge and the leather paper corners
            stitch: #f6e7c8, dashed stitching
            creamPaper: #fbf6ea, the card and the style sheet
            ruledLine: #e7dcc4, ruled paper lines and dividers
            ink: #2f2216, text and headings
            embossedBrown: #3b2615, the brand and any text on leather
            muted: #6b5640, the or divider and meta text
            feltGreen: #2f6b3a, the glossy primary button and the checkbox tick
            waxRed: #a3271c, error text and the error field border
            focusBlue: #3d7bc4, the focus glow
            link: #6a3e17, underlined links
        type:
            Georgia, Times New Roman, serif for the brand, headings and asides,
            and Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, system-ui, sans-serif for
            controls. The brand is 34px bold italic serif, the heading 26px
            bold serif, buttons 15 to 16px bold sans, body 15px at 1.5, the
            create account line 16px italic serif, and labels 12px bold
            uppercase sans with 0.06em tracking. All text carries a 1px white
            or cream emboss shadow below.
        layout:
            A leather folio 920px wide on a desk. The left flap, 300px wide,
            holds a round debossed badge with a sun icon, the brand, a one
            line motto and a stitched strap with a brass stud at the bottom.
            The right side is a cream ruled paper card with a pink margin rule,
            held by two stitched leather corners at the top, carrying the form.
            Privacy and Terms sit below the folio. Below 760px the flap becomes
            a short header row with the badge and brand, and the paper fills
            the width.
        spacing: An 8px base on a 28px ruled paper rhythm. 12px between sign-in buttons, 18px between fields and 36 to 40px paper padding.
        density: Medium. Two panels with comfortable controls.
        corners: 14px on the folio, 8px on buttons, 6px on fields and notes, 4px on the paper.
        borders: Dashed 2px cream stitching inset 8px on all leather. 1px tan borders on buttons and wells. A pink margin rule on the paper.
        shadows:
            Lit from above. Inset shadows on fields and the badge, a soft drop
            under the folio and paper, 1px white highlights on top edges, and
            glossy buttons split by a hard highlight at the half line.
        icons:
            A line sun debossed into the leather badge, round letter coins G
            and M on sign-in buttons, a filled triangle with an exclamation
            mark in a pale red note for the error, and a tick in the checkbox.
        focus: A 2px white gap then a 3px blue glow ring around buttons and rows. A focused field gets a blue border and a soft 3px blue glow.
        tone: Warm and personal, a little old-fashioned, such as Projects for small teams, kept in one well-worn folio.

    style31:
        number: 31
        run: 7
        screen: SignIn
        name: Glossy aqua
        idea: An early-2000s desktop window, brushed metal chrome on a pinstripe backdrop, with blue jelly buttons that look wet enough to press.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/31.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            pinstripe: #f7f7f7 and #ececec, the page in alternating 2px stripes
            brushedMetal: #e9ebee to #c9ccd1, the title bar and toolbar with fine vertical streaks
            window: #f4f5f7, the window body
            text: #1d1d1f, body text
            muted: #4f545c, sub lines and the status bar
            bevelLine: #a7acb4, group borders and section tabs
            jellyBlue: #2a6bc2, the primary gel button and the selected row
            jellyDeep: #0e4a9c, the lower half of the gel
            jellyGlow: #8cc0f4, the inner glow at the bottom of the gel
            focusRing: #6fa8eb, the focus halo
            link: #0b4fae, links
            error: #b3141b, error text and the error field border
            done: #23733a, On track text
        type:
            Lucida Grande, Lucida Sans Unicode, Lucida Sans, Helvetica Neue,
            Verdana, Tahoma, system-ui, sans-serif. The brand is 22px bold with
            a white emboss, the heading 17px bold, labels 13px bold and right
            aligned with a trailing colon, field text 14px, body 13px at 1.45,
            and the status bar 11px.
        layout:
            A single desktop window 640px wide floating on the pinstripe. A
            brushed metal title bar with one grey glossy orb at the left and
            the word Brightwork centred. A toolbar band with a glossy blue app
            orb holding a tick, the brand and a sub line. The body has the
            heading, two pill sign-in buttons side by side, an etched or
            divider, then a sunken group box with a two column form of right
            aligned labels and fields. The bottom of the group holds the create
            account line on the left and the jelly Sign in button on the right.
            A status bar closes the window with Privacy and Terms. At 375px the
            pills and labels stack and Sign in goes full width.
        spacing: Tight, a 4px base. 12px between form rows and 24 to 28px window padding.
        density: Compact desktop density, 13px type and 30px controls.
        corners: Fully round pill buttons, 10px top window corners, 6px group boxes and 4px fields.
        borders: 1px grey bevels, darker on top for sunken fields. Dividers are a grey line over a white line.
        shadows:
            A deep soft window shadow, inset field shadows, and gel buttons
            with a white reflection over the top half and a light blue inner
            glow at the bottom.
        icons:
            Glossy orbs and gel balls with a white reflection. Grey letter
            orbs G and M on sign-in buttons, a red octagon with a cross for the
            error, a tick inside the app orb, and a small triangle on the
            selected list row.
        focus: A 1px blue line and a 3px light blue halo around any control. A focused field gets a blue border and the same halo.
        tone: Plain desktop dialog words with a colon after each label, such as Email and Password followed by a colon.

    style32:
        number: 32
        run: 7
        screen: SignIn
        name: Zen ink
        idea: Japanese ink-brush calm, one sumi stroke and one red sun above a narrow column of hairline fields, with the brand written vertically down the edge and space doing most of the work.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/32.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            ricePaper: #fbfaf6, the page
            sumi: #1c1b19, text, the brush stroke, field lines and the primary button
            wash: #5e5b55, labels, small text and the or divider
            mist: #d9d6ce, resting hairlines between rows
            pale: #efede6, the half height wash behind a focused field
            sun: #c0392b, the single red dot, used nowhere else
        type:
            A Mincho serif for almost everything, Hiragino Mincho ProN, Yu
            Mincho, Noto Serif CJK JP, Songti SC, Georgia, Times New Roman,
            serif, and a Gothic sans for tiny labels, Hiragino Sans, Yu Gothic
            UI, Segoe UI, system-ui, sans-serif. The vertical brand is 26px with
            0.5em tracking, the heading 24px light with 0.08em tracking, field
            text 17px, body 15px weight 300 on a 1.9 line, labels 12px sans
            with 0.3em tracking, and the button 15px with 0.5em tracking.
        layout:
            A wide sheet of rice paper. One rough sumi brush stroke sweeps
            across the top left, and a red dot 44px wide sits alone near the
            top right. The brand runs vertically down the right edge with a
            small for small teams line beside it. The form is a narrow 340px
            column left of centre that starts about 220px down, under a short
            ink dash below the heading. Sign-in choices are hairline rows with
            ringed initials and an arrow. Privacy and Terms sit far below in
            tiny tracked sans. At 375px the stroke runs off the left edge, the
            vertical brand stays in a narrow strip on the right and the column
            fills the rest.
        spacing: An 8px unit used in large steps. 32px between fields, 48px between groups, 96px above the screen and about 220px of empty paper above the heading.
        density: Very sparse. A 340px column on a 1200px page.
        corners: Square buttons and fields. Only the sun, the round checkbox and the ringed initials are round.
        borders: 1px hairlines under fields and rows only. A dashed underline marks the field in error.
        shadows: None. Depth comes from the brush stroke alone.
        icons:
            Almost none. A hand drawn SVG brush stroke roughened with a
            turbulence filter, ringed letters G and M, a thin arrow on
            sign-in rows, a cross before the error, a filled dot in the
            round checkbox and a tick for done.
        focus: A 1px sumi outline offset 6px. A focused field gets a 3px sumi underline and a pale wash over its lower half.
        tone: Very few words, calm and unhurried. Labels whisper in widely tracked small type.

    style33:
        number: 33
        run: 7
        screen: SignIn
        name: Origami
        idea: The sign-in form is one sheet of paper folded into three panels, with crisp creases, a dog-eared corner and light triangular facets on every surface.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/33.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #f3efe8, the background behind the sheet with large faint facet triangles
            sheet: #fffdf9, the lit side of the paper
            facetLight: #f8f4ee, the second half of every facet
            facetMid: #ece5da, the middle panel turned away from the light
            facetShade: #ddd3c3, the dog-ear and the icon triangles
            crease: #cfc3b0, fold lines between panels
            edge: #8a7d68, field and button edges
            ink: #2a2620, text
            muted: #5f574b, labels, the brand line and the divider
            tealFold: #2b7479 with #1f5f63, the two tone primary button, links and the checked box
            coral: #b5462c, the focus outline
            error: #a63a22, error text and the error field edge
            done: #2d6b3c, On track text
        type:
            Avenir Next, Avenir, Century Gothic, Futura, Segoe UI, system-ui,
            sans-serif. The heading is 26px weight 500, the brand 13px weight
            600 uppercase with 0.32em tracking, the primary button 16px weight
            600, field text 16px, body 15px at 1.55, and labels 12px weight
            600 uppercase with 0.14em tracking.
        layout:
            A centred sheet 460px wide on a page of pale facet triangles, with
            a small folded paper crane of light triangles above it. The sheet
            is split into three stacked panels like a tri-fold. The top panel
            is the brightest and holds the brand, heading, sign-in buttons and
            the or divider. The middle panel is shaded as if turned away and
            holds the fields, checkbox row and Sign in. The bottom panel holds
            the create account line. Two faint diagonal creases cross the whole
            sheet and the top right corner is dog-eared. Privacy and Terms sit
            below. At 375px the sheet fills the width.
        spacing: An 8px base. 28px by 32px panel padding, 12px between sign-in buttons and 18px between fields.
        density: Medium. One sheet in three panels.
        corners: No rounding. Corners are cut on the diagonal instead, a 44px dog-ear on the sheet, 14px cuts on the primary button and small folded corners on secondary buttons.
        borders: 1px crease lines with a white highlight below, 1px edge on fields and buttons. An error field gets a 3px bottom edge.
        shadows: A tight 1px drop and a soft 14px drop under the whole sheet. Facets are hard half and half diagonal splits, never blurred.
        icons:
            Everything is a triangle. A folded crane above the sheet, triangle
            tabs holding the letters G and M, a two tone triangle with an
            exclamation mark for the error, a small triangle on the primary
            button and a tick in the checked box.
        focus: A 3px coral outline offset 3px on every control. A focused field also darkens its edge to ink.
        tone: Neat, quiet and precise, with short plain words.

    style34:
        number: 34
        run: 8
        screen: TaskBoard
        name: Sketch wireframe
        idea: The app drawn as a pencil wireframe on dotted paper, wobbly hand-drawn boxes in greyscale with one blue pen for the things that need attention.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/34.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            paper: #fdfdfb, the page with a 24px dot grid in #d9d9d6
            sheet: #ffffff, boxes, cards and fields
            tray: #f3f3f1, the column fill
            pencil: #222222, text and every outline
            graphite: #595959, meta text and field labels
            smudge: #e4e4e4, hatching on Engineering labels and Done cards
            bluePen: #1a4fd6, the Add task button, the Overdue mark, the title underline and focus
            penWash: #e3ebff, hover, the focused row and the offset behind the primary button
        type:
            One handwriting stack for everything, Segoe Print, Bradley Hand,
            Marker Felt, Chalkboard SE, Comic Sans MS, cursive. The project
            title is 34px bold, column titles 20px bold, card titles 17px bold,
            body 15px at 1.5 line height, meta 13px in graphite and field
            labels 13px. Code notes in the style sheet use a monospace stack.
        layout:
            The whole screen sits inside a sketched browser frame with three
            circles and a fake address bar. Inside, a crossed placeholder box
            and Brightwork sit on the left with Mara Okafor and a circled MO on
            the right. The title Mobile app 2.0 has a boxed At risk tag and a
            wavy blue pen underline. A row of labelled sketched dropdowns for
            Assignee, Label and Due, a Search tasks box and the Add task button
            on the right. Four dashed column trays hold wobbly white cards,
            each with the title, a label chip, the due date with a clock, a
            dashed divider and then a circled initial avatar with the name and
            points. Below 1040px the board has two columns, and below 640px one,
            with the controls stacking full width.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px between cards, 24px between columns, 24px screen padding.
        density: Medium. The whole board fits one laptop screen.
        corners:
            No straight edges. Boxes use asymmetric elliptical radii such as
            255px 15px 225px 15px over 15px 225px 15px 255px, with two other
            variants alternated between cards. Avatars and count circles are
            slightly lopsided circles.
        borders:
            2px pencil outlines on cards, fields and buttons, plus a faint
            second stroke at 45 percent opacity slightly offset and roughened
            with an SVG turbulence filter. Columns use a 2px dashed outline.
            Card footers have a dashed divider.
        shadows: None, except the primary button which has a blue pen offset outline 3px right and 4px down.
        icons:
            Hand-drawn line icons with a 2px round stroke at text size,
            slightly uneven paths. Overdue is a triangle with an exclamation
            mark plus the word Overdue, circled by a blue pen loop. Done is a
            tick plus the word Done, with the title struck through and the card
            hatched. Unassigned is a dashed circle with a question mark. The
            logo is a crossed placeholder box.
        focus: A 2.5px dashed blue pen outline offset 4px. A focused field turns its outline blue and gets a pale blue offset block.
        tone: Plain sketch notes in sentence case, such as Add task, type to search, 5 pts.

    style35:
        number: 35
        run: 8
        screen: TaskBoard
        name: Scrapbook collage
        idea: The board as a scrapbook spread, with torn paper scraps, washi tape, label-maker strips and rubber stamps pasted onto a kraft board.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/35.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            board: #d9c4a0, the page with faint fibre stripes
            kraft: #c9a877, the To do scrap
            cream: #fffcf2, lined paper, notes and the style sheet
            tissuePink: #f7d9dc, the In progress scrap and one cut title letter block
            graph: #f4f9f1, the Review scrap with a #cfe3c8 16px grid
            newsprint: #ece8de, the Done scrap
            sticky: #fbeea0, sticky note cards
            manila: #f2e0ad, the filter tags
            ink: #2a211a, text and count chips
            pencil: #5a4a3b, small caps labels
            labelTape: #1c1c1c, the brand strip and the Add task button, with white text
            stampRed: #b3261e, the At risk and Overdue stamps
            stampGreen: #2d6a2d, the Done stamp
            navy: #1f3a6b, focus
            tape: #faf4d6, washi tape strips at 72 percent opacity
        type:
            Georgia, Times New Roman, serif bold for headings and card titles,
            and Courier New, Courier, American Typewriter, monospace for body
            and labels. The title is cut letters at 34 to 40px, one word each in
            serif, typewriter and serif italic. Column titles are 22px serif
            bold, card titles 17px serif bold, body 14px typewriter, field
            labels 11 to 12px uppercase with 0.08em tracking. The brand is 16px
            bold uppercase typewriter with 0.18em tracking.
        layout:
            A brand label-maker strip top left, tilted, and a small white
            polaroid tag with MO and Mara Okafor top right. The title Mobile app
            2.0 is three cut paper blocks beside a tilted red At risk stamp.
            Filters are manila luggage tags with a punched hole, a lined paper
            search strip with a red margin, and the black Add task strip at the
            right. Four torn-edged scraps of different paper hold the columns,
            each tilted under a degree with washi tape on top. Cards are index
            cards, sticky notes, receipts with zigzag bottoms and torn notes,
            each tilted about 1.3 degrees, with a dashed round points sticker
            and a two column list of Label, Who and Due. Below 1040px two
            columns, below 640px one.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between notes, 24px between scraps, 24px padding inside scraps.
        density: Loose. Paper needs room to tilt and overlap.
        corners:
            Square paper with torn, zigzag or receipt edges cut by clip-path.
            The filter tags have a pointed left end. Only the points sticker
            and the Done stamp are round.
        borders: None on paper. Stamps have 3px outlines in their ink. Fields use a 2px dashed underline.
        shadows: Paste shadows, a drop-shadow of 1px 2px 1.5px in rgba of 40,25,5 at 0.35, with scraps tilted between minus 1.4 and 1.2 degrees.
        icons:
            Bold 2.2 stroke line icons at text size, mostly inside stamps.
            Overdue and At risk are a triangle in a red rectangular stamp. Done
            is a tick in a green oval stamp. Comments use a speech box.
        focus: A 3px navy outline offset 3px. A focused field gets a solid navy underline and a pale blue fill.
        tone: Crafty and short, with typewriter labels such as Who, Due and Notes.

    style36:
        number: 36
        run: 8
        screen: TaskBoard
        name: Metro tiles
        idea: Flat solid colour tiles packed edge to edge with hairline white gaps, where big thin lowercase type does all the work and nothing has a border or a shadow.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/36.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #ffffff, the page and the 4px gaps between tiles
            night: #1a1a1a, text, the add task button and the overdue tile
            field: #ececec, the search field fill and the secondary button
            muted: #5c5c5c, small labels on white
            teal: #005f73, the to do head tile, with #0a6e84 card tiles
            cobalt: #1e4fb4, the in progress head tile, with #2a5cc2 card tiles, and field focus
            plum: #7b2d8e, the review head tile, with #8a3a9e card tiles, and the avatar
            leaf: #2f6b1e, the done head tile, with #3a7a28 card tiles
            ember: #a33a00, the at risk tile
            sun: #ffd23f, the overdue word and date on the night tile
        type:
            Segoe UI Light, Segoe UI, Helvetica Neue, Noto Sans, Open Sans,
            Arial, sans-serif. The project title is 64px weight 200, column
            counts 72px weight 100, column names 28px weight 200, tile titles
            22px weight 300, points 40px weight 100, facts 14px weight 400 and
            field labels 13px weight 400. Everything is lowercase except
            people's names.
        layout:
            A white top area with brightwork lowercase on the left and Mara
            Okafor with a square plum MO tile on the right. Below it the huge
            thin title mobile app 2.0 beside a solid ember at risk tile. A
            pivot row of filters reads assignee, label and due as small labels
            over big thin dropdown text, then the search tasks field and a black
            add task tile on the right. The board runs edge to edge across the
            full viewport in four columns with 4px white gaps. Each column has a
            darker head tile with the name top left and a huge count bottom
            right, then one solid tile per task with the title, big points top
            right and one fact line at the bottom with the hash label, the
            assignee and a calendar date. Below 1040px two columns, below 640px
            one, with the head tile in a single row.
        spacing: 4px gaps between tiles, 16px by 20px tile padding, a 32px page gutter above the board and none beside it.
        density: Sparse type in big blocks. One fact line per tile, tiles at least 168px tall.
        corners: 0 everywhere.
        borders: None. Fields carry a 3px inset bottom bar in night so they still read as fields.
        shadows: None. Depth comes only from a darker head tile above lighter task tiles.
        icons:
            Square-cap 1.5 stroke glyphs at text size, white on tiles and
            never boxed. The overdue tile turns night with a triangle and the
            word overdue in sun. Done tiles show a tick and the word done.
        focus: On tiles a 3px white outline inset 9px. On white a 3px night outline offset 2px. A focused field turns white with a 3px cobalt inset ring.
        tone: Lowercase and terse, such as add task, at risk, no due date, while people keep their capitals.

    style37:
        number: 37
        run: 8
        screen: TaskBoard
        name: Claymorphism
        idea: Everything is a puffy piece of soft candy clay, pressed out of a lilac surface with fat rounded corners, an inner highlight and a soft coloured drop shadow.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/37.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            lilacPage: #f3eefc, the page with soft pink and sky glows in two corners
            cloud: #fbf9ff, the top bar, the hero, fields, counts and points chips
            tray: #ebe3fb, the pressed-in column trays
            sky: #cfe6ff, Engineering cards
            peach: #ffdcc9, Design cards
            mint: #c9f2df, Done cards
            lemon: #fff1b8, the At risk pill with #6e4a00 text
            ink: #2b2340, text
            muted: #5e5675, field labels and the eyebrow
            grape: #6a3fd1, the primary button gradient and focus
            cherry: #b4233c, the Overdue pill text on #ffd9de and the dashed overdue ring
            forest: #1e6b45, the Done pill text on white
        type:
            ui-rounded, SF Pro Rounded, Nunito, Varela Round, Quicksand, Arial
            Rounded MT Bold, system-ui, sans-serif. The title is 40px weight
            900 with tight tracking, column titles 19px weight 900, card titles
            17px weight 800, body 15px weight 500, meta 13px weight 700, label
            chips 12px weight 800 uppercase and pills 14px weight 800.
        layout:
            A floating pill top bar with a glossy grape B ball, Brightwork, and
            Mara Okafor with a peach clay avatar ball. Then a big clay hero
            panel with a small Task board eyebrow, the title Mobile app 2.0 and
            the At risk pill, and the grape Add task button on the right. A row
            of pressed-in pill fields for Assignee, Label, Due and Search tasks.
            Four pressed-in trays each start with a round count bubble and the
            column name, then puffy candy cards coloured by label. Each card has
            a label chip and a points chip on top, the title, the due date with
            a calendar and an avatar ball with the name. Below 1080px two
            columns, below 640px one, with the hero stacking and the button full
            width.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 20px between cards, 28px between trays, 18px card padding, 24 to 40px between sections.
        density: Low. Big soft shapes with lots of air.
        corners: 36px trays, 32px panels, 28px cards, and fully round buttons, fields, chips, counts and avatars.
        borders: None on clay. Fields get a 1.5px #c9bdea ring so they read as wells.
        shadows:
            Raised clay has an outer shadow of 10px 12px 24px in grape at 18
            percent, a dark inner shadow bottom right at 8 percent and a white
            inner highlight top left. Trays and fields are pressed in, with only
            the inner shadows, reversed. The primary button has a deeper grape
            glow.
        icons:
            Chunky filled rounded glyphs at text size. Overdue is a filled
            triangle with the word Overdue in a cherry pill, and the card gets a
            3px dashed cherry ring. Done is a filled circle tick with the word
            Done. No due date is a circle with a dash. Avatars are glossy clay
            balls with initials.
        focus: A 4px grape outline at 55 percent offset 4px. A focused field gets a 3px grape ring and a soft 4px halo outside it.
        tone: Warm and plain sentence case, such as Find a task, Add task, 5 pt.

    style38:
        number: 38
        run: 8
        screen: TaskBoard
        name: Comic book
        idea: The board as a comic page, with inked panels on white gutters, halftone dot skies, task cards spoken in speech bubbles and a starburst that shouts what is overdue.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/38.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            paper: #fffdf5, the page and gutters
            ink: #111111, outlines, text and points chips
            yellow: #ffd60a, the logo panel, title fill and burst fill
            caption: #ffe98a, caption boxes and column titles
            red: #d1221d, the Add task button, the At risk banner and the overdue bubble outline
            blue: #1858c4, focus and sound effects
            yellowDots: #fff6c2, the To do panel with #f2c94c dots
            roseDots: #ffe4e1, the In progress panel with #f4a8a0 dots
            skyDots: #e6f0ff, the Review panel and the filter panel with #a9c8f5 dots
            mintDots: #e3f6e3, the Done panel with #9fd59f dots
            grey: #4a4a4a, placeholders and small notes
        type:
            Headings in Impact, Haettenschweiler, Arial Narrow Bold, Franklin
            Gothic Bold, Arial Black, sans-serif, always uppercase. Lettering
            in Comic Sans MS, Comic Neue, Chalkboard SE, Trebuchet MS,
            sans-serif. The title is 64px Impact in yellow with a 3px ink
            stroke and a 4px solid ink drop. Column titles are 20px Impact,
            card titles 15px bold uppercase lettering, meta 13px lettering,
            captions 13px bold uppercase and points 15px Impact.
        layout:
            A masthead row of three panels, a yellow Brightwork logo panel, a
            dotted Task board panel and a panel with Mara Okafor and her face
            circle. A wide title panel with radiating speed lines, a Meanwhile,
            on the board caption box in the corner, the title and a tilted red
            At risk banner. A dotted filter panel with a Filters caption, round
            ink-outlined dropdowns for Assignee, Label and Due, the Search tasks
            field and the red Add task button with a decorative POW above it.
            Four panels on 12px gutters, each with its title in a caption box
            hanging from the top left corner with a black count circle. Each
            task is a white speech bubble with a tail pointing down to its
            speaker row, a face circle with initials, the name in a small boxed
            label and a black points chip. Below 1080px two columns, below 640px
            one, and the POW and middle masthead panel hide.
        spacing: 12px gutters between every panel, 26px between bubbles to fit tails and speakers, 14 to 28px panel padding.
        density: Medium. One bubble and one speaker per task.
        corners: Square panels, captions and buttons, 26px speech bubbles, 20px fields and round faces.
        borders: 4px ink on panels and buttons, 3px on bubbles, captions and fields. The overdue bubble turns to a 4px red outline.
        shadows: None on boxes. Only the title lettering gets a solid 4px ink drop.
        icons:
            Heavy 2.6 stroke line glyphs at text size. Overdue is a jagged
            yellow starburst outlined in ink above the bubble, with a triangle
            and the word Overdue in dark red. Done is an ink tag with a tick and
            the word Done. Sound words such as POW are decoration only and
            hidden from screen readers.
        focus: A 4px blue outline offset 3px. A focused field turns its border blue with a 3px blue ring and a pale yellow halo.
        tone: Comic narration in captions, such as Meanwhile, on the board, while task text stays plain in caps lettering.

    style39:
        number: 39
        run: 9
        screen: ProjectDetail
        name: Academic paper
        idea: The project page is typeset like a journal article, with a centred title block, an abstract, numbered sections, ruled tables, a captioned figure and footnotes.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/39.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            paper: #fdfdfb, the page
            ink: #111111, text, rules, the primary button and the figure bar
            grey: #555555, affiliation, dates, assignees and meta text
            rule: #b8b8b8, the hairline rule between the two columns
            citationRed: #8a1c1c, links, footnote marks and file names
            shade: #f0efea, the fill of a focused list row
        type:
            One Computer Modern-like serif, "Latin Modern Roman", "CMU Serif",
            "Century Schoolbook", "TeX Gyre Schola", Georgia, "Times New
            Roman", serif. File names use "Latin Modern Mono", "Courier New",
            monospace. Sizes are 30px regular centred for the title, 18px bold
            numbered section heads, 16px body at 1.45 line height and justified
            with hyphens, 15px small caps for status words, 13px captions and
            footnotes, and 11px superscript marks.
        layout:
            A thin running head across the top holds Brightwork in small caps,
            italic nav links, a search field drawn as an underline and the
            user name, over a 0.5px rule. The article is 980px wide and centred.
            It opens with a journal line, the title, the three members as
            authors with the owner starred, the team as affiliation, a date and
            status line, and two buttons. A narrow abstract holds the brief and
            a keywords line. The body then runs in two text columns from 900px
            with a hairline column rule. Section 1 Summary has a bar figure and
            a facts table, 2 Milestones a ruled table, 3 Open tasks a numbered
            list, 4 Files a bracketed reference list, and 5 Discussion a quote
            and a reply field. Footnotes sit under a short rule at the end.
            Below 900px the body is one column.
        spacing: Tight book leading. 8px between paragraphs with a 1.5em first-line indent, 20px above section heads and a 36px column gap.
        density: Dense like print. The whole screen fits in about one and a half wide screens.
        corners: Square everywhere.
        borders: Booktabs tables with 1.2px top and bottom rules, a 0.6px rule under the header row, and no vertical lines. Buttons and fields have a 0.8px ink border.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            No pictograms. Typographic marks sit beside every status word, a
            tick for done and on track, a half circle for in progress, an open
            circle for planned and a slashed circle for blocked. The progress
            figure is a filled bar beside an outlined bar with a numbered axis.
        focus: A 1px dashed ink outline offset 3px. A focused list row also takes the shade fill.
        tone: Formal third person with captions, such as Four tasks remain open, and Table 2. Milestones and their state.

    style40:
        number: 40
        run: 9
        screen: ProjectDetail
        name: Encyclopedia
        idea: The project reads like a reference article, with a lead paragraph, a summary infobox on the right, a contents box, serif headings over thin rules, blue links and bracketed citations.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/40.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #f6f6f6, the area around the article and the side nav
            sheet: #ffffff, the article body
            text: #202122, body text and headings
            muted: #54595d, the tagline, captions and side nav headings
            linkBlue: #1d52a3, links, the primary button, the progress ring and the focus outline
            rule: #a2a9b1, heading underlines and box borders
            box: #f8f9fa, the infobox, the contents box and tables
            band: #dde6f3, infobox group header rows
            green: #1e6b35, the On track and Done words
            red: #a3221b, the Blocked word
        type:
            Headings use a serif, "Linux Libertine", Georgia, Times, serif, at
            28px for the title and 22px for section heads, both regular weight.
            Body uses a system sans, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Helvetica,
            Arial, sans-serif, at 15px with 1.6 line height. The infobox
            caption is 16px bold sans, infobox rows, contents and references
            are 13px, and citation marks are 11px superscript.
        layout:
            A white top bar holds a line emblem, the Brightwork name with a
            tagline, a wide search field with a Search button, and the user
            links. Under it a 170px plain side nav lists Navigation, Design team
            and Tools links on the grey page. The white article sheet has view
            tabs Project and Discussion on the left, and Read, Edit and View
            history on the right. The title sits over a thin rule with a from
            line. The infobox floats right at 290px with a progress ring, then
            grouped rows for Project, Dates and People. The lead paragraph holds
            the brief, then a collapsible contents box, then sections
            Milestones as a bordered table, Open tasks as a bullet list, Files,
            Discussion as a quote, and References. Each section head has an
            edit link at the right. Below 860px the side nav hides and the
            infobox spans the full width above the text.
        spacing: 16 to 24px article padding, 22px above section heads and 10px between paragraphs.
        density: Medium dense reading text, with the facts compressed into the infobox.
        corners: Square boxes. Buttons and fields have 2px corners.
        borders: A 1px grey rule under every heading. 1px boxes round the infobox, the contents box and the table cells.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            Almost none. Status uses text marks with words, a tick for Done and
            On track, a half circle for In progress, an open circle for Planned
            and a slashed circle for Blocked. A simple line emblem sits beside
            the brand.
        focus: A 2px link blue outline offset 1px. A focused field gets a blue border with an inset ring.
        tone: Neutral encyclopedic third person, such as Website redesign is a project of the Design team.

    style41:
        number: 41
        run: 9
        screen: ProjectDetail
        name: Technical manual
        idea: The project is a section of an equipment manual, with numbered clauses like 4.4.3, boxed spec tables, symbol warning boxes and a condensed uppercase sans.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/41.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            bench: #e9e9e4, the page behind the document sheet
            paper: #ffffff, the document sheet
            black: #141414, text, rules, table header rows and buttons
            grey: #4d4d4d, captions, labels and assignees
            tint: #ededed, table row heads, the nav bar and the log entry
            safetyYellow: #ffd23f, the warning symbol panel and the focus halo
            caution: #fff4cc, the warning box and a focused row
            note: #e6eef8, the note box
            link: #0b4a8f, task and file links
        type:
            A condensed sans, "Arial Narrow", "Helvetica Neue Condensed",
            "Roboto Condensed", "Liberation Sans Narrow", Arial, sans-serif,
            with font-stretch condensed. Sizes are 34px bold uppercase for the
            title, 18px bold uppercase section heads led by a clause number,
            15px body at 1.4 line height, 12px bold uppercase captions and tags
            with wide tracking, and 13px monospace for file names.
        layout:
            The page is one framed document sheet with a 2px black border. A
            header block splits into cells for the boxed B mark and Brightwork,
            a document id strip with doc number, unit, start and due, and the
            operator Mara Okafor. A grey nav bar holds uppercase links and a
            Find field. The title block shows Section 4, the uppercase title
            over a 3px rule, and the Add task and Edit project buttons. Two
            columns follow. The left holds 4.1 Specifications as a gridded spec
            table with a segmented gauge, 4.2 Purpose as clauses 4.2.1 and
            4.2.2, and 4.3 Milestone sequence as a table. The right holds 4.4
            Open tasks with a yellow warning box, 4.5 Reference documents as a
            table, and 4.6 Operator log with a note box, the quote and a reply
            field. A footer strip shows the doc id and page number. Below 820px
            everything is one column.
        spacing: A 4px base. 3 to 7px cell padding, 18px between clauses and a 28px column gap.
        density: High. Two columns of clauses on wide screens.
        corners: Square only.
        borders: A 2px black frame round the document, a 1px black table grid, a 3px rule under the title and dotted rules between task rows.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            ISO style safety symbols. A yellow triangle with an exclamation
            mark heads the warning box and a circled i heads the note box, each
            in its own panel. Tags are boxed uppercase words with a tick for On
            track, a solid square for Done, a triangle for Active, a hollow
            square for Pending and a slashed circle for Blocked.
        focus: A 3px black outline offset 2px with a 6px safety yellow halo.
        tone: Imperative and terse, such as Do not publish the customers page until permission is received.

    style42:
        number: 42
        run: 9
        screen: ProjectDetail
        name: Architectural
        idea: The project is laid out like a floor plan on a drawing sheet, with hairline walls between numbered rooms, grid bubbles, a dimension line timeline, a scale bar and a title block, all in lowercase geometric type.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/42.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            white: #ffffff, the page and the rooms
            ink: #1a1a1a, text, walls, the primary button and the scale bar
            grey: #666666, labels, dates, assignees and grid leaders
            hairline: #d4d4d4, row dividers inside rooms and link underlines
            faint: #f4f4f2, the fill of a focused list row
            markupRed: #b3261e, the blocked word and symbol only, like a redline
        type:
            One geometric sans, Futura, "Futura PT", "Century Gothic", "Avenir
            Next", Avenir, "URW Gothic", "Trebuchet MS", sans-serif, with all
            text lowercase. Weight is 300 for text and 400 for labels. Sizes are
            44px for the title, 64px for the percent figure, 19px for the brief
            and quote, 15px body at 1.6 line height, and 11px labels with 0.18em
            tracking. File names are a small monospace.
        layout:
            A sparse top line holds the widely tracked brightwork wordmark,
            grey nav links with the current one underlined, an underline search
            field and the user name. The title sits left with the buttons right.
            The plan is a four column grid of rooms drawn with shared 1px ink
            walls. Circled grid bubbles a to d sit above the column lines and 1
            to 3 left of the rows, joined by dashed leaders. Row 1 holds 01 brief
            across two columns, 02 status and 03 people. Row 2 holds 04
            milestones as a dimension line with slashed ticks, and 05 open tasks.
            Row 3 holds 06 files, 07 discussion and a title block with project,
            team, owner, viewer, sheet and a north arrow. A scale bar of
            alternating black and white segments from 0 to 25 tasks marks 18 done
            below the plan. Below 1000px the rooms go two across, and below 640px
            the bubbles hide and the rooms stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 22 to 26px room padding, 36 to 56px between major blocks and a 44px gutter for the grid markers.
        density: Sparse with lots of white and few items per room.
        corners: Square. Only the grid bubbles are round.
        borders: 1px ink walls shared between rooms, 1px light grey rows inside rooms and dashed grey grid leaders.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            Tiny 11px drawn glyphs beside words, a tick for on track, a filled
            square for done, a half filled square for in progress, a hollow
            square for planned and a slashed circle for blocked. People show as
            lowercase initials in square frames.
        focus: A 1.5px ink outline offset 4px. Fields also thicken their underline to 2px.
        tone: Lowercase nouns over sentences, numbered like drawing references, such as 05 open tasks.

    style43:
        number: 43
        run: 9
        screen: ProjectDetail
        name: Card catalogue
        idea: The project is a drawer of library index cards, each one typewritten on ruled stock with a call number, a punched hole and rubber stamps for status.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/43.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            linen: #efe8da, the page and the punched holes
            card: #fffdf4, index cards and fields
            ink: #26221d, typed text and the primary button
            faded: #5e564b, tracings and labels
            ruledBlue: #c9daea, the ruled lines on cards, decorative only
            redLine: #d98b80, the header rule on cards, decorative only
            stampRed: #a3231a, the Blocked stamp
            stampGreen: #1f5a37, the On track stamp
            oak: #d8c3a0, the drawer front
            brass: #b08d3c, the label holder and the drawer pull
            guideBuff: #f3e7c4, guide cards with tabs and the focus halo
            pencilBlue: #1b3f73, the handwritten discussion note
        type:
            A typewriter mono, "Courier Prime", "American Typewriter", "Courier
            New", Courier, monospace, on a 24px line grid. Sizes are 22px bold
            for the drawer label, 15px bold card headings ending in a full stop,
            15px regular body, 12px bold stacked call numbers at 12px line
            height, and 13px bold uppercase tabs and stamps with wide tracking.
            The discussion note uses a hand font, "Bradley Hand", "Segoe Print",
            cursive, at 18px.
        layout:
            A cream top bar holds BRIGHTWORK in tracked caps, nav links, a Look
            up field and Reader Mara Okafor. Below sits a wide oak drawer front
            with a brass label holder showing DSN 01 and the title, the Add card
            and Edit buttons, and a brass pull. The cards follow in a grid of
            330px minimum cards, three across on wide screens. A main entry card
            carries the facts, a typed progress bar of X and dots, and an On
            track stamp. A summary card carries the brief and tracings. Buff
            guide cards with raised tabs span the full width to divide
            Milestones, Open tasks and Discussion. Each open task gets its own
            card. The files card is a See also list. The notes card holds the
            pencilled quote and a reply line. Each card has a stacked call
            number at top left, a hanging indent, a red header line, blue ruled
            lines and a punched hole at the bottom centre. Below 600px the cards
            stack in one column.
        spacing: The 24px line grid set by the ruled cards. 24 to 30px between cards and an 86px hanging indent after the call number.
        density: Medium. One fact per typed line and one task per card.
        corners: Square cards, 3px tab tops, a 4px drawer and round punched holes.
        borders: 1px warm grey card edges, a 2px oak brown drawer frame, and a double line border on the Blocked stamp.
        shadows: A 1px edge line and a soft 2px drop under cards, and an inset shadow in each punched hole.
        icons:
            Typed brackets beside words, X for done, a slash for in progress and
            a blank for planned. Rubber stamps carry a tick for On track and a
            slashed circle for Blocked, tilted a few degrees. The drawer pull
            is drawn in SVG.
        focus: A 2px ink outline offset 3px with a 5px buff halo.
        tone: Cataloguer shorthand ending in full stops, such as Assigned, Aiko Tanaka, and See also.

    style44:
        number: 44
        run: 10
        screen: Settings
        name: Control panel
        idea: Settings laid out like an industrial equipment panel in light brushed metal, with rocker switches, engraved labels, rivets and shaped indicator lamps.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/44.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            housing: #c3c8cd, the page behind the plates with faint horizontal lines
            plate: #dde0e3, brushed module plates as a gradient from #e5e8eb to #d5d9dd with fine vertical streaks
            plateHigh: #eceef0, the nameplate tag, raised keys and demo rows
            edge: #8a9198, borders on plates, keys and tab buttons
            engrave: #2b3035, labels, body text and the primary button
            label: #454c53, secondary engraving and the OFF lamp word
            lampOn: #155f29, the round lit ON lamp and its word
            pointerAmber: #9a5b00, the triangle above the selected tab and the selected digest key
            lcd: #cdd5c0, readout windows and the saved status, with ink #1e2a14
            danger: #a3221b, the Leave workspace button
            hazard: #f2c400, the danger stripe band in diagonals with #1f2326, decoration only
            focus: #0b57d0, the focus outline
        type:
            A condensed technical sans, Bahnschrift, DIN Alternate, D-DIN, Roboto
            Condensed, Arial Narrow, Arial, sans-serif. The page title is 26px
            bold in capitals with 0.06em tracking. The brand is 22px bold
            capitals with wide 0.28em tracking. Engraved labels are 12px bold
            capitals with 0.12em tracking and a white 1px text shadow below.
            Row text is 15px semibold, hints 13px regular. Readouts and lamp
            words use Consolas, Menlo or another monospace, 18px bold in the
            readout and 12px bold beside lamps.
        layout:
            A nameplate plate across the top with the brand, a small Settings
            tag and Operator Mara Okafor on the right. Next a plate with the
            Settings title and five tab push buttons in a row. Below, a grid
            with a wide Notifications plate on the left and a narrower stack on
            the right holding Time and language, a Commit plate with the
            buttons and saved readout, and the Danger zone plate. Under 860px
            everything stacks, and under 520px the tab buttons wrap three to a
            row.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px between plates, 24px plate padding, 14px vertical padding on each row.
        density: Medium. One control per row with a groove line between rows.
        corners: 6px plates, 4px keys, rockers and buttons, 3px fields and readout windows.
        borders:
            1px #8a9198 on every metal part. Section titles run into a groove
            made of a dark line over a light line. Each plate has a small
            domed rivet in all four corners.
        shadows:
            Raised parts carry a solid 3px bottom edge in a darker grey and a
            white inner top highlight. Pressed parts drop 2px and use an inset
            shadow. Readouts and fields are recessed with an inset shadow.
        icons:
            Indicator lamps carry meaning by shape. A round glowing lamp with
            the word ON means on, a hollow square with the word OFF means off.
            A solid amber triangle marks the selected tab and digest key while
            other keys show a hollow circle. Saved shows a filled circle tick.
            The danger zone shows a yellow warning triangle and a door exit
            icon on its button. Switches are two-half rockers printed On and
            Off, with the active half raised and pale.
        focus: A 3px #0b57d0 outline offset 3px around the button, rocker, key or field.
        tone: Terse panel labels in capitals, such as Operator, Commit and Changes saved.

    style45:
        number: 45
        run: 10
        screen: Settings
        name: Big and simple
        idea: One wide column of extra large text and huge tap targets in plain words, built for low vision and older users with AAA contrast everywhere.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/45.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #ffffff, the background everywhere
            ink: #111111, text, row borders and ticked boxes
            softInk: #333333, hints and the Off word
            blue: #0a3a82, links, the primary button, the current section and the focus outline
            blueSoft: #e6eefb, the row being focused
            green: #0b5a2a, the On word and the saved note on #e3f3e8
            red: #8a1010, the danger zone on #fbeaea
        type:
            A wide, clear sans with a large x height, Verdana, Tahoma, Segoe UI,
            DejaVu Sans, sans-serif. Body text is 22px at 1.6 line height and
            never goes below 20px. The page title is 44px bold, section titles
            34px bold, group labels 26px bold, row text 22px bold and hints
            20px regular. At phone width the body drops to 20px.
        layout:
            A single centred column 760px wide. A header with the brand and
            Signed in as Mara Okafor sits above a 3px rule. The five sections
            are a stack of full width rows, with the current one filled blue
            and marked You are here. Then the Notifications rows, the Time and
            language fields, the digest radios, two full width stacked buttons,
            the saved note and the danger box. Nothing sits side by side.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px between rows, 24px inside rows, 56px above each section heading.
        density: Very low. One thing per row, about five rows per screen.
        corners: 14px on rows, fields and buttons, 10px on tick boxes, round radio dots.
        borders: 3px solid #222222 on every row and field, 4px on tick boxes and the danger box.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            Few and large, 32 to 44px, always next to a word. A white tick in a
            filled black box means on and an empty box means off, with the word
            On or Off at the end of the row. A filled dot in a ring marks the
            chosen radio and its label is underlined. A filled green circle
            tick shows Changes saved and a solid red triangle heads the danger
            zone. Sections that are not current end in a plain arrow.
        focus: A 5px #0a3a82 outline offset 4px, and the focused row turns #e6eefb.
        tone: Plain short instructions, such as You are here and Tick a box to turn a message on.

    style46:
        number: 46
        run: 10
        screen: Settings
        name: Public service plain
        idea: A plain public-service form in black on white, one bold sans and a thick yellow focus, where nothing is decoration and every heading sits hard left.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/46.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            ink: #0b0c0c, text, checkbox borders, the primary button and the header rule
            paper: #ffffff, the page and fields
            hint: #4f575b, hint text and captions
            rule: #b1b4b6, thin dividers and the bar beside nested options
            link: #1a4f8b, underlined links
            focus: #ffdd00, the focus fill and ring, always paired with black
            panel: #f3f2f1, the secondary button
            success: #1a6b3c, the saved banner border, its title bar and tick
            warning: #b3261e, the Leave workspace button
        type:
            One sans only, Arial, Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Liberation Sans,
            sans-serif. The page title is 48px bold at 1.04 line height with a
            19px grey caption above it. Section titles are 32px bold, legends
            24px bold, body 19px regular at 1.45 and hints 19px in grey. Buttons
            are 19px bold.
        layout:
            A white header with the brand on the left and Mara Okafor on the
            right, closed by a 10px black rule. The content is 1020px wide. A
            one third column holds the section links as a plain list, the
            current one bold black with a 5px black bar on its left. The two
            thirds column holds the saved banner, the form as one long column,
            the buttons, a thin rule and the Danger zone. Under 760px the
            columns stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit used as 16, 24 and 40. 16px between options, 32px between groups, 40px between columns.
        density: Low to medium. A single long form read top to bottom.
        corners: Square everywhere. Only radios are round.
        borders: 2px black on fields and boxes, 10px black under the header, 1px #b1b4b6 dividers, a 5px green frame on the saved banner.
        shadows: Only a flat 3px bottom edge on buttons, grey on the black and light buttons and dark red on the warning button.
        icons:
            Almost none. A thick black square tick inside 40px square boxes, a
            filled dot inside 40px round radios, a green tick before Changes
            saved, and a white exclamation mark in a black circle before the
            danger warning.
        focus:
            Links and buttons turn #ffdd00 with black text and a 4px black bar
            beneath. Fields get a 3px #ffdd00 outline plus a 2px black inner
            ring. Boxes get a 4px yellow ring.
        tone: Direct and instructional, such as Select all that apply and If you leave, you lose access to this workspace.

    style47:
        number: 47
        run: 10
        screen: Settings
        name: Raw HTML
        idea: The page looks almost unstyled, like hand-written HTML from the late 1990s, with Times, blue underlined links, grey bevel buttons, rules and bordered tables.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/47.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            white: #ffffff, the page and fields
            black: #000000, all text and the dotted focus outline
            linkBlue: #0000ee, unvisited links, always underlined
            visitedPurple: #551a8b, visited links
            buttonGrey: #c0c0c0, buttons, table header cells and bevels
            shadowGrey: #808080, rules and bevel shade
            darkBevel: #404040, the outer shadow edge of buttons
            warningYellow: #ffff99, the WARNING cell in the danger table
        type:
            Browser default serif, Times New Roman, Times, Liberation Serif,
            serif, 16px at 1.25. The brand is 32px bold with a small italic
            line under it. The page title is the default h1 at 32px bold,
            sections are h2 at 24px bold, sub sections h3 at 19px bold.
            Controls use Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif at 13px. Captions and the
            footer are small italic.
        layout:
            No layout beyond the flow. A borderless header table puts the brand
            left and Logged in as Mara Okafor right. A grooved rule, then the
            sections as links in square brackets split by bars, with the
            current one bold between double arrows. Then Settings, Notifications,
            a Changes saved line, a full width bordered table of settings with
            columns for setting, checkbox and status, the selects on their own
            lines, a fieldset of inline radios, two buttons, a rule, the danger
            table and a small address footer.
        spacing: Browser defaults. 8px body margin, normal paragraph gaps, 4px cell padding, 2px cell spacing.
        density: Dense and long. Everything flows top to bottom.
        corners: Square, always.
        borders: Tables use a 2px outset border with 1px inset cells. Rules are a 1px grey line over a white line. The final rule is 4px solid black.
        shadows: None. Buttons are bevelled with white top left edges and dark grey bottom right edges, inverted when pressed.
        icons:
            None. Text symbols only, a check mark before Changes saved, a
            warning sign beside WARNING and double arrows around the current
            section. On and off show as native checkboxes plus the words ON or
            off in italic.
        focus: A 2px dotted black outline offset 2px.
        tone: Literal and a bit stiff, such as Logged in as, WARNING! and Table 1. Notifications.

    style48:
        number: 48
        run: 10
        screen: Settings
        name: Scandinavian
        idea: Birch and oat surfaces with muted sage and dusty blue, soft rounded type and thin calm lines, so settings feel like a quiet, airy room.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/48.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            oat: #f4efe6, the page
            linen: #fbf8f2, cards
            birch: #e9dfcf, the header strip with faint wood grain lines and the off switch track
            line: #ddd3c3, hairlines and card and field borders
            wood: #2f2a24, text and headings
            stone: #675e54, labels, hints and inactive tabs
            sage: #4f6b55, the primary button, the on switch and the current tab underline
            sageSoft: #e3ebe2, selected chips and the saved note
            fjord: #4a6680, links and the focus ring
            clay: #9b3b2e, the danger zone on #fdf8f6
        type:
            A soft rounded sans, ui-rounded, SF Pro Rounded, Nunito, Quicksand,
            Varela Round, Segoe UI, system-ui, sans-serif. The page title is
            34px medium with slight negative tracking. Card titles are 19px
            semibold, body 16px regular at 1.6, hints and labels 14px in stone
            and buttons 15px semibold. No heavy weights.
        layout:
            A birch header strip 72px tall with the brand left and the name and
            a round initials avatar right. The content is 1040px wide with
            56px above the title. Tabs are plain words on one hairline. Below,
            a three to two grid puts the Notifications card on the left and a
            stack on the right with the Time and language card, which holds the
            buttons and saved note, and the Danger zone card. Under 860px
            everything stacks and under 520px the tabs wrap.
        spacing: An 8px unit used generously. 32px card padding and gaps, 18px row padding, 48px under the tabs.
        density: Airy. Few rows per screen with plenty of oat around them.
        corners: 18px cards, 12px fields, fully round buttons, chips, switches and the avatar.
        borders: Thin 1px warm hairlines only. The current tab gets a 2px sage underline.
        shadows: None. Depth comes from linen cards on the oat page.
        icons:
            Thin round line icons with a 1.4 stroke at text size. The switch
            knob shows a check when on and a dash when off, with the word On or
            Off beside it. Selected chips show a check, and the current tab has
            a small filled dot before its name. Saved shows a circled check and
            the danger zone a thin triangle.
        focus: A 2px #4a6680 outline offset 3px.
        tone: Soft and brief, such as What Brightwork tells you, and when.

    style49:
        number: 49
        run: 11
        screen: Pricing
        name: Private bank
        idea: A conservative wealth-management letterhead in navy and ivory, with engraved serif capitals, a thin gold rule and a framed schedule of fees in a formal voice.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/49.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            ivory: #f8f4ea, the page
            vellum: #fffdf7, the plan frame and the style sheet ground
            navy: #13254a, text, rules, the primary button and the featured Team column
            slate: #5a6378, captions, italic notes and meta text
            gold: #a8843c, thin rules, the inner frame line and the focus halo, decoration only
            goldInk: #7a5c22, small gold capital labels on ivory
            paleGold: #c9a75a, gold accents and roman numerals on navy
            hairline: #d9d0bc, row dividers
            ledgerGreen: #1f5a3a, included ticks in the table
        type:
            Display is Didot, Bodoni 72, Bodoni MT, Baskerville, Times New Roman,
            serif, always uppercase with wide tracking. Text is Baskerville,
            Hoefler Text, Georgia, serif. Sizes are 52px for the page title at
            0.14em tracking, 56px regular lining figures for prices, 26px plan
            names at 0.24em, 17px body on a 1.6 line, 15px italic notes and
            12px capital labels at 0.22em.
        layout:
            A centred letterhead with a monogram crest in a double circle, the
            brand in spaced capitals and a small capital nav, closed by a double
            gold rule. Below sit a small gold overline, the title, an italic
            lede, a diamond flourish and a square two part billing switch with
            the free months note in italic gold. The three plans share one
            certificate frame, a navy line with a gold line inset 6px, split
            into columns by hairlines. Team is a solid navy column with the
            Most popular label sitting on the top frame edge. Each plan shows a
            roman numeral, the name, a short gold rule, the price, an italic
            billing line, a dash list and a button. Then a comparison table with
            a tinted Team column and a centred list of questions with roman
            numerals. Below 900px the plans stack inside the same frame.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 36 to 40px inside plans and 72 to 88px between sections.
        density: Sparse. Few words per line with generous leading.
        corners: None. Every edge is square.
        borders: A double frame of 1px navy then 1px gold. Hairlines between rows and a 1px navy rule under the table head and at its foot.
        shadows: None. Buttons carry an inset keyline in gold 3px inside the edge.
        icons:
            No pictograms. A monogram crest, a diamond flourish, roman
            numerals, em dashes as list marks, a tick and a dash in the table,
            and plus and minus on the questions. The billing switch shows a
            filled diamond on the chosen option.
        focus: A 1px navy outline offset 4px with a 1px gold halo outside it. A focused field gets a 2px gold underline on white.
        tone: Formal and measured, such as Schedule of fees, Particulars and Questions answered.

    style50:
        number: 50
        run: 11
        screen: Pricing
        name: Constructivist
        idea: An avant-garde propaganda poster in red, black and cream, where tilted slabs, heavy condensed capitals and solid arrows drive the eye from plan to button.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/50.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            cream: #f2e8d5, the page ground
            paper: #faf4e6, plan slabs, question boxes and the style sheet
            red: #b3121b, the hero slab, plan heads, the primary button, arrows and the badge
            black: #141414, text, frames, the top bar, the featured plan, the table band and focus
            umber: #6b5e4e, secondary labels on cream
            stone: #d8ccb4, large ghost numerals and the caption on black
            oxide: #2a1416, the Team column in the black table
        type:
            Display is Impact, Haettenschweiler, Franklin Gothic Condensed,
            Oswald, Barlow Condensed, Arial Narrow, DejaVu Sans Condensed,
            sans-serif, bold and always uppercase. Text is Franklin Gothic
            Medium, Arial Narrow, Arial, sans-serif at semibold. The title is up
            to 210px on a 0.9 line, prices are 112px, plan names 52px, section
            titles 72px, controls 24 to 26px and body 17px.
        layout:
            A black top bar with a red square logo and the current nav item on
            a red block. The hero is a full width red slab rotated minus 6
            degrees that carries the title, half cream and half black, crossed
            by a black disc and a thin black diagonal bar, with a short boxed
            line below at the right. A square billing switch is followed by a
            bar arrow pointing to a tilted red 2 months free tag. Three plan
            slabs sit edge to edge with 4px black frames, each stepped 48px
            lower than the last. Each has a head cut on a diagonal, a huge
            price, triangle bullets and a ghost numeral. The comparison sits on
            a black band whose top edge is cut on a slant, and the questions
            sit beside a big red title rotated to read upward. Below 900px the
            plans stack with small sideways offsets and the title stops
            rotating.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 20px inside slabs and 40 to 72px between blocks.
        density: Loud and medium. Few words, huge figures and short bold lists.
        corners: Square, except one black disc. Plan heads and swatches are cut on a diagonal.
        borders: 4px solid black on every box, 2px rules between list items and rows, and 6px red under the table head.
        shadows: Only a hard 6px black offset block behind the primary button, cream on the black plan. No blur.
        icons:
            Solid geometric shapes. Bar and triangle arrows on buttons,
            triangles as list bullets and included marks, a flat bar for not
            included, a star on the badge and a triangle on the chosen billing
            option.
        focus: A 4px black outline offset 3px with a cream gap. A focused field turns its frame red and gains a 16px left slab.
        tone: Short commands in capitals, such as Pick one and Plan against plan.

    style51:
        number: 51
        run: 11
        screen: Pricing
        name: 50s diner
        idea: A retro American diner menu in cherry red and mint, with script headings, a checkerboard band, chrome trim and dotted price leaders that make choosing a plan feel like ordering lunch.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/51.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            cream: #fffaf0, the page
            vanilla: #fff3dc, the menu card and the table caption
            cherry: #c41e3a, script titles, prices, the primary button and the table head
            cherryShade: #8f1028, the pressed lip under red buttons
            mint: #a8e6cf, the header band, the free months note and the title shadow
            mintPale: #dff5ec, the featured plan, striped rows and the style sheet
            teal: #1d6b55, small capital labels, the secondary button and tick discs
            cocoa: #3a2e2a, body text, outlines and the checkerboard
            cocoaSoft: #6a5a52, italic notes and captions
            chrome: #fbfcfd to #c9d0d7 to #8e98a3 to #dfe4e9, a vertical gradient for the menu rim and the toggle track
        type:
            Script is Brush Script MT, Segoe Script, Snell Roundhand, Lucida
            Handwriting, cursive, set italic. Sans is Futura, Century Gothic,
            Avenir Next, Trebuchet MS, sans-serif. The title is 96px script
            with a 3px mint offset shadow, section titles 52 to 56px script,
            plan names 28px extra bold capitals, prices 40px extra bold, body
            17px on a 1.5 line, and labels 13px bold capitals at 0.14em.
        layout:
            A mint header band with a red star badge logo, the brand in script
            and pill nav links, closed by a cocoa and cream checkerboard band
            between cherry lines. A centred hero holds the script title, a teal
            tagline, a short line and a chrome pill toggle beside a mint 2
            months free pill. The plans sit in one menu card with a chrome rim
            and rounded corners. Each plan is a menu line, the name in capitals,
            a dotted leader and the price at the right, then the billing words,
            the features joined by red bullets and a pill button. Team is a mint
            panel inside the menu with a red starburst reading Most popular.
            Then a rounded white comparison card with a red head and mint
            striped rows, questions as speech bubbles with a red Q disc, and a
            checkerboard band above the footer. Below 720px menu lines wrap
            and buttons drop under the features.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between menu items, 36 to 40px card padding and 72px between sections.
        density: Medium. Plans read as stacked menu lines, not cards side by side.
        corners: Round. 28px menu rim, 20px table card, 16px swatches, fully round pills and buttons, and speech bubbles with one sharp corner.
        borders: 2px cocoa outlines, dotted leaders and dividers, a double cherry rule under the menu title and the checkerboard bands.
        shadows: One soft drop under the menu, 0 10px 24px at 18 percent cocoa. A hard mint offset behind the table. Red buttons carry an inset cherryShade lip and a white then grey chrome ring.
        icons:
            Few and sign-like. A star badge logo, a starburst for Most
            popular, white ticks in filled teal circles, a Q disc on each
            question, a tick on the chosen billing option and plus and minus
            toggles.
        focus: A 3px dashed cherry outline offset 4px. A focused field gets a white gap and then a 2px cherry ring.
        tone: Warm counter talk, such as Today's plans, Ask the counter and What comes on each plate.

    style52:
        number: 52
        run: 11
        screen: Pricing
        name: Sports magazine
        idea: An energetic sports print spread, with slanted italic condensed headlines, plans as numbered jerseys, diagonal stripes and a scoreboard of amber figures for the comparison.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/52.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            white: #ffffff, the page
            court: #f1f4f9, plan cards, unchosen tabs and the style sheet
            electricBlue: #0047bb, the featured plan, the headline accent, the ticker and the chosen tab
            flame: #c23f00, the primary button, kickers and bullets
            ink: #111827, text, heavy rules, the masthead and the scoreboard
            steel: #4b5563, small capital labels and meta
            volt: #d4ff00, the badge, the current nav, the focus glow and accents on blue or black, always with ink text
            amber: #ffd200, scoreboard figures on black
            line: #d5dbe5, stat dividers
        type:
            Headlines are Oswald, Barlow Condensed, Roboto Condensed, Arial
            Narrow, Impact, sans-serif at 800 italic in capitals. Body is
            Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif. Scores are
            Bahnschrift, DIN Alternate, ui-monospace, monospace. The cover line
            is up to 150px on a 0.84 line, section titles 56px, plan names 48px,
            the deck 20px semibold, body 16px and kickers 12px bold capitals
            at 0.16em.
        layout:
            An ink masthead with a slanted volt logo and the current nav item
            on a volt parallelogram, then a blue ticker of plan prices. The
            cover pairs a giant two line headline reading Pick your plan with a
            billing block of slanted tabs and a volt 2 months free tag, then a
            striped bar of blue and flame diagonals. Each section starts with an
            italic title over a 6px ink rule. The roster is three plan cards
            with thick top bars, each with a jersey number line, the name, an
            SVG jersey whose shirt number is the price, the billing words, a
            stat list and a slanted button. Team is the blue card with a volt
            jersey and the badge. The comparison is a dark scoreboard with a
            hazard stripe top and amber figures in black cells. Questions sit
            in three columns with big blue italic numbers. Below 960px
            everything stacks.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 20px card padding, 24px gutters and 48px between sections.
        density: Busy and punchy. A ticker, stat lists and a packed scoreboard.
        corners: No round corners. Tabs, buttons, badges and the current nav are parallelograms cut 12px at each end.
        borders: 8px ink top bars on plans, 6px ink under section titles, 2px stat dividers and a 6px slate frame on the scoreboard.
        shadows: None. Energy comes from stripes and slants.
        icons:
            SVG jerseys carry the price as the shirt number. Play triangles as
            bullets, a heavy tick and a cross on the scoreboard, a star on the
            badge, a play triangle on the chosen tab and a double chevron on
            every button.
        focus: A 3px ink outline offset 2px with a 7px volt glow. Slanted buttons drop their clip shape while focused.
        tone: Coach talk in capitals, such as The roster, The scoreboard and Post-game Q and A.

    style53:
        number: 53
        run: 11
        screen: Pricing
        name: Risograph
        idea: A two-ink risograph zine in fluorescent pink and blue, where the inks overprint into violet, every heading sits slightly off register and a fine grain covers the paper.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/53.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            paper: #f4f1ea, the page and the Free plan card
            fluoroPink: #ff48b0, ink for shapes, offset heading copies, halftone dots and hard shadows, never small text
            pinkInk: #b0125f, small pink words, arrows and not included crosses
            pinkTint: #ffc2e2, the Team card, the Team column and the current nav
            risoBlue: #0078bf, large headings and blue shapes
            blueInk: #3255a4, the primary button, links and included dots
            deepOverprint: #1a2a6c, body text, rules, outlines and focus
            blueTint: #bfe0f5, the Business card
            overprint: multiply, where pink and blue cross and turn violet
        type:
            Display is Arial Black, Helvetica Neue, Franklin Gothic Heavy,
            Arial, sans-serif at 900 with tight tracking. Text is Courier
            Prime, Courier New, ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas, monospace. The
            title is up to 168px on a 0.88 line, prices 76px, section titles
            52px, plan names 40px, questions 20px, body 16px on a 1.6 line and
            labels 13px bold mono capitals.
        layout:
            A light header with a logo of a pink circle overprinting a blue
            square, mono capital nav with the current item on a pink
            highlighter band and a wavy underline, and a torn zigzag strip in
            blue. The hero sets the title in riso blue with a pink copy offset
            slightly down and right beneath it, a tilted dark label above, a
            mono line and a square billing switch with a dashed pink stamp for
            2 months free. A large pink circle with halftone dots overprints a
            tilted blue rectangle at the right. Three plan cards tilt by
            different small angles, each with a deep outline and a pink
            duplicate outline offset 5px, a halftone or solid spot at the top
            corner, a pink dollar sign, a big price, an arrow list on dotted
            rules and a button. Team is pink tinted with a dark Most popular
            sticker, Business blue tinted. The comparison table tints the Team
            column pink, and questions use pink number discs. Below 900px the
            cards stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px card padding, 28px gutters and 88px between sections.
        density: Medium and loose, like a zine spread with tilted, staggered cards.
        corners: Square cards and buttons. Round only for ink blobs, halftone dots and number discs.
        borders: 2px deep outline on cards with a pink duplicate offset 5px right and 4px down, dotted 2px rules between rows and a torn zigzag strip under the header.
        shadows: No blur. Hard pink offsets of 5px by 4px behind buttons, as a second ink layer. A fractal noise grain covers the whole page at 22 percent opacity, multiplied.
        icons:
            Printed glyphs only. Arrows as list marks, a filled dot for
            included, a cross for not included, an empty and a filled circle on
            the billing switch and a star on the sticker.
        focus: A 3px deep outline offset 3px with a pink offset halo. A focused field gains a pink offset shadow and a blue border.
        tone: Plain and a little handmade, such as Printed in two inks and plan by plan.

    style54:
        number: 54
        run: 12
        screen: Inbox
        name: Chat-first
        idea: The inbox reads like a messaging app, with people as round avatars, notifications as speech bubbles and a composer bar always ready for a reply.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/54.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #e9f1ee, the pale green page behind the app
            panel: #ffffff, the app shell and message bubbles
            bubbleIn: #f1f4f3, the composer field and quiet tiles
            selected: #d8efe7, the open conversation in the list
            text: #14231f, body text, names and the active filter chip
            muted: #4f625c, previews, project names and times
            line: #d3e0db, dividers and bubble edges
            accent: #0b6e5f, the Reply button, outlined chips, links and the focus ring
            unread: #b5342a, the unread dot, the Unread word and the count badge
            mention: #4a1f78 text on #e7dcf3, the at name inside a message
        type:
            Segoe UI, system-ui, -apple-system, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial,
            sans-serif. The Inbox title is 24px bold. Names are 15px semibold,
            and 15px extra bold when unread. Bubble text is 15px on a 1.45 line
            height. Previews are 14px muted, and times, projects and badges are
            12px.
        layout:
            One rounded app shell 1240px wide at most. On the left a column
            380px wide holds the brand, Mara as a round avatar with an online
            dot, the Inbox title, the line 3 people are waiting on you, the
            filter chips and the conversation list. Each row has a 40px
            initials avatar, the name and time on one line, the preview below
            and the project with status words under it. The weekly report row
            uses a square chart tile in place of an avatar. On the right the
            open thread has a header with Priya, the task and project, a day
            pill, a centred context line, Priya's message bubble with her small
            avatar at its foot, the three option thumbnails as bubble cards,
            the time with Unread, then outlined chips for Mark as done and Open
            task. A composer bar at the bottom has an attach button, a round
            reply field and a pill Reply button. Below 820px the shell loses
            its corners and the list sits above the thread.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 12px between bubbles and rows, 20 to 24px panel padding.
        density: Comfortable. Six conversations fill the list with room to spare.
        corners: 24px on the shell, 20px bubbles with a 6px tail corner at bottom left, 18px list rows, round avatars, chips, field and buttons.
        borders: 1px #d3e0db on bubbles and dividers, 1.5px accent on the outlined chips.
        shadows: The shell has 0 10px 30px rgba(11,60,50,0.12). Bubbles have a faint 0 1px 2px.
        icons:
            18px round line icons with a 2px stroke. People are initials
            avatars in six deep colours with white letters. Unread is a red
            dot with the word Unread, done is a tick with the word Done, the
            open row shows an eye with Open, and Mark as done uses a double
            tick.
        focus: A 3px accent outline offset 2px. A focused field gets an accent border and a soft 3px accent ring.
        tone: Conversational and warm, such as 3 people are waiting on you and Reply to Priya.

    style55:
        number: 55
        run: 12
        screen: Inbox
        name: Typewriter
        idea: Every notification is a typed paper slip in an in-tray, and the open item is a memo with carbon-blue type, index-tab filters and finished work struck through.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/55.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            desk: #e7e1d3, the page behind the paper
            paper: #fffdf6, the memo, the tray and unread slips
            slip: #f7f1e1, read slips and inactive tabs
            onionskin: #eef2f7, the open slip and the sheet behind the memo
            ink: #1d1c1a, typed text, rules and the key buttons
            faded: #555046, slip headers, times and Re lines
            carbon: #24408e, the memo body, reply text, links and focus
            ribbonRed: #a1221b, unread marks, the unread slip edge and the count
            rule: #cfc6b2, paper and tab edges
            ruleBlue: #c4d0e6, the ruled lines of the reply field
        type:
            One typewriter stack, Courier New, Courier, Nimbus Mono PS,
            Liberation Mono, monospace. The brand is 28px bold uppercase with
            wide tracking. Memorandum is 22px bold uppercase with 0.35em
            tracking. The memo body is 17px in carbon blue on a 1.75 line
            height. Slip text is 15px on a 1.6 line height, and headers and
            times are 12px uppercase.
        layout:
            A masthead with the brand, the subtitle Inter-office memoranda, and
            Desk of Mara Okafor with the date at right, over a double rule.
            Below sit two columns, five to six. On the left, index tabs for
            All, Mentions, Assigned and Unread (3) hang over a paper in-tray
            titled In-tray with a key line, then six stacked slips each tilted
            a fraction of a degree. Each slip has a header line of status marks
            and the time, the typed sentence, and a Re line with the project.
            On the right the open item is a memo with a paper clip, a centred
            Memorandum heading, To, From, Date and Re lines, a dashed rule, the
            message, Encl. 3 prints as three slightly tilted photo prints with
            captions, a ruled reply field and three key buttons. Below 860px
            the memo stacks under the tray.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 12px between slips, 36 to 40px memo margins, 32px between columns.
        density: Medium. Each slip is three short typed lines.
        corners: Square everywhere. Slips and prints tilt a fraction of a degree.
        borders: 1px #cfc6b2 paper edges, a 4px ribbon red left edge on unread slips, 2px ink on key buttons, a double ink rule under headings and dashed rules inside the memo.
        shadows: Flat offset shadows with no blur, 3px 3px rgba(60,50,30,0.12) on paper and 2px 2px ink under the keys.
        icons:
            No drawn icons apart from the paper clip. Status is typed in
            brackets, with [*] unread in ribbon red, [/] done in ink with the
            task name struck through, [ ] read, and two arrows with on the desk
            for the open slip.
        focus: A 2px dashed carbon outline offset 3px. A focused reply field gets the same dashed outline around its ruled lines.
        tone: Office formal and terse, such as In-tray, Memorandum, Re, Encl. 3 prints and cc. Website redesign file.

    style56:
        number: 56
        run: 12
        screen: Inbox
        name: Thermal receipt
        idea: The inbox prints out as narrow thermal receipts, with numbered line items, dot leaders, dashed tear lines, a totals block and a barcode at the foot.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/56.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            counter: #dcdad4, the counter top behind the receipts
            roll: #fbfbf8, the receipt paper
            print: #232323, text, barcodes, filled tags and buttons
            thermalGrey: #585858, meta lines, read items and labels
            faint: #bdbdb8, tear lines and dot leaders, decoration only
            fade: #ecece7, the open line item
            stamp: #9c1f3c, the dashed OPEN tag
        type:
            One monospace stack, ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas, DejaVu
            Sans Mono, Liberation Mono, monospace. The brand is 22px extra bold
            uppercase with 0.3em tracking. The Unread total is 16px extra bold.
            The message is 15px on a 1.6 line height. Line item heads are 14px
            bold uppercase, body lines 13px, and meta, tags and barcode digits
            11 to 12px.
        layout:
            Receipts stand side by side on the counter, centred, with a small
            uppercase line above naming the terminal and the operator. The
            list receipt is 360px wide. It has a boxed BW mark, the brand, two
            small header lines, a double rule, the Inbox heading, a two by two
            grid of filters as [x] and [ ] boxes with the active one printed in
            reverse, a tear line, six numbered line items, a tear line, totals
            for Items, Read and Unread, and a barcode with digits. Each line
            item has the number and kind, a dot leader and the time, then the
            sentence, the project and status tags. The item receipt is 420px
            wide with Item 01 of 06, a label and value block, the message with
            a thick left bar, three outlined option prints, a dashed reply
            field, full width Reply, Mark as done and Open task buttons, a
            barcode and Answer due Monday. Both receipts have zigzag torn ends.
            On a phone the receipts stack.
        spacing: 4px steps. 8px line item padding, 20px paper margins and 40px between receipts.
        density: Tight. A strip 360 to 420px wide, never wider.
        corners: Square, with zigzag torn ends at top and bottom drawn with gradients.
        borders: 2px dashed tear lines, 3px double rules under headers, 1px dotted lines between items, 2px solid button borders and a dashed reply field.
        shadows: One drop shadow under each receipt, 0 6px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.12).
        icons:
            Printed glyphs only. Filters use [x] and [ ]. Unread is a boxed
            star with UNREAD, done is a reverse block with a tick and DONE, and
            the open item has a dashed OPEN tag with an arrow. Barcodes are CSS
            stripes with a text alternative.
        focus: A 2px print outline offset 2px with a paper gap and a faint outer ring. A focused field turns its dashed border solid.
        tone: Till-roll uppercase, such as ITEM 01 OF 06, UNREAD 3 and ANSWER DUE MONDAY.

    style57:
        number: 57
        run: 12
        screen: Inbox
        name: Code editor light
        idea: The inbox opens like files in a light code editor, with a file tree for filters, tabs for open items, numbered lines and syntax colours that tell names, verbs, titles and times apart.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/57.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            chrome: #eceef2, the title bar, tab strip and activity bar
            side: #f5f6f8, the file tree and the reply panel
            editor: #ffffff, the editor panes
            selection: #e6eefc, the open line and the active file
            text: #24292f, default code text
            dim: #5c6570, breadcrumbs and inactive tabs
            function: #0a5bb5, person names, the primary button, links and focus
            keyword: #8a2bb5, verbs and the at mention
            string: #0f6e3a, quoted task titles and the done tag
            number: #a14a00, times and dates
            comment: #5f6b5a, projects and comment lines in italic
            error: #b42318, unread tags and the unread count
            status: #2d4b8a, the status bar with white text
        type:
            Code is ui-monospace, SF Mono, Cascadia Code, JetBrains Mono,
            Menlo, Consolas, DejaVu Sans Mono, monospace at 13px on a 1.6 line
            height. Priya's message alone is in system-ui at 15px on a 1.55
            line height. Breadcrumbs are 12px, tags 11px bold, and panel
            headings 11px semibold system-ui uppercase.
        layout:
            A window 1280px wide at most with a title bar of three grey dots,
            the app name, a command field reading Go to task, project or person
            and mara.okafor. Below sit a 44px activity bar of icons, a 220px
            Explorer tree with an inbox folder holding all, mentions, assigned
            and unread with 3 U, and the editor. The editor has tabs for
            inbox/all and hero-image-options with an unread dot, then two split
            panes. The left pane lists the inbox as numbered lines between a
            header comment and an end comment, each line reading name, verb,
            quoted title, project as a comment, time and tags. The right pane
            shows from and task lines, the message in a pale yellow note box,
            an attachments comment and three thumbnails with Option labels. A
            Reply panel under both panes has a prompt field and buttons with
            keyboard hints, and a blue status bar closes the window. Below
            1000px the tree becomes a strip of file links and the panes stack.
            Below 600px the activity bar turns into a top row.
        spacing: A 4px unit. 21px code lines, 12px pane gutters, 44px line number gutter.
        density: High. One notification per numbered line.
        corners: 8px on the window, 4px on note boxes and thumbnails, 3px on buttons, fields and tags.
        borders: 1px #d5d9e0 between every region, a 2px accent line on top of the active tab and at the left of the selected line.
        shadows: Only the window, 0 8px 24px rgba(30,40,60,0.12).
        icons:
            16px thin line icons with a 1.6 stroke, tinted by kind, orange for
            folders and blue for files. Tags are small outlined boxes, a dot
            with unread, a tick with done and a triangle with open. Buttons
            carry keyboard hints in small key boxes.
        focus: A 1px accent outline with a soft 3 to 4px accent ring. A focused field gets an accent border and the same ring.
        tone: Lowercase paths and code comments, such as inbox › all, // end of inbox and reply to Priya.

    style58:
        number: 58
        run: 12
        screen: Inbox
        name: Clinical
        idea: A calm records system in pale blue-green, where every fact sits under a careful small-caps label and every alert is gentle, boxed and marked by a symbol.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/58.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #eef6f5, the background
            surface: #ffffff, panels and fields
            band: #f6fbfa, the quoted message and row hover
            text: #17302e, body text and field values
            label: #4a6563, field labels and meta text
            line: #c8dcd9, panel borders, with #e1ecea for inner lines
            teal: #0e6763, the primary button, selection, links and focus
            tealSoft: #d9eeeb, the selected row and active nav item
            info: #1d5a8c text on #e8f1f9, the Unread tag and the mention symbol
            ok: #1f6b3d text on #e6f3ea, the Done tag and the completed symbol
            notice: #7a5100 text on #fbf3df, gentle alerts, the review symbol and the unread count
        type:
            Segoe UI, system-ui, -apple-system, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial,
            sans-serif. The page title is 24px semibold. The message is 17px on
            a 1.55 line height. Rows are 15px medium, bold when unread. Meta
            and times are 13px. Labels are 12px semibold uppercase with 0.05em
            tracking, and panel headings 13px semibold uppercase.
        layout:
            A white top bar with a teal outlined pulse mark, the brand, nav for
            Projects, Inbox and Reports, and Mara Okafor with Signed in at
            right. The page has the Inbox title with a short description and
            three bordered summary chips for items, unread and the reply
            requested by Monday. Below sit two panels, five to six. The left
            panel is titled Notifications with a segmented filter control and
            six rows, each with a 28px symbol disc, the sentence, status tags,
            a kind and project meta line and the time at right. The selected
            row has a teal left bar. The right panel shows the open mention
            with a four cell fact strip for From, Task, Project and Received, a
            gentle note with a clock symbol, the message as a quote with a teal
            left bar, three captioned thumbnails, a labelled reply field with
            a hint, and Reply, Mark as done and a quiet Open task link. Below
            960px the panels stack and the fact strip becomes two by two.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 12 by 16px row and field padding, 24px between panels.
        density: Medium. Two lines per notification and a four cell fact strip for the open item.
        corners: 8px on panels, 6px on buttons, fields, alerts and thumbnails, 4px on status tags, round symbol discs.
        borders: 1px #c8dcd9 on panels with #e1ecea inside, a 4px teal left bar on the selected row and the quote.
        shadows: None. Structure comes from borders and labels.
        icons:
            16px line icons with a 1.8 stroke inside 28px tinted discs, an at
            sign for mentions, a tick for completed, an eye in a square for a
            review request and plain grey discs for the rest. Tags pair a dot
            with Unread, a tick with Done and an eye with Viewing.
        focus: A 2px teal outline offset 2px with a 5px soft teal ring. A focused field gets a teal border and the same ring.
        tone: Careful and factual, such as Received, Your reply and Note. Priya asks for a choice by Monday.

    style59:
        number: 59
        run: 13
        screen: Calendar
        name: Botanical herbarium
        idea: Each day is a pressed-plant specimen sheet taped to parchment, its events written on small inked labels in a quiet museum hand.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/59.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            parchment: #efe8d4, the page background
            sheet: #fbf8ee, day sheets, the index panel, labels and the masthead
            ink: #2b2a1f, text, label borders, buttons and the selected view
            sepia: #635639, times, meta, Latin day names and sheet footers
            olive: #4b5626, the primary button, the today ring and the Team key
            oliveWash: #e3e5c8, the current week row and the focused field
            rust: #8a3b1e, Deadline labels and their pennant key
            slate: #4d5a63, Out of office labels and their crossed square key
            rule: #c7bb98, sheet edges and hairlines
            pencil: #b3aa86, the decorative plant drawings only
        type:
            Old style serif for almost everything, Iowan Old Style, Palatino
            Linotype, Palatino, Book Antiqua, Georgia, serif. Typewriter mono for
            times, eyebrows and sheet numbers, Courier New, Courier, monospace.
            Sizes are 34px regular for the week title with a 20px italic subtitle,
            22px regular day headings, 14px italic Latin day names, 15px semibold
            event titles, 13px mono times and 15px small caps section labels.
        layout:
            A thin masthead with a sprig mark, the wordmark in small caps, a text
            nav where the current item gets an ink underline and a fleuron, and a
            round double ring initials stamp for Mara. Below sit the eyebrow, the
            week title and the controls on one row. The week is a flowing grid of
            seven specimen sheets, about 210px minimum each, beside a 280px index
            panel on the right holding the month table, the calendar checkboxes
            and an out of office note. Each sheet has two strips of tape at the
            top, the day name and its Latin name, the event labels stacked, a
            faint pencil plant in the lower right and a footer reading Sheet 01
            and Coll. Brightwork. Below 1000px the index moves under the sheets,
            and below 640px the sheets stack in one column.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between sheets, 16 to 20px inside them, 10px between labels and 32px between areas.
        density: Airy. Seven sheets with at most two labels each, plenty of empty paper.
        corners: Square everywhere. Only the initials stamp and the today ring in the month are round.
        borders: 1px ink on labels and buttons, 1px rule on sheets. Deadlines use a 3px double rust rule and out of office a dashed slate rule. The today sheet gets an inset olive double line.
        shadows: One flat paper offset of 2px 3px with no blur in sepia at 12 percent. Translucent tan tape strips sit over the top edge.
        icons:
            Fine ink line icons at text size with a 1.4 stroke. A leaf marks Team,
            a pennant marks Deadline and a crossed square marks Out of office,
            always beside the word. Large pencil plant drawings decorate each
            sheet and carry no meaning.
        focus: A 2px dashed ink outline offset 3px. A focused field also gains the olive wash.
        tone: Calm and catalogue-like, such as Collected this week, Nothing scheduled and Sheet 04.

    style60:
        number: 60
        run: 13
        screen: Calendar
        name: Watercolour
        idea: Events bloom as soft watercolour washes on warm paper, with handwritten headings and no hard lines, so the week feels painted rather than ruled.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/60.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            paper: #fdfbf7, the page, with faint blue, rose and sage blooms in the corners
            ink: #2f3640, text and event titles
            washGrey: #545c68, meta, hour labels and day names
            indigo: #2e4a7a, the primary button, the today ring, checkboxes and focus
            ceruleanWash: #6ea0d2, Team events and the current nav item at 35 to 60 percent
            sageWash: #8cb68c, longer team sessions and the month card
            ochreWash: #e4b860, Deadline events and the brand blot
            lilacWash: #aa96d2, Out of office events and the avatar
            roseWash: #e28c96, the page corner bloom only
            pencilLine: #e8e1d6, faint hour rules
        type:
            Handwritten headings in Segoe Print, Bradley Hand, Chalkboard SE,
            Marker Felt, Comic Sans MS, cursive. Body in a soft humanist sans,
            Avenir Next, Avenir, Segoe UI, Nunito, Ubuntu, system-ui, sans-serif.
            Sizes are 36px hand for the week title, 24px hand day numbers, 20px
            hand panel headings, 13.5px bold event titles, 15px body and 12px meta
            with tabular figures.
        layout:
            A light top row with the handwritten brand on an ochre blot, a text
            nav where the current item sits on a blue wash, and Mara on the right.
            The title row holds the week title and the controls. A 250px left
            column holds the month card on a sage wash, the calendar checkboxes
            and a dotted note about Lena. The main area is a true time grid with a
            52px hour gutter and seven day columns, an all day row, then sixteen
            half hour rows of 44px from 09 to 17 hours. Events sit in their slots
            and grow taller when their text needs it. Below 1100px the side column
            moves under the week, and below 820px the grid becomes an agenda list
            with each day heading followed by its washes.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 6px between day columns, 44px per half hour, 28 to 32px between areas.
        density: Relaxed. The full working day is shown and events are sized by their length.
        corners: Irregular blob radii such as 30 40 36 44 percent, never a perfect circle or rectangle.
        borders: None. Wash edges come from an SVG turbulence displacement filter on the wash layer only, never on text.
        shadows: Only under the primary button and the selected view, soft and pooled below.
        icons:
            Hand-drawn 1.8 stroke line shapes at 13 to 18px. A circle marks Team,
            an hourglass marks Deadline and a crescent marks Out of office, each
            beside its word.
        focus: A 3px indigo outline at 55 percent offset 3px with softly rounded corners. A focused field turns white with a 2px indigo ring.
        tone: Gentle and personal, such as November, week one and A blank page today.

    style61:
        number: 61
        run: 13
        screen: Calendar
        name: Mid-century modern
        idea: A 1950s hi-fi console of a calendar, with walnut, mustard and teal, starbursts and boomerangs, and each day as a long rounded lane along an hour dial.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/61.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            cream: #f4ecd8, the page
            card: #fffaf0, day lanes, the console band and the style sheet
            walnut: #5a3a22, the top bar, borders, the view switch and the console ledge
            teal: #1d6b67, the primary button, event duration bars and the today lane border
            tealTint: #cfe6e1, the current week row in the month
            mustard: #e2a72e, the selected nav item and view, the starburst and the focus outline
            mustardTint: #f8e4b5, deadline chips
            tomato: #b4432a, deadline chip borders and the starburst key
            ink: #2a2118, text
            muted: #6b5a48, labels, times and the hour ruler
        type:
            Rounded geometric sans throughout, Futura, Century Gothic, Avenir
            Next, URW Gothic, Trebuchet MS, sans-serif. Sizes are 32px bold for the
            week title, 34px bold day numbers, 13px bold uppercase labels with
            0.2em tracking, 14px bold event titles and 13px body. Nav and view
            labels are uppercase with wide tracking.
        layout:
            A walnut top bar with a mustard and teal starburst mark, the spaced
            uppercase wordmark, pill nav with the current item in mustard and a
            boomerang outline drifting off the right edge. Below come the week
            title and the controls. The side panel becomes a console band across
            the page in three parts, the month table, the calendar checkboxes as
            cream pills, and an away card for Lena with a boomerang medallion. The
            week is seven horizontal lanes, a 150px day label on the left and a
            lane marked every hour from 09 to 17 hours under a shared ruler. All
            day items are chips at the top of a lane. Each timed event is a teal
            bar exactly as long as the event, with its time, title and people
            beneath, aligned right for late events. Below 760px the console stacks
            and each lane becomes a plain list with short bars as bullets.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 10px between lanes, 18 to 24px inside panels and 32px between areas.
        density: Medium. One lane per day about 104px tall.
        corners: Full pills for controls and chips. Lanes alternate 18px and 60px corners like a boomerang, event bars use 12px and 2px.
        borders: 2px walnut on secondary buttons, fields and the console, dotted 2px tan dividers inside the console. Deadline chips have a 2px tomato border and out of office chips a 2px dashed walnut border.
        shadows: Hard offsets only. A 4px mustard offset under the primary button and a walnut ledge under the console.
        icons:
            Solid filled shapes at text size. A dot marks Team, a four point
            starburst marks Deadline and a boomerang marks Out of office, each
            with its word. Today in the month is a mustard starburst.
        focus: A 3px mustard outline offset 2px with a 6px dark walnut halo.
        tone: Breezy and period, such as The week ahead, Calendars on air and Nothing on the dial.

    style62:
        number: 62
        run: 13
        screen: Calendar
        name: Art nouveau
        idea: The week as seven arched gallery windows inside a gilded frame, with whiplash flourishes, a lancet side panel and soft greens and golds.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/62.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            paleSage: #eef0e4, the page around the frame
            ivory: #fbfaf2, the frame, windows and fields
            forest: #23402e, text, the primary button and the today window border
            moss: #4a634a, labels, people and day names
            oldGold: #806217, times, the outer frame line and focus
            gilt: #c3a250, ornaments and inner rules only
            goldLeaf: #f3ead0, the selected view, the lancet glow and the focus halo
            plum: #6b2d4a, Deadline entries on #f6ecf0
            dusk: #3e5566, Out of office entries
        type:
            Display high contrast serif for headings, numerals and entry titles,
            Didot, Bodoni 72, Bodoni MT, Big Caslon, Cochin, Baskerville, Georgia,
            serif. Body in a flared humanist sans, Optima, Candara, Segoe UI, Noto
            Sans, Gill Sans, sans-serif. Sizes are 30px for the week title with a
            15px italic subtitle, 36px day numerals, 17px entry titles, 12px
            uppercase day names with 0.1em tracking, 13px italic people and 12px
            bold gold times.
        layout:
            The whole screen sits in an ivory frame with a double gold rule and
            whiplash corner ornaments. A centred masthead shows the spaced
            uppercase wordmark between two whiplash flourishes, a centred
            uppercase nav with fleurons around the current item, and Mara at the
            top right. The week title and controls sit between two gilt rules. A
            230px lancet panel on the left, arched at the top, holds the month,
            the calendar checkboxes and the away note. The week is seven tall
            arched windows in one row, each with the day name, a large numeral, a
            small ornament and its entries centred and divided by gilt rules. The
            today window has a thicker forest border, a gold leaf glow and a
            Today ribbon. Below 1240px the windows wrap, below 900px the lancet
            moves under them, and below 640px the windows stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 14px between windows, about 44px arch headroom, 12px between entries and 32px between areas.
        density: Ceremonial. Seven tall windows and centred, generously spaced entries.
        corners: Semi elliptical arch tops on windows and the lancet. Buttons and fields use leaf corners of 20px and 4px.
        borders: Double rules everywhere, a 1.5px old gold line with a 1px gilt line inset 5 to 8px. Deadline entries get a plum line and an arched top, out of office a dashed dusk line.
        shadows: None. Depth comes from inset double rules and the gold leaf gradient.
        icons:
            Botanical line icons at text size with a 1.5 stroke. A four petal
            flower marks Team, a diamond marks Deadline and an arched door marks
            Out of office, each with its word. Today in the month is a filled
            forest seal.
        focus: A 2px old gold outline offset 3px with a 6px gold leaf halo.
        tone: Formal and graceful, such as The Week of the Second of November and A quiet day, nothing planned.

    style63:
        number: 63
        run: 13
        screen: Calendar
        name: Psychedelic 60s
        idea: A warm concert poster of a week, with swirling orange, magenta and yellow waves, bubble lettering and an op-art medallion, while the event cards stay plain and easy to read.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/63.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            peachPage: #fff1d6, the page
            cream: #fffaf0, day cards, boxes and pills
            plum: #3a1030, text, all outlines and the selected nav and view
            duskyPlum: #6e3a5a, times and meta
            magenta: #b0125b, the primary button and the today card shadow
            sunshine: #ffd23f, the poster base, the Team badge and the focus halo
            orange: #e8590c, bubble letter shadows, waves and medallion rings
            bubblegum: #ffd0e4, the today card
            tangerine: #ffd9b0, the current week row and the Deadline badge
            burntOrange: #a63600, Deadline text and dashed borders
            violet: #5b2a86, Out of office text and dotted borders
        type:
            Bubble display for headings and day numbers, Cooper Black, Cooper Std,
            Arial Rounded MT Bold, Bookman Old Style, URW Bookman, Georgia, serif,
            in plum with a 3px yellow then 6px orange offset text shadow. Body in
            Trebuchet MS, Segoe UI, Lucida Grande, Verdana, sans-serif. Sizes are
            64px bubble for the poster title, 44px bubble day numbers, 24px bubble
            box headings, 18px bold day names, 16px bold event titles, 16px body
            and 14px bold times.
        layout:
            A full width poster header on sunshine yellow with four stacked wavy
            bands in light orange, orange, pink and yellow, closed by a wavy plum
            edge. On it sit cream pill chips for the brand, the nav and Mara, the
            big bubble title, the dates in a pill and the controls. Below, a 320px
            left column holds a round op-art medallion of concentric orange,
            yellow and magenta rings with the month table on a cream disc, then a
            Tune in box with the checkboxes and a Far out box about Lena. The
            week is two staggered columns of day cards zigzagging down either side
            of a striped centre ribbon, each event on its own white rounded card
            with a round badge icon. Below 1060px the side column moves above in a
            row, and below 720px the days stack in one column beside a thin stripe.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between cards, a 40px gutter around the centre stripe and 18 to 20px card padding.
        density: Loose and loud. Two staggered columns with roomy cards.
        corners: Big and lopsided. Day cards alternate 48px and 16px corners, events are 20px and controls are full pills.
        borders: Thick plum outlines, 3px on cards and controls and 2px on events. Deadline borders are dashed burnt orange, out of office dotted violet.
        shadows: Hard offsets only, 4px plum under the primary button and 6px magenta under the today card.
        icons:
            Chunky filled shapes in 30px round badges. A four petal flower marks
            Team, a lightning bolt marks Deadline and rainbow arcs mark Out of
            office, with the word shown for deadlines and absences. Today is a
            plum dot with a double ring.
        focus: A 4px plum outline offset 3px with a 10px sunshine halo.
        tone: Playful and warm, such as Groovy week ahead, Tune in, Far out and Free and easy.

    style64:
        number: 64
        run: 14
        screen: Onboarding
        name: Picture book
        idea: The setup reads like a children's picture book, with crayon drawings, wobbly hand-cut boxes and big friendly words across a two-page spread.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/64.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            paper: #fff8e1, the page behind the book, with a faint dotted grain
            page: #fffdf4, the open book and the style sheet card
            ink: #2b2118, text and every outline
            pencil: #5c5047, field labels, hints and page numbers
            crayonBlue: #1f4fbf, the Continue button, links and the focus outline
            crayonRed: #c8231b, the You are here and Still writing words and the title underline
            crayonGreen: #1e7b34, the done step and the Added sticker
            crayonYellow: #ffd84d, the seat sticky note, heading highlights and the current star
            orange: #f08a24, sun rays and faces, as fill only
            sky: #cfe6ff, role tags and the Copy invite link button
        type:
            A rounded hand font, Comic Sans MS, Chalkboard SE, Comic Neue, Segoe
            Print, Bradley Hand, Marker Felt, then Trebuchet MS and Verdana. The
            heading is 52px bold at 1.05 line height. The lead line is 21px,
            body is 18px at 1.55, buttons are 20 to 22px bold, and labels are
            15px in pencil grey. Everything is sentence case.
        layout:
            A small top line with a sun logo on the left and a smiling face with
            Hello, Mara Okafor on the right. Below it the screen is an open book
            in a two to three column split with a soft gutter shadow in the
            middle. The left page has a tilted yellow Step 2 of 4 label, a
            crayon drawing of Mara on a hill waving to three stick friends, and
            the four steps as a vertical list of stepping stones. The right page
            has the big heading with a red crayon underline, the line, the
            invites as hand-cut cards, the seat note as a tilted sticky note,
            Copy invite link, then Back, a wavy underlined Skip for now and a
            big Continue at the far right. Small page 2 and page 3 numbers sit
            at the bottom corners. Below 900px the pages stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 32px page padding, 16px between invite cards, 24px between groups.
        density: Very loose. One idea per line, with words big enough to read aloud.
        corners:
            Wobbly elliptical radii, 255px 18px 225px 18px over 18px 225px 18px
            255px, and a second mirrored set, so no two boxes match. Cards are
            rotated by half a degree, the sticky note by about one degree.
        borders: 3px solid ink on every box. Things not done yet use a 3px dashed ink border.
        shadows: One flat offset of 4px 5px with no blur at 18 percent ink, on the book, the note and Continue.
        icons:
            Hand-drawn inline SVG passed through a turbulence displacement
            filter for crayon wobble, with a second grain filter giving waxy
            fills. A green tick disc marks done, a yellow star marks the
            current step, and dashed numbered ovals mark later steps. Added
            shows a green crayon tick and the typed row shows a yellow pencil.
            Seats are five little people, three filled red and two dashed.
        focus: A 4px dashed crayon blue outline offset 4px. A focused field turns its 3px underline blue.
        tone: Cheerful and short, such as You are here, Still writing, Coming up and Done, gold star.

    style65:
        number: 65
        run: 14
        screen: Onboarding
        name: Vaporwave pastel
        idea: Retro computer windows float over a pastel sunset with a pink grid horizon, a striped sun and a marble bust, so setup feels like a dreamy 1990s desktop.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/65.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            skyPink: #ffd6ec, the top of the sky gradient
            hotPastel: #ff9ed2, title bar start, the Continue button and horizon grid lines
            cyan: #bff3ff, the seat note and icon fills
            cyanDeep: #7fe3f7, title bar end, the Copy invite link button and the focus glow
            lavender: #e7dcff, secondary buttons, the list header and the current step
            window: #fbf7ff, window bodies
            bevel: #9b84c4, the dark edge of every bevel
            ink: #2d1747, text and window frames
            plum: #5a3d7a, meta text, labels and line art
            mintInk: #0f6b5c, the Done and Added words
            magentaInk: #b0186e, the Running now and Typing words and the eyebrow
            grape: #6a2c91, progress blocks, used seats and links
        type:
            Tahoma, Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif for the interface at 15px with
            1.5 line height. The heading uses Arial Black, Gadget, Verdana at
            38px weight 900 with 6 percent tracking, and a cyan 3px and pink
            minus 2px offset text shadow. Title bars are 13px bold. The eyebrow
            and section labels are 12px bold caps with 35 percent tracking. A
            decorative line of spaced katakana sits under the heading.
        layout:
            A full width scene with a pink to lavender to cyan sky, a striped
            sun in the middle, a pink perspective grid floor in the lower
            third, a simple marble bust with tinted shades bottom left and a
            cyan palm bottom right. On top sits a slim beveled taskbar with the
            brand and Mara Okafor. Below it two windows, a 280px setup.progress
            window with a segmented block meter and the four steps, and a wide
            invite_team.exe window with the eyebrow, heading, line, a list view
            with Email, Role and Status columns, the seat note, then Copy
            invite link left and Back, Skip for now and Continue right. Below
            900px the windows stack and the bust shrinks.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px window padding, 32px between windows, 8px list cell padding.
        density: Medium. Invites sit in a file manager style list view with column headers.
        corners: Square everywhere. The sun is the only circle.
        borders:
            A 2px ink frame on windows, buttons and fields, plus a 2px bevel
            with white on the top left and #9b84c4 on the bottom right. Fields
            and the list are sunken with a lavender inner shadow. The seat note
            has a 2px dashed ink border.
        shadows: A flat 8px 8px offset with no blur in magenta at 22 percent behind every window.
        icons:
            Chunky 16 to 20px glyphs with 2px ink outlines and pastel fills. A
            ticked square marks done, a pink play triangle marks the current
            step and dashed squares mark queued steps. Added shows a tick, and
            Typing shows three fading bars. Window buttons are tiny beveled
            boxes and arrows are text triangles.
        focus: A 2px dotted ink outline offset 2px plus a 5px cyan glow ring.
        tone: Computer speak with a wink, such as setup.progress, invite_team.exe, Running now and Queued.

    style66:
        number: 66
        run: 14
        screen: Onboarding
        name: Isometric
        idea: Progress is built as a staircase of isometric blocks drawn at 30 degrees, and every card, row and button is a flat shaded slab with a visible bottom face.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/66.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            ground: #eef2f8, the page, with faint indigo grid lines at 30 and 150 degrees
            top: #ffffff, top faces, the main slab and fields
            side: #dfe6f1, left faces and row bottom faces
            edge: #c3cee0, right faces and the slab bottom face
            indigoTop: #8f9bff, the current platform top and the typed row edge
            indigo: #4f5fe0, the Continue button, links and the focus outline
            indigoDeep: #3a48b8, button bottom faces and the Building word
            tealTop: #3fd0ac, the finished platform top
            teal: #147a61, the Built and Added words
            amber: #f2a93b, teammate figures and the brand cube
            ink: #1d2433, headings and body
            muted: #556074, labels, the line and dashed outlines
            rose: #b8325f, the Typing word
        type:
            Avenir Next, Avenir, Century Gothic, Futura, Segoe UI, system-ui. The
            heading is 40px bold with minus 2.5 percent tracking. The lead line
            is 17px in muted, body is 15px at 1.55 with emails at weight 600,
            step names are 14px bold, and labels are 11 to 12px bold caps with
            12 to 18 percent tracking.
        layout:
            A plain top line with an amber cube logo and Mara Okafor beside a
            teal cube. Below, a two column stage. The left column has a small
            caps eyebrow, then an SVG illustration of four isometric platforms
            on a grey base rising from front left to back right. The first is
            teal with a red flag, the second is indigo with three small block
            people, and the last two are white with dashed tops. Under it the
            four steps sit in a four column row with a coloured left rule. The
            right column is one white slab with the heading, line, invite rows,
            the seat note, Copy invite link, then Back, Skip for now and
            Continue. Below 960px the columns stack, and below 560px the steps
            become a two by two grid.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 40px slab padding, 12px between rows, 48px between illustration and slab.
        density: Airy. Half the screen is illustration and the form holds only what the step needs.
        corners: Nearly square at 3 to 4px. Isometric faces are true parallelograms.
        borders: None on surfaces. Only planned things get a dashed 1.5px muted outline. The typed row has a 2px indigo inset ring.
        shadows:
            A solid bottom face instead of blur, 10px of #c3cee0 under the slab,
            5px under buttons and 4px under rows. The slab also has a soft 40px
            drop below. Buttons press down by 5px when active.
        icons:
            Built on a hexagon, the outline of a cube seen from its corner. An
            outlined hexagon with a tick means done or added, a filled hexagon
            with a play mark means building, and a dashed hexagon means planned.
            Avatars are three tone cubes, and seats are three solid indigo cubes
            and two dashed wireframe cubes. Line icons are 18px with a 1.8 stroke.
        focus: A 3px solid indigo outline offset 3px. A focused field gets a white fill, an indigo underline and a 2px indigo inset ring.
        tone: Calm builder words, such as Built, Building and Planned.

    style67:
        number: 67
        run: 14
        screen: Onboarding
        name: Flat long-shadow
        idea: Solid bright fields and big circles, with long 45 degree shadows trailing off every icon and the headline, straight out of 2013 flat design.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/67.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            cloud: #ecf0f1, the page, fields, role tags and secondary buttons
            white: #ffffff, the invite panel and text on colour
            asphalt: #2c3e50, text, the top bar and used seats
            concrete: #5d6d7e, labels and role tag text
            sea: #107f6e, the hero band
            seaDeep: #0c6a5c, long shadows and status chips in the hero
            orange: #e67e22, the current step circle and the typed row underline
            pumpkin: #a84300, the Continue button and the Typing chip
            sun: #f1c40f, the seat note and the focus ring
            green: #1e8449, the Added chip
            blue: #2a6fb0, links, the copy icon and an avatar
            violet: #8e44ad, avatars
        type:
            Helvetica Neue, Segoe UI, Lato, Helvetica, Arial. The heading is 60px
            weight 300 with the first word in 700, white on the sea band, with a
            40 step text shadow trailing 1px at a time to the bottom right in
            #0c6a5c. The lead line is 20px weight 300, rows are 18px, step names
            are 17px weight 600, and chips are 13px bold caps with 8 to 14
            percent tracking.
        layout:
            A slim asphalt top bar with an orange circle logo and Mara Okafor in
            a violet circle. Then a full width sea band with Step 2 of 4 in caps,
            the big heading, and a row of four big circles with names and status
            chips underneath. Done is a white circle with a teal tick, the
            current step is a larger orange circle with two people, and later
            steps are white rings with thin numbers. Below, a centred white
            panel 880px wide holds the line, the invite rows with 64px initial
            circles, a full width yellow seat band, a Copy invite link circle
            button, then Back, Skip for now and Continue. Below 820px the circles
            form a two by two grid.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 48px panel padding, 16px row padding, 40px between blocks.
        density: Sparse and poster like. Big circles carry the progress.
        corners: Square blocks and chips, 3px on buttons, and perfect circles for icons, avatars and remove buttons.
        borders: None, except 2px cloud row dividers and a 4px orange underline on the row being typed.
        shadows:
            No blur anywhere. Long shadows only, a 45 degree band at 20 percent
            black clipped inside each circle and starting at the icon, plus the
            stepped headline shadow.
        icons:
            Solid white glyphs centred in flat circles, each casting a long
            shadow to the bottom right. Status chips are solid colour blocks
            with a white tick for Added and a white pen for Typing. Seats are
            three filled asphalt dots and two asphalt rings.
        focus: A 4px sun yellow outline with a 3px asphalt ring outside it.
        tone: Short and upbeat, with status in caps, such as Done, Now, Next and Later.

    style68:
        number: 68
        run: 14
        screen: Onboarding
        name: Nautical
        idea: A ship's setup log in navy, white and signal red, framed in rope, with numeral pennants hoisted on a halyard as the step markers and a compass rose behind the form.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/68.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            sailcloth: #f7f5ef, the page
            white: #ffffff, the log card, fields and the current step
            navy: #13294b, text, the header, table rules and secondary buttons
            seaGrey: #4a5a72, labels, the lead line and later step words
            signalRed: #b3121f, the Continue button, the eyebrow, the current step word and the focus outline
            ropeLight: #e0c38f, the light strand of the rope frame
            rope: #b8935a, the middle strand and the halyard
            ropeDark: #7a5a2e, the dark strand, halyard rings and the frame edge
            brass: #8a6a1f, the seat plaque border and porthole rims
            flagBlue: #1f4f9c, pennant fills
        type:
            Headings use Stencil, Stencil Std, Impact, Haettenschweiler, Arial
            Narrow Bold in caps with 8 percent tracking, 46px on the screen and
            34px in the sheet. Body uses Gill Sans, Gill Sans MT, Calibri,
            Trebuchet MS at 16px with 1.55 line height and the lead line at 18px
            in sea grey. Labels, table heads, chips and buttons are 11 to 14px
            bold caps with 14 to 24 percent tracking.
        layout:
            A navy header with an anchor and the brand in spaced caps, Mara
            Okafor in a white ring, and a thin white, red, white stripe below.
            Then a two column harbour. The left 300px mast has a caps label and
            a vertical rope halyard with four numeral pennants hoisted on it,
            each with the step name and a status word, the current one on a
            white panel. The right column is a rope framed white card with a
            faint compass rose in the top right corner, the eyebrow, the stencil
            heading, the line, the invites as a ruled manifest table with Email,
            Role and Status columns, a brass seat plaque, Copy invite link, then
            Back, Skip for now and Continue. Below 900px the pennants move above
            the card in two columns, and below 600px the table rows stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 40px card padding, 12px table cells, 40px between mast and card.
        density: Moderate. The invites read as a ruled manifest table.
        corners: 18px on the rope frame, 10px on the card inside it, 2px on buttons and fields, and round portholes and remove buttons.
        borders:
            A 10px rope frame made of repeating diagonal light, middle and dark
            strands. Tables have double 3px navy rules at top and bottom and
            dashed 1px rows. Buttons and fields have 2px navy borders and the
            field being typed turns red.
        shadows: None, except a 2px dark rope edge under the frame.
        icons:
            International numeral pennants as step markers. One is white with a
            red ball, two is blue with a white ball, three is red, white and
            blue bands, and four is red with a white cross. Status icons are 2px
            navy lines, a ringed tick for done and added, a raised triangle for
            flying, a dashed ring for not yet and a quill for writing. Seats are
            brass portholes, three with a person and two empty.
        focus: A 3px signal red outline offset 3px. A focused field turns its border red.
        tone: Crisp caps labels with a light sea flavour, such as Flying now and Writing, while the screen words stay plain.

    style69:
        number: 69
        run: 15
        screen: TodayMobile
        name: Boarding pass
        idea: Every meeting is a line on a departure board and every task a paper ticket with a torn-off stub, so the day reads like a travel itinerary.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/69.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            tarmac: #e7e9ec, the page behind the tickets and the round notch cut-outs
            ticket: #fffdf8, ticket bodies, the header pass and the nav strip
            stub: #f3efe4, the tear-off stub on the right of each ticket
            navyInk: #15233f, text, the header band, gate signs and the Due today stamp
            slate: #4d5a70, field captions and the Upcoming stamp
            perforation: #9aa3b2, dashed tear lines, decorative only
            signalOrange: #b23c0c, the add button, the priority tag, the badge and focus
            board: #1b2433, the departure board panel for meetings
            flap: #f6f3e8, split-flap digit tiles on the board
            clearedGreen: #1d6b45, the Done stamp with a tick
            delayRed: #a8201a, the Overdue stamp with a triangle and the overdue ticket ring
        type:
            Two families. Condensed sans is Arial Narrow, Roboto Condensed,
            Helvetica Neue, Arial, sans-serif, used for names, headings and
            caps captions. Monospace is ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo,
            Consolas, monospace, used for codes, counts, times and field values.
            Body falls back to system-ui. Sizes are 26px bold mono for the
            manifest counts, 20px bold mono gate codes, 18px bold condensed caps
            for header values, 17px bold condensed task names, 15px bold mono on
            flap tiles, 13px bold mono field values and 10px bold condensed caps
            captions with 0.14em tracking.
        layout:
            A single phone column up to 400px wide centred on the tarmac grey
            with generous space around it. The header is a boarding pass with a
            navy band holding a paper plane mark, the brand in spaced caps and
            the avatar, then Passenger and Date fields and a route line reading
            6 TSK to 2 MTG with a small plane, plus the line 6 tasks, 2
            meetings. Each section opens with a navy gate sign, a dashed rule
            and a two digit count. Meetings sit in a dark departure board table
            with split-flap time digits, the name in caps and a Next or Later
            remark. Each task is a ticket with a flight number such as BW 101,
            the name, and Project and Due fields, joined by a dashed perforation
            with round notches to a 92px stub showing the gate code and a status
            stamp. The bottom bar is a ticket strip with a dashed top edge, four
            tabs and a raised round orange add button in the middle.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 12px between tickets, 12 to 14px ticket padding, 28px before each gate sign.
        density: Medium. About five tickets fit on one phone screen.
        corners: 10 to 14px on tickets, the header and the board, 2 to 3px on stamps and gate signs, round avatar and add button.
        borders: 2px dashed perforations between ticket and stub. Stamps use 1.5 to 2px outlines. The overdue ticket gets a 2px red ring.
        shadows: A 1px hard bottom edge in #c9ced6 plus 0 4px 10px navy at 8 percent, like paper on a desk.
        icons:
            2px stroke line icons with square ends at 22px in the nav. A paper
            plane is the brand mark. Status stamps pair a word with a filled
            dot for Due today, a hollow ring for Upcoming, a tick for Done and a
            triangle for Overdue. The done stamp is tilted six degrees and the
            done name is struck through.
        focus: A 3px signal orange outline offset 2px on buttons, fields and rows.
        tone: Travel words as short caps labels, such as Passenger, Gate, Departures and Boarding. Task names stay plain sentence case.

    style70:
        number: 70
        run: 15
        screen: TodayMobile
        name: Spreadsheet
        idea: The Today list is a live worksheet with lettered columns, numbered rows, a formula bar showing the selected cell and sheet tabs for navigation.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/70.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            desk: #eceef1, the page around the workbook
            cell: #ffffff, every cell and the active tab
            gridline: #d3d7dd, 1px cell borders, decorative only
            header: #f1f2f4, column letters, row numbers, bars and tabs, with #4a5260 text
            text: #1c2129, cell values, with muted #555e6c for project lines
            selectionTeal: #0b6e74, the selected cell border and handle, the active tab, the add button and focus
            selectionFill: #e3f2f2, inside the selected cell, with #cfe6e6 on its column and row headers
            todayFill: #fff3c4, Due today status cells with #6e4a00 text
            overdueFill: #fde2e0, the Overdue cell with #9e1c14 text, also the High flag and badge
            doneFill: #e1f1e4, the Done cell with #1f6130 text
        type:
            System sans, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial,
            sans-serif, at 13px with 1.35 line height for cells. The title row
            is 17px bold, task names 13px semibold, project lines 12px muted
            and section bands 11px bold caps. Times, durations, the name box
            and the formula use ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas at 12px, right
            aligned for numbers. Column letters and row numbers are 11 to 12px
            centred.
        layout:
            A phone-width workbook up to 390px with a 1px grey frame, centred
            on the desk. From the top come a title bar with a teal grid file
            icon, Brightwork and Today.sheet, and a square teal avatar. Then a
            toolbar with All, Due today and Overdue filter toggles, Sort and a
            filter icon. Then a formula bar with the name box B9, an italic fx
            and a TASK formula for the selected task. The grid has a row number
            column and columns A, B and C, with a sliver of column D on wide
            screens. Row 1 merges into the title Monday 2 November, row 2 holds
            6 tasks, 2 meetings with a COUNT formula hint, then a Meetings band,
            a header row Time, Meeting, Length and two meeting rows. A Tasks
            band follows with header row Due, Task and project, Status, and six
            task rows where the project wraps under the name in the same cell.
            Cell B9 is selected. A status bar sums the selection, and sheet tabs
            Today, Projects, Inbox and Me with a square teal add button form the
            bottom bar.
        spacing: A 4px unit. Cells pad 4px by 6px. Nothing has gaps, everything butts against gridlines.
        density: High. All eight items and every header fit on one phone screen.
        corners: Square everywhere, 2px at most on buttons, the badge and the avatar.
        borders: 1px gridlines on every cell. The selected cell has a 2px teal border and a small square fill handle at its bottom right corner, and its column letter and row number turn teal and bold.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            Small square-ended line icons from 11 to 18px. Status cells use a
            conditional fill plus a word and a shape, a filled dot for Due
            today, a ring for Upcoming, a tick for Done and a triangle for
            Overdue. High priority is a small red flag with the word High.
        focus: A 2px teal outline drawn inside the cell or field, like a cell selection.
        tone: Terse and literal like column headers, such as Due, Task, Status and Length.

    style71:
        number: 71
        run: 15
        screen: TodayMobile
        name: Cartographic
        idea: The day is drawn as a survey map on contour-lined paper, with tasks as stops along a dashed route, meetings as waypoints and a legend for every marker.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/71.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            land: #f2f0e4, the page outside the map
            surveyPaper: #fbfaf3, the map sheet, cards and the legend
            contour: #cfd3b4, contour lines, decorative only
            water: #d6e7ec, the lake shape, the avatar and the active nav disc
            surveyInk: #24301f, text, frames and the compass
            moss: #545d48, meta text and upcoming rings
            boundary: #7d8466, card and field borders
            routeRed: #b0331f, the route line, the overdue triangle, the add button and focus
            pinBlue: #1e5a7a, due today pins and meeting diamonds
            forest: #2f6b3a, the done flag and tick
        type:
            Serif italic Georgia, Iowan Old Style, Palatino Linotype, serif for
            place-like names, 26px for the date, 15px for project and meeting
            names. Humanist sans Gill Sans, Gill Sans MT, Optima, Candara,
            Segoe UI, system-ui for everything else, with 16px semibold task
            names, 20px semibold tabular meeting times, 13px meta, and 10 to
            12px semibold caps labels tracked 0.24 to 0.36em.
        layout:
            A framed map sheet up to 400px wide centred on the land colour, with
            a double frame. Faint contour lines, a pale lake shape and a dotted
            survey grid fill the background. A title cartouche with a double
            frame holds the brand, the date, 6 tasks, 2 meetings and a round
            avatar with a dashed ring. A scale bar reading 1 day and a small
            compass rose follow. Waypoints shows the two meetings as side by
            side cards with a diamond, time, name and length. The route lists
            the six tasks with a 36px marker column joined by a dashed red line
            and a card for each stop. A legend box explains every marker, then
            the bottom bar sits under a rule with a raised round red add button.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 8px between stops, 10px between waypoint cards, 24px before region labels.
        density: Medium. Each stop is two short lines.
        corners: Square frames and cards. The avatar, badge, add button and pill buttons are round.
        borders: 1px boundary lines on cards. The map and cartouche have double frames with a 3 to 4px gap. The overdue card gets a 2px route red border.
        shadows: None. Depth comes from frames and the contour paper.
        icons:
            Map markers show status by shape, a blue teardrop pin for Due today,
            a hollow ring for Upcoming, a green flag for Done and a red triangle
            with an exclamation mark for Overdue. Meetings use blue diamonds.
            Every marker also has a word beside it. Nav icons are thin 1.6
            stroke map symbols such as a compass and a folded map.
        focus: A 2px dashed route red outline offset 3px.
        tone: Gentle surveyor words for headings, such as Waypoints, The route and Legend. Item text stays plain.

    style72:
        number: 72
        run: 15
        screen: TodayMobile
        name: Lab instrument
        idea: The phone becomes a bench instrument with a screwed chassis, inset readouts on graph paper, tasks logged as labelled samples and meetings plotted on a time axis.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/72.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            bench: #dfe3e1, the page around the device
            chassis: #eef0ee, the device body and panel headers
            graph: #f8fbf7, readout and panel paper and fields
            gridMajor: #c5d8cb, major graph lines every 40px, decorative only
            gridMinor: #e2ece5, minor graph lines every 8px, decorative only
            ink: #1a2626, text, axes and readout figures
            graphite: #4b5a59, engraved labels, units and the Queued flag
            bezel: #8d9896, panel, sample and field edges
            traceGreen: #0b6e4f, the add key, primary button, Done and the power light
            probeBlue: #0e5f86, Due today, meeting blocks and focus
            alarmRed: #b02a1e, Overdue with a cross, the hatched sample tab and the badge
            caution: #f5c542, the High priority tag with #4a3500 text
        type:
            Monospace ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Cascadia Mono, Menlo,
            Consolas for every value, 26px bold readout counts with small unit
            letters, 20px bold for the date, 16px bold meeting times and 11 to
            12px meta with units and deltas. Engineering sans DIN Alternate,
            Bahnschrift, Segoe UI, Helvetica Neue, Arial for names and labels,
            15px semibold task names and 9 to 11px heavy caps engraved labels
            tracked 0.18 to 0.2em.
        layout:
            A device body up to 396px centred on the bench, with four corner
            screws. An engraved plate holds a green power light, Brightwork,
            Daily analyser and a square avatar. Below it an inset readout shows
            Run date Monday 2 November and large Tasks 6 and Meetings 2 counts,
            with 6 tasks, 2 meetings as a small line. Two graph-paper panels
            follow. Scheduled runs has a time axis plot from 8 to 16 h with the
            two meetings as blocks, then two run rows with time, name and a
            delta length. Samples has a due date plot with error bars, a now
            line and one marker per sample, then six sample labels each with a
            6px coloured tab, an id such as S-01 and a project code, the name,
            the project and due date with a day delta, and a status flag. A
            control strip of round knob tabs and a square green add key ends
            the device.
        spacing: A 4px base on an 8px graph grid. 12px between panels, 8px between samples, 6 to 10px padding.
        density: Dense but ordered. Every value carries a unit or a delta.
        corners: 2 to 6px like softened metal. Knobs and screws are round.
        borders: 1px bezel lines everywhere. Sample labels have a 6px tab, hatched red and white for overdue. The current knob gets a 2px ink ring and a small triangle pointer below.
        shadows: Inset 0 1px 3px for readouts and fields, a white top highlight and a 2px hard bottom edge for the chassis and keys.
        icons:
            1.8 stroke line icons inside round knob discs, with a flask for
            Projects. Status flags pair a word with a filled dot for Due today,
            a hollow ring for Queued, a tick for Done and a cross for Overdue.
            High priority is a yellow caution tag with a triangle.
        focus: A 2px probe blue outline offset 2px plus a soft 5px blue halo.
        tone: Measured and technical, such as Runs, Samples, Queued, Δt 30 min and +2 d.

    style73:
        number: 73
        run: 15
        screen: TodayMobile
        name: Letterpress Victorian
        idea: The day is set as a Victorian playbill in black and red ink on cream stock, with mixed wood-type headings, fleurons and double rules announcing each task like an act.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/73.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            creamStock: #f4ecd6, the page behind the bill
            billPaper: #faf4e2, the printed sheet and fields
            tint: #ebdfc0, the avatar disc
            blackInk: #1b1712, type, rules and frames
            fadedBrown: #4f4234, meta, project lines and upcoming notices
            vermilion: #a11d17, the second ink for fleurons, overdue, priority, the add button and focus
        type:
            Mixed wood type, changing per entry. Condensed display Impact,
            Haettenschweiler, Arial Narrow Bold, sans-serif in caps for the
            46px wordmark, 22px section heads and every third task name at
            24px. Slab Rockwell, Clarendon, Roboto Slab, Georgia at 700 for the
            26px date, 20px meeting hours and the next task names. Didone
            Didot, Bodoni MT, Big Caslon, Georgia in bold italic for the other
            task names and meeting names at 18 to 21px, and at 10 to 11px caps
            tracked 0.2em for small labels. Body text is Bookman Old Style,
            Palatino, Georgia at 15 to 16px italic.
        layout:
            A centred playbill up to 400px. A 3px black border, a cream gap and
            a hairline make the outer frame, and an inner hairline frame has
            red corner ornaments. Everything is centred. The header has the
            issue line No. 306 and a ringed avatar, The in red italic over
            BRIGHTWORK in wood type, a fleuron row, a double rule, the date in
            slab and Featuring 6 tasks and 2 meetings in italic with the counts
            in red. Section heads sit between twin hairlines. Meetings show a
            boxed hour with morning or afternoon beside the name and length.
            Each task is a centred entry with an ordinal such as The first, the
            name, for and the project, and a notice. The bottom bar sits under a
            double rule with a ringed red round add button.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 10px above and below each entry, 18px before section heads.
        density: Medium and theatrical, with large headings and ornaments between sections.
        corners: Square. Only the avatar, badge and add button are round, each with an extra ring.
        borders: 3px double rules, 1px rules between tasks, dotted rules between meetings, and twin hairlines beside section heads.
        shadows: None on the screen. Buttons use a hard 3px offset ink shadow like a misregistered print.
        icons:
            Printer's ornaments and glyphs. Fleurons ❦ ❧ ✥ divide sections. A
            pointing hand marks the current tab and high priority. Notices pair
            a word with ✦ for Due today, a ring for upcoming, ✓ for Done and ✗
            on a solid red block for Overdue. Nav icons are thin engraved line
            drawings such as a sun for Today.
        focus: A 2px vermilion outline offset 3px with an extra vermilion hairline ring outside.
        tone: A playbill announcer, such as Featuring 6 tasks and 2 meetings, The first and lasting 30 min.

    style74:
        number: 74
        run: 16
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Cockpit avionics
        idea: A light-mode flight deck where every number is an instrument in a screwed-down bezel, projects are vertical tape gauges and trouble lights up as an amber caution caption.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/74.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            deck: #dfe2dc, the page behind the panels
            bezel: #eef0eb, raised instrument housings and nav keys
            face: #fafbf7, dial faces, displays and fields
            ink: #15191c, text, needles, tape fill and the primary key
            dim: #4b534f, captions and meta
            selectedMagenta: #a1166f, tape bugs, log times, the week marker and focus
            green: #1b6a3a, the On track caption and normal arcs on dials
            cautionAmber: #f0b13a, caution fills with near-black text, never text itself
            warningRed: #b11f1a, the Behind caption with white text
            sky: #cfe2f1, the upper half of the attitude indicator
            ground: #e8d6b8, the lower half of the attitude indicator
        type:
            Two stacks. Captions use Arial Narrow, Roboto Condensed, Helvetica
            Neue, Arial in bold caps tracked 0.14em at 11 to 12px. Readouts,
            times and the activity log use ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo,
            Consolas. The greeting is 26px bold condensed, readouts 22px bold
            mono in a small boxed window, tape percents 20px bold mono, project
            names 13px bold condensed and log lines 13px mono with bold magenta
            times.
        layout:
            A grey glareshield bar holds the brand with a small dial mark and
            the subtitle FLIGHT DECK, a row of square push keys for nav with a
            green lamp strip lit on Home, a monospace scratchpad search, a black
            New project key, an amber Notices 3 caution button and Pilot in
            command Mara Okafor. Below, a long bezel is the message line with
            the greeting, the date in mono caps and an amber caption reading
            Caution 4 tasks overdue. A row of five bezels follows, four round
            dials with a 270 degree tick arc, a coloured value arc, a needle and
            a boxed readout for the four summary numbers, the overdue dial with
            an amber caution band, and an attitude indicator whose horizon sits
            nose up for the week trend 73 against 59. The lower area has a wide
            Project systems bezel with six vertical tape gauges side by side,
            each with its percent above, a magenta bug at the fill level, name,
            team, tasks and due in mono, and a status caption under it. The
            right column stacks a Climb log bar chart on a display, last week as
            outlined bars and this week solid with a dashed magenta divider, and
            a Datalink messages log. At 375px the dials go two by two, the
            attitude indicator spans the row and the tapes go three across.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px between bezels, 20px inside them and 10px between keys and tapes.
        density: Medium. Few large instruments with small captions, readouts carry the weight.
        corners: 14px on bezels, 6px on displays, 4px on keys and fields and 2px on captions.
        borders: A 1px grey rim on bezels and displays, 1px ink on dials and tapes, dashed rows in the log, and an 8px screw drawn in each bezel corner.
        shadows: Bezels are raised with a white top highlight, a 2px lip and a soft blur. Displays and fields are inset.
        icons:
            Instrument drawings only, dials with needles, tape gauges with a
            magenta bug and an attitude ball. Status captions pair the word with
            an open green circle for On track, a solid triangle on amber for At
            risk and a white square on red for Behind. Behind and At risk tapes
            also use striped fills.
        focus: A 2px magenta outline offset 2px with a soft 5px magenta halo at 18 percent.
        tone: Clipped checklist caps such as Caution 4 tasks overdue, Climb log, Datalink messages and 12 MIN.

    style75:
        number: 75
        run: 16
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Weather forecast
        idea: The dashboard is the evening weather map, with projects placed as towns carrying a sun, cloud or rain symbol and a big temperature-style percent, and the overdue count shown as a storm warning.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/75.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            sky: #e6f2fb, the page, fading down from #cfe6f7 at the top
            card: #ffffff, panels, reading tiles and town cards
            sea: #d4e8f6, map water
            land: #e5eed6, map land, with #d9e6c6 for hills
            isobar: #8fb0c9, pressure lines on the map, decoration only
            nightInk: #0f2a44, text and the bulletin time tabs
            haze: #40607b, meta text and the cloud outline
            studioBlue: #1757a6, panel header bars, buttons, the current nav pill, the cold front and focus
            sunshine: #f2b51d, sun fill, always outlined in #6a4800
            fairGreen: #1c6a36, the On track word
            overcastAmber: #7f4f00, the At risk word
            stormRed: #ad2219, the Behind word, the warning edge, the low pressure L and the overdue count
        type:
            One rounded broadcast sans, Avenir Next, Segoe UI, Helvetica Neue,
            Arial. The greeting is 40px at 800 with tight tracking, reading
            numbers 46px at 800, town percents 36px at 800 with a 15px percent
            sign raised like a degree, panel headers 17px at 800 in white on
            blue, body 16px, meta 12px at 600 and status words 12px at 800 in
            caps.
        layout:
            A channel bar holds a sun logo with Brightwork and Project outlook,
            nav as pills in a translucent white capsule with Home filled blue,
            then a round search, a New project pill, a round bell with a red
            count and a sun-yellow avatar for Mara Okafor. The presenter strip
            pairs the big greeting and date with a white Storm warning card that
            has a red left edge, a red triangle with a lightning bolt and 4
            tasks are overdue. Four reading tiles follow with a weather glyph
            and a big number each. The main row has a wide Project map panel, a
            sea and land map with isobars, a red L and a blue H and cold and
            warm fronts, with six white town cards placed over it, each with a
            glyph, the big percent, name, a status word with a weather phrase
            and a meta line, and a legend strip below. Beside it Latest
            bulletins are lower-third bands with a dark time tab. A full-width
            14-day record line chart follows, last week dashed grey, this week
            solid red with a shaded area and the value over every point, and
            tags for 59, 73 and the peak. At 375px the town cards stack as a
            list over the map and the chart scrolls inside its panel.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 12 to 20px between tiles and panels and 14 to 18px inside.
        density: Low to medium. Big readings with compact town cards on the map.
        corners: Round and soft, 18px panels, 14 to 16px tiles and town cards, pills for nav and buttons.
        borders: Almost none. A blue header bar tops each panel and the warning has an 8px red left edge.
        shadows: Soft 0 6px 18px shadows in navy at 8 percent under panels, a little stronger under town cards.
        icons:
            Forecast glyphs drawn with dark outlines. A sun with rays for On
            track, a cloud over a sun for At risk, a dark cloud with rain for
            Behind and a red triangle with a bolt for overdue, each beside its
            word.
        focus: A 3px studio blue outline offset 2px.
        tone: A friendly presenter, such as Storm warning, conditions now, sunny, clouding over and heavy rain.

    style76:
        number: 76
        run: 16
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Exchange board
        idea: The dashboard reads like a light trading-floor board, with projects quoted as tickers carrying a last price, a depth bar and an up, hold or down signal, over a static ticker tape and a volume chart.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/76.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            floor: #eceee9, the page
            board: #ffffff, panes and table rows, zebra rows in #f7f8f5
            grid: #c8ccc4, cell rules and pane borders
            ink: #101820, text, depth bars and the primary button
            slate: #4c5660, labels and hatching
            headerNavy: #13263f, the nav bar, the table head and this week bars
            tape: #fff3c4, the ticker band
            lamp: #ffd84d, the current nav tab and the focus halo
            upGreen: #11703d, On track on a #e3f3e8 chip
            holdAmber: #8a5200, At risk on a #fbefd6 chip
            downRed: #b4161b, Behind and overdue on a #fbe4e3 chip
            wireBlue: #0d4f9e, links, newswire times and the focus ring
        type:
            Numbers and codes use ui-monospace, SF Mono, Cascadia Mono, Menlo,
            Consolas with tabular figures. Words use Helvetica Neue, Arial
            Narrow, Arial. Index values are 34px bold mono, the greeting 28px
            at 800, last prices 17px at 800 mono, project names 14px bold sans,
            cells 13px mono, table heads 11px bold mono caps on navy and chart
            labels 12px mono.
        layout:
            A white top row holds a rising arrow mark, Brightwork and a boxed
            BWX code, the date as SAT 31 OCT 2026 WEEKEND SESSION, a FIND
            search box with a black label, a + New project button, an ALERTS
            box with a red 3 and DESK Mara Okafor. A navy nav bar follows with
            Home lit yellow, then a pale yellow ticker tape listing each project
            code with its percent and signal and the week total, scrolling
            sideways inside itself. The greeting row has the heading, the date
            in mono and a red bordered 4 TASKS OVERDUE flash with a down
            triangle. Four index boxes share one bordered strip with codes ACTV,
            DUE.WK, OVRD and HRS.WK and big right-aligned values. The main grid
            has a Project quotes table with columns Sym, Project, Sector, Last,
            Depth, Tasks, Due and Signal, invented codes WEBR, MOB2, Q4SV,
            BILL, SPRC and ONBE, a segmented depth bar and a signal chip. The
            right column stacks a Volume chart with hatched bars for last week
            and navy bars this week, a three-cell strip for 59, 73 and the
            change, and a Newswire list. At 375px the table scrolls inside its
            pane and the index boxes go two by two.
        spacing: A 4px base with 8px most gaps. Cells are 9px by 10px and panes sit 14px apart.
        density: High. Tabular rows and small mono figures.
        corners: Square everywhere.
        borders: 1px grid lines, a 2px ink rule under each pane title and zebra rows.
        shadows: None. Depth comes from the navy header bands.
        icons:
            Market glyphs only. An up triangle for On track, a diamond for At
            risk and a down triangle for Behind and overdue, always with the
            word in a tinted chip.
        focus: A 2px wire blue outline offset 1px with a 4px yellow lamp halo.
        tone: Terse trader codes such as ACTV, DUE.WK, OVRD, Newswire, 12m and YDAY.

    style77:
        number: 77
        run: 16
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Split-flap timetable
        idea: The dashboard is a railway departures hall in light grey, where projects leave from numbered platforms, key words are set in split-flap character cells and the remarks column says whether each one is on time.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/77.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            hall: #e9eaea, the page
            board: #cfd3d6, board housings and the focused list row
            frame: #858b90, the 6px housing frame and row rules
            flap: #fbfbf8, character cells
            ink: #141618, flap letters, buttons and sign borders
            grey: #474d52, captions and the calling at lines
            platformBlue: #1d3f8f, platform number squares and the current nav sign
            noticeYellow: #ffcc33, the customer notice strip and the focus outline
            green: #17663a, On track with a solid disc
            amber: #8a4d00, At risk with a solid triangle
            red: #b01c1c, Behind and the overdue count with a solid square
        type:
            Flap text uses ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas in bold caps,
            one letter per cell. Each cell is 0.92em wide with a 2px gap, a 2px
            radius, a thin dark seam across the middle and a 1px grey lip below.
            The full text is kept for screen readers and the cells are hidden
            from them. Flap sizes are 26px for the greeting, 34px for counts,
            17px in departure rows, 15px for arrival times and 14px in list
            rows. Signs and body use Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, board
            titles 18px at 800, captions 11px bold caps tracked 0.16em.
        layout:
            A station header holds a ring and bar roundel with Brightwork, nav
            as six white signs each with a black number square, Home inverted
            blue, then a FIND search with a ruled label, a black New project
            button, a bell with 3 and Signed in Mara Okafor. A grey housing with
            a 6px frame shows the greeting and the date in flap cells and a
            yellow Customer notice strip with a loudspeaker saying 4 tasks are
            overdue and to check Billing migration first. Four small housings
            show the counts in flap cells, the overdue one in red. The
            Departures board is a table with Due, Destination with calling at
            and the team, a blue platform square, progress in mono with tasks
            below, and Remarks with a shape, the status in flap cells and an
            italic note such as running on time, expect delays or delayed. Below
            sit an Arrivals board for activity with flap times, and a chart
            board where each day is a column of small cells, one per task, open
            cells last week and filled cells this week. At 375px each departure
            becomes a stacked block and arrivals put the time above the text.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 9 to 12px cell padding in rows and 14 to 16px between boards.
        density: Medium high. Long boards with one row per project.
        corners: Square signs, 4px housings and 2px flap cells.
        borders: A 6px grey frame round each board, 2px rules between rows and 2px ink on signs and fields.
        shadows: A flat 3px lip under each housing with no blur.
        icons:
            Station pictograms in solid ink, a train face, an arrow and bars.
            Remarks use a disc for On track, a triangle for At risk and a square
            for Behind beside the flap word.
        focus: A 3px notice yellow outline with a 5px ink ring outside it.
        tone: A station announcer, such as Departures, calling at Design, running on time, expect delays and Customer notice.

    style78:
        number: 78
        run: 16
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Broadsheet
        idea: The dashboard is a dense daily front page where the most urgent fact is the banner headline, each project is a story with a dateline and a jump line, and the numbers live in a ruled sidebar.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/78.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            newsprint: #f3f0e6, the page sheet
            table: #e3dfd3, the surround behind the sheet
            ink: #191919, text, rules and solid bars
            grey: #545454, bylines, cutlines and jump lines
            hairline: #b7b2a5, column rules and dotted list rules
            halftone: #e6e1d2, hatched photo boxes
            red: #9b1b1b, the kicker, wire times and Behind
            green: #2b5a2d, the On track tag
            brown: #774a00, the At risk tag
            highlighter: #fff6c9, the focus fill
        type:
            Four stacks. The nameplate uses Old English Text MT, Goudy Text MT,
            Times New Roman at 76px. Headlines use Times New Roman, Times,
            Liberation Serif at 700, the banner 54px, the lead story 34px,
            second stories 22px and briefs 18px. Decks are 20px italic. Body is
            Georgia 14px at 1.42, justified with hyphens in columns. Labels,
            datelines and tags use Franklin Gothic, Arial Narrow, Arial at 11px
            bold caps.
        layout:
            A utility strip has an underlined search, Notices (3), Mara Okafor
            and a black New project button. The nameplate row has a boxed ear on
            each side, This week 73 done and Outlook 4 overdue, around the big
            Brightwork. A folio line under a 3px rule gives the date, the team
            edition for Mara Okafor and Six projects inside. Nav is a centred
            section index with Home inverted. The banner has the red kicker Good
            morning, Mara, the headline Four Tasks Overdue as Billing Migration
            Falls Behind and an italic deck. The front splits into a main area
            and a rail divided by a 1px ink rule. The lead story is Billing
            migration with a figures line, a drop cap and three justified
            columns with rules, ending in a jump line. Under it Mobile app 2.0
            runs in two columns beside Website redesign with a hatched photo
            box showing 72 percent and a cutline, then three briefs. The rail
            has a boxed By the numbers list, a Fig. 1 bar chart with open bars
            last week and solid bars this week, and an In brief wire. At 375px
            everything is one column.
        spacing: Tight. 14px between stories and 18px gutters with a rule in each.
        density: Very high. Three text columns in the lead and briefs in threes.
        corners: None.
        borders: A 3px rule under the nameplate, 1px ink between main and rail, hairline column rules, 2px boxes in the rail and dotted list rules.
        shadows: None on the page. The sheet sits on a darker table.
        icons:
            No pictograms. Printer’s shapes before status tags, a disc for On
            track, a triangle for At risk and a square for Behind. Each story
            also has a small ruled progress bar.
        focus: A 2px ink outline offset 2px over a pale yellow highlighter fill.
        tone: Headline English, such as Four Tasks Overdue as Billing Migration Falls Behind, desk datelines and Continued in.

    style79:
        number: 79
        run: 17
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Tabloid
        idea: The dashboard shouts like a tabloid front page, with a red masthead, a giant condensed splash for the overdue count, starburst stickers and every project in a tilted cut-out photo box.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/79.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            paper: #fbfaf7, the page and photo frames
            ink: #0b0b0b, type, 3px borders, hard shadows and the nav strip
            mastheadRed: #c8102e, the masthead, the primary button, this week bars, the overdue fact box and Behind
            highlighter: #ffe100, fact boxes, starbursts, the current nav item and At risk, ink text only
            grey: #4a4a4a, captions under photo headlines
            halftone: #d9d6cf, the dot screen inside photo boxes
            cutoutGrey: #9a968e, silhouettes inside photo boxes, decoration only
            green: #0f6b33, the On track sticker
            focusBlue: #123e9c, the 4px focus outline
        type:
            Shouting type uses Impact, Haettenschweiler, Arial Narrow Bold,
            Franklin Gothic Heavy, condensed sans in caps. The splash is 132px
            at 0.86 line height, the masthead 76px italic set on a red block
            skewed 4 degrees, section bars 32px, photo headlines 26px, fact
            figures 64px and nav 18px. Body uses Arial, Helvetica Neue in bold
            at 22px for the deck and 15 to 16px for text.
        layout:
            A black nav strip runs across the top with caps links, Home on
            yellow, and Signed in Mara Okafor at the right. The masthead is a
            skewed red block with Brightwork in white italic and a small strap,
            casting a 6px ink shadow, beside the date in caps over a thick rule,
            a boxed FIND search, a red New project button and a yellow starburst
            reading 3 new. The splash sits between 6px rules, a yellow tilted
            kicker Morning, Mara, the headline 4 TASKS OVERDUE with the first
            words red, a bold deck with Billing migration highlighted, and a big
            rotated yellow starburst reading 73 done this week. Four yellow fact
            boxes tilt alternately with hard shadows, the overdue box red. The
            main area is The big six, a grid of tilted white photo boxes, each
            with a halftone picture of a simple drawn object such as a browser,
            phone, clipboard, card, book or envelope, a black percent flag in
            the corner, a caps headline, a meta line and a status sticker. Team
            gossip runs beside it with caps names and red time chips. The
            fortnight that was is a boxed bar chart with a red hard shadow,
            white bars last week, red bars this week and big numbers on top. At
            375px the photos stack in one column and the burst moves under the
            splash.
        spacing: An 8px unit, loud and packed. 16 to 22px between boxes and 6px rules between blocks.
        density: Medium. Few words, each one huge.
        corners: Square boxes. Only the On track sticker is a pill. Boxes tilt by 1 to 2 degrees.
        borders: 3px ink on boxes and fields, 4 to 6px ink rules above and below the splash.
        shadows: Hard offset ink shadows of 4 to 8px with no blur. The chart casts a red one.
        icons:
            Stickers with different shapes. A green disc with a tick on a white
            pill for On track, a yellow sign with a black triangle for At risk
            and a red jagged burst with a cross for Behind. Starbursts hold the
            big numbers.
        focus: A 4px focus blue outline offset 2px.
        tone: Exclaiming headlines, such as Morning, Mara, 4 tasks overdue, Shock as, The big six and Team gossip.

    style80:
        number: 80
        run: 17
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Recipe card
        idea: Every project is a handwritten index recipe card on a gingham-bordered counter, with tasks measured in cups, a jug that fills as work is done and a stamp for the status.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/80.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            gingham: #c94141, the checked border at 55 percent on white
            counter: #fbf6ea, the page inside the border
            card: #fffdf6, index cards
            topRule: #d0453f, the red line under card titles
            ruledBlue: #a9cbe8, card lines, decoration only
            pencil: #26262f, writing and outlines
            faded: #57525c, typed field labels
            butter: #f8e7b0, jug fill and the notification badge
            tomato: #ac2727, the primary button, Behind, the overdue line and this week bars
            herb: #2e6a30, the On track stamp
            honey: #875700, the At risk stamp
            blueInk: #1f4e9a, links, jug marks and focus
        type:
            Handwriting uses Segoe Print, Bradley Hand, Chalkboard SE, Comic
            Sans MS, Comic Neue, cursive for the brand at 34px, the greeting at
            30px, card titles at 21px on a 38px line and card lines at 16px on a
            26px rule. Typed field labels use Courier New, Courier at 11px bold
            caps. Body notes use Trebuchet MS, Gill Sans, Segoe UI at 13 to
            15px.
        layout:
            The whole page sits inside a red gingham border with a white and red
            double edge. The header has a basket mark with Brightwork in tomato
            script and THE TEAM RECIPE BOX in type, a hand-cut search, a tomato
            New project button, a round timer bell with a butter 3 badge and
            Head cook Mara Okafor. Nav is a row of recipe-box divider tabs with
            Home raised in front. The greeting card says Good morning, Mara,
            the date, a tomato line that 4 tasks are overdue and to check the
            oven first, and that everything else is simmering. Beside it an In
            the pantry card lists the four summary numbers with a cup, spoon,
            timer and sand glass. Recipes on the go is a grid of six tilted
            cards, each with a ruled body, a red title rule, the title with a
            status stamp, typed fields From, Measured as tasks in cups, Done and
            Ready by, a jug drawing filled to the percent and a one-line method.
            Below sit Batches baked, a bar chart with open rounded bars last
            week and tomato bars this week, and Kitchen notes on a ruled card.
            At 375px the border thins and cards stack.
        spacing: Set by the 26px ruled line. 22px between cards and 18px card padding.
        density: Medium. Four facts per card plus a jug.
        corners: 3px card corners. Buttons and fields use uneven hand-cut corners such as 4px 16px.
        borders: The gingham frame round the page, a 2px red title rule and blue lines on cards, and 2px pencil outlines on controls.
        shadows: A soft paper shadow under cards and a 2px by 3px pencil offset under buttons. Cards tilt under one degree.
        icons:
            Kitchen line drawings, a jug, a spoon, a timer and a sand glass.
            Stamps are rotated outlined boxes pairing the word with a ticked
            circle for On track, a triangle for At risk and a crossed solid
            square for Behind.
        focus: A 3px dashed blue ink outline offset 3px.
        tone: Warm and homely, such as Heads up, check the oven first, Recipes on the go, Kitchen notes and Ready by.

    style81:
        number: 81
        run: 17
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Wine label
        idea: The dashboard is an estate cellar where an engraved crest heads the page, each project is a cream wine label with its cuvée, vintage and percent complete set like strength, and status is a small seal.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/81.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            cellar: #efe6d2, the page
            label: #fbf6ea, labels and panels
            burgundy: #6d1424, frames, accents, this week bars and the primary button
            claret: #8b2b3b, a second accent for hover
            gilt: #a88443, inner hairlines and ornaments, never text
            ink: #2a1a17, text
            sepia: #5d4a43, captions and italics
            hairline: #cdbf9f, dotted rules
            bottleGreen: #2c5934, the On track seal
            amber: #7c5000, the At risk seal
            red: #a01d1d, the Behind seal
        type:
            Display uses Didot, Bodoni 72, Bodoni MT, Big Caslon, Hoefler Text,
            Garamond, Georgia. The house name is 46px caps tracked 0.3em, the
            greeting 40px italic, label names 26px, percent figures 44px with
            lining numerals and section titles 22 to 28px caps tracked 0.14em.
            Small caps labels are 11 to 12px at 600 tracked 0.24em. Text uses
            Hoefler Text, Garamond, Baskerville, Georgia at 16px, with italics
            for vintages and times.
        layout:
            A thin utility row has an underlined Seek search, Notes iii, Cellar
            master Mara Okafor and a burgundy New project button with an inset
            cream line. A centred shield crest with a B sits over BRIGHTWORK in
            wide caps and Project estate, the team cellar. Nav is centred small
            caps between burgundy rules with gilt diamonds between items and
            Home underlined. The greeting is an oval cartouche with an inner
            gilt line holding the date, Good morning, Mara in italic and Four
            tasks are overdue between diamonds. Four rounded neck collars show
            the summary numbers. The cellar is a grid of six labels, each a
            burgundy line, a cream gap and a double frame, with Cuvée and the
            team, an engraved sprig, the name, Vintage 2026 and a number, the
            percent large with complete, a ruled meter, tasks and bottled by
            the due date, and a seal. Below sit a Harvest record bar chart with
            engraved line-filled bars last week and solid burgundy this week,
            and The cellar book with italic times. At 375px labels stack and
            the cartouche becomes a rounded panel.
        spacing: An 8px unit, generous. 26px between labels and 26 to 34px inside panels.
        density: Low. Centred, symmetrical and lots of cream.
        corners: Square labels. The greeting is an oval cartouche and the summary sits on rounded neck collars.
        borders: Engraved stacks of an outer burgundy line, a cream gap and an inner gilt or double burgundy line.
        shadows: A soft 12px shadow as if labels sit on bottles.
        icons:
            Engraved sprigs, a shield crest and diamond dividers. Seals pair the
            word with a round seal holding a tick for On track, a lozenge with
            an exclamation for At risk and a square seal with a cross for
            Behind, each with a thin outer ring.
        focus: A 2px burgundy outline offset 3px with a 6px burgundy halo at 15 percent.
        tone: Courtly and calm, such as The cellar, Cuvée Design, bottled by 14 November and The cellar book.

    style82:
        number: 82
        run: 17
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Coffee menu board
        idea: The dashboard is a café menu board on kraft paper in a wooden frame, with projects as menu items priced in percent with dotted leaders, the summary in cup sizes and the overdue count as the day’s special.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/82.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            wall: #efe7da, the page behind the board
            wood: #6a4528, the 16px frame, with a #4a2f1a edge
            kraft: #d8bb8d, the board surface with faint fibres
            lightKraft: #e3caa1, last week bars
            milk: #f7eedc, the order slip, tags, search and fields
            espresso: #2a180b, text, outlines and the primary button
            roast: #4f3320, script notes, dotted leaders and this week bars
            crema: #c98b3c, foam caps on the bars, decoration only
            green: #1e5a2a, On track on milk
            caramel: #7a4a00, At risk on milk
            cherry: #9e1f17, Behind, the overdue count and the special ribbon
        type:
            Three stacks. Slab caps use Rockwell, Rockwell Nova, Roboto Slab,
            Courier New, Georgia at 700, the brand 30px tracked 0.12em, section
            heads 26px tracked 0.14em, menu items 21px, prices 30px and summary
            figures 46px. Hand lettering uses Marker Felt, Ink Free, Chalkboard
            SE, Comic Sans MS for the 52px greeting and notes at 15 to 21px.
            Descriptions use Gill Sans, Trebuchet MS, Segoe UI at 15px italic.
        layout:
            The dashboard sits on a kraft board inside a 16px wood frame with a
            dark inner line. The header has a steaming cup mark with BRIGHTWORK
            and today’s project menu in script, a pill search, a dark New
            project pill, a bell with a red 3 and on shift Mara Okafor. Nav is
            centred slab caps between two espresso rules with a coffee bean
            between items and Home inverted. The greeting is centred script with
            the date in slab caps and a red ribbon reading Today’s special, 4
            tasks are overdue. Four cups of growing size show the summary
            numbers, labelled small, medium, too hot and large, the overdue cup
            red. On the menu lists the six projects as items with a dotted
            leader to the percent as a price and a description line with team,
            tasks, due and a tag. Below, Cups poured is a bar chart of rounded
            cups, light kraft last week and dark roast with crema caps this
            week. From the counter is a taped milk slip of Fresh orders with
            dark time chips, then a key of the three tags. At 375px the menu
            and counter stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 10 to 12px between menu items and 34px between menu columns.
        density: Medium. One line per item plus a description line.
        corners: Pill buttons, fields and search, 4 to 6px on tags, swatches and the board.
        borders: A 16px wood frame with a dark inner line, 2px espresso rules round the nav and dotted price leaders.
        shadows: One soft shadow under the board and one under the taped order slip, which tilts slightly.
        icons:
            Cups in four sizes and a bean between nav items. Tags on milk pair
            the word with a coffee bean for On track, a triangle for At risk and
            a square for Behind.
        focus: A 3px espresso outline offset 2px with a 6px milk halo.
        tone: A friendly barista, such as Today’s special, On the menu, Cups poured, From the counter and Fresh orders.

    style83:
        number: 83
        run: 17
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Bakery box
        idea: The dashboard is a pink pastry box tied with striped tape, with projects sitting in its compartments as round cakes that fill like a pie, numbers hanging on cake tags from twine and every status on a notched tag.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/83.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            shop: #fff6f2, the page
            boxPink: #f9dfe6, the lid band and the box
            deepPink: #f2bccb, tag lips, dotted rules and last week bars
            tape: #e2789a, diagonal stripes with white on tape bands, decoration only
            cream: #fffaf6, compartments, tags and panels
            cocoa: #3b1f2b, text and 2 to 3px outlines
            milkCocoa: #6a4553, secondary text
            raspberry: #a3224d, the primary button, cake fill, this week bars, the overdue tag and focus
            mint: #2c6a4d, the On track tag
            caramel: #7b4a00, the At risk tag
            cherry: #a11c1c, the Behind tag
            twine: #b08a6e, the dashed string, decoration only
        type:
            Script headings use Snell Roundhand, Segoe Script, Lucida
            Handwriting, Brush Script MT at weight 400, the greeting 50px, box
            and panel titles 32 to 38px and the brand 30px. Everything else uses
            Avenir Next Rounded, Nunito, Varela Round, Arial Rounded MT Bold,
            Trebuchet MS, hanging tag figures 44px at 800, project names 18px at
            800, tags 13px at 800, body 14 to 16px and labels 11px bold caps
            tracked 0.16em.
        layout:
            A pink lid band starts with a striped tape strip and holds an oval
            cream seal with Brightwork in raspberry script and a dashed pink
            inner line, nav as cream pills with Home in raspberry, a round
            search, a raspberry New project pill, a round bell with a 3 and a
            dashed avatar ring for Mara Okafor. The greeting sits beside a large
            tilted cake tag reading 4 tasks are overdue. A dashed twine curve
            crosses the page with four tags hanging from it, each with a punched
            hole, a slight tilt and a pink lip, for the summary numbers. The
            projects sit in a pink box with a 3px outline and a striped tape
            band down its middle, under the script title Today’s box of six, as
            six cream compartments, each with a round cake whose raspberry
            slice is the percent and a cream pill with the figure, the name,
            team and tasks, Ready and the due date, and a status tag. Below
            sit Out of the oven, a bar chart of cupcake bars with round tops,
            pale pink last week and raspberry this week, and an Order slip with
            a piece of tape on its corner. At 375px compartments stack and the
            tags go two by two.
        spacing: An 8px unit, soft. 14px between compartments and 22px box padding.
        density: Low to medium. Six compartments with one cake each.
        corners: Very round. 22px panels, 16px compartments, pill buttons and notched tags.
        borders: 2 to 3px cocoa outlines everywhere, with striped tape bands across the lid, the box and the style sheet.
        shadows: Flat coloured lips only, 3 to 6px of pink or deep raspberry under tags and buttons.
        icons:
            Pie cakes for progress and hanging tags for numbers. Status tags
            have a notched end and a punched hole and pair the word with a disc
            tick for On track, a triangle for At risk and a crossed square for
            Behind.
        focus: A 3px raspberry outline offset 3px with a 7px pale pink halo.
        tone: A sweet shopkeeper, such as fresh from the oven, Today’s box of six, Out of the oven, Order slip and Ready 14 Nov.

    style84:
        number: 84
        run: 18
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Farmers market
        idea: A Saturday market stall where projects sit in wooden crates filled with produce to their progress, the week's numbers hang as price tags on twine, and every sign looks hand painted.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/84.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            canvas: #f5eedf, the page
            pine: #ecd3a2, the header board, crates and section signs
            pineShade: #c9a46a, slat lines and last week bars, never text
            kraft: #e2c99a, nav slats and slip edges
            tagCard: #fffaf0, price tags, activity slips, crate feet and fields
            ink: #2a1f14, text and outlines
            soil: #5a4632, crate frames and small notes
            twine: #9b7b4f, strings and tag cords, never text
            leaf: #2f5d2a, the brand, the current nav slat, On track, this week bars and focus
            carrot: #9a4a08, At risk and Marketing produce
            tomato: #a3261b, the New project button, overdue and Behind
            plum: #5b2a5e, Research produce
        type:
            Three stacks. Signs use Cooper Black, Bookman Old Style, Rockwell
            Extra Bold, Georgia, serif at 400 for the 46px greeting, 52px price
            tag numbers, 34px brand, 24px section signs, 26px crate percentages
            and 20px crate names in caps. Handwriting uses Segoe Print, Bradley
            Hand, Chalkboard SE, Comic Sans MS, cursive at 15 to 20px for dates,
            tag captions, due dates and times. Body uses Trebuchet MS, Gill
            Sans, Segoe UI, sans-serif at 16px with 1.5 line height, and status
            words at 14px bold.
        layout:
            A striped green and cream awning with a scalloped edge runs across
            the top. Under it a pine header board with plank lines holds a
            tomato brand mark, the brand, a tag shaped search field, the New
            project button, a round bell and the user. A dark rail carries the
            nav as small kraft slats hung on two twine strings each. The
            greeting is a big painted line with the date in handwriting, and a
            red tag tilted 2 degrees on the right says 4 tasks are overdue. The
            four numbers are price tags with a pointed left end and a punched
            hole, hung from a sagging twine line and alternately tilted. Below,
            a wide column titled On the stall holds six crates in a three
            column grid. Each crate has a painted end board with the name and
            team, a slatted strip filled from the left with produce dots in the
            team colour to the percentage, and a cream foot with percentage,
            due date, task count and status. The side column has a stall board
            of slightly tilted paper slips for activity and a framed bar chart
            whose bars are drawn as stacked crate slats. Below 960px the side
            column moves under the crates and tags go two by two.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between crates and tags, 40px between the two columns, 56px below the stall.
        density: Medium and chunky. Six big crates, four big tags and short slips.
        corners: 4 to 6px on boards and crates. Tags have a pointed end. Status chips are pills.
        borders: 2 to 3px soil or ink outlines on everything, slat lines inside wood, and a dashed ink edge where the produce stops.
        shadows: A flat 3px ink drop under buttons and tags, as if propped up. No blur.
        icons:
            Chunky filled shapes with ink outlines and a tomato brand mark.
            Status pills pair the word with a filled circle for On track, a
            filled triangle for At risk and a filled square for Behind.
            Overdue adds an exclamation octagon.
        focus: A 3px leaf outline offset 3px, then a canvas gap and a 2px ink ring out to 9px. A focused field turns its border leaf green.
        tone: A friendly stallholder, such as On the stall, Picked each day, ready to pick and pick these first.

    style85:
        number: 85
        run: 18
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Seed packet
        idea: Every project is a vintage seed packet with a small painted vignette and its progress read as germination, while the fortnight sits in a sowing chart of growing stems.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/85.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            cream: #f7f1e1, the page
            packetPaper: #fffbef, packets, panels and the masthead
            sky: #d7e7e6, the sky behind each vignette
            ink: #2b2a22, text and frames
            soilBrown: #5e5440, labels and notes
            chaff: #c9bc9c, grid lines and meter ticks, never text
            tomato: #a8331f, Design packets, the pinked edge, overdue and Behind
            bean: #3d6b2c, Engineering packets, On track, this week stems and the primary button
            carrot: #8f4a0c, Research packets and At risk
            tulip: #8e2f5a, Marketing packets
            mustard: #d9a72b, the avatar and the focus glow, never text
        type:
            Three stacks. Slab uses Rockwell, Roboto Slab, Clarendon, Georgia
            at 700 for the 38px greeting, 34px contents numbers, 30px brand,
            24px section titles and 18px germination figures. Variety names
            use Georgia bold italic at 21px. Body is Georgia at 16px with 1.5
            line height. Labels use Franklin Gothic Medium, Arial Narrow, Arial
            at 700, 11 to 13px caps tracked 0.12 to 0.14em.
        layout:
            A paper masthead with a red pinked top edge holds a round sprout
            badge, the brand with the line Projects grown from seed, a square
            search field, the New project button, a bell and the user. The nav
            is a row of caps cells split by hairlines, the current one black.
            Two framed panels follow, each with an inset hairline frame. The
            left is the back of a packet with the greeting, the date, a
            sowing note with a red diamond saying 4 tasks are overdue, and a
            packet contents grid of four cells with caps headings and slab
            numbers. The right is the sowing chart, two week blocks of seven
            ruled columns where each day is a stem with a pair of leaves grown
            to its count, with day letters on top and counts below. Below, the
            seed rack shows six portrait packets in three columns. Each packet
            has a team colour frame, a coloured band with the number and the
            brand, a painted vignette of sunflower, bean, carrot or tulip,
            then the variety, the italic name, a ten tick germination meter,
            Sprouted and Harvest facts and the status. A garden diary of six
            dated lines sits beside the rack. Below 1000px the columns stack
            and packets go two across, and one across on a phone.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between packets, 32px between panels, a 6px gap inside each packet frame.
        density: Medium. Each packet carries a picture, a meter and two facts.
        corners: Square, 2px at most. The masthead has a pinked edge.
        borders: A 3px team colour frame plus a 1px inner frame on packets. 2px ink on panels with an inset hairline.
        shadows: A flat 4px offset tint behind packets, like card stock on a shelf.
        icons:
            Small painted plant vignettes per team built from simple shapes.
            Status boxes pair the caps word with a check in a circle for On
            track, an exclamation in a diamond for At risk and a cross in a
            square for Behind. Overdue uses the red diamond.
        focus: A 2px dashed ink outline offset 3px with a 6px mustard glow. A focused field fills pale yellow #fdf3d4.
        tone: A gardener's notes, such as Germination, Sprouted, Harvest and Sow these first.

    style86:
        number: 86
        run: 18
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Apothecary
        idea: An old pharmacy counter in black and gold on cream, where each project is a numbered bottle filled to its progress and every figure sits on a framed label with a Latin-style caption.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/86.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            cream: #f4eedd, the page
            label: #fbf7ea, labels, the day book, the register and fields
            drawer: #e9dfc4, cabinet drawer fronts
            jet: #17140f, text, the fascia, frames, bars and the primary button
            umber: #4f4536, the shelf, the cabinet body and notes
            goldLeaf: #b08d3c, inner frames, rules, bottle scales and the focus ring, never text
            goldInk: #6b5114, Latin captions on cream
            goldOnJet: #d8b968, lettering and lines on the fascia
            tincture: #c9862b, the liquid in each bottle, never text
            verdigris: #1f5f52, On track
            sienna: #8a4b0e, At risk
            carmine: #8e1b22, Behind and overdue
        type:
            Two stacks. Didone uses Didot, Bodoni 72, Bodoni MT, Big Caslon,
            Georgia, serif for the 46px greeting, 48px drawer numbers, 30px
            brand in caps tracked 0.3em, 26px section titles in caps and 18px
            bottle names, plus 12 to 14px caps tracked 0.2em for labels, nav
            and buttons. Book uses Hoefler Text, Baskerville, Georgia, serif at
            17px with 1.55 line height, with 14 to 15px italic gold ink for the
            Latin-style captions.
        layout:
            A black fascia with a doubled gold lower edge holds the spaced
            caps brand, the italic line dispensary of projects, an underlined
            search, the gold framed New project button, a round bell and the
            user. The nav sits centred below on cream, the current item in a
            double frame. The greeting is centred in a large oval label with
            a doubled gold and black ring, captioned Salve, and under it a
            tilted carmine stamp with an hourglass says 4 tasks are overdue.
            The four numbers are drawers in an umber cabinet, each with a
            framed label holder, a Latin caption, a big number and a brass
            knob. The shelf is a row of six identical bottles whose amber
            liquid rises to each percentage, with a small label showing the
            percentage and a gold scale beside, standing on a thick umber
            shelf. Under each bottle a framed card gives the roman numeral,
            name, ex team caption, tasks, due date and status. Below, a day
            book lists numbered entries and a register shows fourteen
            horizontal measures, hatched for last week and solid black for
            this week. Below 1000px bottles go three across and the lower
            panels stack, and two across on a phone.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 48px between counter sections, 16px between bottles and 8px cabinet joints.
        density: Medium. Ordered rows of identical vessels and drawers, all centred.
        corners: Square labels and drawers. Curves only in the oval greeting, the bottle shoulders and oval swatches.
        borders: A 1px jet outline with a 3px gap and an inner gold hairline on every label. A double gold rule under the fascia.
        shadows: None. Depth comes from nested frames and the umber shelf.
        icons:
            Thin line glyphs at text size. On track is a ring with a dot, At
            risk an outlined triangle, Behind a solid square and overdue an
            hourglass, each with its caps word between two hairlines.
        focus: A 2px jet outline offset 4px, a cream gap, then a 3px gold ring. On the fascia the outline is gold on jet.
        tone: Measured and old-fashioned with Latin-style captions, such as The shelf, Day book, Register, Opera activa and Attend first.

    style87:
        number: 87
        run: 18
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Hotel concierge
        idea: The dashboard arrives as a grand hotel's letter on cream stationery under an embossed crest, with every project hanging as a brass room-key fob in a pigeonhole rack and each fact put politely.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/87.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            lobby: #ebe7df, the page around the sheet
            stationery: #fdfbf6, the letter sheet
            navy: #1d2b47, text, rules, progress bars and the primary button
            slate: #55607a, notes, times and the last week line
            linenLine: #d8d2c4, hairlines, never text
            brass: #b4914d, the crest, room plates and the focus glow, never text
            brassInk: #6d5520, eyebrows and the desk bell
            fobBrass: #e7d5a6, the key fobs
            pine: #2f6045, On track
            amber: #8a5300, At risk
            burgundy: #7a1f2f, Behind and the overdue notice
        type:
            Two stacks. Garamond, EB Garamond, Baskerville, Palatino Linotype,
            Georgia, serif for everything you read, with the greeting at 44px
            italic, room numbers 40px, the brand 30px caps tracked 0.42em,
            folio numbers 30px, section titles 28px and body 18px with 1.55
            line height. Gill Sans, Optima, Segoe UI, sans-serif at 600 for
            10 to 13px caps tracked 0.2em on eyebrows, nav, floors and buttons.
        layout:
            A cream sheet up to 1140px with a navy top edge floats on a taupe
            lobby. The letterhead is centred, an embossed crest with a shield,
            a B and laurels, the spaced caps brand and an italic motto. A desk
            row between two hairlines holds an underlined search asking How may
            we help, the New project button, a desk bell and the guest name.
            The nav is one centred caps line with brass dots between items. The
            letter has a right aligned date, an italic Good morning, Mara, a
            short polite paragraph and a burgundy notice with a clock saying 4
            tasks are overdue, signed by the desk. Beside it a framed guest
            folio lists the four numbers with dotted leaders. The key rack is a
            three column grid of pigeonholes ruled in navy, each with a brass
            room plate, a hook and a brass fob rounded at the top with the
            room number 101 to 106, the floor named after the team, the
            project, tasks with a thin bar, the departure date and the status.
            Below, Messages for you shows six message slips with the sender
            and time in a side column, and a housekeeping report shows a
            dashed line for last week and a solid line for this week. Below
            960px panels stack and the rack goes two across, then one.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 56px sheet margins, 40px between letter parts and 20px inside pigeonholes.
        density: Low to medium. A letter, a folio of four lines and six fobs.
        corners: Square paper and rack. Key fobs are rounded 120px at the top and 28px at the foot.
        borders: 1px navy rules with a 4px inset linen line on the folio. Thin brass plates on each pigeonhole.
        shadows: The sheet floats on a soft 32px shadow and fobs hang with a 6px shadow. The crest has a one pixel light and dark emboss.
        icons:
            Fine 1.5px line icons and a desk bell for notifications. On track
            is a filled diamond, At risk a filled triangle, Behind a filled
            circle with a bar and overdue a clock, each in a small enamel chip
            with the caps word.
        focus: A 2px navy outline offset 3px with a 6px brass glow. A focused field gets a 2px underline and a warm fill.
        tone: Courteous and formal, such as Kindly note, We would suggest, With our compliments and Departure 14 Nov.

    style88:
        number: 88
        run: 18
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Museum placard
        idea: The dashboard hangs on a vast white gallery wall, each project a framed colour field filled to its progress with a small neat wall label beside it, and every fact given an object number.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/88.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            wall: #fbfbf9, the page
            mat: #f6f3ec, the mats inside frames
            ink: #141414, text, slim frames, this week stems and the primary button
            labelGrey: #5e5e5e, captions, object numbers and quiet nav
            hairline: #dcdbd6, room rules, never text
            walnut: #3d2b1f, wooden frames
            gilt: #b59a5b, gilt frames, never text
            terracotta: #b0563a, the Design canvas
            cobalt: #2f4f7a, the Engineering canvas
            sage: #6f7f5a, the Research canvas
            ochre: #c99a3a, the Marketing canvas
            green: #276a3a, On track
            umber: #8a5a00, At risk
            red: #a1251b, Behind and overdue
        type:
            Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Nimbus Sans, Arial, sans-serif in light
            weights. The greeting is 72px at 200 tracked minus 0.02em, framed
            numbers 56px at 200, label titles 16px at 600, body 13 to 17px at
            300 with 1.5 line height, and room headings 13px caps tracked
            0.08em. Object numbers use SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas, monospace at
            11px in grey.
        layout:
            A slim header line with the bold brand, plain grey nav links with
            the current one underlined, an underlined search, a black New
            project button, a bare bell and the user. A title wall follows with
            120px of air above, Gallery 1 as a caption, a huge light Good
            morning, Mara and the date, and on the right a wall text behind a
            thin rule with a red square saying 4 tasks are overdue. Room 1
            hangs the four numbers as small black frames with a white mat,
            each with a placard of object number, title and one line. Room 2
            hangs six projects in three columns with big gaps, frames mixing
            walnut, gilt and slim black in portrait, landscape and square
            shapes. Each canvas is a pale field with a team colour block rising
            from the bottom to the percentage under a thin black line. Under
            each work a label gives the object number BW.2026.01 to 06, the
            name, team and year in italic, tasks, percentage and due date as a
            sentence, and the status. Room 3 lists activity with times in mono
            and Room 4 hangs the chart as a framed print of thin stems with
            round heads. Below 1000px works go two across, one on a phone.
        spacing: An 8px unit in large steps. 120px between rooms, 96px between works and 64px page margins on wide screens.
        density: Very sparse. One fact per frame, one short label per work and emptiness on purpose.
        corners: Square everywhere.
        borders: Thick frames of 14px walnut or gilt, or 6px black, around a 28px mat. Elsewhere only 1px hairlines.
        shadows: A soft drop below each frame, 18px down with negative spread, as if lit from above.
        icons:
            Almost none. Tiny line marks with the status word, an open circle
            for On track, an outlined triangle for At risk, a cross for Behind
            and a solid square for overdue.
        focus: A 1px ink outline offset 6px with a 1px grey ring further out at 11px, like a museum rope.
        tone: Quiet curatorial captions, such as Room 2, Projects in progress and Visitors are advised to begin with these.

    style89:
        number: 89
        run: 19
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Exhibition catalogue
        idea: The dashboard is bound as an art catalogue of open spreads, with numbered plates for each project, catalogue entries on the facing page and wide calm margins that pair a book serif with a clean sans.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/89.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            table: #e7e5df, the surface behind the book
            page: #ffffff, every spread and the colophon
            plateGround: #f3efe7, plate backgrounds
            ink: #1b1b1b, text, rules and plate frames
            captionGrey: #616161, running heads, captions and folios
            rule: #d9d6cf, hairlines, never text
            vermilionInk: #a8321f, the primary button, the drop cap, overdue, Behind and focus
            vermilion: #c2412b, the Design plate and the this week fill
            prussian: #24476b, Engineering plates
            olive: #6d7436, the Research plate
            rose: #c98a8a, Marketing plates
            green: #2c6a3f, On track
            ochre: #8a5600, At risk
        type:
            Two stacks. The serif is Charter, Bitstream Charter, Sitka Text,
            Cambria, Iowan Old Style, Georgia, serif for the 54px greeting,
            32px page titles, 22px entry titles and 17px body with 1.6 line
            height, with italic ledes and dates. The sans is Avenir Next,
            Avenir, Segoe UI, Helvetica Neue, Arial at 300 for 64px figures
            tracked minus 0.03em, 13px plate captions, and 11px caps tracked
            0.14em for running heads, labels and statuses.
        layout:
            A slim header row on the grey table holds the brand with the italic
            line catalogue of the week, plain nav links with the current one
            underlined in vermilion, a boxed search, the New project button, a
            square bell and the user. Below sit three open book spreads, each a
            white two page sheet with a shaded gutter down the middle, 72px
            outer and 88px inner margins, a running head over a hairline on
            each page and a folio number at the foot. Spread one has the
            greeting with a vermilion drop cap essay and a diamond line saying
            4 tasks are overdue, facing The week in figures as a two by two
            table of light sans numbers with italic notes. Spread two has six
            plates in a two column grid, each a framed ground filled from the
            left to the percentage in the team colour with a black dot at the
            edge and a caption such as Plate 1, facing the catalogue with Cat.
            1 to 6 entries giving name, team, plate, due date, tasks and
            status. Spread three has a chronology on a ruled timeline facing
            Plate 7, a stepped line chart. Below 980px each spread becomes one
            column with its pages stacked.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 72px outer and 88px inner page margins, 48px under running heads and 36px between plates.
        density: Low. One subject per page, generous white space and long calm lines.
        corners: Square throughout.
        borders: 1px hairlines under running heads and between entries, and a 1px ink frame inside each plate.
        shadows: Each spread lifts off the table with a soft 40px shadow and a shaded gutter down its middle.
        icons:
            Small solid shapes with the caps word. On track is a filled
            circle, At risk a filled triangle, Behind a flat bar and overdue a
            diamond.
        focus: A 2px vermilion ink outline offset 3px. A focused field turns its border vermilion.
        tone: Curatorial and measured, such as Plates, Catalogue, Chronology, Cat. 4 and shown in plates 1 to 6.

    style90:
        number: 90
        run: 19
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Film festival
        idea: The home screen reads like a festival programme on light stock, with laurel wreaths around the week's numbers, a screening schedule grid that runs each project to its premiere, and programme codes on every film.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/90.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            screen: #f6f3ee, the page
            card: #ffffff, the top bar, the schedule and panels
            ink: #161616, text, codes and done bars
            grey: #5d5a55, notes and last week frames
            rule: #dcd6cc, the week grid and hairlines, never text
            film: #e4dfd6, the film strip and time still to go
            redCarpet: #b3202a, the top bar edge, the current nav item and this week frames
            carpetInk: #a01c25, the primary button, red text, overdue and Behind
            laurel: #8a6d1f, wreaths, never text
            green: #276638, On track
            amber: #8c5200, At risk
        type:
            Three stacks. Condensed caps use Avenir Next Condensed, Roboto
            Condensed, Arial Narrow, Helvetica Neue, Arial with font-stretch
            condensed at 800 for the 76px greeting, 52px laurel numbers, 30px
            section titles and 26px brand, and at 700 for 12 to 15px nav,
            buttons and statuses tracked 0.08 to 0.14em. Text uses Futura,
            Century Gothic, Avenir Next, Segoe UI at 16px with 1.5 line height
            and 19px bold film titles. Programme codes use SF Mono, Menlo,
            Consolas at 600 and 12px.
        layout:
            A white top bar with a 4px red lower edge holds a reel mark, the
            condensed caps brand, caps nav with the current item on a red
            block, a boxed search for the programme, the New project button, a
            square bell and the user. The hero is centred like a poster, a red
            caps line Brightwork presents, a huge condensed Good morning, Mara,
            the date in spaced caps and a red ruled line with an exclamation
            disc saying 4 tasks are overdue. The four numbers sit in a row,
            each between two gold laurel branches with the label in tiny caps
            under it. The screening schedule is a table with a black header
            row. Each row has a black code chip such as DES-01, the title, team
            and tasks, then a lane ruled by weeks from 31 Oct to 15 Jan where a
            bar runs from today to the due date labelled Premiere, filled in
            black to the percentage, with the status under it. The schedule
            scrolls sideways inside its box on narrow screens. Below, a
            festival bulletin lists activity with red mono times, and the reel
            shows the chart as a film strip with sprocket holes and one frame
            per day. Below 960px the bulletin and reel stack and laurels go two
            by two.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 56px between programme sections and 14px inside schedule rows.
        density: Medium. A big poster top, then a tight schedule grid.
        corners: Square everywhere, like printed programme boxes.
        borders: 2px ink on controls and schedule bars, a 4px red edge under the top bar and 1px rules in the grid.
        shadows: None. Flat print.
        icons:
            Gold laurel wreaths and a reel mark. On track is a star, At risk a
            triangle, Behind a square and overdue an exclamation disc, all with
            condensed caps words.
        focus: A 3px ink outline offset 2px, then a screen coloured gap and a 2px red ring out to 9px.
        tone: A festival announcer, such as Brightwork presents, Premiere 14 Nov, Screening schedule and The reel.

    style91:
        number: 91
        run: 19
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: End credits
        idea: The dashboard rolls like film end credits on a pale screen, everything centred on one axis with italic roles on the left and spaced capital names on the right, and the week's chart mirrored across the same line.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/91.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            screen: #f5f3ee, the page
            tint: #ebe8e1, the focus halo
            ink: #121212, names, rules, this week bars and the primary button
            dim: #5a5752, roles and captions
            smoke: #8e8a83, last week bars, never text
            faint: #d6d2c9, axis lines and meter tracks
            green: #2a6537, On track
            amber: #8a5400, At risk
            red: #9d2020, Behind and overdue
        type:
            Two stacks. Names use Optima, Candara, Noto Sans, Segoe UI, Arial
            in capitals, the greeting 64px at 300 tracked 0.06em, figures 44px
            at 300, project names 19px at 500 tracked 0.14em, block titles
            13px tracked 0.4em, and values 15 to 16px. Roles use Hoefler Text,
            Iowan Old Style, Georgia italic at 16 to 19px in dim grey.
        layout:
            Everything is centred on a single vertical axis with a 980px
            column. The header is a title card, the brand in capitals spaced
            0.5em, a centred nav line, then a centred underlined search, the
            New project button, a round bell and the user in italic. The
            opening reads Brightwork presents, a huge thin capital Good
            morning, Mara and the italic date, then with special attention to
            over a red clock line saying 4 tasks are overdue. Starring lists
            the four numbers as credit pairs, the italic role right aligned to
            the axis and the big figure left aligned. The projects appear as
            six credit blocks in three columns, each a spaced capital name
            over role and value pairs for Team, Progress with a thin meter,
            Tasks, Due and Status. Recent scenes pairs each time with its
            event across the axis. Running time is a mirrored bar chart, last
            week growing left in grey and this week growing right in black,
            with weekday and both dates in the middle. A closing line credits
            the Brightwork team. Below 900px blocks go two across, then one,
            and on a phone the scene pairs stack centred.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 72px between credit blocks, 32px between the role and name columns and 64px between project blocks.
        density: Sparse and slow, read top to bottom like a roll.
        corners: Square. Swatches and the bell are the only circles.
        borders: Almost none. A 48px rule under each block title and 1px underlines on fields.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            Thin marks only where they carry meaning. On track is a tick, At
            risk a triangle, Behind double down chevrons and overdue a clock,
            each beside its spaced capital word.
        focus: A 2px ink outline offset 4px with an 8px pale tint halo.
        tone: Credit roll phrasing, such as Brightwork presents, Starring, with special attention to and Running time.

    style92:
        number: 92
        run: 19
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Vinyl sleeve
        idea: The home screen is a 70s record sleeve with the greeting as the album title, the fortnight pressed into a pale vinyl disc as groove wedges, and the projects listed as tracks on side A and side B.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/92.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            shop: #efebe3, the page
            sleeve: #f8f4ea, the sleeve front, the sleeve back and panels
            paleVinyl: #e9e4d8, the record
            groove: #cfc7b7, grooves and dashed rules, never text
            ink: #1a1a1a, text, buttons and playheads
            brown: #594f44, notes and day letters
            tangerine: #e0662b, the sleeve stripe and record label, never small text
            tangerineInk: #a8420f, track numbers and overdue
            mustard: #e8b931, the sleeve stripe and the hype sticker
            teal: #1f6f73, the sleeve stripe, this week wedges and focus
            dust: #857b6c, last week wedges
            green: #24663a, On track
            amber: #8a5000, At risk
            red: #a3271c, Behind
        type:
            Three stacks. Display uses Arial Black, Helvetica Neue at 900,
            Avenir Next, Arial in lowercase tracked minus 0.04em for the 64px
            album title, 56px figures, 26px brand and 22px side headings. Text
            uses Avenir Next, Avenir, Segoe UI, Noto Sans at 16px with 1.5
            line height, 19px bold track titles and 11px bold caps tracked
            0.16em for small labels. Track numbers and percentages use SF
            Mono, Menlo, Consolas at 700 and 13 to 18px.
        layout:
            A header with a small record mark and the lowercase brand, pill
            nav with the current item filled black, a pill search, a black
            pill New project button, a round bell and a teal avatar with the
            user. The stage puts a square sleeve on the left and the record on
            the right, the record tucked a little behind the sleeve edge. The
            sleeve front has Brightwork records and a catalogue number, the
            lowercase album title good morning, mara, Released Saturday 31
            October 2026, three skewed stripes of tangerine, mustard and teal
            across the bottom and a mustard starburst sticker saying 4 tasks
            are overdue. The record is a pale disc with grooves and an orange
            label, holding fourteen wedges played clockwise from the top,
            last week in dust on the right half and this week in teal on the
            left, with counts at the tips and day letters around the label.
            The sleeve back lists the four numbers in a row over a heavy rule,
            then side A with tracks A1 to A3 and side B with B1 to B3. Each
            track has its number, title, percentage, team, tasks, due date, a
            playhead line with a ring at the percentage and the status. Liner
            notes list activity in two columns. Below 960px the record sits
            under the sleeve and the sides stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 40px sleeve padding, 14px per track and 40px between sides.
        density: Medium. One huge cover, then a compact back with six tracks.
        corners: Square sleeves. Everything you press is a full pill, and the record, label, swatches and avatar are circles.
        borders: 2px ink on controls, 3px ink rules on the sleeve back and dashed groove lines between tracks.
        shadows: The sleeve lifts with a long soft 40px shadow. No other shadows.
        icons:
            Solid simple shapes. On track is a disc, At risk a triangle,
            Behind a square and overdue a starburst like a hype sticker, each
            with its word.
        focus: A 3px teal outline offset 3px that follows the pill shape.
        tone: Record shop chatter with lowercase headings, such as side a, liner notes, Released Saturday and tracks A1 to B3.

    style93:
        number: 93
        run: 19
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Cassette J-card
        idea: The dashboard is a home-made mixtape, with the week written on a cassette label, the projects as a hand-lettered track list on a folded J-card with tape counters and reels, and the chart as segmented recording levels.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/93.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            desk: #eceef0, the page
            card: #fbfaf6, the J-card, labels and panels
            shell: #d9dce1, the cassette shell and the header
            shellLine: #9aa0aa, shell edges and fold lines, never text
            print: #222428, printed text and counters
            grey: #575c66, small print and day letters
            penBlue: #1f3a8a, handwriting, this week segments and focus
            ruledLine: #c9d3e6, label lines, never text
            labelRed: #c8323a, label stripes and the focus ring
            recordRed: #ad2530, the primary button, track numbers, overdue and Behind
            mint: #9fd8c8, a cover stripe, never text
            lilac: #c7b8e6, a cover stripe, never text
            peach: #f6c39b, a cover stripe, never text
            tape: #5a4a3a, tape wound on the reels
            green: #23663f, On track
            amber: #8a5100, At risk
        type:
            Three stacks. Handwriting uses Marker Felt, Segoe Print, Bradley
            Hand, Chalkboard SE, Comic Sans MS, cursive in pen blue for the
            52px greeting, 40px label numbers, 22px track names, times, the
            user and the search. Printed text uses Eurostile, Microgramma, Bank
            Gothic, Michroma, Verdana at 15px, with 11 to 15px bold caps
            tracked 0.2em for labels and 34px caps on the cover. Counters and
            track numbers use SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas at 700 and 15 to 18px.
        layout:
            A grey deck strip holds the brand handwritten on a white tape
            label with a red top stripe, nav as raised keys with a 3px bottom
            edge where the current key is black and pressed down, a search
            with handwritten placeholder, a red key with a record dot for New
            project, a bell key and the user in pen. The top row has Side A
            Home, a tilted handwritten Good morning, Mara, the date in caps and
            a red boxed line with a record dot saying 4 tasks are overdue.
            Beside it a cassette shell carries a label with a red, peach and
            lilac stripe, the title this week's mix and the four numbers
            handwritten over caps labels, above a tape window with two reels.
            The J-card unfolds as a front cover with diagonal pastel stripes
            and Projects mix vol. 6, a vertical spine with a red stripe, and a
            wide flap with the track list. Each track has a red mono number,
            the handwritten name, team, tasks and due date, a black three digit
            tape counter showing the percentage, two reels whose tape has
            wound from left to right by the percentage, and the status. Below,
            a recording log and a levels chart where each day is a column of
            segments, one segment per task. Below 960px the J-card panels
            stack and the spine turns horizontal.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 10px per track row and 32px between the cassette, the card and panels.
        density: Medium. Each track packs a name, a counter, reels and a status into one row.
        corners: 14px on the cassette shell, 6px on the label, 3px on keys and fields, square on the J-card.
        borders: 1px shell grey on paper, dashed fold lines between card panels and 3px bottom edges on keys like a tape deck.
        shadows: One soft drop under the J-card. Keys press down by losing their thick bottom edge.
        icons:
            Tape deck transport marks with the caps word. On track is Play, At
            risk is Pause, Behind is Rewind and overdue is the round Record
            dot.
        focus: A 2px pen blue outline offset 2px, then a card coloured gap and a 2px label red ring.
        tone: A friend's mixtape, such as this week's mix, Track list, Recording log and Rec 4 tasks are overdue.

    style94:
        number: 94
        run: 20
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Festival lineup
        idea: The dashboard printed as a music festival lineup poster, with projects billed on stage columns, headliners sized by how many tasks they carry, and set times for the team's activity.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/94.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            cream: #fff4e3, the poster paper and the page
            nightInk: #22102e, all text, rules and the primary button
            smoke: #4a3a52, meta lines and day labels
            stageTeal: #0d5c63, week one bars, On track and links
            magenta: #b3165f, week two bars, act progress bars, stage tags and nav stars
            sirenRed: #a3122a, Behind and overdue
            amberInk: #8a4b00, At risk
            sun: #f6b93b, the sunburst behind the brand and the focus glow, never text
            lilac: #ecdcf5, the box office bar and empty progress tracks
        type:
            Display is a condensed heavy sans, Avenir Next Condensed, Roboto
            Condensed, Arial Narrow, sans-serif at 800 with font-stretch
            condensed, always uppercase. Text is system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto,
            sans-serif. The brand is 56 to 150px fluid caps at 0.85 line height,
            the greeting 34 to 64px caps, summary numbers 64px, headliner names
            48px, then 36, 28 and 22px by task count, section bills 34px, body
            15px at 1.5 and labels 12px caps tracked 0.14em.
        layout:
            A slim lilac box office bar holds a Box office tag, the search field,
            New project, the bell with a count and the user. Below it a centred
            poster head has the date and presents line, the huge brand over pale
            sun rays fanning from a half sun, and caps nav links split by
            magenta stars. The greeting is centred with a red outlined warning
            box. The four numbers sit in one band between 3px ink rules, split
            by hairlines. The lineup has three stage columns, Engineering, Design
            and Research, and Marketing, each with two acts centred under a 3px
            rule, the bigger project billed larger, with meta, a magenta progress
            bar, percent and status. Below, a bar chart called Fourteen nights
            sits beside Set times, a list with the time in magenta caps and the
            person in condensed caps. Stages stack below 900px and the numbers
            go two by two on phones.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px gutters between stage columns and 48 to 56px between bands.
        density: Medium. Big type up top and tighter fine print lower down, like a poster.
        corners: Square everywhere except the round avatar and notification count.
        borders: 3px ink rules over each stage and around the numbers band, 1px ink rules between acts and set times.
        shadows: None. Depth comes from the sunburst behind the brand.
        icons:
            Solid shapes in currentColor at text size. A filled circle for On
            track, a filled triangle for At risk and a heavy cross for Behind and
            overdue, always with the caps word. Stars divide the nav.
        focus: A 3px ink outline offset 2px inside a 7px sun yellow glow.
        tone: Festival billing in caps, such as The lineup, Fourteen nights, Set times and Tonight's warning.

    style95:
        number: 95
        run: 20
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Sheet music
        idea: The dashboard engraved as a page of a printed score, with five line staves under the numbers, projects as numbered movements with tempo markings, and the fortnight's tasks as notes on a staff.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/95.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            manuscript: #fbfaf5, the score page and the style sheet
            desk: #e9e6dc, the backdrop around the page
            engraverBlack: #141414, notes, text, bar lines and the primary button
            staffGrey: #8a867c, the five staff lines, never text
            pencil: #4a463e, meta lines, captions and small numbers
            markingRed: #7d1d2c, dynamics, numbers over notes, rehearsal bars, Behind and overdue
            forest: #1e4d2b, On track
            umber: #7a4a00, At risk
            vellum: #efece2, the focus wash
        type:
            One serif family, Palatino Linotype, Book Antiqua, Palatino, Georgia,
            serif. The brand is 64px bold small caps, the greeting 42px italic,
            summary numbers 60px at 900 like a time signature, section heads
            24px bold small caps, movement names 24px italic, markings 15 to 22px
            bold italic, body 16px at 1.55 and captions 13 to 15px italic.
        layout:
            A thin top line holds the underlined search, the bell with a count
            and New project. The page is a white score sheet with wide margins on
            a grey desk. Its title block centres the brand in small caps over a
            subtitle, with Allegro moderato at top left and the date and the
            user as credits at left and right. The nav is a ruled row of links,
            each with a boxed rehearsal letter A to F, the current one filled
            black. The greeting is italic with a red sfz before the overdue
            line. The four numbers sit on one staff split into four measures by
            bar lines, each number set over five staff lines with its label
            below. Projects are six movements numbered I to VI, each row with
            the italic name and meta, a mini staff of ten note heads filled for
            each tenth done, the percent, and a tempo marking with the status.
            Below, the chart on a staff sits beside Programme notes, numbered by
            measure. Rows fold to two lines below 960px and the chart scrolls
            inside its box on phones.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 14px rows, 48 to 64px between sections and 72px page margins.
        density: Sparse. One project per line with lots of white between staves.
        corners: Square. The only curves are note heads and the fermata.
        borders: Hairline staff lines in fives, thin bar lines between measures, a thin and thick double bar to close a section, 1px ink rules under headings.
        shadows: None, apart from a 1px edge under the score page.
        icons:
            Engraving glyphs drawn in SVG. A stemmed note for On track with a
            tempo, a fermata for At risk with poco rit., and a hanging rest
            block for Behind with rall. Each status also shows its word.
        focus: A 2px black outline offset 3px with a vellum wash behind the control.
        tone: Concert programme Italian beside plain English, such as a tempo On track, The movements and Programme notes.

    style96:
        number: 96
        run: 20
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Theatre playbill
        idea: The dashboard as an open theatre programme, two framed pages under a crimson valance, with the team as the company, projects as scenes in Act I, the fortnight as Act II and activity written as stage directions.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/96.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            programmeIvory: #fbf7ef, both pages, fields and the style sheet
            foyer: #efe7da, the table behind the open programme
            crimson: #8e1b2b, the valance, act labels, week two bars, Behind and overdue
            houseInk: #1c1a1f, text, rules and frames
            usherGrey: #4d4650, subtitles, roles and cues
            brass: #7a6328, ornaments, scene numbers, inner frames and week one bars
            lampGold: #e8c66a, the focus halo, never text
            laurel: #2d5a3a, On track
            amber: #83500a, At risk
        type:
            Titles and body use Baskerville, Baskerville Old Face, Libre
            Baskerville, Georgia, serif. Labels use Optima, Candara, Segoe UI,
            sans-serif in caps tracked 0.16 to 0.3em. The brand is 34px italic,
            the greeting 44px italic, act heads 28px small caps under a 12px
            caps act label, figures 30px italic, scene names 20px, stage
            directions 16px italic, labels 11 to 12px.
        layout:
            A crimson valance holds the italic brand, an outlined search field,
            the bell, an ivory New project button, the user in caps and a row of
            caps nav links, and ends in a scalloped swag edge. Below sits an open
            programme with a five to seven column split, a soft spine shadow
            where the pages meet, and each page framed by an ink line with a
            brass rule inside. The left page has the date kicker, the greeting,
            an ornamental rule, the overdue notice, Tonight's figures as four
            dotted leader lines with large italic numbers, and The company, the
            seven people in small caps with their projects in italic. The right
            page has Act I The projects with six scenes, each name joined to its
            percent by a dotted leader, meta, status and a thin brass bar, an
            ornament marked Interval, Act II The fortnight as a slim bar chart
            topped with diamonds, and Act III From the wings with each event as
            a stage direction starting Enter. Pages stack below 900px.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 40px page margins, 32px between sections, everything on the page axis.
        density: Medium. Leader dots let names and values share long lines, as in a cast list.
        corners: Square pages and buttons. Only the valance hangs in soft scallops.
        borders: A 1px ink frame with a 3px brass rule 8px inside it on each page. Looped ornamental rules divide sections. Dotted leaders join names to values.
        shadows: Only the spine, a soft inner shadow where the pages meet, and a light lift under the spread.
        icons:
            Small solid emblems. A four pointed spark for On track, a half filled
            moon in a ring for At risk and a falling curtain triangle for Behind
            and overdue, each beside the caps word.
        focus: A 2px ink outline offset 3px inside a 6px lamp gold halo. On the valance the outline is ivory.
        tone: Front of house voice, such as Tonight's figures, The company, Interval and Enter Sam Ortiz.

    style97:
        number: 97
        run: 20
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Circus poster
        idea: The dashboard as a big-top circus bill, with a striped tent crown, figures blazing in starbursts, each project in its own ring and the ringmaster calling out the team's news.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/97.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            canvas: #fdf6e7, the page, panel stripes and tent stripes
            bigTopRed: #b5202e, tent stripes, progress rings, week two poles, ribbons, Behind and overdue
            ringmasterNavy: #1e2a5e, outlines, hard shadows, headings, links and the nav bar
            spotlightGold: #e3a51c, starbursts, pole tops, the current nav pill and the focus halo, never text
            sawdust: #f6e7c4, ring centres and the brand banner
            sawdustEdge: #e7d3a6, the empty ring track and dashed list rules
            showbillInk: #1d1a17, body text
            greasePaint: #3e3a35, meta lines and captions
            ringGreen: #1f6b45, On track
            lionAmber: #8a5300, At risk
        type:
            Display is a heavy slab, Rockwell, Roboto Slab, Clarendon, Bookman
            Old Style, Georgia, serif at 800, often in caps. Text is system-ui,
            Segoe UI, Roboto, sans-serif. The brand is 40 to 88px red caps, the
            greeting 36 to 60px navy, burst numbers 40 to 64px, ribbon heads 20px
            caps in white, project names 21px, body 15px and tags 12px caps
            tracked 0.12em.
        layout:
            The top is a big-top crown, a triangle of red and cream stripes with
            a navy edge and a gold pennant, with a sawdust banner across it cut
            with swallowtail ends holding the brand and a caps tagline with the
            date. A navy bar holds slab caps nav links, the current one a gold
            pill, a round search field, the bell, a red New project button and
            the user. The greeting is centred, with a red pill warning. The four
            numbers sit inside starbursts, gold, pink, red for overdue and pale
            blue, each with a hard navy shadow. Projects fill a white panel whose
            title is a red ribbon on its top edge, three by two, each a circus
            ring donut showing percent and tasks, with name, team and due, and a
            status pill. Below, a striped pole chart sits beside The ringmaster
            announces, a list with megaphone discs and a red Presenting tag.
            Bursts go two by two below 960px. Rings go two across on phones.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px panel padding and 32px between panels.
        density: Loud and roomy. Few items per panel, each billed large.
        corners: 16px on panels, 12px on buttons, round rings, pills and avatars, swallowtail notches on ribbons and the banner.
        borders: 3px navy outlines on every panel, button, field and ribbon.
        shadows: A hard 5px navy offset with no blur, like a second ink colour.
        icons:
            Chunky solid shapes. A pennant for On track, a diamond for At risk,
            a stop octagon with a bar cut out for Behind and overdue, each in an
            outlined pill with the caps word. A megaphone marks announcements.
        focus: A 3px navy outline offset 3px inside an 8px gold halo. On the navy bar the outline is cream.
        tone: Ringmaster patter with exclamation marks, such as Step right up, Presenting and Hold your breath.

    style98:
        number: 98
        run: 20
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Board game
        idea: The dashboard laid out as a family board game, with a checkered track round the board, each project racing a pawn along its own lane, dice for the totals and a rule card that explains the statuses.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/98.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            boardCream: #f7f1df, the play area, squares and fields
            table: #e9e4d4, the page around the board
            feltGreen: #2f6b3f, the header, the board frame and sheet labels
            gameInk: #1f1d1a, text, outlines, lips and pips
            pencil: #4a453d, captions and meta lines
            redPiece: #c8452f, the Design lane and week two tiles
            bluePiece: #1f4e9c, the Engineering lane, week one tiles and links
            purplePiece: #7a4fa3, the Research lane
            greenPiece: #2f7a46, the Marketing lane and On track
            yellowPiece: #e0a91a, the primary button, the player's pawn and the focus halo, never text
            stopRed: #a8261b, Behind and overdue
            waitAmber: #86520a, At risk
        type:
            One rounded sans, Nunito, Varela Round, Arial Rounded MT Bold,
            Trebuchet MS, system-ui, sans-serif. Headings are 800 and body 500.
            The greeting is 28 to 40px, dice numbers 56px, card titles 22px,
            lane names 18px, body 15px and labels 12px caps.
        layout:
            A felt green header holds a die logo and the brand, pill nav links
            with the current one cream, a cream search field, the bell, a yellow
            New project pill and the user with a yellow pawn. The page is one big
            board, a green frame with a checkered strip of red, blue, yellow and
            green squares at top and bottom around a cream play area. Inside, a
            Player one kicker, the greeting Good morning, Mara. Your move., and a
            red box for the overdue tasks. The four numbers are white dice tiles
            with corner pips, the overdue die solid red. The main column is The
            race to done, six lanes, each a white card with a coloured number
            badge, name, meta, percent and status, over a track of ten squares
            tinted to the pawn, which stands on its tenth, and a chequered flag
            square at the end. The side column has a dashed yellow Rule card that
            explains each status and Tiles won per day, a chart of stacked
            squares. Below, the Turn log shows six cream cells with coloured
            pawns. Columns stack below 1000px.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px inside chips, 24px card padding and 28 to 32px between bands.
        density: Medium. Each project is one lane of ten squares, the side column holds small cards.
        corners: 12px on cards, 18px on dice, 6px on track squares, pill buttons and nav, round pawns.
        borders: 3px ink outlines on cards, dice and buttons, 2px on track squares, a dashed border on the rule card.
        shadows: A chunky 0 4px 0 ink lip under cards, dice and buttons, like moulded plastic.
        icons:
            Solid game shapes with ink outlines. Pawns stand for people, pips sit
            on dice and a chequered flag marks the finish. A play arrow for On
            track, pause bars for At risk and a rewind for Behind and overdue,
            each in an outlined pill with the word.
        focus: A 3px ink outline offset 3px inside a 7px yellow halo. In the header the outline is white.
        tone: Game rules language, such as Your move, Turn log, Miss a turn and Go back.

    style99:
        number: 99
        run: 21
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Playing cards
        idea: The dashboard dealt onto a light sage card table, with every project a playing card whose suit is its status, the totals held as a fanned hand and the fortnight stacked in chips.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/99.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            sageFelt: #dfe8d8, the card table and the page
            feltShade: #c9d6c0, the top rail and card lips
            cardWhite: #fffdf8, cards, panels and fields
            cardInk: #16130f, text and outlines
            tableGrey: #38423a, captions and meta
            clubGreen: #1e5b3a, the club suit for On track
            diamondAmber: #8a4b00, the diamond suit for At risk
            spadeRed: #9b1c1c, the spade suit for Behind, overdue and week two chips
            chipBlue: #2c4f8a, week one chips, card back avatars, links and the primary button
            brass: #c9a44a, the focus halo, never text
        type:
            Indices and names use Georgia, Cambria, Times New Roman, serif in
            bold. Text uses Gill Sans, Gill Sans MT, Seravek, Calibri, Segoe UI,
            sans-serif. The greeting is 32 to 48px, hand ranks 46px, section
            heads 26px, card corner indices 18px, card names 18px, body 15px and
            caps labels 11 to 13px tracked 0.14em.
        layout:
            A sage rail holds a small white card logo with a diamond, the brand,
            nav links with an underline on the current one, a white search
            field, the bell, a blue New project button and the user as a blue
            card back with initials. The top is split in two, the date, greeting
            and a white overdue slip on the left, and the four totals on the
            right as a fanned hand of white cards turned from minus 9 to 9
            degrees, each with a corner rank, a big number and a caps label,
            the overdue card in red. The deal is a row of six playing cards on
            the felt, each 5 by 7.4 with an inner hairline frame, the percent
            and suit as corner indices top left and upside down bottom right,
            and the team, name, a large suit pip, percent, tasks, due and status
            in the middle. Below, Chips won stacks poker chips per day beside
            Hand history, a list with card back avatars. Cards go three across
            below 1100px, the hand straightens into a two by two grid on phones
            and cards go two across.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 20px between cards, 16px inside a card and 40 to 48px between sections.
        density: Roomy. Six cards in one row on a wide table.
        corners: 10px on cards and panels, 8px on buttons and fields, 5px on card back avatars, round chips.
        borders: A 1px warm grey card edge with an inner hairline frame 6px in.
        shadows: Cards cast 0 2px 0 felt shade plus 0 8px 18px rgba(30,50,30,0.18). Hand cards lift a little more.
        icons:
            The suit shapes drawn solid in SVG. Club for On track, diamond for At
            risk and spade for Behind and overdue, each with its word. People are
            blue card backs with diagonal stripes and initials.
        focus: A 2px ink outline offset 2px inside a 6px brass halo.
        tone: Card room words in plain sentences, such as The deal, Chips won, Hand history and Play those first.

    style100:
        number: 100
        run: 21
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Tarot
        idea: The dashboard read as a gentle tarot spread on pale lavender parchment, with arched gold-lined cards, roman numerals and fine line drawings, and the fortnight drawn as two constellations.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/100.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            lavenderParchment: #f6f2fb, the page
            cardCream: #fffdf6, cards, panels and fields
            nightIndigo: #2a2350, text, numerals, the primary button and week two stars
            dusk: #4f4870, meta lines, captions and axis labels
            goldInk: #7a5a12, small gold text, numerals on cards and week one stars
            goldLeaf: #b8913a, frames, rules and line art, never text
            mist: #e7def2, the progress track and the focus halo
            sage: #2f5d46, On track
            amber: #8a4e0b, At risk
            garnet: #9b2335, Behind and overdue
        type:
            Capitals and numerals use Trajan Pro, Optima, Palatino Linotype,
            Palatino, Georgia, serif, uppercase and tracked 0.1 to 0.3em. Text
            uses Iowan Old Style, Palatino Linotype, Palatino, Georgia, serif.
            The brand is 30 to 54px caps tracked 0.3em, the greeting 34 to 48px
            italic, altar numbers 52px, section heads 15px caps tracked 0.24em
            over a 15px italic subtitle, card names 14px caps, body 16px at 1.6
            and numerals 12 to 15px.
        layout:
            The header is centred. A top row holds a pill search field, the bell,
            an indigo pill New project with a gold inner ring, and the user in a
            gold ringed disc. Below sit a line crest with a moon, the spaced caps
            brand and caps nav links with a small star before the current one.
            The greeting is centred under a gold caps line, The reading for
            Saturday 31 October 2026, with a garnet italic warning. The four
            totals stand as an altar of four arched windows I to IV with large
            numerals. The spread is a row of six arched cards, each with a gold
            frame and a second hairline frame inside, a roman numeral at the top,
            a gold line drawing, a star, a wheel, a lantern, scales, a blossom or
            a winged letter, and the name in caps on a rule at the base. Under
            each card sit team and due, a thin indigo progress bead, percent and
            tasks, and the status. Below, a constellation chart sits beside
            Recent signs, a list marked with small gold stars. Cards go three
            across below 1100px and two across on phones.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 20px between cards, 40 to 64px between sections and generous margins inside frames.
        density: Calm and sparse. Little text on each card.
        corners: Arched tops on cards and altar windows, a 50 percent horizontal radius over 56 to 80px, with 6px base corners. Buttons and fields are pills.
        borders: A 1px gold leaf frame with a second hairline 5px inside, like a printed card border.
        shadows: One soft violet lift, 0 6px 20px rgba(42,35,80,0.10), on cards and panels.
        icons:
            Fine 1.2px gold line drawings for the cards. Status marks are solid,
            a sun with rays for On track, a crescent moon for At risk and a
            lightning bolt for Behind and overdue, each beside caps words.
        focus: A 2px indigo outline offset 3px inside a 6px mist halo.
        tone: Soft and a little ceremonial but plain, such as The reading, The spread and Recent signs.

    style101:
        number: 101
        run: 21
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Chess notation
        idea: The dashboard kept like a tournament scoresheet, with board files for navigation, the totals on a checkered rank, projects in a standings table with chess pieces and annotation marks, and activity written as numbered moves.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/101.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            scoresheet: #fbfaf7, the page, tables and fields
            ink: #161616, text, rules, week two squares and the primary button
            graphite: #3b3b3b, meta, legends and axis labels
            walnut: #6b4a2b, dark board squares, week one squares and file letters
            lightSquare: #f1e9da, light board squares and header cells
            darkSquare: #e2d4bb, empty dark squares on the chart and the focus halo
            green: #24603e, On track
            amber: #8a5200, At risk
            red: #a02020, Behind and overdue
        type:
            Headings use Futura, Century Gothic, Avenir Next, Segoe UI,
            sans-serif. Body uses Georgia, serif. Notation and numbers use
            ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas, monospace. The greeting is 30
            to 44px Futura at 500, summary numbers 52px mono bold, block heads
            18px Futura caps tracked 0.14em, project names 16px Georgia, notation
            14px mono and legends 13px Georgia.
        layout:
            The header has a king glyph and the caps brand at left and a mono
            search field, the bell and a black New project button at right. A
            ruled scoresheet table below gives Player Mara Okafor and the date.
            The nav is a full width row of ruled cells, each with a walnut file
            letter a to f, the current cell filled black. The greeting sits left
            with Check. 4 tasks are overdue at right. The four totals are one
            checkered rank of alternating light and walnut squares in a 2px ink
            frame. Standings is a ruled table with number, a chess piece for the
            team, project and team, tasks as 18/25, a rank of eight squares
            filled for progress with the percent, due date and status, with
            striped rows. Below, Fourteen ranks, two checkered boards of seven
            files each filled one square per task, sits beside Moves, a numbered
            list with a short walnut mono code, the plain sentence and the time.
            On phones the table becomes stacked rows and the nav wraps into
            three cells across.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 8 to 10px table cell padding and 40px between blocks.
        density: Dense and orderly, like a scoresheet. Tables carry most of the content.
        corners: Square everywhere.
        borders: 1px ink rules for tables and the nav, 2px ink rules under block heads and around the totals rank.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            Unicode chess pieces for teams, a bishop for Design, a rook for
            Engineering, a knight for Research and a queen for Marketing, and a
            king for the brand. Annotation marks are drawn in SVG, an
            exclamation in a circle for On track, a query and exclamation in a
            diamond for At risk, and a double query in a solid square for Behind
            and overdue, each with the word.
        focus: A 3px ink outline offset 2px inside a 6px dark square halo.
        tone: Terse tournament shorthand with a plain sentence beside it, such as Check, Standings, Fourteen ranks and Moves.

    style102:
        number: 102
        run: 21
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Crossword
        idea: The dashboard set as a newspaper crossword, with the brand and totals written into numbered squares, the fortnight filled in on a grid split by black squares, projects as the Across clues and activity as the Down clues.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/102.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            newsprint: #fbfbf8, the page
            squareWhite: #ffffff, grid squares, the header and fields
            blackSquare: #111111, text, grid lines, the divider column and the primary button
            pencil: #444444, clue lengths, axis labels and notes
            deepBlue: #8db1de, filled squares this week on the grid
            wordBlue: #bcd3ee, filled squares last week, progress squares, first answer squares and the current nav tab
            paleBlue: #e3ebf5, the highlighted first clue in each list
            cursorYellow: #ffe36b, the active first brand square and the focus fill
            green: #1d6b3a, On track
            amber: #8a5300, At risk
            red: #b3261e, Behind and overdue
        type:
            Labels and grid letters use Franklin Gothic Medium, Libre Franklin,
            Arial, sans-serif. Clues use Georgia, Times New Roman, serif. Brand
            letters are 22px bold in 36px squares, the greeting 30 to 44px bold,
            answer digits 30px bold in 48px squares, clue heads 16px caps, clue
            text 16px Georgia, lengths 14px grey and square numbers 9px bold.
        layout:
            A white header spells BRIGHTWORK in ten squares inside a 3px frame,
            the first square yellow with a tiny 1. At right are a Find a clue
            labelled search field, the bell, a black New project button and the
            user. The nav is a row of plain links, the current one a blue tab.
            The greeting has a caps edition line and a red overdue line. The four
            totals sit in a ruled band as answers, each written digit by digit in
            framed squares with a clue number, then a caps clue such as 1 Across
            and the label with its length. The puzzle below has three columns.
            The grid is the chart, fourteen columns of squares split by a black
            column between weeks, filled from the bottom one square per task,
            with the count in the top filled square. Across lists the six
            projects as numbered clues with team, tasks and due, the percent as
            the length, and a row of ten progress squares with the status. Down
            lists the six activity items with the time as the length. The grid
            spans the top below 1100px and all stacks below 700px.
        spacing: An 8px unit. Squares are 22 to 48px, 8px between clues and 32px between columns.
        density: Dense like a puzzle page.
        corners: Square everywhere.
        borders: 1px black square edges, a 3px black outer frame on every grid and answer, a 2px rule under clue heads.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            Plain geometric marks in currentColor. An open circle for On track,
            an open triangle for At risk and a solid square for Behind and
            overdue, each with the caps word.
        focus: A 3px black outline with the control filled cursor yellow, like the active square.
        tone: Puzzle setter's voice, such as Find a clue, Across the projects and Solve those first.

    style103:
        number: 103
        run: 21
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Dominoes
        idea: The dashboard laid out in ivory and black domino tiles, with every total spelled in pips, each project a long tile with a pip track for progress, and the fortnight stood up as a row of dominoes whose height is the day's count.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/103.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            tableIvory: #f3eee2, the page
            tileIvory: #fffaf0, ivory tiles, the header, panels and fields
            tileBlack: #161513, text, outlines, black tiles, pips on ivory and the primary button
            pipIvory: #fbf6ea, pips and text on black tiles
            feltGrey: #4a463d, captions, meta and axis labels
            spinnerBrass: #b08d3c, the centre spinner dot on summary tiles and the focus halo, never text
            bone: #ddd5c3, empty pip slots and tile lips
            green: #1f5f3e, On track
            amber: #865100, At risk
            red: #a3231b, Behind and overdue
        type:
            Avenir Next, Avenir, Montserrat, Segoe UI, sans-serif, at 700 with
            tabular figures for numbers and headings and 400 for text. The
            greeting is 30 to 44px, summary numbers 40px, tile percents 44px,
            project names 18px, body 15px and caps labels 11 to 13px tracked
            0.12 to 0.14em.
        layout:
            An ivory header with a 3px black base holds a small black domino
            logo and the brand, pill nav links with the current one black, a
            search field, the bell, a black New project pill and the user as a
            tiny two half domino with initials. The greeting sits left with a
            black overdue tile at right. The four totals are domino tiles that
            spell each number in pips, 0 and 6, 2 and 3, a black 0 and 4, and a
            three half 1, 8 and 6 tile, each above its numeral and label. The
            projects are long tiles in two columns, a left half with the big
            percent and a right half with name, meta, a track of ten pips filled
            for each tenth done and the status. The Behind project is turned to
            the black side. Below, the fortnight shows a standing domino per day,
            two pip columns tall with one pip per task, ivory for last week and
            black for this week, beside Line of play, a list with initial
            dominoes. Projects go one column below 1000px.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px between tiles, 16 to 24px tile padding and 40px between sections.
        density: Medium. Two columns of long project tiles and a row of standing tiles.
        corners: 12px on tiles and panels, 5 to 6px on small dominoes, round pips, pill buttons and nav.
        borders: 3px black outlines with a 2px black or ivory centre line between halves.
        shadows: Tiles sit on a bone lip, 0 4px 0 #ddd5c3, plus a soft 0 8px 16px rgba(22,21,19,0.08) on project tiles.
        icons:
            Solid pips and simple shapes in currentColor. A round pip for On
            track, a diamond for At risk and a cross for Behind and overdue, each
            in an outlined pill with the word. People are tiny dominoes with an
            initial on each half.
        focus: A 3px black outline offset 3px inside a 7px brass halo.
        tone: Short and steady, such as Line of play and Ten pips per tile.

    style104:
        number: 104
        run: 22
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Toy bricks
        idea: The dashboard is built from chunky interlocking plastic bricks on a studded baseplate, so every panel, number and progress bar snaps together in primary colours.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/104.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            baseplate: #e9eaec, the page, tiled with #dcdee2 studs every 24px
            brickRed: #c8191f, the current nav brick, the overdue alert and number, Behind chips, white text
            brickBlue: #0b5cad, the top bar, progress studs and this week bars, white text
            brickYellow: #f6c90e, the primary button, the avatar, At risk chips, last week bars and the focus halo, dark text only
            brickGreen: #1e7a3c, the active projects brick and On track chips, white text
            brickWhite: #fbfbf8, panels, nav bricks, the search tile and fields
            ink: #1b1b1b, text and the focus ring
            slate: #4a4d52, meta lines, captions and day letters
        type:
            Two stacks. Display uses Arial Rounded MT Bold, Nunito, Varela
            Round, Trebuchet MS, system-ui in bold. Text uses system-ui, Segoe
            UI, Roboto, Arial. The greeting is 40px at 1.05, summary numbers
            56px, panel titles 24px, project names 19px, body 16px at 1.45,
            meta 14px, chip labels 13px bold.
        layout:
            The page background is a grey baseplate of round studs. The header
            is one long blue brick holding a two brick logo, a smooth white
            search tile, a yellow New project brick, a round white bell stud
            with a red count and a yellow MO stud with the name. Below it the
            nav is a row of small white bricks with their own studs, and the
            current Home brick is red and raised 6px. A wide white plate holds
            the greeting Hi Mara, let's build, the date, and a red brick that
            says 4 tasks are overdue with a cross. The four numbers are bricks
            of lengths 3, 4, 3 and 4 in green, yellow, red and blue. The main
            area has a wide white Projects plate on the left, where each project
            row has a name, a meta line, a status chip brick and a progress
            track filled with blue studs plus the percent. On the right a
            Tasks completed plate shows 14 bars built as stacks of one task
            bricks, yellow for last week and blue for this week, with a small
            stud on top and the value above. An Activity plate lists six items
            with round coloured initial studs. Below 960px the plates stack
            and the numbers go two by two. Below 600px the search drops to its
            own row.
        spacing: A 4px unit on a 24px stud grid. Panels pad 20px, gaps of 12 and 24px.
        density: Medium. Big bricks and clear rows, one project per row.
        corners: 4px on every brick, round studs, round avatar and bell.
        borders: None. Rows divide with a 3px stud grey groove.
        shadows: Each brick has a 6px darker inset lip along its bottom and a hard 3px drop below, with no blur.
        icons:
            Solid filled shapes in currentColor at about 14px. A round stud for
            On track, a triangle for At risk, a square for Behind and a thick
            cross for overdue, always with the word. Studs are a row of round
            bumps along the top edge of each brick in the brick colour.
        focus: A 4px ink outline offset 3px inside a 9px yellow halo, on bricks, fields and rows alike.
        tone: Cheerful build talk, such as Let's build and One brick is one task.

    style105:
        number: 105
        run: 22
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Felt patches
        idea: The dashboard is a craft fair table of cut felt shapes, each sewn down with a running stitch, so numbers sit in round badges and progress is a line of thread.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/105.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            linen: #efe6d4, the page, with a faint woven crosshatch
            creamFelt: #f8f1e2, project patches, the activity strip, the chart patch, the search and the sheet
            tealFelt: #2f6a6b, the sidebar ribbon, thread progress and this week columns, white text
            mustardFelt: #d9a93a, the current tab, the bell and last week columns, dark text only
            sageFelt: #a9c3a4, the greeting pennant and the avatar, dark text
            roseFelt: #9c3d4e, the primary button, the overdue badge and activity bullets, white text
            bark: #2f2a24, text, stitches and the focus outline
            twine: #5e5348, meta lines and times
            okTint: #dfe9dc, the On track chip with #23524f text
            riskTint: #f3e2b8, the At risk chip with #6e4d00 text
            badTint: #f1d9dd, the Behind chip with #82283a text
        type:
            Two stacks. Text uses Gill Sans, Gill Sans MT, Trebuchet MS,
            Calibri, Segoe UI. The greeting and section titles use Iowan Old
            Style, Georgia, Times New Roman in italic 600. The greeting is 40px
            at 1.1, badge numbers 52px serif bold, section titles 28px, patch
            titles 19px humanist bold, body 17px at 1.5, meta 14px.
        layout:
            A 220px teal felt ribbon on the left holds the brand with a star
            button logo and six nav tabs cut as cream felt with uneven corners,
            the current one mustard with a heart. The main column starts with
            a cream felt search pill, a rose New project button, a round
            mustard bell and a sage MO circle. The greeting is a wide sage felt
            pennant with a notched right end, Good morning, Mara in italic serif,
            the date, and a small cream tag in rose that says 4 tasks are overdue
            with a diamond. The four numbers are round stitched felt badges in
            teal, mustard, rose and cream, two of them slightly wobbly. Below,
            Projects on the table shows six cream patches two across, each cut
            with different corner radii and tilted under one degree, with the
            name, meta, a thread progress line ending in a button knot, the
            percent in serif and a status chip. On the right, Around the table
            is a cream felt strip of six activity rows with rose dots, then a
            felt chart patch with 14 rounded columns outlined by a dashed stitch.
            Below 1040px the ribbon becomes a top band with wrapped tabs. Below
            640px badges go two by two and patches go one across.
        spacing: An 8px unit. Patches pad 22px, gaps of 20 and 32px.
        density: Relaxed. Two patches across with plenty of linen between.
        corners: Uneven hand cut radii between 10 and 34px, every patch different. Badges are circles or slightly squashed circles.
        borders: No outer border. A 2px dashed running stitch sits 7px inside every felt shape, pale on dark felt.
        shadows: A soft 6px blur under each patch and a 2px lip, like felt resting on cloth. Felt carries a fine speckled texture.
        icons:
            Filled craft shapes at about 22px. A two hole button for On track,
            a triangle with a mark for At risk, a square with a stitched cross
            for Behind and a diamond with a mark for overdue, always with the
            word.
        focus: A 3px dashed bark outline offset 4px inside a soft 10px mustard halo. A focused field turns its dashed edge solid.
        tone: Warm and handmade, such as Around the table and Good morning.

    style106:
        number: 106
        run: 22
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Cross-stitch
        idea: The dashboard is an embroidered sampler on aida cloth, where every bar and border is counted out one cross stitch at a time on an 8px grid.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/106.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            aida: #f7f3e8, the cloth, with an 8px grid and #e4dccb holes at each corner
            fineLinen: #fffdf8, the count panel, the chart box, fields and the sheet
            navyFloss: #1d2d50, text, this week crosses, numbers and the primary button
            backstitch: #23395f, dashed rules and dividers
            redFloss: #a3263a, the current nav, overdue, Behind and the dashed focus outline
            greenFloss: #2e6b3a, On track and the heading motifs
            goldFloss: #8a5a00, At risk text, with #a06d12 crosses for last week
            hoopWood: #c99a5b, the greeting hoop ring, decoration only
            greyFloss: #4d4a44, meta, dates and times
        type:
            Two stacks. Labels, numbers and nav use ui-monospace, SF Mono,
            Menlo, Consolas, Liberation Mono. Text uses Baskerville,
            Baskerville Old Face, Hoefler Text, Georgia. Counts are 64px mono
            800, the greeting 32px serif bold on a 40px line, section titles
            14px mono caps tracked 0.2em, project names 17px serif bold, body
            16px on a 24px line, meta 12px mono.
        layout:
            A plain header row holds a stitched X logo, Brightwork in mono, a
            navy bordered search box, a navy New project button, a square bell
            with a red count and a green bordered MO square. The nav is mono
            caps, with Home in red led by a single cross and a dashed underline,
            and a dashed backstitch rule closes the header. The dashboard sits
            inside a sampler frame stitched all round with a repeating red,
            navy and green cross border. At the top a round wooden embroidery
            hoop holds Welcome back, Hello, Mara, the date and 4 tasks are
            overdue with a pixel X. Beside it a navy bordered panel splits into
            2 by 2 with dashed dividers for the four counts. Projects is one
            row per project with name and meta, a 25 cell chart bar filled with
            cross stitches in the status colour, the percent and the status.
            Below, two columns hold Tasks done in a linen box, where each day
            is a single column of crosses one per task, gold then navy, and
            Latest stitches, six activity rows each led by a red or green cross.
            Section titles are flanked by three green crosses and a backstitch
            line. Below 1000px the hoop centres above the counts and project
            rows put the bar on its own line.
        spacing: An 8px stitch unit. Every size and gap is a whole number of stitches, 8, 16, 24 and 40px.
        density: Medium. Projects are single stitched rows, numbers sit in a 2 by 2 panel.
        corners: Square everywhere except the round greeting hoop.
        borders: 2px solid navy for panels, 2px dashed backstitch for rules and a 16px cross stitched border around the sampler.
        shadows: None. The cloth is flat. The hoop has a darker wood ring inside and out.
        icons:
            Pixel motifs drawn on an 8 by 8 grid with crisp edges at 16px. A
            stitched tick for On track, a stepped solid triangle for At risk, a
            hollow square with a centre block for Behind and a pixel X for
            overdue, always with the caps word. Crosses are an 8px SVG X tile.
        focus: A 2px dashed red outline offset 4px with an 8px aida gap and a 2px navy ring outside it.
        tone: Quiet needlework words, such as Latest stitches and 1 cross = 1 task.

    style107:
        number: 107
        run: 22
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Patchwork quilt
        idea: The dashboard is one bound quilt, its blocks butted edge to edge in homey fabrics, each with a muslin centre that holds a number, a project or the chart.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/107.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            calico: #f6efe2, the page behind the quilt
            muslin: #fffaf0, block centres, the nav and the header strip
            denim: #2f4f7a, the quilt binding, section strips, progress patches and the focus ring
            barnRed: #9b2f2a, the brand label, the primary button, Behind and overdue
            butter: #f2d58a, the stripe fabric, the bell and the current tab
            sage: #8fae8b, half square triangles and the sprig fabric
            fern: #1f5a33, the On track tag
            toffee: #7a4a00, the At risk tag
            ink: #2b2622, text and block edges
            thread: #5a5048, meta and times
        type:
            Two stacks. Headings and numbers use Rockwell, Roboto Slab, Zilla
            Slab, Georgia in bold. Text uses Avenir Next, Avenir, Segoe UI,
            system-ui. The greeting is 38px at 1.1, numbers 52px, block titles
            19px, section strips 22px, body 16px at 1.5, meta 14px.
        layout:
            The header is a muslin strip framed in denim with a barn red label
            block holding a pieced square logo and Brightwork, then the search,
            New project, a butter bell and a triangle pieced MO avatar. Under it
            the nav is six equal muslin cells split by dashed quilting lines,
            the current cell filled with butter stripe and the word in a small
            boxed label. The quilt has a 12px denim binding with a dashed stitch
            inside and four columns of blocks with no gaps. A wide medallion
            block framed in red half square triangles holds Welcome home, Mara,
            the date and a red outlined 4 tasks are overdue with an octagon.
            Four log cabin blocks in blue gingham, butter stripe, red gingham
            and sprig hold the numbers in muslin centres. A denim strip titles
            Projects, then six blocks three across, each a fabric frame around
            a muslin centre with name, meta, ten little denim patches for
            progress, the percent and a dashed status tag. The last row pairs a
            gingham chart block, where 14 dashed day columns hold butter stripe
            or denim dot bars, with a sprig block for News from the sewing
            circle. Below 980px the quilt is two columns, below 640px one.
        spacing: An 8px unit. Fabric frames are 16 to 20px wide around each muslin centre.
        density: Medium. Blocks touch with no gaps, like a finished quilt top.
        corners: Square, 2px at most on controls.
        borders: A 12px denim binding with a dashed stitch inside, 2px ink edges on centres and 1.5px dashed quilting lines.
        shadows: None. Texture comes from fabric patterns made with gradients, gingham, dots, stripe, half square triangles and sprig.
        icons:
            Solid shapes with white marks at 16px. A ticked circle for On
            track, a triangle for At risk, a square with a down arrow for
            Behind and an octagon for overdue, inside a dashed tag with the word.
        focus: A 3px denim outline offset 3px, a 6px muslin gap and a 3px barn red ring outside.
        tone: Homey and kind, such as Welcome home and News from the sewing circle.

    style108:
        number: 108
        run: 22
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Knitting pattern
        idea: The dashboard reads like a printed knitting pattern, with row counters for numbers, yarn ball bands for projects, stitch charts for progress and pattern abbreviations for status.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/108.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            paper: #fdfcf8, the booklet page
            table: #ece9e1, behind the page
            charcoal: #2a2a2e, text, rules, stitch marks and the primary button
            chartGrid: #c9c6bd, chart cells and dotted rules, decoration only
            heatherBlue: #3d5a80, last week stitches and the focus halo
            rose: #a23e50, this week stitches, row labels, the progress marker, Behind and overdue
            moss: #4f6b3a, On track
            ochre: #8a5300, At risk
            counter: #e9e4d8, row counter bodies
            graphite: #5c5a55, meta and abbreviations
        type:
            Three stacks. Titles, labels and nav use Futura, Century Gothic,
            Avenir Next, Trebuchet MS. Text uses Charter, Bitstream Charter,
            Sitka Text, Cambria, Georgia. Counters, facts and abbreviations use
            ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas. The title is 46px geometric
            500, counter digits 26px mono 600, band titles 19px geometric 600,
            section heads 13px geometric caps tracked 0.16em, body 16px serif
            at 1.55, facts 13px mono.
        layout:
            A white booklet page on a beige table with a soft shadow. A runner
            line holds a yarn ball logo, an underline search, a black Cast on a
            project button, a round outlined bell and a round MO. The nav is
            geometric caps over a double rule, Home bold with a rose underline.
            The title block reads Pattern of the week with the date in rose
            caps, Good morning, Mara, a line about six projects, and on the
            right a boxed gauge note with a crossed box and 4 tasks are overdue.
            A 300px left column shows Row counters, four barrel counters with
            three white digit windows each, 006, 023, 004 in rose, and 186,
            beside their labels, then an Abbreviations box defining ot, ar, bh,
            od, sts and co with their glyphs. The main column lists six yarn
            ball bands, each a white band with heathered diagonal yarn ends in
            its own colour, the name, a status pill, a mono line of Fibre, sts
            and co, and a 20 stitch chart row filled with V stitches to the
            percent and marked with a rose line. Chart A is a knitting chart
            grid with columns of V stitches, heather then rose, row numbers on
            the right and day letters below. Instructions so far lists the six
            activity items as Row 1 to Row 6.
        spacing: An 8px unit with a 10px stitch cell in charts. Page margins 48px.
        density: Medium high. Pattern like columns with small mono facts.
        corners: Square paper and bands. Round bell and avatar, pill status tags and soft 14px counter bodies.
        borders: 1.5px charcoal lines, a double rule under the nav and dotted grid rules between rows.
        shadows: Only the page lifts off the table with a soft shadow. Counters have a small inset lip.
        icons:
            Chart key glyphs at 12px. An open ring for On track, a solid
            triangle for At risk, a solid square for Behind and a crossed box for
            overdue, in a pill with the word.
        focus: A 2px charcoal outline offset 2px, a 5px paper gap and a 2px heather blue ring.
        tone: Pattern shorthand, such as sts 18 of 25, co 14 Nov, Row 3 and Cast on a project.

    style109:
        number: 109
        run: 23
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Garment labels
        idea: Projects hang from a clothes rail as woven labels, numbers are size tags, the greeting is a kraft swing tag, and every status is a care symbol sewn on a satin strip.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/109.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            closetWall: #f0eeea, the page
            navyWeave: #1f2a44, the neck label header, navy labels, size tags, text and the chart
            creamWeave: #f4ecd8, the nav strip, cream labels, the chart label and label text on navy
            redWeave: #8e1f2b, the primary button, the overdue tag and the Behind label
            satin: #fbfbf9, care strips, the activity label and the sheet
            kraft: #d9c3a0, the greeting swing tag with #2b2117 text
            goldThread: #c9b98f, frames around numbers on navy and the focus halo
            green: #2e6a45, the On track care mark
            amber: #8a5200, the At risk care mark
            greyPrint: #4f4f52, satin label print and meta
        type:
            Two stacks. Labels use Avenir Next Condensed, Roboto Condensed,
            Arial Narrow, Helvetica Neue, Arial with font-stretch condensed,
            mostly uppercase and tracked 0.06 to 0.26em. Text uses Helvetica
            Neue, Helvetica, Arial, system-ui. The swing tag title is 40px
            condensed caps, size numbers 44px, label titles 18px caps, the
            brand 26px caps tracked 0.26em, section heads 15px caps tracked
            0.24em, body 15px at 1.5.
        layout:
            The header is a woven navy neck label with a gold framed spaced caps
            brand and star, a cream search, a red New project button, a gold
            outlined bell and a cream MO square. The nav is a cream strip of caps
            cells split by dashed seams, the current cell navy. The top row pairs
            a kraft swing tag with clipped left corners and a punched hole,
            holding the date, Hello, Mara, a line about the collection and a
            dashed Care note with an iron icon saying 4 tasks are overdue, with
            four woven size tags, three navy and one red, each a gold framed
            number over a caps label. On the rail shows a grey metal rod with
            six tall narrow labels hanging from wire loops, alternating navy,
            cream and red, each with a darker fold at the top, the caps name,
            department, a boxed percent like a size, a woven progress bar, Tasks
            and Due rows, and a satin care strip sewn at the bottom with the care
            symbol and status word. Below, a cream jacquard label with stitched
            ends holds the chart, hatched bars for last week and solid navy bars
            for this week, and a long satin care label with a pinked bottom edge
            lists the activity centred. Below 1100px labels go three across,
            below 640px two.
        spacing: An 8px unit. Labels pad 16 to 22px, 16px between labels on the rail.
        density: Medium. Six tall narrow labels in one row on wide screens.
        corners: Square cut fabric. The swing tag has clipped corners and a punched hole, hanger loops are round.
        borders: 1.5px gold or cream frames around numbers, dashed seam lines where strips are sewn on, a woven weft texture on labels.
        shadows: None, except a 1px lift on the satin label.
        icons:
            Laundry care style marks at about 22 by 18px. A square with a filled
            dot for On track, an outlined triangle with a mark for At risk, a
            filled tub with a down arrow for Behind and an iron for overdue,
            always beside the caps word.
        focus: A 2px navy outline offset 3px inside a 6px gold halo. On navy the outline is cream.
        tone: Clothing label words, such as On the rail, Care note and Care and content.

    style110:
        number: 110
        run: 23
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Sewing pattern
        idea: Every panel is a numbered pattern piece on tissue paper, with a dashed cutting line, an inner stitching line, notches and grain arrows, and progress drawn as a grain arrow sewn part way.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/110.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            tissue: #f3e9d2, the page, with faint crinkle lines and pale highlights
            lightTissue: #f8f1e0, piece fills, the search and the instruction sheet
            printBlack: #1d1b17, text, cut and stitch lines, notches and the primary button
            patternBlue: #1f4e8c, grain arrows, progress, this week bars, piece letters and focus
            markingRed: #a12a2a, the overdue mark, Behind and the count badge
            green: #2f6233, On track
            amber: #7d4e00, At risk
            tapeYellow: #f2d04a, the tape measure axis with dark text
            pencil: #5b5345, meta and times
        type:
            Two stacks. Labels and titles use Franklin Gothic Medium, Franklin
            Gothic, ITC Franklin Gothic, Arial at regular weight. Text uses
            Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans, Tahoma. The greeting is 40px at 1.08,
            measurements 52px, piece titles 19px, piece letters 30px blue,
            labels 12 to 14px caps tracked 0.14 to 0.18em, body 14px at 1.6.
        layout:
            A pattern envelope header shows a pattern piece logo, Brightwork
            with Pattern no. 1031, a boxed search, a black New project button,
            a round bell and a round MO, over a solid rule. The nav is caps, the
            current item blue with a small triangle notch. The board is a 12
            column cutting table of pieces, each with a 2px dashed cut line, a
            1px solid stitch line 12px inside, black triangle notches on edges,
            scissors on the top cut line and a circled piece number with a caps
            note like Front Cut 1. Piece 1 has a big curved bottom right corner
            and holds Good morning, Mara, the date, a red underlined 4 tasks are
            overdue with a crossed circle and a grain arrow. Piece 2 holds
            Finished measurements, four numbers each over a blue dimension line.
            Piece 3 is the cutting layout, six smaller pieces lettered A to F
            three across, some with one curved corner, each with name, meta, a
            grain arrow solid to the percent and dashed after, the percent and
            status. Piece 4 is the chart with dashed outline hatched bars for
            last week and solid blue bars for this week standing on a yellow
            tape measure marked 18 to 31. Piece 5 is Sewing steps, six activity
            items with circled numbers. Below 1000px pieces go full width.
        spacing: An 8px unit. A 12px seam allowance between the cut line and the stitch line, 28px between pieces.
        density: Medium. Pieces of different sizes laid out on a 12 column cutting table.
        corners: Square, with one big curved corner on some pieces, like an armhole or hem curve.
        borders: 2px dashed outer cut line, 1px solid inner stitch line and black triangle notches on edges.
        shadows: None. Tissue lies flat.
        icons:
            Pattern markings at 16px. A filled dot for On track, a filled
            triangle for At risk, a square inside a square for Behind and a
            crossed circle for overdue, with the caps word. Line scissors sit on
            every cut line.
        focus: A 2px blue outline offset 3px with a soft 6px blue tint around it.
        tone: Pattern instructions, such as Cut 1, Finished measurements and Sewing steps.

    style111:
        number: 111
        run: 23
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Sticker sheet
        idea: The dashboard is a sheet of glossy die-cut stickers with thick white borders on a pale backing, each number, project and chart bar its own sticker, slightly tilted as if just placed.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/111.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            backing: #e8edf2, the page behind the sheet, with faint diagonal lines
            sheet: #f6f8fa, the sticker sheet card
            dieCutWhite: #ffffff, sticker borders, chips, the chart card and fields
            yellow: #ffd23f, the current nav and a sticker fill
            pink: #ff8fb1, this week bars and a sticker fill
            mint: #6fd6a8, the bell and a sticker fill
            sky: #7cc6fe, the greeting and last week bars
            lilac: #c3a6ff, a sticker fill
            orange: #ff9f5a, a sticker fill
            violet: #5b3fd1, the primary button and the focus ring, white text
            ink: #1a1a2e, all text on stickers and the progress fill
            green: #0f7a4a, the On track chip
            amber: #9a5b00, the At risk chip
            red: #b3261e, the Behind chip, the overdue burst and the count badge
        type:
            One stack, Avenir Next, Segoe UI, system-ui, Roboto, at heavy
            weights with tight tracking. The greeting is 44px 900 at 1.02,
            numbers 48px 900, section titles 24px 900, sticker titles 19px 800,
            percents 26px 900, body 15px at 1.45, chips 13px 800.
        layout:
            A large rounded sheet card sits on the backing with a perforated
            strip along its top and a tiny caps line Sheet 31 Peel and plan.
            The header is a tilted white pill sticker brand with a star, a white
            search pill, a violet New project pill, a round mint bell sticker
            with a red count and a round pink MO sticker. The nav is white pills,
            the current one a yellow sticker tilted and lifted. The greeting is
            a big sky sticker, Hey Mara!, the date and a red starburst sticker
            with 4 tasks are overdue. Beside it the numbers are four stickers of
            different shapes, a yellow circle, a mint rounded square, a pink
            pill and a lilac leaf shape, each tilted. Projects are six coloured
            rounded stickers three across with name, meta, a chunky ink progress
            pill, the big percent and a white status chip, and the Billing
            migration sticker has a peeling top right corner. The chart is a
            white card where each day is a pill sticker bar with a gloss spot,
            sky for last week and pink for this week. Just stuck on lists the
            activity with round initial stickers. Below 1000px sections stack,
            below 640px stickers go one across.
        spacing: An 8px unit with wide 24 to 32px gutters so each sticker has room for its white border.
        density: Low to medium. Big type, three stickers across.
        corners: Round. 20 to 28px on stickers, full pills for nav, buttons and chart bars, and one circle sticker.
        borders: A 5 to 6px white die-cut border drawn as a spread shadow. Dashed kiss-cut lines on the backing.
        shadows: A soft 8px lift under every sticker, plus a diagonal gloss highlight across the top left of each.
        icons:
            Filled sticker shapes at 22px. A ticked circle for On track, a
            rounded triangle for At risk, a rounded square with a bar for
            Behind and a red starburst with a mark for overdue, on a white chip
            with the word.
        focus: A 3px violet outline offset 4px, outside the white sticker border.
        tone: Bubbly, such as Hey Mara and Just stuck on.

    style112:
        number: 112
        run: 23
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Polaroid wall
        idea: The dashboard is a wall of instant photos taped up with washi tape, where captions are written by hand in the white margins and each project photo develops from left to right as its work is done.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/112.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            plasterWall: #f4f2ee, the page, with a fine plaster speckle
            photoFrame: #ffffff, polaroid frames, the booth strip, fields and the sheet
            marker: #222222, captions, text and the primary button
            oakLedge: #dcc39c, the header picture ledge with #2a1f12 text
            undevelopedFilm: #c9cbc4, the part of a project photo still to do
            dateStamp: #ff8a2a, the percent and date imprint, always on a dark chip
            photoTones: #2e4a66, photo areas, with #3d4f3a, #5a3550, #6a4528, #2b3a4a and #8a2a20, white text
            greenMarker: #1d6b3a, On track
            amberMarker: #8a5000, At risk
            redMarker: #b42318, Behind, overdue and the count badge
            pencil: #5c5650, dates, meta and times
        type:
            Three stacks. Captions, nav and headings use Segoe Print, Bradley
            Hand, Marker Felt, Noteworthy, Chalkboard SE, Comic Sans MS, Comic
            Neue, cursive. Interface text uses Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial,
            system-ui. Imprints use ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas bold in
            orange. The greeting is 34px hand at 1.15, numbers in photos 52px
            Helvetica bold, caption titles 24px hand, nav 22px hand, body and
            meta 14 to 15px.
        layout:
            The header is a light oak picture ledge holding a small photo logo,
            the brand, a white search, a black New project button, a white bell
            and a tiny tilted polaroid with MO. The nav is handwritten words on
            the wall, Home marked with a yellow highlighter stroke. The wall is
            a 12 column grid of tilted polaroids, each a white frame with a deep
            caption margin and a strip of washi tape on top. The greeting is a
            large sunset landscape photo with a 26 10 31 date imprint, captioned
            Morning, Mara!, the date and a red star with 4 tasks are overdue.
            Four small square shots show the numbers in white on dark tones with
            handwritten labels. Projects are six 4 by 3 photos three across,
            where the developed image covers the percent from the left and grey
            undeveloped film covers the rest, with an orange percent imprint in
            the corner, then the handwritten name, the meta with the percent,
            and a marker status. A wide panorama photo holds the chart, pale
            blue bars for last week and warm yellow for this week on a dusk
            sky. A photo booth strip titled Who did what pairs six initial shots
            with the activity text. Below 1000px items go full width, projects
            two across, below 640px one.
        spacing: An 8px unit. Frames pad 12px with a deep caption margin, 32 to 48px of wall between photos.
        density: Low. Few large photos and generous wall.
        corners: Square photos and frames. Controls 4px.
        borders: None. The white frame is the border.
        shadows: A soft 18px drop under each photo, which is tilted 1 to 3 degrees either way. Washi tape strips in yellow, sky, pink and mint at 65 to 70 percent opacity.
        icons:
            Hand drawn marker outlines at 22px. A ticked circle for On track,
            a triangle with a mark for At risk, a square with a dash for Behind
            and a star for overdue, beside the handwritten word.
        focus: A 3px blue #1f5fae outline offset 3px.
        tone: Casual notes on the back of a photo, such as Morning, Mara and Who did what.

    style113:
        number: 113
        run: 23
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Corkboard
        idea: The dashboard is a framed corkboard where index cards, sticky notes and paper slips are held up with push pins, and the project cards hang from a sagging red yarn strung pin to pin.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/113.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            wall: #efe9df, around the board and behind the header
            cork: #d9b98a, the board, speckled with #b8935e, #c9a571 and #e8cfa6
            frameWood: #a87d4c, the 16px board frame
            indexCard: #fffdf6, cards, slips, fields and the sheet
            ruledBlue: #a9c4e0, card lines, decoration only
            marginRed: #e08a86, the card header line, decoration only
            stickyYellow: #fff1a8, the overdue note, the avatar and the current nav tab
            maskingTape: #efe3c2, section labels
            redYarn: #b3262e, the string between pins and this week bars
            ink: #2b2118, text and marker lines
            blueBiro: #1d5fa8, progress hatching and the focus ring
            redPen: #a8201a, the primary button, overdue and Behind
            greenPen: #236b3a, On track
            amberPen: #8a4f00, At risk
        type:
            Three stacks. Headings and numbers use Marker Felt, Chalkboard SE,
            Comic Sans MS, Comic Neue, Trebuchet MS in bold. Card text uses
            American Typewriter, Courier Prime, Courier New, Courier. Controls
            use system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Arial. The greeting is 38px marker
            at 1.15, card numbers 50px, card titles 21px on 26px, section labels
            20px, card text 14 to 15px on a 24px ruling.
        layout:
            A wall header holds a small corkboard logo, a card coloured search,
            a red New project button with a hard ink drop, a bell and a yellow
            MO circle. The board has a 16px wood frame with an inset shadow.
            Along its top, six white paper nav tabs each hang from a coloured
            pin, the current one yellow and tilted with a red marker underline.
            The first row pairs a pinned card with a red top edge holding Hi
            Mara, the date and a line about the board, plus a taped yellow
            sticky note in red marker with a burst saying 4 tasks are overdue,
            with four small pinned cards for the numbers, tilted alternately.
            A masking tape label marks Projects, then six ruled index cards three
            across, each pinned and tilted, joined pin to pin by a sagging red
            yarn, with the marker name, typed Team, Tasks and Due rows, a marker
            drawn bar hatched in blue to the percent, the percent and status. The
            last row has a graph paper card pinned twice with hatched last week
            bars and red this week bars, and Latest notes as six pinned paper
            slips tilted left and right. Below 1040px cards go two across, below
            640px one, and the yarn drops straight down behind the cards.
        spacing: An 8px unit with 24px card ruling. 40px gaps between cards leave room for pins and yarn.
        density: Medium. Cards three across, slips stacked in a column.
        corners: Square paper. Controls 6px, marker bars slightly uneven.
        borders: A 16px wooden frame around the cork, 1.5 to 2px ink lines on controls and marker bars.
        shadows: Soft drops under every paper, a hard pin shadow and an inset shadow inside the frame.
        icons:
            Solid filled shapes with white marks at 18px. A ticked circle for On
            track, a triangle for At risk, a crossed square for Behind and a
            burst for overdue, with the typed word. Push pins in red, blue, green
            and yellow are decoration.
        focus: A 3px blue outline offset 3px inside a 6px card coloured halo.
        tone: Office board notes, such as Pinned up for the team and Latest notes.

    style114:
        number: 114
        run: 24
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Whiteboard
        idea: The dashboard is a dry-erase board in an aluminium frame, written up in four marker colours, with magnets for navigation and faint eraser smudges left behind.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/114.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            wall: #e4e1da, the page behind the board
            board: #fbfcfc, the writing surface, fields and nav labels
            aluminium: #a7aeb5, the frame and the marker tray, decorative only
            blackMarker: #1c2024, text, drawn rules, axes and last week bars
            blueMarker: #1d4fb3, the brand, column heads, names, this week bars, At risk and focus
            redMarker: #bd232b, the overdue circle, Behind and the ring on the current nav label
            greenMarker: #1c6a37, On track, the hours figure and style sheet labels
            ghost: #5d656d, dates, captions and half erased writing
            magnetYellow: #f1c22e, the primary button with black text
        type:
            Two stacks. Hand is Marker Felt, Segoe Print, Bradley Hand,
            Chalkboard SE, Comic Sans MS, cursive, used for the greeting,
            figures, zone titles, project names, statuses, nav and notes. Sans
            is Segoe UI, system-ui, Helvetica Neue, Arial, sans-serif for table
            cells and activity text. Sizes are 44px bold hand for the greeting,
            64px bold hand summary figures, 28px bold hand zone titles, 17 to
            19px hand names and statuses, 15px sans body and 13px sans team
            names.
        layout:
            One whiteboard fills the page inside a 14px aluminium frame with a
            marker tray along the bottom holding four marker pens and an eraser.
            The top row has the blue brand with a starburst mark, six nav labels
            stuck on with round coloured magnets, and on the right a dashed
            marker search box, a yellow pill New project button, a round bell
            with a red count and a green circled MO avatar. The greeting is
            written large with the date tilted in the corner and an arrow
            pointing at 4 tasks are overdue, circled in red marker. The four
            figures are written huge in different marker colours with a double
            underline stroke, split by curved vertical strokes. A long drawn
            line then splits the board into a wide left zone and a narrow right
            zone. The left zone holds a hand ruled project table with hatched
            marker progress bars and the 14 day chart of tilted marker bars,
            black for last week and blue for this week, with values written on
            top. The right zone lists six activity notes with marker icons and
            dashed dividers. Grey blurred smudges sit behind the writing. Below
            860px the zones stack, and below 640px the figures go two by two
            and the table scrolls inside its zone.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px around the board, 20px zone padding, 10px table rows.
        density: Medium. One board, zones split by drawn lines, nothing boxed in cards.
        corners: Uneven hand corners such as 10px 4px 12px 5px on drawn boxes and bars. Round magnets, pill buttons and 6px on the frame.
        borders: 3px marker strokes for the zone dividers and chart axes, 2px for drawn boxes, dashed 2px for the search box and activity rows.
        shadows: Only physical things cast one, the magnets, the nav labels and the frame. The primary button has a 3px hard black lip.
        icons:
            Line icons drawn at a 2.4px stroke in the marker colour. A circled
            tick for On track, a triangle with a mark for At risk, a crossed box
            for Behind and a clock for overdue, always beside the word.
        focus: A 3px blue marker outline offset 3px on every control.
        tone: Friendly team room shorthand, such as Morning, Mara and Latest scribbles.

    style115:
        number: 115
        run: 24
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Ring binder
        idea: The dashboard is the first sheet in a team ring binder, with coloured index tabs for navigation, punched holes and every panel slipped into a clear sheet protector.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/115.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            desk: #e1e4e7, the page and the punched holes
            coverNavy: #22375a, the binder spine, decorative only
            sheet: #ffffff, paper, the current tab and fields
            sleeve: #d6e6f5, sheet protector tint at 28 percent with a diagonal gloss
            ink: #1f2328, text and heavy rules
            muted: #545b63, captions, codes and the last week line
            officeBlue: #1d4f91, the primary button, meters, this week line and focus
            green: #1f6b3a, the On track sticker with a dot
            amber: #8a5300, the At risk sticker with a triangle
            red: #b42318, the Behind sticker with a square and overdue text
            tabYellow: #f6d55c, an index tab and summary tab
            tabBlue: #9cc3ef, an index tab and summary tab
            tabGreen: #a6d9a8, an index tab and summary tab
            tabPink: #f3a6b8, an index tab and summary tab
            tabOrange: #f7b77a, an index tab
            tabLilac: #c9b6ec, an index tab
            graphGrid: #d7e6f2, 16px squares behind the chart
        type:
            Three stacks. Head is Franklin Gothic Medium, Franklin Gothic, ITC
            Franklin Gothic, Arial Narrow, Arial, sans-serif. Body is Verdana,
            DejaVu Sans, Geneva, sans-serif. Mono is ui-monospace, Menlo,
            Consolas, monospace for codes, dates and counts. Sizes are 30px
            head greeting, 40px head summary figures, 22px head section title,
            19px head sleeve titles, 15px head tab labels, 13px Verdana body
            and 11 to 12px mono.
        layout:
            An open binder in three columns. On the left a navy spine carries a
            vertical brand label and three metal rings that reach into the
            sheet. In the middle a white sheet has three punched holes down a
            72px left margin with a dashed guide line. On the right six
            coloured index tabs stick out of the sheet edge as the navigation,
            the current Home tab white and pulled forward with a blue dot. The
            sheet header reads Section 1, Home with a mono line Brightwork team
            binder, sheet 1 of 6, then the search, a blue New project button,
            the bell and the user, over a 2px ink rule. The greeting and date
            sit on one line with a red overdue line under them. Four white
            divider cards each carry a small coloured tab on top with the
            figure inside. The projects table sits inside a sheet protector
            with a thumb notch at the top. Below, two protectors side by side
            hold a graph paper sheet with a week on week line chart, last week
            dashed grey with hollow squares and this week solid blue with dots,
            and a printed activity log with mono times. Below 760px the spine
            turns into a top band with rings along its lower edge, tabs move
            above it as a wrapping row of top tabs, and the holes run across the
            top of the sheet.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 22px between sleeves, an 18px sleeve inset and a 72px left gutter for the holes.
        density: Office dense. Small Verdana, 10px table rows, everything filed on one sheet.
        corners: Square paper. Tabs round 10px on the outer edge, summary tabs 6px on top, controls 4px.
        borders: A 1px blue grey sleeve edge with a semicircle thumb notch, 1px rules and a 2px ink header rule.
        shadows: A soft paper shadow under the sheet and tabs, inset shadows in the punched holes and a faint diagonal gloss across sleeves.
        icons:
            Filled sticker shapes in round outlined pills, a dot for On track,
            a triangle for At risk and a square for Behind, plus a clock for
            overdue. Other icons are 2px line icons.
        focus: A 3px office blue outline offset 2px with a 6px white halo.
        tone: Filing language, such as Section 1, sheet 1 of 6 and Activity log.

    style116:
        number: 116
        run: 24
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Manila folders
        idea: The dashboard is a desk file pulled from a steel drawer, with manila folders behind typed tab labels, rubber stamped dates and statuses, and paper clipped cards for the numbers.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/116.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            floor: #e6e3dc, the page behind everything
            drawerSteel: #c8ccc6, the header drawer front
            manila: #ead39b, the main folder and the current tab
            manilaDeep: #dfc282, project folders and back tabs
            folderEdge: #cfae68, edges and stacked sheets, decorative only
            labelWhite: #fbfaf4, typed labels, clipped cards and memos
            ink: #2a2015, text and the primary button
            brown: #59432a, captions and field keys
            stampRed: #a3201a, overdue, Behind and the current tab mark
            stampBlue: #1d3c86, the date stamp, At risk, this week bars and focus
            stampGreen: #2a5a22, the On track stamp
        type:
            Three stacks. Typed is Courier New, Courier, Nimbus Mono PS,
            Liberation Mono, monospace, for labels, figures and keys, often in
            caps with 0.06 to 0.14em tracking. Stamp is Impact, Haettenschweiler,
            Arial Narrow Bold, sans-serif in caps. Body is Gill Sans, Gill Sans
            MT, Trebuchet MS, system-ui, sans-serif. Sizes are 30px bold typed
            greeting, 34 to 40px bold typed figures, 17 to 22px stamps, 13px
            typed caps labels, 14 to 15px sans body and 12px typed caps keys.
        layout:
            A steel drawer front heads the page with a brass label holder
            showing the brand, a drawer pull, and the search, a black New
            project button, the bell and the user in typed caps. Below it the
            navigation is a row of manila folder tabs with typed white labels,
            the current tab taller and joined to the main folder. The main
            folder has two offset deeper manila sheets behind it like a stack.
            Inside, the typed greeting and a red rubber stamp reading 4 tasks
            overdue sit left, and a round blue Received stamp with 31 OCT 2026
            sits right. Four white cards held by steel paper clips carry the
            figures, each turned slightly. Six project folders follow in three
            columns, each with its own tab at a staggered position holding the
            typed name, a key and value list for team, tasks and due date, a big
            typed percent, a striped tally bar and a tilted status stamp. At the
            bottom a clipped memo holds the chart as two typed horizontal bar
            lists, last week in ink and this week in blue with totals, and a
            routing slip lists activity with boxed initials. Folders go two
            across below 980px and one across below 640px.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 48px between folder rows to leave room for tabs, 28 to 32px folder padding.
        density: Medium. One project per folder, facts as a short key and value list.
        corners: Folder tabs 8 to 10px on top, folders 4 to 6px except the corner under the tab, labels and buttons 2px, a round date stamp.
        borders: 1px folder edges. Stamps have a 3px frame with an inner ring, dashed for At risk and 4px for Behind.
        shadows: Flat offset copies of the folder in deeper manila like a stack, plus one soft drop under the main folder.
        icons:
            Inked stroke marks inside stamps, a tick for On track, a triangle
            for At risk, a cross for Behind and a clock for overdue. Steel paper
            clips are decoration.
        focus: A 3px dashed stamp blue outline offset 3px.
        tone: Office filing words in typed caps, such as Desk file, Routing slip and Received.

    style117:
        number: 117
        run: 24
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Passport stamps
        idea: The dashboard is an open passport, with a holder page for the user and contents, and a visa page where each project is an inked entry stamp whose shape and mark give its status.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/117.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            table: #e7e5ea, the page behind the book
            cover: #3a2a4a, the thin book edge, decorative only
            visaPaper: #eef3ee, pages under the guilloche
            securityTeal: #1d5f63, guilloche lines at 10 percent, microprint and section labels
            ink: #1d2833, text and the machine readable lines
            muted: #4a5662, field keys, times and last week
            violetInk: #5a2a86, the primary button, the current page, this week and focus
            greenInk: #1f6340, the round On track stamp with a tick
            blueInk: #1f4b8f, the double framed At risk stamp with a triangle
            redInk: #a1262c, the leaf shaped Behind stamp with a crossed square and the overdue notice
        type:
            Three stacks. Serif is Palatino Linotype, Book Antiqua, Palatino,
            URW Palladio L, Georgia, serif. OCR is OCR B, OCR-B, Consolas,
            Lucida Console, monospace. Stamp is Arial Black, Arial, sans-serif
            in caps. Sizes are 30px serif greeting, 30 to 34px bold OCR figures,
            14px black caps stamp titles, 15px bold OCR caps field values, 15 to
            16px serif body and 10 to 13px OCR caps keys and labels.
        layout:
            A dark thin cover frames a two page spread, a narrow holder page on
            the left and a wide visa page on the right, with shaded gutters
            where they meet. Both pages carry a guilloche of overlapping fine
            rings. The holder page has a microprint band, a compass rose mark
            with the spaced caps brand, a hatched photo box with MO, Surname,
            Given name and Date fields, the greeting and date, a tilted red
            notice reading Overdue, 4 tasks are overdue, and the navigation as a
            Contents list with dotted leaders and page numbers. Two machine
            readable lines sit at its foot and folio numbers mark the corners.
            The visa page has the underlined search, a violet pill New project
            button, a round bell and the user, then four teal outlined boxes
            for the figures, then six entry stamps on a loose three column grid,
            each turned 3 to 6 degrees. A stamp holds the project name, team
            between rules, a big percent, tasks and due date, and a status pill.
            Its outline is the status, round with an inner ring for On track,
            a 6px double frame for At risk and a leaf with 28px and 6px corners
            for Behind. Below the spread a second spread holds a lollipop chart
            of ink circles on stems, grey last week and violet this week, and
            an Observations list. Below 820px pages stack, and below 560px the
            stamps go one per row, alternating left and right.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 28 to 32px page margins, 18 to 20px between stamps.
        density: Medium and scattered. Stamps sit loosely on a grid, each turned slightly.
        corners: Book 14px, pages 8px, summary boxes 6px. Stamp outlines follow the status shapes described above.
        borders: 3px ink frames, 6px double for At risk, hairline teal for summary boxes and observation rules.
        shadows: Only the gutter, an inset shade where the pages meet, and a soft drop under the book.
        icons:
            Solid ink marks, a tick for On track, a filled triangle for At
            risk, a crossed filled square for Behind and a clock for overdue,
            each beside the caps word. A compass rose emblem.
        focus: A 2px violet outline offset 3px with a soft violet halo.
        tone: Travel document words, such as Contents, Entries, Observations and Given name.

    style118:
        number: 118
        run: 24
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Postage stamps
        idea: The dashboard is a page in a stamp album, where numbers are denominations, projects are a perforated souvenir sheet with an overprinted status, and the chart is a coil of one task stamps.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/118.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            album: #f5f0e1, the page and the perforation holes
            quadrille: #e4dccb, the 12px album grid, decorative only
            gumPaper: #fffdf6, stamp faces and fields
            sheetMargin: #e9e1cc, the souvenir sheet selvage
            ink: #22201c, text, frames and the On track overprint
            muted: #5b5348, captions and meta
            carmine: #9e2b3a, the primary button, overdue, Behind and this week
            ultramarine: #2b3f8f, a stamp colour and focus
            bottleGreen: #24604a, a stamp colour
            sepia: #6b4523, a stamp colour
            violet: #5d3b7a, a stamp colour
            slate: #37505e, a stamp colour and last week
            cancel: #3a3a44, postmarks
        type:
            Three stacks. Caps is Copperplate, Copperplate Gothic Light,
            Engravers MT, Felix Titling, Didot, Georgia, serif, set in caps with
            0.1 to 0.16em tracking. Numbers are Didot, Bodoni 72, Bodoni MT,
            Big Caslon, Georgia, serif. Body is Baskerville, Baskerville Old
            Face, Libre Baskerville, Georgia, serif. Sizes are 52 to 56px Didone
            denominations, 36px Didone greeting, 11 to 15px engraved caps
            labels, 17px bold Baskerville stamp names and 15px body.
        layout:
            The page is an album leaf on a quadrille ground with a thin rule and
            a double outer rule. The header has the brand in spaced caps with a
            framed star mark and, on the right, the search, a carmine New
            project button with an inner white line, the bell and the italic
            user name. The navigation is a row of small perforated definitive
            stamps, each a line icon and a caps label in its own stamp colour,
            the current one filled carmine. The greeting and date sit left with
            a carmine overdue line, and a round postmark reading Brightwork, 31
            OCT, 2026 with wavy cancel lines sits right. Four perforated stamps
            show the figures as big Didone denominations with an engraved icon
            and a caps caption. The projects form a souvenir sheet on a tinted
            margin with italic selvage text, six stamps in three columns. Each
            stamp has Brightwork and the team in caps along the top, a hatched
            vignette with a line drawing for its team, the percent as the
            denomination, the name, tasks and due date, and a full width status
            overprint bar along the bottom. The chart is a coil of stacked
            blocks where one block is one task, slate last week and carmine this
            week. Activity sits beside it, each line with a round postmark for
            its time. The sheet goes two across below 1000px and one across
            below 640px.
        spacing: An 8px unit. A 9px perforated margin round every stamp, 16px between stamps and 36px before sections.
        density: Medium. Each project is one self contained stamp, read at a glance.
        corners: Square. Edges are perforated with holes on a 10px pitch cut into the margin.
        borders: A 2 to 3px frame in the stamp colour inside the perforations. The album leaf has a thin rule and a double outer rule.
        shadows: A 1px drop shadow so stamps lift off the album.
        icons:
            Engraved line vignettes per team. Overprint bars carry the status,
            a filled dot on black for On track, a triangle on a white bar with a
            dashed top for At risk and a square on carmine for Behind. A clock
            marks overdue.
        focus: A 3px ultramarine outline offset 4px.
        tone: Philatelic and calm, such as The project issue, Recent post and denomination.

    style119:
        number: 119
        run: 25
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Airmail
        idea: The dashboard is an airmail envelope addressed to Mara, with red and blue chevron edges, a par avion label, postcode boxes for the numbers, and each project flying a dashed route towards its due date.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/119.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            sky: #e8eef7, the page behind the envelope
            envelope: #f8fafd, the main surface
            tissueBlue: #eef3fa, aerogramme cards and rows
            ink: #1b2433, text and postcode digits
            muted: #4c5868, captions and the dashed part of a route still to fly
            airmailRed: #b3202a, chevrons, the primary button, overdue, Behind and this week
            airmailBlue: #1f3e8c, chevrons, the par avion label, the brand, the flown route, At risk and focus
            green: #1f6a45, the On track label
            rule: #c5d0e0, dividers and card edges
        type:
            Two stacks. Geometric is Futura, Century Gothic, Avenir Next,
            Avenir, URW Gothic, Trebuchet MS, sans-serif, for labels, names,
            digits and buttons, often caps with 0.1em tracking. Letter is
            Georgia, Iowan Old Style, Times New Roman, serif, for the greeting
            and body. Sizes are 34px Georgia italic greeting, 30px bold
            geometric postcode digits, 26px bold percent, 18px bold project
            names, 12 to 14px geometric caps labels and 15 to 17px body.
        layout:
            The whole dashboard sits inside a 14px border of red, white and blue
            diagonal chevrons. The top left has a blue Par avion, By airmail
            label and the brand in blue and red, with caps nav links under it,
            the current one red with a small paper plane mark and an underline.
            The top right has a dashed Postage paid box with a round blue
            postmark reading 31 OCT 2026 and cancel lines. A ruled tools row
            holds a pill search, a red pill New project button, a round bell and
            the user. The letter opens with Dear Mara in italic, the date line
            and a red urgent line, beside a To address block with a red left
            bar. The four figures are written one digit per red or blue outlined
            postcode box. Six aerogramme cards follow in three columns, each
            with a chevron strip on top, the name, an italic care of team line,
            a route from Start to the due date where a filled plane sits at the
            percent along a dashed line, the percent flown, the task count and a
            status label. The chart is a flight log line, last week dashed blue
            with hollow circles and this week solid red with diamonds, values on
            each point. Correspondence lists activity with envelope icons.
            Cards go two across below 1000px and one across below 700px.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24 to 30px envelope padding, 18px between cards, 32px before sections.
        density: Airy. A letter opening, one row of postcodes, cards with one route each.
        corners: Square envelope and cards. Pill buttons, search and fields at 20px. Round bell and avatar.
        borders: A 14px chevron border round the envelope, an 8px chevron strip on each card top, 2px postcode boxes and a dashed stamp box.
        shadows: One soft blue shadow under the envelope and a 2px flat lip under cards.
        icons:
            A filled plane rides each route. Labels pair the caps word with a
            filled circle for On track, a diamond on a dashed label for At risk
            and a square on a solid red label for Behind. A clock marks overdue
            and envelope outlines mark activity.
        focus: A 3px blue outline offset 3px with a 6px soft red halo.
        tone: Warm letter writing, such as Dear Mara, Projects in transit and Correspondence.

    style120:
        number: 120
        run: 25
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Telegram
        idea: The dashboard is a telegram form, with printed brown field labels and boxes and every fact pasted on as an uppercase teletype tape strip closed with STOP.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/120.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            counter: #dcdcd2, the page behind the form
            formBuff: #f4ecd2, the form and the style sheet
            formPrint: #8a2f1d, labels, rules, frames, the primary button, this week and focus
            tape: #fffcf0, pasted strips that carry all data
            ink: #1f1c17, teletype text
            muted: #5c5345, STOP separators and placeholders
            okGreen: #2b5e2b, the On track code with a dot
            riskBrown: #7f4500, the dashed At risk code with a triangle
            lateRed: #9b1c1c, the heavy Behind code with a square and overdue text
            focusYellow: #fff3b8, the fill behind focused controls
        type:
            Three stacks. Teletype is Lucida Console, Andale Mono, DejaVu Sans
            Mono, Liberation Mono, Monaco, monospace, always uppercase on tape.
            Slab is Rockwell, Roboto Slab, Clarendon, Century Schoolbook, Bookman
            Old Style, Georgia, serif for the masthead. Narrow is Arial Narrow,
            Liberation Sans Narrow, Roboto Condensed, Arial, sans-serif for
            printed labels. Sizes are 34px bold slab caps masthead, 30px bold
            teletype figures, 20px teletype greeting, 13 to 15px teletype data
            and 10 to 12px bold narrow caps labels with 0.12em tracking.
        layout:
            One buff form framed by a printed 2px line and a 1px line inside it.
            The masthead has a round lightning bolt seal, the brand in brown
            slab caps with Telegraph, team wires under it, and three boxed
            fields on the right for No. 1031, Filed 31 OCT 26 and Day SAT, over
            a double rule. A service row labelled Check service desired holds
            the navigation as printed checkboxes, the current one crossed with
            an X and underlined, and on the right a labelled Query field, a
            brown New project button, a bell with its count and a To field with
            the user. The Message area pastes three tape strips, the greeting,
            the date and a red urgent strip, each ending in STOP. Four boxed
            fields each hold one figure on tape. Project wires is a ruled grid
            with a number column, and every cell is a tape strip, the name and
            team joined by STOP, a text bar such as seven hashes and three
            dashes in brackets with 72 pct, tasks, due date and a status code.
            The chart is a tape ticker in a pre block, one line per day with
            hashes for the count, last week in ink with its total and this week
            in brown with its total. Incoming wires lists activity as tape
            strips. Below 1000px each project row stacks its cells under the
            number.
        spacing: An 8px unit. The form inset 30px inside the double frame, 9px row padding and 28px before sections.
        density: Dense like a form. Data in columns of printed boxes, one wire per project.
        corners: Square everywhere. No rounding at all.
        borders: 1px form print rules, a 3px double rule under the masthead, and a 2px plus 1px frame round the form.
        shadows: Only the tape strips lift, with a 1px shadow like glued paper, and the form has a soft drop.
        icons:
            Few. A lightning bolt seal. Status codes pair the caps word with a
            filled dot, a triangle or a square in a 1.5px, dashed or 3px frame.
            Overdue is red tape text. Nav uses printed checkboxes.
        focus: A 3px form print outline offset 2px over a pale yellow fill.
        tone: Clipped wire language in caps, ending phrases with STOP, such as Good morning Mara STOP.

    style121:
        number: 121
        run: 25
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Tax form
        idea: The dashboard is an official return, with numbered lines, dotted leaders and amount boxes, black Part bars for each section, comb boxes for the date and one status box per project.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/121.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            desk: #eceeea, the page behind the sheet
            paper: #ffffff, the form
            ink: #111111, text, rules, Part bars, the primary button and this week bars
            muted: #474747, captions, small print and last week bars
            shade: #e2ede5, column heads, box numbers and entry fields
            shadeInk: #1c4a31, text on the shade
            green: #1d5c3a, the On track box with a tick
            amber: #8a4a00, the At risk box with a triangle
            red: #a3161a, the Behind box with a cross and the overdue line
            highlighter: #ffe680, the focus fill
        type:
            Three stacks. Sans is Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, Liberation
            Sans, sans-serif. Narrow is Helvetica Neue Condensed, Arial Narrow,
            Liberation Sans Narrow, Roboto Condensed, Helvetica, sans-serif for
            the form number, titles and Part labels. Mono is OCR A Std, OCR A,
            ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas, monospace for amounts and dates.
            Sizes are 26px bold narrow form number, 20px bold narrow title,
            40px outlined year, 20px bold mono amounts, 13 to 14px bold narrow
            Part titles, 13px sans line text and 10 to 11px small print.
        layout:
            One white sheet on a pale desk with a vertical margin note. The
            header is a three cell grid, Form BW-1031 on the left as the brand
            link, the title Weekly Project Return with the week ending date in
            the middle, and 2026 with an outlined 20 and Week 44 on the right,
            over a 3px rule. The navigation is a row of boxed Part labels, Part
            I Home to Part VI Settings, the current label in a black cell.
            Identity cells hold first name, last name and the date in comb
            boxes. Line 0 holds the search field on a shaded strip, the black
            New project button, the bell and the user. Part I is a list of
            numbered lines with dotted leaders and right hand amount boxes, the
            greeting, the date, the overdue line boxed in red, then the four
            figures. Part II is a ruled table with lettered column heads (a) to
            (f) and a status cell with an 18px box mark and the word. Part III
            is Schedule D, a 14 column grid with a bar inside each cell over a
            row of values, then lines 15 and 16 with the weekly totals. Part IV
            lists activity as numbered lines with times in a right cell. A
            small print footer explains the marks. On a phone the header and
            identity cells stack, amount boxes narrow and the table scrolls.
        spacing: 4px steps. 34px line height, 6px cell padding and 14px before each Part.
        density: Very dense. Every fact has a line number and nothing floats free.
        corners: Square. No rounding anywhere.
        borders: 1px ink rules, 1px grey between lines, 3px under the header and 2px above each Part bar.
        shadows: One faint shadow so the sheet sits on the desk.
        icons:
            Marks inside 18px boxes, a tick for On track, a filled triangle for
            At risk and a cross in a heavy red box for Behind, plus a clock for
            the overdue line.
        focus: A 2px ink outline with a highlighter yellow fill.
        tone: Bureaucratic and exact, such as Add line 14 and Mark one status box per line.

    style122:
        number: 122
        run: 25
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Cheque
        idea: The dashboard is a chequebook, where counterfoils hold the numbers, the greeting is a cheque made out to Mara on a wavy security background, and projects are lines in a register.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/122.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            desk: #e9e8e4, the page
            chequeMint: #eef4f2, the start of the security paper gradient
            chequeLilac: #eef0f8, the end of the security paper gradient
            stub: #f7f8f5, counterfoils and table heads
            navyInk: #15233a, text, rules, the current nav item and this week bars
            muted: #4a5568, captions and labels
            securityGreen: #2f6f62, wave lines at 13 percent, headings, meters and the last week hatch
            signatureViolet: #43358a, the primary button, the signature and focus
            green: #1f6a3f, the On track chip with a ticked disc
            amber: #8a4d00, the At risk chip with a triangle
            red: #a01d2b, the Behind chip with a crossed square and the overdue amount
        type:
            Three stacks. Serif is Garamond, Adobe Garamond Pro, EB Garamond,
            Cormorant Garamond, Palatino Linotype, Georgia, serif. Bank is MICR,
            E-13B, Lucida Sans Typewriter, Lucida Console, ui-monospace,
            monospace, set with 0.14 to 0.24em tracking. Labels are Gill Sans,
            Gill Sans MT, Segoe UI, system-ui, sans-serif. Sizes are 32px
            italic serif payee, 20px italic serif amount in words, 34px
            semibold serif stub figures, 26px bold bank amount, 18px bank line,
            18px semibold serif project names and 11 to 15px sans labels.
        layout:
            A plain bank style top row has a guilloche globe mark with
            Brightwork and Team account, sans nav links with the current one in
            a navy block, an underlined italic search, a violet New project
            button, the bell and the italic user name. The chequebook below is a
            white book with four counterfoils stacked in a 270px left column,
            each with a mono counterfoil number, the caption and a big figure,
            split from the cheque by a dashed perforation. The cheque sits on a
            mint to lilac gradient with fine wave lines. It has Brightwork,
            Weekly order to the team lead, date digits on underlines, Good
            morning beside Mara Okafor in large italic on a write on line, a
            boxed red 4 overdue amount with a clock, the words line Four tasks
            are overdue, settle these first, a memo line with the date, a violet
            signature over Authorised, Brightwork, and a bank number line drawn
            with bar glyphs. The project register is a striped table with
            number, name and team, a hatched paid out meter with percent, tasks,
            due date and a status chip. Below, Daily deposits shows hatched
            green bars for last week and solid navy bars for this week, and
            Recent transactions lists activity with times on the right. Below
            980px the counterfoils become a two by two grid above the cheque.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 26 to 30px cheque padding, 12px table cells and 36px before sections.
        density: Medium. One big cheque, then a tidy register and two panels.
        corners: Small, 3 to 4px on the book, panels, buttons and chips.
        borders: 1.5px ink write on lines for payee, words, memo and signature, and a 2px dashed perforation between stubs and cheque.
        shadows: A 2px flat edge and one soft drop under the chequebook.
        icons:
            Solid chips with an outline, a ticked disc for On track, a triangle
            with a mark for At risk and a crossed square for Behind, plus a
            clock for overdue. Bank line symbols are small bar glyphs.
        focus: A 2px violet outline offset 2px with a soft violet halo.
        tone: Banking words, such as The sum of, Counterfoil, Register and Deposits.

    style123:
        number: 123
        run: 25
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Stock certificate
        idea: The dashboard is an engraved share certificate made out to Mara, with hatched borders and guilloche rosettes, share numbers in corner cartouches, projects as a schedule of holdings, and a gold seal.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/123.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            wall: #ece6d8, the page behind the certificate
            cream: #fbf7ea, certificate paper and cartouches
            vellum: #f6efd9, the edge glow of the paper and fields
            engraverSienna: #7a3b12, borders, the title, rules, the primary button, this week bars and focus
            lightSienna: #c98a5a, dotted rules and the last week hatch, never text
            ink: #2a1c10, body text and figures
            muted: #5d4a36, caps labels, classes and times
            signatureNavy: #22325a, the holder name and signature text
            sealGold: #b08a2e, the embossed seal and the focus halo, decorative
            green: #235c33, On track with a ticked rosette
            amber: #8a4a00, At risk with a diamond
            red: #9c1f1f, Behind with a crossed square and the overdue notice
        type:
            Three stacks. Caps is Trajan Pro, Trajan, Cinzel, Optima, Times New
            Roman, serif, always uppercase with 0.1 to 0.3em tracking. Text is
            Big Caslon, Caslon, Libre Caslon Text, Book Antiqua, Palatino
            Linotype, Georgia, serif. Figures are Bodoni 72, Bodoni MT, Didot,
            Big Caslon, Georgia, serif. Sizes are 56px engraved caps title,
            40px italic Caslon holder name, 40px Didone cartouche figures, 18px
            semibold Caslon project names, 15 to 18px body and 11 to 15px caps
            labels.
        layout:
            A transfer agent strip above the certificate holds a rosette mark
            with the brand in spaced caps, caps nav links divided by small
            floral marks with the current one under a double rule, a pill
            search, a sienna New project button with an inner light line, a
            round bell and the italic user. The certificate has a 16px diagonal
            hatch border, a 2px outer line and a 3px double inner frame, with a
            guilloche rosette in each corner and a large faint rosette
            watermark behind the centre. Four oval cartouches with double rings
            hold the figures, active projects and due this week at the top
            corners, overdue and hours at the lower corners of the opening. In
            the centre sit Team holdings of, the huge sienna title, a ribbon
            reading Certificate of progress, a line drawn rising sun vignette,
            then This certifies that, good morning, Mara Okafor in navy italic
            on a rule, the date line and a ruled red notice reading 4 tasks are
            overdue. Ornamental headings with double rules introduce a Schedule
            of holdings table with shares held, percent with a fine line bar,
            matures and standing, then a Record of dividends chart of round
            topped hatched bars and a Transfer ledger. At the foot two
            signature lines, Mara Okafor as holder and 31 October 2026 as
            dated, flank a scalloped gold seal reading BW. Below 980px the
            cartouches sit two by two under the title.
        spacing: An 8px unit. A 16px hatched border, 28 to 40px inner margin and 30px before each ornamental heading.
        density: Formal and centred. One ceremonial top, then a ruled schedule and two half columns.
        corners: Square certificate. Oval cartouches at a 40px by 24px radius, round topped bars and a round seal.
        borders: A 16px diagonal hatch frame, a 2px outer line, a 3px double inner line, double rules under headings and table heads, and dotted row rules.
        shadows: A soft drop under the certificate and under the seal. Everything else is flat engraving.
        icons:
            Solid standing marks beside caps words, a ticked rosette for On
            track, a diamond with a mark for At risk and a crossed square for
            Behind, plus a clock for overdue. Guilloche rosettes decorate the
            corners and the watermark.
        focus: A 2px sienna outline offset 3px inside a 6px gold halo.
        tone: Ceremonial share language, such as This certifies that, Schedule of holdings, Matures and Transfer ledger.

    style124:
        number: 124
        run: 26
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Diploma
        idea: The dashboard as a formal certificate on parchment, with a double gilt frame, wax seals for the numbers, a numbered register of projects and a signature line under every activity.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/124.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            parchment: #f3ead2, the page behind the certificate
            sheet: #fbf5e4, the certificate, fields and the style sheet
            ink: #2a2118, text, the 2px frame, rules and bar outlines
            sepia: #5c4a33, meta lines, captions and nav links
            gilt: #b8963f, frame hairlines, corner ornaments and the focus halo, never text
            goldInk: #6b5317, roman numerals, the kicker and progress fill
            sealWax: #ead9a2, the four summary seals
            oxblood: #7d1f1f, the primary button, overdue, the Behind square and the big seal
            laurel: #2e5a35, the On track round seal
            amber: #7a4a00, the At risk diamond
        type:
            Text uses Palatino Linotype, Palatino, Book Antiqua, URW Palladio L,
            Georgia, serif. Signatures use Snell Roundhand, Apple Chancery, URW
            Chancery L, Lucida Calligraphy, cursive. The greeting is 64px italic
            at 1.1, section titles 26px small caps tracked 0.14em and centred,
            project names 22px italic 600, seal numbers 40px 600, body 17px at
            1.6, meta 15px small caps, signatures 22px script.
        layout:
            One centred certificate up to 1200px wide with a 2px ink border, a
            gilt double hairline inside and curled gilt ornaments in each corner.
            The masthead has a shield mark and the spaced small caps brand on the
            left, then an underlined italic search, an oxblood New project button
            with an inset gold line, a round bell and a monogram seal with the
            name. The nav is one centred row of small caps links split by gilt
            bullets, Home bold and underlined in oxblood. A centred proclamation
            follows with the kicker Brightwork hereby greets, the big italic
            greeting, the date written as Saturday, the 31st of October 2026, and
            Be it noted that 4 tasks are overdue between two rules. Four scalloped
            wax seals hold the numbers with small caps captions, the overdue seal
            in pink and oxblood. The Register of Projects is a list ruled with
            triple lines, each row a roman numeral, an italic name over team and
            due date, a dotted leader from percent to tasks above a thin framed
            bar, and the status on the right. Below sit two columns, a framed
            hatched bar chart titled Record of Tasks Completed, and Attestations,
            where each activity sentence sits over a signature rule with the name
            in script and the time in small caps. Two signature lines and a round
            oxblood star seal close the page. Below 900px seals go two by two and
            rows stack, below 560px the masthead centres and the sign-off stacks.
        spacing: An 8px unit. Rows have 16px padding, seals 24px gaps and sections 48px between them.
        density: Ceremonial and centred. One register of six rows, then a chart and six attestations side by side.
        corners: Square everywhere. Only seals, the monogram and the bell are round.
        borders: A 2px ink frame with gilt hairlines inside, triple ruled register ends, dotted leaders and signature rules.
        shadows: None. Inset double lines on buttons and frames stand in for depth.
        icons:
            Filled seal-like status marks at 18px with the small caps word, a
            round seal with a check for On track, a diamond with a bar for At
            risk and a square with a cross for Behind. Tools use thin 1.4 stroke
            line icons.
        focus: A 2px oxblood outline offset 3px inside a 6px soft gilt halo. A focused field gets a pale gold fill and a 2px oxblood underline.
        tone: Formal and ceremonial, such as Brightwork hereby greets and Be it noted that 4 tasks are overdue.

    style125:
        number: 125
        run: 26
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Subway map
        idea: Each project is a coloured transit line running from its start to a terminus at the due date, with station dots, a train marker at the current percent, and the navigation drawn as a line you ride.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/125.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            platform: #f4f4ef, the page
            white: #ffffff, panels, fields and station dots
            ink: #111111, text, 2px borders, the primary button and the train marker
            greyLine: #56565a, the nav line, meta text and last week in the chart
            signYellow: #ffd23f, the service notice, time tags and avatar, never text
            lineW: #b3261e, Website redesign and the Behind octagon
            lineM: #1d4ed8, Mobile app 2.0, this week in the chart and focus
            lineQ: #15803d, Q4 customer survey
            lineB: #7e22ce, Billing migration
            lineS: #8a5a00, Spring catalogue
            lineO: #0f766e, Onboarding emails
            onTrack: #15703a, the filled circle with a tick
            atRisk: #9a4d00, the triangle with a bar
        type:
            One stack, Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, Segoe UI, sans-serif.
            The greeting is 40px 800 at 1.1 with tight tracking, summary numbers
            44px 800, section titles 22px 800, line names 18px 800, body 16px at
            1.45, meta 14px 600 grey, time tags 14px bold monospace.
        layout:
            A white top bar with a dark rounded square logo showing a yellow line
            and two stations, then a pill search, a black pill New project
            button, a round bell and a yellow avatar. Under it the nav is a thick
            grey line with a white station dot per item, the current Home a large
            interchange ring with the words you are here. The greeting is a white
            platform sign with a 16px black left edge, and a yellow service notice
            on the right says 4 tasks are overdue. Four boards with a grey top
            band hold the numbers, the overdue one with a red band. The Project
            network panel lists six lines. Each row has a coloured round code
            letter, the name over a linked rings team tag, then a 10px track in
            the line colour, solid up to the percent and dashed beyond, white
            station rings at 0, 25, 50 and 75 percent, a terminus bar at the
            end, a black pill train marker showing the percent, and below it the
            task count and Terminus with the due date. Status sits on the right.
            Below, a chart panel draws the 14 days as a thick metro line with
            ring stations and values, grey for last week and blue for this week,
            joined by an interchange ring at Saturday 24, with pill labels for
            the week totals. Recent arrivals lists activity with a coloured line
            roundel and a yellow time tag. Below 980px status drops under the
            name and the track goes full width, below 640px the nav line scrolls
            sideways inside itself and boards go two by two.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px between rows and boards, 24px panel gaps and 32px between sections.
        density: Medium. One full width line per project, read left to right.
        corners: Full rounds for stations, roundels, pills and buttons, 8px on panels, a square platform sign.
        borders: 2px ink on every panel and control and a 16px ink edge on the greeting sign.
        shadows: None. Contrast comes from thick lines and white station dots.
        icons:
            Solid transit pictograms at 20px with a white inner mark, a circle
            with a tick for On track, a triangle with a bar for At risk and an
            octagon with a bar for Behind. Linked rings mark team interchanges.
        focus: A 3px blue outline offset 2px with a 6px white gap ring around it.
        tone: Station announcements, such as Service notice, you are here, Terminus 14 Nov and Recent arrivals.

    style126:
        number: 126
        run: 26
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Circuit board
        idea: The dashboard laid out as a light green circuit board, with numbers on chips, projects as dashed component footprints carrying LED bar graphs, activity as test points on a trace, and the chart built from stacked copper pads.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/126.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            solderMask: #e4efe0, the board, with a #d3e4cd 32px grid
            componentBody: #f7faf4, fields, footprints and the style sheet
            silkscreen: #163521, main text and outlines
            silkMuted: #3c5c45, designators, meta and dashed courtyards
            trace: #9cc396, 4px traces and section rules, never text
            copper: #b8732f, pads, vias and mounting rings
            tinnedPad: #d39a5c, chart pads and the primary switch
            chip: #26302a, chip bodies, the nav pin header and the LED bar housing
            ledGreen: #7fe08e, lit LED segments on dark only
            onTrack: #1d7337, the ring LED
            atRisk: #8f4f00, the triangle LED
            behind: #b42318, the square LED, overdue and the alarm chip edge
        type:
            One monospace stack, ui-monospace, SF Mono, Cascadia Mono, Roboto
            Mono, Menlo, Consolas, monospace. The greeting is 34px 700, chip
            values 40px 700, section labels 15px 700 caps tracked 0.14em,
            project names 16px 700, body 14px at 1.5, designators and meta 12px
            caps tracked 0.1em.
        layout:
            One board up to 1280px with 14px corners, a 32px faint grid and
            copper ringed mounting holes in each corner. The header has a chip
            logo, the spaced caps brand with PCB-01 REV 2026.10 under it, a slot
            search, a tactile switch New project button with a round black cap, a
            round black buzzer for notifications and a U0 chip tag with the name.
            The nav is a dark pin header labelled J1, each link a pad and label,
            the current Home a lit copper pad. Horizontal traces with two vias
            divide sections. The greeting sits in silkscreen text with the date
            in spaced caps, and a boxed LED reads D1, 4 tasks are overdue. Four
            dark DIP chips labelled U1 to U4 hold the numbers, with grey pin legs
            above and below, the overdue chip edged in red. Projects are six
            dashed footprints labelled R1 to R6 in two columns, each with the
            name and team, a ten segment LED bar lit by tens of percent, the
            percent, tasks and due date, and a boxed status LED. Beside them,
            activity runs down a green trace as test points TP1 to TP6 with a
            copper pad, a dark tag, the sentence and the time. The chart is a
            panel of stacked copper pads, one pad per task, with values above,
            dates below and LAST WK = 59 and THIS WK = 73 over the two halves.
            Below 1000px chips go two by two and columns stack, below 640px the
            board loses its frame and footprints go single file.
        spacing: An 8px unit on a 32px board grid. 16px between footprints, 24px between chips, traces between sections.
        density: Medium dense, like a populated board, with two columns of modules beside a test point rail.
        corners: 14px on the board, 6px footprints, 2 to 4px chips and controls, round pads and holes.
        borders: 1.5px silkscreen lines, dashed courtyards round modules and 4px trace rules.
        shadows: Only a glow on lit LED segments and the board edge ring. Nothing floats.
        icons:
            Solid 16px LEDs with a hole punched in, a ring for On track, a
            triangle with a bar for At risk and a square with a square hole for
            Behind, always with the caps word in a bordered tag. Pads, vias and
            pins are ornament.
        focus: A 2px dashed silkscreen outline offset 3px with a 6px soft copper halo.
        tone: Terse engineering labels in caps, such as U1, R3, TP2, D1 and LAST WK = 59.

    style127:
        number: 127
        run: 26
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Periodic table
        idea: Every number and project becomes an element tile with a number, a two-letter symbol and a mass, arranged in the classic table shape with the greeting in the gap and the chart and activity as detached series rows below.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/127.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #fafaf7, the page
            ink: #1a1a1a, text, 1.5px tile borders, the primary button and the current nav cell
            muted: #4d4d4d, masses, meta and captions
            summary: #e3e0f3, the four number tiles
            design: #ffd8b0, design family tiles
            engineering: #c7dcf7, engineering family tiles
            research: #cdeccd, research family tiles
            marketing: #f3cde6, marketing family tiles
            alarm: #f9c8c3, the overdue tile and alert
            lastWeekFill: #a9c46b, day tile fill on #eef2e2 for last week
            thisWeekFill: #7fb0e8, day tile fill on #eaf1fa for this week
            onTrack: #17663a, the filled circle
            atRisk: #8a4b00, the filled triangle
            behind: #a3201a, the heavy cross
            focus: #5b3fd1, the 3px focus outline
        type:
            Symbols and values use Helvetica Neue, Arial Black, Arial, sans-serif
            at 800. Text uses Avenir Next, Segoe UI, system-ui, Roboto, Arial,
            sans-serif. The greeting is 40px 700 at 1.1, symbols 40 to 44px,
            values 32px, names 14px 700, body 15px at 1.45, meta and atomic
            numbers 12px, series labels 13px caps.
        layout:
            A header with a Bw element tile as the logo, the brand with the line
            The periodic table of your week, then a square search, a black New
            project button, a square bell and an Mo tile avatar. The nav is a
            row of six ruled cells numbered 1 to 6, Home filled black. The main
            table is an eight column grid with 6px gutters. Rows one and two hold
            the number tiles at the far left and right, Ap 6, Dw 23, Ot 4 in the
            alarm colour and Hl 186, with the greeting, date and an alert chip
            for 4 tasks are overdue filling the gap between them on faint ruled
            lines. Row three holds the six project tiles numbered 7 to 12, each
            in its team colour with the percent as mass in the top right, a big
            symbol such as Wr or Bm, the name, team, tasks and due date, a thin
            black progress bar and a white bordered status chip. A dashed Key
            tile explains the tile anatomy and the colour families. Below, two
            series rows with a thick rule label on the left. The chart is
            fourteen day tiles filled from the bottom to each value, green for
            last week and blue for this week, with week totals under them.
            Reactions shows activity as tiles with an initials symbol. Below
            1000px the table becomes four columns with the greeting on top and
            projects two per row, and day tiles wrap to two rows of seven.
        spacing: 6px gutters between tiles like a printed chart, 8px tile padding and 28px between the table and each series row.
        density: A dense grid of equal cells. Eight columns wide, four below 1000px.
        corners: Square on every tile, field and button.
        borders: 1.5px ink round every cell, dashed for the key, a 3px rule above series labels.
        shadows: None. Colour families and borders do all the grouping.
        icons:
            Tiny solid status glyphs at 14px in a white chip with the word, a
            filled circle for On track, a filled triangle for At risk and a
            heavy cross for Behind. Two-letter symbols stand in for icons
            elsewhere.
        focus: A 3px violet outline offset 2px.
        tone: Chemistry class labels such as Key, Reactions and The periodic table of your week, plain values otherwise.

    style128:
        number: 128
        run: 26
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Anatomy chart
        idea: The dashboard as an antique scientific plate in sepia, where projects are segments of a sectioned specimen with lettered leader lines, numbers are labelled measurements and activity reads as numbered field notes.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/128.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            agedPaper: #e9dcbf, the page around the plate
            plate: #f6edd8, the plate, the figure centre and label discs
            ironGallInk: #33241a, text, outlines and leader lines
            sepia: #5f4730, captions, key details and stipple
            redOchre: #8e3b22, label letters, overdue, the Behind square and focus
            hairline: #b49c78, dotted rules and grid lines, never text
            washes: #d9b98f #b9c4d6 #c4d3b0 #d8b4a6 #cdbfd4 #bccfcf, figure segments a to f
            onTrack: #2f5d34, the ring with a dot
            atRisk: #80500a, the open triangle
        type:
            One stack, Baskerville, Baskerville Old Face, Libre Baskerville,
            Hoefler Text, Garamond, Times New Roman, serif. The greeting is 46px
            400 at 1.1, measurements 52px with old-style numerals, section
            titles 20px small caps tracked 0.14em over a rule, figure captions
            15px small caps then italic, body 17px at 1.55, label letters 20px
            bold italic in red ochre.
        layout:
            A plate up to 1240px with a 1px ink edge doubled 8px outside and a
            soft drop shadow. A centred masthead reads A systematic chart of the
            working week, then BRIGHTWORK in widely spaced caps and with figures
            drawn from life, over a double rule. A ruled bar holds the nav as
            roman numbered small caps links and the tools, a ruled italic search,
            a dark New project button, a round bell and a line drawn avatar with
            the name. The title block has a boxed Plate XXXI, the greeting with
            the date in italic, and an Observation note with a red ochre edge
            saying 4 tasks are overdue. Two columns follow. On the left, Fig. 1
            is a sectioned ring of six segments sized by task count, each in its
            own wash with the completed part hatched outward from the centre,
            170 tasks in all in the middle, and leader lines ending in lettered
            discs a to f. A Key to Fig. 1 lists each letter with the name, team,
            percent, tasks and due date, and the status. On the right, Fig. 2
            shows the four numbers as large numerals over caliper rules with
            lettered italic captions, Fig. 3 is an engraved line chart with a
            stippled area, values on each point and a dashed week divider, and
            Notes from the field is a numbered list of activity. A double rule
            and an italic credit line close the plate. Below 960px the columns
            stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between sections, 40px between columns, 28px plate margins.
        density: Moderate, like a printed plate. One large figure and a key, then smaller figures and notes.
        corners: Square frames and boxes. Round only for label letters, the bell and the figure.
        borders: A 1px ink plate edge doubled 8px out, double rules at top and foot, dotted hairlines between key rows.
        shadows: One soft drop under the plate, as if pinned to a wall. Nothing else.
        icons:
            Engraved line marks at 15px with the small caps word, a ring with a
            dot for On track, an open triangle for At risk and a solid square
            for Behind. Leader lines end in small ink dots.
        focus: A 2px red ochre outline offset 3px.
        tone: Victorian naturalist, such as Plate XXXI, Observation, Notes from the field and drawn from life.

    style129:
        number: 129
        run: 27
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Star chart
        idea: A pale celestial chart where projects are stars plotted on a dotted coordinate grid and joined by a constellation line, numbers are magnitudes in an oval cartouche and the daily chart is a light curve.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/129.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            skyPaper: #eef1f8, the page, with a #cfd5ea dot field
            chartField: #fbfcff, panels and fields
            nightNavy: #1b2550, text, stars, borders and the On track star
            dusk: #46507a, axis labels and captions
            grid: #cdd3e6, dotted coordinate lines and the inner frame line
            constellation: #7584bf, lines joining stars, never text
            halo: #e3e8f7, soft discs behind stars and the avatar
            brass: #7f5a00, the week divider and week totals
            atRisk: #7a3e8c, the diamond
            behind: #a2262e, the crossed circle and overdue
            focus: #3953c9, the 2px focus ring
        type:
            One stack, Optima, Candara, Segoe UI, Noto Sans, Seravek, sans-serif.
            The greeting is 46px 400 at 1.1, magnitudes 34px 400, panel titles
            22px 400 tracked 0.06em, Greek star letters 18px bold italic, body
            16px at 1.5, labels and the date 12 to 13px caps tracked 0.18 to
            0.3em.
        layout:
            A header ruled underneath with a compass star logo, the spaced caps
            brand, nav links in small spaced caps each led by a dot, Home led by
            a small filled star, then a pill search, a navy pill New project
            button, a round bell and a round avatar with the name. The intro has
            the light greeting, the spaced caps date and a crossed circle line
            saying 4 tasks are overdue, and on the right an oval cartouche with
            a double line border titled Magnitudes this week, holding the four
            numbers each beside a navy dot sized by its value, overdue as an open
            red ring. The main panel, The project sky, has an engraved double
            border and plots the six projects on a dotted grid, due date across
            from 1 Nov to 15 Jan and percent complete up, each a navy mark on a
            halo disc sized by task count, its shape showing status, labelled
            with its Greek letter, name and percent, all joined in due date order
            by a thin constellation line. Below, a Catalogue table lists Greek
            letter, project, team, percent, tasks, due date and status, beside
            an Observation log with the time in spaced caps. A wide Light curve
            panel plots the 14 days as dots sized by value on a thin line, with
            a brass dashed divider and week totals. Below 1060px the cartouche
            and panels stack, below 640px both charts scroll sideways inside
            their panels.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between panels, 20 to 24px panel padding, a 24px dot field behind.
        density: Airy. One wide sky chart, then catalogue and log side by side, then the light curve.
        corners: Fully round search, buttons and fields, a 120px oval cartouche and 6px panels.
        borders: A 1px navy outer line with a 1px grid blue inner line 5px inside, like an engraved map border.
        shadows: None. Stars sit on soft halo discs instead.
        icons:
            Celestial marks at 16px with the word, a five point star for On
            track, a diamond for At risk and a crossed circle for Behind. In the
            sky the same shapes are drawn larger, sized by task count.
        focus: A 2px blue outline offset 3px with a 6px soft blue halo.
        tone: Calm observatory words, such as Magnitudes this week, Catalogue, Observation log and Light curve.

    style130:
        number: 130
        run: 27
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Field guide
        idea: The dashboard as a pocket naturalist's guide, with thumb index tabs for navigation, each project written up as a species account with a plate drawing, field marks and a range map to its due date, and the chart drawn as a seasonal abundance band.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/130.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            desk: #dcd8c6, behind the book
            page: #faf7ee, the guide's pages
            ink: #232a22, text, line drawings and rules
            pencil: #55594d, captions, times and map labels
            rule: #cfc8b0, thin rules between accounts, never text
            moss: #3c6b3f, the primary button and the kicker
            rangeOchre: #c99a3c, range map shading on #ebe6d3
            abundance: #5d7f4c, last week in the band, with #2f5d73 for this week
            plateWashes: #f0d9b5 design, #cfdcea engineering, #d6e6c9 research, #ecd0cf marketing
            onTrack: #2c6a33, the dot
            atRisk: #8a4f00, the triangle
            behind: #9b2f2a, the diamond and overdue
        type:
            Names and labels use Franklin Gothic Medium, Franklin Gothic, ITC
            Franklin Gothic, Arial Narrow, Arial, sans-serif. Text uses Iowan Old
            Style, Charter, Bitstream Charter, Georgia, serif. The greeting is
            42px 700 sans at 1.08, section titles 22px 700 sans, species names
            19px 700 sans, team lines 16px italic serif, body 15 to 16px serif
            at 1.5, run-in labels such as Field marks in bold sans, times 12.5px
            caps sans.
        layout:
            A book spread up to 1240px on the desk colour, its fore edge rounded
            14px with stacked page edges below, and six coloured thumb index tabs
            standing off the right edge with vertical labels, the current Home
            tab wider with a heavy outline. A ruled running head has a round bird
            mark, the brand with A field guide to the team's projects, a search,
            a moss New project button, a square bell and the avatar with the
            name. The intro has the kicker Today in the field, the greeting, the
            italic date and a pink bar with a diamond saying Look out first for
            4 tasks that are overdue, beside a boxed Quick identification key
            with four small pictures and the numbers. Species accounts fill two
            thirds in two columns. Each account has a round wash plate with a
            line drawing for the team, a pen nib, a gear, a magnifier or a
            megaphone, and a black plate number, then the name, the team in
            italic, Field marks with percent and tasks, Status, and Range from
            now to the due date over a small Nov Dec Jan map shaded up to a dot
            on the due date. Recent sightings fills the last third. Seasonal
            abundance draws the 14 days as one horizontal band whose thickness
            follows each value, green then blue, with values, day letters and
            dates. Below 900px the tabs become a row of tabs under the header
            and everything stacks.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px between accounts, 32 to 40px between columns and 24px section padding.
        density: Bookish and fairly dense. Two columns of accounts beside a sightings column.
        corners: 3px on controls, round plates and avatars, and the book rounds 14px on its fore edge.
        borders: 1px ink under the running head, 1px pale rules between accounts and one boxed key.
        shadows: Stacked page edges under the spread and one soft drop. Accounts have none.
        icons:
            Hand drawn line pictures at 2.4 stroke on soft round washes, and
            tiny solid status marks at 14px with the word, a dot for On track, a
            triangle for At risk and a diamond for Behind.
        focus: A 3px slate blue outline offset 2px.
        tone: Naturalist's notes, such as Field marks, Range, Look out first for and Recent sightings.

    style131:
        number: 131
        run: 27
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Merit badges
        idea: The dashboard as an earned badge sash, with the four numbers sewn on a khaki sash, each project a round embroidered badge whose stitched ring fills with progress, and woven name tapes for navigation.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/131.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            canvas: #f4eedf, the page, with a fine weave
            felt: #fffaf0, panels, badge discs and fields
            khaki: #c9b88a, the sash, edged #8c7a4b
            threadBrown: #3b3020, text and 2px outlines
            fadedBrown: #5e5139, meta and times
            nameTape: #fbf7ec, nav tabs, banners and labels
            scarlet: #b23a2e, the primary button, the tape stitch and overdue
            navy: #24406b, the current tab, this week bars and focus
            forest: #2f6b3a, last week bars and the On track round patch
            goldThread: #d7a531, inner badge rings and avatars, never text
            atRisk: #8a5200, the triangle patch
            behind: #a8322a, the square patch
        type:
            Headings and labels use Arial Rounded MT Bold, Nunito, Varela Round,
            Helvetica Rounded, Trebuchet MS, sans-serif. Text uses Trebuchet MS,
            Lucida Grande, Verdana, sans-serif. The greeting is 38px 700 at 1.1,
            sash numbers 34px 700, section titles 22px 700, banners 15px 700,
            body 15px at 1.5, meta 13px.
        layout:
            A 240px khaki sash runs down the left with darker edges and a dashed
            stitch line inside. It carries a gold star burst logo with the brand,
            a woven name tape reading MARA OKAFOR with a red stitch, and four
            round felt badges with thick coloured borders and a gold inner ring
            for the numbers, each with a tape label below. The right side starts
            with woven name tape tabs for the nav, Home in navy with a white
            stitch, then a pill search, a scarlet pill New project button with an
            inner white stitch, a round bell and a gold avatar with the name. A
            felt panel with a dashed stitch inside holds the greeting with an
            exclamation mark, the date and a pink patch saying 4 tasks are
            overdue. Badges in progress shows six round badges three across, each
            a coloured edge with a white running stitch, a pale face, a thick
            ring in the thread colour filled to the percent, a line icon and the
            percent, a notched banner with the name, a meta line with team, tasks
            and due date, and the status patch. Below sit two felt panels,
            Stitch count with bars filled with cross stitch, green then navy,
            and Troop log with gold initials badges. Below 1100px badges go two
            across, below 820px the sash becomes a band under the header with
            badges two by two.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 18px between sash badges and 24px between project badges and panels.
        density: Roomy and proud. Big round badges three across with plenty of canvas between.
        corners: Round badges and pill controls, 14px felt panels and 4 to 6px tapes.
        borders: A 2px brown outline plus a dashed stitch line 5 or 6px inside every panel, tape and badge.
        shadows: A small drop under sewn badges and the sash so they sit on the fabric.
        icons:
            Chunky 3px line pictures inside badges. Status patches at 20px carry
            a stitch edge and the word, a round patch with a tick for On track,
            a triangle with a bar for At risk and a square with a bar for Behind.
        focus: A 3px dashed navy outline offset 3px.
        tone: Warm and encouraging like a troop leader, such as Good afternoon, Mara!, Badges in progress and Troop log.

    style132:
        number: 132
        run: 27
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Field manual
        idea: The dashboard written as a light olive drab field manual, with stencil headings, numbered paragraphs, a boxed WARNING for the overdue tasks, ruled tables with hatched progress bars and figures with numbered captions.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/132.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            paper: #e3e1cc, the page around the manual
            page: #f5f3e6, manual pages, fields and the hatch ground
            oliveDrab: #4b5320, the top band, table heads, the current item and this week bars
            darkOlive: #363c17, the band edge and the bell
            ink: #1f2113, text, 2px rules, hatching and focus
            fadedInk: #4a4c36, captions, times and page numbers
            khaki: #a59f78, dotted leaders, never text
            signalYellow: #f2d24b, the primary button and the focus halo
            onTrack: #36561f, the filled circle
            atRisk: #7d5300, the triangle with a bar
            behind: #9e2a1e, the crossed square, the WARNING label and the stamp
        type:
            Headings use Stencil, Stencil Std, Stencilia, Arial Black, Impact,
            sans-serif. Labels use Arial Narrow, Roboto Condensed, Helvetica Neue
            Condensed, Liberation Sans Narrow, Arial in bold caps tracked 0.06
            to 0.16em. Text uses Century Schoolbook, New Century Schoolbook, TeX
            Gyre Schola, Georgia, serif. The chapter title is 30px stencil,
            strength numbers 40px stencil, paragraph heads 17px narrow caps with
            a stencil number, the greeting 26px serif, body 15px at 1.5, times
            12.5px narrow caps in brackets.
        layout:
            An olive band with a darker 6px bottom edge holds a shield logo, the
            stencil brand with FIELD MANUAL BW 10-31 DAILY SITUATION under it, a
            boxed caps search, a yellow New project button, a square bell and
            the name boxed as OKAFOR, MARA. A 220px CONTENTS box on the left
            lists the nav with chapter numbers 1-1 to 6-1 on dotted leaders,
            Home filled olive, with a tilted red FOR TEAM USE stamp. The page on
            the right opens with CHAPTER 1 SITUATION REPORT over a 4px rule and
            SECTION I 31 OCT 2026. Numbered paragraphs follow. 1-1 Greeting
            gives Good afternoon, Mara. and the date. 1-2 Priority is a boxed
            WARNING with a red label saying 4 tasks are overdue, Clear these
            first. 1-3 Strength is a four cell ruled box of stencil numbers,
            the overdue cell tinted. 1-4 Operations is Table 1-1 with olive
            heads, a serial letter, project, unit, a hatched progress bar with
            percent, tasks, due date in caps and status. 1-5 Activity log lists
            lettered sub paragraphs with bracketed times, beside 1-6 Tempo, a
            boxed Figure 1-1 with hatched bars for last week and solid olive bars
            for this week, axis ticks and bracketed week totals. A ruled foot
            gives BW 10-31 and the page number. Below 980px the contents become
            a grid above the page, the table scrolls inside itself.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 20px between paragraphs, 24px page padding and 32px between side by side paragraphs.
        density: Dense and orderly. Everything sits in numbered paragraphs on one long page.
        corners: Square, always.
        borders: 2px ink boxes, 1px ruled table cells, a 4px rule under the chapter title and a 3px WARNING box.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            Solid 16px symbols with the caps word, a filled circle for ON TRACK,
            a triangle with a bar for AT RISK and a crossed square for BEHIND.
            Hatching marks figures.
        focus: A 3px ink outline offset 2px inside a 5px signal yellow halo.
        tone: Orders and reports, such as Situation report, Strength, Operations, Tempo and Clear these first.

    style133:
        number: 133
        run: 27
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Warehouse logistics
        idea: The dashboard as a warehouse dispatch board, with aisle signs for navigation, numbers on hazard striped counters, each project a shipping label with a bin location, a barcode and cartons loaded, and the daily chart as a row of conveyor belts.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/133.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            concrete: #e9e8e3, the floor, with a faint 120px grid
            labelWhite: #ffffff, labels, panels and fields
            black: #111111, text, 2 to 3px borders, aisle signs and barcodes
            steel: #4f4f4b, small codes and meta
            forkliftYellow: #f5c400, the top band, bins, the current aisle and the focus halo, never text on light
            kraft: #c89b62, cartons and the label offset shadow, edged #8a6233
            rule: #b9b8b0, table rules
            onTrack: #17663a, the ticked box
            atRisk: #8a4b00, the triangle
            behind: #b3121b, the crossed octagon, the overdue tag and the late label shadow
        type:
            Labels and text use Arial Narrow, Roboto Condensed, Helvetica Neue
            Condensed, Liberation Sans Narrow, Arial, sans-serif, with bold caps
            for labels. Codes and numbers use OCR A Std, OCR A Extended,
            ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas, monospace. The greeting is
            40px 700 at 1.05, counters 46px 700 mono, label names 24px 700,
            pallet codes 13px mono tracked 0.2em, body 15px at 1.45, field
            labels such as SHIP TO and BIN 11px mono.
        layout:
            A forklift yellow top band with a kraft carton logo, the caps brand
            with DC-01 DISPATCH BOARD in mono, a boxed search, a black New
            project button with yellow text, a square bell and a black MO badge
            with the name, edged below by a black and yellow hazard stripe. The
            nav is six black aisle signs hanging on short posts, each with a
            yellow square letter A to F and the label, the current Home sign
            yellow with a black letter. The greeting sits on a white dock door
            panel tagged DOOR 01 with the date in mono, and a red luggage tag
            shape says 4 TASKS ARE OVERDUE. Four counters with a hazard striped
            top hold the numbers in mono with bin codes K-01 to K-04, the overdue
            counter striped red and white. Outbound projects shows six shipping
            labels three across, each with a 3px black border and a hard kraft
            offset shadow, red for the late one. A label has a SHIP TO team cell
            and a yellow BIN cell, the project name, a row of ten carton boxes
            filled by tens of percent with the percent, cartons done of total
            and the due date, a barcode with a pallet code such as BW-WR-1114,
            and a bordered status stamp. Below, Throughput draws each day as a
            conveyor belt with carton segments, one per task, under black week
            headers with totals, beside a Dock log table with mono times. Below
            1100px labels go two across and aisles three, below 600px everything
            stacks and aisles go two across.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16 to 20px between counters and labels and 24px between panels.
        density: Busy but scannable, like a dispatch board. Three labels across with codes everywhere.
        corners: Square. The overdue tag has a cut luggage tag point.
        borders: 3px black on labels with 3px divider rows, 2px on everything else, hazard stripes on top edges.
        shadows: A hard 6px kraft offset under each label, red when the project is behind. No blur.
        icons:
            Bold filled signs at 18px inside a bordered stamp with the caps word,
            a ticked box for ON TRACK, a triangle with a bar for AT RISK and a
            crossed octagon for BEHIND, plus a carton logo.
        focus: A 3px black outline offset 2px inside a 6px forklift yellow halo.
        tone: Floor operations, such as Outbound projects, Ship to, Bin, Cartons, Throughput and Dock log.

    style134:
        number: 134
        run: 28
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Shipping labels
        idea: Every panel is a white parcel label stuck on kraft cardboard, with thick black rules, barcodes, tracking codes and handling pictograms for status.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/134.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            kraft: #e3d1b0, the page as cardboard
            tape: #c9ae7f, translucent tape strips on label tops, decoration only
            label: #ffffff, every panel, field and nav code
            ink: #111111, text, rules, barcodes, fill bars and the primary button
            grey: #4d4d4d, units and type notes
            green: #1d6a33, the On track mark with two up arrows
            amber: #8f5300, the At risk mark with a wine glass
            red: #b8141b, the Behind mark with a crossed box, the overdue box and number
            marker: #ffe14a, the focus halo only
        type:
            Two stacks. Condensed sans for nearly everything uses Arial Narrow,
            Helvetica Neue Condensed, Roboto Condensed, Arial at weight 800 for
            titles and numbers. Mono for codes and dates uses SF Mono, Menlo,
            Consolas, monospace. Summary numbers 64px, greeting 44px, label
            titles 24px, body 15px, captions 11px bold caps tracked 0.14em,
            tracking codes 12px mono.
        layout:
            The header is one wide label split by 3px rules into a From cell
            with a box logo and the brand, a search cell, and a Deliver to cell
            with New project, a square bell and the user. Nav is a row of boxed
            service codes numbered 01 to 06, the current one inverted black.
            Below sit a Dispatch note label with the greeting, the date in mono
            and a red boxed overdue warning, beside a Manifest label holding the
            four numbers in ruled cells. Projects are six labels in three
            columns, each with a category and status mark on top, the name, a
            barcode and tracking code, a dashed tear grid of Done, Weight and
            Deliver by, and a black fill bar. A Tracking history label lists
            activity with mono times on the left. A Daily scans label holds the
            black bar chart with values, a divider between weeks and two ruled
            total cells. Below 1000px labels go two across and the top stacks.
            Below 680px everything is one column and header cells stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 12px inside label cells, 20 to 24px between labels.
        density: Medium dense. Each label packs code, name, three fields and a bar.
        corners: 4px on labels, 3px on nav codes, square buttons and fields.
        borders: 3px solid ink around labels and between header cells, 2px dashed ink tear lines inside.
        shadows: One hard brown shadow 2px right and 3px down, like a sticker lifting off board.
        icons:
            Filled handling pictograms at 20px in a 2px bordered mark with the
            caps word. Two up arrows on a base for On track, a wine glass for At
            risk, a crossed box for Behind, a filled warning triangle for
            overdue. The bell is a 2px outline.
        focus: A 3px ink outline offset 2px inside a 7px marker yellow halo.
        tone: Courier terms in caps, such as Dispatch note, Manifest, Deliver by and Tracking history.

    style135:
        number: 135
        run: 28
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Flight strips
        idea: Projects are paper flight progress strips slotted into a grey bay, read left to right in tidy columns of callsign, route, progress boxes, due time and a status code.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/135.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            console: #e6ebe5, the page
            bay: #c9d1c9, strip bays and the side rack
            rail: #5d665f, bay headers, holder edges and borders
            ink: #1b2420, text, filled progress boxes, this week bars and the primary button
            muted: #4b5650, column keys and task counts
            buffStrip: #f5e7ae, Design and Research strips and last week bars
            blueStrip: #d4e5f4, Engineering strips
            pinkStrip: #f3d8de, Marketing strips
            normal: #1e6b3a, On track with a ring
            caution: #8a5100, At risk with a solid triangle
            alert: #a3191f, Behind with a barred square, overdue text
            focus: #0b57a8, the focus outline only
        type:
            Mono for data uses IBM Plex Mono, SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas,
            monospace. Sans for names and prose uses Helvetica Neue, Helvetica,
            Arial. Board digits 34px mono bold, greeting 28px sans bold,
            callsigns 18px mono bold, project names 16px sans bold, body 14px,
            keys 10px bold caps tracked 0.12em.
        layout:
            A 168px left side rack holds the brand in mono and nav as stacked
            strips with a 6px rail edge and a three letter code, the current
            one dark with a buff edge. A pale top bar holds a framed search, New
            project, a square bell and On position Mara Okafor. A status line
            has the mono date, the greeting and a red Attention line with a
            triangle, and on the right a boxed board of four mono numbers. The
            Active bay lists six strips under column keys, each strip a grid of
            callsign with category, name with task count, ten progress boxes
            with a percent, due date and status with a short code, sorted by
            due date and coloured by department. A right column has a Radio log
            of small strips and a Movements chart with outline bars for last
            week and solid bars for this week. Below 820px the rack becomes a
            top row and strips wrap into two rows.
        spacing: A 4px base. 6px between strips, 10px inside cells, 24px between bays.
        density: High. One strip per project about 58px tall, every fact in its own column.
        corners: Strips square, bays and buttons 2 to 3px.
        borders: A 10px rail holder edge on the left of each strip, 1px grey around, hairline column dividers.
        shadows: A hard 2px drop under each strip so it sits in the bay. Nothing else.
        icons: Ring for On track, solid triangle for At risk, solid square with a white bar for Behind, beside the word and codes NML, RISK, BHND.
        focus: A 3px blue outline offset 2px.
        tone: Terse controller speech, such as Active bay, Radio log, Movements and On position.

    style136:
        number: 136
        run: 28
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Racing telemetry
        idea: A daylight timing screen where projects race in a position tower, progress reads as three sector bars, and italic slanted numbers carry the speed.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/136.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            pitLane: #f3f4f6, the page, nav tabs and field fill
            panel: #ffffff, panels and the header
            tarmac: #1c1f24, text, position chips, sector fill and checkers
            muted: #545a63, keys, gaps and axes
            line: #d5d8dd, row rules and grid
            raceRed: #c8102e, brand plate, primary button, this week line, Behind
            purple: #6a1fb0, best sectors, the best day and focus
            green: #1a7a35, On track and the Research team bar
            amber: #8c5a00, At risk text
            flagYellow: #f6c90e, the race control flag, never text
        type:
            Sans uses Helvetica Neue, Arial Black, Arial, mostly italic 800 to
            900 caps. Numbers use DIN Alternate, Bahnschrift, Roboto Condensed,
            Arial Narrow in italic. Mono for gaps and times uses SF Mono, Menlo,
            Consolas. Hero numbers 48px, greeting 40px caps, panel titles 18px
            caps, project names 16px italic, body 14px, keys 11px italic caps.
        layout:
            A checkered band runs across the top and again before the sheet.
            The header has a red slanted brand plate, an underlined search, a
            slanted red New project button, a round bell and Driver Mara
            Okafor, then slanted nav tabs with the current one black with a red
            base. The race row has the date, a big italic caps greeting and a
            Race control message bar with a yellow flag cell, beside four
            slanted number tiles with thick left bars. The Timing tower table
            orders projects by completion from P1 to P6 with a slanted position
            chip, a team colour bar, name and category, three sector bars,
            tasks, percent, gap in points to the leader, due and status. The
            right column holds a Pace line chart comparing this week solid red
            against last week dashed by weekday, and Team radio activity. The
            table scrolls inside its panel on small screens.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 10px table cells, 24px between panels.
        density: Dense in the tower, airy in the hero numbers.
        corners: None. Shapes are parallelograms slanted minus 12 degrees instead of rounded.
        borders: 1px light line on panels, a 3px tarmac rule under panel titles, 6px left bars on number tiles.
        shadows: None.
        icons: Filled circle for On track, half filled diamond for At risk, downward triangle for Behind, as position change marks beside the italic caps word.
        focus: A 3px purple outline offset 2px.
        tone: Pit wall shorthand in italic caps, such as Timing tower, Race control, Pace, Team radio, Leader and plus 18.

    style137:
        number: 137
        run: 28
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Ski trail map
        idea: The dashboard opens on a painted mountain where each project is a numbered run, and status uses the trail sign shapes, green circle, blue square and black diamond.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/137.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            sky: #e4f1fa, the page top and totals
            snow: #ffffff, panels and the mountain face
            shade: #c9def0, shadow faces, dividers and last week bars
            night: #12233a, text, borders and the ridge line
            slate: #47596e, captions and meta
            pine: #1f5135, board headers, trees and the avatar
            greenRun: #15803d, the On track circle and word
            blueRun: #1d4ed8, the At risk square, this week bars
            blackRun: #111111, the Behind diamond and word
            liftRed: #b4232a, primary button, lift line and overdue
            patrolAmber: #f59e0b, the focus halo only
        type:
            Geometric sans for headings and numbers uses Futura, Century Gothic,
            Avenir Next, Trebuchet MS. Body uses Avenir Next, Segoe UI,
            Trebuchet MS, system-ui. Numbers 46px bold, greeting 36px, board
            titles 18px caps, run names 17px bold, body 15px at 1.5, captions
            11px caps tracked 0.14em.
        layout:
            The header has a peak logo, a pill search, a red pill New project,
            a round bell and an avatar with the name, then pill nav with the
            current item dark. The greeting sits left with a red outlined
            overdue pill right. A wide framed trail map follows, an inline
            mountain with trees, a dashed red lift line and six coloured runs,
            each marked by its trail sign holding the run number, names shown
            beside runs on wide screens, and a legend strip below. Four
            outlined tiles with dark caps headers hold the numbers, overdue in
            red. A Trail report board lists runs with number, sign, name,
            category, tasks, a striped groomed bar and status with due date.
            The right column has a Snow report bar chart and Mountain news.
            Below 720px names hide and the map scrolls inside its frame.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 12 to 16px inside boards, 24px between them.
        density: Open. A big map first, then a calm board with one row per run.
        corners: 16px boards, 12 to 14px tiles, full pills for buttons, search and nav.
        borders: 2px night outline on map, boards and tiles, 1px shade dividers inside.
        shadows: None. Depth lives in the mountain shading.
        icons: Trail signs with a white edge. Green circle On track, blue square At risk, black diamond Behind, red octagon with a white bar for overdue, always with the word.
        focus: A 3px night outline offset 2px inside a 7px amber halo.
        tone: Resort friendly, such as Trail report, Snow report, Mountain news, runs open and groomed.

    style138:
        number: 138
        run: 28
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Surf report
        idea: A beach shack surf forecast where the week is a smooth swell chart, projects are breaks in a forecast table, and progress stands up as rounded waves.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/138.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            sand: #f7eedb, the page and sheet rows
            foam: #fffaf0, panels and text on deep sea
            sea: #0e6973, nav, table head and the swell line
            deep: #0b3d4a, header, headings and big numbers
            shallow: #cdeef0, swell fill, condition tiles and focus fill
            sun: #f7c948, primary button and sun disc, never text
            coral: #b23a2f, the Behind flag and the overdue banner
            coralSoft: #f6c6b8, the overdue tile and avatar
            driftwood: #4a3a2a, body text
            bark: #6a5644, captions and row keys
            palm: #1f6f3c, the On track sun
            rust: #8a5300, the At risk fin
        type:
            Rounded sans for headings and numbers uses Arial Rounded MT Bold,
            Varela Round, Nunito, Trebuchet MS, Verdana. Body uses Verdana,
            Tahoma, DejaVu Sans. Tile numbers 38px, greeting 36px, section
            titles 22px, chart labels 13px bold, body 14px at 1.55, captions
            11px caps tracked 0.1em.
        layout:
            A deep sea header holds a sun over wave logo, a pill search, a
            yellow pill New project with a ledge, a round bell and the user,
            over a sea nav with rounded top tabs where the current tab is sand.
            The first row pairs a Today's report panel with a corner sun, the
            greeting, a coral overdue banner and four rounded condition tiles,
            with a wide swell chart panel showing a smooth filled curve with
            dots and values for the 14 days and two total pills. The Break
            forecast is a table with projects as columns and rows for
            conditions, progress as rounded wave bars, tasks done and due, which
            scrolls sideways inside its panel on small screens. Below are a
            Beach log and a key panel explaining the three status icons.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 20 to 24px padding in panels, 24 to 28px between sections.
        density: Relaxed. Big rounded numbers, one forecast table, generous line height.
        corners: Very soft. 24px panels, 16 to 18px tiles, 22px pill buttons, wave bars rounded on top.
        borders: Mostly none. Dotted 2px sand lines between table cells and log rows.
        shadows: Only the primary button, a 3px solid darker sun ledge below it.
        icons: Chunky filled beach signs at 30px above the word. Rayed sun On track, fin over a wave At risk, square beach flag Behind, rounded exclamation tile for overdue.
        focus: A 3px dashed deep sea outline offset 3px with a shallow fill, sun yellow on dark bars.
        tone: Laid back, such as Today's report, Heads up, Break forecast, Beach log and how the week is breaking.

    style139:
        number: 139
        run: 29
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: National park
        idea: Routed wooden park signs on a meadow page, with projects as arrow boards on a signpost, the week as a mileage sign and status as painted trail markers.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/139.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            meadow: #edefe0, the page
            paper: #fbf6e6, pinned notices, markers and the sheet
            wood: #5b3b20, every sign board and headings
            darkWood: #3a2512, carved text shadow and board ledge
            routedLine: #8f6a43, the inner groove and leader dots
            carvedCream: #f6ecd2, text on wood and blazes
            moss: #2f5a32, primary button and On track
            fern: #dfe7cf, chart fill and totals
            barkInk: #2b2116, body text on paper
            caution: #e0ac2b, the caution diamond, focus ring and overdue number on wood
            ochre: #7f5200, the At risk marker
            rust: #9c2a1a, the Behind marker and pin
            lightWood: #e3d3ad, nav plates
        type:
            Slab serif for signs uses Rockwell, Roboto Slab, Clarendon, Serifa,
            Museo Slab, Egyptienne, Georgia, in caps tracked 0.04 to 0.08em with
            a 2px dark carved shadow on wood. Body uses Gill Sans, Seravek,
            Trebuchet MS, Ubuntu. Greeting 40px slab, brand 30px caps, sign
            names 22px caps, mileage figures 30px, body 16px at 1.5, captions
            12px caps tracked 0.14em.
        layout:
            A trailhead board header holds a round tree emblem, the carved
            brand, a pinned paper notice as the search, a moss New project, a
            round bell and the user. Nav is a row of arrow shaped light wood
            plates, the current one dark wood. The greeting sits beside a
            caution diamond and line, opposite a mileage sign board listing the
            four numbers with dotted leaders. Projects hang as six arrow boards
            on a tall post, each with the carved name and category, a cream
            status marker, ten blazes for progress with percent and tasks, and
            the due date. Below are a Ranger log board holding pinned paper and
            a Trail profile board with an elevation style line chart and a flag
            on the best day. On small screens arrow boards stack their facts.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 12px between signs, 20 to 24px inside boards, 32px between sections.
        density: Medium. One project per arrow board, facts read across.
        corners: 8px boards, 4px paper and markers, arrow boards end in a pointed tip.
        borders: A routed groove, a 2px lighter line set 5px inside each board, dashed lines on paper.
        shadows: A 4px solid dark wood ledge under boards and 2px under pinned paper.
        icons: Painted trail markers on cream plates. Up arrow On track, triangle with a bar At risk, crossed sticks Behind, yellow caution diamond for overdue.
        focus: A 3px caution yellow outline offset 3px ringed by dark wood. Nav plates drop their arrow clip while focused.
        tone: Ranger plain speech, such as Trails, Ranger log, Trail profile, Caution and the trail ahead.

    style140:
        number: 140
        run: 29
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Vintage travel poster
        idea: A 1930s railway poster wall, where the greeting sits under a sunlit flat landscape and each project is a little poster whose sun rises as its tasks are done.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/140.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            wall: #efe3c8, the page and field fill
            cream: #fbf3e0, poster mounts, bands and cards
            navy: #1f2f4a, text, frames and the primary button
            slate: #55607a, captions and meta
            sun: #f6c453, suns and the focus halo, never text
            apricot: #f2a65a, sky gradients and last week bars
            rose: #d9675a, far hills and the nav underline
            teal: #2b6f6b, middle hills and this week bars
            sea: #1d4e5f, near hills and cypress trees
            pineText: #22625e, the On track star
            ochre: #8a4f00, the At risk half sun
            terracotta: #a63d22, the Behind cloud and overdue stamp
        type:
            Display uses Futura, Century Gothic, Avenir Next, Gill Sans in bold
            caps tracked 0.08 to 0.3em. Condensed lettering uses Futura
            Condensed, Avenir Next Condensed, Arial Narrow at 800. Body uses
            Optima, Candara, Segoe UI. Destination lettering up to 120px,
            numbers 46px condensed, greeting 32px caps, poster titles 15px caps,
            body 16px at 1.55, captions 11px caps tracked 0.24em.
        layout:
            A cream header with the spaced brand, an underlined search, a navy
            New project, a round bell and the user name in caps, over centred
            spaced caps nav with a rose underline, closed by a double rule. The
            hero is a mounted poster with a flat sunset scene of hills, cypress
            and a sailboat under huge Brightwork lettering, and a cream band
            with the date, greeting and a tilted overdue stamp. Four mounted
            tickets carry flat icons and the numbers. Six portrait mini posters
            show a gradient sky, a percent, a sun whose height follows progress
            and hills, then name, category, tasks, due and status. Below are a
            Travel diary and an Itinerary bar chart with sunset bars for last
            week and sea bars for this week.
        spacing: An 8px unit. Cream mounts 8 to 12px wide, 18 to 28px gaps, 44px between sections.
        density: Low. A big hero poster, four tickets, six small posters.
        corners: Square everywhere, only suns and the bell are round.
        borders: A 2px navy frame inside a cream mount, double rules under the header and above the sheet.
        shadows: Soft hung on a wall drops, 0 8px 18px navy at 15 to 20 percent.
        icons: Flat filled shapes. Four point star On track, half sun on the horizon At risk, cloud Behind, ringed exclamation stamp for overdue.
        focus: A 3px navy outline offset 3px inside an 8px sun halo.
        tone: Travel copy in spaced caps, such as Visit the week ahead, Destinations, Travel diary and Itinerary.

    style141:
        number: 141
        run: 29
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Space age 1960s
        idea: The dashboard is a filled in mission control form on white paper, with numbered fields, embroidered style patches, T minus countdown clocks for due dates and GO, HOLD, SCRUB status.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/141.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            paper: #f7f5ef, the page
            form: #ffffff, the form sheet and fields
            ink: #141414, text, form rules and patches
            graphite: #555149, field labels
            rule: #b9b4a8, inner rules and the planned path
            grid: #e6e1d4, graph paper
            orange: #e8590c, top stripe, trajectories and this week bars, never small text
            burntOrange: #b33f00, field numbers, the primary button and times
            console: #161a1d, countdown clock faces
            digit: #ff8a3d, clock digits and the focus halo
            earthBlue: #2a5d8f, the insignia globe only
            goGreen: #1d6b3a, On track
            holdAmber: #8a5300, At risk
            scrubRed: #b3261e, Behind and overdue
        type:
            Extended head type uses Eurostile, Microgramma, Michroma, Bank
            Gothic, Helvetica Neue at 800. Body uses Helvetica Neue, Helvetica,
            Arial. Mono uses SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas. Readouts 48px, greeting
            30px, mission names 17px, clocks 18px mono, body 14px, field labels
            10px caps tracked 0.16em with a burnt orange field number.
        layout:
            An orange stripe tops a white header with a round orbit insignia,
            Program office over the spaced brand, a boxed search with a ruled
            label cell, a burnt orange New project, a square bell and Flight
            director Mara Okafor, over ruled nav cells with the current one
            black with an orange base. A Mission status report title with a
            form number leads into one ruled form sheet. Its first row holds
            field 01 with the greeting, date and a red Hold box, then fields 02
            to 05 as big readouts. Six mission cells follow in three columns,
            each with a round patch and initials, numbered category, name, an
            orange trajectory arc over a dashed planned path, a field grid of
            tasks and percent with a black T minus clock, and a status row. The
            last row holds a Communications transcript and Fig. 1, a graph paper
            bar chart with outline bars for last week and orange bars for this.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 14 to 16px inside form cells, cells abut on shared rules.
        density: Dense like paperwork. One form sheet holds every section.
        corners: Square forms and buttons, round patches and insignia, 4px clocks.
        borders: A 1px ink form grid, a 4px orange top rule, 1px light rules inside mission fields.
        shadows: None.
        icons: Filled circle with check On track GO, framed pause bars At risk HOLD, solid cross Behind SCRUB, each with the word and a boxed code.
        focus: A 2px ink outline offset 2px inside a 6px digit orange halo.
        tone: Program office formal, such as Mission status report, Flight director, Communications transcript, Fig. 1 and Hold.

    style142:
        number: 142
        run: 29
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Pulp sci-fi
        idea: A 1950s pulp magazine printed in two inks on yellowed paper, where the greeting is a cover headline with a starburst, projects are the contents page and progress is a little ship on a dashed flight path.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/142.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            pulp: #f4e4c1, the page
            page: #fbf1da, cover, panels and text on ink
            redInk: #b5121b, masthead band, starburst, Behind and the primary button
            navyInk: #1a2a5e, header, frames, On track and At risk
            keyBlack: #1c1a24, body text and hard shadows
            greyInk: #4d4a5a, small labels
            halftone: #b5121b, red or navy dots at 16 to 18 percent as cover and chart texture
        type:
            Masthead and headlines use Impact, Haettenschweiler, Arial Narrow
            Bold, Oswald in caps, slanted minus 6 to 10 degrees. Labels use
            Franklin Gothic Medium, Arial Narrow in caps tracked 0.08em. Body
            uses Century Schoolbook, TeX Gyre Schola, Georgia. Masthead up to
            92px, headline up to 58px, numbers 40px, contents titles 19px bold
            italic serif, body 16px at 1.5.
        layout:
            A navy header holds a slanted brand, a paper search, a red New
            project with a raygun and hard shadow, a round bell and the user,
            over a red nav where the current item is paper with a raygun. The
            cover sits left in a 6px navy frame with a red masthead band, a
            week and date price box, a navy tagline strip and a halftone scene
            with a rocket and ringed planet, the date, a huge slanted greeting,
            a red starburst for 4 tasks overdue and four callout boxes with hard
            shadows. In this issue sits right as a contents list numbered 01 to
            06 in red, with italic serif names, category and due, a dashed
            flight path with a red trail and a ship at the percent, and tasks
            with status. Below are Dispatches from the crew with red time tags
            and a bar chart of rocket nosed bars, striped navy last week and
            solid red this week.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 12 to 18px inside panels, 28px between cover and contents.
        density: Busy cover, orderly contents list, big type everywhere.
        corners: Square. Curves only in planets, rockets and the starburst.
        borders: Thick ink frames, 6px navy on the cover, 3px black on panels, 2px dotted navy between entries.
        shadows: Hard offset 4px solid shadows in navy, red or black, like misregistered print.
        icons: Two ink silhouettes. Rocket On track, ringed planet At risk, comet Behind, red starburst for overdue, a raygun on the primary button and current nav item.
        focus: A 3px navy outline offset 3px, then a paper gap and a red ring.
        tone: Breathless cover lines with exclamation marks, such as In this issue, Dispatches from the crew and Launches per day.

    style143:
        number: 143
        run: 29
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Steampunk
        idea: A Victorian engine room on parchment, where the week reads from brass pressure gauges, projects are riveted brass plates with copper filled glass tubes, and the fortnight scrolls out of a chart recorder.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/143.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            parchment: #f1e6cc, the page with faint stains
            vellum: #faf3e1, ledger, tags and status pills
            brassLight: #e2c57a, plate highlight and rivet rings
            brass: #b8933f, plates and bezels, never text
            brassDeep: #6b4f16, rules, rivets and the last week line
            copper: #9a4a24, tube fluid, primary button, this week line and focus
            iron: #2e2a24, text, needles and the nav rail
            umber: #5d513f, small caps labels
            rule: #cbb98f, ledger lines
            verdigris: #2f6b5f, the On track cog and safe arc
            amber: #7d5200, At risk
            oxideRed: #9a2a1c, Behind and the pressure warning
        type:
            Display uses Playfair Display, Didot, Bodoni 72, Baskerville,
            Georgia at 700. Text uses Baskerville, Libre Baskerville, Hoefler
            Text, Garamond, Georgia. Labels are small caps tracked 0.1em.
            Greeting 42px, gauge numbers 34px with old style figures, plate
            titles 20px, body 17px at 1.5, labels 15px small caps.
        layout:
            A riveted brass plate header holds a cog emblem, Patent project
            engine over the brand, an inset vellum search, a copper pill New
            project, a round brass bell and Chief engineer Mara Okafor, over a
            dark iron nav rail with small caps links where the current one is a
            brass tab. The greeting with a long form date sits over a double
            rule, opposite a vellum Pressure warning tag. Four brass plates hold
            round gauges with cream faces, ticks, needles set to each number on
            a stated scale and a red zone for overdue, with the number below.
            The six engines are brass plates in two columns, each with category,
            name, a glass tube filled with copper to the percent, tasks, a due
            tag and a status pill. The right column holds an Engine room ledger
            with a red margin line and an Output recorder plate with a graph
            paper line chart, dashed for last week and solid copper for this.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16 to 22px inside plates, 16 to 20px between them, 28 to 32px between sections.
        density: Medium. Four gauges, six plates in two columns, a ruled ledger.
        corners: 6px plates, 3 to 4px paper, full pills on buttons and status, round gauges.
        borders: Brass bevels instead of lines, a rivet in each plate corner, double rules under the greeting, a red margin line in the ledger.
        shadows: Bevel highlights inside plates plus a soft 0 3px 6px brown drop. Fields are inset.
        icons: Engraved solid shapes in vellum pills with the small caps word. Cog On track, triangle with a bar At risk, hex nut with a bar Behind.
        focus: A 3px double copper outline offset 4px with a 2px vellum ring.
        tone: Victorian engineering labels, such as The six engines, Engine room ledger, Output recorder, Pressure warning and Chief engineer.

    style144:
        number: 144
        run: 30
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Illuminated manuscript
        idea: The dashboard is a page of a medieval book of hours, with vellum, ruled text blocks, a gilded drop capital for the greeting, red rubrics for headings and a vine growing down the margin.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/144.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            outerParchment: #e8d9b5, the page around the folio
            vellum: #f8f0dc, the folio, panels and fields
            ironGallInk: #2b1d10, body text and the chart baseline
            sepia: #5b4630, dates, notes, labels and italic asides
            rubric: #a3271c, rubric headings, pilcrows, overdue, Behind, this week bars and the primary button
            lapis: #22408a, the drop capital ground, last week bars, project links and focus
            goldLeaf: #b98a2e, frames, progress fills and the focus halo, never text
            goldInk: #6f4f12, At risk and the small roman numerals
            verdigris: #2e5e3b, the vine, the avatar and On track
            ruling: #d9b9a6, ruled lines and double margins
        type:
            Two old style serifs. Display uses Goudy Old Style, Garamond, EB
            Garamond, Palatino Linotype, Georgia, serif. Text uses Palatino
            Linotype, Book Antiqua, Palatino, URW Palladio L, Georgia, serif
            with old style numerals throughout. The drop capital is 76px bold
            white in a 104px box, the greeting 44px, summary figures 52px,
            rubrics 15px caps tracked 0.2em in red, entry titles 20px
            semibold, body 17px at 1.55, notes 14 to 15px italic, labels in
            small caps.
        layout:
            One folio up to 1260px on a darker parchment page. A 200px left
            margin holds the brand with a blue boxed initial B, an italic
            incipit, a Contents rubric and the nav as ruled lines each led by
            a red pilcrow, with a fleuron on the current page. A green vine
            with red and gold berries climbs the margin's right edge below the
            nav. The text block starts with a ruled header line holding an
            underlined italic search, a red New project button with a gold
            inner line, a round bell and a ringed avatar with the name in
            italic, closed by a red double rule. The greeting opens with a
            gilded lapis drop capital G beside the rest of the words, the date
            in italic and a red Take heed line naming the 4 overdue tasks. The
            four totals sit in one ruled row split by double rules, each with
            a small caps label, a large figure and a roman numeral beneath.
            Below, a wide Register of works lists the six projects as ruled
            entries with a large coloured initial alternating red and blue,
            the title and italic category, a gold striped progress rule,
            percent, tasks, due date and the status at the right. A narrower
            column holds the chart framed as a gilded miniature and a Chronicle
            of activity led by pilcrows. A colophon closes the page. Below
            900px the margin becomes a top strip with the nav in a row, the
            vine is hidden and columns stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 32 to 48px text margins, 40px between columns, 14px inside each register entry.
        density: Medium. A full text block per column, read slowly like a page.
        corners: Square, except a worn rounded top right corner on the folio and round arched tops on chart bars and swatches.
        borders: Red double rules under the header, a double ruling between margin and text, hairline ruling between entries and a gold frame with lapis and vellum rings around the miniature.
        shadows: None. Frames are layered rings of gold, vellum and lapis.
        icons:
            Thin line icons at text size, pilcrows and fleurons as markers.
            Status uses a green quatrefoil for On track, a gold brown triangle
            with a mark for At risk and a red crossed square for Behind, each
            beside the small caps word.
        focus: A 2px lapis outline offset 2 to 3px inside a 5 to 7px translucent gold halo. A focused field gets a lapis underline and a gold glow.
        tone: Gently archaic but clear, such as Good morrow, Mara, Take heed and The register of works.

    style145:
        number: 145
        run: 30
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Roman inscription
        idea: The dashboard is a marble temple front, with the brand carved in a pediment, the four totals on fluted columns and each project cut into an inscribed tablet with dovetail handles.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/145.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            marble: #f4f2ec, the page, with faint grey veining from a noise texture
            vein: #dedad0, veins and the column dividing the chart weeks
            tablet: #ebe7dd, tablets, slabs, the architrave and fields
            cutStone: #2f2b25, carved lettering and body text
            slate: #57514a, secondary text, nav links and last week bars
            porphyry: #7a2626, the primary button, overdue, Behind and focus
            bronze: #73541a, progress fills, this week bars, roman numerals, the avatar medal and At risk
            laurel: #3d5a33, the wreath and On track
            groove: #c9c2b2, frames, mouldings and grooves, never text
        type:
            Inscriptional capitals in Optima, Optima Nova, Candara, Trajan
            Pro, Palatino Linotype, serif, always uppercase and tracked 0.14
            to 0.42em, carved with a white highlight below and a faint dark
            line above. Text uses Palatino Linotype, Book Antiqua, Palatino,
            Georgia, serif. The pediment brand is 30px tracked 0.42em, the
            greeting 56px, column figures 54px, tablet titles 17px, labels 12
            to 14px, body 16px at 1.55, subtitles italic.
        layout:
            Centred on one axis up to 1240px. A shallow triangular pediment
            spans the top with BRIGHTWORK carved in it. Under it an
            architrave band carries the caps nav split by interpuncts with a
            red underline on Home, then an inset search, the porphyry New
            project button, a square bell and a bronze medal avatar with the
            name. The greeting is centred, a laurel wreath over SALVE, MARA,
            the date in spaced caps and a tabula ansata plaque with 4 TASKS
            ARE OVERDUE in porphyry. A colonnade of four fluted columns, each
            with a capital with round volutes, a white plaque holding the
            figure and its roman numeral, the label below and a base with a
            cast shadow. Projects are six tablets in three columns, each with
            dovetail handles at both sides, a double inner frame, the category
            above the carved title, a carved groove progress bar with a bronze
            fill, three facts and the status under a rule. Below, two framed
            slabs, the chart with bars inset like carving and the weeks split
            by a stone column, and Acta diurna, the activity log with caps
            names and caps times. On phones the columns go two by two and the
            tablets stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between columns, 28 by 60px between tablets to leave room for handles, 48px between bands.
        density: Sparse and monumental.
        corners: Square stone. Tablets have dovetail handles on both sides and capitals have round volutes.
        borders: Mouldings as inner frames, a 1px groove line, an 8px gap and another groove. Double rules under the architrave.
        shadows: Inset shadows for carved text, grooves and fields, and a soft cast shadow under column bases.
        icons:
            Plain line icons for tools. Status uses Roman interpuncts, a round
            dot for On track, a triangle for At risk and a square for Behind,
            beside the spaced caps word.
        focus: A 2px porphyry outline offset 3px.
        tone: Inscriptional and brief, such as Salve, Mara and Acta diurna, with plain English for the facts.

    style146:
        number: 146
        run: 30
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Greek classical
        idea: The dashboard is painted round a black-figure vase, in stacked registers shaped like its silhouette, framed by Greek key bands, with the four totals in terracotta tondo medallions.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/146.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            clay: #f6e7d4, the page between registers
            lightClay: #fbf3e8, register grounds, cards and fields
            slip: #d27a48, terracotta fills, key band grounds, medallion rings, the primary button and last week bars
            deepTerracotta: #8e3b14, ivy marks and focus
            blackGlaze: #1c1612, text, key lines, amphora fills, the top bar, frieze heads and this week bars
            umber: #5c4636, dates, meta and captions
            miltos: #8a2b1a, overdue and Behind
            olive: #3f5320, On track
            ochre: #7a5200, At risk
            addedWhite: #fffaf2, text on black glaze
        type:
            Baskerville, Baskerville Old Face, Libre Baskerville, Hoefler Text,
            Garamond, serif for the greeting, figures, titles and body.
            Labels use Gill Sans, Gill Sans MT, Seravek, Trebuchet MS,
            sans-serif in caps tracked 0.08 to 0.2em. Greeting 46px, tondo
            figures 50px, register titles 28px, project names 19px on black,
            labels 13 to 15px, body 15 to 16px at 1.55.
        layout:
            Registers stacked down the centre with widths that trace a vase,
            a narrow neck for the header at 820px, a shoulder at 1100px for
            the greeting and totals, the widest belly at 1240px for projects,
            a hip at 1040px for chart and activity and a narrow foot at 640px.
            The neck is a black bar with the brand and a small amphora mark,
            a pill search, a terracotta pill button, a ring bell and the user,
            then a Greek key band, the pill nav with a black current pill and
            a row of black tongues. The shoulder opens with a dotted band, a
            centred greeting, the date in spaced caps and a red pill naming 4
            overdue tasks, then four round tondi, terracotta discs with black
            rings and a clay centre holding the figure, with Overdue inverted
            to a black centre. The belly is a six panel frieze split by black
            lines, each panel with a black head holding category and name, an
            amphora that fills with black glaze to its percent, the percent,
            tasks and due date, and the status. The hip pairs the chart,
            terracotta then black round tipped bars, with the activity list
            led by ivy leaves. Key bands close each register. On phones the
            frieze goes two across and tondi two by two.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24 to 32px register padding, 20px between registers, 24px between tondi.
        density: Medium. Each register holds one kind of content.
        corners: Square registers and panels. Round tondi, pill buttons, pill fields, pill nav and round tipped bars.
        borders: 3px black lines between frieze panels, 24px Greek key bands with black edges, dotted and tongue bands as lighter dividers.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            Black-figure silhouettes. An amphora shows progress and ivy leaves
            mark activity. Status uses a filled diamond for On track, an
            outlined triangle with a mark for At risk and a hollow square for
            Behind, beside the caps word.
        focus: A 2px deep terracotta outline offset 3px, terracotta on the black bar.
        tone: Plain and calm, with one painterly aside per register such as Each vessel fills with black glaze.

    style147:
        number: 147
        run: 30
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Moroccan tiles
        idea: The dashboard is a tiled courtyard, with white plaster walls, zellige star patterns as borders and dados, the totals set in horseshoe-arched niches and progress filled with glazed tile colours.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/147.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            plaster: #fbf7ef, the page and arch interiors
            sand: #f2e8d6, niches, panel heads and totals
            cobalt: #1f4e8c, the brand, frames, the current tab, this week tiles and the outer focus ring
            emerald: #14654a, the primary button, last week tiles and On track
            saffron: #d9a227, tile centres, heading stars and the inner focus line, never text
            terracotta: #a84a22, the overdue banner, overdue figures and Behind
            amberGlaze: #7a5300, At risk
            ink: #1f2a36, text
            muted: #4f5b66, dates, labels and meta
            grout: #d9ccb4, hairlines and field borders
        type:
            Headings and figures use Hoefler Text, Iowan Old Style,
            Constantia, Cambria, Georgia, serif. Everything else uses
            Seravek, Avenir Next, Avenir, Segoe UI, Noto Sans, sans-serif.
            Greeting 40px in cobalt, niche figures 58px, panel titles 22px
            semibold, row titles 17px semibold, body 16px at 1.5, column
            labels 13px caps.
        layout:
            A 20px zellige dado of cobalt eight point stars with saffron
            centres runs across the top over a cobalt line. The header has
            the star brand, tabs with round arched tops where Home is solid
            cobalt, and on the right an arch topped search, an emerald New
            project button, a round bell and a tile pattern avatar, all over
            a cobalt rule. The courtyard row pairs a horseshoe arch doorway
            framed in tile pattern, holding the greeting, date and a
            terracotta overdue banner, with four tall arched niches, each with
            an icon, a large figure, the label and a tile strip at its foot.
            Below, a cobalt framed table of projects with a coloured star per
            row, name with category and due date, a tile coloured progress bar
            with percent, task count and status, beside the chart panel whose
            bars have pointed tile filled tops, green tiles last week and blue
            this week, plus two totals. Activity spans the width in three
            columns with arch topped initials. A wide tile band closes the
            page. On phones the arch goes above the niches, the niches go two
            by two and table rows become stacked cards.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 32px gutters, 16px between niches, 14 to 16px cell padding.
        density: Medium. A full table beside a calm arched greeting.
        corners: Arched. Niches, tabs, buttons, fields and initials have round tops and 4px bottoms, the greeting is a full horseshoe arch and panels are 6px.
        borders: 2px cobalt frames, zellige bands as dado, footer and style sheet border, dashed grout lines between feed items.
        shadows: None, except a 4px inner shade along the bottom of the primary button like a glazed tile edge.
        icons:
            Eight point stars as markers and the brand, line icons in cobalt
            and emerald. Status uses an eight point star for On track, a
            triangle with a bar for At risk and a hexagon with a dash for
            Behind, beside the word.
        focus: A 3px saffron outline offset 2px inside a 5px cobalt ring.
        tone: Warm and plain, such as Good morning and Green tiles last week.

    style148:
        number: 148
        run: 30
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Papel picado
        idea: The dashboard hangs from strings of cut tissue paper banners, with bright paper flags carrying the totals, scalloped and pierced edges on every panel and a festive but readable layout on white.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/148.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            tissueWhite: #fffdf8, the page and the punched holes in every flag
            ink: #2a2340, text, outlines and the button shadow
            muted: #5b5470, dates, labels and meta
            pinkPaper: #ff5fa8, flags, this week bars and panel tops
            tealPaper: #24c1c1, flags, last week bars and the bell
            yellowPaper: #ffd23f, flags, the current tab and section tags
            purplePaper: #9a6bf0, garland flags only, never behind text
            orangePaper: #ff8a3d, flags and the avatar
            greenPaper: #48c774, flags
            magenta: #c2185b, the brand, the primary button and dashed focus
            okGreen: #1d7a3a, On track
            riskAmber: #8a5a00, At risk
            overdueRed: #b4232a, Behind and overdue
            string: #7a6f8f, the strings flags hang from
        type:
            Headings, labels and figures use ui-rounded, SF Pro Rounded,
            Arial Rounded MT Bold, Nunito, Varela Round, Trebuchet MS,
            sans-serif at weight 800. Body uses Trebuchet MS, Segoe UI,
            Ubuntu, Verdana, sans-serif. Greeting 48px with the name in
            magenta, flag figures 52px, section titles 28px, row titles 19px,
            body 16px at 1.5, status pills 15px.
        layout:
            A garland of sixteen small flags in all six paper colours hangs
            along the top from a curved string, each pierced with a polka dot
            of holes, a zigzag bottom and a diamond or round cut out, tilted
            slightly. The header bar overlaps it with a magenta zigzag
            bottomed brand flag, pill nav with a yellow current pill, a pill
            search, a magenta pill button with a hard ink shadow, a teal round
            bell and an orange avatar. The hero pairs a big greeting, date and
            an outlined red notice naming 4 overdue tasks with four large
            flags hung on a curved string, each a pierced coloured flag with a
            white arched card holding the figure and label, alternately
            tilted. Projects sit in one outlined panel topped by a pierced
            teal strip, each row with a small pierced flag showing the
            percent, the name with category and due date, a striped paper
            progress bar with tasks and percent, and an outlined status pill.
            Chart and activity sit side by side in panels topped with yellow
            and orange strips, the chart with scalloped topped bars pierced by
            diamonds, teal last week and pink this week. Each section title
            has three tiny flags before it. On phones the garland shortens,
            totals go two by two and rows stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 32px gutters, 48px between sections, 14 by 20px rows.
        density: Airy and festive.
        corners: Pills for buttons, tabs, fields and status, 18px panels, zigzag bottoms on flags and round arched tops on cards inside them.
        borders: 2px ink outlines on panels, buttons and fields, dotted dividers between rows and a pierced coloured strip at the top of each panel.
        shadows: Only a hard 4px ink shadow under the primary button.
        icons:
            Bold rounded line icons. Status uses a ticked circle for On track,
            a triangle with an exclamation for At risk and a rounded square
            with a down arrow for Behind, inside outlined pills with the word.
        focus: A 3px dashed magenta outline offset 3px.
        tone: Cheerful and short, such as Good morning, Mara! and Last week 59.

    style149:
        number: 149
        run: 31
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Block print
        idea: The dashboard is a hand block printed cloth, with an indigo border of repeated motifs, madder red stripes between printed panels, stamped figures with slightly rough edges and progress counted in printed dots.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/149.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            cotton: #f4eee2, the printed field, fields and swatch cards
            unbleached: #e8dcc6, the page behind the cloth
            indigo: #1f3a6b, the border ground, headings, figures, progress dots, the current tab and last week hatching
            indigoWash: #dfe5ef, alternate project rows and the bell
            madder: #9e2f24, stripes, the primary button, overdue, Behind, this week bars and focus
            madderWash: #f3ddd4, the overdue notice
            turmeric: #c99a2e, small motif accents, never text
            ink: #1d1d26, body text
            muted: #544f5f, meta and labels
            leafGreen: #35582a, On track
            ochre: #7a5300, At risk
        type:
            Labels, headings and figures use Futura, Futura PT, Century
            Gothic, URW Gothic, Avenir Next, sans-serif. Text uses Charter,
            Bitstream Charter, Sitka Text, Cambria, Noto Serif, Georgia,
            serif. Greeting 44px with the name in italic indigo, stamped
            figures 60px bold, panel titles 22px tracked 0.06em, row titles
            18px semibold serif, categories 13px caps, body 15 to 16px at
            1.55.
        layout:
            The whole dashboard is one cloth up to 1280px. A 36px border of
            cotton butas and dots on indigo wraps a cotton field printed with
            faint indigo and madder six petal flowers over a fine weave. The
            header has a buta mark with the brand, plain nav with a solid
            indigo current item, a square search, a madder button with a 2px
            indigo offset, a square bell and a round avatar, then a madder
            stripe of cotton diamonds runs edge to edge. The greeting sits
            left with the date in spaced sans, and a madder wash notice with a
            thick left edge names 4 overdue tasks on the right. The four
            totals are one ruled band split by dashed lines, each a large
            stamped figure beside its label. Below, the field splits into two
            panels by a vertical madder stripe, projects on the left as rows
            with alternating indigo wash, the category, title, status and a
            row of ten printed dots where each filled dot is a tenth of the
            work, then percent, tasks and due date. On the right the chart,
            hatched indigo bars last week and solid madder this week with a
            rough edge, two outlined totals, a stripe, then activity led by
            small madder flower stamps. On phones the stripe turns
            horizontal, totals go two by two and rows stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. A 36px printed border, 28 to 32px inside the field, 14px row padding.
        density: Medium. Panels sit edge to edge like blocks on one cloth, split by stripes rather than gaps.
        corners: Square, only dots and the avatar are round.
        borders: A wide repeat border of indigo butas, 12px madder stripes with cotton diamonds between panels, dashed indigo lines between figures.
        shadows: None, except a 2px indigo offset under the primary button like a misaligned second block.
        icons:
            Stamped shapes passed through a slight roughening filter. Status
            uses a six petal flower for On track, a triangle for At risk and a
            square with an inner square for Behind, beside the word.
        focus: A 3px madder outline offset 2 to 3px.
        tone: Quiet workshop voice, such as one printed dot for every tenth of the work.

    style150:
        number: 150
        run: 31
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Folk rosemaling
        idea: The dashboard is a painted farmhouse cupboard, with the totals on drawer fronts, each project on a small painted door, and blue frames carrying red and ochre scrolls and flowers in their corners.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/150.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            wallCream: #f3ead8, the page behind the cupboard
            panelCream: #fcf6ea, painted panels and fields
            cupboardBlue: #234a78, the cupboard frame, headings, figures, the current tab, last week bars and the outer focus ring
            skyWash: #dde7f1, progress tracks, the bell and list rows
            folkRed: #a3302a, flowers, the brand, the primary button, the overdue banner, Behind and this week bars
            ochre: #c8892a, inner frame lines, flower centres and the focus outline, never text
            leafGreen: #3c6a37, leaves, progress fills and On track
            drawerWood: #e7d6b6, drawer fronts
            ink: #2a2522, text
            muted: #5e544a, dates and meta
            amber: #7d5100, At risk
        type:
            Brand, greeting and style title use Segoe Script, Apple Chancery,
            Brush Script MT, URW Chancery L, cursive at 34 to 46px. Headings,
            figures, nav and buttons use Bookman Old Style, URW Bookman,
            Cambria, Georgia, serif in bold. Body uses Candara, Segoe UI, Noto
            Sans, Calibri, sans-serif. Drawer figures 54px, panel titles 24px
            centred, door titles 17px, body 15 to 16px at 1.55.
        layout:
            One painted cupboard up to 1240px, a 16px blue frame with round
            top corners and a darker ledge below. The header is a cream crest
            with a wide arched top and a red inner line, holding a tulip and
            the script brand, rounded nav with a blue current pill, a round
            search, a red pill button with a cream inner line, a sky bell and
            a red avatar ringed in ochre. A cream greeting panel with ochre
            inner line and painted C scrolls with tulips in both top corners
            centres the script greeting, date and a red pill naming 4 overdue
            tasks. Four drawer fronts in wood colour each have a red knob on
            the top edge, a large figure, the label and a small red flower.
            Below, a wide panel with corner scrolls holds six painted doors in
            three columns, white with arched tops and blue and red inner
            lines, each with a tulip, the name, category and due date, a green
            vine progress bar ending in a red leaf, the percent, task count
            and status. A narrow column holds the chart, round blue then red
            bars with ochre flame marks on a green ground line, and the
            activity list led by small red and blue leaves. On phones
            everything stacks to one column.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px between all panels like boards in one frame, 24 to 28px inside panels.
        density: Medium. Everything sits inside one painted cupboard.
        corners: Soft. 10px panels, wide arched tops on the crest and doors, pills for buttons and banners.
        borders: A 16px blue cupboard frame, ochre inner lines inset 5px in every panel, red inner lines on doors, dotted lines between feed items.
        shadows: Only a solid darker blue ledge under the cupboard.
        icons:
            Painted folk shapes, C scrolls with tulips in panel corners and
            small flowers on drawers. Status uses a heart for On track, a
            diamond with a mark for At risk and a down pointing triangle for
            Behind, beside the word.
        focus: A 3px ochre outline offset 2px inside a 6px blue ring.
        tone: Homely and kind, such as Six doors, one for each piece of work and What the team has been up to.

    style151:
        number: 151
        run: 31
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Mosaic
        idea: The dashboard is laid as a floor mosaic, where small stone tesserae set in pale grout form the totals, the progress of each project and one tile for every task completed in the chart.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/151.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            grout: #d8d0bf, the page, gaps between tiles and panel borders
            panel: #f7f1e4, panels, fields and the chart ground
            creamTile: #efe6d2, background tesserae and empty progress tiles
            sandTile: #e3d3b0, scattered background tesserae and the current tab
            slate: #36506a, progress tiles, last week tiles, one figure and the focus outline
            terracotta: #a4452a, the primary button and this week tiles
            ochre: #b98326, border waves and the outer focus halo, never text
            olive: #55662e, one figure and On track
            basalt: #2a2723, text, outlines and one figure
            muted: #58524a, meta and day labels
            oxideRed: #8c2a1e, overdue and Behind
            amber: #7a5200, At risk
        type:
            Headings use Cochin, Constantia, Sitka Heading, Iowan Old Style,
            Georgia, serif in bold, panel titles in small caps. Text uses
            system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Noto Sans, sans-serif. Greeting 44px,
            panel titles 24px, row titles 17px bold, body 16px at 1.5, meta 13
            to 14px. The totals are never set in type, they are drawn in a 5
            by 7 tessera font at 10px per tile.
        layout:
            A floor of small cream tiles in grout behind everything, up to
            1260px. Every panel is an emblema with a 2px basalt line, a 6px
            grout band and an inner basalt line. The header holds a nine tile
            brand mark, small caps brand, nav with an outlined sand current
            item, a square search, a terracotta button, a square bell and a
            round tile cluster avatar, closed by a three row tessera band of
            basalt and an ochre, cream and terracotta wave. The top row pairs
            the greeting panel, with date and an outlined red notice naming 4
            overdue tasks, with four small emblemata, each with a label, the
            figure laid in tesserae, slate, olive, oxide red or basalt on
            cream tiles, and a short note such as running now. Projects list
            name, category and due date, a bar of twenty tiles where each
            slate tile is 5 percent, percent and tasks, and the status. The
            chart lays two tiles per row and one row per task, slate last week
            and terracotta this week, with values above. Activity spans the
            width in three columns led by small rotated tiles, closed by
            another tessera band. On phones panels stack and totals go two by
            two.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between panels, 12 by 20px rows, tiles on a 10 to 12px grid with about 1.6px grout.
        density: Medium to dense. Many small tiles with calm text around them.
        corners: Nearly square. Tiles 1.2px, controls 3px, the avatar is a round tile cluster.
        borders: Emblema frames of basalt, grout and basalt, and tessera bands of basalt and ochre wave under the header and feed.
        shadows: None. Depth comes from grout and tiles each rotated a few degrees with slightly varied size and colour.
        icons:
            Simple line icons for tools and tessera shapes for markers. Status
            uses a round tile for On track, a triangular tile for At risk and
            a square tile with a hole for Behind, beside the word.
        focus: A 3px slate outline offset 2px inside a 6px ochre halo.
        tone: Plain and craft minded, such as one tile per 5% and One row of tiles per task.

    style152:
        number: 152
        run: 31
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Stained glass
        idea: The dashboard is one leaded church window, with every panel a pane of pale jewel glass, black lead cames as the gaps between them, pointed lancets for the totals and a rose window beside the greeting.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/152.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            stone: #ecebe6, the wall around the window
            lead: #1b1b1f, lead cames between panes, outlines and text
            clearGlass: #f7f5ef, neutral panes, fields and progress gaps
            rubyGlass: #f8d9d9, Behind panes, the overdue notice, the activity heading and this week bars
            sapphireGlass: #d8e3f7, the header and last week bars
            emeraldGlass: #d6eedc, On track panes and the chart heading
            amberGlass: #f8e8c2, the greeting, At risk panes and the focus halo
            amethystGlass: #e7ddf5, the projects heading and a lancet
            rubyDeep: #9b1c2c, Behind and overdue text
            sapphireDeep: #1d4c8f, the primary button, the current tab and progress segments
            emeraldDeep: #1d6a3f, On track
            amberDeep: #7a5000, At risk
            amethystDeep: #5b3a8c, a spare accent for links
            muted: #4a4a52, meta and labels
        type:
            Headings and figures use Lucida Bright, Lucida Serif, Cambria,
            Noto Serif, Georgia, serif in bold. Text uses Lucida Grande,
            Lucida Sans Unicode, Lucida Sans, Segoe UI, Tahoma, sans-serif.
            Greeting 34px, lancet figures 48px, pane titles 22px, project
            names 17px, body 15px at 1.55.
        layout:
            One window up to 1240px with rounded 14px corners and a stone
            surround. It is a twelve column grid whose black background shows
            through 8px gaps as lead. Every pane is a pale glass tint with a
            white highlight in its top left. A sapphire header pane holds a
            small leaded lancet mark, the brand, outlined tabs with round tops
            where Home is deep sapphire, a square search, a deep sapphire
            button, a round bell and a four colour roundel avatar. An amber
            greeting pane spans five columns with a rose window of eight petal
            roundels beside the greeting, date and a ruby notice naming 4
            overdue tasks. Four lancets fill seven columns, each a pointed
            arch cap with tracery over a glass body with the figure and label.
            Projects span eight columns as a six pane grid, each pane tinted
            green, amber or red by status, with category, name, a ten segment
            leaded progress strip, percent, tasks, due date and status. The
            chart spans four columns, pointed arch bars in sapphire then ruby
            glass with a lead bar across, and two leaded week totals. Activity
            spans the width as three columns of panes with round initials. On
            phones every pane spans the full width and lancets go two by two.
        spacing: An 8px unit. The grid gap is the lead, 8px between major panes and 6px inside them, 14 to 24px padding in each pane.
        density: Medium. A twelve column window with no empty wall between panes.
        corners: Square panes softened to 3px, pointed arch tops on lancets and chart bars, round tops on tabs and swatches.
        borders: Black lead everywhere, 8px between panes, 6px under pane headings, 2 to 3px around controls and inside the chart.
        shadows: None. Each pane has a soft white highlight like light through glass.
        icons:
            Leaded shapes with a black outline. Status uses a roundel for On
            track, a triangle for At risk and a diamond with a cross for
            Behind, beside the word, with the pane tint as a second cue.
        focus: A 3px lead outline offset 2px inside a 6px amber glass halo.
        tone: Calm and plain, such as Each pane is tinted by its status.

    style153:
        number: 153
        run: 31
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Sign painter
        idea: The dashboard is a hand-painted shop front, with a green fascia in gold-leaf letters, the greeting arched across the window, the totals on painted show cards and the projects listed on a lettered directory board.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/153.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            wall: #f5efe1, the page around the shop front
            windowGlass: #fbf8f0, the window, fields and search
            fasciaGreen: #1f3d2b, the fascia, window frame, last week bars and progress stripes
            goldLeaf: #c9962e, drop shadows, pinstripes and card shadows, never small text
            paleGold: #e9c96e, gold lettering and lines on green, the greeting outline and the focus halo
            oxblood: #6e1d17, the greeting, script accents, the primary button, overdue, Behind, this week bars and focus
            signBlack: #1c1a17, block lettering, outlines and dotted leaders
            muted: #5a5246, meta and day labels
            showCard: #fffaf0, show cards and boards
            okGreen: #2d5a2a, On track
            riskAmber: #7a5100, At risk
            rule: #d8c9a8, hairlines between directory lines
        type:
            Block lettering uses Rockwell, Rockwell Nova, Roboto Slab,
            Clarendon, Superclarendon, Georgia, serif in bold caps. Script
            accents use Brush Script MT, Segoe Script, Apple Chancery, URW
            Chancery L, cursive at 19 to 30px and never carry a fact alone.
            Body uses Georgia, Times New Roman, serif. Fascia brand 44px in
            pale gold with a gold and black drop, the window greeting 58px
            caps set on an arc, show card figures 64px with a pale gold drop,
            directory names 18px caps, body 15 to 16px.
        layout:
            A shop front up to 1240px. The fascia is a green board with a
            double gold pinstripe inset, the brand in gilt letters with a
            script line under it, caps nav in cream with a pale gold
            underline on Home, a cream search, an oxblood button with a gold
            inner line and black drop, a gold ring bell and a gold avatar. The
            window below has a 12px green frame, a gold inner line and two
            faint diagonal glare streaks. GOOD MORNING, MARA is painted in
            oxblood caps with a gold shade along an arc, the date sits under
            it in script, and 4 TASKS ARE OVERDUE sits between double rules.
            Four show cards, each slightly tilted, have a script eyebrow such
            as Now showing, a large figure, a rule and the caps label, with a
            hard gold shadow. Below, a directory board lists each project as
            a caps name, dotted leaders and a large percent, then the
            category in script, a pinstriped progress bar, tasks, due date and
            status. A side column holds two smaller boards, Tasks done with
            green then oxblood bars carrying gold shade and a pale gold inner
            line, and Lately, the activity with times in script. On phones
            cards go two by two and boards stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24 to 32px between cards and boards, 12px between directory lines.
        density: Medium. Big showy lettering up top and a tidy directory below.
        corners: Square cards and boards, 3 to 6px on the fascia, buttons and fields, round bell and avatar.
        borders: Gold pinstripes inset in the fascia, the window frame and every board, 2px black around show cards, dotted leaders and double rules.
        shadows: Hard offset drops only, gold under black letters and cards and black under the primary button, like painted shade lines.
        icons:
            Solid painted shapes. Status uses a ticked circle for On track, a
            triangle with an exclamation for At risk and a crossed square for
            Behind, beside the caps word.
        focus: A 3px oxblood outline offset 2 to 3px inside a 6 to 8px pale gold halo, a pale gold outline on the green fascia.
        tone: A friendly shopkeeper, such as Now showing, the full directory and news from the workshop.

    style154:
        number: 154
        run: 32
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Tattoo flash
        idea: A traditional tattoo flash sheet on warm paper, where every project is a bold outlined design with a ribbon banner, numbers sit in arched badges and swallows, stars and daggers carry the meaning.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/154.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            paper: #f3e9d2, the page behind the sheet
            sheet: #fbf5e6, panels, badges, the header and the greeting banner
            ink: #141210, all text and every heavy outline
            flashRed: #a8201a, the primary button, ribbons, this week bars, the overdue badge and Behind
            leafGreen: #2b5e33, ribbons and the On track word
            sailorBlue: #1d4470, ribbons, swallows and eye motifs
            mustard: #e3b23c, stars, meter stripes, banner tails and the focus halo, never text
            tobacco: #5a4632, notes, team names, times and the At risk word
            skin: #efc9a4, the avatar disc only
        type:
            Three stacks. Labels, numbers and titles use Rockwell, Clarendon,
            Roboto Slab, Courier New, Georgia, serif in heavy weights, mostly
            uppercase. The greeting uses Brush Script MT, Segoe Script, Snell
            Roundhand, cursive at 46px. Body uses Georgia, Times New Roman,
            serif at 17px with 1.5 line height. Badge numbers are 58px 900,
            section titles 26px caps, ribbon names 15px caps, labels 13 to
            14px caps tracked 0.06 to 0.2em.
        layout:
            A boxed header with a swallow and red outlined brand, centred
            outlined nav chips with a star on Home, then search, New project,
            a round bell with a red count and the avatar. The greeting is
            centred, a spaced caps date above a script line set inside an
            outlined banner with mustard tails and a swallow on each side,
            then an outlined box with a crossed square saying 4 tasks are
            overdue. Four badges with arched tops hold the numbers, each with
            a black caps label strip, the overdue badge filled red. Below, a
            two to one grid. The projects panel is a dotted flash sheet of
            six cards in three columns, each with a flash motif drawing such
            as a rose, ship, eye, anchor, swallow or banded heart, a red,
            green or blue ribbon with forked tails carrying the name, the team
            in italic, a striped pill meter, the facts line and a status chip.
            The side column holds the activity list with a swallow before each
            row and dashed dividers, then the chart panel with outlined bars,
            cream for last week and red for this week. Below 980px the grid
            stacks and cards drop to two columns, then one below 440px.
        spacing: A 4px base in steps of 8, 12, 16, 24 and 32. The sheet has a 24px gutter and 20px panel padding.
        density: Medium. Each design is a self-contained motif with name, team, meter, facts and status.
        corners: Small 3 to 8px radii. Badges have arched tops. Ribbons have forked tails.
        borders: Heavy ink outlines, 4px on panels and badges, 3px on cards and buttons, 2px on chips, nav and fields.
        shadows: Only a hard 3px ink offset under buttons. Panels carry a faint 12px dot stipple.
        icons:
            Flash motifs with thick ink outlines and flat fills. A filled star
            means On track, a dagger means At risk, a red box with a white
            cross means Behind and overdue, and swallows mark activity rows.
        focus: A 3px ink outline offset 3px inside a 7px mustard halo.
        tone: Warm and proud, with short caps labels and a script greeting, such as Latest work and six designs on the sheet.

    style155:
        number: 155
        run: 32
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Xerox zine
        idea: A photocopied punk zine spread, stapled down the middle, with ransom-note cut-out letters, typewritten listings and nothing but toner black on white paper.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/155.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            paperWhite: #ffffff, pages, cut-outs and fields
            toner: #0d0d0d, all text, bars, solid blocks and the primary button
            smudge: #4a4a4a, speckle and halftone texture only
            wash: #e6e6e6, grey cut-out letters and the focus fill
            desk: #c9c9c6, the surface under the zine and the tape strips
            staple: #8a8f94, staples on the fold, decorative
        type:
            Four stacks mixed like cut-outs. Headings and numbers use Impact,
            Haettenschweiler, Arial Narrow Bold, Franklin Gothic Heavy,
            sans-serif, with 64px numbers, 32px section heads and 20px
            buttons. Project names use Arial Black at 19px caps. Asides use
            Times New Roman italic at 15 to 20px. Body and labels use Courier
            New, Courier, Nimbus Mono PS, monospace at 16px with 1.45 line
            height, labels 13px bold caps. The greeting is a ransom note, each
            word on its own boxed scrap in a different stack, rotated 2 to 5
            degrees.
        layout:
            A white two page spread on a speckled grey desk with a dashed fold
            down the middle and two grey staples on it. The left page has the
            masthead, a black rotated Brightwork block and an issue note, nav
            as boxed typewriter tabs tilted alternately with Home inverted,
            then search as an underline, New project, a BELL count button and
            the name. Below come a black date strip, the ransom note greeting,
            a black splat with a bang beside the scrawled overdue line, four
            taped cut-out boxes in a two by two grid with the overdue one
            inverted, and a scene report list with black time tags floated
            right. The right page holds a numbered track listing of the six
            projects with big 01 to 06 numerals, caps names, a status box, and
            a meta line with a hatched bar and the facts, then the tally chart
            with dotted halftone bars for last week and solid bars for this
            week. Small page folios sit at the foot. Below 900px the pages
            stack and the staples hide.
        spacing: Loose 4px base, mostly 8, 12, 18 and 32. Pages have 36px margins like a folded A5 sheet.
        density: Packed and lumpy. Listings are tight, cut-outs float with uneven gaps.
        corners: Square everywhere. Scraps are rotated rather than rounded.
        borders: Solid toner lines from 2 to 4px. Dashed lines for the fold and soft dividers.
        shadows: Only the spread sits on the desk with a flat 6px grey offset. Speckle gradients fake copier noise.
        icons:
            Hand drawn feel in toner. A wobbly circled tick means On track, an
            outline triangle with a bang means At risk, a solid black box with
            an X means Behind, and a black splat with a bang marks overdue.
        focus: A 3px dashed toner outline offset 4px, with a wash fill on fields and rows.
        tone: Blunt lower case asides and shouted caps, such as scene report, track listing and deal with it today.

    style156:
        number: 156
        run: 32
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Wheatpaste poster
        idea: A street wall of pasted posters, torn and overlapping, where each part of the dashboard is its own bill in huge condensed capitals and flat ink colours.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/156.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            wall: #d9d3c8, the brick wall page
            mortar: #c7c0b3, brick joint lines only
            poster: #f7f4ec, white bills and fields
            yellow: #f3d23a, the greeting bill, At risk tags and the active nav item
            pink: #f4b3c2, the chart bill and one number bill
            red: #b0161f, the primary button, due dates, the overdue bill, Behind and this week bars
            blue: #1b3a8c, the focus outline only
            black: #111111, type, the header strip, On track tags and last week bars
            grey: #4d4a44, small notes
        type:
            Display uses Arial Narrow, Roboto Condensed, Helvetica Neue
            Condensed, Liberation Sans Narrow, Nimbus Sans Narrow, Arial,
            sans-serif in bold condensed caps. The greeting runs 56 to 128px
            at 0.82 line height, numbers 92px, section heads 54px, project
            names 26 to 40px, tags and labels 17 to 22px. Body uses Helvetica
            Neue, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif at 15 to 16px.
        layout:
            A long black strip poster across the top with a yellow wordmark,
            nav words split by slashes with Home on a yellow block, then a
            cream search, red New project, a yellow bell count and the name in
            caps. Below, a twelve column wall with no gutters where bills
            overlap by 10 to 30px and tilt half to two degrees. A huge yellow
            bill on the left says Morning, Mara with the date above and a
            black overdue band with a stop octagon. Four small number bills in
            a two by two series to its right, white, pink, red and white. A
            white gig bill lists the six projects as acts with the name huge
            on the left, the due date in red on the right, then a tag, the
            facts and ten square progress boxes. To the right a white flyer
            lists activity and ends in vertical tear-off tabs with one tab
            missing, and a pink chart bill shows flat black and red bars. Each
            bill has one torn edge cut by a clip path. Below 1000px everything
            stacks in one column.
        spacing: Bills butt together with no gutter and overlap by 10 to 30px. Inside, 22 to 30px padding.
        density: Loud and big. Few words per bill, set huge, with the facts in one small line underneath.
        corners: Square paper with torn jagged edges on one side of each bill.
        borders: None on bills. Thick 6px black rules head lists, 2px rules split rows, dashed lines mark tear-off tabs.
        shadows: None. Pasted paper lies flat with faint diagonal sheen and wrinkle lines.
        icons:
            Solid printed shapes inside caps tags. A circle on black means On
            track, a triangle on yellow means At risk, a square on red means
            Behind, and a yellow stop octagon with a bang marks overdue.
        focus: A 4px blue outline offset 3px. Inside the black header the search gets a yellow outline.
        tone: Gig bill shouting, such as Now playing, Latest, Done daily and Morning Mara.

    style157:
        number: 157
        run: 32
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: 90s rave flyer
        idea: A light acid-house flyer on white, with warped and stretched extra black caps, an arched logo, fluorescent blobs and stickers behind black type, and the projects billed as a line-up by room.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/157.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            white: #ffffff, the flyer and fields
            ink: #101010, all text, rules and the Behind chip
            acidLime: #c8ff1a, the greeting highlight, On track chips and the focus halo
            hotPink: #ff4fc4, the primary button, the logo outline and this week segments
            cyan: #3ee8ff, stickers, the main room tag and last week segments
            orange: #ff9a1f, At risk chips and the overdue sticker
            violet: #4b10b0, the focus outline only
            fog: #f1f1f4, spare quiet fill
        type:
            Display uses Arial Black, Helvetica Neue, Segoe UI Black, Verdana,
            sans-serif in 900 caps. The logo is 96px set on an SVG arc with a
            pink stroke. The greeting is 30 to 64px, stretched 1.35 tall and
            skewed minus 12 degrees on a lime highlight. Numbers are 56px
            widened 1.2. Line-up acts are 18 to 26px caps, labels 10 to 13px
            caps tracked 0.12 to 0.5em. Body uses Verdana, DejaVu Sans,
            Tahoma, sans-serif at 14 to 15px, dates use Lucida Console.
        layout:
            A ruled info line on top with pill nav links, Home inverted to
            lime on black, a pill search, a skewed pink New project pill, a
            cyan round bell count and the name. Soft fluorescent blobs sit
            behind the page. A centred flyer head reads Your crew presents in
            wide tracked caps, then the arched Brightwork logo, the warped
            greeting, a boxed date and a tilted black band with an orange
            warning triangle for the overdue line. Four round stickers in
            cyan, lime, orange with a dashed edge and pink hold the numbers,
            each rotated. Below, two columns. The line-up groups projects by
            team under coloured room tags, Main room for Engineering, Room 2
            for Design and Research, Terrace for Marketing, each act with its
            due date right, a status pill, the facts and a tiny equaliser
            meter. The right column lists Set times with times on the left
            and a Levels chart of segmented cyan and pink bars. A ruled small
            print strip closes the flyer. Below 900px the columns stack.
        spacing: An 8px base. Big 34 to 48px breaks between flyer bands, tight 10px rows in lists.
        density: A centred headline zone, then a denser two column line-up like the back of a flyer.
        corners: Fully round pills for nav, buttons, fields and chips. Stickers are circles. Lists are square.
        borders: Solid ink lines of 2 to 3px. Dashed 1px ink between rows. The overdue sticker has a dashed edge.
        shadows: None. Depth comes from soft fluorescent blobs behind content at low opacity.
        icons:
            Solid ink glyphs inside pills. A four point sparkle means On
            track, a lightning bolt means At risk, a slashed circle means
            Behind, and a warning triangle marks overdue.
        focus: A 3px violet outline offset 3px inside a 9px lime halo.
        tone: Party flyer billing, such as Your crew presents, Line-up, Set times and Levels.

    style158:
        number: 158
        run: 32
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Grunge
        idea: A 90s grunge magazine page in muted dirt tones, with doubled misregistered type, scratched paper, panels whose ghost frames slip out of line and project rows that refuse to sit straight.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/158.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            paper: #e7e2d7, the scratched page
            card: #efebe2, panels and fields
            ink: #24201b, text, rules and the primary button
            rust: #7d3a1f, ghost frames, the overdue card, Behind and accents
            olive: #4c522c, On track and the second type ghost
            slate: #3f4a55, At risk, asides and the last week line
            dust: #b8ad95, masking tape and the bang icon on ink
            stain: #a99b78, coffee ring blooms in the page, never text
        type:
            Display uses Trebuchet MS, Gill Sans, Gill Sans MT, DejaVu Sans,
            sans-serif, bold lowercase at minus 0.06em, doubled with a rust
            ghost 3px right and an olive ghost 2px left. The greeting is 48 to
            116px at 0.82 line height, numbers 64px, section heads 40px,
            project names 22px. Accents use Times New Roman italic at 0.6 of
            the line, and asides at 14 to 16px. Body, nav and labels use
            American Typewriter, Courier New, Courier, monospace at 13 to 16px
            in lowercase.
        layout:
            A masthead with a tilted lowercase brightwork logo, work in rust,
            beside lowercase typewriter nav with a thick rust underline on
            home, a tilted boxed search, a black new project button with a
            rust offset, a dashed alerts button and the name in italic serif.
            The greeting spans the width in huge lowercase with Mara. in rust
            italic stepped in beneath, the date set vertically at the right,
            and a black slanted strip with a double bang for the overdue line.
            Below, a 260px column and a fluid column. The numbers stack down
            the left in layered boxes nudged sideways by different amounts,
            the overdue one filled rust. The projects panel is a table of
            rows with a big name and italic team, task count and due date,
            a scratchy bar with a ragged clip path end and a percent, and a
            status box, with alternate rows shifted 5 to 8px. Under it, two
            panels, lately with activity on slightly rotated paper strips
            edged in ink, and done per day as a doubled line chart, dashed
            slate for last week and solid ink for this week, each with an
            offset ghost line. Every panel has a 2px rust ghost frame slipped
            7px right and 6px up. Below 960px the columns stack and the
            numbers sit two by two.
        spacing: An 8px base with uneven offsets of 5 to 18px on purpose. Columns of 260px and fluid.
        density: Medium. Big lowercase headings over dense typewriter detail.
        corners: Square. Rough edges come from clip paths on bars and slight rotations.
        borders: A 2px ink box with a 2px rust ghost frame offset behind it. 1px ink row rules.
        shadows: No blur. Hard offset rust or olive slabs behind buttons and swatches. Fractal noise and faint diagonal scratches across the page.
        icons:
            Rough outline strokes. A wobbly ring means on track, a hollow
            bevelled triangle in a dashed box means at risk, a heavy cross on
            rust means behind, and a double bang marks overdue.
        focus: A 2px ink outline offset 2px with a 4px rust slab down right and a 3px olive slab up left.
        tone: Flat, wry and lowercase, such as lately, six give or take nothing and sorted by nothing.

    style159:
        number: 159
        run: 33
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Web 2.0 beta
        idea: A 2006 web 2.0 app, with a lowercase two tone logo and its mirror reflection, an orange Beta starburst, rounded tabs attached to a white content box, and glossy gel buttons and tiles over soft sky gradients.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/159.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            sky: #e8f2fb, the page under a fade from #cfe4f7
            white: #ffffff, the content box and the active tab
            ice: #f4f9fe, zebra rows, widget fills and list rows
            line: #b9d3ea, 1px borders, decorative
            blue: #1f6fc0, links and the focus glow
            blueGel: #1a5fa8, panel heads and blue gels, with a #2a72c0 top
            deepBlue: #154f8c, the logo, headings and numbers
            green: #2a6e0c, the primary gel with a #3a8519 top, and the logo half
            lime: #8fd13f, progress gloss and this week bars, never text
            orange: #ff8a1c, the Beta burst and small badges with dark text
            rust: #b54700, the burst edge and the overdue clock
            red: #b01822, Behind and the overdue tile, with a #d23a44 top
            text: #2b3540, body copy, with muted #56636f
        type:
            The logo uses Trebuchet MS, Lucida Grande, Verdana, sans-serif in
            bold 44px at minus 0.04em, lowercase, bright in deep blue and work
            in green, mirrored below at 18 percent opacity under a fading
            mask. Headings use Trebuchet MS bold, 26px page title, 16px
            section titles, 34px stat numbers. Body uses Lucida Grande,
            Lucida Sans Unicode, Trebuchet MS, Verdana, Arial, sans-serif at
            13px with 1.5 line height, meta 11px.
        layout:
            A centred 1060px column. The header has the reflected logo with a
            rotated orange Beta starburst on its corner, and on the right a
            small avatar tile, Signed in as Mara Okafor, a pill Alerts button
            with a red count and a green gel New project. Rounded gradient
            tabs sit on top of a white content box, the current tab merging
            into it, with a pill search and Go button at the far right. Inside
            the box a welcome row says Welcome back, Mara! with the date and a
            silver Customize this page gel, then a yellow alert bar with a
            clock icon for the overdue line. Below, a main column and a 300px
            sidebar. The main column has four glossy stat tiles, the overdue
            tile red, then Your projects with an orange count badge over a
            rounded zebra table with linked names, glossy green pill progress
            bars, tasks, due dates and status pills. The sidebar has a Recent
            activity widget with a glossy blue head, coloured initial tiles
            and linked task names, and a Tasks completed widget with glossy
            blue and green bars standing on a reflection. A small centred
            footer closes the page. Below 900px the sidebar drops under and
            the table scrolls inside its frame.
        spacing: A compact 4px base, 8 to 12px inside widgets and 20 to 24px between blocks.
        density: Medium. A table plus a sidebar of boxed widgets.
        corners: Generous. 10 to 12px panels, 16px gel buttons, 10px top corners on tabs, 14px pill fields.
        borders: 1px pale blue on everything, darker 1px edges on gels.
        shadows: A soft blue 8px drop under the box. Gloss is a white top half on gels, tiles and panel heads. Reflections under the logo and the chart bars.
        icons:
            Small colourful filled icons at 14px. A green circle with a tick
            means On track, an orange triangle with a bang means At risk, a
            white octagon with a red cross on a red pill means Behind, and a
            clock marks overdue.
        focus: A 2px white ring inside a 2px blue ring with a soft blue glow.
        tone: Friendly and exclaiming, such as Welcome back, Mara!, Heads up! and Customize this page.

    style160:
        number: 160
        run: 33
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: 1998 homepage
        idea: A hand made 1998 personal homepage, with a tiled star background, centred bevelled tables, grey outset buttons, hazard striped under construction bars and the weekly numbers on green odometer hit counters.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/160.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            tile: #fff8dc, the tiled page background
            star: #c9dcff, tile stars with pink #f2d0e6, never text
            cell: #ffffff, table cells
            cream: #ffffe0, odd rows, list rows and system labels
            black: #000000, body text and counter cases
            linkBlue: #0000ee, links, with visited #551a8b
            navy: #000080, table heads and the logo
            teal: #008080, the greeting, column heads and last week bars
            magenta: #c000c0, this week bars
            maroon: #800000, the overdue alert, Behind and the tagline
            green: #006400, On track, with At risk in #8a4b00
            hazard: #ffd700, construction stripes with black and the note
            silver: #c0c0c0, buttons and the logo shadow
        type:
            The logo uses Times New Roman, Times, Liberation Serif, serif in
            bold italic 52px with a 3px silver drop, framed by tildes. The
            greeting uses Comic Sans MS, Comic Neue, Chalkboard SE, Trebuchet
            MS, sans-serif in bold 32px teal. Table heads, buttons and labels
            use Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif at 13 to 15px. Body uses Times New
            Roman at 15 to 16px with 1.35 line height. Counters use Courier
            New bold 22px.
        layout:
            One centred 800px column over a tiled star pattern. A black and
            yellow hazard stripe tops the page, then the italic logo, a maroon
            italic tagline, a row of grey outset nav buttons with Home pressed
            in and marked with a pointer, and a line holding the search label
            and inset field, Search, a yellow New project, Mail (4) and Signed
            in Mara Okafor. Grooved rules split every section. The welcome is
            centred, Welcome, Mara!! with the date and a double maroon box with
            diamonds for the overdue line. A bevelled table of four cells shows
            each number as a black odometer counter with green digits, the
            overdue counter in red, under a note that counters reset on
            Sunday. A bevelled projects table has a navy title row, teal
            column heads, cream striping, linked names, a striped blue
            progress strip, tasks, due and status. Two tables sit side by side,
            What's New? with red NEW! labels on the first items, and a bar
            chart built from table cells with values over each bar. A yellow
            under construction note and a second stripe close the page. Below
            640px the side by side tables stack, counters sit two by two and
            the projects table scrolls inside.
        spacing: Table cellspacing 2px and cellpadding 6 to 8px. Sections split by grooved rules with 16px around.
        density: Everything in one centred column, stacked like a long homepage.
        corners: All square.
        borders: 3px outset table frames, 1px inset cells, 3px outset buttons that turn inset when current, a double 3px box for the alert.
        shadows: None except the flat silver shadow on the logo. Bevels give depth.
        icons:
            Tiny solid glyphs. A tick means On track, a triangle with a bang
            means At risk, a cross means Behind, and a diamond with a bang
            marks overdue. Red NEW! labels flag fresh activity.
        focus: A 2px dotted black outline offset 2px.
        tone: Proud and excited with double exclamation marks, such as Welcome, Mara!!, What's New? and always under construction.

    style161:
        number: 161
        run: 33
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: PDA LCD
        idea: A late 90s handheld organiser in a grey plastic case, with silkscreened app buttons beside a greenish monochrome LCD, inverted title bars, small round ended stylus buttons, pixel glyphs and dotted record lists.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/161.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            desk: #e9e8e3, the page
            case: #b4b8b0, the device body, with light #d3d6cf
            caseDark: #6e726b, seams and button edges
            silk: #2e312c, silkscreen labels and icons on the case
            bezel: #4a4f47, the recess around the screen
            lcd: #c4d0a8, the screen and text on inverted bars
            lcdShade: #b3c095, the inner screen shadow and the focused field
            pixel: #1d2616, all LCD text, bars and inverted rows
            pixelSoft: #3a4630, times and secondary LCD text
        type:
            The LCD uses Lucida Console, Monaco, DejaVu Sans Mono, Courier New,
            monospace with font smoothing off, bold 20px greeting, bold 14px
            pane titles, bold 28px numbers at minus 0.04em, 14px body and 12
            to 13px records and memo. The case uses Helvetica Neue, Arial,
            sans-serif in bold 10 to 12px caps tracked 0.06 to 0.24em.
        layout:
            The whole dashboard lives inside one landscape organiser. The case
            has a printed model name and a power LED on top, a column of six
            lozenge silkscreen buttons with line icons down the left for the
            nav, Home filled dark, and a dark bezel framing the LCD. A stylus
            rests against the right edge. On the screen a black title bar
            carries a Home tab, the name and the date, then a command row with
            Find and an underline field, an inverted New project stylus button,
            a bell count button and User Mara Okafor. The greeting reads Hello,
            Mara. with the date and an inverted Alarm line for the overdue
            tasks. A ruled split makes two panes. The left pane has a four cell
            boxed summary, the overdue cell inverted, then six project records
            with a checkbox, bold name, a code like OK on track, and a line
            with the team, a ten cell segment meter and the facts, the second
            record shown selected in inverse. The right pane has the activity
            memo with short times on the right and a pixel bar graph, dithered
            for last week and solid for this week. Five round hardware buttons
            and an up and down rocker sit under the screen with printed
            labels. Below 980px the panes stack. Below 680px the silkscreen
            buttons move under the screen in a three column grid.
        spacing: A tight 2px grid on the LCD with 5px record padding. The case uses 12 to 22px margins.
        density: Dense like a small pixel screen scaled up. Two panes split by a 1px line.
        corners: The case is 28px on top and 44px at the bottom. Screen 3px. Stylus buttons 8px. Silkscreen buttons are lozenges.
        borders: 1px pixel lines and dotted 1px record separators, 2px under pane titles.
        shadows: Moulded plastic only, a soft case drop, an inset bezel and raised round buttons. None on the LCD.
        icons:
            Hard edged pixel glyphs drawn with crisp edges. A round dot with
            OK means on track, a notched triangle with RISK means at risk, a
            crossed square with LATE means behind, and a bell marks the
            overdue alarm. Line icons sit on the case.
        focus: A 2px pixel outline offset 2px, then a ring of LCD green and a second 2px pixel ring.
        tone: Terse device labels, such as Find, Alarm, Memo, 6 records and yday.

    style162:
        number: 162
        run: 33
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Handheld game LCD
        idea: A grey handheld game console held sideways, whose four shade pea green screen draws the dashboard as a role playing game, with a menu window, a stats sheet, a dialog box greeting, projects as a party with health bars and the chart built from one block per task.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/162.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            shade0: #d0e09a, screen paper and text on dark bars
            shade1: #a8c060, selection, highlighted party rows and the focus fill
            shade2: #4f7a32, inner window lines and last week blocks, never text
            shade3: #173d17, all screen text, borders, bars and this week blocks
            shell: #cfcdc6, device plastic, with highlight #e4e2dc and edge #9c9a93
            frame: #5d6070, the screen surround
            keys: #3b3d4a, the D-pad and the round A and B buttons
            print: #2f3140, labels printed on the shell
            room: #efeee9, the page behind the device
        type:
            The screen uses Lucida Console, DejaVu Sans Mono, Monaco, Courier
            New, monospace in bold caps at 0.04em with smoothing off, 18px
            dialog, 14px project names, 13px body, 11 to 12px details and 16px
            stat values. Shell printing uses Futura, Century Gothic, Trebuchet
            MS, Arial, sans-serif, italic 900 for the Brightwork name and bold
            10 to 13px tracked caps for button labels.
        layout:
            A wide grey shell with a big rounded swoop at the bottom left
            holds a D-pad with Select and Start pills on the left, the screen
            in the middle and tilted round B and A buttons over a speaker
            grille on the right. The dark frame above the screen carries a
            striped label line and a red battery dot, and Brightwork pocket is
            printed under it. On the screen a dark top bar holds Find with a
            field, an A badge New project button and a MSG count. Below, three
            pixel windows across. The left has a MENU window with a triangle
            cursor on Home and Player Mara Okafor, then a STATS window with
            dotted leaders to the four values, overdue inverted. The middle
            has a dialog box with the greeting, the date and an hourglass
            overdue line, with a blinking style down arrow, then a PARTY
            window of six bordered member cards with name, team and due date,
            a status sprite and word, and a health bar with tasks and percent,
            the at risk and behind members highlighted. The right has a LOG
            window with triangle bullets and a TASKS CLEARED window where each
            day is a stack of blocks, one block per task. Below 1120px the
            right windows drop under, and below 860px the screen goes to the
            top with the controls in a row underneath.
        spacing: Pixel steps of 2, 4, 6 and 10px on the screen. Windows sit 10px apart.
        density: Busy like a game menu. Three windows across, collapsing to one column.
        corners: Windows 4px. The shell is 36px with a 90px bottom left swoop. The frame has a 40px bottom right curve.
        borders: Each window has a 3px shade3 line, a 2px paper gap and a 2px shade2 inner line. Member cards have a 2px shade3 line.
        shadows: None on screen. The shell has moulded highlights and keys stand on a 4px solid under edge.
        icons:
            Eight by eight pixel sprites. A heart means On track, a warning
            triangle means At risk, a crossed box means Behind, an hourglass
            marks overdue, and a solid triangle cursor marks the current item.
        focus: A 3px shade3 outline offset 2px with a shade1 fill.
        tone: Game speak in caps, such as Player, Party, Stats, Log and Tasks cleared.

    style163:
        number: 163
        run: 33
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Calculator LCD
        idea: A beige solar desk calculator with a printing tape, where the weekly numbers glow in seven segment digits over ghost segments, the nav is a pad of chunky keys with an orange equals key for New project, and the projects print out on paper tape.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/163.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            desk: #f1efe9, the page
            body: #e6e1d3, calculator plastic, with edge #c9c3b2
            lcd: #cdd3c0, displays and the search field
            segment: #1f231c, lit digits and LCD text
            ghost: #bcc3ad, unlit segments, never meaning
            bezel: #3a3833, display frames, with labels in #ece8dc
            solar: #3b2e33, the solar cell strip
            key: #f4f2ec, light keys, with edge #a9a493
            darkKey: #4a4843, function keys and the pressed current page key
            orange: #e8823a, the equals key and the focus halo, with dark text #2a1606
            tape: #fdfcf7, printed tape and list rows
            redInk: #a3241c, Behind and its percent, printed like a negative number
            ink: #26241f, tape text and key legends, with muted #55524a
        type:
            Digits are inline SVG seven segment polygons with slanted ends,
            skewed 6 degrees, with all unlit segments drawn in ghost, 72px in
            the main display and 30px in the readouts. LCD and tape text use
            OCR A Std, OCR A Extended, Courier New, Courier, monospace at 13
            to 15px. Key legends and labels use Helvetica Neue, Helvetica,
            Arial, sans-serif in bold 13px caps, with 10 to 11px sub legends
            and annunciators.
        layout:
            A desk with the calculator on the left and the tape on the right.
            The calculator has the brand and a small model line, a five cell
            solar strip, then a dark bezel around the main LCD. The LCD shows
            annunciators M, WK and an inverted E lit with MEM, GT and percent
            unlit, the greeting and date in small mono text, a big seven
            segment 4 with TASKS OVERDUE beside it, and an E box with the
            overdue sentence. Four small bezelled readouts show the four
            numbers in seven segment digits with labels under them. A Find
            field styled as an LCD and the user line follow. The keypad is a
            four column grid of chunky keys, six light keys for the nav with
            short sub legends and Home pressed down in dark, dark Alerts with
            4 new, dark Clear, a wide orange = New project key and a wide
            Print tape key. On the right a printed tape with a zigzag torn
            foot lists the projects with percent on the right, a facts line
            and status, closes with a Tasks done 78 of 170 total under a heavy
            rule, then lists activity with short times. Under the tape a
            bezelled LCD bar graph shows 14 columns of 17 segments each, lit
            up to the day's count, with day letters. Below 960px the tape goes
            under the calculator and below 480px the readouts sit two by two.
        spacing: 8 to 10px between keys, 14px between calculator zones and 40px between the calculator and the tape.
        density: A compact device on the left and a long airy tape on the right.
        corners: Keys 8px on top and 12px at the bottom. The body is 18 to 26px. LCD 3px. The tape has a zigzag torn foot.
        borders: Keys have a 1px edge. Displays sit in a dark bezel. Tape rows are dotted and the total gets a 2px rule.
        shadows: Keys stand on a 4px solid under edge and the current key is pressed down to 1px. The body has a soft drop.
        icons:
            A ringed dot means On track, an outline triangle with a bang means
            At risk, a minus box in red ink means Behind, and an E error box
            marks overdue, like a calculator error.
        focus: A 3px ink outline offset 2px inside a 6px orange halo.
        tone: Machine labels and arithmetic, such as Print tape, Clear, = New project and the sigma totals for each week.

    style164:
        number: 164
        run: 34
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Cash register
        idea: The dashboard is a point-of-sale terminal, with green LCD windows ringing up the totals, projects as item lines on the sale screen, the menu as a block of chunky department keys and activity printed on a journal tape.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/164.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            counter: #e9e4d8, the page behind the terminal
            case: #f8f5ee, the terminal body and the style sheet
            caseEdge: #a89f8c, the case border, never text
            lcd: #cbd8bb, every display window and the search field
            lcdInk: #1c2a12, all text and bars on the LCD
            keyCream: #fffdf6, department keys and secondary keys
            keyNavy: #1f3a5f, the New project key and the sale screen title bar
            ink: #23201b, text on paper and on cream keys
            muted: #5b5446, PLU codes, departments and small labels
            green: #24602f, the On track code with a circle check
            amber: #8a4f00, the At risk code with a triangle
            voidRed: #9e2121, the Behind code with a crossed square and the notice count
            focusBlue: #1f5fd1, the focus outline only
        type:
            Two stacks. LCD and receipt text use Consolas, DejaVu Sans Mono,
            Menlo, Liberation Mono, monospace in bold caps. Keys use Arial
            Black, Helvetica Neue, Arial in 900 weight caps. Totals are 44px
            mono, the LCD greeting 26px mono caps, key labels 13 to 20px,
            item lines and tape 13 to 14px mono, and small labels 11px mono
            caps tracked 0.12em. The clerk name is 15px system-ui.
        layout:
            One rounded cream terminal case holds everything. Across the top a
            pole display shows the brand at left, a wide LCD in the middle with
            Good morning, Mara and the date plus an octagon Overdue 4 tasks
            line, and the clerk name at right. Below are four LCD windows for
            the totals, each with a small window number. The left column is a
            white sale screen with a navy title bar and a table of item lines
            with PLU, item, department, quantity done over total, percent with
            a ticked bar, due date and a status code, ending in a subtotal row.
            The right column is the keypad, with six department keys D1 to D6
            for the nav, Home pressed down and tinted yellow, a PLU lookup LCD
            search field, Notices and clerk keys and a full-width New project
            key. Under both sits a white journal tape with a zigzag torn top
            listing activity, beside an LCD Z report bar chart of daily tasks
            closed. Below 960px the keypad drops under the sale screen and the
            tape stacks above the chart. The table scrolls sideways inside its
            screen on phones.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px inside the case and between blocks, 8px between keys.
        density: Busy and tactile like a shop counter. Many small windows, every key large enough for a thumb.
        corners: 18px on the case, 8px on keys and LCD bezels, 4px on status codes.
        borders: A 6px dark bezel round each LCD, 2px taupe key edges, dashed rules between item lines and tape entries, a 2px rule above the subtotal.
        shadows: Keys stand on a hard 4px bottom ledge and the current key is pressed down to 1px. LCDs have an inset shadow. The case has a 6px ledge and a soft drop.
        icons:
            Solid geometric marks at text size. A circle with a check for On
            track, a triangle with a bang for At risk, a square with a cross
            for Behind and an octagon with a bang for Overdue, always beside a
            caps word inside a bordered code box. Chart bars are made of
            stacked LCD segments.
        focus: A 3px focus blue outline offset 3px on keys, fields and rows.
        tone: Register shorthand in caps, such as Item lines, Subtotal, PLU lookup, Journal tape and Z report.

    style165:
        number: 165
        run: 34
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: E-ink
        idea: The dashboard reads like an open e-reader, with grey electronic paper, crisp black serif type and no colour at all, set as a two-page spread with chapter tabs and page-turn controls.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/165.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            desk: #d9d8d3, the page behind the device
            bezel: #f4f4f1, the device frame and field fills
            ePaper: #e8e7e1, the screen and the style sheet
            ink: #111111, type, rules, solid bars and every status
            softInk: #4a4a47, meta, running heads and folios
            rule: #9a9993, hairlines and borders, never text
            tint: #cfcec8, highlights, the gutter shade and meter ticks
        type:
            Text uses Charter, Bitstream Charter, Sitka Text, Cambria, Georgia,
            serif. The greeting is 40px regular, total figures 34px tabular,
            project names 21px, body 18px at 1.6 and meta 15px italic. Small
            caps style labels and the status bar use system-ui at 12 to 14px,
            section heads 13px caps tracked 0.2em between em dashes, and
            status words 13px bold caps.
        layout:
            A light rounded device frame holds a flat e-paper screen. A thin
            status bar carries the brand, a pill search field, a black New
            project button, a round bell and an initials disc with Mara Okafor.
            Below it the nav is a row of numbered chapter tabs, 1 Home to 6
            Settings, with the current one underlined in black. The body is a
            book spread split by a soft grey gutter. The left page has a
            running head, the greeting and date in italic, the overdue line
            between two thick rules, a two by two table of the four totals and
            the six projects as numbered entries with status at right, meta in
            italic and a thin ticked meter. The right page has the chart and
            Recent highlights with grey marker highlights on task names. Each
            page ends in a folio number. A page-turn bar at the bottom shows
            previous Settings, Home 1 of 6 with six dots, and next Projects.
            Below 900px the spread becomes one page and the search wraps under
            the brand.
        spacing: An 8px unit. Book margins of 40 to 56px, 14px between entries, 32px before section heads.
        density: Calm and bookish, with long lines of prose and one column per page.
        corners: Square pages. Only the 22px device frame, the search pill, avatar and bell are round.
        borders: 1px ink under the status bar and above the page-turn bar, 2px ink rules round the overdue line, grey hairlines between entries, dotted rules between highlights.
        shadows: None. A soft grey gradient down the gutter is the only depth.
        icons:
            Black only. A filled circle for On track, a hollow triangle for At
            risk, a filled square for Behind and a crossed box for Overdue,
            each beside its word. In the chart last week is diagonally hatched
            and this week is solid black.
        focus: A 3px ink outline offset 3px with a paper gap and a second 2px ink ring outside.
        tone: A book's voice, such as Chapter one, Recent highlights and Home 1 of 6.

    style166:
        number: 166
        run: 34
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Punch card
        idea: Every panel is an 80-column punch card on manila stock, and the data is literally punched, so summary digits, finished tasks and daily counts appear as dark rectangular holes beside printed column numbers.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/166.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            desk: #e4e9ef, the page behind the deck
            manilaStock: #f3e7c6, every card
            paleStock: #f7eedb, alternate cards, status boxes and rows
            printBrown: #6a4a22, printed labels, digits and field lines
            rule: #b49a6a, unpunched slots and hairlines, never text
            typedInk: #1d1a14, interpreted text and the primary button
            hole: #2b3440, punched holes as data
            tabBlue: #cfdcea, deck divider tabs
            green: #1f5c34, the On track ring
            amber: #85480a, the At risk triangle
            red: #8f1f1f, the Behind oblong and the Overdue diamond
            focus: #1b4fae, the focus outline
        type:
            Typed text uses Courier New, Nimbus Mono PS, Courier, monospace.
            Printed labels use Arial Narrow, Helvetica Neue Condensed, Roboto
            Condensed, Liberation Sans Narrow, Arial in bold caps. Total
            figures are 48px bold mono, the greeting 30px bold caps, card
            titles 17px bold caps, body 14 to 15px, labels 11px narrow caps
            tracked 0.08em and printed digits 9px narrow.
        layout:
            Every block is a card with its top-left corner clipped at 45
            degrees. The header card has the spaced brand with a job card
            caption, a Keypunch search field over faint column ticks, a black
            Punch new project button, a bell and the operator name. Under it a
            row of blue deck divider tabs is the nav, with Home in manila and
            raised. The greeting card shows the greeting, date and a dashed red
            overdue box. The summary card splits into four fields by brown
            column lines, each with a column range label, the big typed figure
            and a printed 0 to 9 grid where each digit of the figure is punched
            out. Below, a wide column is the project deck, one card each, with
            sequence number, name, department and due date typed on top, a row
            of slots punched one per finished task, a status box at right and
            printed column numbers 1 to 80 along the bottom. The narrow column
            holds the chart card, 14 columns of 17 slots punched from the
            bottom, and a stack of thin activity strips with BW sequence
            numbers. Below 960px the columns stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 10px between cards, 16 to 24px between sections, a 32px left inset that clears the clipped corner.
        density: Dense and data-literal, with rows of tiny slots and printed digits and one big typed number per field.
        corners: A 22px clipped top-left corner on large cards and 14px on strips, 6px rounding elsewhere, tabs rounded 8px on top.
        borders: 2px brown field dividers, a 1px rule above the column numbers, outlined unpunched slots, 2px currentColor status boxes.
        shadows: Only a 1px brown edge under each card, like stacked stock.
        icons:
            Hole shapes beside caps words. A ring for On track, a solid
            triangle for At risk, a solid oblong for Behind and a diamond with
            a bang for Overdue.
        focus: A 3px focus blue outline offset 3px.
        tone: Data-processing jargon, such as Keypunch, Operator, Punch new project and Project deck.

    style167:
        number: 167
        run: 34
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Dot-matrix greenbar
        idea: The dashboard is one long dot-matrix printout on continuous greenbar paper, with tractor-feed margins, banded rows every three lines, a run header, fixed-width columns and charts drawn with asterisks.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/167.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            desk: #eceee9, the page and the tractor holes
            paper: #ffffff, the white bands
            greenbar: #dcefd9, every other three-line band
            margin: #f7f8f4, the tractor strips
            ribbon: #23272f, all printed text
            redRibbon: #a3231b, overdue lines and Behind
            formGreen: #2c5e33, column heads, section heads and typed rules
            perf: #9aa394, perforations, never text
            focus: #1d4fb8, the dashed focus outline
            focusFill: #fff6c9, the fill behind a focused item
        type:
            One stack, Courier New, Nimbus Mono PS, Liberation Mono, Courier,
            monospace, always bold with a 0.4px side shadow for impact weight.
            The wordmark is 26px on a 40px line, double struck and tracked
            0.14em. Summary figures are 30px on 40px. All report text is 15px
            on a 20px line in caps, 13px on phones. Perforation notes use 12px
            system-ui.
        layout:
            A single sheet with a 36px tractor strip on each side, punched with
            round holes every 40px and edged by dashed perforations. The body
            is banded green and white every 60px. It opens with a run header
            line, prepared for line, a row of equals signs, the wordmark, a
            MENU line of bracketed numbered links with Home starred and
            underlined, and a control line with a QUERY prompt field, a solid
            New project button, a bracketed NOTICES button and the user name.
            Then the greeting with the date, a red overdue line, Section 1 as
            a four-cell summary box in dashed rules, Section 2 as a fixed-width
            project table with number, name, department, done over total,
            percent, a hash progress bar, due and status, and a status code
            key. A dashed tear line with tear here leads to Section 3, a
            preformatted asterisk histogram per day with weekly totals and a
            double rule, beside Section 4, an activity log. It ends with END
            OF REPORT. The table scrolls sideways on phones and the tractor
            strips shrink to 20px.
        spacing: A 20px line grid. Everything sits on whole lines, bands are 60px and gaps are one blank line.
        density: Very dense, report style, with fixed-width columns and full caps.
        corners: None. Only the tractor holes are round.
        borders: Typed rules of equals and hyphen characters, 2px dashed lines under column heads and round the summary, dashed perforations.
        shadows: A faint 1px shadow under the paper. Type gets a 0.4px side shadow.
        icons:
            ASCII only. A lowercase o in parentheses for On track, a slash bang
            backslash wedge for At risk, an X in square brackets for Behind and
            a bang in angle brackets for Overdue, each beside its caps word.
            Asterisks draw chart bars and hashes draw progress.
        focus: A 2px dashed focus blue outline offset 2px over a pale yellow fill. The solid button keeps its dark fill and gets a solid 3px outline.
        tone: Batch-job report, such as RUN DATE, QUERY, Section 2 Project detail and END OF REPORT.

    style168:
        number: 168
        run: 34
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Fax
        idea: The dashboard arrives as a faxed cover sheet, with a transmission line across the top, a boxed To and From form, heavy black toner on slightly grainy paper, halftone bars and rubber-stamped statuses.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/168.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            tray: #e3e1da, the page behind the sheet
            thermalSheet: #f5f4ef, the paper, under a 14 percent noise grain
            toner: #141414, all text, rules, stamps and buttons
            greyToner: #4a4a46, departments and placeholders
            scanStreak: #d8d6cf, faint vertical streaks, never text
            halftone: #8a8a85, how dotted fills read at a distance
            focus: #1748b0, the focus outline and the only colour
        type:
            Three stacks. Headings and the FAX mark use Arial Black, Helvetica
            Neue, Arial at 900. Body and form values use Helvetica Neue,
            Helvetica, Arial, Liberation Sans. The header line and log columns
            use Lucida Console, Courier New, Liberation Mono. The FAX mark is
            64px, the title 30px caps, total figures 52px heavy, form values
            16px bold, body 15px, form keys 12px bold caps tracked 0.08em and
            the header line 12px mono. Text has a 0.7px blur bleed.
        layout:
            One sheet tilted 0.35 degrees with grain and two faint vertical
            scan streaks. A mono transmission line runs across the top with
            the date and time, FROM BRIGHTWORK, TO MARA OKAFOR and P.01 of 01.
            The cover has a reversed black FAX block, the title Brightwork
            cover sheet and the signed-in name, over a 6px black bar. A boxed
            form follows with To, From, Date and Pages in two columns, Re
            holding the greeting and the overdue line, Route holding the nav
            as checkboxes with Home crossed, and Look up holding the search,
            New project and Notices. Then four boxed totals with the overdue
            box double framed, a black-headed project table with halftone
            progress bars and stamped statuses, and two columns with a framed
            bar chart, dotted last week and solid this week, beside an activity
            report table with number, time, activity and an OK result column.
            A mono footer closes the sheet. Below 860px the tilt is removed,
            the form becomes one column and the table scrolls sideways.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 10px cell padding, 12px between boxes, 28px above section heads.
        density: Medium-dense office form, with boxed fields and tables edge to edge.
        corners: Square everywhere. Only the On track stamp is a full pill.
        borders: 2px toner boxes, a 6px bar under the cover, a 6px double frame on the overdue figure, dotted log rules.
        shadows: One soft shadow under the sheet. Text bleeds with a 0.7px blur.
        icons:
            Rubber stamps tilted 2 degrees. A pill stamp with a ringed check
            for On track, a dashed stamp with a triangle for At risk, a solid
            black stamp with a crossed box for Behind, and a filled circle with
            a bang for Overdue.
        focus: A 3px focus blue outline offset 2px.
        tone: Office paperwork, such as Re, Route, Look up, Activity report and P.01 of 01.

    style169:
        number: 169
        run: 35
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Accounting ledger
        idea: The dashboard is a page of a green bookkeeping ledger, with ruled columns, black and red ink, projects kept as accounts with double-underlined totals, a tally of completed tasks and thumb-index tabs down the edge.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/169.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            binding: #e6e2d6, the page behind the book
            ledgerGreen: #eef5e6, the leaf
            lineGreen: #c6dcc0, horizontal rulings every 32px, never text
            columnGreen: #8fb98c, money column rules
            headGreen: #2f5a33, column heads, section heads and the On track tick
            blackInk: #1a1d1a, entries, figures and totals
            softInk: #46503f, dates, departments and notes
            redInk: #ad1f1a, the Behind account row and overdue figures
            umber: #7a4a00, At risk
            marginRed: #d77a73, the double margin rule, never text
            tabCream: #f8f4e6, thumb-index tabs
            focus: #1f4fbf, the focus ring
        type:
            Entries use Baskerville, Libre Baskerville, Baskerville Old Face,
            Book Antiqua, Palatino, Georgia with lining tabular figures.
            Labels use Gill Sans, Gill Sans MT, Seravek, Trebuchet MS,
            system-ui. Total figures are 40px regular, the greeting 30px
            italic, the book title 30px small caps tracked 0.06em in head
            green, account names 17px, body 16px at 1.5, and column heads
            11 to 13px sans caps tracked 0.1em.
        layout:
            A ledger leaf with a red double margin rule 52px in and green
            ruled lines every 32px, with six cream thumb-index tabs standing
            off its right edge as the nav, Home flush with the leaf. The top
            has the title Brightwork General ledger of projects, a Folio 31
            caption, a Find field, a black Open new project button, a bell and
            Keeper Mara Okafor, over a double green rule. An entry line gives
            the date in caps, the greeting in italic with a note, and a red
            clock Overdue 4 tasks flag. A trial balance strip shows the four
            totals right aligned in columns, each figure double underlined,
            the overdue one in red. The project accounts table has folio,
            account, department, Done, Left and Total money columns, percent,
            due date and status, with Billing migration written in red and a
            totals row single ruled above and double ruled below. Below sit a
            tally of tasks completed, one row per day drawn in tally marks of
            five with the count right aligned and weekly subtotals double
            underlined, and a day journal with time, particulars and initials.
            Below 900px the tabs move to a scrolling row above the leaf and
            the table and tally scroll sideways.
        spacing: An 8px unit on a 32px ruled line. Rows are 48px, sections 32px apart, an 80px left margin for the red double rule.
        density: Medium. Tabular and orderly, figures right aligned in narrow money columns.
        corners: Square leaf. Index tabs round 8px on their outer edge, buttons 2px.
        borders: A double rule under the title, 2px green under column heads, 1px column rules, a single rule over and a double rule under every total.
        shadows: Two stacked 2px page edges under the leaf. Tabs cast a 2px flat edge.
        icons:
            Bookkeeper marks beside words. A tick for On track, an outlined
            triangle with a bang for At risk, a red cross wrapped in brackets
            for Behind and a clock ring for Overdue. Tally marks in fives draw
            the chart.
        focus: A 2px focus blue outline offset 2px with a soft 5px blue halo.
        tone: Counting-house language, such as Trial balance, Project accounts, Day journal, Folio and Keeper.

    style170:
        number: 170
        run: 35
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Pool tiles
        idea: The dashboard is a lap pool seen from the deck, with white grouted tiles, a stone coping header, depth-marker tiles for the totals and one swimming lane per project divided by striped lane ropes.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/170.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            tileWhite: #f7fcfd, page tiles and fields
            grout: #d3e6eb, the 24px grout grid and dashed dividers
            coping: #efe9dd, the header, pool rim and lane end wall
            poolAqua: #c4ecf2, lanes, the current nav item and rows
            deepAqua: #9fdde8, last-week chart tiles
            navyTile: #0b4a6f, brand tiles, the nav band, borders and T-lines
            ink: #0d2f44, text
            softInk: #355a6d, meta and times
            ropeRed: #c8312b, lane rope floats and the swimmer marker
            ropeBlue: #1b6fa8, lane rope floats, never text
            green: #17663a, the On track buoy
            amber: #8a4b00, the At risk flag
            red: #b02520, the Behind block and the overdue sign
            whistleYellow: #e0a100, the focus halo
        type:
            Signs use Bahnschrift, DIN Alternate, DIN Condensed, Roboto
            Condensed, Arial Narrow, Arial in 700 caps. Text uses Arial
            Rounded MT Bold, Nunito, Trebuchet MS, system-ui. Depth marker
            figures are 64px stencil, the deck sign greeting 34px caps,
            headings 18px caps tracked 0.06em, labels 13px caps, lane names
            18px bold rounded and body 15px.
        layout:
            A stone coping header spells the brand in ten navy letter tiles,
            then a pill search, a navy New project button, a bell and an avatar
            ringed in red, edged below by a navy, white and navy tile band. A
            navy nav band follows with dashed dividers and Home on aqua. The
            deck row has a white sign with Good morning, Mara, the date and a
            red bordered overdue sign, beside four depth-marker tiles, a big
            figure over a navy label strip, the overdue tile in red. The pool
            is an aqua basin with an 8px coping rim and a navy outline. Each of
            six lanes has a navy lane number block, the project name and meta,
            a black T-line with a dotted wake and a red swimmer disc at the
            percent done, and a coping end wall with the percent and status.
            Lanes are separated by 10px ropes striped red, white, blue and
            white. Below sit a white board with a bar chart whose bars are
            filled with small square tiles, deep aqua last week and navy this
            week, and a poolside log with initial tiles. On phones the end
            wall drops under each lane and the chart scrolls sideways.
        spacing: An 8px unit on a 24px tile module. 24px between deck blocks, 36px above sections, 10px lane ropes.
        density: Medium and bold. Few large signs, one lane per project.
        corners: Tile corners of 3 to 6px, 12px buttons, a pill search, a round swimmer and avatar.
        borders: 3px navy outlines on signs and boards, an 8px coping rim round the pool, striped lane ropes, a 4px navy end wall.
        shadows: None. The header edge is a stacked navy, white and navy tile band.
        icons:
            Poolside shapes beside words. A ringed buoy circle for On track, a
            pennant flag for At risk, a solid block with a white bar for
            Behind and a diamond with a bang for Overdue.
        focus: A 3px ink outline offset 2px inside a 6px whistle yellow halo.
        tone: Lifeguard-plain signage, such as The pool, Poolside log and Hours this week.

    style171:
        number: 171
        run: 35
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Tea house
        idea: The dashboard is laid out like a quiet tea room, where panels are tatami mats edged in dark cloth, a wooden beam carries the header, a bamboo pole divides the room and progress grows as bamboo segments in tea green and wood.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/171.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            shoji: #f6f2e4, the page under a 160 by 96px lattice
            lattice: #ddd1b3, lattice lines, never text
            tatami: #e9e2c3, mat panels with a fine woven texture
            straw: #d9cf9f, rules inside mats
            heriCloth: #3e4a26, the dark mat edges
            wood: #6e4a2c, the header beam and the plaque frame
            lightWood: #b08a5e, hairlines and unfilled bamboo segments
            ink: #2a2418, text
            softInk: #5a4a33, meta and dates
            teaGreen: #3f5a1f, headings, the primary button and On track
            youngBamboo: #a3b56f, last-week stalks
            bamboo: #4d6a28, this-week stalks and filled segments
            roasted: #8a4a12, At risk
            persimmon: #9b2c1e, Behind and overdue
            focus: #2f5bb0, the focus outline
        type:
            Text uses Hiragino Mincho ProN, Yu Mincho, Noto Serif CJK JP, Iowan
            Old Style, Palatino Linotype, Georgia. Labels and controls use
            Hiragino Sans, Yu Gothic, Noto Sans CJK JP, system-ui. Total
            figures are 52px regular mincho, the greeting 34px at 500 tracked
            0.04em, project names 19px, body 16px at 1.7, and headings 13px
            gothic semibold tracked 0.3em with a trailing wood hairline.
        layout:
            A dark wood beam header holds the widely tracked brand, a paper
            search field, a paper New project button, an outlined bell and the
            user name. A pale sliding-door strip below is the nav, each item
            framed by lattice lines, Home on tatami with a dark cloth underline.
            The room is three columns, a wide stack, a vertical bamboo pole
            with dark nodes, and a narrow stack. The wide stack has the
            greeting mat with the date and a wood-framed overdue plaque, four
            square half mats for the totals with cloth on the left and right,
            and the projects mat listing each project with name and meta, a
            row of ten bamboo segments filled to the percent, the percent with
            tasks done and the status. The narrow stack has vertical mats for
            the chart and the recent activity. The chart draws each day as a
            rounded bamboo stalk with dark nodes every three tasks, young green
            last week and deep green this week. Below 960px the pole turns
            horizontal and everything stacks.
        spacing: An 8px unit with generous steps of 24 and 40px. Mats have 24 to 28px padding.
        density: Sparse and quiet, with even rhythm and plenty of empty mat.
        corners: Square mats and 2px controls. Only bamboo is rounded.
        borders: 8px heri cloth on the two long sides of each mat, 1px straw rules inside, a 4px dark beam edge.
        shadows: None. Depth comes from the woven straw texture and the bamboo gradient.
        icons:
            Simple natural shapes beside words. A leaf for On track, an
            outlined triangle for At risk, a solid square for Behind and a
            clock ring for Overdue. Line icons for search and the bell.
        focus: A 2px focus blue outline offset 4px, white on the wood beam.
        tone: Calm and brief, such as This week, Fourteen days and Recent.

    style172:
        number: 172
        run: 35
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Kawaii
        idea: The dashboard is a sheet of cute stickers, where pastel blobs with little faces hold the totals, every corner is round, sparkles float behind, and each status wears its own face on its own shape.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/172.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            cream: #fff7fb, the page, chat bubbles and fields
            strawberryMilk: #ffd6e7, a card, the current tab and the overdue pill
            sky: #d4ecff, a card and a blob
            mint: #ccf3e2, a card and a blob
            lavender: #e6deff, a card, the search field and rows
            butter: #fff1b8, a card and a blob
            peach: #ffe0cc, a card and the avatar
            plum: #4a2350, text, outlines and sticker shadows
            softPlum: #6e4a72, dates and hints
            hotPink: #c2185b, the primary button and the candy stripe
            star: #ffd34d, sparkles and heading stars, never text
            green: #17694a, On track
            caramel: #8c4a00, At risk
            cherry: #b3123f, Behind and overdue
            grape: #5b3fd6, the dashed focus ring
        type:
            One rounded stack, ui-rounded, SF Pro Rounded, Hiragino Maru
            Gothic ProN, Varela Round, Nunito, Quicksand, Arial Rounded MT
            Bold, system-ui. Total figures are 52px at 800, the greeting 34px
            at 800, card names and headings 20 to 22px at 800, body 15 to 16px
            and chips 13px at 800.
        layout:
            A white pill header sticker holds a smiling star mark with the
            brand, a lavender pill search, a hot pink New project button, a
            round bell and a peach avatar. Below it the nav is a centred row of
            pill stickers, Home in pink with a sparkle. A white cloud character
            with blush and a sparkle speaks a speech bubble holding Good
            morning, Mara!, the date and a pink overdue pill. Four pastel blob
            characters, each with a different shape and mood face, hold the
            totals, the overdue blob worried with a sweat drop. Six project
            cards in three columns, each in its own pastel, show a department
            chip, a status face chip, the name, a candy-striped pill bar and
            percent, tasks and due date. Below sit a white chart sticker with
            pill-shaped bars outlined in plum, lavender last week and pink this
            week, with a star beside the top day, and a What's new panel of
            chat bubbles with initial avatars. Headings carry a small star.
            Cards go to two columns, then one, and the chart scrolls sideways
            on phones.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 18px gaps between stickers, 28 to 36px between sections.
        density: Airy and playful. Big soft shapes, one idea per sticker.
        corners: Round everything. 26 to 28px cards, full pills for buttons, fields, chips and bars, and wobbly blob radii on the totals.
        borders: A 2.5 to 3px plum outline on every shape, like a die-cut sticker.
        shadows: A hard plum drop of 4 to 6px straight down, with no blur.
        icons:
            Faces on shapes beside words. A smiling circle for On track, a
            rounded triangle with a wobbly mouth for At risk, a rounded square
            with a sad mouth for Behind and a star with a bang for Overdue.
            Total blobs have happy, busy, worried and proud faces.
        focus: A 3px dashed grape outline offset 4px.
        tone: Cheerful and kind while facts stay exact, such as Good morning, Mara!, Uh-oh and What's new.

    style173:
        number: 173
        run: 35
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Soft UI
        idea: The dashboard is moulded from one pale grey surface, where panels, knobs and buttons are extruded by paired light and dark shadows and wells and grooves are pressed in, yet text keeps full AA contrast and focus is a solid indigo ring.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/173.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            base: #e4e8ef, the single surface everything is moulded from
            highlight: #ffffff, the top-left shadow, never text
            lowlight: #b6bfcc, the bottom-right shadow, never text
            lift: #eef1f6, knob dishes and outlined last-week bars
            ink: #263040, text
            softInk: #4d5868, meta, labels and last-week bar outlines
            indigo: #3346c2, the primary button, fills, the current nav and focus
            green: #1d6b45, On track
            amber: #8a4b00, At risk
            red: #b4232c, Behind and the overdue ring and text
        type:
            One stack, system-ui, Segoe UI Variable, Segoe UI, SF Pro Display,
            Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial. Knob figures are 34px bold, the
            greeting 32px bold at minus 0.01em, project names and headings 16
            to 17px bold, body 14 to 15px, and meta and chips 13px at 600 to
            700.
        layout:
            A raised sidebar holds the brand with a small indigo dot in a
            raised disc and six raised nav pills with line icons, Home pressed
            in and indigo. The main column starts with a pressed pill search,
            a raised indigo New project button, a raised round bell and a
            pressed initials disc with Mara Okafor. A raised greeting panel
            has the greeting and date at left and a pressed red Overdue pill
            at right. Four raised tiles each hold a knob, a pressed ring with
            a raised dish and the figure, over a label, the overdue knob ringed
            in red with a clock. Projects are raised rows with name and meta,
            a pressed groove filled indigo to the percent with a raised round
            thumb, the percent and a pressed status chip. Below sit a raised
            chart panel with a pressed trough of raised pill bars, outlined
            light last week and indigo this week, and a raised activity panel
            with pressed initial discs. Below 1000px the sidebar becomes a
            three by two grid of pills on top, and rows wrap on phones.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16 to 20px between raised items so shadows can breathe, 28px between sections.
        density: Low to medium. Few, large soft objects.
        corners: Very round. 20 to 28px panels, 14px buttons and nav, circles for knobs and icon buttons, pills for fields and chips.
        borders: None. Edges come only from shadow pairs, except a 1.5px soft ink outline on last-week bars.
        shadows: Raised uses 7px 7px 14px lowlight with minus 7px minus 7px 14px highlight, small raised uses 4px, and pressed wells use the same pair inset. The current nav item is pressed in.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.7px for nav. Status icons are solid, a check
            circle for On track, a triangle with a bang for At risk, a rounded
            crossed square for Behind and a clock ring for Overdue, inside
            pressed chips with their word.
        focus: A solid 3px indigo outline offset 3px on every control, never a shadow change alone.
        tone: Plain and neutral, such as Projects, 6 active and Activity.

    style174:
        number: 174
        run: 36
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Icon rail master-detail
        idea: A three-pane work surface where a slim dark icon rail, a white list pane with the greeting, figures and projects, and a wide detail pane for the selected project sit side by side, quiet slate with one blue.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/174.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            rail: #1e2733, the 64px icon rail
            railInk: #b8c4d2, rail icons that are not current
            railCurrent: #34425a, the current rail item behind a white icon and a white edge bar
            canvas: #f4f6f8, the detail pane background and the search field
            surface: #ffffff, the list pane, cards, the top bar and the style sheet
            ink: #1c2430, text
            muted: #5a6576, meta, labels, dates and day letters
            line: #dde2e8, every border and divider
            accent: #3451a8, the primary button, links, the selected row edge, meters, this week bars and focus
            selected: #eaf0fb, the selected project row
            lastWeek: #8794a8, outlines of last week bars
            ok: #1a7048, On track text and icon on a pale green chip
            risk: #8f5200, At risk text and icon on a pale amber chip
            bad: #b42318, Behind and overdue text and icon on a pale red chip
        type:
            One system stack, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
            Arial. Base 14px at 1.45. The detail title is 26px at 650 weight,
            the greeting 20px, figures 20 to 22px with tabular numbers, card
            titles 15px, meta 12 to 13px, and pane labels 12px caps tracked
            0.06em.
        layout:
            Three columns at full height. A 64px dark slate rail holds a white
            square B mark, six icon-only links with tooltips and accessible
            names, Home current with a lighter tile and a white edge bar, and
            the initials disc at the foot. Next a 336px white list pane holds
            the greeting, the date and a pale red overdue line, then the four
            figures as a two by two ruled grid, then a Projects label and six
            full-width rows with name, status chip, category and due date, and a
            thin meter with percent and task counts. Mobile app 2.0 is selected
            with a pale blue fill and a blue left edge. The detail pane fills
            the rest. Its white top bar has search, New project, a bell and Mara
            Okafor. Below sit a breadcrumb, the project title with its At risk
            chip, meta with days left, an Edit project button, underlined tabs,
            a ruled four-cell facts strip, and then the team chart and the team
            activity side by side in bordered cards, activity for this project
            tagged. Below 1180px the cards stack. Below 760px the rail becomes a
            sticky top bar of icons and the panes stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 20px pane padding, 24px detail padding, 12px row padding, 20px between detail blocks.
        density: Medium to dense. Three panes visible at once, compact rows, small type.
        corners: Small. 6px panes and cards, 4px buttons, fields and chips, round initials.
        borders: 1px light slate lines between panes, rows and fact cells. The selected row has a 3px blue left edge.
        shadows: None. Separation comes from borders and the dark rail.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.75px stroke, 22px in the rail, 18px elsewhere.
            Status uses a check circle for On track, a triangle with a bang for
            At risk, a crossed square for Behind and a clock for overdue, always
            with the word.
        focus: A 2px blue outline offset 2px, white on the dark rail.
        tone: Plain and neutral, such as Tasks completed, all projects and Team activity.
    style175:
        number: 175
        run: 36
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Top nav hub
        idea: A classic hub page with a navy bar of horizontal navigation and sub-tabs on top, a full-width stone band of four large figures, and three equal ruled columns for projects, the chart and activity, on warm grey paper.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/175.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            navy: #1d2c54, the top bar, headings, figures, panel top rules, the primary button, this week bars and focus
            navyInk: #c9d1e6, nav links that are not current on navy
            page: #f3f1ed, the warm grey page
            paper: #ffffff, panels, the sub-tab bar, fields and the style sheet
            band: #e8e4dc, the full-width figures band and initials squares
            ink: #25262b, body text and project names
            muted: #5e5a53, labels, notes, meta and day numbers
            line: #d9d4cb, panel borders and row rules
            strongLine: #858077, dividers inside the figures band, field borders and last week bar outlines
            ok: #2d6a3e, On track text and check circle
            risk: #8a4d00, At risk text and triangle
            bad: #a8261e, Behind and overdue text, crossed square and clock
        type:
            One humanist stack, Avenir Next, Avenir, Segoe UI, Helvetica Neue,
            Helvetica, Arial. Base 15px at 1.5. Band figures are 44px at 600
            with tabular numbers, the greeting 30px bold navy, panel titles and
            band labels 12 to 13px bold caps tracked 0.1em, project names 15px
            bold, meta 13px.
        layout:
            Stacked full-width bands inside a 1232px container. A navy top bar
            holds a square outline mark and the Brightwork wordmark, the six nav
            items as horizontal tabs with a white underline on Home, then a
            white search field, a white New project button, an outlined bell and
            Mara Okafor at right. A white sub-tab bar beneath holds Overview, My
            tasks, Timeline and Workload with a navy underline on Overview, and
            the date with a calendar icon at right. The greeting sits on the
            page with the overdue line and a Review them link. A full-width
            stone band runs edge to edge with four figures split by vertical
            rules, each a caps label, a 44px navy number and a short note,
            overdue in red with a clock. Then three equal columns of white
            panels with a 3px navy top rule. Projects lists six rows of name,
            status, category and due, and a 6px bar. The chart panel shows
            fourteen bars, hatched outlined last week and solid navy this week,
            over a small table of week totals and change. Activity lists six
            entries with square initials. Below 1040px the nav wraps under the
            brand and activity spans two columns. Below 760px the nav becomes a
            three by two grid, figures go two by two and panels stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px gutters between columns, 20px figure padding, 12 to 18px row padding, 28px above the columns.
        density: Medium. Figures are large and airy, the columns beneath are compact.
        corners: Nearly square. 3px panels, buttons and fields, round avatar, square initials.
        borders: 1px warm grey panel borders and row rules, a 3px navy top rule on panels, darker vertical rules in the band.
        shadows: None. Hierarchy comes from the navy bar, the stone band and rules.
        icons:
            Line icons at 2px stroke, 18px. Status is text with a check circle
            for On track, a triangle for At risk, a crossed square for Behind
            and a clock for overdue.
        focus: A 3px navy outline offset 2px with a white gap, white and inset on the navy bar.
        tone: Formal and businesslike, with caps labels such as Due this week and Hours logged and plain links such as All projects.
    style176:
        number: 176
        run: 36
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Command first
        idea: A sparse home built around one large search and command field with keyboard hints, followed by a hairline strip of four figures and quiet unboxed lists, graphite text with a single violet accent.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/176.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #fbfbfc, the near-white page
            paper: #ffffff, the command field, buttons and fields
            ink: #22242a, graphite text
            muted: #5c5f69, labels, meta, times and day letters
            hair: #e4e5ea, hairline rules under rows and around the figure strip
            violet: #5b3fd1, the primary button, links, progress, this week bars and focus
            violetSoft: #efebfc, the focus halo of the command field and the initials disc
            keycap: #f1f1f4, keyboard hint caps and the current nav pill
            keycapLine: #d3d4dc, keycap borders
            keycapInk: #3b3e47, keycap letters
            lastWeek: #8a8d98, dashed outlines of last week bars
            ok: #1f7a4d, On track text and check circle
            risk: #925400, At risk text and triangle
            bad: #b3261e, Behind and overdue text, crossed square and clock
        type:
            Two stacks. Text uses system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
            Arial at 15px and 1.55. Keycaps and sheet notes use ui-monospace, SF
            Mono, Cascadia Mono, Menlo, Consolas at 12px. The greeting is 34px
            at 600 with minus 0.02em tracking, the command input 17px, figures
            26px at 600 with tabular numbers, list headings 13px at 600 in muted
            sentence case, rows 15px and meta 13px.
        layout:
            A slim top line in a 1120px container with a small violet diamond
            and the wordmark, the six nav items as quiet text pills with Home in
            a grey pill, and a bell and Mara Okafor at right. Then a centred
            720px hero with lots of air above it, the date in muted text, a 34px
            greeting, a red overdue line with a Show them link, and the command
            field, 60px tall with a 14px radius, a search icon, the placeholder
            Search or type a command, and Ctrl K keycaps at the right end. Under
            it three centred action buttons each carry a keycap, a violet New
            project with N, Overdue tasks with G O and Log time with T. Next a
            full-width strip of four figures between hairlines, each a number
            followed by a lowercase label on one line. Below sit two unboxed
            lists side by side, Projects at three fifths and Recent activity at
            two fifths, each under a muted heading and hairline. Project rows
            show name over category, a thin violet progress line with percent,
            due date and status. Activity rows show the sentence and the time at
            right. The chart runs full width beneath, airy bars with dashed
            outlines last week and violet this week. A footer hint reads Press ?
            for all keyboard shortcuts. Below 960px the lists stack, below 760px
            figures go two by two and keycaps leave the field.
        spacing: An 8px unit with generous gaps. 72px above the hero, 32px from greeting to field, 40px between sections, 56px between the two lists, 11px row padding.
        density: Sparse at the top, medium in the lists. One focal control and little chrome.
        corners: Soft. 14px on the command field, 8px on buttons and fields, 5px keycaps, 4px bar tops, round initials.
        borders: Hairlines only, under rows and around the figure strip. No cards. The command field has a 1px grey edge.
        shadows: One soft violet-tinted shadow under the command field. Nothing else is raised.
        icons:
            Thin line icons at 1.5px stroke, 18px, 22px in the field. Status
            icons use 2px stroke, a check circle for On track, a triangle for At
            risk, a crossed square for Behind and a clock for overdue, always
            with the word. Keycaps carry shortcuts.
        focus: A 2px white gap then a 2px violet ring as a box shadow, and the command field gains a violet edge and a soft violet halo.
        tone: Calm and terse with lowercase figure labels such as tasks due this week, and command verbs such as Show them and Log time.
    style177:
        number: 177
        run: 36
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Two sidebars
        idea: A three-column workspace with labelled navigation on the left, a centre feed of project cards with progress rings, and a pale green context panel on the right holding the week chart and an activity timeline, cool white with one green.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/177.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #f6f8fa, the cool white page behind the feed
            paper: #ffffff, the left sidebar, project cards, top bars, chips and the chart well
            context: #eef4f1, the right context panel
            ink: #18232b, text
            muted: #55636e, meta, labels, section captions and day letters
            line: #dfe5ea, card borders and dividers
            green: #146c43, the primary button, links, the current nav item, rings, this week bars, timeline nodes, On track and focus
            greenSoft: #e3f2ea, the current nav item fill
            ringTrack: #dfe8e3, the empty part of progress rings
            lastWeek: #7f9a8b, outlines of last week bars
            risk: #8b5000, At risk text and triangle
            bad: #b02a1e, Behind and overdue text, crossed square, clock and the overdue chip
        type:
            One stack, Segoe UI, system-ui, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial. Base
            14px at 1.5. The greeting is 24px bold, project names 15px at 650,
            the feed heading 16px bold, panel captions and nav groups 11 to 13px
            bold caps tracked 0.08em, chip figures 16px bold, week totals 22px
            bold, meta 13px and ring figures 11px bold.
        layout:
            Three full-height columns of 232px, the flexible centre and 344px.
            The white left sidebar holds a green rounded square mark and the
            wordmark, a Workspace caption over six icon and label nav items with
            Home filled pale green and a count of 6 beside Projects, and a Needs
            attention group linking Billing migration and Mobile app 2.0 with
            their status. The centre has a white top bar with a wide search
            field and a green New project button, then the greeting, date and
            red overdue line, then the four figures as rounded pill chips in one
            row, overdue in pale red with a clock. Under a Projects heading the
            feed is six separate white cards, each with a 44px green progress
            ring holding the percent, name over category and task count, due
            date over days left, and the status at the right end. The pale green
            right panel starts with a bell and Mara Okafor, then a Tasks
            completed caption, two small white tiles with last week 59 and this
            week 73 up 14, the fourteen-day bar chart in a white well with
            outlined last week bars and green this week bars, and an Activity
            timeline down a vertical line with hollow green nodes. Below 1200px
            the right panel drops under the feed as two columns. Below 760px the
            nav becomes a three by two grid, the bell and user sit top right,
            and everything stacks.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 32px centre gutters, 20px panel padding, 8px between feed cards, 12 to 16px card padding.
        density: Medium. Three columns of context at once, roomy cards in the centre.
        corners: Rounded. 8px cards, buttons, fields and tiles, 12px on the style sheet, pill chips, round rings and nodes.
        borders: 1px cool grey borders on cards, chips and sidebars. The right panel uses pale green edged tiles.
        shadows: None. Columns separate by tone, white left, cool white centre, pale green right.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.8px stroke, 18px, muted in the nav and green when
            current. Status uses a check circle for On track, a triangle for At
            risk, a crossed square for Behind and a clock for overdue, always
            with the word.
        focus: A 2px green outline offset 2px on every control.
        tone: Friendly and plain, with lowercase chip labels such as tasks due this week and short captions such as Needs attention.
    style178:
        number: 178
        run: 36
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Focus column
        idea: The whole dashboard as one calm 720px column read top to bottom in priority order, a sentence that names what matters, then numbered sections set in a bookish serif on off-white paper with ink blue accents and rules instead of boxes.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/178.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            paper: #faf8f3, the off-white page
            ink: #1b2433, text, section rules and the nav top rule
            inkBlue: #1d3c78, the wordmark, links, figures, section numbers, the primary button, progress lines, this week bars and focus
            muted: #5b5f68, meta, captions, times and the date kicker
            rule: #d8d3c7, hairlines between rows and figures
            lastWeek: #8a8f9c, outlines of last week bars
            ok: #2f6b3a, On track text and check circle
            risk: #8a4a00, At risk text and triangle
            bad: #a3261b, Behind and overdue text, crossed square and clock
        type:
            Two stacks. Reading text uses Charter, Bitstream Charter, Iowan Old
            Style, Palatino Linotype, Palatino, Georgia at 17px and 1.6. Meta,
            nav, buttons and labels use Helvetica Neue, Segoe UI, system-ui,
            Roboto, Arial at 13 to 15px. The greeting is 44px serif bold at
            minus 0.02em, the lead 21px serif, section titles 22px serif bold,
            project names 19px serif bold, figures 40px serif regular in ink
            blue, and the date kicker and section numbers 13px sans caps tracked
            0.08 to 0.14em.
        layout:
            One centred column 720px wide with 16px side padding and nothing
            beside it. The masthead has the wordmark in ink blue, Bright bold
            and work italic, with a round outlined bell and Mara Okafor at
            right. Under it the six nav items run as one line of sans text links
            between a 2px ink rule above and a hairline below, Home underlined
            in ink blue. Then an underlined search field and a New project
            button on one line. The greeting follows with generous space, a caps
            date kicker, a 44px serif Good morning, Mara. and a lead sentence
            that starts with 4 tasks are overdue in red with a clock and names
            the behind and at risk projects. Five numbered sections follow, each
            titled under a 2px ink rule. 01 Needs attention lists the overdue
            tasks, Billing migration and Mobile app 2.0 with icons in the margin
            and open task counts. 02 This week shows the four figures as large
            serif numbers in a row split by hairlines. 03 All projects is an
            ordered list, most urgent first, with an index number, the serif
            name, the status at right, meta with category, tasks, due date and
            days left, and a 2px progress line. 04 Tasks completed opens with a
            sentence of the week totals over square outlined and solid bars. 05
            Recent activity puts the time in a left margin column. A closing
            line ends the page. Below 760px figures go two by two and the margin
            times move under each entry.
        spacing: An 8px unit with a reading rhythm. 56px above the greeting, 48px between sections, 16px row padding.
        density: Low. One column, one thing after another, wide line height.
        corners: Square. Only the bell, avatar and buttons at 2px or round.
        borders: Rules only. A 2px ink rule over each section and the nav, 1px warm hairlines between rows, an underline for the search field.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.6px stroke, 18px, set in the text or in a 28px left
            margin. Status uses a check circle for On track, a triangle for At
            risk, a crossed square for Behind and a clock for overdue, always
            with the word.
        focus: A 2px ink blue outline offset 3px on every control and field.
        tone: Written and calm, in full sentences such as Billing migration is 30% done with 28 tasks open and 20 days to go.

    style179:
        number: 179
        run: 37
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Grouped data grid
        idea: The dashboard is one hierarchical grid, projects grouped under team header rows with subtotals, a sticky column header and inline progress strips, set in cool grey with a single teal accent.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/179.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #eef1f2, the page behind panels
            surface: #ffffff, the top bar, panels and fields
            columnHead: #e6ebed, the sticky grid header row
            grid: #f6f8f8, row hover, the total row and the focused row
            ink: #1c2427, text
            muted: #4f5e65, labels, meta and column heads
            line: #d3dadd, panel edges and rules, with #e4e9eb for row rules
            slate: #7c8fa0, field edges and last week bars
            teal: #0f766e, the primary button, progress fills, this week bars, the current tab and focus
            tealTint: #e1f1ef, team group rows
            tealInk: #0b5c55, text on group rows and links
            green: #1d6b3c, On track
            amber: #8a5200, At risk
            red: #b3261e, Behind, the overdue figure and the overdue line
        type:
            One stack, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica
            Neue, Arial, with tabular figures. KPI figures 22px at 650, the
            greeting 20px at 650, group rows 14px bold, cells 14px regular,
            column heads and panel titles 12 to 13px bold caps tracked 0.03
            to 0.04em, meta 12px.
        layout:
            A white top bar holds a small four square teal mark with the
            brand, a wide search field, then at right a teal New project
            button, a square bell with a red dot and the initials disc with
            Mara Okafor. Under it a row of text tabs, Home underlined in teal.
            The main area opens with one line holding the greeting, the date
            and a red clock with 4 tasks are overdue. Below sits a single
            bordered summary strip split into four cells by thin rules, each a
            figure beside its label, the overdue figure in red. Then two
            columns. The wide left panel is the grid titled Projects by team,
            with a grey sticky header row of Project, Status, Progress, Tasks,
            Due and Days left. Each team, Design, Engineering, Marketing and
            Research, has a teal tinted group row with a chevron, the project
            count, a subtotal progress strip and percent, done over total tasks
            and the next due date with its days left. Project rows are indented
            under it with the status word and shape, a 72px progress strip and
            percent, tasks, due date and days left. A grey All teams total row
            ends the grid with a teal sparkline of the 14 daily values, 46
            percent and 78 of 170. A status mix line under the grid counts 4
            On track, 1 At risk and 1 Behind. The 320px right column stacks a
            Tasks completed panel with 14 square bars, slate last week and teal
            this week, and an Activity panel as a two column table of time and
            sentence. Below 1060px the right column moves under the grid, and
            below 760px the grid scrolls sideways inside its panel with the
            project column pinned, the summary becomes two by two and the
            search takes its own row.
        spacing: An 8px unit. Cells are 7 by 12px, 16px between panels, a 24px page gutter.
        density: High. Every team, project, subtotal and total fits in one grid at 1280px.
        corners: 4px panels, 3px controls, square bars and strips.
        borders: 1px #d3dadd panel edges and #e4e9eb row rules, slate field edges, a teal 2px tab underline.
        shadows: None. Separation comes from lines and the teal tint on group rows.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.8px stroke at text size in the header. Status
            shapes are filled at 13px beside the word, a check circle for On
            track, a triangle with a bang for At risk and a crossed square for
            Behind, plus a clock ring for overdue.
        focus: A 2px teal outline offset 1px. A focused field gets a teal border and outline, a focused row an inset outline on the grid grey.
        tone: Plain data labels, caps column heads and numbers before words, such as Next 20 Nov.

    style180:
        number: 180
        run: 37
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Card masonry
        idea: Every piece of the dashboard is a soft paper card of its own height, dropped into masonry columns on warm beige, so busy projects get tall detailed cards and quiet ones stay a single line, with rust as the one accent.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/180.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            beige: #f4eee4, the page
            sidebar: #ebe2d3, the navigation column
            paper: #fffcf7, cards, fields and the current nav item
            ink: #2b231d, text
            muted: #665a4f, meta, eyebrows and notes
            line: #e3d8c7, dashed rules inside cards
            clay: #9a8670, field edges and last week bars
            track: #eadfce, empty bars and the ring track
            rust: #a3441f, the primary button, fills, this week bars, focus and the overdue card
            rustDeep: #7f3315, links, project names in activity and the current nav text
            rustTint: #f7e4d8, the urgent note and the avatar
            moss: #3a6a2c, On track
            ochre: #865700, At risk
            berry: #8e1f33, Behind
        type:
            Two stacks. Headings and figures use Iowan Old Style, Palatino
            Linotype, Palatino, Book Antiqua, Georgia, serif. Text uses
            system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial. KPI figures
            44px serif bold, the greeting 30px serif bold, card titles 19px
            serif bold, body 15px sans at 1.5, eyebrows 12px sans at 600.
        layout:
            A 232px beige sidebar holds a four block rust mark with the serif
            brand and six nav links with line icons, Home as a raised paper
            pill in rust deep. The main column has a top row with a pill search
            field, then at right a rust pill New project button, a round bell
            with a rust dot and a round initials avatar with Mara Okafor. Below
            everything is a card in CSS columns, three columns of about 280px
            at 1280px with 20px gaps, each card as tall as its content. In
            source order the cards are the greeting card with the date eyebrow,
            a serif greeting, a line about six projects and a rust tinted
            urgent note with a clock, then Website redesign in full with team
            eyebrow, status pill, bar, a facts list of due, days left and open
            tasks and the latest comment, then a solid rust Overdue tasks card
            with a big 4, then Mobile app 2.0 with a progress ring beside its
            facts and two recent events, then a one line Active projects card,
            then the Tasks completed chart card with rounded bars, then Billing
            migration with bar and latest event, then a Due this week card, a
            short Q4 customer survey card, the Recent activity card with
            initial discs, a one line Onboarding emails card, an Hours logged
            card noting about 31 hours per project, and a Spring catalogue card
            with only its numbers and the latest event. Below 900px the sidebar
            becomes a scrolling top strip, and below 640px the masonry is one
            column and the search takes its own row.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 20px card padding, 20px between cards and columns, 32px page gutter.
        density: Medium and uneven on purpose. A card carries as much detail as its project needs.
        corners: 16px cards, 10 to 12px fields, swatches and nav items, pills for buttons, search, status and the avatar.
        borders: None on cards. 1px clay edges on fields and search, dashed #e3d8c7 rules inside cards.
        shadows: Two soft warm layers on cards and the current nav item, 0 1px 2px and 0 6px 18px in brown at 6 to 7 percent.
        icons:
            Rounded line icons at 1.8px stroke at text size. Status sits in a
            pale tinted pill with a filled shape and the word, a check circle
            for On track, a triangle with a bang for At risk and a crossed
            square for Behind.
        focus: A 2px rust outline offset 3px, following the rounded shapes. A focused field gets a rust border as well.
        tone: Warm and conversational, such as 4 tasks are overdue, start there.

    style181:
        number: 181
        run: 37
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Timeline first
        idea: A blue-grey planning view where the projects are the hero as bars on a September to January date axis, cut by a today line at 31 October, with a slim KPI band above and the chart and activity below.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/181.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #f1f4f7, the page
            band: #e3e9ef, the header band
            surface: #ffffff, the timeline, panels and fields
            past: #e9eef3, the shaded time before today and row rules
            ink: #1a2632, text, the today line and its label
            muted: #4c5d6e, labels, dates and axis months
            line: #d3dce5, borders and dashed month lines
            steel: #2f5d86, the primary button, this week bars, the avatar and focus
            steelDeep: #244a6c, links and the current nav text
            steelSoft: #7a8fa6, last week bars, KPI rules and field edges
            greenBar: #cfe3d6, On track bars, with #22683e for the word and shape
            amberBar: #f0dfc2, At risk bars, with #875200 for the word and shape
            redBar: #f2d2cd, Behind bars, with #ad2a1f for the word, shape and overdue
        type:
            One stack, Avenir Next, Segoe UI, Helvetica Neue, system-ui,
            Roboto, Arial. KPI figures 28px at 600, the greeting 24px at 650,
            panel titles 16px at 650, project names 14px at 650, axis months
            and the column label 12px at 650, notes 12 to 13px.
        layout:
            A blue-grey band spans the top. Its first row has a three bar
            stepped mark with the brand at left, the six nav links centred as
            text with Home in a white tab, and a bell, a square steel avatar and
            Mara Okafor at right. Its second row has the greeting with the date
            and a red clock with 4 tasks are overdue at left, and the search
            field and a steel New project button at right. Below the band four
            KPIs sit in one row without boxes, each a figure over its label
            behind a 3px left rule, the overdue rule and figure in red. The
            timeline panel follows across the full width. Its axis row has a
            250px Project column label then the months Sep 2026, Oct, Nov, Dec
            and Jan 2027 placed by date, with a dark Today 31 Oct tag. Each of
            the six rows, sorted by days left, has a label cell with name, team,
            percent, tasks and the status word with shape, and a lane where the
            time before today is shaded, dashed month lines run down, a solid
            dark today line cuts through, and a status tinted bar runs from
            today to the due date, ending in the filled status shape with the
            due date and days left beneath. A footnote names the nearest and
            furthest due dates. Below, two panels side by side, Tasks completed
            as seven weekday pairs of bars, last week beside this week, and
            Activity as rows of time then sentence. Below 1000px the nav wraps
            to its own row and the lower panels stack. Below 720px each project
            label sits above its lane, the axis keeps all five months at phone
            width and the KPIs become two by two.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 20px panel padding, 72px timeline rows, 20px between panels, 32px page gutter.
        density: Medium. One project per lane, read left to right through time.
        corners: 8px panels, 6px controls, tabs and avatar, 4px bars.
        borders: 1px #d3dce5 panels, dashed month lines, a 2px ink today line, 3px left rules on KPIs.
        shadows: One faint 0 1px 2px at 5 percent ink on the timeline panel only.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.8px stroke at text size. Filled status shapes mark
            each bar end and the label cell, a check circle for On track, a
            triangle with a bang for At risk and a crossed square for Behind,
            plus a clock ring for overdue.
        focus: A 2px steel outline offset 2px with a 5px pale steel halo.
        tone: Calm planning language built on dates and days left, such as 20 Nov, 20 d.

    style182:
        number: 182
        run: 37
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Status columns
        idea: A portfolio board on white, where three status columns, On track, At risk and Behind, hold the project cards, a charcoal icon rail and charcoal type carry the structure, and soft status tints only mark the column heads.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/182.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            white: #ffffff, the page and cards
            well: #f5f6f7, column bodies and initials tiles
            charcoal: #2a2c30, the rail, the primary button and progress fills
            ink: #202124, text, heavy rules and focus
            muted: #585c64, labels and meta
            line: #dcdee1, card edges and rules
            fieldEdge: #8a8e95, inputs and search
            greyLine: #80848c, the last week line in the chart
            onTint: #e5f2e8, the On track column head, with #1d6a37 for its text, shape and top rule
            riskTint: #fbefd9, the At risk column head, with #875000
            behindTint: #fbe4e2, the Behind column head, with #ad261f, also the overdue text
        type:
            One stack, Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, system-ui. The
            greeting 28px at 800 with minus 0.02em tracking, KPI figures 26px
            at 800, card titles 16px bold, column heads 15px at 800, body 14px,
            card fact labels 11px caps tracked 0.06em.
        layout:
            A 76px charcoal rail at left holds a white square B mark and six
            nav items as icons with small labels underneath, Home as a white
            tile. The top bar on white has the bold wordmark, a square search
            field, then at right a charcoal New project button, a square bell
            with a red dot and a square initials tile with Mara Okafor. The
            intro row has the greeting and the date with a red clock and 4
            tasks are overdue at left and four figures at right split by thin
            rules, closed by a 2px ink rule. The board is a three column grid.
            On track spans both rows of column one. At risk and Behind sit at
            the top of columns two and three. Each column has a 4px top rule
            and a tinted head with the filled shape, the word and a count box,
            a pale well holding white cards, and a footer of done over total
            tasks. A card shows team and percent, the project name, a thin
            charcoal bar, Tasks, Due and Left facts and the latest event for
            that project when one exists. Under At risk sits Tasks completed as
            a line chart by weekday, a solid line with dots for this week and a
            dashed grey line with square markers for last week. Under Behind
            sits Activity as rows of initials tile, sentence and time. Below
            1080px the board is two columns, and below 760px everything stacks
            and the rail becomes a top strip.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 20px between columns, 10px between cards, 12 by 14px card padding, 28px page gutter.
        density: Medium. Status is read from column position, details from small cards.
        corners: 2px everywhere, nearly square.
        borders: 1px #dcdee1 cards, a 4px status rule on each column top, a 2px ink rule under the intro and under the sheet.
        shadows: Only a 1px bottom line at 4 percent black under cards.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.8px stroke, 22px on the rail with labels. Filled
            status shapes in the column heads and rows, a check circle for On
            track, a triangle with a bang for At risk and a crossed square for
            Behind.
        focus: A 2px ink outline offset 2px, white on the rail.
        tone: Direct portfolio language with short labels, such as Left 20 d.

    style183:
        number: 183
        run: 37
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Metric wall
        idea: A navy monochrome scoreboard, where eight large figures, four given and four derived, fill a two by four wall of ruled cells under a navy band, and the projects and activity follow as compact ruled lists.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/183.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            navy: #13294b, the band, text, figures, status shapes, the overdue cell and focus
            navy2: #22416f, the search field on the band
            mid: #4a5d7c, labels, notes and field edges
            soft: #7f93b2, last week bars and the search edge, never text
            line: #c6d0df, wall cell rules and list rules
            pale: #e4e9f2, progress tracks
            wash: #f3f5f9, derived cells and the style sheet
            onNavy: #c9d5e8, secondary text on navy
            white: #ffffff, the page and given cells
        type:
            One stack, SF Pro Display, Segoe UI Variable Display, Segoe UI,
            system-ui, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial, with tabular figures.
            Wall figures 64px at 250 weight with minus 0.03em tracking and
            units at 28px, the greeting 30px light with the name at 650, row
            names 14px at 650, notes 13px, labels 11px bold caps tracked 0.12
            to 0.14em.
        layout:
            A 60px navy band holds a four square mark with the brand in spaced
            caps, six text nav links with a white underline under Home, and at
            right a navy search field, a white New project button, a bell with
            a white dot and an outlined initials square with Mara Okafor. Below
            on white the greeting sits at left in light type, and the date with
            an underlined clock and 4 tasks are overdue sits at right. The wall
            is a four by two grid of square cells ruled in thin lines under a
            2px navy top rule. The first row holds the given figures, Active
            projects 6 with the status mix 4, 1 and 1, Tasks due this week 23,
            Overdue tasks 4 as the one inverted navy cell tagged Act first, and
            Hours logged this week 186 h. The second row holds derived figures
            on a pale wash, each tagged Derived, Completed this week 73 with
            14 mini bars, Week over week up 24 percent, Overall progress 46
            percent with 78 of 170 tasks, and Hours per project 31 h. Below,
            two columns split two to one. Projects is a ruled table sorted by
            days left with name and team, status, a thin bar and percent,
            tasks, due and days left. Activity is a ruled list with caps times
            above each sentence. Section heads are small caps over a 2px navy
            rule. Below 1100px the wall is two by four and the lists stack.
            Below 820px the search and nav wrap into rows in the band and the
            table scrolls inside its section.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 20 by 24px cell padding, 40px page gutter, 40px between the wall and the lists.
        density: Low on the wall with eight figures only, then dense ruled lists.
        corners: Square everywhere.
        borders: 2px navy top rules on the wall and section heads, 1px #c6d0df cell and row rules, outlined tags.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            Line icons at text size in the band. Status shapes are filled navy,
            a check circle for On track, a triangle with a bang for At risk and
            a crossed square for Behind, and the word is plain for On track,
            italic for At risk and underlined for Behind.
        focus: A 3px navy outline offset 2px, white on the band.
        tone: Terse caps labels with plain notes that say how a derived figure was made.

    style184:
        number: 184
        run: 38
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Fintech
        idea: A crisp banking grade ledger, deep green and white with precise tabular figures, hairline dividers and nothing decorative, so every number reads as trustworthy.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/184.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            deepGreen: #0b4d3a, the 3px header top rule, the full width summary band, the primary button, the this week line and focus
            green2: #0f6a4f, links and the thin progress fills
            mint: #cfe8dd, labels and captions on the green band and the focus halo
            white: #ffffff, the header, panels, fields and the overdue chip on the band
            page: #f6f8f7, the page background
            ink: #0f1d17, text and figures
            muted: #4a5a53, column heads, meta, axis labels and timestamps
            rule: #dfe5e2, row and panel hairlines and empty bar tracks
            ruleStrong: #c3ccc8, table head rules, field borders and the chart baseline
            onTrack: #0b6b45, the On track word with a filled circle
            atRisk: #8a5300, the At risk word with a filled triangle
            behind: #b42318, the Behind word with a filled square and the overdue chip
        type:
            One stack, system-ui, apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica
            Neue, Arial, with tabular lining numerals on the whole page. KPI
            figures are 32px at 600 and minus 0.02em, the greeting 26px at 650,
            panel titles 15px at 650, table and activity text 13px, column
            heads and band labels 11 to 12px caps at 600 tracked 0.04 to
            0.06em.
        layout:
            A white header with a 3px deep green top rule holds the brand mark
            and name, the six nav links inline with a 2px green underline on
            Home, then at the right a search field, a green New project button,
            a square bell with a red dot and the initials disc with Mara Okafor.
            Under it a full width deep green band carries a caps dateline, the
            greeting and a small white chip reading 4 tasks are overdue with a
            red square, then a row of four KPI figures in white split by thin
            translucent vertical dividers, each with a mint caps label above
            and a small caption below, such as 78 of 170 tasks done. The main
            area is a two to one grid. The wide left panel is a projects ledger
            table sorted by due date with columns Project with team below,
            Progress as a thin bar and percent, Tasks as 18 / 25, Due, Days
            left and Status, closed by a Total row of 46 percent and 78 / 170.
            The right panel is an activity ledger with the action on one line,
            the project below in muted text and the time right aligned. Below
            both, a full width chart panel has a stats column at left with This
            week 73, Last week 59, Change plus 14 at plus 23.7 percent in green
            and Daily average 10.4 against 8.4, and at right a line chart that
            overlays the two weeks on a Sunday to Saturday axis, last week as a
            dashed grey line and this week as a solid green line with hollow
            points and a faint green area. Below 1000px the grid stacks. Below
            720px the nav wraps onto its own row under the brand, the search
            hides, KPIs go two by two, the stats sit in two columns above the
            chart, and the table and chart scroll sideways inside their panels.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px page gutters and gaps, 16px panel padding, table cells 10px by 12px.
        density: Medium high. Projects are a ledger table rather than cards.
        corners: 4px on panels, buttons, fields and chips. Bars 2px. The avatar is round.
        borders: 1px hairlines between every row and around panels, a stronger line under table heads, and a 3px deep green rule on top of the header.
        shadows: None. Structure comes from rules alone.
        icons:
            16px line icons at 1.6 stroke for search, plus and bell. Status
            uses solid 10px shapes, a circle for On track, a triangle for At
            risk and a square for Behind, always beside the word.
        focus: A 2px deep green outline offset 2px with a 4px mint halo. A focused field gets a deep green border and outline.
        tone: Exact and neutral, figures first, such as Due this week, Days left and Change plus 14.

    style185:
        number: 185
        run: 38
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Healthcare SaaS
        idea: A calm, reassuring workspace in soft teal with 8px corners, roomy spacing and plain sentences, so the busiest day still feels under control.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/185.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            teal: #0f766e, the primary button, progress fills, this week bars, timeline rings and focus
            deepTeal: #115e59, current nav text, links, the avatar and style sheet headings
            tealTint: #e3f2f0, the current nav item, KPI icon discs and last week bars
            calm: #eef6f5, progress bar tracks
            page: #f3f7f7, the page background
            white: #ffffff, the side rail, cards and fields
            ink: #1d2b2e, text
            muted: #4f6266, plain sentences, meta and axis labels
            line: #dbe6e5, card, row and timeline lines
            onTrack: #1a7a43, On track on #e6f4ec with a check in a circle
            atRisk: #8f5200, At risk on #fdf1de with a triangle and bang, also the overdue notice
            behind: #b42318, Behind on #fdecea with a cross in a diamond
        type:
            One stack, system-ui, apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica
            Neue, Arial. KPI figures 40px at 650, the greeting 30px at 650,
            card titles 20px at 650, project names 17px at 650, body 16px at
            1.6, meta 14px and status pills 14px at 600.
        layout:
            A white left rail 248px wide holds the brand with a teal rounded
            square mark, then six nav items with 20px line icons, Home filled
            teal tint. The main area starts with a roomy row of a wide search
            field, a teal New project button, a bell and the avatar with Mara
            Okafor. A white welcome card has Hello, Mara and the date at left
            and a soft amber notice at right with a triangle, 4 tasks are
            overdue in bold and a gentle line to open Tasks when ready. Next is
            one wide white card split into four KPI cells by thin dividers,
            each with an icon in a teal tint disc, the label, a 40px figure and
            a short plain caption such as tasks are past their date, the
            overdue disc amber. Below sits a grid of 1.7 to 1. The left card,
            Your projects, lists each project as a bordered row with name and
            team, a status pill at right, a 10px full width bar and a sentence
            such as 72% done. 18 of 25 tasks finished. Due 14 Nov, in 14 days.
            The right card, What happened recently, is a vertical timeline of
            teal ring dots joined by a grey line, each entry with the time
            below. A full width chart card closes the dashboard, with the title,
            the two week totals and a plain sentence at left and fourteen
            rounded bars at right, last week outlined in teal over tint and
            this week solid teal. Below 1100px the grid stacks and KPIs go two
            by two. Below 820px the rail turns into a wrapped row of nav pills
            without icons on top, cards lose padding, and the chart scrolls
            sideways inside its card.
        spacing: An 8px unit used generously. 32px between sections, 28px card padding, 48px tall controls, 40px page gutter.
        density: Low. One project per full width row, each with a sentence.
        corners: 8px on cards, rows, buttons, fields and nav items. Pills for status. Circles for icon discs and timeline dots.
        borders: 1px soft teal grey lines on cards and rows. Fields use a firmer 1px grey teal line.
        shadows: None. Calm comes from space and soft tints.
        icons:
            20px rounded line icons at 1.75 stroke, shown in teal tint discs on
            KPIs. Status icons are filled 18px shapes with a white mark, a
            circle with a check, a triangle with a bang and a diamond with a
            cross, inside tinted pills with the word.
        focus: A 3px teal outline offset 3px on every control. A focused field also turns its border teal.
        tone: Warm, plain and reassuring, full sentences such as 18 of 25 tasks finished and What happened recently.

    style186:
        number: 186
        run: 38
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Consulting
        idea: A formal partner's briefing on warm paper, with a serif voice, a burgundy accent, numbered sections and exhibits, all held to one narrow reading column.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/186.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            paper: #fbfaf7, the page and the hollow last week dots
            white: #ffffff, fields and the bell button
            ink: #1e1b18, text, the table head rule and the 2px rule that opens each exhibit
            stoneInk: #5b544c, labels, meta, nav, axis and last week dot outlines
            rule: #d9d3ca, row hairlines and chart gridlines
            burgundy: #7a1f33, the primary button, the finding rule, section numbers, the current nav, this week dots and focus
            burgundyTint: #f4e9eb, the focused row fill
            onTrack: #2f6b3a, On track with a filled circle
            atRisk: #8a5a00, At risk with a half filled diamond
            behind: #9b2c1f, Behind with a crossed square
        type:
            Two stacks. Headings and figures use Iowan Old Style, Palatino
            Linotype, Palatino, Book Antiqua, Georgia, serif at 600. Body uses
            system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial. The greeting is
            40px serif at 1.15, section heads 24px serif, the finding 20px
            serif, figures 40px serif, project names 16px serif, body 15px sans
            at 1.6, exhibit labels and nav 12px sans caps tracked 0.12 to
            0.14em.
        layout:
            A masthead up to 1080px wide has a serif Brightwork wordmark with a
            burgundy outlined square mark at left and at right an underlined
            search field, a square burgundy New project button, a square bell
            and the words Signed in as Mara Okafor. Below a hairline the six
            nav links sit centred in small spaced caps, Home burgundy and
            underlined. Everything after is one centred 760px column like a
            printed memo. A burgundy caps kicker Portfolio briefing sits over
            Welcome, Mara in large serif and the date in serif italic, then a
            pull line with a 3px burgundy left rule reading Principal finding.
            4 tasks are overdue and require attention. Four numbered sections
            follow, each with a small burgundy number beside a serif heading.
            Section 1 Summary is Exhibit 1, four large serif figures in a row
            split by vertical hairlines with labels under them, the overdue
            figure burgundy. Section 2 Projects has a one sentence lead, then
            Exhibit 2, a formal table of Project with team below, Complete,
            Tasks as 18 of 25, Due and Status, with an italic note that
            explains the status symbols. Section 3 Throughput has a lead
            sentence and Exhibit 3, a dumbbell chart with one row per weekday
            joining a hollow last week dot to a filled burgundy this week dot,
            each row labelled like 12 then 15, over a 0 to 20 axis. Section 4
            Recent activity is a list with the time in a narrow left column and
            the entry at right with item names in serif italic, ended by a
            centred row of three burgundy dots. Below 640px the figures go two
            by two, the table turns into stacked blocks with inline labels, the
            activity time moves above each entry and the chart scrolls
            sideways.
        spacing: An 8px unit. A 760px column, 36px between sections, 48px above the title, 12px table cells.
        density: Medium. One column of prose, figures and tables read top to bottom.
        corners: Square everywhere.
        borders: Hairlines between rows, a 2px ink rule opening each exhibit, a 1px ink rule under table heads and a 3px burgundy rule on the finding.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            Very few. Thin 1.4 stroke line icons for search and the bell only.
            Status uses 12px geometric marks with the word, a filled circle, a
            half filled diamond and a crossed square.
        focus: A 2px burgundy outline offset 3px. A focused row also takes the burgundy tint fill.
        tone: Formal and measured, in full sentences, such as Principal finding and Six engagements are active.

    style187:
        number: 187
        run: 38
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Developer platform
        idea: A light developer console in indigo, where projects read like a list of build checks, figures sit in monospace and the overdue alert looks like a failed check annotation.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/187.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            indigo: #4338ca, the primary button, the current tab rule and icon, links and style sheet labels
            indigo2: #4f46e5, progress segments, heat level three and the focus ring
            indigoDeep: #312e81, the primary button border and heat level four
            indigoSoft: #c7cbfb, heat level two
            indigoTint: #eef0ff, heat level one, the avatar and the focused row
            background: #ffffff, the page, boxes and fields
            canvas: #f7f8fa, the header, box header strips and code chips
            ink: #1f2328, text
            muted: #5a6270, meta, monospace timestamps and labels
            line: #dadfe6, box borders, with #eaedf1 for row lines and empty segments
            onTrack: #17803d, On track with a circle and check
            atRisk: #94630a, At risk with a diamond and bang
            behind: #c62a2f, Behind with an octagon and cross, and the overdue annotation on #fdeced
        type:
            Two stacks. Sans is system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
            Arial. Mono is ui-monospace, SF Mono, Cascadia Mono, Segoe UI Mono,
            Roboto Mono, Menlo, Consolas. The greeting is 22px sans at 650, box
            titles 14px sans at 650, body 14px sans, figures 16px mono at 600,
            and meta, dates, task counts and timestamps 12px mono.
        layout:
            A pale grey header holds a breadcrumb at left, an indigo code
            bracket mark, Brightwork in bold, a slash and home in mono, and at
            right a search field with a slash key hint, an indigo New project
            button, a square bell with an indigo dot and a square MO avatar.
            Under it the six nav items run as tabs with small icons, Home
            carrying a 2px indigo underline. The main area has the greeting
            Welcome back, Mara with Signed in as Mara Okafor and the date in
            mono, then a grid of a wide column and a 340px side column. The
            wide column has a Projects box whose grey header strip reads 6
            active, 4 on track, 1 at risk, 1 behind, then a pink annotation row
            with an octagon reading 4 tasks are overdue and a mono overdue 4.
            Each project is one checks row with a status badge, the name over
            team and mono task count, a ten segment progress bar, a mono
            percent, and the coloured status word with a mono due date. Under
            it an Activity box lists entries like a commit log with square
            initial tiles, item names in grey code chips and mono times below.
            The side column has a This week box of key and value rows split by
            dashed lines with mono figures, the overdue figure red, and a Tasks
            completed box drawn as a two row heat grid of fourteen cells, one
            row per week, Sunday to Saturday, each cell holding its number,
            with week totals 59 and 73 at the right, a green plus 14 note, an
            outlined today cell and a Fewer to More legend. Below 1060px the
            side boxes sit side by side under the main column. Below 720px tabs
            wrap without icons, the button shows only its plus, side boxes
            stack, and each check row wraps to name, bar and percent, then
            status and due date.
        spacing: A 4px base on an 8px rhythm. 24px gutters, 16px box padding, 10px row padding.
        density: Medium high. One line per project like a checks list.
        corners: 6px on boxes, buttons, fields and the avatar. 3px on heat cells and 4px on code chips.
        borders: 1px line on every box with a grey header strip, lighter lines between rows, dashed lines between key and value rows.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            16px line icons at 1.5 stroke on tabs and tools. Status uses solid
            16px badges with a white mark, a circle with a check, a diamond
            with a bang and an octagon with a cross, beside the coloured word.
        focus: A 2px indigo outline offset 2px. A focused field gets an indigo border and a 3px indigo tint ring, and a focused row takes the tint fill.
        tone: Terse and technical, such as 6 active, 4 on track, 1 at risk, 1 behind and overdue 4 in mono.

    style188:
        number: 188
        run: 38
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Design tool
        idea: The dashboard laid out like a design file, white sections floating as frames on a dotted grey canvas between a compact pages panel and a properties inspector, all in tight 11px interface text.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/188.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            canvas: #e4e4e7, the page, with #cfcfd4 dots every 16px
            panel: #ffffff, the toolbar, floating panels and frames
            well: #f4f4f5, filled fields, property values and segmented control tracks
            ink: #1c1c1e, text and the black progress fills
            muted: #5c5c63, labels, column heads and meta
            canvasInk: #52525b, frame labels sitting on the canvas
            line: #d4d4d8, dividers and field edges, with #e4e4e7 for table rows
            selectionBlue: #2a5bd7, the primary button, the selection outline, this week bars, the slider and focus
            blueTint: #e8eefc, the current page, the selected row and the selected layer
            greyBar: #71717a, last week bars
            onTrack: #1d7a46, On track with a filled circle
            atRisk: #8f5600, At risk with a filled triangle
            behind: #c0262d, Behind with a filled square and the overdue pill
        type:
            One stack, system-ui, apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica
            Neue, Arial. Interface text in panels is 11px, headings 11px at 600.
            Inside frames the greeting is 20px at 650, KPI figures 24px at 650
            and minus 0.02em, and table, chart and activity text 12px.
        layout:
            Everything floats on a dotted grey canvas with 12px gaps. A full
            width white toolbar with 10px corners holds a black rounded mark
            and Brightwork, a divider, Workspace / Home, and at the right a
            filled search well, a blue New project button, a bare bell icon and
            a small violet avatar with Mara Okafor. Below it three columns run
            208px, flexible and 248px. The left floating panel has Pages with
            the six nav items as 26px rows, Home in blue tint, then Sections
            listing Greeting, Summary, Projects with Billing migration nested
            and selected, Tasks completed and Activity, each with a tiny hash
            grid mark. The middle is the canvas itself, a six column grid of
            frames, each a white board with a small hash labelled caption above
            it in canvas ink. The Greeting frame spans four columns with Hi
            Mara, the date and a red outlined pill with a square reading 4
            tasks are overdue. The Summary frame is four separate small white
            KPI boards. The Projects frame is a compact table of Name, Team,
            Progress as a thin black bar and percent, Tasks, Due and Status,
            with the Billing migration row selected by a blue tint and a 1.5px
            blue outline. Then Tasks completed spans three columns as two small
            multiple rows of seven columns, last week in grey and this week in
            blue, with the week total at the left of each row and the day under
            the lower row, and Activity spans three columns with coloured
            initial discs and right aligned times. The right floating inspector
            has Project, Tasks and History tabs, the selected name, a three way
            status segment with Behind raised, a progress slider at 30 percent
            with Complete 30 and Tasks 12 of 40, and Details for Team, Due, Days
            left 20 and Remaining 28 as filled value wells. Below 1120px the
            inspector moves under the canvas as three side by side sections.
            Below 760px the pages panel becomes a wrapped row of page names,
            Sections hides, frames stack, KPIs go two by two, the table
            scrolls sideways inside its frame and the inspector stacks last.
        spacing: A 4px base. 12px between floating panels, 20 to 28px between frames, 26px control height, 16px frame padding.
        density: High in the panels, medium inside the frames.
        corners: 10px floating panels, 6px buttons and fields, 5px rows, 4px frames and KPI boards, round avatars.
        borders: Almost none. Fields are filled wells. A 1.5px blue outline marks the selection.
        shadows: Floating panels use a 1px ring at 6 percent black plus soft 4px 12px and 12px 32px shadows. Frames carry only a 1px 2px shadow.
        icons:
            14px line icons at 1.3 stroke in the panels and toolbar. A tiny
            hash grid marks each frame and section. Status uses 8px solid
            shapes, a circle, a triangle and a square, beside the word.
        focus: A 2px selection blue outline offset 1px. A focused field turns white with a blue border, and a focused row takes the blue tint.
        tone: Tool like nouns and short labels, such as Pages, Sections, Selected in Projects and Days left.

    style189:
        number: 189
        run: 39
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Warm minimal
        idea: A calm, paper-like workspace in cream and warm brown, where one terracotta accent marks what to act on, corners are a soft 6px and a humanist sans keeps the tone friendly and unhurried.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/189.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            cream: #f7f1e6, the page and the top bar
            paper: #fffbf4, panels, fields and the style sheet
            ink: #2b2420, headings and body text
            bark: #665548, meta, labels and axis text
            sand: #e4d8c6, 1px lines and the progress track, never text
            terracotta: #a8492a, the primary button, current nav text, this week's line, links and focus
            clay: #f5e3d6, the tint behind the current nav, the overdue figure and avatars
            moss: #2f6a3e, On track with a line circle and check
            ochre: #855300, At risk with a line triangle and bar
            brick: #962a2a, Behind and the overdue figure, with a line square and cross
        type:
            One humanist stack, Seravek, Gill Sans Nova, Ubuntu, Calibri,
            Optima, Candara, DejaVu Sans, sans-serif, in weights 400 and 600.
            The greeting is 34px semibold, KPI figures 30px semibold tabular,
            section titles 19px semibold, body 15px at 1.55, and meta, labels
            and chips 13px.
        layout:
            A cream top bar edged by one sand line holds a terracotta square
            mark with the brand, six text nav links with Home in a clay pill,
            and at right a search field, a terracotta New project button, a
            bell button and the initials disc with Mara Okafor. Content sits
            in a centred 1120px column. The hero row puts the greeting, date
            and an overdue line with a square symbol and a Review them link at
            left, and at right one paper strip split by thin rules into four
            figures with a small icon and label, the overdue cell tinted clay
            with a brick figure. Below, two columns at 7 to 5. The left panel
            lists the six projects as rows with name, team, due date and days
            left, then a 6px bar with percent and tasks, then the status word
            with its line symbol. The right column stacks a line chart panel,
            this week as a solid terracotta line over a faint area with value
            labels and last week as a dashed bark line with square markers,
            totals beneath, and an activity panel with clay initial discs and
            times under each line. Below 1040px everything stacks and the
            search fills the bar. On phones the nav wraps under the brand,
            the New project button shows only its plus, the figures form a 2
            by 2 grid and project bars drop under the name.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px panel padding, 32px between sections and columns, 16px row padding.
        density: Comfortable. Six project rows and six activity items without crowding.
        corners: 6px on panels, buttons, fields, the progress bar and nav pills. Avatars are round.
        borders: 1px sand lines around panels and between rows and figures.
        shadows: One soft warm shadow, 0 1px 2px at 6 percent brown, on panels only.
        icons: Thin 1.6px line icons at 15 to 18px in bark. Status symbols are line shapes in the status colour, a circle with a check, a triangle with a bar and a square with a cross.
        focus: A 2px terracotta outline offset 2px. A focused field also takes a clay fill.
        tone: Warm and plain in sentence case, such as Welcome back, Mara and 4 tasks are overdue.

    style190:
        number: 190
        run: 39
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Cool corporate
        idea: A dependable enterprise console with a strong blue masthead, a light grey shell, crisp 2px corners and every section framed as a tabbed panel, so the dashboard reads like a well-ordered set of files.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/190.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            shell: #eef1f5, the page behind panels
            white: #ffffff, panels, the nav tab bar, table rows and fields
            ink: #1b2533, headings, table text and body
            slate: #4a5768, labels, column heads, meta and axis text
            rule: #cfd6e0, 1px panel borders and table rules, never text
            blue: #1748b8, the masthead, primary button, current tabs, links, this week's bars and focus
            navy: #0f3487, the search well inside the masthead and hover on blue
            ice: #e5ecfa, the current tab fill, last week's bars and hovered rows
            green: #17673a, On track with a solid circle and check
            amber: #874d00, At risk with a solid triangle and bar
            red: #b0231b, Behind, the overdue alert edge and the overdue KPI, with a solid square and cross
        type:
            One stack, Segoe UI, Selawik, Helvetica Neue, Arial, Liberation
            Sans, sans-serif, in weights 400 and 600. The page title is 24px
            semibold, KPI figures 28px semibold tabular, panel titles 15px
            semibold, tabs and body 14px, and column heads 12px semibold caps
            tracked 0.04em.
        layout:
            A full width blue masthead 56px tall holds a white outlined square
            mark with the brand, a wide navy search well, and at right a white
            New project button with blue text, a bell and a white initials disc
            with Mara Okafor. Under it a white bar of six icon tabs, Home with
            a 3px blue underline. The 1280px main area starts with a Home /
            Overview crumb, the greeting and the date at the far right, then a
            white alert bar with a 4px red left edge, a solid red square, the
            overdue line and a View overdue tasks link. A single bordered KPI
            band follows, split into four cells, each with an icon and label,
            the figure and a note, the overdue cell topped by a 3px red rule
            with red figure. Below, two columns at 8 to 4. The left Projects
            panel has a tab strip of team filters with counts, then a six
            column table of project, team, a bar with percent, tasks, due date
            with days left and status, and a footer line with totals and the
            next due project. The right column stacks a Tasks completed panel
            with Daily and Weekly tabs, grouped bars per weekday, last week as
            outlined ice and this week solid blue, and a small table of week
            totals and change, then an Activity panel with All, Comments and
            Files tabs and rows with initials, text and time at right. Below
            1100px the right column moves under the table. On phones the
            search drops to its own line, the nav tabs scroll sideways inside
            their bar, KPIs form a 2 by 2 grid and table rows become stacked
            cards.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px panel padding, 24px between panels, 10px by 16px table cells.
        density: Medium high. A real six column table with rows near 44px.
        corners: 2px on everything. Avatars are round.
        borders: 1px rule borders on every panel, table row and KPI cell. Current tabs carry a 3px blue underline.
        shadows: None. Panels sit flat on the grey shell.
        icons: 1.6px line icons at 18px beside nav tabs and KPI labels. Status uses solid shapes with a white glyph.
        focus: A 2px blue ring outside a 2px white gap, drawn with box shadow. Tabs show an inset 2px blue ring.
        tone: Neutral and precise. Short labels, caps column heads and counts inside tabs.

    style191:
        number: 191
        run: 39
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Bold modern
        idea: A confident, editorial dashboard of black heavy headings and oversized numbers on white, where generous whitespace replaces boxes and a single dark lime accent marks progress, the current page and the primary action.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/191.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            white: #ffffff, the page and fields
            chalk: #f4f4f0, the style sheet band
            black: #0d0d0d, headings, figures, body, the 4px section rules and the secondary button outline
            graphite: #5a5a55, meta, labels, axis text and last week's outlined bars
            hairline: #deded8, 1px row dividers and the empty progress line, never text
            lime: #456300, the one accent, the primary button, current nav bar, progress fills, this week's bars, the brand full stop and focus
            limeWash: #f1f6df, the focused search and field fill
            signal: #b42318, Behind, the overdue figure and its rule, with a solid square and cross
            rust: #8a4b00, At risk with a solid triangle and bar
        type:
            One grotesque stack, Helvetica Neue, Inter, Arial Nova, Arial,
            Liberation Sans, sans-serif, in weights 400, 700 and 800 with tight
            negative tracking on large sizes. The greeting is 96px extra bold
            at minus 0.045em, KPI figures 104px extra bold, section titles
            40px extra bold, project names 24px bold, row percents 56px extra
            bold, body 16px at 1.5, and labels 13px bold caps tracked 0.08em.
        layout:
            No sidebar and no cards. A slim white header holds the bold
            wordmark with a lime full stop, six plain bold word links with Home
            in black over a 4px lime bar, an underlined search field, a lime
            pill New project button, a round outlined bell and a black initials
            disc with Mara Okafor. The hero is a small caps date, a huge Hi,
            Mara. headline and a 28px overdue line with a red square and a See
            them link. Four giant figures follow in a row, each under a 4px
            black rule with a caps label below, the overdue figure red under a
            red rule with a square symbol. Projects run full width under a 4px
            rule with the title at left and totals at right, as numbered rows
            01 to 06 with a big name, a meta line of team, tasks, due date and
            days left, the status word, a giant percent at the far right and a
            4px progress line beneath. The last band splits 7 to 5, a Tasks
            completed block with a giant 73, the change against 59, and 14 bars
            dated 18 to 31, last week outlined graphite and this week solid
            lime, beside an Activity list with caps times in a left column.
            Below 1100px the last band stacks. On phones the nav wraps under
            the wordmark, figures form a 2 by 2 grid at 64px, project rows put
            status and percent on a second line, and the chart scrolls sideways
            inside its block.
        spacing: An 8px unit with big jumps of 24, 48, 80 and 120px. 80px above each section, 24px between project rows.
        density: Low. Few, very large elements, with whitespace doing the grouping.
        corners: Square for rules, bars and fields. Buttons, the bell and avatars are pills or circles.
        borders: 4px black rules above sections and figures, 1px hairlines between activity rows. No boxes.
        shadows: None.
        icons: Almost none. Solid status shapes at 16px and 2px line icons for search, bell and plus.
        focus: A 3px lime outline offset 3px. Fields get a 3px lime underline and a lime wash.
        tone: Short and direct with full stops, such as Hi, Mara. and 4 tasks are overdue.

    style192:
        number: 192
        run: 39
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Soft premium
        idea: A quiet, high-end workspace on pale lavender grey, where floating 16px cards with faint gradients and soft shadows, a serif for headings and generous spacing make the dashboard feel calm and considered.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/192.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            mist: #f2f1f7, the page, a pale lavender grey
            pearl: #ffffff, cards, the rail and fields, fading to #faf9fe at the bottom
            aubergine: #221f33, headings and body text
            heather: #5a5670, meta, labels, eyebrows and axis text
            veil: #e4e1ee, 1px card edges, ring tracks and dividers, never text
            iris: #4f3ca8, the primary button gradient, current nav text, rings, links, this week's bars and focus
            lilac: #ece8fa, the hero gradient start, current nav fill, KPI icon circles and last week's bars
            blush: #f8f0f3, the hero gradient end and the overdue icon circle
            jade: #1e6a4e, On track with a solid circle and check on a pale green pill
            bronze: #874a0e, At risk with a solid triangle and bar on a pale amber pill
            garnet: #a3263d, Behind and overdue, with a solid square and cross on a pale rose pill
        type:
            Two stacks. Headings and figures use Iowan Old Style, Palatino
            Linotype, Palatino, Book Antiqua, Georgia, serif at weight 500.
            Text uses Avenir Next, Avenir, Segoe UI, Helvetica Neue, system-ui,
            sans-serif. The greeting is 40px serif, KPI figures 32px serif,
            card titles 24px serif, project names 17px sans semibold, body
            15px at 1.6, and eyebrows 12px semibold caps tracked 0.12em.
        layout:
            A floating white rail 248px wide, inset 16px with 16px corners,
            holds a gradient rounded mark with the serif brand, six icon and
            label nav items with Home in a lilac pill, and a user tile at the
            bottom with Mara Okafor. The main column opens with a white pill
            search, then a round bell and a gradient pill New project button at
            the right. A wide hero card with a lilac to blush gradient puts the
            caps date, the serif greeting and a white overdue pill with a
            square symbol and Review link at left, and four translucent white
            KPI tiles in a 2 by 2 grid at right, each with an icon in a lilac
            circle, a serif figure and a label, the overdue tile white with a
            garnet figure. Projects follow as six cards in three columns, each
            with a progress ring holding the percent, a caps team eyebrow and
            the name, three facts for tasks, due date and days left, and a
            status pill. The last row splits 3 to 2, a chart card with rounded
            bars for both weeks, last week lilac and this week an iris
            gradient, and three serif totals below, beside an activity card
            with gradient initial discs. Below 1180px project cards go two
            across and the hero stacks. Below 860px the rail becomes a top card
            with nav in a 3 by 2 grid. On phones cards go one across and the
            chart scrolls inside its card.
        spacing: An 8px unit, generous. 24 to 36px card padding, 24px gaps, 40px between rows.
        density: Low. Six project cards, each with three facts.
        corners: 16px cards and rail, 12px tiles, nav items and fields, pills for buttons, search and status chips.
        borders: A 1px veil edge on every card so it holds its shape on mist.
        shadows: Soft and layered, 0 1px 2px at 4 percent ink plus 0 12px 32px at 8 percent iris. The primary button has its own iris glow.
        icons: 1.5px line icons at 18px, KPI icons inside 40px lilac circles. Status uses solid shapes with a white glyph.
        focus: A 1px iris edge inside a 3px iris ring at 35 percent opacity, following the control's corners.
        tone: Gracious and calm, such as Good to see you, Mara.

    style193:
        number: 193
        run: 39
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Nordic neutral
        idea: An airy, Scandinavian workspace of warm stone greys and hairlines, light large numerals and wide margins, with one forest green accent and a quiet due-date timeline that lets the week breathe.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/193.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            stone: #f5f4f1, the page, a warm pale grey
            snow: #fcfcfa, the sidebar, fields and the style sheet
            granite: #262624, headings, figures and body text
            slate: #5d5b56, labels, meta, axis text and last week's rings
            lichen: #d8d5ce, every 1px hairline, timeline tracks and the empty progress line, never text
            forest: #2d5a44, the one accent, the primary button, current nav, progress, due markers, this week's dots and stems, links, On track and focus
            moss: #e6ede8, the focused field fill
            umber: #7b5400, At risk with a line triangle and bar
            rust: #9a3223, Behind and overdue, with a line square and cross
        type:
            One stack, Avenir Next, Helvetica Neue, Segoe UI, system-ui,
            Cantarell, sans-serif. The greeting is 44px light, KPI figures
            48px light tabular, section titles 13px medium caps tracked
            0.14em, project names 16px medium, body 15px at 1.65, and meta
            13px.
        layout:
            A pale snow sidebar 220px wide, edged by one hairline, holds a
            forest dot with the brand, six text nav links with Home marked by
            a 2px forest left line, and Mara Okafor at the bottom over a
            hairline. The main column, with 48px side margins, opens with a
            slim row of the date at left and at right a hairline search box,
            a square bell and a forest New project button, closed by a
            hairline. A light 44px Hello Mara follows, then the overdue line
            with a square symbol and a link. Four light figures sit in a row
            between hairlines, split by vertical hairlines, the overdue figure
            in rust with a square symbol. Projects form a hairline list of four
            columns, name with team, percent beside a 2px progress line over
            tasks, a due-date timeline track from 31 Oct to 15 Jan with month
            ticks and a forest dot at the due date over the date and days left,
            and the status word. An axis of dates sits above the timeline
            column. The last band splits 3 to 2, a lollipop chart pairing
            last week's hollow slate ring and this week's forest dot on thin
            stems per weekday with three light totals below, beside an activity
            list with times in a left column. Below 1100px the last band
            stacks. Below 820px the sidebar becomes a top strip with wrapped
            nav, figures form a 2 by 2 grid, project rows stack with status at
            top right, and the chart scrolls inside its section.
        spacing: An 8px unit, airy. 56px between sections, 20px project row padding, 48px side margins.
        density: Low to medium. One line per project with plenty of air.
        corners: 4px on buttons, fields and the bell, square everywhere else.
        borders: 1px lichen hairlines between rows, sections, figures and along the sidebar. No boxes.
        shadows: None.
        icons: Sparse 1.25px line icons at 18px for search, bell and plus only. Status uses thin line shapes, a circle with a check, a triangle with a bar and a square with a cross.
        focus: A 2px forest outline offset 3px. A focused field also takes a moss fill.
        tone: Calm and understated in short sentences, such as Hello Mara and 4 tasks are overdue.

    style194:
        number: 194
        run: 40
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Written brief
        idea: The dashboard opens with a short written paragraph that states the week in plain sentences, then hands over to one carefully set sortable table, like a briefing memo from a good analyst.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/194.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            paper: #faf8f4, the page behind the brief
            surface: #ffffff, the top bar, the table body, fields and the style sheet
            ink: #1d232b, text, progress fills and the 2px section rules
            slate: #535d6a, meta, notes and axis labels
            rule: #ddd7cc, hairlines between rows, never text
            ruleStrong: #8c8477, the table header rule, field borders and last week bars
            teal: #0d5c63, the primary button, the sorted column, this week bars and focus
            tealTint: #e4efee, the focused or selected table row
            green: #1b6b3a, On track with a solid dot
            amber: #8a5100, At risk with a solid triangle
            red: #a8261f, Behind with a solid square and the overdue phrase
            redTint: #f8e6e3, the highlight behind the overdue phrase
        type:
            Two stacks. Prose and headings use Charter, Bitstream Charter,
            Iowan Old Style, Sitka Text, Cambria, Georgia, serif. Interface text
            uses system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial. The greeting
            is 34px serif regular, the summary paragraph 21px serif at 1.6 with
            figures in bold, fact figures 22px sans semibold tabular, table text
            14px, and section labels 12 to 13px semibold caps tracked 0.08em.
        layout:
            A white top bar holds a square outline mark with the serif brand,
            six text nav links with a 2px teal underline on Home, then a search
            field, a teal New project button, a square bell and initials with
            Mara Okafor. Content sits in one centred 1040px column. A caps
            dateline and the serif greeting lead into a written paragraph that
            opens with a red tinted clock phrase for the 4 overdue tasks and
            names totals and the two troubled projects in sentences. Under it a
            ruled facts line shows the four summary numbers inline, split by
            thin vertical rules. The table follows with a caps heading, a note
            that it is sorted by due date, and a segmented filter of All 6,
            Needs attention 2 and On track 4. Columns are Project with team,
            Status, Progress as a thin ink bar with percent, Tasks done, Due and
            Days left, with sort buttons in a warm header row and Due marked
            ascending. Troubled rows carry a 3px red or amber inset edge and a
            footer row totals 78 of 170. Below, a 5 to 7 split puts a paired bar
            chart of last week and this week by weekday beside an activity list
            with times in a left column, each topped by a 2px ink rule. Below
            1000px the nav moves to its own scrolling row and the lower band
            stacks. On phones table rows become ruled cards with name and
            status on top, the bar, then tasks, due and days left.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px cell padding and 40 to 48px between the brief, the table and the lower band.
        density: Medium. Prose and facts carry the headline and one table carries the detail.
        corners: Nearly square. 3px on controls and nothing on the table, tracks or swatches.
        borders: Warm 1px hairlines between rows, a stronger rule under the table header and a 2px ink rule over the chart and activity.
        shadows: None. Depth comes only from paper against white.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.6px and 18px for search, bell, plus and sort
            arrows. Status uses small solid shapes beside the word, a dot for
            On track, a triangle for At risk and a square for Behind, and the
            overdue phrase carries a clock.
        focus: A solid 2px teal outline offset 2px, and a teal tint plus outline on a focused table row.
        tone: Full sentences in the brief and short nouns in the table, such as Days left and Needs attention 2.

    style195:
        number: 195
        run: 40
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Sectioned report
        idea: The home screen reads as a numbered status report on a white sheet, with large light section numerals in the margin and a sticky contents list on the left, so the week can be read top to bottom or jumped to by section.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/195.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            desk: #eef0f3, the page behind the sheet and the contents rail
            sheet: #ffffff, the report sheet, the header and fields
            ink: #16202e, text, the heavy rules and the nav band
            muted: #4f5b6b, labels, refs and meta
            rule: #d5dae1, row hairlines, never text
            navy: #1f3a68, the primary button, the current nav item, the this week line and focus
            navyTint: #e6ebf3, initials and the focused row
            numeral: #5a6b8c, the large section numerals and the last week line
            green: #1e6b45, On track with a check in a circle
            amber: #8f4f00, At risk with a bang in a triangle
            red: #a3222b, Behind with a cross in an octagon and overdue figures
        type:
            One sans stack, Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, Liberation Sans,
            system-ui, with ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas for refs.
            Section numerals are 56px light at minus 0.04em, the greeting 40px
            bold at minus 0.02em, summary figures 44px light tabular, section
            titles 22px bold, body 15px at 1.55, refs 12px mono and table
            labels 11px bold caps tracked 0.1em.
        layout:
            A white header row holds a navy square B mark with the brand, a
            square search field, a navy New project button, a square bell with
            a red count and an initials square with Mara Okafor. Beneath it a
            full width ink band carries six caps nav links with Home filled
            navy. The body is a 220px contents rail and a white report sheet on
            the grey desk. The rail has a Contents label, a numbered list of
            Summary, Projects, Needs attention, Throughput and Activity with a
            3px navy edge on the current item, and a note that the report is
            for the week ending 31 Oct and prepared for Mara Okafor. It stays
            sticky while the sheet scrolls. The sheet opens with a caps
            eyebrow, the greeting and a lede that starts with the red overdue
            clause, closed by a 3px ink rule. Each section is a two column row
            with a large light numeral under a 3px navy cap in a 72px margin,
            and a heading under a 1px ink rule. Section 1 shows the four
            figures in a row split by thin rules. Section 2 is a ledger table
            with refs 2.1 to 2.6, team, status, percent with an outlined meter,
            tasks and due, and a total row. Section 3 lists numbered findings
            for the overdue tasks and the two troubled projects with derived
            remaining tasks and target pace. Section 4 overlays this week as a
            solid navy line with dots on last week as a dashed line with
            squares, beside a totals list. Section 5 is a when, who and what
            log. Below 1080px the contents become a horizontal tab row above
            the sheet, and on phones numerals sit above headings and the
            ledger scrolls inside its own frame.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 40px above each section, 56px sheet padding and 24px between numeral and text.
        density: Medium. Reading pace, with one idea per numbered section.
        corners: Square everywhere.
        borders: A 3px ink rule under the report head, a 3px navy cap over each numeral, 1px ink over each heading and ledger head, and 1px grey between rows.
        shadows: None. The white sheet sits on the grey desk with a 1px border.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.5px with square caps. Status is an outline check
            circle, bang triangle or crossed octagon beside its word, and
            overdue uses a clock.
        focus: A solid 2px navy outline offset 2px with a white gap ring, and a navy tint on a focused ledger row.
        tone: Report voice with refs, such as 3.2 Billing migration, Total and Change.

    style196:
        number: 196
        run: 40
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Mini dashboards
        idea: Every project gets its own small dashboard tile, with a status chip, a sparkline of this week's completions and three stats in a ruled footer, so the home screen reads as a wall of six comparable instruments.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/196.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            canvas: #f1f3f7, the page behind the tiles
            tile: #ffffff, tiles, the rail, panels and fields
            ink: #182033, text and figures
            muted: #556075, labels, meta and axis text
            line: #dfe3ea, tile borders and stat dividers, never text
            violet: #5b3fc4, the primary button, sparklines, this week bars, progress edges and focus
            violetTint: #efebfc, the current nav item, sparkline areas and last week bar fills
            green: #18794e, On track with a check disc on #e3f3ea
            amber: #8a5a00, At risk with a diamond on #fbf0d9
            red: #c0272d, Behind with a down triangle and overdue figures on #fbe7e7
        type:
            One stack, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Ubuntu, Helvetica Neue,
            Arial. The greeting is 22px bold, strip figures 22px bold tabular,
            tile stats 20px bold with a 12px muted unit, tile names 16px bold,
            body 14px, and stat labels 11px semibold caps tracked 0.04em.
        layout:
            An 80px white icon rail on the left holds a violet square logo of
            four tiles, six nav items with an icon over a small label, Home in
            a violet tint, and initials at the foot. The main area opens with
            a greeting line that holds Hello, Mara, the brand, the date and a
            red clock note for the 4 overdue tasks, with a search field, a
            violet New project button, a bell and Mara Okafor at the right. A
            single white strip splits the four summary numbers into cells with
            tinted icon squares, the overdue cell red. The projects band is a
            three by two grid of tiles in due date order. Each tile has the
            team label, the project name and a status chip on top, then a
            violet sparkline of tasks done per day this week beside a large
            violet count of done this week, then a ruled three cell footer of
            Complete, Tasks and Due with days left, and a 4px progress edge
            along the base in violet, amber or red. Below, a two to one split
            puts a 14 day bar chart, last week as outlined tint bars and this
            week as solid violet split by a dashed divider with values on top,
            beside an activity panel with coloured initial discs. Below 1100px
            tiles go two across, and on phones the rail becomes a scrolling top
            bar and tiles stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px gaps between and inside tiles and 24px between bands.
        density: Medium high. Six instruments at once, each with a chart and three numbers.
        corners: 12px tiles and panels, 10px controls and rail items, 6px chips and 3px bars.
        borders: A 1px cool grey border on every tile, ruled stat footers and a 4px progress edge at the base.
        shadows: One soft pair, 0 1px 2px and 0 2px 8px at 5 to 6 percent ink.
        icons:
            Round line icons at 1.8px with labels in the rail. Status is a
            solid check disc, diamond with a bang or down triangle in a tinted
            chip with its word.
        focus: A solid 2px violet outline offset 2px, and a violet tint on a focused list row.
        tone: Instrument labels, such as Complete, Tasks, Due 14 Nov and 7 done this week.

    style197:
        number: 197
        run: 40
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Triage first
        idea: The home screen is an inbox for problems, where a red headed Needs attention list leads with overdue, behind and at risk work and offers the next action on each row, while the healthy projects follow as a quiet table and the week's numbers sit in a right rail.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/197.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #f6f7f8, the page behind the boxes
            card: #ffffff, boxes, the tab bar and fields
            ink: #1c2026, text
            muted: #5a616b, hints, meta and axis text
            line: #d9dce1, borders, never text
            graphite: #24292f, the header, action buttons and this week bars
            headText: #e6e9ed, text on the graphite header
            lastWeek: #7d848f, last week bars
            focus: #0b5cd5, the focus ring only
            green: #1a7f45, On track with a check disc
            amber: #8a4b00, At risk with a triangle on #fff5e0
            red: #b42318, Behind with a chevron square and overdue with a clock on #fdf0ef
        type:
            One stack, Segoe UI, system-ui, Roboto, Noto Sans, Helvetica Neue,
            Arial. The greeting is 20px bold, KPI figures 18px bold tabular,
            triage titles 15px bold, body 14px at 1.45, facts and feed 13px, and
            buttons and tags 12 to 13px at 600 to 700.
        layout:
            A graphite header bar holds a white hexagon mark with the brand, a
            dark search field, a white New project button, an outlined bell
            with a red count and initials with Mara Okafor. A white tab bar
            beneath it carries the six nav links with a graphite underline on
            Home. A one line greeting with the date says the 4 overdue tasks
            lead the list. The body splits into a wide left column and a 340px
            right rail. On the left, the Needs attention box has a red tinted
            head with a triangle and a count of 3. Its rows each carry a 4px
            red or amber left edge, a 24px solid severity glyph, a title with
            an outlined status tag, one line of detail with a mini bar, a line
            of facts such as days left, tasks to go and target pace, and two
            buttons at the right, a graphite primary and an outlined secondary
            such as Review tasks and Reassign, Open and Change date, or Open and
            Message team. Under it an On track box with a green check and a
            count of 4 is a quiet table of the healthy projects with progress,
            due with days left, status and an Open button. The right rail
            stacks a This week list of the four numbers with overdue first in
            red, a compact 14 day bar chart with grey last week and graphite
            this week, and the activity feed. Below 1060px the rail drops under
            the main column in two columns, and on phones everything stacks and
            buttons wrap under each triage row.
        spacing: 4px and 8px steps. 12 to 16px row padding and 20px between boxes.
        density: High. Compact 34px controls and 14px text, built for working through a list.
        corners: 6px on boxes, buttons and fields, and 4px on tags.
        borders: 1px grey boxes, with a 4px left edge in the severity colour on every triage row.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            Solid 24px severity glyphs lead each triage row, a clock disc for
            overdue, a chevron square for Behind and a triangle for At risk.
            Status tags are outlined and hold a solid check disc, triangle or
            chevron square plus the word. Line icons at 1.8px elsewhere.
        focus: A solid 2px blue outline offset 2px, light blue on the dark header.
        tone: Direct and action led, such as Review tasks, Change date and No action needed.

    style198:
        number: 198
        run: 40
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Asymmetric feature
        idea: A 12 column asymmetric grid gives one project the stage, a large navy feature card with a progress ring and its key figures, while a tall watch card, four small project cards, a chart and the activity feed support it at smaller sizes.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/198.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #f4f4f1, the warm grey behind the cards
            card: #ffffff, cards, the sidebar and fields
            ink: #1c2333, text and figures
            muted: #5b6170, labels, meta and axis text
            navy: #14213d, the feature card, the current nav item and the this week line
            navySoft: #e8ebf2, bar tracks, the this week chart band and initials
            onNavyMuted: #b9c2d6, labels on the feature card
            coral: #c2410c, the New project button and the focus ring
            coralLight: #ffb38a, the ring arc and focus on navy
            series: #6f7fa3, the dashed last week line
            green: #1d7a4a, On track with a solid dot on #e6f4ec
            amber: #8d5000, At risk with a solid triangle on #fdf1dc
            red: #b3261e, Behind with a solid square and overdue on #fdecea
            redOnNavy: #ffb4ab, the outlined Behind tag inside the feature
        type:
            Display figures and headings use Avenir Next, Avenir, Segoe UI
            Variable Display, Segoe UI, system-ui. Text uses system-ui, Segoe
            UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial. The ring figure is 56px bold at
            minus 0.04em, the greeting 44px bold at minus 0.03em, the feature
            title 36px bold, card figures 26 to 28px bold, body 15px, and
            eyebrows 12px bold caps tracked 0.08em.
        layout:
            A floating white sidebar card with 20px corners holds the brand
            with a navy rounded mark, six nav items with icons where Home is a
            filled navy pill, and Mara Okafor with initials in a coral disc at
            the foot. The main column has a pill search, a round bell and a
            coral pill New project button. Then a 12 column grid with 20px
            gutters. Row one gives 8 columns to the date, a 44px greeting and a
            red clock line for the 4 overdue tasks, and 4 columns to a two by
            two summary card. Row two gives 8 columns to the navy feature card
            for Billing migration, with a Featured project kicker and an
            outlined Behind tag, a 180px coral ring showing 30 percent at left,
            and at right the title, team and due date, a two by two grid of
            tasks done, to go, days left and target pace, a tinted note of the
            latest activity and white and outlined pill buttons. The other 4
            columns hold a tall Also watching card for Mobile app 2.0 with a
            large percent, an amber bar, ruled facts and an outlined Open
            button. Row three is four 3 column cards for the healthy projects,
            each with a status chip, name, team, a large percent, a bar and
            tasks and due. Row four gives 7 columns to an area line chart with
            the this week half on a tinted band and 5 columns to activity.
            Below 1180px the feature and watch cards go full width and project
            cards go two across. On phones the sidebar becomes a top card with
            a scrolling pill nav and everything stacks.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 20px card padding, 28 to 32px inside the feature and 20px gutters.
        density: Low at the top, rising toward the small cards and the feed.
        corners: 20px on the feature and sidebar, 14px on cards, pills for buttons, search and chips, and 12px fields.
        borders: Almost none. 1px warm lines divide the summary cells and the watch facts.
        shadows: A soft lift on cards of 0 1px 2px and 0 8px 24px at low navy. The feature has a deep 0 20px 48px navy shadow.
        icons:
            Round line icons at 1.7px in the sidebar and header. Status chips
            use a solid dot, triangle or square with the word, and overdue uses
            a clock.
        focus: A solid 3px coral outline offset 3px, light coral on the navy feature.
        tone: Editorial and warm, such as Featured project, Also watching and Plan catch-up.

    style199:
        number: 199
        run: 41
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Ink header band
        idea: A strong ink-navy header band carries the navigation, the greeting and the four headline figures, and a quiet light body below holds the work.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/199.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            ink: #142030, the header band and the primary button
            inkRaised: #1d2b3e, the search field on the band
            inkLine: #3a4d66, rules and outlines on the band
            onInk: #ffffff, headings, figures and the current nav on the band
            onInkMuted: #b9c5d4, labels, the date and idle nav on the band
            coral: #ffab99, the overdue line and overdue figure on the band
            page: #f4f5f7, the light body
            surface: #ffffff, panels and the style sheet
            line: #dce1e7, panel borders and row rules
            text: #17202b, body text
            muted: #535e6d, meta and table headings
            blue: #1f5bbf, links, progress fills, this week bars and focus
            lastWeek: #7f8a9b, last week bars
            ok: #1a6f3f, On track with a check circle
            risk: #8a5000, At risk with a triangle
            behind: #b0261c, Behind with a crossed square
        type:
            One stack, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica
            Neue, Arial, sans-serif. The greeting is 40px bold at minus 0.02em
            on the band, band figures 44px at 650 with tabular numbers, panel
            titles 16px bold, row names 15px at 650, body 15px at 1.5, table
            headings 12px caps at 0.06em and meta 13px.
        layout:
            A full width ink band runs across the top. Its first row, under a
            thin rule, holds a white square B mark with the brand, six nav links
            with Home underlined in white, a dark search field, a white New
            project button, an outlined bell and the initials disc with Mara
            Okafor. Below sit the date, a large white greeting and a coral line
            with a clock saying 4 tasks are overdue plus a Review overdue tasks
            link, with a small right aligned note of 78 of 170 tasks done. The
            band ends with four figures in a row split by vertical rules, each a
            small label, a big number and a note, the overdue one coral with a
            clock. The light body below is a two column grid. The wide left
            column is a white bordered panel with a five column projects table
            of name and team, a thin progress bar with percent, tasks, due date
            with days left and status. The narrow right column stacks a chart
            panel with three totals over grouped bars, last week and this week
            side by side for each weekday, and an activity panel of rows with
            initials discs. Below 1000px the nav drops to its own row and the
            body stacks. On phones the figures become a two by two grid and
            table rows turn into stacked cards.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 32px gutters, 24px between panels, 20px panel padding and 40px above the greeting.
        density: Medium. The band is spacious and the body is a compact six row table.
        corners: 6px on panels, buttons and fields, 3px bars, round avatars.
        borders: 1px #dce1e7 around panels and between rows. 1px #3a4d66 rules on the band.
        shadows: None. Depth comes only from the dark band over the light body.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.8 stroke sized to the text. Status words in colour
            with a check circle, a triangle or a crossed square, and a clock
            for overdue.
        focus: A 2px blue outline offset 2px in the body and a 2px white outline on the band.
        tone: Plain and direct, such as Projects, 4 tasks are overdue and Review overdue tasks.

    style200:
        number: 200
        run: 41
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Page tabs
        idea: A white workspace organised by page tabs, Overview, Projects and Activity, with segmented controls for views, a single stat strip and compact teal-accented cards.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/200.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #ffffff, the workspace and cards
            subtle: #f6f7f8, the search field and the style sheet
            segment: #eceef1, the segmented control track and tab counts
            line: #dfe2e6, card borders, the stat strip and the tab rule
            text: #1c1f24, body text and the current nav item
            muted: #5d646e, labels, idle tabs and meta
            teal: #0e6b63, the current tab, primary button, this week bars and focus
            tealSoft: #e2f1ef, avatars and the current tab count
            lastWeek: #7b9894, last week bars
            ok: #1b7543, On track outlined tag with a check circle
            risk: #885200, At risk outlined tag with a triangle
            behind: #b3261e, Behind tag with a crossed square and the overdue figure
            behindSoft: #fbe9e7, the overdue chip
        type:
            One stack, Segoe UI Variable Text, Segoe UI, system-ui, -apple-system,
            Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial, sans-serif. The
            greeting is 24px at 650, stat values 28px at 650 tabular, card
            titles 15px at 650, tabs 14px with the current one at 650, body
            14px at 1.5, segments 12.5px and bar values 11px.
        layout:
            A 56px white app bar with a bottom rule holds a teal round B mark
            and the brand, six nav links with Home underlined in dark text, a
            grey search field with a slash key hint, a teal New project button,
            a bell and the initials disc with the name. Under it the page head
            shows a small Home crumb, the greeting, the date and a pale red
            overdue chip with a clock. A tab row follows with Overview current
            in teal with a teal underline, then Projects and Activity each with
            a count pill. The Overview content starts with one bordered stat
            strip split into four cells by vertical rules, each an icon label
            and a value with a short grey note, overdue in red. Next a two to
            one row puts a chart card on the left, with a Daily and Weekly
            segmented control, week totals and fourteen bars with values on
            top and a rule between the weeks, beside a dense activity card
            with times right aligned. Last comes a projects card with a Cards
            and List segmented control and a three by two grid of small
            bordered project cards. Below 1100px the nav moves to a second row,
            the cards go two across and the chart row stacks. On phones the
            strip is two by two and the cards stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px gutters and gaps, 16 to 20px card padding and 12px between project cards.
        density: Compact. 14px body, 34px controls and a value printed on every bar.
        corners: 8px cards and the stat strip, 6px buttons and fields, 7px segment track and 4px tags.
        borders: 1px #dfe2e6 on every card. The stat strip is one bordered box split by vertical rules. Status tags are outlined in their own colour.
        shadows: Only the selected segment gets 0 1px 2px. Cards are flat.
        icons:
            18px line icons at 1.8 stroke on stat labels and the bar. Status
            tags use a check circle, a triangle or a crossed square with the
            word.
        focus: A 2px teal outline offset 2px. A segment shows its focus on the inner pill.
        tone: Short labels, such as Overview, Recent activity, Daily and Weekly.

    style201:
        number: 201
        run: 41
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Floating panels
        idea: White panels float with soft, wide shadows over a tinted blue-grey page, steered from a collapsed icon rail, so every block reads as its own lifted surface.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/201.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #dde4ed, the tinted blue-grey page behind every panel
            panel: #ffffff, floating panels, the rail and the top bar
            well: #eff3f7, pill fields, chips and secondary buttons inside panels
            hair: #e6ebf1, hairlines inside panels and chart gridlines
            text: #1b2533, text and the brand tile
            muted: #536071, labels, meta and idle rail icons
            blue: #2c50c8, the current rail item, primary button, this week line, rings and focus
            blueSoft: #e7ecfb, the this week area, the delta chip and avatars
            lastWeek: #6f7c8e, the dashed last week line
            ok: #1d7446, On track with a check circle
            risk: #895300, At risk with a triangle
            behind: #b02a2a, Behind with a crossed square and overdue
            behindSoft: #fbeaea, the Behind chip
        type:
            Text uses SF Pro Text, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto,
            Helvetica Neue, Arial, sans-serif. Figures and the greeting use
            ui-rounded, SF Pro Rounded, Segoe UI, system-ui. The greeting is
            28px bold, the chart total 34px bold, KPI figures 32px bold, panel
            titles 15px at 650, body 14.5px at 1.5 and meta 13px.
        layout:
            A 72px wide white rail floats at the left with 20px rounded corners,
            holding a dark B tile and six icon only links named by their
            labels, Home as a filled blue tile, Settings pushed to the bottom.
            To its right a floating top bar holds a wide pill search, a blue
            pill New project button, a round bell and a pill with the initials
            disc and name. The greeting sits straight on the tinted page with
            the date above it, and a white floating pill with a red clock says
            4 tasks are overdue at the right. Below, a main column and a 340px
            side column. The main column floats a chart panel with a big 73,
            a delta chip and a line chart over fourteen dated days, last week
            dashed grey and this week solid blue over a soft area, then a
            projects panel of rows with a progress ring holding the percent,
            name with team and due date, tasks and a pill status. The side
            column floats a This week panel with the four figures in a two by
            two grid split by hairlines, then an activity panel. Below 1080px
            the side panels move above the main column. Below 860px the rail
            becomes a horizontal floating bar of icons on top.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 20px between all panels and around the page, 20 to 22px panel padding.
        density: Comfortable. Two working columns, about eight blocks on a wide screen.
        corners: 18 to 20px panels, 13px rail tiles, full pills for fields, buttons and chips.
        borders: None on panels. Only 1px #e6ebf1 hairlines inside panels between rows and KPI cells.
        shadows: Every panel uses 0 1px 2px plus a wide 0 12px 32px, both blue-grey at 6 and 11 percent.
        icons:
            22px line icons alone in the rail, each named by its link label.
            Status chips use a check circle, a triangle or a crossed square
            with the word.
        focus: A 3px blue outline offset 2px on every control and field.
        tone: Light and conversational, such as This week, See all and +14 on last week.

    style202:
        number: 202
        run: 41
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Outline only
        idea: Every component is drawn as a crisp 1px outline in black or blue on white paper, with no fills and no shadows, so structure comes from line alone.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/202.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            paper: #ffffff, the page, nothing is ever filled
            black: #111111, text, every outline and the last week bars
            gray: #585858, mono captions, axis labels and meta
            rule: #bdbdbd, row rules inside tables and chart gridlines
            blue: #1546c4, the current nav, primary button, overdue, Behind, this week hatch and focus
        type:
            Text uses Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif. Figures,
            captions and section titles use ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo,
            Consolas, Liberation Mono, monospace. The greeting is 36px regular
            at minus 0.02em, KPI figures 44px light, row names 15px at 600,
            body 15px, section titles 12px mono caps at 0.1em, captions 11px
            mono caps grey and table figures 13px mono.
        layout:
            A single outlined top bar is split into cells by vertical rules,
            the outlined B mark with the brand, a wide search cell, a cell with
            a blue outlined New project button, a square bell cell and the
            outlined initials circle with the name. Below, a 200px left nav is
            a ruled outlined list with icons, Home in blue with an inset blue
            outline and an arrow. The main column starts with the date in mono
            caps, a large light greeting and a blue clock with 4 tasks are
            overdue and a Show overdue link. Four KPI cells share collapsed
            1px borders in one row, the overdue cell in blue with an inset blue
            outline. A full width outlined projects table follows, with mono
            caps headings, name and team, an outlined progress track holding a
            blue hatched bar, mono tasks, due date with days left and an
            outlined status tag. The bottom row pairs a chart box, with a
            three cell totals strip and open black bars for last week beside
            blue hatched bars for this week on a ruled axis, and an activity
            box drawn as a vertical line through outlined initial circles.
            Below 960px the nav becomes a three by two ruled grid and the
            bottom row stacks. On phones the top bar becomes three rows and
            table rows turn into stacked cards.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px page padding and gaps, 32px between main blocks and 12 to 16px inside cells.
        density: Medium. A full width ruled table with values set in mono.
        corners: Square everywhere. Only avatars and the timeline circles are round.
        borders: 1px #111111 on every component with shared edges collapsed into one rule, 1px #bdbdbd between rows, and a blue inset second outline for the current or urgent item.
        shadows: None and no fills. Progress and this week bars use a 1px blue diagonal hatch.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.6 to 1.8 stroke in currentColor. Status tags use a
            check circle, a triangle or a crossed square with the word, and
            Behind is doubled in blue.
        focus: A 2px blue outline offset 2px, drawn inside the cell for top bar cells and nav items.
        tone: Terse and technical, such as Due this week, 14 d left and Show overdue.

    style203:
        number: 203
        run: 41
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Tonal blocks
        idea: Each section is a soft block of its own muted colour, sand, sage, sky, rose and lilac, separated only by space, with no outlines or shadows anywhere.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/203.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #f8f6f1, the warm page between blocks
            deep: #2e3f3a, the header block
            deepRaised: #415550, the search field and bell on the header
            onDeepMuted: #cfdcd7, idle nav and the placeholder on the header
            sand: #ede4d4, the greeting block, current nav, header button and fields
            sage: #dde7da, the chart block and the active projects block
            sageBand: #ccdac8, the last week band inside the chart
            sky: #dce6ef, the projects block and the tasks due block
            skyRow: #eaf0f6, project rows inside the sky block
            lilac: #e7e1ef, the activity block and the hours block
            rose: #f3dedb, the overdue block and the overdue line
            text: #1e2522, text
            muted: #4a524e, labels and meta on every tone
            accent: #2b5a4d, the primary button and this week bars
            lastWeek: #5e7560, last week bars on the sage band
            skyInk: #284f78, progress fill on the sky track
            ok: #21613c, On track on #d4e6d5 with a check circle
            risk: #774800, At risk on #f2e2c4 with a triangle
            behind: #9e261d, Behind on #f3d6d2 with a crossed square and overdue
        type:
            Body uses system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica
            Neue, Arial, sans-serif. Headings and figures use Charter,
            Bitstream Charter, Sitka Text, Cambria, Georgia, serif. The
            greeting is 38px serif at 600, KPI figures 44px serif, block titles
            22px serif, row names 15px sans at 650, body 15px at 1.55 and meta
            13px.
        layout:
            A deep green header block with rounded corners holds a sand B tile
            with the serif brand, six pill nav links with Home on a sand pill,
            a darker pill search, a sand New project pill, a round bell and
            the initials disc. The first row splits five to seven. On the left
            a tall sand greeting block has the date and a serif greeting at
            top and a rose inner block at the bottom with a clock, 4 tasks are
            overdue and a Review them link. On the right four KPI blocks sit
            two by two, sage, sky, rose and lilac, each a small icon label over
            a big serif figure, overdue in red with a clock. The second row
            splits eight to four. A sky projects block lists six lighter sky
            rows, each with name and team, percent and tasks over a tonal
            progress bar, due date with days left and a tinted status tag. A
            lilac activity block lists entries with lilac initial discs. The
            last row is a full width sage chart block with serif totals 73, 59
            and +14 on the left and two tonal week bands on the right, last
            week bars in muted green and this week bars in deep green. Below
            1100px the rows stack. On phones project rows wrap and the week
            bands stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px between blocks, 24 to 32px inside blocks and 8px between rows inside a block.
        density: Comfortable and calm. Large serif figures and one subject per block.
        corners: 14px blocks, 10px inner rows and bands, full pills for nav, search and buttons.
        borders: None at all. Blocks and rows are told apart by tone and space only.
        shadows: None. Depth is only a step lighter or darker in tone.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.8 stroke beside block labels. Status tags are
            tinted with a check circle, a triangle or a crossed square and the
            word.
        focus: A 2px deep green outline offset 3px, white on the header block.
        tone: Warm and plain, such as Review them, All activity and more than last week.

    style204:
        number: 204
        run: 42
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Serif professional
        idea: A calm report-like workspace where a modern serif carries headings and every figure, a plain sans carries the interface, and ruled lines replace cards.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/204.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            paper: #fbfaf7, the page background
            surface: #ffffff, the masthead, fields and swatch cards
            ink: #1f2430, text, heavy rules and progress fills
            muted: #5a5f6b, labels, meta lines and captions
            rule: #dcd8cf, hairlines between rows, never text
            navy: #23407a, the primary button, links, focus and this week bars
            mist: #b9c3d6, last week bars, never text
            pine: #1e6b47, On track with a filled circle
            ochre: #8a5300, At risk with a filled triangle
            brick: #a3262a, Behind with a crossed square and the overdue count
        type:
            Two stacks. Headings, project names and every figure use Charter,
            Bitstream Charter, Sitka Text, Cambria, Georgia, serif with lining
            tabular numerals. The interface uses system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto,
            Helvetica Neue, Arial, sans-serif. KPI figures are 44px serif
            regular, the greeting 40px serif regular, the lede 19px serif in
            muted ink, section titles 22px serif semibold, project names 18px
            serif semibold, body 15px sans, meta 13px sans and the dateline 13px
            sans capitals tracked 0.08em.
        layout:
            A white masthead holds the serif brand, a search field, the New
            project button, a square bell and the user, with the six nav links
            as a text row underneath where Home has a 2px ink underline. The
            content is one centred column up to 1200px. A caps dateline, the
            serif greeting and a serif lede naming the 4 overdue tasks in brick
            open the page. The four KPIs sit in one ruled row with a 2px ink
            rule above, a hairline below and hairline dividers, no boxes, each
            with a small label, a big serif figure and a note. Below, two
            columns at about 1.75 to 1. The left holds Projects as a ruled
            list, each row with the serif name and team and task count, a thin
            ink progress bar with its percent, and the status word with its
            due date. The right holds Tasks completed with three serif totals
            and a two tone bar chart, then Recent activity as a ruled list with
            task names in serif italics. Below 900px the columns stack and the
            KPIs become two by two. On phones the search drops to its own row
            and each project row puts its progress bar under the name.
        spacing: An 8px unit. Rows have 16px padding, columns 24 to 48px gaps, sections 40 to 48px apart.
        density: Medium. Roomy rows of about 72px, read top to bottom like a report.
        corners: 4px on buttons and fields only. Lists and figures have no boxes.
        borders: A 2px ink rule opens the figures and the style sheet, a 1px ink rule sits under each section title, and 1px warm hairlines divide rows.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            Thin 1.6px outline icons at 18px for search, bell and plus. Status
            marks are solid shapes in the status colour beside the word, a
            circle for On track, a triangle for At risk and a square with a
            white cross for Behind.
        focus: A 2px navy outline offset 3px. Fields get a navy border plus a 1px navy ring. A focused list row gets a 2px navy outline.
        tone: Measured full sentences, such as Good morning, Mara and Everything else is moving.

    style205:
        number: 205
        run: 42
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Condensed efficient
        idea: A tight operations console where condensed uppercase headings save width, 32px rows fit everything on one screen, and a slim icon rail keeps the canvas wide.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/205.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #f2f4f5, the canvas behind panels
            panel: #ffffff, panels, the rail, the top bar and fields
            header: #e7ebed, panel title bars and the table footer
            ink: #172026, text, the avatar tile and the chart baseline
            muted: #4f5b63, column heads, times and labels
            line: #d3d9dd, borders and row rules, never text
            teal: #0b6466, the primary button, links, the current rail item and this week bars
            tealTint: #e0eff0, the current rail item and a focused row
            haze: #a9bcc0, last week bars, never text
            green: #19663e, On track with a check
            amber: #855000, At risk with a diamond holding a bang
            red: #b0222a, Behind with a down triangle and the overdue alert
        type:
            Headings, labels, buttons, project names and KPI values use Roboto
            Condensed, Arial Narrow, Helvetica Neue Condensed, sans-serif with
            font-stretch condensed. Body text uses Roboto, Segoe UI, system-ui,
            Arial, sans-serif. KPI values are 22px condensed bold, the greeting
            18px condensed bold, project names 14px condensed bold, panel
            titles 13px condensed bold capitals tracked 0.06em, column heads
            and rail labels 11px condensed bold capitals, body 13px.
        layout:
            A 64px white icon rail on the left holds a teal B tile and six nav
            items, each an icon over an 11px caps label, the current one with a
            3px teal left edge and teal tint. A 48px top bar holds the caps
            breadcrumb Brightwork slash Home, the search field, the New project
            button, a bell with a red count of 4 and the user. Under it one
            white strip holds the greeting, the date, a red tinted overdue
            alert and, pushed right, the four KPIs inline as caps label then
            big value with hairline dividers. Below, a grid of the projects
            panel and a 340px right column. The projects panel is a zebra
            table with Project, Team, Progress bar and percent, Tasks, Due,
            Days left and Status, plus a totals footer. The right column
            stacks a compact two tone bar chart with a dashed divider between
            the weeks and three inline totals, then the activity log with a
            caps time column. Every panel has a grey 32px caps title bar.
            Below 1080px the right column moves under the table. Below 700px
            the rail becomes a top strip of icons, the KPIs a two by two
            grid, and the table scrolls inside its panel.
        spacing: A 4px unit. Gaps of 8 and 12px, 10px cell padding.
        density: High. 32px rows, 32px controls and a 48px top bar.
        corners: 2px on everything.
        borders: 1px cool grey around every panel, grey title bars and zebra rows.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            2px stroke outline icons at 16 to 18px. Status uses a square ended
            check for On track, a filled diamond with a white bang for At risk
            and a filled down triangle for Behind, always with the caps word.
        focus: A 2px teal outline offset 1px. Fields get a teal border and an inset teal ring. Rows get an inset teal outline and the teal tint.
        tone: Terse caps labels, such as Due this week, Days left and Latest 6.

    style206:
        number: 206
        run: 42
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Executive large
        idea: A dashboard built for a thirty second read by a manager, with 18px text, huge numbers, one idea per row and lots of air.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/206.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            linen: #f6f5f2, the page background and resting rows
            white: #ffffff, cards, the top bar and the style sheet
            ink: #1a1d1c, text and big numbers
            slate: #555b59, labels and secondary lines
            forest: #0d5c4a, the primary button, links, progress, focus and this week bars
            sage: #e3efeb, the current nav pill, activity avatars and a focused row
            lichen: #b5c9c3, last week bars, never text
            green: #1b6b3f, On track on #e6f2ea with a circle and check
            amber: #8a4f00, At risk on #fbf0dd with a triangle and bang
            red: #ab2328, Behind and the overdue callout on #fcecea with an octagon and bar
        type:
            One stack, Inter, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
            Arial, sans-serif. Base text is 18px at 1.55. The greeting is 56px
            at weight 750 tracked minus 0.025em, the overdue number 64px extra
            bold, KPI values 52px, project percents 44px, section titles 32px
            bold, card titles 24px bold and labels 17px in slate.
        layout:
            A white top bar holds the brand with a rounded forest tile, the six
            nav links as soft pills with Home filled sage, and on the right a
            pill New project button, a round bell and a round dark avatar.
            Under it a full width rounded search bar with a soft shadow. The
            hero row has the date and name above a 56px greeting on the left
            and a red tinted callout on the right with a huge 4 and the words
            tasks are overdue. Next, four tall white KPI tiles in one row.
            Then a section titled Where projects stand with the status counts
            on the right, and six project cards in a three by two grid, each
            with a status pill, a 24px name, the team, a 44px percent with the
            task count, a thick round progress bar and the due date with days
            left. Then a wide chart card with the week totals large on the
            left, 73 with Up 14 on last week over a smaller 59, and on the
            right fourteen rounded bars in two groups with each value printed
            on top. Last, Recent activity as a two column list with initials
            in sage circles. Below 1000px nav moves under the brand and grids
            go two wide. On phones everything is one column with KPIs two by
            two.
        spacing: An 8px unit in large steps. 24px gaps, 28px card padding and 64px between sections.
        density: Low. Six project cards and no table. The dashboard fits in about two screens.
        corners: 20px cards, 14 to 16px fields and rows, full pills for buttons, nav and chips.
        borders: Almost none. Hairlines only under the top bar and between activity rows.
        shadows: One soft lift on cards and the search bar, 0 8px 24px at 7 percent ink.
        icons:
            24px outline icons at 1.75px stroke. Status pills carry a filled
            circle with a white check, a filled triangle with a white bang, or
            a filled octagon with a white bar, plus the word.
        focus: A 3px forest outline offset 3px on every control, fields and rows included.
        tone: Plain sentences a manager would say aloud, such as Where projects stand and Up 14 on last week.

    style207:
        number: 207
        run: 42
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Mono numbers
        idea: A crisp sans interface where every number, date and ID is set in a monospace, so columns align like a ledger and figures read as data.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/207.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            white: #ffffff, the page, panels and fields
            fog: #f4f4f6, the sidebar and table heads
            ink: #18181f, text, the logo tile and the chart axis
            graphite: #565667, labels, row numbers, times and axis text
            line: #e1e1e8, borders and rules, never text
            violet: #4b3fc4, the primary button, links, progress, the this week line and focus
            violetTint: #eeedfb, the focus halo, the avatar and a focused row
            pewter: #8f8fa3, the dashed last week line, never text
            green: #17693f, On track with a ring and centre dot
            amber: #875000, At risk with an outlined triangle
            red: #b3202b, Behind with a filled square and down arrow and the overdue flag
        type:
            Words use system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial,
            sans-serif. Every number, date, ID and time uses ui-monospace, SF
            Mono, Cascadia Mono, JetBrains Mono, Menlo, Consolas, Liberation
            Mono, monospace with tabular and slashed zero figures, zero padded
            where it helps alignment, as in 01, 07 and 09/10. The greeting is
            24px sans at 650, sidebar KPI values 20px mono semibold, section
            titles 15px sans at 650, body 14px sans, table numbers 13px mono and
            group labels 11px sans capitals tracked 0.08em.
        layout:
            A 248px fog sidebar on the left holds the brand with a dark B slash
            tile, the six nav links where Home is a white tile with a hairline
            ring, and a This week group showing the four KPIs as a white ledger
            list with the label left and the mono value right, overdue in red.
            The top bar holds a search field with a slash key hint, the violet
            New project button, a bell and the user. The main column opens
            with the greeting and mono date on the left and a red overdue flag
            on the right. Next a full width bordered Projects table with a row
            number, Project, Team, Done percent with a mini bar, Tasks as
            18/25, Due as 14 Nov, Days left and Status, all numbers right
            aligned in mono, and a mono totals footer. Below, two panels side
            by side. The left is a line chart overlaying both weeks by weekday,
            this week solid violet with dots and last week dashed grey with
            squares, over a small mono table of the fourteen values and their
            totals. The right is Recent activity as a timeline with a mono time
            gutter such as 12m, 40m and 1h behind a vertical rule. Below 1100px
            the panels stack. Below 820px the sidebar becomes a top block with
            nav in a three column grid and the ledger two by two, and the table
            scrolls inside its panel.
        spacing: A 4px base with steps of 8, 12, 16 and 24px. Table cells have 16px side padding.
        density: Medium high. 40px table rows with numbers in aligned columns.
        corners: 6px on panels, buttons and fields, 4px on code chips and keys.
        borders: 1px cool grey around every panel and between rows, with fog table heads.
        shadows: None, apart from a 1px ring on the current nav item.
        icons:
            1.7px outline icons at 18px. Status uses a ring with a centre dot
            for On track, an outlined triangle with a bang for At risk and a
            filled rounded square with a white down arrow for Behind.
        focus: A 2px violet outline offset 2px. Fields get a violet border and a 3px violet tint halo. Rows get the violet tint fill.
        tone: Precise and short, such as Days left, Latest first and a sigma for totals.

    style208:
        number: 208
        run: 42
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Humanist
        idea: A warm, serious workspace set in a humanist sans, with soft ivory surfaces, clay accents, rounded but restrained shapes and plain friendly words.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/208.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            ivory: #fbf8f4, the page, resting fields and fact tiles
            white: #ffffff, cards, the top bar and the style sheet
            oat: #f3ece4, the navigation band
            cocoa: #2a2522, text
            stone: #625a55, secondary text, dates and chart axis
            sand: #e9dfd5, borders and dividers, never text
            clay: #a8441f, the primary button, links, progress rings, the chart line and focus
            blush: #f8e9e1, the focus halo and the logo disc
            peach: #f1d9cc, the chart area fill, never text
            sage: #3d6b55, KPI icons on #e7f0ea
            green: #2f6a4b, On track on #e7f0ea with a circle and check
            amber: #8a5000, At risk on #fbefd9 with a rounded triangle
            roseRed: #a92f3a, Behind and the overdue note on #fbe9ea with a rounded square and back chevron
        type:
            One humanist stack, Segoe UI, Optima, Candara, Gill Sans, Noto Sans,
            Trebuchet MS, sans-serif. Body is 15px at 1.6. The greeting is 30px
            at 600, week totals 28px, KPI values 24px, section titles 17px at
            600, project names 16px at 600 and meta lines 13px in stone. No
            capitals styling anywhere.
        layout:
            A white top bar holds the brand with a clay sun on a blush disc, a
            wide round search field in the middle, the clay New project
            button, a rounded bell and the user with a lilac initials disc.
            Under it an oat band holds the six nav links as a segmented
            control, a pale rounded tray with Home as a raised white tab. The
            date and greeting sit above three columns, 260px, flexible and
            300px. The left column stacks a rose tinted note saying 4 tasks
            are overdue with a short friendly line, then a Your week card
            listing the four KPIs with a sage icon tile, label and value per
            line, split by dashed rules. The middle card lists the projects,
            each row with a clay progress ring holding the percent, the name
            with team and task count, and on the right the status chip over
            the due date with days to go. The right card, What the team did,
            lists activity with pastel initials discs. A full width chart
            card follows with title and the two week totals on the left and a
            smooth clay line over a peach area on the right, the second week
            softly shaded. Below 1150px the activity card drops under the
            projects. On phones everything is one column, KPIs two by two and
            chips move under each project name.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16 to 24px gaps, 20px card padding and 32px above the content.
        density: Comfortable. 76px project rows with rings, easy to scan.
        corners: 16px cards, 12px buttons, fields and rows, 10px tabs, a fully round search field.
        borders: 1px warm sand on cards, with dashed dividers inside the KPI list.
        shadows: A faint two layer shadow, 0 2px 8px at 5 percent cocoa.
        icons:
            Rounded 1.8px outline icons at 20px. Status uses an outlined circle
            with a check for On track, a rounded outlined triangle with a bang
            for At risk and a rounded outlined square with a back chevron for
            Behind, always with the word in a tinted chip.
        focus: A 2px clay outline offset 2px plus a 5px blush halo. Fields show the clay border and halo only.
        tone: Warm and plain, such as Your week, What the team did and Worth a look before anything else today.

    style209:
        number: 209
        run: 43
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Scorecard
        idea: A board report you can work from, where every figure sits on a ruled row beside its target, drawn as a bullet chart with a red target tick, so the page answers whether the team is meeting its numbers.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/209.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #f6f6f3, the page behind the report
            paper: #ffffff, the top bar, tables and the style sheet
            inkNavy: #14213d, text, actual bars, the primary button and heavy rules
            sub: #4a5468, notes, column heads and dates
            rule: #d5d6d0, row rules and field borders, never text
            bandPoor: #c5cad3, the poor range of a bullet and last week bars
            bandFair: #dadde3, the fair range of a bullet and initials squares
            bandGood: #eceef1, the good range of a bullet
            targetRed: #b42318, target ticks, the Missed result and the overdue line
            metGreen: #166534, the Met result and positive variance
            nearAmber: #8a4b00, the Near result
            focusBlue: #1d4ed8, the focus outline
        type:
            One stack, Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, Liberation Sans,
            sans-serif, with tabular figures everywhere. The greeting is 30px
            bold tracked tight, actual figures 26px bold, body 15px, section
            labels 13px bold caps tracked 0.1em and column heads 12px bold caps
            in the sub colour.
        layout:
            A white top bar edged by a 2px navy rule holds a small square
            brand mark and Brightwork, a horizontal text nav whose current item
            has a 3px navy underline, then a square search field, a navy New
            project button, a square bell with a red dot and Mara Okafor with
            initials. Under it a 1216px column opens with a caps eyebrow giving
            Weekly scorecard and the date, the greeting, a red square with 4
            tasks are overdue, and a legend for actual bar, target tick and
            ranges on the right. The first section is a scorecard table with
            the columns Measure, Actual, Target, Against target, Variance and
            Result. Its five rows are tasks completed this week 73 against 59
            or more, overdue tasks 4 against 0, hours logged 186 against a 200
            hour target, tasks due this week 23 against 73 or fewer, and
            projects on track 4 against 6, each with a full width bullet chart
            of grey ranges, a navy actual bar and a red target tick. The second
            table lists the six projects with status, a percent bullet with the
            target tick at 100 percent, tasks, due date, days left and tasks
            needed per day. Last comes a two to one row with a grey and navy
            daily column chart crossed by a dashed red line at last week's
            average of 8.4 a day, beside a ruled activity list with initials
            squares and times. Below 860px the nav becomes a scrolling row and
            the search hides. Below 700px each table row becomes a stacked
            block with small labels before each figure.
        spacing: An 8px unit. Rows have 14px padding, sections sit 40px apart, a 24px gutter and 16px on phones.
        density: Medium. One measure per row with actual, target, chart, variance and result side by side.
        corners: Square everywhere, including buttons, fields, initials and status marks.
        borders: 1px warm grey rules between rows. A 2px navy rule under the top bar and under every section label.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            Thin square capped line icons at text size. Results and statuses
            use filled shapes, a circle for Met and On track, a triangle for
            Near and At risk, and a square for Missed and Behind, always with
            the word.
        focus: A 2px focus blue outline offset 2px. A focused row gets a pale blue fill.
        tone: Plain and numerate like a finance pack, such as Team measures this week and Needed per day.

    style210:
        number: 210
        run: 43
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Chart grid
        idea: Four equal chart cards answer the week at a glance, with tasks per day, status, completion per project and hours, framed by an icon rail on the left and a running activity column on the right.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/210.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            mist: #eef1f4, the page and inset panels
            white: #ffffff, cards, the rail and the activity column
            ink: #1c2733, text and figures
            slate: #52606d, labels, axes and times
            line: #dde3e9, dividers and gridlines, never text
            teal: #0f766e, the primary button, this week bars, On track and the focus ring
            tealLight: #9fd8cf, last week bars, never text
            tealTint: #e3f4f1, the current rail item and a focused row
            track: #e6eaee, the empty part of bars and the gauge
            amber: #b7791f, the At risk slice, never text
            amberText: #8a5300, the At risk label
            red: #c53030, the Behind slice
            redText: #b42318, the Behind label, the overdue figure and the badge
        type:
            One stack, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Ubuntu, Helvetica Neue,
            Arial. The gauge figure is 34px bold, KPI figures 24px bold, the
            greeting 22px bold, card titles 15px bold, body 14px and meta and
            axis text 12px in slate.
        layout:
            A 76px white icon rail on the left holds a teal rounded square
            logo and six nav items stacked, each a 22px line icon with an 11px
            label beneath, Home on a teal tint. A 300px white activity column
            runs down the right as a vertical timeline of round initials with
            a thin connecting line. The centre starts with a row of the
            greeting Hello Mara, here is your week in charts with the date and
            a red square with 4 tasks are overdue, then a pill search, a teal
            pill New project button, a round bell with a red count badge and a
            round avatar. One white card splits into four KPI cells by thin
            dividers. Then a two by two grid of equal cards holds a column
            chart of tasks per day in light and dark teal, a status donut whose
            slices carry white circle, triangle and square marks beside a list
            of counts, horizontal bars of done against total tasks per project
            scaled by project size, and a half circle gauge of 186 hours
            against a 200 hour target tick. A full width card below lists the
            projects in a compact table with mini bars. Below 1180px the
            activity column drops under the centre. Below 860px the charts go
            to one column and the KPIs to two by two. Below 640px the rail
            becomes a fixed bottom tab bar.
        spacing: An 8px base with 20px gaps between cards and 28px page padding.
        density: Medium. Four equal chart cards carry the page, figures share one strip.
        corners: 16px cards, 12px rail items and swatches, 10px fields, pill buttons and search.
        borders: Almost none. A 1px line splits the rail, the activity column and the KPI cells.
        shadows: A soft two layer card shadow, 1px tight plus 6px 20px diffuse.
        icons:
            Rounded 1.8px line icons at 22px in the rail with labels below.
            Status shapes are a filled circle, triangle and rounded square,
            also printed in white on the donut slices.
        focus: A 2px white gap then a 2px teal ring.
        tone: Friendly and brief, such as Hello Mara, here is your week in charts.

    style211:
        number: 211
        run: 43
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Status matrix
        idea: A planning grid of projects against weeks, where each row shows this week's status as a shaped marker, hatched weeks running to a due flag, and summary rows below, read like a spreadsheet.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/211.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #f4f5f7, the page, column heads and table footers
            paper: #ffffff, the header, panels and the matrix body
            ink: #101828, text, figures and the frozen column rule
            sub: #475467, week labels, team names and times
            grid: #d0d5dd, cell borders and panel edges, never text
            band: #e9ecf1, the tab band and initials
            blue: #175cd3, the primary button, the active tab, the this week outline, focus and the darkest heat cell
            nowTint: #eaf1fd, the this week column, the lightest heat cell and a focused row
            planBlue: #b8cdef, hatched weeks before the due date, never text
            heatMid: #b2ccf5, heat cells of 5 to 9
            heatHigh: #6f9ae8, heat cells of 10 to 13 with ink figures
            green: #067647, the On track circle and word
            rust: #8f4a00, the At risk diamond and word
            red: #b42318, the Behind crossed square and the overdue line
        type:
            Two stacks. Labels and figures use ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo,
            Consolas, Liberation Mono. Text uses Segoe UI, system-ui, Roboto,
            Helvetica Neue, Arial. Heat figures are 18px mono bold, the
            greeting 16px sans bold, project names 13px sans semibold, body
            13px, panel labels 12px mono bold caps and week heads 11px mono.
        layout:
            A two tier header. The first tier is white with a six dot brand
            mark and Brightwork in mono, a wide centred search with a slash
            key hint, a blue New project button, a square bell with a count
            and Mara Okafor. The second tier is a grey tab band with the six
            nav tabs, the current one white with a blue underline. Below, one
            white strip holds Hello, Mara, the date in mono, a crossed red
            square with 4 tasks are overdue and four outlined chips on the
            right for the summary figures. The main panel is the matrix, a
            table with a frozen project column carrying name, team, tasks and
            percent, then thirteen week columns from 18 Oct to 10 Jan. The
            18 Oct column is last week with dots. The 25 Oct column is this
            week, tinted and outlined in blue, holding each project's status
            marker and word. Following weeks are hatched blue up to a pennant
            flag cell reading the due date. A footer gives projects due per
            week and tasks completed, 59 and 73. Below, two panels side by
            side hold a calendar heat grid of the fourteen days with the count
            printed in every cell and weekly totals at the row starts, and an
            activity log table of time, person and action. The matrix scrolls
            sideways inside its panel on small screens, the search drops to its
            own row and the log rows stack.
        spacing: A 4px unit. Cells are 44px tall, panel padding 10 to 14px, 16px between panels.
        density: High. Thirteen week columns by six projects in one grid, with summary rows in the footer.
        corners: 4px on panels, buttons, fields and heat cells. Markers are sharp except the circle.
        borders: 1px cool grey lines on every cell. A 2px ink rule freezes the project column and a 2px blue outline marks this week.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            1.8px line icons at 16px. Status markers are a filled circle for
            On track, a filled diamond for At risk and a square with a white
            cross for Behind. A pennant flag marks the due week.
        focus: A 2px blue outline offset 1px. A focused row gets the now tint.
        tone: Terse and operational, such as This wk, Projects due and Activity log.

    style212:
        number: 212
        run: 43
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Progress led
        idea: Huge pill shaped progress bars are the page, one full width row per project in order of due date, each with a large percentage, so how far along everything is reads from across the room.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/212.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            linen: #fbfaf7, the page and control panels
            white: #ffffff, the totals card, fields and the style sheet
            ink: #22201c, text, big percentages and the all projects bar
            stone: #5e5a52, team names, dates and captions
            hairline: #e4dfd4, dividers between projects, never text
            track: #ebe6dc, the empty part of every bar, the nav track and initials
            indigo: #3730a3, progress fill, this week columns, the primary button and focus
            indigoLight: #c7c4ee, last week columns, never text
            green: #1f6f43, On track pill text and its check circle
            greenWash: #e6f2ea, the On track pill fill
            amber: #8a4f00, At risk pill text and its triangle
            amberWash: #fbefdc, the At risk pill fill
            red: #b3261e, the Behind pill, the overdue figure and the badge
            redWash: #fbe5e3, the Behind pill and the overdue banner fill
        type:
            One stack, Avenir Next, Avenir, Nunito Sans, Segoe UI, system-ui,
            sans-serif. The greeting is 44px bold tracked tight, project
            percentages 40px bold with a 20px percent sign, figures 30px bold,
            section titles 22px bold, project names 20px bold, body 16px and
            captions 14px in stone.
        layout:
            One centred 920px column with no sidebar. The top row has a
            progress bar shaped brand mark and Brightwork, then a pill search,
            an indigo pill New project button, a round bell with a red dot and
            a round avatar. Under it the nav is a pill segmented control on a
            beige track, Home raised in white. A roomy hero gives the date, a
            44px greeting Hi Mara, here is how far everything has come, and a
            red pill with 4 tasks are overdue, then a strip of four figures
            split by hairlines. The main section, Projects, soonest due first,
            lists the six projects from Q4 customer survey to Spring catalogue,
            each a full width row with the name and team on the left, a 40px
            percentage on the right, a 36px tall pill bar in indigo on a beige
            track, and a line with the status pill, tasks done, tasks to go and
            Due date in N days. A white rounded card closes the list with an
            ink bar for all projects together, 78 of 170 tasks, 46 percent.
            Below, two columns hold a rounded column chart of daily pace and a
            recent activity list with round initials. On phones the search
            takes its own row, the figures go two by two and the nav track
            scrolls.
        spacing: An 8px unit, generous. 24px above and below each project and 40px between sections.
        density: Low. One project per full width row, the bar is the hero of each row.
        corners: Fully round. Bars, buttons, fields, pills and the nav track are pills, the totals card is 20px.
        borders: 1px warm hairlines between projects and around the figure strip. No boxes around projects.
        shadows: Only the selected nav pill has a 1px soft shadow.
        icons:
            Rounded 1.8px line icons at 20px. Status marks are a white check
            in a circle for On track, a white bang in a triangle for At risk
            and a white bar in a square for Behind.
        focus: A 3px indigo outline offset 3px. A focused row gets a pale indigo fill.
        tone: Warm and plain, such as Hi Mara, here is how far everything has come, and Due 7 Nov in 7 days.

    style213:
        number: 213
        run: 43
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Portfolio quadrant
        idea: A portfolio review where one large scatter of percent done against days left sorts projects into four labelled quadrants, with the figures and a numbered project list set beside it like an analyst's exhibit.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/213.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            white: #ffffff, the main canvas and cards
            mist: #eef2f7, the sidebar
            wash: #f6f8fb, the right half of the quadrant chart and the style sheet
            navy: #1b2a4a, text, the primary button, split lines and heavy rules
            slate: #4e5b70, notes, axis labels and captions
            rule: #cfd6e0, hairlines and the chart frame, never text
            orange: #c2410c, the single accent for overdue, the needs attention label, the current nav edge and focus
            peach: #fdf1ea, the needs attention quadrant and a focused row
            sage: #eef6f1, the finishing quadrant
            green: #1d6b45, the On track circle and word
            amber: #8b5000, the At risk triangle and word
            red: #b42318, the Behind square and word
        type:
            Two stacks. Headings and figures use Charter, Bitstream Charter,
            Iowan Old Style, Palatino Linotype, Georgia in regular weight.
            Text uses Segoe UI, system-ui, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial. The
            greeting is 34px serif, figures 28px serif, section titles 22px
            serif, body 15px sans, notes 13px and labels 12px bold caps
            tracked 0.12em.
        layout:
            A 240px pale blue grey sidebar holds a quartered square brand mark
            with an orange dot and Brightwork in serif, then the six nav items
            with line icons, Home white with a 3px orange left edge, and Mara
            Okafor signed in at the bottom. The main area starts with a top
            row of a square search on the left, a navy New project button and
            a bell with an orange count, over a hairline. A caps eyebrow reads
            Portfolio review and the date above the serif greeting and a line
            with 4 tasks are overdue in orange. The board is a large framed
            scatter with a 300px column beside it. The scatter plots percent
            done up against days left across, 0 to 80, split by dashed navy
            lines at 50 percent and 30 days into Finishing in sage, Needs
            attention in peach, Ahead, none yet, and Early days. Each project
            is a white edged circle, triangle or square with its number and
            name. The side column has the four figures as a ruled list with
            serif numbers, then the numbered project list with status, team,
            percent, tasks and due date with days left. Below, two columns
            topped by navy rules hold a line chart comparing this week and last
            week by weekday, solid with squares against dashed with hollow
            circles, and a ruled activity list. Below 1100px the side column
            moves under the chart. Below 820px the sidebar becomes a top band
            with scrolling text tabs and the scatter scrolls sideways.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 40px page padding, 32px between the chart and its side column, 40px before the lower row.
        density: Medium low. One large chart leads, with figures and a keyed list beside it.
        corners: 2px on boxes, buttons and fields. Avatars, number keys and swatches are round.
        borders: 1px cool hairlines. A 2px navy rule tops each side block and section, and the current nav item has a 3px orange left edge.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            1.6px line icons at 18px. Status marks are a filled circle,
            triangle and square, drawn white edged on the chart and numbered to
            match the list.
        focus: A 2px orange outline offset 2px. A focused field gets an orange underline.
        tone: Measured and analytical like a portfolio review deck, such as Where each project stands.

    style214:
        number: 214
        run: 44
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Desktop native
        idea: A generic desktop application window, with a title bar, a toolbar of small push buttons, a grey source list on the left and a zebra striped table view, so the dashboard feels installed rather than visited.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/214.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            desktop: #dde1e7, the backdrop behind the floating window
            chrome: #f5f5f6, the title bar, toolbar, table column heads and status bar
            sourceList: #e9eaed, the grey sidebar
            pane: #ffffff, the content pane, group boxes and the style sheet
            zebra: #f4f5f7, every second table row
            grid: #e2e4e8, lines between every cell and around group boxes
            text: #1c1e22, labels and values
            secondary: #595d65, meta, column heads, counts and chart labels
            selection: #2456c4, the selected sidebar row, push button, sidebar icons and this week bars
            focusRing: #4b7fe2, the 3px keyboard ring
            onTrack: #1d7436, On track text with a circle and tick
            atRisk: #885500, At risk text with a triangle and bang
            behind: #b02a20, Behind text and overdue figures with an octagon and cross
        type:
            One system stack, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Segoe UI,
            system-ui, Cantarell, Ubuntu, Helvetica Neue, Arial, sans-serif.
            Base text is 13px at 1.45. The page title is 20px semibold, KPI
            values 22px semibold with tabular figures, the toolbar title 14px
            semibold, column heads 12px semibold grey, sidebar group headings
            11px bold grey and the status bar 11px.
        layout:
            The page is a grey desktop with one window centred on it, at most
            1232px wide with a 24px margin. A 30px title bar holds a small
            app mark and the name Brightwork on the left, the word Home in the
            centre and minimise, maximise and close glyph buttons on the
            right. Below it a toolbar holds a sidebar toggle, a joined back
            and forward pair, the bold title Home, then on the right a 240px
            search field, a blue New project push button, a bell with a red
            dot and the avatar with the name Mara Okafor. The body is a 216px
            grey source list beside a white pane. The source list has a
            Brightwork heading over the six nav rows with blue line icons, Home
            filled blue with white text and a count of 6 on Projects, then an
            Active projects heading listing the six projects with their
            percent as a grey count. The pane opens with the greeting and a
            line giving the date and a red 4 tasks are overdue. Next comes a
            single bordered inspector strip of four cells split by hairlines,
            each with a small icon label, a value and a note. Then a Projects
            heading with 6 items and 78 of 170 tasks done, over a bordered
            table with lines between all cells and zebra rows, sorted by due
            date, with columns for name, team, a thin level bar with percent,
            tasks as 18 / 25, due with days left, and status. Below sit two
            group boxes side by side, the bar chart on the left slightly wider
            and activity on the right with initials avatars and times on the
            far right. A status bar closes the window with counts and the date.
            Below 860px the window loses its margin and corners, the sidebar
            becomes a scrolling row of nav items, the search moves to its own
            toolbar row, the strip becomes two by two, the table scrolls
            inside its box and the group boxes stack.
        spacing: A 4px grid. Table rows are 26px, toolbar controls 28px, and the pane has 16 by 20px padding with 16px between blocks.
        density: Compact like a utility app. All six projects, the chart and the activity fit one 1280 by 800 screen.
        corners: 10px on the window, 6px on buttons, fields, the strip, table and group boxes, 5px on the sidebar selection.
        borders: 1px #d2d4d8 under the title bar and toolbar and beside the sidebar. 1px #e2e4e8 between every table cell and around boxes.
        shadows: Only the window floats, with a 1px dark ring, 0 18px 48px at 22 percent and 0 2px 6px. Everything inside is flat.
        icons:
            16px rounded line icons at stroke 1.7, blue in the sidebar and grey
            in the toolbar. Status uses a circle with a tick, a triangle with a
            bang and an octagon with a cross, always beside the coloured word.
        focus: A 3px #4b7fe2 outline offset 1px on every control and field. A focused table row is filled blue with white text plus the ring.
        tone: Terse system labels such as Name, Team, Due, 6 items and Latest first, with one warm greeting.

    style215:
        number: 215
        run: 44
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Fluent-like
        idea: A modern desktop look built from soft layers, a tinted base, a lighter content layer with one rounded corner, and white 4px cards stacked like settings rows beside a navigation pane with a small accent pill.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/215.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            base: #eef0f3, the window base under the title bar and navigation pane
            layer: #f9f9fa, the content layer and the style sheet
            card: #ffffff, project rows, KPI tiles and panels
            stroke: #e3e5e8, the layer edge, dividers and field sides
            text: #1a1a1a, primary text and the focus ring
            textSecondary: #5c5f64, captions, meta and chart labels
            accent: #0a5cb0, the accent button, nav pill, field underline, progress and this week bars
            accentTint: #e6f0fa, the project icon tiles
            caution: #fff4ce, the overdue info bar, with its icon in #8a5300
            onTrack: #0f7b2e, a filled circle with a white tick
            atRisk: #9a5a00, a filled triangle with a white bang
            behind: #c0261b, a filled octagon with a white cross and the overdue value
        type:
            Text uses Segoe UI Variable Text, Segoe UI, system-ui,
            -apple-system, Roboto, Noto Sans, Helvetica Neue, Arial,
            sans-serif, and titles use the Display cut of the same family. A
            ramp of Title 28 on 36 semibold for the greeting, Subtitle 20 on
            28 semibold for section heads, KPI values 28 semibold, body strong
            14 on 20 for project names, body 14 on 20 and caption 12 on 16.
        layout:
            No top header band. A 48px title bar sits on the base with a back
            button, a small gradient app mark and the name Brightwork on the
            left, a 480px search box in the centre and the accent New project
            button, a bell with a red dot and a round persona on the right.
            Under it a 264px navigation pane on the base holds a hamburger
            button and five 36px items with icons, the current one with a
            light grey fill, bold text and a 3 by 16px accent pill at its left
            edge, and Settings pinned at the bottom under a divider. The
            content layer fills the rest, lighter, with a hairline edge and an
            8px top left corner. Inside it a small date caption sits over the
            greeting title, then a full width yellow info bar says Caution,
            4 tasks are overdue, with an Open Tasks button at its end. Below,
            two columns. The wide left column has a Projects subtitle with a
            See all projects link and six white cards stacked 4px apart, each
            a row of a 40px tinted icon tile, name over team and due date, a
            progress block with tasks and percent over a 3px bar, the status
            and a chevron. The 320px right column has a This week subtitle
            over a two by two grid of KPI tiles, then a chart panel and a
            recent activity panel with round personas and times under each
            line. Under 1100px the columns merge with the KPI tiles first in
            a row of four. Under 760px the pane becomes a Home disclosure
            button that opens a menu of all six items, the search drops to its
            own row and project cards stack their progress and status.
        spacing: A 4px base. Cards sit 4px apart, sections 24px apart, and the layer has 28 by 40px padding.
        density: Comfortable. 36px nav items, 32px controls and 68px project rows.
        corners: 4px on controls, cards and tiles, 8px on the content layer and flyouts, round personas.
        borders: Hairline strokes, with a darker bottom edge on fields and buttons in the manner of a soft bevel.
        shadows: Cards lift with a 1px ring at 5 percent plus 0 2px 4px at 5 percent. Flyouts use 0 8px 16px at 12 percent.
        icons:
            16px thin line icons at stroke 1.5 for navigation and labels.
            Status icons are filled shapes with a white mark, a circle with a
            tick, a triangle with a bang and an octagon with a cross, beside
            the word in plain text.
        focus: A 2px near black outline offset 1px with a 4px white halo outside it. A focused field instead gets a 2px accent bottom border.
        tone: Calm and plain, such as Caution, See all projects, Open Tasks and Recent activity.

    style216:
        number: 216
        run: 44
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Breadcrumb web app
        idea: A conventional business web app with a dark top navigation bar, then a white page header with breadcrumbs, a title and its actions, then a filter bar, a sortable table and pagination, all in flat bordered boxes.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/216.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            navbar: #1e2733, the top navigation bar, with links in #d3dae4 and its search field in #2c3746
            navMark: #2bb3a8, the brand mark and the current link underline on the dark bar
            page: #f7f8fa, the page background below the header
            surface: #ffffff, the page header band, cards and table
            head: #f3f5f7, table heads and disabled pager buttons
            line: #dfe3e8, every box border and divider
            text: #17202b, titles and cell text
            muted: #56606d, labels, meta and uppercase heads
            primary: #0b6b66, the primary button, current page number, progress bars and the this week line
            primaryTint: #e3f2f0, the selected filter segment
            link: #0a5f91, breadcrumbs, links and the focus ring
            onTrack: #17703a, an outlined badge with a circle and tick
            atRisk: #8a5600, an outlined badge with a triangle and bang
            behind: #b3261e, an outlined badge with an octagon and cross, and overdue figures
        type:
            One stack, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica
            Neue, Arial, sans-serif. Body and cells 14px at 1.5, the page
            title 24px bold, stat values 26px bold, card titles 16px bold,
            breadcrumbs and meta 13px, and stat labels and column heads 12px
            semibold uppercase tracked 0.05em.
        layout:
            A full width dark bar 52px tall holds the brand on the left, then
            six text links with the current one white and underlined in teal,
            then a 280px dark search field with a slash key hint, a bell and
            the avatar with the name. Under it a white header band with a
            bottom border holds the breadcrumb Brightwork then Home, and a
            title row with the greeting, a meta line of the date and a red
            4 tasks are overdue, and on the right a View reports secondary
            button and a New project primary button. The body is a 1280px
            column. First a single bordered stat strip of four cells split by
            lines, each an uppercase label, a big value and a sub line. Then
            the Projects card, whose header has the title with a count pill
            and an Open Projects link, then a filter bar holding a joined
            segmented control for All 6, On track 4, At risk 1 and Behind 1
            with status glyphs, a Team select, a Sort select and a filter
            field pushed right. The table has uppercase heads, a sort arrow on
            Due, rows with the name in bold, team, a progress bar with
            percent, tasks as 9 of 10, due with days left, an outlined status
            badge and a row actions button. A footer says Showing 1 to 6 of 6
            projects beside Previous, 1 and Next buttons. Below, two cards in
            a three to two split, a line chart comparing the two weeks by
            weekday with a small values table under it, and activity as a
            vertical timeline with event icons in grey circles, linked project
            names and a Showing 6 of 6 events footer. Under 760px the links
            become a scrolling strip under the brand row, the search takes its
            own row, the segmented filter becomes two by two, each table row
            becomes a stacked block and the lower cards stack.
        spacing: A 4px base. 16px cell and card padding, 20px between boxes and a 24px page gutter.
        density: Medium. 44px table rows, 36px buttons and 32px filter controls.
        corners: 6px on every box, button, field and pager button, 4px on status badges.
        borders: 1px #dfe3e8 on all boxes and between header rows, #edf0f3 between table rows.
        shadows: None. Structure comes from borders and the dark bar.
        icons:
            16px line icons at stroke 2. Timeline events sit in 28px grey
            circles. Status glyphs are a circle with a tick, a triangle with a
            bang and an octagon with a cross. This week is a solid line with
            round dots and last week a dashed grey line with hollow squares.
        focus: A 2px #0a5f91 outline offset 2px. On the dark bar the ring is #7fd3cb. A focused field gets a blue border plus the ring.
        tone: Plain business labels in title case with uppercase column heads, such as Showing 1 to 6 of 6 projects and View reports.

    style217:
        number: 217
        run: 44
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Mobile first
        idea: Designed for one thumb on a phone, with big rounded cards in a single column, progress rings, 48px touch targets and a bottom tab bar with a raised New project button, which becomes a navigation rail and a three column grid of the same cards on a desktop.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/217.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #f5f4f1, the warm off white behind the cards
            card: #ffffff, cards, the tab bar, the rail and the search pill
            line: #e6e4df, dividers inside cards and above the tab bar
            text: #17171c, titles and body
            muted: #595964, meta, inactive tabs and labels
            indigo: #3b3fc4, the raised New project button, active tab, rings, this week bars and focus
            indigoTint: #ecebfd, the active tab pip and KPI icon tiles
            onTrack: #157a3c, text on a #e2f4e8 pill with a circle and tick
            atRisk: #8f5200, text on a #fcf0dc pill with a triangle and bang
            behind: #b8202e, text on a #fde8ea pill with an octagon and cross, and the overdue card
        type:
            Display text uses ui-rounded, SF Pro Rounded, system-ui,
            -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, sans-serif, and body text uses
            system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Noto Sans, Helvetica
            Neue, Arial, sans-serif. The greeting is 30px extra bold rounded,
            KPI values 32px extra bold rounded, section heads 21px, card
            titles 17px bold, body 16px and never smaller in fields, meta 14px
            and tab labels 12px semibold.
        layout:
            On a phone a single column with a 16px gutter. An app bar holds
            the mark and the name Brightwork with a round bell button and the
            avatar at the right. Then the date over a big greeting, a full
            width 52px search pill, and a soft red card with an octagon,
            4 tasks are overdue in bold and a chevron. The KPIs are a two by
            two grid of white tiles, each with a tinted icon tile, a big value
            and a label. A Projects head with See all leads to six stacked
            cards, each with a 56px progress ring showing the percent in its
            centre, the name, the team and tasks, and a divided footer row
            with the due date and days left on the left and a status pill on
            the right. Then a chart card with two week total tiles, last week
            59 and this week 73 up 14, over the bar chart, and an activity card
            with round initials. The tab bar is sticky at the bottom of the
            dashboard and sits at its end, with Home, Projects, a raised 56px
            indigo plus button for New project, Tasks and a More menu that
            opens upward with Team, Reports and Settings. From 900px a 96px
            white rail replaces the tab bar on the left with the mark, the
            raised plus button and stacked icon and label items, Settings at
            the foot. The app bar then holds the greeting, a 380px search, the
            bell and avatar. Content becomes a three column grid with the
            overdue card full width, the KPIs four across, the six project
            cards three across, and the chart card spanning two columns beside
            the activity card.
        spacing: A 16px phone gutter, 12px between cards and 20px between sections. On a desktop a 32px gutter and 20px gaps.
        density: Roomy and touch sized. Every control is at least 44px, tabs are 52px and the raised button 56px.
        corners: 20px cards, 16px tiles and fields, 18px on the raised button, full pills for search, buttons and status.
        borders: Almost none. A 1px line inside project cards and above the tab bar.
        shadows: A faint 0 1px 2px under cards. The raised button has a 0 4px 12px indigo glow and the More menu floats at 0 8px 28px.
        icons:
            22px line icons at stroke 2, inside 56 by 30px pips on tabs and
            36px tinted tiles on KPIs. Status pills carry a circle with a
            tick, a triangle with a bang or an octagon with a cross.
        focus: A 3px indigo outline offset 3px on every control. A focused field also turns its border indigo.
        tone: Short and friendly, such as See all, More, up 14 and The most urgent thing today.

    style218:
        number: 218
        run: 44
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Embedded panel
        idea: Brightwork as a guest, a compact 480px panel living inside someone else's page with its own small header, tabs and one quiet plum accent, so it reads clearly as a separate app without fighting the host.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/218.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            hostBackground: #eceef1, the host page, never inside the panel
            hostSkeleton: #d9dde2, grey placeholder bars for host content
            panel: #ffffff, the panel body
            panelSub: #f7f7f9, the KPI strip and panel footer
            line: #e2e3e8, rows, tabs and section rules inside the panel
            text: #1d1b22, names and values
            muted: #5a5764, sub lines, caps headings and times
            plum: #84276f, the active tab, New project button, links, progress, this week bars and focus
            plumTint: #f6e9f2, a focused or selected row
            onTrack: #18733a, text with a circle and tick
            atRisk: #8c5400, text with a triangle and bang
            behind: #b3261e, text with an octagon and cross, and the overdue banner on #fcebea
        type:
            One stack, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica
            Neue, Arial, sans-serif, small throughout. Panel base 13px at
            1.45, the greeting 15px bold, KPI values 17px bold, row names
            13px semibold, activity 12px, sub lines and times 11px, and
            section heads 11px bold uppercase tracked 0.06em.
        layout:
            A host page frames the panel. The host has a white top bar with a
            grey circle logo, the words Team portal and grey skeleton links,
            and a main column of white skeleton cards. The panel sits in a
            480px right column under a small host caption reading Embedded app
            and 480px wide. The panel is one bordered white box. Its header
            row has the plum mark and Brightwork, then a bell, the avatar with
            the name and an open in new window icon. A tab row follows with
            Home underlined in plum, Projects, Tasks, Team and a More
            disclosure at the right holding Reports and Settings. Then a
            search field with a small New project button, then the greeting
            with the date in grey on one line and a slim red banner saying
            4 tasks are overdue with a View link. A four cell KPI strip runs
            edge to edge on the grey sub surface. Projects is a caps head with
            a count and an All projects link over six two line rows, the name
            over team, tasks and due date, then a 64px mini bar, the percent
            and the status. The chart is a short 14 bar chart with last week
            59 and this week 73 stacked beside it. Activity is a tight list
            with 24px initials and short times like 12 min. A grey footer says
            Powered by Brightwork with an Open full app link. Under 1000px the
            panel moves above the host content, centred at up to 480px. Under
            600px the mini bars hide, the search takes a full row with the
            button below it and the week totals sit under the chart.
        spacing: A 4px base. 12px side padding inside the panel, 5px row padding and 24px between the host column and the panel.
        density: Very compact. Everything fits the 480px column, about 1000px tall, with no inner scrolling.
        corners: 8px on the panel, 6px on buttons, fields and host cards, 5px on the banner, round avatars.
        borders: 1px #d3d4db around the panel, 1px #e2e3e8 between rows and sections, 1px #d9dde2 around host cards.
        shadows: One soft lift on the panel only, 0 1px 2px and 0 6px 18px at 8 percent, to separate it from the host.
        icons:
            14px line icons at stroke 2, used sparingly. Status glyphs are 13px,
            a circle with a tick, a triangle with a bang and an octagon with a
            cross, beside a bold 11px word.
        focus: A 2px plum outline offset 2px. A focused row also takes the plum tint, and a focused field a plum border.
        tone: Clipped, such as Due this week, View, All projects and 12 min, with host labels kept neutral.

    style219:
        number: 219
        run: 45
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Quiet ops
        idea: A calm operations console in low chroma greys with hairline rules and tabular figures, where the only colour on screen belongs to status, so anything green, amber or red is news.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/219.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #f3f3f2, the page behind panels
            surface: #ffffff, panels, the header and fields
            sunken: #ebebea, table heads and the avatar
            line: #d6d6d3, hairline rules, panel edges and KPI cell dividers
            edge: #8a8c88, field and secondary button borders
            ink: #1d1e20, text and figures
            ink2: #4f5155, secondary text and chart values
            muted: #63666b, labels, meta and timestamps
            graphite: #2f3134, the primary button, this week bars, progress fills and focus
            bar: #8b8d91, last week bars, never text
            green: #1d6a3c, On track with an outlined circle and check
            amber: #8a5200, At risk with an outlined triangle and bang
            red: #b0261c, Behind with an outlined square and down arrow, and every overdue mark
        type:
            Two stacks. Text uses system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
            Arial. Figures, timestamps and task counts use ui-monospace, SF
            Mono, Menlo, Consolas. The greeting is 18px 600, KPI figures 26px
            500 mono, panel titles and column heads 11 to 12px caps tracked
            0.06em, row names 13px 600, body 13px and timestamps 11px mono.
        layout:
            One white header bar 48px tall with a hairline below. It holds a
            small outlined square mark and the brand, then the six nav items
            as text tabs with small grey icons, the current tab underlined in
            graphite. At right sit a 240px search field, a graphite New
            project button, a bell with an outlined count and the avatar with
            Mara Okafor after a hairline. Below, a status line reads Hello,
            Mara and the date at left with 4 tasks are overdue in red with a
            clock at the far right, over a hairline. The four KPIs are one
            white strip split into four cells by hairlines, each a caps label
            over a mono figure and a short grey note, the overdue cell red. The
            body is two columns, a wide left and a 360px right. Left holds the
            projects table with columns for project and department, status,
            a thin 4px progress bar with percent, tasks as 18/25 and due date
            with days left, then the chart panel with fourteen thin bars, grey
            last week and graphite this week, split by a dashed line, values
            printed above and day letter and date below, and a legend with
            the week totals and the change. Right holds a status mix panel
            with a thin three part bar and the counts 4, 1 and 1, then an
            activity log with a mono time column beside each entry. Below
            800px the tabs drop to their own scrolling row and KPIs become two
            by two. Below 640px table rows become small grids and the chart
            scrolls sideways.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 4px inside controls, 8 to 12px cell padding, 16px between panels.
        density: High. 40px table rows and many facts on one screen.
        corners: Square panels. 3px on buttons and fields, and only the avatar is round.
        borders: 1px hairlines around panels, between rows and between KPI cells.
        shadows: None. Depth comes only from grey page against white panels.
        icons:
            16px line icons at 1.8px stroke in grey for nav and tools. Status
            icons are 14px outlined shapes in their status colour, a circle
            with a check, a triangle with a bang, a square with a down arrow,
            and a clock ring for overdue.
        focus: A 2px graphite outline offset 2px on every control.
        tone: Terse and factual, such as Activity log, Status mix and 4 tasks are overdue.
    style220:
        number: 220
        run: 45
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Bright confident
        idea: A crisp white workspace under a bold saturated blue band, with big friendly figures, rounded cards that lift off the band and one confident blue doing all the work.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/220.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            blue: #1650f0, the band, primary buttons, this week bars, rings, links and focus
            blueDeep: #0b2f9e, blue text on white and tint and the current nav label
            blueTint: #e9efff, icon bubbles, department tags, ring tracks and last week fill
            blueLine: #b9cbff, field and secondary button borders, never text
            white: #ffffff, cards, panels and text on the band
            page: #f6f8fc, the page below the band
            ink: #111a2e, text and figures
            ink2: #435069, secondary text and labels
            line: #e1e6f0, card borders and dividers
            green: #137a3a, On track with a solid circle and check
            amber: #975a00, At risk with a solid triangle and bang
            red: #c4242b, Behind with a solid square and down arrow, and overdue
            redTint: #fdecec, the overdue bubble and the Review now pill
        type:
            One stack, Inter, Segoe UI Variable Display, Segoe UI, system-ui,
            Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial. The greeting is 40px 800 at minus
            0.03em, KPI figures 36px 800, section titles 22px 800, card titles
            18px 700, body 15px, meta and labels 14px 600.
        layout:
            A full width saturated blue band opens the page. Its top row holds
            a white rounded square mark with a blue check and the brand in
            white, the six nav items as pills inside a translucent pill track
            with the current one white and blue, then a white pill search, a
            round translucent bell and a white initials disc. Under it the
            hero shows Good to see you, Mara in big white type, the date with
            a line saying 73 tasks closed this week and 14 more than last,
            and a white pill reading 4 tasks are overdue with a clock and a
            Review now chip. A large white New project button sits at the
            hero's right. Four white KPI cards with 20px corners and soft
            shadows overlap the bottom of the band, each a tinted icon bubble
            beside a big figure and its label, the overdue one red. Below, Your
            projects is a three by two grid of white cards, each with a
            department tag, the name, tasks done and percent, a ring with the
            percent at right and a footer with a solid status chip and the due
            date with days left. Last comes a two to one row, a chart card with
            three totals for this week, last week and the change over grouped
            bars by weekday, last week outlined in blue on tint and this week
            solid blue with values on top, and a team activity card with
            initials discs. Below 980px nav scrolls on its own row, KPIs and
            cards go two across, and on phones everything stacks in one column
            with the chart scrolling sideways.
        spacing: An 8px unit, generous. 20px gaps between cards, 24px card padding, 40px between sections.
        density: Low to medium. Six project cards, big figures and plenty of air.
        corners: Round. 20px cards, 12px buttons and fields, and pills for nav, tags, search and the overdue alert.
        borders: 1px line on cards. 2px blueLine on fields and secondary buttons.
        shadows: KPI cards float with a 12px offset 32px blur shadow at 10 percent ink so they lift off the band. The hero button has a deeper blue shadow.
        icons:
            Line icons at 2px stroke sized to their text. Status icons are 16px
            solid shapes, a circle with a check, a triangle with a bang and a
            square with a down arrow, beside their word.
        focus: A 3px solid blue outline offset 3px, and white on the blue band.
        tone: Upbeat and direct, such as Good to see you, Mara, Review now and Up 24 percent.
    style221:
        number: 221
        run: 45
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Earthy professional
        idea: A serious, grounded workspace in olive, sand and clay, with a dark olive sidebar, serif figures set like a ledger and projects filed under their departments.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/221.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            sand: #f1ebdf, the page
            paper: #fbf8f1, cards, fields and the style sheet
            olive: #33391f, the sidebar
            oliveMid: #4b5330, the current nav item
            olivePrimary: #4f5a26, the primary button
            sandText: #ece4cf, text on the sidebar
            clay: #a85a33, progress lines, this week bars and the mark, never small text
            clayInk: #8c4423, department labels, links and the focus ring
            clayTint: #f3e2d4, the overdue notice and the focus halo
            ink: #2a2620, text and figures
            ink2: #5a5244, secondary text and labels
            line: #ddd2bb, rules and card edges
            edge: #8f8166, field borders and the ledger double rule
            green: #2f6b34, On track with an outlined circle and check
            amber: #875700, At risk with an outlined triangle and bang
            red: #a1221f, Behind with an outlined square and down arrow, and overdue
        type:
            Two stacks. Headings, figures and project names use Iowan Old
            Style, Palatino Linotype, Palatino, Book Antiqua, Charter, Georgia.
            Text and labels use Avenir Next, Segoe UI, system-ui, Roboto,
            Arial. The greeting is 38px serif 500, ledger figures 46px serif,
            section titles 24px serif, project names 17px serif 600, caps
            labels 12px tracked 0.14em, body 14px sans.
        layout:
            A 240px dark olive sidebar runs the full height. It holds a clay
            disc mark with the serif brand, a small Workspace caption, the six
            nav items with thin line icons where the current one has a lighter
            olive fill and a clay left bar, and the signed in user Mara Okafor
            pinned at the bottom. The main area starts with a row holding a
            wide search field at left and an olive New project button and a
            square bell at right, over a rule. The greeting has the date as a
            small caps eyebrow over Good day, Mara in serif, with a clay edged
            notice at right reading 4 tasks are overdue and need attention
            first. The KPIs are a ledger, four columns under a double rule and
            over a single rule, split by thin vertical rules, each a large
            serif figure, a caps label and a short note. Below are two
            columns. The wider left is Projects by department, with clay caps
            headings for Design, Engineering, Research and Marketing, and under
            each a row with the serif name, the percent and tasks, the status
            and the due date with days left, and a thin clay line for progress
            across the row foot. The right column holds a paper card titled
            Week over week with seven day rows of paired horizontal bars, last
            week sand with an outline above this week clay, the two values at
            the row end and totals below, then a recent activity card with
            small clay diamonds on a vertical rule. Below 1100px the columns
            stack. Below 860px the sidebar becomes a top band with the nav
            scrolling sideways and the ledger goes two by two.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 40px page padding and column gap, 12 to 14px row padding.
        density: Medium. Rows read like a ledger, grouped under department labels.
        corners: Small, 4px on cards, buttons and fields. Only the avatar is round.
        borders: 1px line rules. A 3px double rule tops the ledger and the style sheet.
        shadows: None. Surfaces separate by sand against paper.
        icons:
            18px line icons at 1.6px stroke. Status icons are 15px outlined
            shapes, a circle with a check, a triangle with a bang and a square
            with a down arrow. Activity uses small clay outlined diamonds on a
            rule.
        focus: A 2px clayInk outline offset 2px with a 5px clayTint halo, and a sand outline in the sidebar.
        tone: Measured and formal, such as Good day, Mara, Need attention first and Week over week.
    style222:
        number: 222
        run: 45
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Single blue
        idea: Every colour on the page is a shade of one steel blue, from a pale wash to a near navy rail, with neutral grey text, so hierarchy comes from tone and weight and status from shape.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/222.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            b50: #f3f7fc, the page, fields and the On track chip
            b100: #e2ebf6, the Today panel, empty segments, the chart area and the At risk chip
            b200: #c4d5ec, borders and the focus halo, never text
            b400: #6f97c9, field borders and outlines, never text
            b600: #2d66ad, filled segments, the last week line and icons
            b700: #1f5190, the primary button, current rail item, links, this week line and focus
            b800: #163e6e, the overdue KPI row and blue labels and counts
            b900: #0e2a4b, the rail, headings, the Behind chip and the overdue note
            white: #ffffff, panels and cards
            ink: #1b1f24, body text, the only colour outside the blue family besides ink2
            ink2: #525a63, meta and secondary text
        type:
            One stack, SF Pro Text, Segoe UI, system-ui, Roboto, Helvetica
            Neue, Arial. The greeting is 26px 700, KPI figures 24px 700
            tabular, panel titles 15px 700, department labels 12px 600 caps,
            body 14px and meta 12px.
        layout:
            An 88px navy rail on the left holds a blue rounded square mark
            and the six nav items as an icon over a small label, the current
            one on a lighter blue tile. The main area has a white header with
            the brand in blue, a wide search, a blue New project button, a
            bell with a navy count and the initials disc with Mara Okafor.
            Below sits a two column board. The left 340px column is a pale
            blue Today panel holding the greeting Hi Mara, here is your
            Saturday with the date, a navy note reading 4 tasks are overdue,
            the four KPIs as a stacked list of white rows with an icon and
            label at left and the figure at right, the overdue row in dark
            blue with white text, and then the activity feed with outlined
            initials discs. The right column holds a white chart panel with
            legend pills, a line chart overlaying the two weeks by weekday,
            this week a solid line with square points and a light area fill,
            last week a dashed line with hollow round points, all values
            labelled, then a projects panel with a two across grid of cards,
            each with a caps department, a status chip, the name, a progress
            bar of twenty segments and a line with percent, tasks and due date
            with days left. Below 1100px the board stacks. Below 760px the
            rail becomes a sticky bottom bar of six icon tabs, cards go one
            across and the chart scrolls sideways.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px gutters and panel padding, 12px between project cards.
        density: Medium. The left Today column carries the summary so the right holds the chart and cards.
        corners: 16px panels, 12px cards and rail items, 10px buttons and fields, and pills for legend chips.
        borders: 1px b200 around panels and cards, and b400 on fields and the secondary button.
        shadows: None. Depth is tone alone, a navy rail, a pale panel and white cards on the wash.
        icons:
            20px line icons at 1.7 to 1.8px stroke. Status uses shape and fill
            weight in blue, an outlined circle with a check on a pale chip, a
            solid triangle with a bang on a mid chip, and an inverted white
            square with a down arrow on a navy chip.
        focus: A 2px b700 outline offset 2px plus a 6px b200 halo, and a white outline on the rail.
        tone: Friendly and plain, such as Hi Mara, here is your Saturday and This week against last.
    style223:
        number: 223
        run: 45
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: High contrast professional
        idea: Strict black on white with heavy 2px rules, large plain type and no colour at all except a bright yellow focus ring, built first for people who need maximum contrast and still calm enough for daily work.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/223.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            black: #111111, text, rules, the header, primary button, this week bars and the Behind chip
            white: #ffffff, the page, fields, text on black and last week bars
            grey: #f2f2f2, reserved for disabled surfaces, never behind text that matters
            mid: #4a4a4a, placeholder text only
            yellow: #ffd60a, the focus ring, never text and never decoration
        type:
            One stack, Atkinson Hyperlegible, Segoe UI, system-ui, Roboto,
            Helvetica Neue, Arial. The greeting is 36px 800, KPI figures 52px
            800, section titles 26px 800 over a 4px rule, project names 17px
            800 underlined, body 16px and meta 15px 700. Nothing is smaller
            than 15px.
        layout:
            A black masthead holds a white square mark with a black check, the
            brand in white, a white search field, a white New project button,
            a square outlined bell with a count and a round outlined initials
            disc with Mara Okafor. Under it the nav is a row of six equal
            boxed links split by 2px black rules, the current one filled black
            with white underlined text. The body is one 1120px column. The
            greeting Hello, Mara sits over the date, then a box with a 3px
            border and a 12px left bar reads 4 tasks are overdue with a clock
            and a Show overdue tasks link. The four KPIs are one bordered box
            split into four cells by 2px rules, each a label over a 52px
            figure, the overdue cell inverted black. Projects is a full width
            table with 2px row rules, columns for project and department, a
            bordered status chip, a bordered progress bar with percent, tasks
            done and due date with days left. Last, two columns hold the chart
            with paired bars by weekday, last week white with a black outline
            and this week solid black with values on top, and a numbered list
            of recent activity with boxed numbers. Below 760px the nav becomes
            a three by two grid of boxes, KPIs go two by two, table rows become
            stacked blocks and the chart scrolls sideways.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 44px minimum targets, 14px row padding, 40 to 48px between sections.
        density: Medium low. One column for summary and table, then chart and activity side by side.
        corners: Square everywhere. Only the avatar and the notification count are round.
        borders: 2px black on every box, rule and row. 4px under section titles, a 12px left bar on the overdue note and 8px over the style sheet.
        shadows: None. The only box shadow is the yellow focus ring.
        icons:
            Line icons at 2px stroke sized at 1.25em. Status shapes are 20px,
            an outlined circle with a check, an outlined triangle with a bang
            and a solid square with a down arrow in an inverted chip for
            Behind, each with its word in a bordered chip.
        focus: A 3px black outline with a 7px yellow ring outside it on white, and a 3px yellow outline on black.
        tone: Direct and literal, such as Hello, Mara, 4 tasks are overdue and Show overdue tasks.

    style224:
        number: 224
        run: 46
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Graphite neutral
        idea: The baseline professional dark, with balanced mid-dark graphite greys in three steps, quiet borders and one soft blue accent, so nothing but the work and the statuses draws the eye.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/224.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #1b1d21, the page background and the style sheet
            surface: #24272c, the sidebar, cards and the search field
            raised: #2d3137, hover rows, secondary buttons and status chips
            line: #3a3f47, every border, divider and meter track
            ink: #e7e9ec, text
            muted: #a4abb6, labels, meta and axis text
            accent: #8ab4f8, the primary button, meters, this week bars and focus
            onAccent: #0f1f3d, text on the accent
            accentSoft: #2b3546, the current nav item
            accentText: #b3cdfb, links and the current nav label
            lastWeek: #7b8494, last week bars
            ok: #7dd3a0, On track text and icon
            risk: #f0c36b, At risk text and icon
            bad: #f59b93, Behind and overdue text and icon
        type:
            One system stack, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
            Arial. Base 14px at 1.5. The greeting is 24px at 650, KPI figures
            26px at 650 with tabular numbers, card titles 14px at 650, meta and
            table headers 12px, and status chips 12px at 600.
        layout:
            A classic app frame. A 224px graphite sidebar holds a blue square B
            mark with the name, then six nav links with line icons, Home filled
            with the soft blue tile. The main column starts with a top bar
            ruled below, holding search on the left and New project, a square
            bell with a red dot and Mara Okafor on the right. Then the greeting
            Good morning, Mara over the date and a red clock line reading 4
            tasks are overdue. Four equal KPI cards follow, the overdue figure
            red with a clock. Below, a wide Projects card holds a table with
            columns for project and category, a status chip, a thin blue meter
            with percent, tasks done and due date. A narrower right column
            stacks the Tasks completed card with paired weekly bars and a
            legend with totals, then Recent activity with initials discs.
            Below 1100px the right column moves under the table. Below 760px
            the sidebar becomes a row of icons, KPIs go two by two and table
            rows become stacked blocks.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px card padding, 12px gaps between cards and KPIs, 28px page gutter.
        density: Medium. A full table of six projects sits beside the chart and the feed.
        corners: 8px cards, 6px buttons, fields and nav items, round chips and avatars.
        borders: 1px #3a3f47 on every card, row and field. Surfaces step up in lightness instead of using heavy lines.
        shadows: A faint 0 1px 2px black at 30 percent under cards only.
        icons:
            Rounded line icons at 1.75 stroke, 18px. Status uses a check circle
            for On track, a warning triangle for At risk and a crossed square
            for Behind, always beside the word inside a round chip. Overdue
            uses a clock.
        focus: A 2px soft blue outline offset 2px on every control, and around the whole search field.
        tone: Plain and neutral, such as Projects, Tasks completed, Recent activity and View all.
    style225:
        number: 225
        run: 46
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Midnight navy
        idea: Deep blue-black surfaces cut by crisp 1px hairlines, cool ice text and one ice cyan accent, laid out as a precise ruled instrument with a top nav and thin light figures.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/225.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            night: #070d1c, the page, the table ground and the style sheet
            panel: #0c1529, the masthead and swatch cells
            hairline: #1e2d4d, row rules, cell dividers and grid lines
            rule: #2e4370, section rules, the masthead edge and outlined controls
            ice: #dde8ff, text and figures
            frost: #93a6c9, labels, meta and axis text
            cyan: #8fd3ff, the primary button, the current tab, progress ticks, the this week line and focus
            onCyan: #03172a, text on the cyan button
            focusHalo: #13284a, a 4px halo outside the focus outline
            lastWeek: #6c7fa6, the dashed last week line and empty ticks
            ok: #6ee7b7, the On track word and check circle
            risk: #fcd34d, the At risk word and triangle
            bad: #fca5a5, Behind, the overdue box and the overdue figure
        type:
            Segoe UI first, then system-ui, Roboto, Helvetica Neue and Arial,
            with ui-monospace for times and dates. Base 14px. The greeting is
            30px at 300 with the name at 600, the four figures 40px at 200 with
            tabular numbers, section and column labels 11px caps tracked 0.14em,
            and status words 12px caps at 700 tracked 0.1em.
        layout:
            A full-width masthead on the panel tone holds an outlined cyan B
            square, the name, six text tabs with a 2px cyan underline on Home,
            then search, New project, a square bell and an outlined initials
            square with Mara Okafor. The body is one 1240px column. The date
            sits as a small caps label over Good morning, Mara, and on the right
            a red outlined box reads 4 tasks are overdue with a clock. The four
            figures are one strip ruled above and below and split by vertical
            hairlines, the overdue figure red. Projects is a full-width hairline
            table with columns for project, team, a ten-tick progress meter with
            percent, tasks, due and a status word in caps. Below, two columns
            hold Throughput, a line chart with last week dashed with round dots
            and this week solid cyan with square dots, and an Activity log whose
            times sit in a mono column on the left. Below 900px the tabs move
            to their own scrolling row. Below 700px a search field sits above
            the greeting, the figures go two by two and table rows stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 12px cell padding, 40 to 48px between sections, 24px gutters.
        density: Medium. Everything is one ruled column, then chart and log side by side.
        corners: 2px on buttons and fields. Everything else is square.
        borders: 1px hairlines everywhere, #1e2d4d between rows and cells and #2e4370 above and below each section.
        shadows: None. Depth comes only from hairlines and the panel tone of the masthead.
        icons:
            Square-capped line icons at 1.5 stroke, 16px. Progress is ten small
            outlined ticks, filled cyan for each tenth done. Status is a check
            circle, a triangle or a crossed square beside the word in caps.
        focus: A 1px cyan outline offset 2px plus a 4px deep blue halo.
        tone: Precise and instrument-like, such as Throughput, Activity log and Projects · 6 active.
    style226:
        number: 226
        run: 46
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: True black
        idea: Pure black for OLED screens with white type, razor-thin 1px separators and no tint anywhere, so the only colour on the screen is the status of a project.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/226.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            black: #000000, the page, every surface and the style sheet
            separator: #262626, 1px rules and the progress track
            white: #ffffff, text, figures, progress, this week bars, the primary button and focus
            grey: #a3a3a3, labels, meta and times
            dim: #737373, last week bars, link underlines and the secondary button edge
            ok: #4ade80, the On track word and check circle, the only green
            risk: #facc15, the At risk word and triangle, the only yellow
            bad: #ff7a7a, Behind, the overdue line and figure, the only red
        type:
            Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, then system-ui. Base 15px at 1.5.
            The greeting is 44px at 300 tracked minus 0.03em, the figures 52px
            at 200, project names 18px at 400, section labels 13px at 500 in
            grey, and status words 13px.
        layout:
            A slim top line ruled below holds the bold wordmark, six text links
            with Home white and underlined, an underline-only search field, a
            square white New project button with black text, a bare bell and an
            outlined round MO disc with Mara Okafor. Below, two columns split by
            a 1px rule. The 400px left column is today. It shows the date, Good
            morning, Mara. in light 44px type, a red clock line reading 4 tasks
            are overdue, the four figures as a two by two grid of huge thin
            numbers over small labels split by hairlines, and the chart with
            thin needle bars, grey for last week and white for this week, over
            the two totals. The right column lists Projects as rows with the
            name, category, percent with tasks, due date and the status word,
            and under each row a full-width 1px track with a 3px white progress
            line that doubles as the row separator. Activity follows as a ruled
            list with times on the right. Below 860px the nav and search take
            their own rows and the columns stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit with generous air. 40px gutters, 18px above each row, 48 to 56px between blocks.
        density: Low to medium. Two columns, a today column on the left and the work on the right.
        corners: Square everywhere. Only the avatar is round.
        borders: 1px #262626 separators between figures, columns and activity rows, nothing heavier. Fields are a single underline.
        shadows: None. Pure black cannot carry a shadow.
        icons:
            Thin line icons at 1.25 stroke, 16px, used only for status, search,
            the bell and overdue. Status is a check circle, a triangle or a
            crossed square with the word.
        focus: A 2px white outline offset 3px.
        tone: Terse and calm, such as Good morning, Mara. and Projects and Activity.
    style227:
        number: 227
        run: 46
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Warm charcoal
        idea: A brownish charcoal room lit by one amber lamp, with cream text, serif headings, soft rounded cards with progress rings and a journal of the day, cosy but still serious.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/227.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            charcoal: #1c1714, the page, the sidebar and the style sheet
            card: #272019, cards, fields and the journal
            ember: #322920, status chips and the top of the greeting card
            seam: #45392d, borders, dashed dividers and ring tracks
            cream: #f3e8d8, text and figures
            parchment: #c4b49e, labels, meta and times
            amber: #f0a94b, the primary button, progress rings, this week bars, journal icons and focus
            onAmber: #2a1903, text on the amber button
            amberGlow: #3d2e1b, the current nav item
            lastWeek: #97836b, last week bars
            ok: #a8d8a0, the sage On track chip
            risk: #f5d77a, the straw At risk chip
            bad: #ffa28c, the coral Behind chip and the overdue line
        type:
            Headings and figures in a serif stack, Iowan Old Style, Palatino
            Linotype, Palatino, Book Antiqua, Georgia. Body in system-ui, Segoe
            UI, Roboto. Base 15px at 1.55. The greeting is 34px serif at 500,
            figures 34px serif with old style numbers, section titles 21px serif
            at 500, project names 16px at 650, times 12px serif italic.
        layout:
            A 240px charcoal sidebar holds an amber flag icon and the name in
            serif, then six nav links with icons, Home on an amber glow tile
            with a 3px amber inner edge. The main column starts with a pill
            search on the left and an amber pill New project, a round bell and
            Mara Okafor on the right. A large rounded greeting card follows,
            shaded from ember to card, with the date, Good morning, Mara in
            serif and a coral line reading 4 tasks are overdue and need you
            first, and on its right the four figures in serif. Below sit two
            columns. The left holds Your projects as a grid of six rounded cards,
            each with name, category, a 56px amber progress ring with the
            percent inside, a status pill, then tasks and due date under a dashed
            seam, followed by a chart card titled Tasks finished, day by day.
            The right 340px column is Today's journal, a timeline with amber
            icons on a thin line and italic serif times. Below 1180px the
            journal moves under the projects. Below 760px the sidebar becomes a
            row of icons and the figures go two by two.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 18px card padding, 16px card gaps, 28 to 32px between areas and a 36px gutter.
        density: Comfortable. Six project cards with rings, the chart below and the journal at the side.
        corners: Soft. 18px greeting card, 14px cards, 10px nav items and fields, pill buttons and chips.
        borders: 1px #45392d around cards, dashed seams inside cards, a 3px amber inner edge on the current nav item.
        shadows: Warm and soft, 0 6px 18px black at 28 percent on cards and 0 10px 30px at 35 percent on the greeting card.
        icons:
            Rounded line icons at 1.8 stroke, 18px, amber in the journal. Status
            is a check circle, a triangle or a crossed square inside a pill with
            the word.
        focus: A 2px amber outline offset 3px.
        tone: Warm and personal, such as Your projects, Today's journal and 4 tasks are overdue and need you first.
    style228:
        number: 228
        run: 46
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Dim mode
        idea: A soft low-contrast slate around #22272e for long sessions, with muted colours, generous line height and one reading column that groups projects by what needs attention, while every text pair still passes AA.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/228.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            dim: #22272e, the page, the header and the style sheet
            panel: #2b3139, project groups, the chart box, summary chips and fields
            raised: #343b44, the current nav item, the secondary button and the avatar
            line: #444c56, every border and divider and the meter tracks
            text: #c9d1d9, body and names, held well below white
            muted: #9aa5b1, labels, meta and axis text
            blue: #7ea9dc, links, meters, this week bars and focus
            button: #41618a, the primary button fill, a muted blue
            onButton: #e6edf5, text on the primary button
            lastWeek: #7d8794, last week bars
            ok: #8fc49c, the On track word and icon
            risk: #d8b46c, the At risk word and icon
            bad: #e3958c, the Behind word and icon and the overdue line
        type:
            One stack, -apple-system, Segoe UI, system-ui, Roboto, Noto Sans.
            Base 15px at 1.65. The greeting is 26px at 500, the lede 17px,
            section titles 15px at 600, group labels 13px at 500 and meta 13px.
            Nothing is bold beyond 600.
        layout:
            A 200px sidebar ruled on the right holds a small blue dot with the
            name and six text-only nav links, Home on a raised tile. The header
            bar holds search, a muted blue New project button, a quiet bell and
            Mara Okafor. The content is one 760px reading column. It starts
            with the date and Good morning, Mara, then a lede where a clock and
            4 tasks are overdue sit in soft red, followed by Start there, then
            the rest of the week. The four figures follow as small inline chips
            with the number in bold, the overdue chip red. Projects by status
            then shows three groups in order, Behind, At risk and On track, each
            labelled with its status and a count, and each a bordered panel of
            rows with name, category, a thin blue meter with percent, due date
            and tasks. Tasks completed is a bordered chart box with a caption
            naming the totals and colours. Recent activity is a ruled list with
            times on the right. Below 760px the sidebar becomes a scrolling row
            and search moves to its own row.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 12px row padding, 48px between sections, a 760px column with 32px sides.
        density: Low. One column, with projects grouped into Behind, At risk and On track.
        corners: 6px on panels, fields, buttons and chips. Round avatar.
        borders: 1px #444c56 around panels and between rows. No heavier rules.
        shadows: None. Low glare matters more than depth.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.6 stroke, 17px, only where they carry meaning.
            Status is a check circle, a triangle or a crossed square with the
            word, also used as the group heading.
        focus: A 2px soft blue outline offset 2px.
        tone: Calm and guiding, such as 4 tasks are overdue. Start there, then the rest of the week.

    style229:
        number: 229
        run: 47
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Dark icon rail
        idea: A dense three-pane dark work surface, with a near-black icon rail, a list pane holding the greeting, figures and projects, and a wider detail pane with Mobile app 2.0 open, stepped in cool greys with one violet accent.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/229.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            rail: #0b0c10, the 60px icon rail
            listPane: #14161c, the list pane, fields and the style sheet
            detailPane: #1a1d24, the detail pane and its top bar
            card: #21252e, cards and the facts strip
            line: #2e333d, borders, dividers and meter tracks
            ink: #e4e6ec, text
            muted: #9ea4b2, meta, labels and axis text
            railInk: #9aa0ad, rail icons that are not current
            violet: #b49cff, the primary button, the selected edge, meters, this week bars, tags and focus
            onViolet: #1b1036, text on violet
            selected: #2a2440, the selected project row and the current rail item
            lastWeek: #7a8192, outlined last week bars
            ok: #7fd8a6, the outlined On track tag
            risk: #f3c56a, the outlined At risk tag
            bad: #ff9a8f, the outlined Behind tag and the overdue line
        type:
            One system stack, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Ubuntu. Base 13px at
            1.45. The detail title is 24px at 650, the greeting 18px at 650,
            figures 20px at 650 with tabular numbers, pane labels 11px caps
            tracked 0.08em, tags 11.5px at 650.
        layout:
            Three columns at full height. The 60px rail holds a violet B tile,
            six icon-only links with names and tooltips, Home on a violet tinted
            tile with a 3px violet edge bar, and the MO disc at the foot. The
            340px list pane holds the date, Good morning, Mara, a red clock line
            reading 4 tasks are overdue, the four figures as a two by two grid
            split by 1px lines, then a Projects label with the count and six
            rows. Each row has the name, an outlined status tag, category and
            due date, and a 3px meter with percent and done over total. Mobile
            app 2.0 is selected with a violet tint and a violet left edge. The
            detail pane has a top bar with search and a slash key hint, New
            project, a bell and Mara Okafor. Below sit a breadcrumb Projects,
            Engineering, Mobile app 2.0, the 24px title with its At risk tag and
            an Open project button, the line Engineering · due 2 Dec, 32 days
            left, a four-cell facts strip for progress, tasks done, due and
            status, then two cards side by side. The chart card shows last week
            as outlined bars and this week as solid violet. The Team activity
            card tags the two items about Mobile app 2.0 with This project.
            Below 1180px the cards stack. Below 860px the rail becomes a sticky
            top row, and the top bar, the list pane and the detail follow in
            that order.
        spacing: An 8px unit, tight. 16 to 20px pane padding, 9px row padding, 14px between cards.
        density: Dense. Three panes at once, a 13px body and small figures.
        corners: 6px panes, cards and buttons, 8px rail tiles, 4px tags, round avatars.
        borders: 1px #2e333d between panes, rows and cells. A 3px violet edge on the selected row and the current rail item.
        shadows: None. Panes separate by four stepped greys from #0b0c10 to #21252e.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.75 stroke, 16px, and 20px in the rail. Status tags
            are outlined in the status colour with a check circle, a triangle or
            a crossed square and the word.
        focus: A 2px violet outline offset 2px.
        tone: Plain and neutral, such as Team activity, Tasks completed, Open project and This project.
    style230:
        number: 230
        run: 47
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Dark command first
        idea: A sparse dark home centred on one large command field with keyboard hints, where the urgent items appear as palette rows under it and the rest of the dashboard sits quietly below in small monospace-labelled lists.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/230.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            void: #0d0e10, the page and the style sheet
            palette: #16181c, the command panel, fields and hover rows
            key: #1f2328, key caps, the current nav item and the secondary button
            line: #2b2f36, panel edges, group dividers, rules and meter tracks
            ink: #ececee, text
            muted: #9ca1aa, labels, hints, meta and times
            teal: #5fd4c4, the selected row edge, meters, this week bars, the primary button and focus
            onTeal: #062a25, text on teal
            tealWash: #13302c, the selected palette row
            lastWeek: #6f7580, last week bars
            ok: #7ddc9a, the On track word and icon
            risk: #f2c66d, the At risk word and icon
            bad: #ff9585, the Behind word and icon and the overdue row
        type:
            Body in system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto. Labels, figures, keys and times
            in ui-monospace, SF Mono, Cascadia Code, Menlo, Consolas. The
            command input is 18px, the greeting line 15px, rows 14px, figures
            24px mono at 600, group labels 11px mono caps at 600 tracked 0.08em,
            key caps 11.5px mono.
        layout:
            A borderless top line holds the lowercase mono wordmark in teal, six
            small text links with Home on a key tile, then a square bell and an
            MO tile with Mara Okafor. The first screen is mostly empty. Centred
            at 720px sit the line Good morning, Mara · Saturday 31 October 2026
            and then the command panel with a deep shadow. Its field reads
            Search projects and tasks, or type a command with a Ctrl K key. Under
            the field a Needs you group lists 4 tasks are overdue as the selected
            row with a teal edge and an Enter key, then Billing migration with
            Behind and Mobile app 2.0 with At risk. An Actions group holds the
            New project button as a palette row with an N key. A row of hints
            follows with keys for move, open, new project, 1 to 6 to jump and
            search. Far below, the four figures sit in one mono strip ruled
            above and below. Then two columns. Projects is a compact numbered
            list from 1 to 6 with name, category, due, tasks, a teal meter and
            the status. The right column holds a small Completed per day chart
            with the totals in mono and an Activity list with mono times on the
            left. Below 700px the nav takes its own row, only two hints show,
            the figures go two by two and lists stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 72px of air above and below the command panel, 8 to 10px palette row padding.
        density: Sparse at the top, compact below. One field owns the first screen.
        corners: 14px command panel, 8px rows and buttons, 5px key caps.
        borders: 1px #2b2f36 on the panel and dividers. Key caps have a 2px bottom edge.
        shadows: One deep shadow, 0 20px 60px black at 55 percent, under the command panel only.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.75 stroke, 16px, and 20px in the field. Status is a
            check circle, a triangle or a crossed square with the word in mono.
        focus: A 2px teal outline offset 2px, and a 2px inset teal ring on the command field.
        tone: Imperative and keyboard-led, such as Needs you, Actions, move, open and 1 to 6 to jump.
    style231:
        number: 231
        run: 47
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Dark bento
        idea: An asymmetric bento of rounded tiles in different sizes and faint tints on near-black, where size carries priority, so the greeting and the overdue count are the biggest tiles and the two troubled projects outsize the healthy ones.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/231.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            night: #09090b, the page gaps and the style sheet
            tile: #151518, plain tiles, fields and the nav pill
            greetingTile: #1a1724, the violet tinted greeting and hours tiles
            overdueTile: #2a1517, the coral tinted overdue tile
            overdueInk: #ffb4a8, text and the huge figure on the overdue tile
            chartTile: #0f1b1c, the teal tinted chart tile
            okTile: #111a15, faint green project tiles
            riskTile: #211c10, the faint amber project tile
            badTile: #261416, the faint red project tile
            line: #2a2a30, edges of fields and the nav pill
            ink: #f4f4f5, text, figures, progress fill and the current nav pill
            muted: #a1a1aa, labels and meta
            pink: #ff8fb1, the logo, the primary button and focus
            onPink: #2e0614, text on pink
            teal: #4fd1c5, this week bars
            lastWeek: #71717a, last week bars
            ok: #86e0a5, the On track chip
            risk: #f5cb6b, the At risk chip
            bad: #ff9a8a, the Behind chip and the overdue line
        type:
            One system stack, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue. Base
            14px. The greeting is 52px at 850 tracked minus 0.04em, the overdue
            figure 112px at 900, the hours figure 88px, other tile figures 44px
            at 850, project percents 30px and 64px on the largest tile, project
            names 16px at 800, tile labels 13px at 700 in muted.
        layout:
            A top row holds a pink rounded B logo, a pill nav with icons and
            labels where Home is a white pill with dark text, a pill search, a
            pink pill New project, a round bell and a rounded MO tile named Mara
            Okafor. The bento is a 12 column grid with 12px gutters. The first
            two rows give six columns to the greeting tile with the date, Good
            morning, Mara. in 52px heavy type and 4 tasks are overdue in coral,
            three columns to the overdue tile with a 112px figure 4 and Clear
            these first, and three columns stacked with Active projects 6 and
            Tasks due this week 23. The third row gives nine columns to the
            teal tinted chart tile with values over the bars and the totals, and
            three to the hours tile with 186. The last row gives eight columns
            to a nested project bento of four columns. Billing migration takes a
            two by two tile, Mobile app 2.0 a wide tile, Website redesign and
            Q4 customer survey single tiles, and Spring catalogue and Onboarding
            emails wide tiles. Each project tile is tinted by status and holds a
            status chip, name, category and due, a big percent, a thick white
            track and tasks. Four columns go to What happened, the activity
            list. Below 1180px nav labels hide and tiles reflow. Below 700px the
            grid is two columns and the chart scrolls inside its tile.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 12px gutters between every tile, 22px tile padding, 32px in the greeting tile.
        density: Medium. Few words per tile and very large figures, with size showing priority.
        corners: Big. 22px tiles, 14px logo, avatar and fields, pill nav, buttons and chips.
        borders: None on tiles, which separate by tint and gutter. Only the nav pill and fields carry 1px #2a2a30.
        shadows: None. Near-black gutters do the work.
        icons:
            Bold line icons at 2px stroke, 18px. Status chips sit on a
            translucent black pill with a check circle, a triangle or a crossed
            square and the word.
        focus: A 3px pink outline offset 3px.
        tone: Punchy and direct, such as Good morning, Mara., Clear these first and What happened.
    style232:
        number: 232
        run: 47
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Dark timeline
        idea: The dashboard read as a schedule, where every project is a bar on a shared date axis from October to January with its done share filled, its due date marked and one orange today line cutting through all of them.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/232.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            ground: #0f1113, the page, fields and the style sheet
            panel: #16191c, the top bar, panels and lanes
            band: #1b1f23, the remaining part of a bar, the current tab and the secondary button
            line: #2a2f35, panel edges, axis rules and the activity spine
            grid: #22272c, weekly grid lines and lane dividers
            ink: #e8eaed, text and the due diamonds
            muted: #9ea6af, labels, dates and axis text
            orange: #ff9f5a, the today line and tag, the date line, the current tab edge, the primary button and focus
            onOrange: #2b1302, text on orange
            done: #86b3ff, the done part of each bar and this week bars
            remaining: #68737f, the bar outline for remaining time
            lastWeek: #6e7884, last week bars
            ok: #7fd69e, the On track word and icon
            risk: #f2c66a, the At risk word and icon
            bad: #ff978a, the Behind word and icon and the overdue line
        type:
            Segoe UI first, then system-ui, Roboto. Dates, axis labels and
            figures in ui-monospace, Cascadia Mono, Menlo, Consolas. Base 14px.
            The greeting is 24px at 650, figures 20px mono at 600, lane names
            14px at 600, dates and axis labels 12px mono, the today tag 11px mono
            at 700.
        layout:
            A 56px panel top bar holds an orange calendar icon with the name, a
            segmented nav with Home raised and edged orange below, search, an
            orange New project button, a square bell and a square MO tile with
            Mara Okafor. Below, the date in orange mono sits over Good morning,
            Mara and a red line reading 4 tasks are overdue, with the four
            figures as one bordered strip on the right. The main panel is
            Project timeline · October to January with a key for done,
            remaining, due date and today. A 250px label column, sticky when the
            panel scrolls, lists each project with category, tasks and status.
            The track area spans 1 October 2026 to 20 January 2027 with month
            labels and weekly grid lines. Each lane draws a bar from a sample
            start date to the due date, outlined for remaining time and filled
            blue for the done share, ends in a diamond with the percent and due
            date, and the orange today line at 31 October crosses every lane
            under a Today 31 Oct tag. Below sit two panels, the daily chart with
            paired weekly bars and the totals in its header, and Recent activity
            as a vertical spine with dots, the newest dot orange. Below 960px
            the nav and search take their own rows and the lower panels stack.
            Below 700px the timeline scrolls sideways inside its panel.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 62px lanes, 16px panel padding, 16px between panels.
        density: Medium. Six lanes on one axis, then chart and activity side by side.
        corners: 4px panels, buttons and fields, 3px bars and the today tag.
        borders: 1px #2a2f35 on panels and the axis, #22272c weekly grid lines. Bars have a 1.5px outline for remaining time.
        shadows: None. The orange today line is the only thing that stands out.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.8 stroke, 16px, and a diamond for each due date.
            Status is a check circle, a triangle or a crossed square with the
            word.
        focus: A 2px orange outline offset 2px, also on the scrolling timeline region.
        tone: Schedule-minded, such as Project timeline, Today 31 Oct, due 20 Nov and Newest first.
    style233:
        number: 233
        run: 47
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Dark floating panels
        idea: Opaque indigo panels float over a deep tinted backdrop of slow indigo and teal light, each lifted by a soft periwinkle glow edge and a long shadow, with a floating dock for navigation and a floating pill for the header.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/233.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            deep: #0b0d22, the backdrop base and the style sheet
            indigoLight: #1d1a5c, the upper left backdrop glow
            tealLight: #0b3340, the right backdrop glow
            panel: #151a3c, every floating panel, the dock and the header pill
            inset: #1b2148, rows inside panels, icon tiles and fields
            line: #2c3470, meter tracks, grid lines and field edges
            glowEdge: #5a68c8, the 1px edge on the current dock item and the secondary button
            ink: #eef0ff, text
            muted: #aab1d6, labels and meta
            periwinkle: #a5b4ff, the primary button, meters, the this week line, icons and focus
            onPeriwinkle: #10153a, text on periwinkle
            lastWeek: #7680b0, the dashed last week line
            ok: #7ee8b5, the On track pill
            risk: #ffd479, the At risk pill
            bad: #ffa3b3, the Behind pill and the overdue pill
        type:
            A rounded stack, ui-rounded, SF Pro Rounded, Nunito, then system-ui,
            Segoe UI, Roboto. Base 14px at 1.5. The greeting is 40px at 700,
            chip figures 26px at 800, panel titles 17px at 700, project names
            14px at 700, status pills 12.5px at 700.
        layout:
            The whole screen is a stage with a deep navy base, two large soft
            radial glows in indigo and teal, and two faint thin ring shapes
            clipped by the stage. A floating vertical dock on the left holds a
            periwinkle B tile and six icon-only links with names, Home in an
            inset tile with a glowing edge. A long floating header pill holds
            search, a glowing periwinkle New project pill, a round bell and a
            gradient MO disc with Mara Okafor. The greeting sits straight on the
            backdrop with the date, Good morning, Mara and a pill reading 4
            tasks are overdue with a soft red ring and glow. On the right the
            four figures float as small glowing chips. Below, two columns of
            panels with 28px gaps. Projects, 6 in flight, holds six inset
            rounded rows with name, category and due, a ringed status pill, and
            a glowing periwinkle meter with percent and tasks. The right column
            holds Tasks completed as a glowing line chart, last week dashed and
            this week solid, and Recent activity with periwinkle icons in inset
            tiles. Below 1100px the columns stack. Below 760px the dock becomes
            a horizontal bar near the foot of the screen and the figures go two
            by two.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 28px gaps between panels so the backdrop shows, 22px panel padding, 10px between rows.
        density: Airy. Panels are few and large, with the greeting straight on the backdrop.
        corners: Very round. 22px panels, 28px dock, 16px rows, pill header, buttons and status.
        borders: No hard borders. Each panel has a 1px periwinkle ring at 22 percent as part of its glow.
        shadows: A floating glow made of 0 18px 50px deep navy at 60 percent plus a 36px periwinkle halo at 14 percent.
        icons:
            Round line icons at 1.8 stroke, 18px, periwinkle inside inset tiles.
            Status is a check circle, a triangle or a crossed square in a pill
            ringed in its colour, always with the word.
        focus: A 2px periwinkle outline offset 3px plus a 6px soft periwinkle halo.
        tone: Light and friendly, such as 6 in flight, Recent activity and Good morning, Mara.

    style234:
        number: 234
        run: 48
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Deep forest
        idea:
            A calm woodland workspace in layered pine greens, where projects sit
            as soft cards with growth ring meters, the week is a moss line over a
            fern dashed line, and activity follows a winding trail.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/234.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            pine: #0e1d17, the page and the style sheet
            canopy: #132820, the sidebar and the top bar
            bark: #18322a, cards, tiles and panels
            understory: #1f3d33, meter tracks, the current nav tile and the search field
            line: #2f5446, card borders and dividers
            ink: #e3efe7, text and figures
            lichen: #a9c4b5, meta, labels, dates and day letters
            moss: #b5cf7a, the primary button, ring meters, this week line, links and focus
            fern: #7fb89a, the last week dashed line and trail dots
            ok: #9adbb0, On track text and check circle
            risk: #f0cf7a, At risk text and triangle
            bad: #f5a596, Behind and overdue text, crossed square and clock
        type:
            One humanist stack, Seravek, Gill Sans Nova, Ubuntu, Calibri, DejaVu
            Sans, sans-serif. Base 15px at 1.55. The greeting is 30px at 600, tile
            figures 34px at 600 with tabular numbers, section titles 19px at 600,
            card titles 16px at 600, meta 13px in lichen, and ring percentages
            13px bold.
        layout:
            A 232px canopy sidebar holds a moss leaf mark with the Brightwork
            name, the six nav links as rounded rows with Home on an understory
            tile with a moss notch, and Mara Okafor with a round initials disc at
            the foot. The main area has a canopy top bar with a pill search field,
            a round bell with a count, and a moss New project pill. Below sit the
            greeting Good morning, Mara with the date and a line reading 4 tasks
            are overdue with a clock in coral. Four rounded bark tiles show the
            figures with a small icon each, overdue in coral. Projects are a three
            column grid of bark cards, each with a 56px ring meter holding the
            percent, the name, category, a status line, tasks done and the due
            date. Last, the chart and the activity sit side by side, the chart a
            line chart by weekday with this week as a moss line over a soft moss
            area and last week as a dashed fern line, the activity a vertical
            trail with fern dots and small icons. Below 900px the sidebar becomes
            a top band with the nav wrapping in rows, cards go to one column and
            the chart and trail stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px card padding, 16px gaps in grids, 32px between sections.
        density: Airy to medium. Cards breathe, six projects fill two rows of three.
        corners: Soft. 16px cards and tiles, pill buttons and search, round rings and dots.
        borders:
            1px line on cards and tiles, none on the sidebar. The current nav tile
            has a 3px moss notch.
        shadows: One soft deep shadow under cards, 0 8px 24px of near-black at 35 percent.
        icons:
            Rounded line icons at 1.8px stroke sized to the text. Status uses a
            check circle, a triangle with a bang and a crossed square, always with
            the word, overdue a clock.
        focus: A 2px moss outline offset 3px with a 6px dim moss halo.
        tone: Calm and kind, such as Good morning, Mara and A steady week on the trail.
    style235:
        number: 235
        run: 48
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Aubergine
        idea:
            A plush plum workspace of rounded capsules, with a violet hero that
            holds the greeting and four pill figures, projects as rows with
            segmented pill meters, and rose as the single warm accent.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/235.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            night: #1a1020, the page and the style sheet
            plum: #221528, the top bar
            skin: #2a1a31, panels and project rows
            flesh: #36223f, pill figures, the search field, empty meter segments and the current nav pill
            heroTop: #3b2449, the top of the hero gradient
            line: #4d3557, panel borders and row dividers
            ink: #f3e8f5, text and figures
            mauve: #c9b2cf, meta, labels and axis text
            violet: #b9a0ec, last week capsules, category bubbles and secondary outlines
            rose: #f4a3c0, the primary button, filled meter segments, this week capsules, links and focus
            roseInk: #2b0f1d, text on rose
            ok: #93e0c0, On track text and check circle
            risk: #f3d27a, At risk text and triangle
            bad: #ffab91, Behind and overdue text, crossed square and clock
        type:
            One geometric stack, Avenir Next, Century Gothic, Futura, URW Gothic,
            Trebuchet MS, sans-serif. Base 14px at 1.5. The greeting is 40px at
            700, pill figures 32px at 700 with tabular numbers, panel titles 20px
            at 700, project names 16px at 600, meta 13px in mauve, and nav pills
            14px at 600.
        layout:
            A plum top bar holds a rose round mark with the Brightwork name, the
            six nav links as pills with Home filled, a pill search field, a round
            bell, a rose New project pill and Mara Okafor with a round initials
            disc. Under it a wide hero capsule with 28px corners fades from violet
            plum at top to the panel colour. Its left side holds Hello, Mara, the
            date and a rounded overdue pill reading 4 tasks are overdue with a
            clock. Its right side holds the four figures as a two by two grid of
            pill capsules, each a large number beside a short label. Below, two
            columns. The wide left panel lists the six projects as rows with a
            round violet category bubble showing the first letter, the name and
            category, a status pill, a ten segment pill meter with the percent,
            tasks done and the due date. The narrow right column holds the chart
            as paired capsules by weekday, last week violet outlines and this week
            rose fills with totals, then the activity as rows with round initials.
            Below 980px the columns stack, below 640px the nav pills wrap and
            project rows reflow into two lines.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px panel padding, 16px row padding, 24px between panels.
        density: Medium. Generous hero, compact project rows.
        corners:
            Very round. 28px hero, 22px panels, pills on every button, field,
            chip, meter and bar.
        borders: 1px line on panels and between rows. Last week capsules are 2px violet outlines.
        shadows:
            A soft plum glow under the hero, 0 16px 40px of near-black at 45
            percent, none elsewhere.
        icons:
            Rounded line icons at 1.8px stroke. Status uses a check circle, a
            triangle with a bang and a crossed square inside a pill with the word,
            overdue a clock.
        focus: A 2px rose outline offset 3px.
        tone: Warm and personal, such as Hello, Mara and This week feels busier.
    style236:
        number: 236
        run: 48
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Espresso
        idea:
            A warm coffee house menu board in dark roast browns, where projects
            are listed like menu items with dotted leaders running to their
            percent, figures sit under crema rules, and activity prints on a
            narrow order ticket.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/236.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            roast: #1b130e, the page and the style sheet
            bean: #241913, the header band
            board: #2b1f17, the menu board and chart panel
            cup: #382a20, the search field, meter tracks and the ticket
            line: #54402f, board borders, rules and leaders
            ink: #f3e7d8, text and figures
            steam: #cbb59c, meta, labels, dates and axis text
            crema: #e4b97f, the primary button, figures rules, meters, this week bars, links and focus
            cremaInk: #241508, text on crema
            caramel: #b8844f, last week bar outlines and hatching
            ok: #a9d48f, On track text and check circle
            risk: #f2c862, At risk text and triangle
            bad: #f4977f, Behind and overdue text, crossed square and clock
        type:
            Three warm stacks. Headings use Iowan Old Style, Palatino Linotype,
            Palatino, Book Antiqua, Georgia, serif, with the greeting 38px italic
            at 500, house figures 40px, board headings 22px at 600 and menu items
            18px at 500. Body and meta use Optima, Candara, Segoe UI, sans-serif
            at 14px and 1.5. The order ticket uses Courier New, ui-monospace at
            13px. Nav and small labels are 12px caps tracked 0.14em.
        layout:
            One centred 1080px column. A two tier bean header band holds a serif
            Brightwork wordmark with a small cup mark at left and a search field,
            a bell, a crema New project button and Mara Okafor at right, then
            under a thin rule the six nav links centred as caps text with a crema
            underline under Home. Below, the greeting is centred like a board
            title, with the date and a line reading 4 tasks are overdue with a
            clock in coral. The four figures sit in a row between crema top and
            bottom rules, split by thin vertical rules, each a large serif number
            over a caps label, overdue in coral. The main board is a bordered dark
            panel titled The projects, a two column menu where each item is a
            serif name, a dotted leader and the percent like a price, then
            category, tasks and due date, a 3px crema meter and the status word
            with its symbol. Last, two blocks side by side, a wide chart panel of
            paired bars by weekday with last week as hatched caramel outlines and
            this week solid crema, and a narrow order ticket on a cup surface with
            a zigzag top and bottom edge, listing activity with mono times. Below
            820px the menu becomes one column, figures go two by two and the
            ticket drops under the chart.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 32px board padding, 20px between menu items, 40px between blocks.
        density: Medium. Menu items are roomy, the ticket is tight.
        corners: Mostly square with gentle 6px corners on the board, fields and buttons.
        borders:
            1px line around the board and chart, crema 2px rules above and below
            the figures, dotted leaders in line colour.
        shadows:
            An inset 0 0 0 4px roast band inside the board border, like a frame,
            and no drop shadows.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.6px stroke sized to the text. Status uses a check
            circle, a triangle with a bang and a crossed square, always with the
            word, overdue a clock.
        focus: A 2px crema outline offset 3px.
        tone: Warm and unhurried, such as Good morning, Mara, The projects and Today's ticket.
    style237:
        number: 237
        run: 48
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Dark enterprise
        idea:
            A formal dark suite shell with an app switcher bar, a tree navigation
            that opens Projects into its six projects, breadcrumbs and a command
            bar, square live tiles and a dense sortable data grid, all square and
            quietly blue.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/237.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            base: #101317, the page behind the content and the style sheet
            shell: #181c21, the suite bar, the tree pane and the command bar
            panel: #1d2228, tiles, the grid and panels
            header: #242a31, grid header rows, panel title bars, the search box and the current tree item
            line: #343c45, every border, grid rule and tree guide
            ink: #e6e9ed, text and figures
            muted: #a2acb8, labels, meta, column headers and axis text
            blue: #5aa6f7, links, the current tree edge, this week columns, meters and focus
            action: #2a68b5, the primary button fill behind white text
            slate: #6f7c8b, last week columns
            ok: #6fd08c, On track text and check circle
            risk: #f0c24e, At risk text and triangle
            bad: #ff8f85, Behind and overdue text, crossed square and clock
        type:
            One system UI stack, Segoe UI, system-ui, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
            Arial, sans-serif. Base 13px at 1.4. The page title greeting is 24px
            at 600, tile figures 40px at 300 light with tabular numbers, panel
            title bars 14px at 600, grid cells and tree items 13px, breadcrumbs
            and meta 12px, and column headers 11px caps at 600 tracked 0.06em.
        layout:
            A full shell. A 44px suite bar holds a square app grid button, the
            Brightwork name, an app switcher of Tracker, Canvas, Drive, Code and
            Ops with Tracker underlined, a centred square search box, a bell and
            Mara Okafor with a square initials tile. Under it a 248px tree pane
            lists Home as current with a blue left edge, Projects open with tree
            guides to its six projects, each with a small status shape, then
            Tasks, Team, Reports and Settings. The content area starts with a
            command bar holding a blue New project button, Export, Refresh and a
            view label, then breadcrumbs Brightwork, Home, Overview. The greeting
            is the page title with the date beside it, then a message bar with a
            4px coral left edge reading 4 tasks are overdue with a clock and a
            Review link. Four square tiles sit in a row, each a caps label, a 40px
            light figure and an icon, overdue with a coral edge. The projects are
            a dense data grid with a title bar, column headers with sort marks,
            and columns for project, department, status, progress, tasks and due.
            Last, two panels with grey title bars side by side, a column chart of
            all fourteen days in sequence with a dashed divider between the weeks,
            slate last week and blue this week, and an activity grid with time,
            person and event columns. Below 960px the tree pane collapses to a row
            of nav buttons, tiles go two by two and the grid scrolls inside its
            panel.
        spacing: A 4px unit. 12px panel padding, 8px by 12px grid cells, 16px between blocks.
        density: Dense. Many rows and small type, everything visible at once on a laptop.
        corners: Square everywhere, 0px on tiles, panels, buttons and fields.
        borders:
            1px line around every pane, panel and grid row. A 3px blue edge marks
            the current tree item and a 4px coral edge marks the message bar.
        shadows: None. Depth comes from four flat greys stepping from base to header.
        icons:
            Fine line icons at 1.5px stroke, 16px. Status uses a check circle, a
            triangle with a bang and a crossed square, always with the word,
            overdue a clock.
        focus: A 2px blue outline inset by 1px inside grid rows and offset 2px elsewhere.
        tone: Formal and exact, such as Overview, Projects, 6 items and Activity, last 24 hours.
    style238:
        number: 238
        run: 48
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Night shift clinical
        idea:
            A calm dark teal shift board made for reading at 3 in the morning,
            with large legible type, figures shown as quiet readouts down a
            station column, projects as roomy bed style cards, a soft monitor
            trace for the fortnight and handover notes for activity.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/238.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            ward: #0b1a1d, the page and the style sheet
            station: #0f2226, the header, the tab bar and the station column
            card: #13292d, project cards, readouts and panels
            raised: #1a3439, bar tracks, the current tab, the search field and note times
            line: #2a4a50, borders and dividers
            ink: #dcebe9, text and figures, softened from white to cut glare
            muted: #9dbcb9, labels, meta and axis text
            teal: #6fd3c6, the primary button, bars, this week trace, the current tab edge and focus
            tealInk: #062a27, text on teal
            dimTrace: #5f8f8b, the last week trace
            notice: #262718, the gentle overdue notice background
            ok: #86d9a8, On track text and check circle
            risk: #efc98a, At risk text, triangle and the notice edge
            bad: #f2a7a0, Behind and overdue text, crossed square and clock
        type:
            One highly legible stack, Atkinson Hyperlegible, Verdana, Segoe UI,
            sans-serif, with Cascadia Mono, Consolas, ui-monospace for note times.
            Base 17px at 1.6 and nothing smaller than 15px. The greeting is 30px
            at 700, readouts 36px at 700 with tabular numbers, card titles 20px at
            700, field labels 15px at 700 in muted.
        layout:
            A station header holds a rounded teal mark, the Brightwork name, a
            wide search field, a bell, a teal New project button and Mara Okafor
            with a round initials disc. Under it a tab bar of six large tabs, each
            an icon above its word, Home current on a raised fill with a 3px teal
            top edge. The body has two columns. The 320px station column on the
            left holds the greeting Hello, Mara, the date, a gentle notice card
            with a muted amber left edge reading 4 tasks are overdue with a clock
            and a View tasks link, then the four figures as readout rows, a muted
            label at left and a 36px figure at right, divided by lines. The wide
            right column holds the six projects as two columns of roomy cards,
            each with the name, category, a status badge, a 14px rounded bar with
            the percent at its end, and two labelled fields for tasks and due
            date. Below sit the chart as a monitor style trace across all fourteen
            days on a faint grid, with the week split by a gap, last week dim and
            this week bright teal with dots and values, and the handover notes,
            each with a mono time on a raised block, the event and its project.
            Below 900px the station column moves above the cards, below 600px the
            tabs become a three by two grid and cards go to one column.
        spacing:
            An 8px unit. 24px card padding, 20px row padding in readouts, 24px
            gaps, 48px minimum targets.
        density: Low. Large type and roomy cards so nothing is misread when tired.
        corners: Gentle. 12px cards, 10px buttons and fields, round bars and badges.
        borders:
            1px line on cards and readout dividers. The notice has a 4px muted
            amber left edge and the current tab a 3px teal top edge.
        shadows: None. Glare is the enemy, so depth is a small step in teal greys.
        icons:
            Rounded line icons at 2px stroke, 20px in tabs, sized to text
            elsewhere. Status uses a check circle, a triangle with a bang and a
            crossed square, always with the word, overdue a clock.
        focus: A 3px teal outline offset 3px, thick enough to find at a glance.
        tone: Gentle and clear, such as Hello, Mara, Handover notes and 4 tasks are overdue.

    style239:
        number: 239
        run: 49
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Chalkboard
        idea:
            The whole dashboard is written up on a slate chalkboard in a wooden
            frame, with handwritten headings, wobbly chalk boxes, tally marks
            beside the counts, hatched chalk bars and soft eraser smudges.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/239.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            slate: #27302c, the board, the page and the style sheet
            deepSlate: #202824, the header strip and field fills
            smudge: #323b37, the lightest eraser smudge, the peak any text sits on
            frame: #5a3d26, the wooden frame and the chalk tray
            chalk: #ecebe4, text, box outlines and last week bars
            dust: #b9bdb5, meta, labels and dates
            yellow: #f2e18c, the primary button, this week bars, progress hatching, the Home circle and focus
            blue: #a8d4f0, links and the activity arrows
            ok: #b9e4a7, On track text and check circle
            risk: #f7c38a, At risk text and triangle
            bad: #f4a9b8, Behind and overdue text, crossed square, clock and the overdue tally
        type:
            Two stacks. Headings and counts are handwriting, Chalkboard SE,
            Chalkboard, Segoe Print, Bradley Hand, Comic Sans MS, cursive, with
            the greeting 42px at 700, counts 40px, section headings 28px and box
            titles 20px. Body text is Trebuchet MS, Segoe UI, sans-serif at 16px
            and 1.55, meta 14px italic in dust. All chalk text carries a faint 1px
            chalk blur.
        layout:
            The screen is a chalkboard inside a 14px wooden frame with a chalk
            tray along the bottom edge holding three drawn chalk sticks. Across
            the top the Brightwork name is written by hand, the six nav words
            follow with a wobbly yellow circle drawn round Home, then a dashed
            chalk search box, a chalk bell, a yellow outlined New project box and
            Mara Okafor. The greeting Good morning, Mara! is written large with a
            squiggle under it, then the date and a pink line reading 4 tasks are
            overdue with a clock. Four wobbly chalk boxes hold the counts, with
            tally marks drawn beside active projects and overdue tasks. Projects
            is a three column grid of wobbly boxes, each with the handwritten
            name, category, a status mark drawn in chalk with its word, a hatched
            yellow progress bar with the percent, tasks done and due date. Below,
            the chart is chalk columns across all fourteen days, last week as
            plain chalk outlines and this week hatched yellow, with values on top
            and a written note of the totals, beside the activity written as a
            list with blue chalk arrows. Soft eraser smudges sit behind the
            content. Below 900px the projects go to two columns and the chart and
            list stack, below 600px everything is one column and the frame thins
            to 6px.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 20px box padding, 24px gaps, 40px between board sections.
        density: Medium. Boxes are generous like a teacher's board.
        corners: Hand drawn. Every box uses uneven elliptical corners so no two edges match.
        borders:
            2px chalk lines with uneven corners, dashed for the search box, a 14px
            wooden frame round the board.
        shadows:
            No drop shadows. Text carries a 1px chalk blur and the board carries
            soft white smudges at 4 to 6 percent.
        icons:
            Chalk line icons at 2.2px stroke with rough round ends. Status uses a
            drawn circle with a tick, a triangle with a bang and a crossed box,
            always with the word, overdue a clock.
        focus: A 3px dashed yellow outline offset 4px, like a ring drawn in chalk.
        tone: Friendly classroom, such as Good morning, Mara!, Still to do and What happened today.
    style240:
        number: 240
        run: 49
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Casino felt
        idea:
            The dashboard is laid out on a dark green felt table inside a padded
            leather rail, with the four figures as stacked chips, the projects
            dealt as a fanned hand of dark cards with corner indices, and the
            fortnight drawn as chip stacks.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/240.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            rail: #1c120c, the page, the padded rail, the header and the style sheet
            leather: #26180f, the activity log, fields and the style sheet panels
            felt: #0f3d2c, the table surface at its edges
            feltLight: #145238, the lit centre of the table, the brightest felt any text sits on
            card: #0d2a1f, project cards and chip centres
            gold: #e2c376, the table line, card borders, the primary button, this week chips, links and focus
            goldInk: #1c120c, text on gold
            ivory: #f3eedd, text, figures and last week chip outlines
            sage: #c3cdb9, meta, labels and axis text
            chipRed: #a8323c, the edge of the active projects chip, decoration only
            chipBlue: #2f5d9a, the edge of the due this week chip, decoration only
            ok: #a8f0c0, On track text and check circle
            risk: #f6cf72, At risk text and triangle
            bad: #ffaba0, Behind and overdue text, crossed square, clock and the overdue chip edge
        type:
            Two stacks. Display text uses Didot, Bodoni 72, Bodoni MT, Georgia,
            serif, with the greeting 36px italic, section titles 26px, chip
            figures 28px bold and card corner indices 22px bold. Text uses
            Franklin Gothic Medium, Arial Narrow, Arial, sans-serif at 15px and
            1.5, card names 16px at 600, labels and meta 12px caps at 600 tracked
            0.12em.
        layout:
            A dark rail header holds a gold diamond mark with the Brightwork name,
            the six nav links as caps text with a gold underline on Home, a
            leather search field, a bell, a gold New project button and Mara
            Okafor. Below, the table is a felt panel with 56px rounded ends, a
            radial light in its centre, a 14px padded leather rail around it and a
            thin gold line inset 16px from the edge. On the felt the greeting is
            centred in italic display type with the date and a coral line reading
            4 tasks are overdue with a clock. The four figures are poker chips in
            a row, each a striped edge ring round a dark centre with the number,
            and a caps label below, overdue on a coral edged chip. The projects
            are dealt as a fanned hand of six dark cards with gold borders, each
            tilted a few degrees, with the percent and status symbol as the top
            left index and repeated upside down at bottom right, and the name,
            category, status word, tasks and due date in the middle over a thin
            gold meter. Below the table sit two panels on the rail, the chart as
            chip stacks for each weekday, last week as ivory outlined chips and
            this week as gold chips with counts on top, and the dealer's log of
            activity with gold rules. Below 1100px the hand stops fanning and
            becomes a three column grid, below 640px a two column grid, chips go
            two by two and the panels stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 40px table padding, 16px card padding, 24px between chips.
        density: Medium low. The table is roomy and the cards are small but few.
        corners: 56px rounded table ends, 10px cards, round chips, 6px buttons and fields.
        borders:
            A 14px leather rail, a 1px gold line inset in the felt, 1px gold card
            borders with a second inner gold line.
        shadows:
            Cards cast 0 10px 20px of black at 45 percent onto the felt, chips
            cast 0 4px 0 of a darker rim, and the felt has an inner vignette.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.8px stroke. Status uses a check circle, a triangle
            with a bang and a crossed square, shown as the card index symbol and
            with the word, overdue a clock.
        focus: A 2px gold outline offset 3px.
        tone:
            Light and a little playful, such as The hand, Chips this week and
            Dealer's log, never gambling talk.
    style241:
        number: 241
        run: 49
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Whisky bar
        idea:
            A low lit bar of dark leather and walnut with brass rails, where the
            projects stand on a shelf as glasses filled with amber to their
            percent, the figures sit on engraved brass framed plaques and a warm
            amber glow lights the greeting.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/241.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            leather: #1a110c, the page and the style sheet
            walnut: #2a1a10, the header band, panels and the shelf back
            walnutLight: #352215, plaques, fields and the current nav item
            glow: #3d2716, the brightest point of the amber glow, the lightest surface text sits on
            line: #5a3f27, panel borders and ledger rules
            brass: #d1ad66, rails, frames, the primary button, links, glass outlines and focus
            brassInk: #1d130b, text on brass
            ink: #f2e4cc, text and figures
            muted: #c8b293, meta, labels and axis text
            amber: #f0a24a, the liquid in the glasses and this week bars
            oak: #9a7448, last week bars
            ok: #b6dd8f, On track text and check circle
            risk: #f5cd6a, At risk text and triangle
            bad: #ff9f86, Behind and overdue text, crossed square and clock
        type:
            Two stacks. Headings and body use Baskerville, Baskerville Old Face,
            Hoefler Text, Georgia, serif, with the greeting 36px, plaque figures
            38px with lining numbers, project names 17px at 600 and body 15px at
            1.55. Labels and meta use engraved caps, Copperplate, Copperplate
            Gothic Light, Engravers MT, serif, 12 to 15px tracked 0.18em.
        layout:
            A walnut header band with faint grain ends in a 3px brass rail. It
            holds the Brightwork name engraved on a small brass plaque, the six
            nav links in engraved caps with Home on a darker inset tile with a
            brass underline, a leather search field, a bell, a brass New project
            button and Mara Okafor. Below, a wide walnut panel carries a soft
            amber glow behind the greeting at left, with the date and a coral line
            reading 4 tasks are overdue with a clock, and the four figures at
            right as brass framed plaques with a double bevel border, overdue with
            a coral figure. The projects stand on The shelf, a walnut panel with a
            brass shelf edge, as six tall glasses drawn in brass outline, each
            filled with amber to its percent with the percent above, and under
            each glass the name, category, status with its symbol, tasks and due
            date. Below the shelf two panels sit side by side, the chart as paired
            bars for each weekday with oak last week and glowing amber this week,
            and the ledger of activity with ruled lines and engraved times. Below
            1000px the glasses wrap to three per row and the panels stack, below
            600px the glasses wrap to two per row and plaques go two by two.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 28px panel padding, 20px between glasses, 32px between panels.
        density: Medium. A rich shelf with room around each glass.
        corners: Small. 4px panels, plaques, buttons and fields, glasses with rounded bases.
        borders:
            Brass. A 3px brass rail under the header, double bevelled brass frames
            on plaques, 1px line on panels and ledger rules.
        shadows:
            A warm amber glow behind the greeting and this week bars, and inner
            shadows that make plaques look inset.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.7px stroke in brass. Status uses a check circle, a
            triangle with a bang and a crossed square, always with the word,
            overdue a clock.
        focus: A 2px brass outline offset 3px with a faint amber glow.
        tone: Warm and a little formal, such as Good morning, Mara, The shelf and The ledger.
    style242:
        number: 242
        run: 49
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Velvet theatre
        idea:
            The dashboard is staged inside a theatre, with deep red velvet
            curtains and a scalloped pelmet framing a spotlit stage, the figures
            printed on ticket stubs, the projects listed in a gilt programme and
            the chart drawn as arched gilt columns.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/242.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            house: #120a0b, the page outside the stage and the style sheet
            stage: #1a0e0f, the stage floor behind the content
            spot: #2a1a17, the brightest point of the spotlight, the lightest surface text sits on
            programme: #1f1112, the programme, chart and notices panels
            velvet: #5a0f1a, curtains, the pelmet and ticket stubs
            velvetDeep: #3a0910, curtain fold shadows and the current nav item
            velvetHi: #7a1a28, curtain fold highlights, decoration only
            gilt: #e6c372, programme rules, display type, the primary button, this week columns, links and focus
            giltInk: #2a0d10, text on gilt
            ink: #f5e9d6, body text and figures
            muted: #d1b9a4, meta, labels and axis text
            rose: #e88a9a, last week column outlines
            ok: #a6e0a0, On track text and check circle
            risk: #f4cf6e, At risk text and triangle
            bad: #ff9e93, Behind and overdue text, crossed square and clock
        type:
            Two serif stacks. Display text uses Big Caslon, Goudy Old Style,
            Garamond, Times New Roman, serif, with the greeting 44px, ticket
            figures 40px, section titles 26px in small caps tracked 0.08em and
            programme entries 22px italic. Body text uses Hoefler Text, Garamond,
            Times New Roman, serif at 16px and 1.55, with act numbers and labels
            14px small caps at 600.
        layout:
            A velvet pelmet runs across the top with a scalloped lower edge and a
            gilt fringe line. It holds the Brightwork name centred in gilt display
            type between two small stars, and below it the six nav links in small
            caps with Home on a deeper velvet tab, a search field, a bell, a gilt
            New project button and Mara Okafor at right. Under the pelmet two 88px
            velvet curtains with vertical folds frame the stage, which has a warm
            spotlight from above. On stage the greeting is centred in large gilt
            type with the date and a coral line reading 4 tasks are overdue with a
            clock. The four figures are velvet ticket stubs with notched ends and
            a dashed tear line, each a gilt number and a small caps label, overdue
            with a coral number. Then Tonight's programme, a programme panel with
            a double gilt rule border, lists the six projects as Act I to Act VI
            in two columns of centred entries, each the act number, the italic
            name, the category, a thin gilt meter, the status with its symbol,
            tasks done and due date, with small diamond ornaments between entries.
            Below sit two panels, the chart as paired arched columns by weekday,
            last week as rose outlines and this week solid gilt, and the notices
            of activity as a call board list. Below 900px the curtains shrink to
            16px edges, the programme becomes one column and the panels stack.
        spacing:
            An 8px unit. 32px programme padding, 24px between entries, 40px
            between stage sections.
        density: Low to medium. A staged, ceremonial layout with room to breathe.
        corners: Square panels with arched column tops, notched ticket stubs and a scalloped pelmet.
        borders:
            Double gilt rules on the programme, 1px gilt rules on panels, a dashed
            tear line on each stub.
        shadows:
            The curtains cast deep inner shadows on the stage and a warm spotlight
            falls from above, nothing on the controls.
        icons:
            Thin line icons at 1.6px stroke in gilt. Status uses a check circle, a
            triangle with a bang and a crossed square, always with the word,
            overdue a clock.
        focus: A 2px gilt outline offset 3px.
        tone:
            Ceremonial and playful, such as Tonight's programme, Act I and
            Notices, without overdoing it.
    style243:
        number: 243
        run: 49
        screen: ProjectsDashboard
        name: Candlelight
        idea:
            A quiet near black page lit by warm candle glows, written as one
            narrow serif column like a letter, with the figures told in a
            sentence, projects as entries with a flame marking their progress and
            the fortnight drawn as a row of small candles.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/243.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            night: #0c0907, the page and the style sheet
            glow: #271b10, the brightest point of any candle glow, the lightest surface text sits on
            hairline: #3a2a1c, rules, progress hairlines and the field underline at rest
            ink: #f0e2cc, text and figures
            muted: #bfa88a, meta, margin times, labels and axis text
            flame: #f2b366, the primary button, flames, this week candles, links and focus
            flameInk: #1e1206, text on flame
            wax: #8f7a63, last week candles
            ok: #b4d99a, On track text and check circle
            risk: #f2cf7a, At risk text and triangle
            bad: #f4a088, Behind and overdue text, crossed square and clock
        type:
            One book serif stack, Charter, Bitstream Charter, Sitka Text, Cambria,
            Georgia, serif, for everything. Base 18px at 1.7. The greeting is 48px
            italic, section titles 26px italic, project names 21px, figures inside
            the summary sentence 30px italic with old style numbers, and margin
            times and meta 15px italic in muted. Labels are 13px small caps
            tracked 0.12em.
        layout:
            One 720px column centred on a near black page, with three soft candle
            glows behind it at the greeting, the projects and the chart. A quiet
            top line holds the italic Brightwork name, the six nav links as italic
            words split by middle dots with Home underlined in flame, a search
            field that is only a hairline underline, a bell, a flame New project
            pill and Mara Okafor. A small drawn candle with a glowing flame sits
            above the greeting Good morning, Mara, then the date in small caps and
            a coral line reading 4 tasks are overdue with a clock. The figures are
            written as a sentence, You have 6 active projects and 23 tasks due
            this week, 4 are overdue, and the team has logged 186 hours this week,
            with each number set large in italic. The projects are six entries
            split by hairlines, each the name with the status at right, then
            category, tasks and due date, and a hairline with a small flame at the
            percent and the percent beside it. The chart is a row of fourteen thin
            candles, wax for last week and flame topped for this week, height for
            the count and the count above, with the two week totals written
            beneath. Activity is a journal with italic times in a left margin.
            Below 640px the margin times move above each entry and the type steps
            down.
        spacing:
            An 8px unit. 32px between entries, 72px between sections, 24px column
            gutter on small screens.
        density: Sparse. One column, long line height and wide gaps.
        corners: Round pill buttons and round flames, otherwise no boxes at all.
        borders: Hairlines only, 1px at rest between entries and under the search field.
        shadows:
            No box shadows. Warmth comes from radial candle glows at 9 to 12
            percent and a soft blur round each flame.
        icons:
            Thin line icons at 1.5px stroke. Status uses a check circle, a
            triangle with a bang and a crossed square, always with the word,
            overdue a clock.
        focus: A 2px flame outline offset 4px with a soft flame glow.
        tone:
            Intimate and gentle, such as Good morning, Mara, A quiet note on the
            week and From the journal.

    style244:
        number: 244
        run: 50
        screen: DesignEditor
        name: Slate tool
        idea: Blue-grey professional tool chrome with a compact 11px UI, clear ruled panels and one working blue, built for long sessions in a design tool.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/244.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            well: #161a20, the page and the canvas behind a 16px dot grid in #2c333e
            chrome: #1a1f27, the top bar, the status bar and number fields
            panel: #222831, the layers panel and the inspector
            line: #353d49, every panel edge and section rule
            ink: #dbe1ea, text
            muted: #9ba6b5, panel labels, layer type icons and field prefixes
            accent: #2f6fde, the active tool and the Share button under white text
            accentInk: #8fb6ff, the Selected tag, the selected row edge, tab underline and focus
            row: #2c3a52, the selected layer row and the active direction segment
            saved: #62d29d, the Saved text and icon
            guide: #ff6ba6, spacing guides with dark label text
            pin: #f2b84b, the comment pin behind dark initials
        type:
            One system stack, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
            Arial, with ui-monospace for zoom, sizes and number fields. Base
            11px at 1.4. Panel heads are 11px 600 caps tracked 0.06em, the file
            name 11px 600, values 11px mono, and the style sheet title 22px.
        layout:
            A classic three panel desktop tool. A 40px top bar holds a blue B
            square, the file name over Canvas and Home v3, a recessed group of
            six icon tools with Move filled blue, then the three overlapping
            initials discs, a mono zoom box with a chevron, an icon Present
            button and a blue Share button. Below, a 232px layers panel with
            Layers and Assets tabs and 24px tree rows, the canvas in the middle
            with a dot grid, and a 248px inspector with Design and Prototype
            tabs. The inspector stacks ruled sections for Frame with a two by
            two X Y W H grid, Auto layout with a Vertical and Horizontal
            segment plus gap and padding fields, Corner radius, Fill with a
            white swatch and Export with format, scale and an Export Hero
            button. A 24px status bar runs along the bottom. The Hero frame
            sits white with a blue outline, eight square handles, a blue size
            badge below and the comment bubble in chrome colour. Below 760px
            the side panels and top tools hide, and a bottom bar of six 44px
            tools appears above a wrapping status bar.
        spacing: A 4px unit. 24px rows, 28px panel heads, 8 to 10px panel padding, 40 to 48px around the frame.
        density: Dense. Three panels and a status bar always visible with small type.
        corners: Small. 3 to 4px on fields, buttons and the tool group, square panels, round avatars.
        borders: 1px #353d49 between every panel and inspector section. The selected layer row adds a 2px accentInk inner left edge.
        shadows: None on panels. Only the comment bubble floats with 0 4px 12px black at 40 percent.
        icons:
            16px line icons at 1.5px stroke with round caps, 14px inside panels.
            Layer types use a hash for frames, a T for text, a nested diamond
            for the component instance in soft violet and a picture for the
            image. Saved uses a check circle, editing uses two people and the
            version uses a tag, each with its words.
        focus: A 2px #8fb6ff outline offset 1px. Number fields add a 1px inner ring in the same blue.
        tone: Terse tool labels, such as Design, Auto layout and Export Hero.
    style245:
        number: 245
        run: 50
        screen: DesignEditor
        name: Dark tonal
        idea: Panels float as rounded cards separated by steps of tone instead of lines, so the editor reads as soft layered surfaces with one lavender accent.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/245.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            tone0: #0e1012, the page and the canvas
            tone1: #17191d, the floating header, layers and inspector cards
            tone2: #202328, inspector groups, the tool rail, layer tiles and status chips
            tone3: #2a2e35, fields and secondary buttons
            tone4: #363b44, hover and the active direction segment
            ink: #e6e8ec, text
            muted: #a3a9b3, labels, secondary lines and idle icons
            lavender: #c6b8ff, the primary button, the active tool, the frame selection and focus
            lavenderInk: #191431, text and icons on lavender
            tint: #2c2843, the selected layer row and the frame name pill
            saved: #7ed6a7, the Saved chip text and icon
            pin: #ffc98a, the comment pin
        type:
            One system stack, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
            Arial. Base 13px at 1.45. Names 13px 600, muted labels 12px 600,
            second lines in layer rows 12px muted, values with tabular numbers,
            and the style sheet title 26px 700.
        layout:
            Everything floats inside an 8px gutter on tone0. A 56px header card
            holds a lavender rounded B tile, the crumb Website redesign slash
            Home v3, three rounded square initials tiles, a zoom chip with a
            magnifier, Present and a lavender Share. Below sit three cards, a
            256px layers card, the canvas and a 272px inspector card. Layer rows
            are 10px rounded with a 26px tonal icon tile, two lines for Headline
            and Primary button, a lavender Selected chip on Hero and a muted
            Collapsed note on Features. A vertical tool rail floats at the left
            edge of the canvas in tone2 with 44px tools, Move filled lavender.
            The status sits as three chips at the bottom of the canvas. The
            inspector stacks tone2 groups for Position and size, Fill, Auto
            layout with a two way segment, Corner radius and Export, each with
            34px tone3 pill fields. Below 760px the side cards hide, the rail
            turns horizontal and floats above the status chips.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 8px gutters between cards, 12px card padding, 6px between fields.
        density: Medium. 34 to 44px targets and two line layer rows.
        corners: Generous. 14px cards, 10 to 12px groups, buttons and rows, 8px fields, round handles.
        borders: None anywhere. Every edge is a step between the five tones.
        shadows: None on panels. Only the comment bubble lifts with 0 8px 24px black at 45 percent.
        icons:
            18px line icons at 1.8px stroke inside 26px tonal tiles, which turn
            lavender on the selected row. Saved uses a check circle, editing two
            people and the version a tag, each beside its words.
        focus: A 2px lavender ring offset 2px, an inset 2px lavender ring on fields.
        tone: Friendly plain labels, such as Position and size.
    style246:
        number: 246
        run: 50
        screen: DesignEditor
        name: Outline dark
        idea: Every panel, control and even the canvas preview is a thin line drawing on pure black with no fills, so structure shows as wireframe and one mint line marks what is active.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/246.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            black: #000000, every surface
            line: #7a7a7a, outlines of panels, boxes and controls
            faint: #3a3a3a, inner dividers, rulers and element outlines, never text
            ink: #ededed, text and the outline view drawing
            muted: #a8a8a8, mono labels, key hints and type icons
            mint: #5ef0c0, the active tool, selected row, frame outline, Share, Saved and focus
            pink: #ff8fc8, the spacing guide and one avatar ring
            amber: #ffc46b, the comment pin and one avatar ring
        type:
            System ui for text, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
            Arial, and ui-monospace for labels, values and buttons. Body 13px
            at 1.45. Labels are 11px mono caps tracked 0.1em, buttons 12px mono
            caps, values 13px mono, and the sheet title 24px 600.
        layout:
            A row of separate outlined boxes forms the top, the CANVAS mark
            with the file path, a joined strip of six 52px tools each showing
            its key letter under the icon with Move outlined mint, a Zoom 66%
            box, the three ringed initials and the Present and Share buttons.
            The canvas fills the left in its own outline with mono rulers along
            the top and left. The frame is shown in outline view, a mint frame
            line with square handles, element outlines in faint grey, white
            headline text on black, an outlined button and a crossed screenshot
            box. The right column stacks the inspector over the layers, each
            outlined. The inspector is a ruled grid of 38px property cells for
            X, Y, W, H, Fill, Layout, Gap, Pad, Radius and Export. Layer rows
            are 32px, the selected row outlined mint with a Selected flag.
            Status words sit in three outlined boxes, Saved in mint. Below
            760px the right column hides, the brand takes a full row and an
            outlined strip of six tools sits under the canvas.
        spacing: 12px gutters between outlined boxes, 38px property rows, 32px layer rows, 36 to 40px around the frame.
        density: Medium. Canvas on the left, inspector over layers on the right.
        corners: Square everywhere. Only the avatars are round.
        borders: 1px #7a7a7a outlines on every box and control and #3a3a3a dividers inside. Active things swap to a 1px mint outline.
        shadows: None and no fills at all, even the canvas is drawn as outlines.
        icons:
            18px line icons at 1.25px stroke with square caps and mitred joins.
            Saved uses a check circle, editing two people and the version a tag,
            each in its own outlined box with words.
        focus: A 1px dashed mint outline offset 3px, and a mint inset line on fields.
        tone: Technical mono caps, such as Inspector, Outline view and Export.
    style247:
        number: 247
        run: 50
        screen: DesignEditor
        name: Dark glass
        idea: The canvas sits on a deep, softly glowing colour field and every tool floats above it as translucent dark glass, so the work feels lit from behind while text stays on dark tint.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/247.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            base: #0a0b16, the page under the glow
            violetGlow: #7b3fe4, a large radial blob at 75 percent top left
            tealGlow: #1fa5c9, a radial blob at 70 percent top right
            roseGlow: #e0457b, a radial blob at 60 percent at the bottom, also the spacing guide
            glass: #101220, panels at 72 percent with a 28px blur and 150 percent saturation
            edge: #ffffff, panel rims at 16 percent and a 22 percent inner top highlight
            ink: #f3f4fb, text
            muted: #bcc0d4, labels and idle icons
            cyan: #7fe3ff, Share, the active tool, the selected row ring, frame selection and focus
            cyanInk: #04222c, text and icons on cyan
            saved: #86f0b5, the Saved chip
            pin: #ffd27a, the comment pin
        type:
            One system stack, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
            Arial. Base 13px at 1.45. File name 13px 700, panel titles 12px 600
            muted, values with tabular numbers and the sheet title 28px 700.
        layout:
            The whole editor sits on a 780px colour field made of four radial
            glows. Three glass pills float across the top, the file pill with a
            round gradient B, the tool pill centred with six 40px round tools,
            Move filled cyan, and 66%, and the people pill with overlapping
            ringed initials, Present and a cyan Share. A 248px glass layers
            panel floats left and a 264px glass inspector floats right, both
            hugging their content. The Hero frame floats in the middle with a
            cyan ring, round handles and a deep shadow, and the comment bubble
            is itself glass. The inspector holds tinted blocks for Position and
            size, Fill, Auto layout with pill segments, Corner radius and
            Export. A glass status pill is centred at the bottom. Below 1120px
            the tool pill drops to its own row. Below 760px the side panels
            hide and the tool pill floats under the canvas above the status.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px gaps between floating panels, 14px panel padding, 10 to 12px inside blocks.
        density: Medium. Three floating pills, two side panels and one status pill.
        corners: Large. 20px panels, 14px blocks, 10px fields, pill tools, buttons and segments.
        borders: 1px white at 16 percent around glass and 8 to 10 percent around inner blocks.
        shadows: An inset 1px top highlight plus 0 12px 40px black at 35 percent, and 0 30px 80px under the frame.
        icons:
            18px rounded line icons at 1.6px stroke in 40px round tools. Saved
            uses a check circle on a faint green chip, editing two people and the
            version a tag, each with its words.
        focus: A 2px cyan outline offset 2px with a 6px cyan halo at 25 percent.
        tone: Light and calm, such as Position and size and Export.
    style248:
        number: 248
        run: 50
        screen: DesignEditor
        name: High contrast dark
        idea: Pure white on pure black with 2px white rules, literal labels under every tool and no colour at all except a bright yellow focus ring, so every part of the editor passes AAA.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/248.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            black: #000000, every surface and text on white
            white: #ffffff, text, rules, the selected row, the active tool and the primary button
            grey: #d6d6d6, disabled controls only
            yellow: #ffe500, the focus ring only, never text or decoration
        type:
            One stack, Atkinson Hyperlegible, Verdana, Segoe UI, system-ui,
            Roboto, Arial. Body 16px at 1.5. Panel titles 20px 800, names 16px
            700, the smallest text 15px 700 and the sheet title 32px 800.
            Nothing is smaller than 15px.
        layout:
            A masthead under a 2px rule holds a white B square, Website
            redesign over Canvas, page Home v3, the words In this file with
            three ringed initials, an outlined Present and a white Share. Below
            runs a full width row of 88px boxed tools, each an icon over its
            word, Move inverted white and underlined, then a Zoom 66% box. The
            work area has three columns split by 2px white rules, a 280px
            layers list, the canvas and a 320px inspector. Every layer row is
            48px with its type written as a second line such as Frame, Text or
            Component instance, Hero inverted white with a boxed Selected tag
            and Features with a boxed Collapsed tag. The inspector is a ruled
            definition list of 48px rows, Position, Size, Fill, Layout,
            Spacing, Corners and Export, with white boxed inputs. The canvas
            shows the white frame with a 3px white dashed selection offset
            6px, black squares with white borders as handles and the comment
            in a black box with a white border. Three status boxes sit under
            it. Below 760px the side columns and tool row hide and a three by
            two grid of labelled tools sits under the canvas.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 44 to 64px targets, 16px panel padding, 24 to 32px around the frame.
        density: Low. Labelled tools, two line layer rows and large values.
        corners: Square. Only avatars and the comment pin are round.
        borders: 2px white on every panel, row and control, 4px under sheet headings and 8px over the sheet.
        shadows: None. Selection on the canvas is a 3px white dashed outline offset 6px.
        icons:
            Line icons at 2.25px stroke sized 1.25em, always next to a word.
            Saved uses a check circle, editing two people and the version a
            tag, each in its own ruled box.
        focus: A 3px yellow outline offset 3px, the only colour on the page.
        tone: Literal and complete, such as Hero, selected and Component instance.

    style249:
        number: 249
        run: 51
        screen: DesignEditor
        name: Darkroom
        idea: The editor is a photographic darkroom under a deep red safelight, with the canvas as a print in a developing tray, the inspector as exposure notes and the layers as a numbered film strip.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/249.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            room: #140a09, the page behind the safelight glow
            bench: #1e100e, the top bar, the notes card, the status bar and the sheet cards
            tray: #0d0606, the canvas tray
            film: #0a0505, the film strip base
            line: #4a2a25, edges and rules
            sprocket: #3b2420, film strip holes
            safelight: #be1e14, a radial glow at 42 percent centred on the tray
            ink: #f4ddd6, warm text
            muted: #c99f95, labels and type words
            safeRed: #ff5a4c, selection, the notes heading, the active knob and the lamp
            safeButton: #c4231a, the Share button under white text
            amber: #ffb45e, timer readouts, frame numbers, Saved, the comment pin and focus
            paper: #fbf7f2, the print border around the frame
        type:
            Avenir Next, Segoe UI, system-ui, Roboto, Arial for text, Georgia
            for the frame headline and the sheet title, and ui-monospace for
            readouts and labels. Body 14px at 1.45. Readouts 15 to 16px mono
            600 in amber, labels 11 to 13px mono caps tracked 0.12 to 0.14em,
            and the sheet title 30px Georgia 600.
        layout:
            A bench coloured top bar holds a glowing red lamp, Website redesign
            and Home v3, six round enlarger knobs for the tools with Move ringed
            red, an amber ZOOM 66% timer readout, three ringed initials, Present
            and a red Share. Below, the canvas fills the left as a dark tray
            with 18px corners and a red inner glow, the Hero frame inside as a
            print with a paper border, a red selection line and red crop marks
            at the corners, and the comment as an amber pinned note tilted one
            degree. A 300px Exposure notes card on ruled paper sits right, with
            amber mono readouts for X, Y, W and H, then ruled lines for Fill,
            Auto layout, Gap, Padding, Corner radius and Export, and an Export
            print button. Under both runs a full width film strip with sprocket
            holes top and bottom, each layer a 168px frame numbered 1A to 7A,
            children marked in Hero, Hero outlined red and glowing with
            SELECTED, Features marked COLLAPSED. A mono status bar closes it.
            Below 760px the notes and strip hide and the six knobs sit in a
            short film strip under the canvas.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 28 to 32px around the tray, 16px card padding, 6px between film frames.
        density: Medium. Tray and notes side by side, the film strip across the full width below.
        corners: Mixed. 18px tray, 4 to 6px cards and buttons, round knobs and avatars, square film frames.
        borders: 1px #4a2a25 everywhere, red on the selected film frame, the selection and the active knob.
        shadows: A red inner glow in the tray, a red outer glow on the selected film frame and a dark drop under the print.
        icons:
            18px line icons at 1.7px stroke inside round 40px knobs. Saved uses
            a check circle in amber, editing two people and the version a tag,
            each with its words in mono.
        focus: A 2px amber outline offset 3px.
        tone: Gentle darkroom words, such as Exposure notes and Export print, plain elsewhere.
    style250:
        number: 250
        run: 51
        screen: DesignEditor
        name: Dark Swiss
        idea: A strict twelve column grid on black set in one grotesque, with flush left numbered lists, heavy top rules and a single signal red that marks only what is active.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/250.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            black: #0a0a0a, the page and panels
            column: #161616, the canvas stage
            ink: #f5f5f5, text and heavy rules
            grey: #a6a6a6, labels and list numbers
            rule: #3d3d3d, hairlines between rows
            signalRed: #ff3d2e, the active tool, the selected layer, frame selection, Share under black text and focus
        type:
            One stack, Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, Liberation Sans. Body
            14px at 1.4. The file title is 64px 700 at 0.92 line height and
            minus 0.035em tracking, status figures 36px 700, names and tools
            15px 700, labels 11px 700 tracked 0.04em in grey, and the sheet
            title 44px.
        layout:
            Everything sits on a twelve column grid with 24px gutters and 32px
            margins. The masthead under a 1px ink rule has a small path label
            over a huge Home v3 with a grey dash Hero across seven columns, and
            the initials with full names, Present and a red Share across five.
            The tool row lists 01 Move to 06 Hand as numbered words, Move red
            with a 3px red underline, and Zoom 66% set large at the right. The
            work row gives the layers three columns, the canvas six and the
            inspector three, each headed by a 3px ink rule and a small grey
            label. Layers are a numbered index with names over type words,
            children indented by a hairline, Hero red with a red square and
            Selected. The canvas stage shows faint red column guides behind the
            white frame with small square red handles. The inspector is a
            typographic table grouped under Frame, Auto layout and Export.
            Status runs as three grid thirds, each a small label and a large
            figure, Saved 2 minutes ago, 3 people editing and Version 41.
            Below 1100px the inspector moves under the canvas. Below 760px a
            four column grid, the canvas alone and a three by two grid of
            numbered tools.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px gutters, 32px margins, 8px list row padding.
        density: Medium. Layers three columns, canvas six and inspector three.
        corners: Square everywhere. Avatars are initials only.
        borders: A 3px ink rule over each section, 1px ink under the masthead and table groups, 1px #3d3d3d hairlines between rows.
        shadows: None. The canvas shows faint red column guides instead.
        icons:
            16px line icons at 2px stroke with butt caps, used sparingly at row
            ends. Saved uses a check circle in red, editing two people and the
            version a tag, each beside its label.
        focus: A 2px red outline offset 2px, and a 3px red underline on fields.
        tone: Numbered and factual, such as 01 Move and Inspector, Hero.
    style251:
        number: 251
        run: 51
        screen: DesignEditor
        name: Dark brutalist
        idea: Raw slabs on black with thick white borders, hard lime offset shadows, typewriter text and giant numbers, so the editor feels like a poster bolted together.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/251.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            black: #000000, the page, buttons and the canvas
            slab: #111111, panel fill and the canvas grid lines
            white: #ffffff, text, 4px borders and inverted panel titles
            grey: #bdbdbd, small labels
            acid: #d4ff3a, slab shadows, the active tool, selected row, Share, frame border and the status band, under black text
            hot: #ff5ce1, the comment and focus
        type:
            Courier New, Courier, ui-monospace for text, and Arial Black,
            Helvetica Neue, Arial for display. Body 15px at 1.4. The file title
            40px 900 caps, inspector values 30px 900, panel titles 20px 900
            caps, labels and buttons 13 to 16px 700 caps, and the sheet title
            44px 900 caps.
        layout:
            Slabs with 4px white borders and hard lime shadows stack on black.
            The top row has a wide title slab with HOME V3 and WEBSITE REDESIGN
            slash slash CANVAS, a slab of three joined initials cells, Present
            and a lime Share. The left column stacks a three by two block of
            76px tools, each icon over a caps word, Move filled lime with an ON
            tag, then a ZOOM 66% bar and the layers slab with a white LAYERS
            title and 44px rows split by 2px rules, Hero filled lime with a
            boxed SELECTED tag. The canvas slab has a coarse 48px grid, a white
            HERO 1440 × 820 label and the white frame with a 4px lime border,
            lime square handles and a pink comment tilted two degrees with a
            hard pink shadow. The inspector slab is a grid of cells with giant
            values, X, Y, W, H, Fill, Auto layout, Gap, Padding, Corner radius
            and Export. A lime status band with black text and 4px dividers
            runs below. Below 1180px the inspector moves under the canvas.
            Below 760px only the canvas, the tool block and the band remain.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between slabs, 8 to 12px inside cells.
        density: Low to medium. 56 to 76px targets and 30px values.
        corners: None. Every edge is square.
        borders: 4px white on every slab and cell, 2px between layer rows and 12px over the sheet.
        shadows: Hard 8px 8px lime on slabs and 6px white on buttons, never blurred. Pressed buttons drop their shadow.
        icons:
            22px line icons at 2.75px stroke with square caps above caps
            labels. Saved uses a check circle, editing two people and the
            version a tag, each with caps words on the lime band.
        focus: A 4px hot pink outline offset 4px, and a pink inset on inspector cells.
        tone: Blunt caps, such as HOME V3, ON and COLLAPSED.
    style252:
        number: 252
        run: 51
        screen: DesignEditor
        name: Dark risograph
        idea: The editor is printed like a two colour zine on dark paper, fluorescent pink and teal overprinting each other with a slight misregistration, halftone dots and grain.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/252.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            paper: #1c1a22, the page with a grain of cream and black dots
            card: #25222d, panels and the status stub
            deep: #141218, the canvas behind teal halftone dots, and fields
            cream: #f3ebe0, text as white ink
            dim: #c4b9ad, labels and dotted leaders
            pink: #ff5cb8, headings, the active tool, the selected layer, Share and the frame outline
            teal: #2ad0c2, the misregistered offset, Saved, secondary buttons, numbers and focus
            pinkInk: #2a0b1c, text on pink
            tealInk: #04201d, text on teal
        type:
            Avenir Next Condensed, Roboto Condensed, Arial Narrow for headings,
            tools and buttons in 800 caps, ui-rounded, Segoe UI, system-ui for
            body, and ui-monospace for small labels. Body 14px at 1.5. The file
            title 44px condensed caps in pink with a 2px teal offset shadow,
            panel titles 22px the same way, buttons 15px, labels 11 to 12px
            mono, and the sheet title 46px.
        layout:
            A masthead over a dotted teal rule holds a pink HOME V3 with a teal
            ghost and a mono line Brightwork Canvas, Website redesign, 2 colour
            print, then three overprinted initials discs, an outlined teal
            Present and a pink Share. A row of pill tools follows with icon and
            caps word, idle tools dashed cream, Move filled pink with a teal
            offset, and a teal 66% at the right. The work row puts a 250px
            Print spec card left, the canvas in the middle and a 300px layers
            card right. Print spec shows X, Y, W and H as four pink and teal ink
            blocks with big condensed values, then a dashed ruled list for
            Frame, Fill, Auto layout, Gap, Padding, Corner radius and Export.
            Layers are a numbered zine index with dotted leaders to a type word,
            Hero filled pink with selected. The canvas has teal halftone dots,
            two overlapping pink and teal circles in screen blend at the corner,
            the white frame with a pink outline and teal offset, and a teal
            bordered comment tilted slightly. A ticket stub with dashed
            perforations carries the status. Below 760px the cards and tool row
            hide and a three by two grid of pill tools sits under the canvas.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px between panels, 14px inside, 10px between tools.
        density: Medium. Inspector left, canvas centre, layers right and tools as a row.
        corners: Uneven cut corners of 14 6 16 8px on cards, 12 4px on ink blocks and rows, pill tools and buttons.
        borders: Dashed cream on idle tools, a dotted teal rule under the masthead, dashed rules in the spec list and dotted leaders.
        shadows: Only misregistration, a hard 3px 2px teal offset behind pink shapes and a 2px teal text shadow on pink headings.
        icons:
            18px round line icons at 2px stroke, always beside a word. Saved
            uses a check circle in teal, editing two people in pink and the
            version a tag in cream, each with condensed caps words.
        focus: A 3px teal outline offset 3px plus a 7px pink halo at 35 percent.
        tone: Playful zine words, such as Print spec, plain elsewhere.
    style253:
        number: 253
        run: 51
        screen: DesignEditor
        name: Dark duotone
        idea: Everything is drawn in exactly two tones, deep indigo and electric orange, with hierarchy made by inverting blocks, halftone dots and circles instead of extra colours.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/253.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            indigo: #1b1350, the page, panels and text on orange
            orange: #ff7a1f, all other text, lines, inverted bands, the active tool, the selected row, the frame preview and focus
        type:
            One geometric stack, Futura, Century Gothic, Avenir Next, Segoe UI,
            system-ui, Arial. Body 14px at 1.45 in 600 for weight on orange.
            The file name 26px 700, inspector values 22px 700 inside circles,
            panel heads 13px 700 caps tracked 0.1em, and the sheet title 36px.
        layout:
            An orange header band with indigo text holds an indigo B disc, Home
            v3 over Website redesign and Brightwork Canvas, three initials discs
            alternating filled and outlined, an outlined Present and an indigo
            Share. Below, a 72px tool rail with six 48px ringed circles, Move
            filled orange, and ZOOM 66% set vertically at its foot. The canvas
            has orange halftone dots fading from the top left and shows the
            Hero frame previewed in two tones, an orange frame with indigo
            headline, an indigo pill button and an indigo halftone screenshot
            area, inside a dashed orange selection with ringed round handles
            and an indigo comment bubble. A 300px side column stacks the layers
            and the inspector, each under an inverted orange head. Layer rows
            are pills, Hero filled orange with Selected. The inspector shows X,
            Y, W and H as four ringed circles, then ruled rows for Fill, Auto
            layout, Gap and Padding, Corner radius and Export. An orange status
            band closes the screen. Below 760px the rail and side column hide
            and the six ringed tools sit in a row under the canvas.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16 to 20px panel padding, 28 to 32px around the canvas.
        density: Medium. Tool rail, canvas and one side column with layers over the inspector.
        corners: Round. Pills and circles for tools, rows, buttons and value dials, 24px cards.
        borders: 2px orange lines between rail, canvas and side column and on rows, a dashed 2px orange selection.
        shadows: None. Emphasis is an inverted orange block.
        icons:
            20px round line icons at 2px stroke inside 48px circles. Saved uses a
            check circle, editing two people and the version a tag, each with
            words on the orange band.
        focus: A 3px orange outline offset 3px with a 6px indigo gap and a 2px orange outer ring.
        tone: Calm and graphic, such as Shown in duotone and Inspector.

    style254:
        number: 254
        run: 52
        screen: DesignEditor
        name: Urushi lacquer
        idea: A design tool laid out like a set of black lacquer trays, where gold leaf hairlines frame each panel, the inspector stacks like tiered boxes and a single vermilion marks what is chosen.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/254.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            lacquer: #0e0b0b, the page, canvas and field wells
            tray: #171112, the header, panels, status bar and style sheet
            tier: #1f1617, tool tiles and the comment card
            tierBand: #2a1210, inspector tier heading bands and the selected layer
            ink: #f1e8d8, text
            muted: #b3a48c, meta, layer kinds and status text
            gold: #d6b05a, labels, numerals, handles, the frame outline, status icons and focus
            goldLine: #6e5a35, tray rims and dividers
            seam: #33261f, field and row borders
            vermilion: #a3291c, Share, the pressed Move tool, the seal mark and the comment pin
            rice: #fff4e8, text on vermilion
            guide: #c2291a, the 32 px spacing guide with white text
        type:
            Titles in a book serif stack, Iowan Old Style, Palatino Linotype,
            Palatino, Book Antiqua, Georgia. Text in system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto,
            Helvetica Neue, Arial. Base 14px at 1.5. The sheet title is 30px 600
            serif, the file name 15px 600 serif, layer names 14px 600, meta 12 to
            13px, tray and tier labels 11 to 12px caps tracked 0.14 to 0.16em in
            gold, and layer numerals 01 to 07 in 12px italic serif gold.
        layout:
            Three columns of 252px, the canvas and 292px under a header row. The
            header is one tray split in three. Left holds a round vermilion seal
            with a gold ring and the file as Brightwork Canvas over Website
            redesign / Home v3. The middle holds the six tools as 40px square
            lacquer tiles with Move filled vermilion with a short gold bar under
            it, then a 66% zoom well. Right holds three round avatars, an outlined
            gold Present and a vermilion Share. Below, the layers tray floats 16px
            in from the left with gold numerals, a kind icon, the name and a sub
            line, Hero tinted red with a gold left edge and a Selected tag,
            Features with a Collapsed tag. The canvas is plain lacquer with a
            faint warm gloss from the top and the white Hero frame outlined in
            gold with square gold handles. The inspector tray on the right is a
            stack of tiers like a lidded box set, each with a dark red band
            heading for Position and size, Fill, Auto layout with Vertical, Corner
            radius and Export, holding italic serif keyed fields such as X 0 and W
            1440. The status bar runs the full width with gold diamonds between
            items. Below 860px everything stacks with the canvas first and the
            tools become a sticky bottom tray.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px gutters around trays, 18px tray padding, 10px between fields.
        density: Medium. Seven layer rows with a sub line each and five inspector tiers.
        corners: 10px trays, 6px tiles, fields and buttons, round seal, avatars and pin.
        borders: 1px gold line rims on every tray, 1px seam borders on fields, a 3px gold left edge on the selected layer.
        shadows: A deep soft shadow under trays and the frame, 0 12px 28px black at 55 percent, with a faint warm top highlight.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.5px stroke, 18px. Selected uses a circled check,
            Collapsed a right chevron, Saved a cloud with a check, people editing
            two figures and the version a tag, always with the word.
        focus: A 2px gold outline offset 3px.
        tone: Quiet and formal. Caps tier names such as Position and size and Export.
    style255:
        number: 255
        run: 52
        screen: DesignEditor
        name: Indigo dyed
        idea: Panels sewn from deep indigo cloth, edged with white running stitches over a faint shibori ring pattern, with the inspector read like a woven care label and undyed cream for the one main action.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/255.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            deep: #0b1430, the page with faint repeating ring patterns
            cloth: #12204a, stitched patches and the style sheet
            patch: #1a2d63, the care label inspector
            dyedTwice: #27428a, the selected layer and the pressed tool
            well: #0d1838, fields and the zoom pill
            ink: #eef2fb, text
            faded: #a9b8dc, meta, labels and status text
            stitch: #dfe6f5, dashed running stitch edges and status icons
            thread: #5f74ad, quiet dashed rules, dotted leaders and field borders
            undyed: #f4efe4, Share and the comment pin with deep indigo text
            persimmon: #f2c46b, the focus ring only
            madder: #c2462e, the 32 px guide with white text
        type:
            One humanist stack, Optima, Candara, Noto Sans, Segoe UI, system-ui.
            Base 14px at 1.55. The sheet title is 28px 600, the file name 17px
            600, panel titles 15px 600 beside a 13px faded context, layer names
            14px 600, meta 12px, and care label group names 11px caps tracked
            0.14em.
        layout:
            Every panel is a cloth patch with 14px corners and a dashed white
            stitch line inset 5px. A header patch spans the top with a cream
            square B mark, Canvas, Website redesign and Home v3, then In this file
            with three dashed ring avatars, a dashed Present and a cream pill
            Share. Below sit three columns with 14px gaps. A 76px tool rail patch
            holds six round tools stacked with small key letters, Move filled with
            the twice dyed blue and a dashed ring, then the 66% zoom pill. The
            canvas patch is darker with a dot grid, the white Hero frame and round
            handles, and the status line runs along its foot under a dashed rule.
            A 320px right column holds two patches, the layers list with dashed
            rules between rows, Hero highlighted with a dashed inner stitch and a
            Selected tag, then the inspector as a care label, a lighter rectangle
            where each line reads like a garment tag with a label, a dotted leader
            and a small right aligned value, grouped into Position and size, Fill,
            Auto layout Vertical, Corners and Export, with Export Hero below.
            Below 860px the patches stack with the canvas first and the rail
            becomes a sticky bottom tool bar.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 14px between patches, 18px patch padding, 8px layer rows.
        density: Medium. The rail, the canvas and one column of two patches.
        corners: 14px patches with a 10px stitch inset, round tools, pill buttons and fields, 6px care label.
        borders: A 1.5px dashed white running stitch inside each patch, dashed thread rules between rows and dotted leaders in the care label.
        shadows: None on panels. Only the mobile tool bar casts a soft shadow.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.6px stroke, 18 to 20px. Selected is a circled check,
            Collapsed a right chevron, Saved a cloud with a check, always with the
            word.
        focus: A 3px persimmon outline offset 3px.
        tone: Calm and plain, like a garment tag, with labels such as Width, Padding and Scale.
    style256:
        number: 256
        run: 52
        screen: DesignEditor
        name: Dark workshop
        idea: A woodworker's bench at night, with tools hung on a steel pegboard, layers kept in labelled walnut drawers, an engraved steel plate screwed on for the inspector and a brass rule along the foot.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/256.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            walnut: #1e140e, the page with a faint wood grain
            plank: #2b1d14, the header and the style sheet
            drawer: #34241a, layer drawer fronts
            steel: #3a3f45, tool tiles and the pegboard
            plate: #262a2f, the engraved inspector plate and the comment card
            pit: #15171a, recessed fields and etched tags
            ink: #ece6da, text
            sawdust: #b9ab98, meta and layer kinds
            etch: #c3c9cf, engraved steel labels and ruler numbers
            brass: #c9a256, the pressed tool, Share, handles and the open drawer edge
            brassPlate: #b8924a, the nameplate and the status rule with walnut text
            rust: #b83a0b, the 32 px guide with white text
            lamp: #ffd27a, the focus ring only
        type:
            Three stacks. Labels use Futura, Century Gothic, Trebuchet MS in caps
            tracked 0.1 to 0.16em with an engraved double text shadow. Text uses
            system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto. Values and meta use ui-monospace, SF
            Mono, Menlo, Consolas. The nameplate title is 15px 700, layer names
            13px 600, values 13px mono, meta 11px mono and etched labels 10 to
            12px.
        layout:
            A walnut header plank holds an outlined BW stamp, a brass nameplate
            reading Canvas Website redesign over Home v3, square avatars, a steel
            Present and a brass Share. Below sit a 216px left column, the canvas
            and a 300px plate. The left column starts with a steel pegboard of peg
            holes holding six labelled steel tool tiles in two columns, each hung
            from a hole, Move in brass, and a black zoom readout. Under it the
            layers are drawers, raised walnut fronts with a brass kind icon, name,
            mono sub line and pull, the Hero drawer lit with a brass edge and a
            Selected tag. The canvas is a dark recessed bench with a steel ruler
            along its top marked 0 to 1200 and the white Hero frame outlined in
            brass with square brass handles. The inspector is a brushed steel
            plate with four screws, etched group names and recessed fields keyed
            in brass such as W 1440 and Pad 96, ending in Export Hero. A brass
            rule with tick marks runs the full width as the status bar. Below
            860px the canvas comes first, drawers and plate stack, and the
            pegboard becomes a sticky bottom strip of seven tiles.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px between bench pieces, 8px between tools and drawers, 20px plate padding.
        density: Medium. Labelled tools, seven drawers and a five group plate.
        corners: Nearly square, 3 to 4px everywhere, round only on screws and peg holes.
        borders: 1px near black edges on every piece. A 4px brass inner edge marks the open drawer.
        shadows: Hard 2px drop ledges under tools, drawers and buttons, inset shadows sinking fields, and an inner vignette in the bench.
        icons:
            Square cap line icons at 2px stroke, 18px. Selected is a circled
            check, Collapsed a right chevron, Saved a cloud with a check, always
            with the word.
        focus: A 2px lamp yellow outline offset 2px with a soft 5px halo.
        tone: Stamped and terse caps such as Tools, Pad, Scale and Export Hero.
    style257:
        number: 257
        run: 52
        screen: DesignEditor
        name: Dark marble
        idea: A hushed luxury studio where the whole canvas is a slab of black marble with gold and grey veins, and the layers and inspector float on it as polished stone cards edged in a single gold line.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/257.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            onyx: #0c0c0d, the page, top bar and status band
            slab: #151516, floating cards and the style sheet
            slabLight: #1c1c1e, avatar discs
            hairline: #2a2a2c, rules between rows and sections
            vein: #3a3a3d, field underlines and the secondary button edge
            ink: #efece6, text
            stoneGrey: #a8a39a, meta, labels and status
            champagne: #e9dcc0, Didone titles and values
            gold: #cfae6b, card edges, Share, handles, the selected layer edge, veins and focus
            goldWash: #252119, the selected layer row
            roseGold: #a94e37, the 32 px guide with white text
        type:
            Titles and values in a Didone stack, Didot, Bodoni 72, Bodoni MT,
            Hoefler Text, Georgia. Text in Avenir Next, Avenir, Segoe UI, system-
            ui. Card titles are 21px 400 Didone, the file 20px, field values 17px
            Didone with tabular lining figures, layer names 14px 500, sub lines
            12px italic Didone, and labels 10 to 11px caps tracked 0.2 to 0.32em.
        layout:
            A slim onyx top bar in three parts. Left is a gold spaced caps
            Brightwork Canvas over Website redesign and an italic Home v3. Centre
            is the six bare tool icons with Move lit and underlined by a glowing
            gold line, then 66% in Didone. Right holds gold ringed avatars, an
            outlined pill Present and a gold pill Share. Below, the stage is black
            marble with thin gold and grey vein curves drawn across it. On it
            float three columns, a 262px layers card, the frame in the middle and
            a 282px inspector card, both cards polished slabs with a 1px gold edge
            and a deep shadow. The layers card lists gold kind icons with names
            and italic sub lines, Hero washed in gold with a gold edge and a
            Selected tag in spaced caps. The white Hero frame has a gold outline
            and round gold ringed handles, with a status band of spaced caps under
            it. The inspector uses italic Didone section names, Position, Fill
            with a ringed white swatch, Auto layout with Vertical, Corner radius
            and Export, and underline only fields with large Didone values. Below
            860px cards stack under the frame and the tools become a fixed bottom
            bar.
        spacing: An 8px unit used generously. 32px between floating cards, 20px card padding, 10px layer rows.
        density: Airy. Few lines per card with wide marble gutters.
        corners: 2px stone cards, round handles and avatars, full pill buttons.
        borders: One 1px gold edge at 55 percent on each card, hairline rules inside, fields as underlines only.
        shadows: Deep and soft, 0 30px 60px black at 70 percent under cards and 0 40px 80px under the frame.
        icons:
            Fine line icons at 1.2px stroke, 17px, in gold. Selected is a circled
            check, Collapsed a right chevron, Saved a cloud with a check, always
            with the word.
        focus: A 1px gold outline offset 3px with a 4px gold glow ring.
        tone: Reserved and elegant, Didone titles with spaced caps labels such as Position and Export.
    style258:
        number: 258
        run: 52
        screen: DesignEditor
        name: Dark concrete
        idea: A brutalist editor cast in raw dark concrete slabs with deep seams, form tie holes and spray stencilled labels, where safety yellow marks the active tool, the selection and the one action that matters.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/258.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            seam: #111213, the page and the 8px gaps between slabs
            slab: #2a2b2c, header, layers, inspector, status and the style sheet with a faint noise grain
            cast: #232425, the canvas well and the zoom block
            aggregate: #3a3b3d, avatar squares
            pit: #18191a, recessed fields and layer tiles
            ink: #e6e4df, text and outlines
            dust: #a9a7a1, meta and field captions
            safetyYellow: #f2c230, the active tool, the selected tile, Share, handles, focus and hazard tape
            safetyOrange: #c24e00, the 32 px guide with white text
        type:
            Three stacks. Labels and figures use Stencil Std, Impact,
            Haettenschweiler, Arial Narrow Bold in caps tracked 0.06 to 0.14em.
            Text uses Helvetica Neue, Arial, system-ui. Captions and status use
            ui-monospace. The file name is 24px stencil, panel titles 22px,
            inspector values 26px stencil, layer names 14px 700, status 13px mono
            caps and captions 11 to 12px mono.
        layout:
            Everything is a concrete slab separated by 8px dark seams, and big
            slabs carry two form tie holes at the top corners. The header slab
            holds a yellow BW block, CANVAS / WEBSITE REDESIGN over HOME V3,
            square outlined avatars, an outlined Present and a yellow Share. A
            full width row of seven blocks follows, the six tools as 64px slabs
            with icon, stencil name and key letter, Move solid yellow, and a 66%
            zoom block. Below sit two columns, the wide left and a 340px
            inspector. The left holds the canvas well with a faint 48px grid and
            the white Hero frame outlined 3px in yellow with square yellow
            handles, and under it the layers as a grid of 150px tiles, each with a
            number and kind, a kind icon, the name and note, the Hero tile solid
            yellow with Selected and the Features tile with Collapsed. The
            inspector stacks blocks with yellow stencil headings and sunk fields
            holding 26px figures, X 0, W 1440, #FFFFFF, Gap 32, Padding 96, R 0,
            PNG and 2x, then an outlined Export Hero. The status slab has a yellow
            and black hazard tape top edge and mono caps items. Below 860px slabs
            stack with the canvas first and the tool row becomes a sticky bottom
            row.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 8px seams between slabs, 24px slab padding, 8px between tiles and fields.
        density: Chunky. 64px tool blocks, 104px layer tiles and 26px figures.
        corners: None. Every slab, tile, field and button is square.
        borders: Seams instead of borders, 2px ink outlines on secondary buttons and avatars, a hazard stripe tape over the status slab.
        shadows: Inset shadows sink fields and tie holes. Slabs are flat with a noise grain.
        icons:
            Line icons at 2.4px stroke with square ends, 20px. Selected is a
            circled check, Collapsed a right chevron, Saved a cloud with a check,
            always with the word.
        focus: A 4px solid safety yellow outline, ink on yellow fills.
        tone: Site signage in stencil caps such as POSITION / SIZE, EXPORT HERO and SAVED 2 MINUTES AGO.

    style259:
        number: 259
        run: 53
        screen: DesignEditor
        name: Holographic
        idea: Floating capsules and glass cards on deep black, each rimmed with a thin iridescent foil edge that shifts from cyan to lilac to pink, so the interface reads as light caught in a hologram while the content stays plain.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/259.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            void: #06060a, the page and canvas with two faint lilac and cyan glows
            glass: #0e0e16, capsules, cards and the style sheet
            glassRaised: #151522, fields, layer icon tiles and Present
            selectedGlass: #1a1a2a, the selected layer inside its foil rim
            line: #262636, field borders and dividers
            ink: #f2f2fa, text
            mist: #a9a9c2, meta, labels and status
            foilCyan: #7ef3ff, foil start, handles, status icons and focus
            foilLilac: #b9a4ff, foil middle, field keys and the frame outline
            foilPink: #ff9ad5, foil warm stop
            foilGold: #ffe39a, foil highlight stop
            foilMint: #8affc1, foil end
            magenta: #b0189a, the 32 px guide with white text
        type:
            system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial for text and ui-
            monospace for values. Card titles are 20px 650 filled with the foil
            gradient, layer names 14px 550, values 13px 500 mono, meta 12px, and
            group labels 11px caps tracked 0.16em.
        layout:
            Nothing touches the edges. Three capsules float across the top, a file
            capsule with a foil orb B mark, Canvas · Website redesign over Home
            v3, a centred tool capsule with six round tools where Move is filled
            with foil and dark icon then 66%, and a people capsule with three
            pastel avatars, a foil rimmed Present and a foil filled Share. Below
            float a 264px layers card, the frame and a 284px inspector card, each
            glass with a 1px foil rim and 22px corners. Layers show an icon tile,
            name and sub line, Hero inside a foil rim with a foil tile and a cyan
            Selected. The white Hero frame has a lilac outline and round cyan
            ringed handles. The inspector uses chips with mono keys such as X 0, W
            1440, Gap 32, Pad 96, Fmt PNG and Scale 2x. The status is a foil
            capsule centred at the bottom of the canvas. The foil gradient runs at
            115 degrees through #7ef3ff, #b9a4ff, #ff9ad5, #ffe39a and #8affc1.
            Below 860px the pieces stack with the frame and status first and the
            tool capsule sticks to the bottom.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 20px between floating pieces, 20px card padding, 8px between chips.
        density: Light to medium, everything floating with black between.
        corners: Very round. 22px cards, 14px rows, 12px chips, full capsules for bars and buttons.
        borders: A 1px iridescent foil rim on every capsule, card, the selected row and the comment, with plain 1px lines inside.
        shadows: Soft black 0 20px 50px under cards and a faint cyan bloom under the frame.
        icons:
            Round line icons at 1.5px stroke, 18px, in 30px tiles in the layer
            list. Selected is a circled check, Collapsed a right chevron, Saved a
            cloud with a check, always with the word.
        focus: A 2px cyan outline offset 3px with a 6px cyan haze.
        tone: Light and modern with short labels such as Pad, Fmt and Saved 2 minutes ago.
    style260:
        number: 260
        run: 53
        screen: DesignEditor
        name: Chrome
        idea: A dark brushed steel console where every control is a pill of polished liquid chrome with a hard horizon reflection, pressed tools sink into dark wells and one ice blue light marks focus.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/260.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            night: #0c0d0f, the page and canvas edge
            steel: #1a1d21, brushed bars, the side panel and the style sheet
            steelRaised: #22262b, the comment card
            well: #0f1114, recessed fields, the tool tray and the people tray
            ink: #e9edf1, text on steel
            brushedGrey: #a3acb6, labels and meta
            chromeHigh: #f6f8fa, the chrome top highlight
            chromeMid: #d3d8de, the chrome upper body
            chromeHorizon: #8e959e, the hard reflection line at half height
            onChrome: #101215, text and icons on chrome
            ice: #6fd3ff, the pressed tool icon, status icons and focus
            statusGlass: #0a0d0f, the status readout with #b9e9ff text
            cobalt: #0a6fb0, the 32 px guide with white text
        type:
            Bahnschrift, DIN Alternate, Eurostile, Arial Narrow, system-ui for
            text and ui-monospace for values. Base 14px. The file name is 17px
            600, panel titles 18px 600, buttons 13px 700 caps tracked 0.06em,
            labels 12px caps tracked 0.08em, values 13px mono and the status
            readout 12px mono.
        layout:
            A brushed steel bar on top holds a chrome knob B, CANVAS · WEBSITE
            REDESIGN over Home v3, three chrome avatar buttons in a sunken tray, a
            sunken Present and a chrome Share ringed by a dark bezel. Below, the
            canvas fills the left and a 320px brushed side panel the right. Inside
            the canvas a sunken vertical tray holds six 50px round chrome tools,
            Move pressed into a black well with an ice icon, and a sunken 66%
            readout. The white Hero frame sits beside it with round chrome
            handles. A status readout runs under the canvas as a dark glass bar
            with a chrome bezel and pale blue mono text. The side panel holds
            Layers in a sunken tray, the Hero row a chrome pill with dark text and
            a SELECTED tag, then the Hero inspector as label rows, Position, Size,
            Fill, Vertical, Radius and Export, each with one or two sunken pill
            wells such as X 0, W 1440, Gap 32 and Fmt PNG, and a sunken Export
            Hero. The chrome gradient runs top to bottom through #f6f8fa, #d3d8de
            at 38 percent, #8e959e at 50 percent, #b9c0c8 at 72 percent,
            and #e4e8ec at the bottom. Below 860px the panels stack and the tool
            tray becomes a fixed horizontal tray at the bottom.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 28px canvas padding, 18px panel padding, 8px between wells.
        density: Medium. Big chrome tools with compact layer and property rows.
        corners: Round everywhere. Circles for tools and handles, 17 to 19px pills for buttons and wells, 14px trays.
        borders: 1px dark edges under a 1px white top highlight, and panels part with a black line over a faint light line.
        shadows: Inset shadows sink wells and trays, chrome pills sit proud with a 2px drop, and Share has a double ring bezel.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.9px stroke, 18px. Selected is a circled check,
            Collapsed a right chevron, Saved a cloud with a check, always with the
            word.
        focus: A 2px ice blue outline offset 3px with a 12px ice glow.
        tone: Precise and technical with caps labels such as Position, Size and Export.
    style261:
        number: 261
        run: 53
        screen: DesignEditor
        name: Dark mesh gradient
        idea: Soft blurred glows of violet, teal and coral drift behind smoked glass panels, with the tools in a floating dock at the bottom of the canvas and the file status as quiet chips in the top bar.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/261.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            night: #0d0c14, the page under the glows
            smoke: #141220, glass panels at 78 percent with a 24px blur
            smokeSolid: #1a1830, the comment card
            field: #121022, inputs inside glass
            ink: #f4f2ff, text
            lavenderGrey: #c0bcd8, meta, labels and chips
            glowViolet: #6b4cff, a mesh glow and the selected row tint
            glowTeal: #00b3a4, a mesh glow and the selected row tint
            glowCoral: #ff7a59, a mesh glow
            violet: #8d78ff, frame icons, the frame outline and the focus halo
            teal: #3fd8c6, text icons and the Saved chip icon
            coral: #ff9a7a, instance icons and the version chip icon
            action: #4f35d6, Share and the active tool as a gradient to #2f5fd0 with white text
            guideViolet: #6d3df5, the 32 px guide with white text
        type:
            A rounded stack, SF Pro Rounded, Nunito, Segoe UI Variable Text, Segoe
            UI, system-ui, with ui-monospace for values. Base 14px at 1.5. The
            file name is 15px 700, panel titles 15px 700, layer names 14px 650,
            values 13px mono, chips 12.5px and group labels 12px 700.
        layout:
            Four large blurred radial glows sit behind everything, violet top
            left, teal top right, coral bottom centre and blue bottom left. All
            panels are smoked glass with a 1px faint white rim and 20px corners. A
            full width top bar holds a gradient B tile, Canvas · Website redesign
            over Home v3, three status chips in the middle for Saved 2 minutes
            ago, 3 people editing and Version 41 with teal, violet and coral
            icons, then pastel avatars, Present and a gradient Share. Below sit a
            250px layers panel, the canvas and a 290px inspector. Layers show 32px
            icon tiles coloured by kind, the name and a sub line, Hero tinted
            violet to teal with a Selected tag. The white Hero frame floats with a
            violet outline and glow, and the tools sit in a glass dock centred at
            the bottom of the canvas with Move filled by the action gradient and
            66% after a divider. The inspector groups each property set in a
            lighter block, Position and size, Fill, Auto layout with Vertical,
            Corner radius and Export. Below 860px the panels stack and the dock is
            fixed at the bottom.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px around and between glass panels, 12px inside panels, 8px between blocks.
        density: Comfortable, with icon tiles beside each layer and grouped property blocks.
        corners: Soft. 20px panels, 14px rows, blocks and buttons, 10px fields, 22px dock.
        borders: A 1px white rim at 12 percent on glass and none inside, where blocks are lighter tints.
        shadows: Soft black 0 20px 50px under glass and a violet glow under the active tool, Share and the frame.
        icons:
            Rounded line icons at 1.7px stroke, 18px, coloured by layer kind in
            32px tiles. Selected is a circled check, Collapsed a right chevron,
            Saved a cloud with a check, always with the word.
        focus: A 2px white outline offset 2px with a 5px violet halo.
        tone: Friendly and light, with chips such as Saved 2 minutes ago and short labels such as Pad.
    style262:
        number: 262
        run: 53
        screen: DesignEditor
        name: Synthwave
        idea: A retro future night drive, where the frame floats over a striped sunset sun and a cyan perspective grid, neon magenta and cyan outlines trace the panels, and the inspector runs as a single property strip under the horizon.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/262.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            night: #0d0221, the page and the top of the sky
            panel: #170a33, the header, layers, the property strip and the style sheet
            deep: #0a0119, fields, tools and the status readout
            selected: #2c0e4a, the selected layer behind a magenta line
            line: #3a1f6e, idle outlines and underlines
            ink: #f6eaff, text
            haze: #c4b3e6, meta and labels
            neonMagenta: #ff4fd8, the layers outline, Share, the selected row and field keys
            neonCyan: #3ff0ff, the active tool, the grid floor, the frame outline, handles and focus
            sunGold: #ffb347, the sun top and the version readout
            sunPink: #ff2e88, the sun bottom and the logo
            guide: #c0157f, the 32 px guide with white text
        type:
            Titles in Arial Black, Segoe UI Black, Helvetica Neue at 900 italic in
            caps. Text in system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto. Readouts, tools and keys in
            ui-monospace. The file name is 18px italic caps, panel titles 16px
            italic caps with a neon glow, layer names 14px 650, values 14px mono,
            readouts 12px mono and group labels 11px 700 mono caps tracked 0.1em.
        layout:
            A header panel with a magenta bottom line holds a skewed sunset
            gradient BW logo, CANVAS · WEBSITE REDESIGN in cyan mono over HOME V3,
            a row of six outlined tool buttons with mono names, Move glowing cyan,
            a magenta 66%, outlined square avatars in magenta, cyan and gold, a
            cyan outlined Present and a solid magenta Share. Below sit a 268px
            left column and a wide right. The left is a magenta neon panel with
            the layers, cyan kind icons, names and mono sub lines, Hero outlined
            in magenta with a Selected tag, and at its foot a status readout
            listing Saved 2 minutes ago in cyan, 3 people editing in magenta and
            Version 41 in gold. The right holds the stage, a sky gradient with a
            large striped gold to pink sun and a cyan grid floor in perspective,
            with the white Hero frame centred over it at up to 600px, a glowing
            cyan outline and diamond handles. Under the stage a cyan neon property
            strip lays out five cells in one row, Position / size, Fill, Auto
            layout Vertical, Radius and Export with Export Hero, each with magenta
            keys and underlined mono values. Below 860px the stage comes first,
            the strip wraps to two columns and the tools become a fixed bottom
            bar.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px between panels, 48px around the frame on the stage, 10px between strip cells.
        density: Medium, with layers and the readout on the left and all properties in one strip.
        corners: Tight. 6px panels, 4px controls and rows, diamonds for handles.
        borders: 1.5px neon outlines, magenta around layers, cyan around properties and dim violet for idle controls.
        shadows: Neon glows only, 10 to 24px in the line colour, never a dark drop shadow.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.8px stroke, 18px, in cyan. Selected is a circled
            check, Collapsed a right chevron, Saved a cloud with a check, always
            with the word.
        focus: A 2px cyan outline offset 3px with a cyan glow.
        tone: Arcade cabinet, with italic caps titles and mono caps readouts such as Position / size.
    style263:
        number: 263
        run: 53
        screen: DesignEditor
        name: Dark pastel
        idea: A soft charcoal workspace of rounded cards where each kind of thing has its own pastel, mint for text, lilac for frames, peach for components and sky for images, so the layer tree and the inspector read by colour and by label at once.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/263.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            charcoal: #232428, the page and text on every pastel
            card: #2c2d33, the top bar, layer and inspector cards and the style sheet
            cardRaised: #34353c, property cards, the selected layer and Present
            sink: #1d1e22, the canvas well, fields and the tool track
            line: #3d3e46, tree ticks and quiet rings
            ink: #f1f0f5, text on dark
            muted: #b8b7c4, meta and field keys
            mint: #9fe3c6, text layers, the active tool, Saved and focus
            lilac: #c9b6f2, frames, Share, the selected ring and the frame outline
            peach: #f6c3a3, components, people editing and the comment pin
            sky: #a9d4f5, images, the version and the radius card
            butter: #f3e3a0, the Selected pill and the fill card
            guide: #7048c8, the 32 px guide and handle rims
        type:
            One stack, Avenir Next, Segoe UI, system-ui, Roboto, with ui-monospace
            for the frame size. Base 15px at 1.5. The file name is 16px 700, card
            titles 18px 700, layer names 14px 650, values 14px 600 tabular, badges
            and pills 12px 700, meta 12px.
        layout:
            A top card holds a lilac B tile, Canvas · Website redesign over Home
            v3, a centred segmented tool track where Move is a mint pill with icon
            and word and the other tools are icons only, then a 66% chip, three
            pastel rounded square avatars, Present and a lilac Share. Below sit a
            wide left and a 392px right. The left holds the canvas well with a dot
            grid, a lilac Hero pill label, the white Hero frame with a lilac ring
            and round handles, and three pastel status pills under it, mint Saved
            2 minutes ago, peach 3 people editing and sky Version 41. Under the
            canvas the layers card shows a tree, Hero across the full width with a
            lilac Frame badge, a lilac ring and a butter Selected pill, and its
            six children indented in two columns with badges that carry the kind
            word, mint Text, peach Instance, sky Image and lilac Frame, Features
            with a grey Collapsed pill. The right card is the inspector as a grid
            of small raised cards each headed by a pastel tag, lilac Position and
            size, butter Fill, sky Radius, mint Auto layout with Vertical, and
            peach Export with Export Hero. Below 860px the cards stack, the tree
            becomes one column and the tool track floats fixed at the bottom.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px between cards, 18 to 20px card padding, 12px between property cards.
        density: Comfortable, a two column layer tree and a two column grid of small property cards.
        corners: Round and soft. 20px cards, 16px property cards, 12 to 14px fields, buttons and rows, full pills for status.
        borders: None. Cards separate by tone and selection is a 2px inner lilac ring.
        shadows: Only on floating things, the comment card and the mobile tool track, 0 8px 24px black at 35 percent.
        icons:
            Rounded line icons at 2px stroke, 18px, inside pastel badges with the
            kind word. Selected is a circled check, Collapsed a right chevron,
            Saved a cloud with a check, always with the word.
        focus: A 3px mint outline offset 2px.
        tone: Warm and plain, with kind words on badges such as Frame, Text and Instance and pills such as Saved 2 minutes ago.

    style264:
        number: 264
        run: 54
        screen: CloudFiles
        name: Dark mono minimal
        idea: Black, white and greys only, with wide margins, hairline rules and thin type, so the files read like a quiet gallery list.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/264.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            black: #0a0a0a, page, panels and the style sheet
            raise: #161616, the selected row
            ink: #f2f2f2, text and headings
            muted: #a3a3a3, meta, labels, file icons and inactive nav
            line: #2a2a2a, hairline rules and meter tracks
            strong: #6b6b6b, control outlines and field underlines
            white: #ffffff, the primary button, current markers, meters, status icons and focus
        type:
            One system stack, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
            Arial. Base 15px at 1.6. The folder title is 44px at weight 250,
            the details title 20px at 400, file names 15px, meta 13.5 to 14px
            in muted grey, and column heads and panel labels 12px caps tracked
            0.1em.
        layout:
            A thin header holds the Brightwork Drive wordmark, an underline
            only Search files field and a round MO initials outline. Below it
            three columns sit inside 56px margins. A 200px text nav lists the
            five places with grey icons, My files current with a 1px white
            left bar, then 64.2 GB of 100 GB used with a 2px white meter and
            35.8 GB free. The middle column has the breadcrumb, the light 44px
            title, a white Upload button, an outlined New folder button and a
            List or Grid text switch with List underlined in white. Files are
            unboxed rows on hairlines with name, modified date over the person,
            and size. Status words follow the name. The upload shows as a 1px
            white line along the row foot. A 300px details column shows a
            square outlined preview, the name, facts as a two column list, a
            white Share button, an outlined Download button and an underlined
            Get link text button. Below 1180px details move under the list.
            Below 760px the nav scrolls sideways and rows put meta under names.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 56px page margins and column gaps, 18px row padding, 40px between blocks.
        density: Airy. About eight rows fill a laptop screen and nothing is boxed.
        corners: Square everywhere except the round initials.
        borders: 1px #2a2a2a hairlines under rows and the header. Controls use 1px #6b6b6b.
        shadows: None. The selected row is one step lighter with a 2px white inner left edge.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.75 stroke, 18px, in grey. Starred uses a filled
            star, Shared with 4 people two heads, Uploading 62% an up arrow in
            a ring, each in white beside the word.
        focus: A 2px solid white outline with a 3px offset.
        tone: Spare and literal, such as Upload, 64.2 GB of 100 GB used and 35.8 GB free.
    style265:
        number: 265
        run: 54
        screen: CloudFiles
        name: Dark dense grid
        idea: A graphite data grid with 28px rows, sortable column heads, mono figures and a key value inspector, built for scanning many files fast.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/265.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            base: #111317, grid body, page and style sheet
            panel: #171a1f, sidebar, toolbar and inspector
            head: #1d2127, column heads, the current nav row and secondary buttons
            ink: #d9dfe7, text and the storage fill
            muted: #949fad, meta, mono figures, column heads and icons
            line: #2a2f37, rules between every row, cell and panel
            track: #323844, control borders, flag outlines and meter tracks
            amber: #e3b450, primary button, sort arrow, current markers, selected edge, checkbox and focus
            selected: #2b2516, the selected row fill
        type:
            Two stacks. Text uses system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Arial at 13px.
            Figures, dates, sizes, the breadcrumb and the status bar use
            ui-monospace, SF Mono, Cascadia Mono, Menlo, Consolas at 11 to
            12px with tabular numbers. Column heads are 11px at 600 and panel
            labels 10.5px caps tracked 0.1em.
        layout:
            A 36px near black app bar holds a small amber B square, the word
            Brightwork and suite tabs Canvas, Drive, Code and Ops with Drive
            current, plus Mara Okafor and a mono MO tag. A 40px toolbar holds
            a mono breadcrumb, a Search files field with a slash key hint, an
            amber Upload button, a New folder button and a List or Grid
            segmented switch. A 188px sidebar lists the five places at 28px
            rows and ends with 64.2 GB / 100 GB, a 6px bar and 64.2% used. The
            centre is a full table with columns for row number, a checkbox,
            Name sorted ascending, Type, Size, Modified, By and Flags. Flags
            are outlined mono chips. The selected row is filled amber dark
            with a checked box and an amber left edge. A 288px inspector shows
            a small thumbnail card and a key value table, then Share, Download
            and Get link. A 26px status bar reads 8 items, 1 selected, 1
            uploading and storage. Below 1100px the inspector drops under the
            grid. Below 760px everything stacks and the table scrolls sideways
            inside its own area.
        spacing: A 4px unit. 10px cell padding, 14px panel inset, 6px between buttons.
        density: Dense. 28px rows, 26px controls, a 36px app bar and a 26px status bar.
        corners: 2px on controls and flags, square panels and cells.
        borders: 1px #2a2f37 rules between every row, column head and panel.
        shadows: None. Inner 2px amber edges mark the current tab, nav row and selected row.
        icons:
            15px line icons in muted grey, amber when current. Flags pair a
            filled star with Starred, two heads with Shared · 4 and an up
            arrow ring with Uploading 62% beside a small bar.
        focus: A 2px solid amber outline with a 1px offset.
        tone: Terse and technical, such as Flags, Inspector, 1 selected and 64.2 / 100 GB.
    style266:
        number: 266
        run: 54
        screen: CloudFiles
        name: Dark document
        idea: The folder reads like a calm written page on warm charcoal, with a slim page tree on the left and the selected file opening as a callout inside the text.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/266.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            charcoal: #191817, page, document and style sheet
            tree: #1f1e1c, the page tree
            ink: #e8e4dd, text and headings
            muted: #a9a297, meta sentences, tree labels and icons
            line: #34312d, dividers, dashed list rules and outlines
            tag: #2b2926, status tags, search and the current tree page
            callout: #24222f, the details callout
            lavender: #b8acf6, primary button, callout edge, upload meter, current tree icon and focus
            lavenderInk: #1b1733, text on lavender
        type:
            One system stack, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
            Arial. Base 16px at 1.7. The title is 36px at 700, section heads
            20px at 650, file links 16px at 500 underlined, meta sentences 14px
            muted, tags 13px, tree items 14px.
        layout:
            A 248px page tree holds the B mark and Brightwork Drive, a Places
            group with the five places, a My files group with Fernhill Studio
            open, Website redesign current and Brand assets and Wireframes
            nested on thin guide lines, then 64.2 GB of 100 GB used with a 4px
            bar. The right side has a slim top bar with the breadcrumb and a
            filled Search files field. Below sits a 760px reading column with
            a large folder icon, the title, the sentence A folder in Fernhill
            Studio with two folders and six files, and a row of Upload, New
            folder and a List or Grid switch. A Folders heading and a Files
            heading each hold lines of name, a sentence such as 4.2 MB,
            modified 27 Oct by Priya Nair, and tags. The selected file opens a
            callout under its line with the preview, owner, version, size,
            sharing and the three buttons. Below 860px the tree stacks on top
            and the callout goes full width.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 56px above the title, 36px before each section, 8px line padding, 20px callout padding.
        density: Calm. Each file is one sentence line and the selected file opens in place.
        corners: 6px buttons, fields and callout, 4px tags and tree items.
        borders: 1px #34312d dividers and dashed rules between lines. The callout has a 3px lavender left edge.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            18px line icons in muted warm grey. Tags carry a filled star with
            Starred, two heads with Shared with 4 people and an up arrow ring
            with Uploading, 62%, plus a 4px lavender bar.
        focus: A 2px lavender outline with a 2px offset and 4px rounding.
        tone: Written sentences, such as A folder in Fernhill Studio with two folders and six files.
    style267:
        number: 267
        run: 54
        screen: CloudFiles
        name: Dark editorial
        idea: The folder is laid out like a magazine spread at night, with a serif masthead, a numbered index of files and the selected file run as the cover story.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/267.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            night: #12100e, page, spread and style sheet
            paper: #1b1815, the cover frame
            cream: #efe7d8, headlines, body and outline buttons
            muted: #b5aa95, numerals, bylines, dek and labels
            rule: #3d362d, column rules and double masthead rules
            track: #2f2a24, storage and upload tracks
            vermilion: #f0805f, kicker, primary button, Starred mark, selected numeral, storage fill and focus
        type:
            Serif headings in Iowan Old Style, Palatino Linotype, Palatino,
            Book Antiqua, Georgia. The title is 80px at 400 with 0.95 leading,
            the cover title 32px, index entries 23px, folders 30px, the dek and
            sizes italic 17 to 20px. Labels and bylines use system-ui at 11 to
            12px caps tracked 0.1 to 0.16em.
        layout:
            A centred 1200px spread. The masthead has Brightwork Drive in serif
            with Drive in vermilion italic, the five places as caps section
            links with My files underlined, and an italic underline search,
            closed by a double rule. A hero has the breadcrumb as a vermilion
            caps kicker, the huge title and an italic dek, with Upload, New
            folder and a List or Grid caps switch at the right. Below, a seven
            to four split divided by a column rule. The left is The index, a
            numbered list 01 to 08 with big muted numerals, serif names, caps
            bylines of kind, date and person, and italic sizes, the two folders
            set larger. The right is Selected · cover story with a large
            drawn cover, the name, a dek, caps facts, the three buttons and a
            By the numbers box with 64.2 GB of 100 GB in big serif and a
            vermilion bar. Below 980px the columns stack. Below 760px the
            masthead stacks and the title drops to 52px.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 40px gutters and a 40px column gap split by a rule, 16px between entries, 48px above the title.
        density: Spacious and rhythmic. Eight numbered entries with the two folders set larger as features.
        corners: Square throughout.
        borders: 1px #3d362d rules between entries and columns, 4px double rules under the masthead and above the numbers box.
        shadows: None. The selected entry has a warm left fade and a vermilion numeral.
        icons:
            16px line icons used sparingly in buttons and marks. Status marks
            are caps words with a filled star for Starred in vermilion, two
            heads for Shared with 4 and an up arrow ring for Uploading 62%
            over a 3px rule bar.
        focus: A 2px vermilion outline with a 3px offset.
        tone: Editorial headings over plain facts, such as The index, Selected · cover story and 35.8 GB left on the shelf.
    style268:
        number: 268
        run: 54
        screen: CloudFiles
        name: Dark soft UI
        idea: Every panel, row and button is pressed out of one slate surface with paired light and dark shadows, the selected file sinks in, and text stays crisp with a bright focus ring.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/268.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            slate: #2b2e35, the one surface for page, cards, rows and style sheet
            highlight: #3a3e48, the light top left shadow
            shade: #1c1e23, the dark bottom right shadow
            well: #262930, status chip fill
            ink: #e7eaf0, text
            muted: #b0b7c3, meta, inactive nav, labels and file icons
            blue: #8fbaff, primary button, current icon, storage ring, upload fill and focus ring
            blueInk: #10213d, text and icons on blue
        type:
            One stack, Segoe UI, system-ui, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial.
            Base 15px. The title is 30px at 650, the details title 18px at
            600, file names 15px at 600, meta 13.5px muted, chips 12.5px at
            600, the storage figure 22px.
        layout:
            Three floating areas inside 28px padding. A 240px raised card
            holds a round B mark with Brightwork Drive, the five places with My
            files pressed in, and a raised 150px dial whose blue ring shows
            64.2 of 100 GB, captioned 64.2 GB of 100 GB used. The middle has the
            breadcrumb, the title and a pressed in pill search, then a raised
            blue Upload pill, a raised New folder pill and a pressed List or
            Grid track with List raised. Each file is its own raised 20px
            tile with a pressed round icon well, the name and chips, the date
            over the person, and the size. The selected tile is pressed in
            with its well raised and blue. A 320px raised details card has a
            pressed preview well, the name, a Starred chip, four raised fact
            tiles and three round raised action buttons labelled Share,
            Download and Get link, Share filled blue. Below 1200px details move
            under the list. Below 760px the card puts the dial beside the nav
            and tiles stack their meta.
        spacing: A 4px base on an 8px rhythm. 28px between cards, 16px between tiles, 22px card padding.
        density: Roomy. Each file is a raised tile with a round well.
        corners: 24px cards, 20px tiles, 22px pill buttons, fields and toggles, round wells and action buttons.
        borders: None. Edges come only from light and shade.
        shadows: Raised is 6px 6px 14px #1c1e23 with -6px -6px 14px #3a3e48. Small raised is half that. Pressed is the same pair inset, used for the selected tile, current nav, search and fields.
        icons:
            18px line icons, blue when current. Chips on the well colour pair
            a filled star with Starred, two heads with Shared with 4 people
            and an up arrow ring with Uploading 62%, with a pressed 8px track.
        focus: A 3px solid blue outline with a 4px offset, never a shadow alone.
        tone: Friendly and short, such as Details, Get link and 64.2 GB of 100 GB used.

    style269:
        number: 269
        run: 55
        screen: CloudFiles
        name: Aurora
        idea: Green and violet northern lights ribbon across a deep night sky header, and the files sit below in calm dark panels lit by one thin aurora edge.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/269.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            sky: #080d1c, page and the foot of the header sky
            panel: #0f1730, file and details panels
            row: #131d3a, folder cards
            selected: #18244a, the selected file row
            ink: #eef2ff, text
            muted: #a9b4d0, meta, labels and inactive tabs
            line: #24305a, panel borders and dividers
            auroraGreen: #62e8a6, primary button, current tab edge, Starred, folder icons, selected edge and focus
            auroraViolet: #b9a2ff, file icons, Shared, the view switch edge and the ribbon blend
            greenInk: #04281a, text on green
        type:
            One stack, Avenir Next, Segoe UI Variable Display, Segoe UI,
            system-ui. Base 15px. The title is 46px at 600, the details title
            19px at 600, file names 15px at 500, meta 14px muted, chips 12.5px
            at 600 and labels 12px caps tracked 0.06em.
        layout:
            A full width sky header fades from near black to deep navy, with
            small stars and three blurred green and violet ribbon strokes kept
            to the right of the title. It holds the aurora B mark with
            Brightwork Drive, a dark pill Search files field and an MO disc,
            then the five places as pill tabs with My files ringed in green,
            then the breadcrumb and title on the left and a dark storage card
            with 64.2 GB of 100 GB used and a green to violet bar on the right.
            Below, a wide panel and a 340px details panel, each with a 2px
            gradient line on its top edge. The wide panel has Upload, New
            folder and a List or Grid switch, two folder cards side by side,
            then column heads and six file rows with status chips. The
            selected row is lighter with a green left edge. Details shows a
            preview, the name, a Starred chip, facts and the three buttons.
            Below 1100px details stack under files. Below 760px the tabs scroll
            sideways and the ribbons shrink to the top band.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 32px page gutters, 24px between panels, 16 to 18px panel padding.
        density: Medium. A tall sky header, two folder cards, then six file rows.
        corners: 16px panels, 12px cards and preview, 10px buttons and chips, pill tabs and search.
        borders: 1px #24305a panel borders with a 2px green to violet gradient line across each panel top.
        shadows: None on panels. The ribbons are blurred strokes at 45 to 62 percent opacity kept away from text.
        icons:
            18px line icons in violet, green for folders. Status chips pair a
            filled star with Starred in green, two heads with Shared with 4
            people in violet and an up arrow ring with Uploading 62% over a
            gradient bar.
        focus: A 2px green outline with a 3px offset and a soft green halo.
        tone: Calm and plain, such as Details and 64.2 GB of 100 GB used.
    style270:
        number: 270
        run: 55
        screen: CloudFiles
        name: Bioluminescent
        idea: Files drift as rounded capsules in blue black deep water, lit only by glowing cyan rings, a depth gauge for storage and a round porthole for the selected file.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/270.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            deep: #020d15, page floor and gauge well
            water: #041824, page top, search and fact cells
            capsule: #072535, file capsules and the details panel
            capsuleLit: #0a3448, the selected capsule and the active view
            ink: #def7fa, text
            muted: #93b8c2, meta and inactive rail labels
            line: #0f3a4c, capsule and panel edges
            cyanGlow: #3fe6ee, primary button, current ring, folder orbs, gauge, porthole rim and focus
            foam: #a6f5e4, file icons and status words
            cyanInk: #00262b, text on cyan
        type:
            One humanist stack, Seravek, Gill Sans Nova, Gill Sans, Trebuchet
            MS, Segoe UI. Base 16px. The title is 40px at 500, the details
            title 20px at 600, file names 16px at 600, meta 14px muted, rail
            labels 12px.
        layout:
            The page is deep water, a soft lighter glow at the top and scattered
            blurred cyan plankton dots. A 104px rail holds a ringed B mark,
            the five places as round outlined icon rings with small labels
            beneath, My files ring glowing cyan, and at the foot a vertical
            depth gauge filled 64.2 percent with 64.2 GB of 100 GB. The main
            area has the breadcrumb and a pill search, then the title with a
            glowing Upload pill, a New folder outline pill and a List or Grid
            pill switch. Files are 40px round capsules with a round orb icon,
            the name with its status word, a sentence of kind, date and
            person, and the size. Folder orbs glow cyan. The selected capsule
            has a cyan rim and glow. A 340px rounded details panel has a small
            glowing jellyfish drawing in its corner, a 200px round porthole
            preview, the name, four fact cells and the three pill buttons.
            Below 760px the rail becomes a top strip with a horizontal gauge.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 36px main padding, 10px between capsules, 24px inside the porthole panel.
        density: Medium. One capsule per file, about 70px tall, with a sentence of meta.
        corners: Fully round. 40px capsules, 28px panel, 22px pill buttons and fields, circle orbs and porthole.
        borders: 1px #0f3a4c edges, teal orb rims, cyan rims on folders, the selected capsule and the porthole.
        shadows: Glow only, 0 0 12px cyan at 45 percent, on the primary button, current ring, selected capsule, gauge and meters.
        icons:
            20px line icons in foam inside round orbs. Status words in foam
            pair a filled star with Starred, two heads with Shared with 4
            people and an up arrow ring with Uploading 62% over a glowing bar.
        focus: A 2px cyan outline with a 3px offset plus the cyan glow.
        tone: Quiet and plain, such as Details and 64.2 GB of 100 GB, with the sea only in the visuals.
    style271:
        number: 271
        run: 55
        screen: CloudFiles
        name: Obsidian
        idea: Volcanic black glass cut into chamfered slabs, with glowing lava orange cracks marking the selected file, live meters and the paths through the screen.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/271.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            void: #09080a, page, fact tiles and style sheet
            glass: #141216, slab body, search and view switch
            glassSheen: #1c191f, top left of the slab gradient and secondary buttons
            edge: #2e2930, empty storage shards and tracks
            ink: #f1ebe6, text
            muted: #b3a8a3, meta, caps labels and inactive nav
            lava: #ff7a2f, primary button, cracks, current marker, storage shards and focus
            magma: #ffb07a, badge words and the hot end of the upload flow
            selected: #221510, selected slab and current nav fill
            lavaInk: #1d0900, text on lava
        type:
            One condensed stack, Bahnschrift, DIN Alternate, Roboto Condensed,
            Arial Narrow, Segoe UI. Base 15px. The title is 40px at 700 in caps
            tracked 0.04em, the details title 22px at 700, file names 15px at
            600, meta 14px muted, buttons 13px caps at 700 and labels 12px caps
            tracked 0.12em.
        layout:
            A header with a pentagon mark holding a lava zigzag, BRIGHTWORK
            DRIVE in tracked caps and a chamfered search, underlined edge to
            edge by a glowing jagged lava crack line. Below, three columns. A
            220px slab nav lists the five places, My files with a lava left
            edge, and ends with Storage shown as ten slanted shards, six lit,
            one part lit, three dark, then 64.2 GB of 100 GB. The middle has a
            caps breadcrumb, the caps title, chamfered Upload and New folder
            buttons and a List or Grid chamfered switch, then caps column heads
            and eight chamfered file slabs with name, badges, date, person and
            size. The selected slab glows warm from the left with a lava vein
            drawn down its edge. A 330px details slab shows a chamfered preview
            with a crack line, the name, a Starred badge, four chamfered fact
            tiles and the three buttons. Below 1180px details stack. Below
            760px the nav scrolls sideways and slabs put meta under names.
        spacing: A 4px base. 20px between slabs and columns, 6px between file slabs, 18px slab padding.
        density: Medium dense. Each file is a 52px slab with its meta in columns.
        corners: Chamfered. 12px cuts on the top left and bottom right of slabs, 7px on buttons, fields, badges and tiles.
        borders: No ordinary borders. Inner 1px lines on secondary controls and badges, a 3px lava edge on the current nav item.
        shadows: No drop shadows. Slabs carry a 135 degree glass gradient and a faint white sheen, and lava lines glow with a 2px blur.
        icons:
            18px line icons in muted grey, lava when current or selected.
            Chamfered caps badges in magma pair a filled star with Starred,
            two heads with Shared ×4 and an up arrow ring with Uploading 62%
            over a lava gradient flow bar.
        focus: A 2px lava outline with a 3px offset, and the chamfer drops away so the outline is whole.
        tone: Short caps labels such as Drive, Storage and Shared ×4 over plain values.
    style272:
        number: 272
        run: 55
        screen: CloudFiles
        name: Midnight garden
        idea: Files hang like leaves along a drawn vine on deep night green, the selected file blooms as a moonlit flower, and its details open in an arched garden window.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/272.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            night: #0c1611, page and style sheet
            bed: #12201a, leaf rows, storage bed, arch panel and search
            bedLit: #182a21, selected row and current nav
            vine: #3d5c48, stems, borders and line art
            ink: #edf1e6, text
            muted: #a9baa7, meta and inactive nav
            leaf: #8fd0a2, primary button, file icons, leaf markers, upload and storage growth
            moon: #f3e9c6, moon, Starred word and dashed focus
            petal: #eeb0ca, the selected flower, the selected edge and the Shared word
            leafInk: #0b2214, text on leaf
        type:
            One humanist stack, Optima, Candara, Segoe UI, Noto Sans. Base
            15.5px. The title is italic 40px at 500, the details title italic
            21px, file names 15.5px at 600, meta 13.5px muted and status words
            italic 13px.
        layout:
            A botanical line art vine with small leaves and petal dots runs
            across the top edge, over a leaf and moon mark with Brightwork
            Drive in italic and a leaf cornered search. Three columns follow.
            A 210px nav hangs the five places from a vertical stem, each with a
            small leaf, My files with a bright leaf and a lit fill, then a bed
            card with 64.2 GB of 100 GB used and a vine bar ending in a leaf.
            The middle has the breadcrumb, the italic title, Upload, New folder
            and a List or Grid switch, then a vertical vine down the left of
            the list. Each file row hangs from it on a leaf, folders on a bud
            and the selected file on a petal flower, and holds the name, an
            italic status word, date over person, and size. The selected row
            has a petal edge. A 330px arched panel holds Details, an arched
            preview window with a crescent moon, vines and the cover, the
            italic name, facts and the three buttons. Below 1180px the arch
            moves under the list. Below 760px all stacks.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 36px gutters and column gaps, 8px between leaf rows, 14 by 16px row padding.
        density: Medium. Eight rows hang from one vine with room for the line art.
        corners: Leaf shaped, 16px on two opposite corners and 3px on the others. The details panel is a 170px arch over 18px feet.
        borders: 1px vine green on panels and rows, a 2px vine line down the list and the nav, a petal edge on the selected row.
        shadows: None. Light comes from the moon, cream and petal accents.
        icons:
            18px line icons in leaf green. Rows hang from leaves, folders from
            buds and the selected file from a flower. Italic status words pair
            a filled star with Starred in moon cream, two heads with Shared
            with 4 people in petal and an up arrow ring with Uploading, 62% in
            leaf over a growth bar.
        focus: A 2px dashed moon cream outline with a 3px offset.
        tone: Gentle and plain, such as Details and 64.2 GB of 100 GB used.
    style273:
        number: 273
        run: 55
        screen: CloudFiles
        name: Moonlit zen
        idea: An ink black garden of few things, where a moon shows how full storage is, raked sand lines separate the files and the selected file rests like a stone in a ringed pebble panel.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/273.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            inkBlack: #0e0e10, page and style sheet
            stone: #18181b, the pebble details panel
            shadowStone: #1f1e22, the unlit moon and the selected row glow
            sand: #2e2d31, rings and tracks
            rake: #3a383d, raked lines, outlines and nav dots
            ink: #e7e3d9, text
            muted: #a39f96, meta, labels and icons
            moon: #ece6d4, moon, primary button, selected stone, current dot and upload thread
            paleGold: #dcc98f, the Starred word and focus
            nightInk: #1d1806, text on moon
        type:
            Light Mincho serif headings in Hiragino Mincho ProN, Yu Mincho,
            Noto Serif, Source Serif Pro, Georgia, and a light sans for text in
            Hiragino Sans, Yu Gothic UI, Segoe UI, system-ui. Base 15.5px at
            weight 300 and 1.7. The title is 48px serif at 300, the details
            title 24px serif, file names 16.5px sans at 400, meta 13.5px muted
            and the panel label 13px tracked 0.2em.
        layout:
            Wide 64px gutters. A quiet header has Brightwork Drive in widely
            tracked serif and an underline search. Three columns follow. A
            180px nav lists the five places with a small ring dot each, filled
            moon for My files, and below it a 120px moon whose lit part, about
            two thirds from the right, shows 64.2 GB of 100 GB. The middle has
            the breadcrumb, the light serif title, a moon pill Upload, an
            outline pill New folder and a List or Grid text switch marked by a
            moon dot. Files are unboxed rows of icon, name, status word, a meta
            line such as modified 27 Oct by Priya Nair, and size, each
            separated by three raked wavy lines. The selected file sits on a
            moon coloured stone ringed by two raked circles, with a faint glow.
            A 340px pebble panel with concentric raked rings in its corner
            holds Details, a pale preview, the serif name, facts and the three
            pill buttons. Below 1180px the pebble moves under the files.
            Below 760px the moon sits beside the nav and all stacks.
        spacing: An 8px unit used generously. 64px gutters and column gaps, 14px row padding, 56px above the moon.
        density: Sparse. One line of meta per file and nothing boxed except the pebble.
        corners: Round and organic. 21px pill buttons, a 48 to 56px pebble and a slightly uneven stone.
        borders: Almost none. Three raked wavy lines between files and a 1px underline on search and fields.
        shadows: None. The selected row has a faint radial glow and its icon sits on a moon stone ringed by two raked circles.
        icons:
            18px line icons in muted grey, dark on the selected stone. Status
            words pair a filled star with Starred in pale gold, two heads with
            Shared with 4 people and an up arrow ring with Uploading 62% over
            a 2px moon thread.
        focus: A 1.5px pale gold outline with a 5px offset.
        tone: Hushed and brief, such as Details and 64.2 GB of 100 GB under the moon.

    style274:
        number: 274
        run: 56
        screen: CloudFiles
        name: Rainy neon city
        idea: A wet night street where the file list glows like shop signs on rain soaked asphalt, pink and cyan neon tubes, soft bokeh and reflections pooling under every row.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/274.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            night: #090c15, the page and street background
            asphalt: #111725, the details window and the style sheet
            wet: #1a2136, raised fields and the switch track
            selected: #22183a, the selected row behind a pink edge
            ink: #eef1f8, names and body text
            mist: #a6b1c8, meta, labels, column heads and placeholders
            line: #2b3652, dividers and borders
            pinkNeon: #ff6bb0, the primary button with dark ink #1d0412, the wordmark glow, Starred and the selected edge
            cyanNeon: #4fe5ec, file icons, secondary button outlines, Shared and the focus ring
            amber: #ffc95e, folder icons and Uploading
        type:
            A condensed sans stack, Avenir Next Condensed, Roboto Condensed,
            Arial Narrow, then system-ui, with font-stretch condensed. Base 15px
            at 1.45. The wordmark is 30px bold caps tracked 0.12em with a pink
            glow and a cyan Drive line under it. The folder title is 28px bold,
            file names 16px semibold, column heads and labels 12px caps tracked
            0.14em, buttons 14px bold caps.
        layout:
            A dark street header carries blurred bokeh discs in pink, cyan,
            violet and amber and fine diagonal rain lines, clipped by the
            header section. The neon wordmark sits left and the Search files
            field right. Below are three columns. A 210px sidebar lists My
            files, Shared with me, Recent, Starred and Trash in caps, the
            current item lit by a pink left tube and a fading pink wash, with
            storage below as 64.2 GB of 100 GB used, a thin cyan to pink tube
            and 35.8 GB free. The middle column has the breadcrumb, the title
            Website redesign, then Upload, New folder and a List or Grid switch
            with List underlined in cyan. The list is a header row and eight
            rows of icon, name over kind, size, date and person, and status.
            Each row fades into a centred reflection line. The selected
            brand-guide-v3.pdf row has a violet fill, a pink left edge and a
            pink to cyan line. hero-motion.mp4 shows an amber progress tube. A
            300px details window on the right glows pink and holds the preview,
            name, Starred, owner, size, version, shared with, modified and the
            three buttons. Below 1100px the window drops under the list. Below
            760px everything stacks, the nav becomes two columns and rows wrap
            into name, size, date and status lines.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 32px gutters, 24px between columns, 12px row padding, 20px window padding.
        density: Medium. Eight rows fit with room for the reflection lines.
        corners: 2px everywhere so neon reads as glass tubes and signs.
        borders: 1px dark steel lines. Rows end in a centred fading reflection line. Status chips are 1px outlines in their colour.
        shadows: Coloured glows only, pink round the details window and primary button, cyan on focus.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.6px, 22px in rows, cyan for files and amber for
            folders. Status is an outlined caps chip with a word and a star for
            Starred, two heads for Shared, an up arrow for Uploading and a
            checked box for Selected.
        focus: A 2px cyan outline offset 3px with a soft cyan halo.
        tone: Short caps labels, such as Upload, New folder and Details.
    style275:
        number: 275
        run: 56
        screen: CloudFiles
        name: Film noir
        idea: A black and white case file lit through venetian blinds, typewriter captions on every fact, the selected file printed in reverse like a lone lit window.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/275.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            black: #0b0b0b, the page, the style sheet and text on white
            wall: #141414, the header wall under the blinds
            paper: #1c1c1c, the desk behind the file table
            dossier: #181818, the details column
            print: #2b2b2b, the photo print frame
            ink: #ececec, body text
            grey: #a8a8a8, captions, column heads, meta and placeholders
            rule: #4a4a4a, dotted and double rules
            white: #f4f4f4, the primary button, the selected row, the pressed switch and the focus outline
        type:
            Titles in a high contrast serif, Bodoni 72, Didot, Big Caslon, Times
            New Roman, bold capitals, 46px for the folder title and 24px for
            Details. Everything else in Courier New typewriter at 15px with 1.5
            line height. Buttons 13px bold caps tracked 0.1em, captions and
            column heads 12px caps tracked 0.2em in grey.
        layout:
            A header wall with a soft light pool top right and diagonal blind
            shadows, made of skewed translucent stripes, clipped by the header.
            On it sit a small typed line Brightwork Drive case file, the title
            Website redesign, a boxed typed breadcrumb with slashes, and a row
            of trapezoid folder tabs for My files, Shared with me, Recent,
            Starred and Trash, the current tab lighter with a white top line.
            Below is a desk in two columns. The main column has an underlined
            Search files field, Upload, New folder and a List or Grid switch
            with List in white. Then a real table captioned Contents of Website
            redesign with 8 entries, columns No., Name, Size, Modified and
            Notes, numbered 01 to 08, rows split by dotted rules. The selected
            row is printed in reverse, white with black text. Statuses are
            bracketed typed words. Uploading has ten small boxes with six
            filled. A storage ledger under the table shows a dashed bar and
            64.2 GB of 100 GB used. A 320px details column holds a slightly
            tilted grey photo print of the preview with a typed caption,
            Starred, owner, size, version and shared with as typed rows, and
            full width Share, Download and Get link. Below 960px the details
            drop under the desk. Below 700px table rows become stacked blocks.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 40px gutters, 12px cell padding, 24px between blocks.
        density: Medium. A numbered ledger with dotted rules.
        corners: Square. Folder tabs are trapezoids.
        borders: Double rules above table heads and between sections, dotted rules between rows, 1px grey outlines on secondary controls.
        shadows: Only a hard black offset under the tilted print.
        icons:
            Thin 1.4px line icons in grey and white. Status is a bracketed
            typed word with a filled star for Starred, two heads for Shared, an
            up arrow for Uploading and a checked box for Selected.
        focus: A 2px white outline offset 3px.
        tone: Typed and terse, such as case file, Contents and Notes.
    style276:
        number: 276
        run: 56
        screen: CloudFiles
        name: Jazz club
        idea: A late night lounge where one blue spotlight falls on a numbered set list of files, brass trim and a deep red velvet card hold the details, and titles sing in italic serif.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/276.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            midnight: #0a1120, the page and fields
            navy: #121b30, search, switch, the gauge card and the style sheet
            smoke: #1a2540, the pressed switch segment
            spotlight: #5082dc, the spotlight cone at 42 percent alpha and the selected row tint
            ink: #f3ecdf, warm cream text
            muted: #b7bdcc, meta and labels
            line: #2c3856, row rules and borders
            brass: #d9ad5b, numerals, the primary button with dark text #1c1306, Starred, the current nav and the gauge
            velvet: #561322, the details card
            velvetInk: #f1dcd8, text on velvet
            blue: #9cc8ff, Shared, Selected and focus
            rose: #ffa8a0, Uploading and its groove
        type:
            Titles and file names in Palatino Linotype, Book Antiqua, Georgia.
            The folder title is 52px italic at 400 weight, the list heading
            26px italic, file names 19px roman. Body in Optima, Candara, Segoe
            UI at 15px with 1.55 line height. Nav in 16px small caps, small
            labels 12px caps tracked 0.4em in brass.
        layout:
            A centred stage under a blue spotlight cone falling from the top
            centre, with faint smoke drifts, all clipped by its section. The
            header is centred, a brass line Brightwork Drive and Fernhill
            Studio, the italic title Website redesign, a breadcrumb with
            floral separators, then the five drive links in one centred small
            caps row between brass hairlines, My files underlined in brass.
            Below, a two column stage. The left column has a pill Search
            files, Upload, New folder and a pill List or Grid switch, then the
            heading Tonight's files with 8 in this folder, then an ordered set
            list. Each file gets a brass italic Roman numeral, a type icon, the
            name, a dotted leader and the size, then a second line of kind,
            date and person and any status. The selected row is a rounded blue
            tinted band with a thin blue outline. Uploading adds a rose groove
            bar. A gauge card follows with a brass half dial and 64.2 GB of
            100 GB used. On the right a 330px velvet card with an 18px radius,
            a brass frame and an inner hairline holds Details, the preview,
            the italic name, Starred, small caps facts aligned right, and a
            full width Share over Download and Get link. Below 980px the card
            moves under the list.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 40px between list and card, 14px row padding, 32px gutters.
        density: Relaxed. Each file takes two lines.
        corners: Pills for buttons, search and switch. An 18px velvet card with a 12px inner frame. The selected band is 12px.
        borders: 1px navy rules between rows. Brass hairlines frame the nav and make the double frame on the card.
        shadows: A long soft drop under the velvet card and a brass glow under the primary button.
        icons:
            1.5px line icons in brass. Status is a coloured semibold word with
            a star for Starred, two heads for Shared, an up arrow for Uploading
            and a checked box for Selected.
        focus: A 2px pale blue outline offset 3px with a faint blue halo.
        tone: Warm and a little theatrical, such as Tonight's files and 8 in this folder.
    style277:
        number: 277
        run: 56
        screen: CloudFiles
        name: Cinema
        idea: A dark auditorium where the selected file plays on a glowing screen, the folder is billed on a bulb lit marquee, and every file is a torn ticket stub in the aisle.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/277.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            hall: #0a0809, the page, notch cut outs and status chip grounds
            wall: #140f11, the current aisle item, search and the style sheet
            ticket: #1d1517, file tickets
            edge: #3e2c30, ticket outlines and the perforation
            velvet: #4a1019, the curtain gradient behind the marquee
            screen: #121722, the details screen surface
            screenGlow: #c9dcff, the screen glow, screen labels and Selected
            ink: #f6efe9, text
            muted: #c3b4ad, meta and labels
            bulb: #ffcf6b, marquee bulbs, the primary button with dark text #241703, Starred, file icons and focus
            mint: #8fe3bf, Shared
            coral: #ff9a8a, Uploading and used storage seats
        type:
            Marquee titles and stub figures in Impact, Haettenschweiler, Arial
            Narrow Bold. The marquee title is 54px caps, the screen title 30px,
            stub sizes 22px. Body in Helvetica Neue, Arial at 15px. File names
            16px bold, labels 12px caps tracked 0.3em.
        layout:
            A red curtain band holds a dark marquee box framed by a ring of
            small warm bulbs, with Brightwork Drive now showing, the title
            Website redesign and the breadcrumb, all centred. Below, a 200px
            aisle on the left lists the five drive links with small floor
            lights, the current one lit gold, and storage drawn as ten seats
            with six and a bit filled coral and 64.2 GB of 100 GB used. The
            main column opens with the screen, a wide panel with a gently
            curved bottom edge and a cool glow above and below. It shows
            Details on screen, the preview, the name, Starred, a row of four
            facts and Share, Download and Get link. Under it sit search, Upload,
            New folder and the List or Grid switch with List in cream. Then
            8 in this folder and eight full width tickets. Each ticket has
            round notches cut at both ends, the type icon, name, kind, date and
            person and statuses on the left, and after a dashed perforation a
            stub with Size or Items and the figure. The selected ticket has a
            gold outline and glow. Below 760px the aisle becomes a two column
            grid and the stub drops under a horizontal perforation.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 32px gutters, 10px between tickets, 24px screen padding.
        density: Medium. Single line tickets with a stub for size.
        corners: 6px tickets with round notches, 4px buttons, a screen whose bottom edge curves.
        borders: 1px warm edge on tickets and a 2px dashed perforation before the stub.
        shadows: A cool glow round the screen, a warm glow round the marquee and the selected ticket.
        icons:
            1.6px line icons in bulb gold. Status is a dark caps chip with a
            word and a star for Starred, two heads for Shared, an up arrow for
            Uploading and a checked box for Selected.
        focus: A 3px bulb gold outline offset 3px.
        tone: Showtime labels, such as now showing, on screen and 8 in this folder.
    style278:
        number: 278
        run: 56
        screen: CloudFiles
        name: Gothic cathedral
        idea: A dark stone nave where every panel rises to a pointed arch, files are set like stones between mortar joints, and rose window colours mark file types and statuses.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/278.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            stone: #131217, the page with faint coursing lines, and fields
            nave: #1c1a21, arched panels and the style sheet
            vault: #24212b, the current nav, the pressed switch and gem tiles
            joint: #36313f, mortar lines and borders
            ink: #ece6da, text
            muted: #b4acbd, meta and labels
            gold: #dcab48, arch trim, headings, the primary button with dark text #1b1305, folders, Starred and focus
            ruby: #ef6f80, PDF and video gems
            sapphire: #88a6ff, image and document gems, Shared and storage lancets
            emerald: #5fcf98, the spreadsheet gem and Uploading
            amethyst: #c39af2, the archive gem, the selected row and Selected
        type:
            One carved serif, Iowan Old Style, Charter, Cambria, Georgia. The
            folder title is 42px semibold capitals tracked 0.18em, panel
            labels 13px gold capitals tracked 0.32em, file names 16px
            semibold, body 15px at 1.55. Statuses are 13px italic.
        layout:
            A centred portal header with Brightwork Drive in gold, the title
            Website redesign and a breadcrumb with cross separators. Below,
            three bays side by side, each a dark panel whose top rises in a
            pointed arch 76px tall with a gold inner arch line. The left bay,
            Drive, lists the five links split by joints, the current one with
            a gold edge, then 64.2 GB of 100 GB used over ten small lancet
            windows with six and a bit filled sapphire. The middle bay, The
            files, holds search, Upload, New folder and a List or Grid switch
            with a gold underline on List, then eight rows. Each row has a
            gabled gem tile in its type colour, the name over kind, the size,
            and date and person with statuses below. The selected row has an
            amethyst wash and outline. Uploading shows an emerald bar. The
            right bay, Details, shows the preview inside a rose window of eight
            coloured petals, the name, Starred, facts split by joints and full
            width Share, Download and Get link. Below 1120px Details moves
            under the others. Below 760px the bays stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between bays, 20px bay padding, 10px rows.
        density: Medium. Three bays with plain rows.
        corners: Square, except every bay rises to a pointed arch and gems have a gabled top.
        borders: 1px mortar joints around bays and between rows, a gold inner line inside each arch.
        shadows: None. Depth comes from the arches and coloured glass.
        icons:
            1.5px line icons inside gabled gems coloured by file type. Status
            is an italic word with a star for Starred, two heads for Shared, an
            up arrow for Uploading and a checked box for Selected.
        focus: A 2px gold outline offset 3px with a soft gold halo.
        tone: Quiet and ceremonial, such as The files, Drive and Details.

    style279:
        number: 279
        run: 57
        screen: CloudFiles
        name: Candy dark
        idea: Chunky candy pieces on a dark plum tray, fat rounded file cards with bright sweet coloured blobs, gummy pill tabs and buttons that sit up on a little 3D ledge.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/279.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            plum: #1f1024, the page, fields and fact tiles
            tray: #2c1533, the top bar, file cards, details and the style sheet
            chew: #3b1d44, size chips, secondary buttons and the jelly frame
            ink: #fff4fb, text
            muted: #dcc6e2, meta and labels
            darkPlum: #2a0f2f, text and icons on every candy fill
            bubblegum: #ff7ac6, the primary button, the PDF blob, the selected border, Selected and storage stripes
            lime: #b9f56c, the current tab and sheet headings
            sky: #72d6ff, the pressed switch, links, the image blob and Shared
            lemon: #ffe36b, folder blobs, Starred and the focus ring
            tangerine: #ffa45c, the archive blob and Uploading
            grape: #c3a0ff, the document blob
        type:
            One rounded stack, ui-rounded, SF Pro Rounded, Nunito, Varela Round,
            Arial Rounded MT Bold, in heavy weights. The folder title is 40px at
            800, the details name 22px, file names 17px at 800, meta 13px at
            600, buttons 15px at 800, status pills 13px at 800.
        layout:
            A rounded top bar on the tray holds a pink candy B tile with Drive,
            pill tabs for My files, Shared with me, Recent, Starred and Trash
            with My files in lime on a green ledge, and a pill Search files
            field. Below sit the breadcrumb in sky links, the title Website
            redesign, and on the right Upload, New folder and a List or Grid
            switch with List in sky. The board has two columns. The list is
            eight chunky cards with 24px corners, each with a 56px candy blob
            for the type, lemon circles for folders, bubblegum for the PDF,
            sky for the image, lime for the sheet, grape for the document,
            tangerine for the archive and a domed bubblegum blob for the video.
            Next come the name, kind, date and person, candy status pills and a
            size chip on the right. The selected card has a 3px bubblegum
            border. Uploading adds a candy striped tangerine bar. A 330px
            details panel with 32px corners holds a wobbly jelly frame around
            the preview, the name, Starred, four fact tiles, Share, Download
            and Get link, and a storage tile with a striped bubblegum bar and
            64.2 GB of 100 GB used. A few sprinkles lie on the tray. Below
            1040px details drop under the list. Below 700px the size chip moves
            under the name.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 12px between cards, 16 to 20px card padding, 24px between list and details.
        density: Roomy and chunky. Big blobs and 17px names.
        corners: Very round. 24px cards, 28 to 32px bars and panels, pills for every control, a wobbly jelly frame.
        borders: Mostly none. 3px bubblegum on the selected card and 3px chew rings on fields.
        shadows: Solid 4px ledges under buttons and the current tab, inset highlights and shades on blobs.
        icons:
            2.2px rounded line icons in dark plum on candy blobs. Status is a
            candy pill with dark text, a lemon pill with a star for Starred, a
            sky pill with two heads for Shared, a tangerine pill with an up
            arrow for Uploading and a bubblegum pill with a checked box for
            Selected.
        focus: A 3px lemon outline offset 3px.
        tone: Friendly and short, such as Drive, Details and Upload.
    style280:
        number: 280
        run: 57
        screen: CloudFiles
        name: Dark Memphis
        idea: Memphis squiggles, confetti and dot grids on black, chunky white outlined blocks thrown slightly off grid with hard colour offset shadows, and every nav item wearing its own geometric shape.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/280.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            black: #0d0d0f, the page with a dot grid, fields, status chips and text on colour
            block: #17171b, outlined blocks and the style sheet
            white: #ffffff, text, 2px outlines and the current nav
            muted: #c4c4cc, meta and labels
            pink: #ff5c93, the primary button, the PDF tile and the details shadow
            teal: #2ee0cf, the list shadow, the image tile, Shared and storage stripes
            yellow: #ffd60a, the selected row with black text, the pressed switch, folders, Starred and focus
            lilac: #b99bff, the sidebar shadow and the document tile
            orange: #ff8a3d, the video tile and Uploading
        type:
            Headings and figures in Arial Black. The folder title is 50px, the
            details heading 22px, the small kicker 13px caps tracked 0.2em in
            teal. Body in Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans at 14px, file names 15px
            bold.
        layout:
            A black page with a fine dot grid and scattered confetti, a pink
            squiggle, a teal triangle, a yellow ring, a lilac square and dots,
            clipped by the section. The grid has a header over two columns
            and a details column on the right that spans both rows. The header
            has Brightwork Drive, the title Website redesign, a yellow squiggle
            underline and a breadcrumb with pink diamonds. The sidebar block
            has a lilac offset shadow and lists the five links, each led by a
            pure shape, a pink circle, a teal triangle, a yellow square, a
            lilac cross and an orange ring, the current item white with black
            text. Storage follows below a dashed rule as 64.2 GB of 100 GB used
            and a striped teal bar. The list block has a teal offset shadow, a
            toolbar with a pill search, Upload, New folder and a List or Grid
            switch with List yellow, then eight rows of a shape tile in a type
            colour, name and kind, size, and date and person with statuses.
            The selected row is solid yellow with black text. The details
            block is tilted about one degree, has a pink offset shadow and a
            white zigzag edge on top, and holds the preview, name, Starred,
            facts and the three buttons. Below 1080px details drop under the
            list. Below 720px everything stacks.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 28px between blocks, 14px block padding, 12px rows.
        density: Medium. Rows are plain and the blocks around them are loud.
        corners: Mixed on purpose. Square blocks and buttons, a pill search, file tiles cut as squares, circles, domes and leaves.
        borders: 2px white outlines on every block, tile and control, a zigzag edge on the details block.
        shadows: Hard offset colour blocks of 6 to 8px in lilac, teal and pink. Buttons get a 4px offset.
        icons:
            2.2px line icons inside filled shape tiles. Nav uses pure shapes.
            Status chips differ in outline too, a square chip with a star for
            Starred, a pill with two heads for Shared, a dashed chip with an up
            arrow for Uploading and a white chip with a checked box for
            Selected.
        focus: A 3px yellow outline offset 4px.
        tone: Loud and short, such as Upload, New folder and Details.
    style281:
        number: 281
        run: 57
        screen: CloudFiles
        name: Noir comic
        idea: A dark comic page cut into angled panels with cream ink borders and black gutters, halftone shading, caption boxes and speech bubbles, and one red spot colour for what matters.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/281.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            gutter: #070708, the page and gutters between panels
            panel: #1b1b1f, panels and the style sheet
            panelTwo: #232328, file frames inside the list panel
            black: #0b0b0c, fields, secondary buttons and text on red and cream
            cream: #ece4d4, panel borders, speech bubbles, the current nav and the pressed switch
            ink: #f3eee4, text on dark
            muted: #bdb6aa, meta and labels
            redSpot: #ff5a4a, the only colour, captions, the primary button, Starred, the selected frame and focus
        type:
            One stack, Trebuchet MS, Segoe UI, Tahoma. Lettering is italic 900
            capitals with a hard black drop, 56px for the folder title, 20px
            for the details name and 18px for panel labels. Body 15px. Captions
            13px bold caps on red.
        layout:
            A comic page of panels with 14px black gutters. A wide title panel
            with halftone dots carries a red caption box Brightwork Drive and
            Fernhill Studio, the lettered title Website redesign, a boxed caps
            breadcrumb and a pill Search files field. Below are three panels.
            The Drive panel has a slightly slanted top and lists the five
            links, the current one cream and skewed, then storage as 64.2 GB of
            100 GB used over a halftone bar filled cream to 64 percent. The
            files panel opens with the label 8 files, Upload, New folder and a
            List or Grid switch with List cream, then eight small frames, one
            per file, with icon, name and kind, size, and date and person.
            Statuses are speech bubbles with tails. The selected frame has a
            3px red border, a red wash and a black drop. Uploading adds a
            halftone bar. The details panel has a slanted top, a red caption
            brand-guide-v3.pdf is selected, the preview with halftone and a
            light shaft, the lettered name, Starred, an oval cream speech
            bubble holding owner, size, version and shared with, and the three
            buttons. Below 1100px details drop under the files. Below 740px the
            panels stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 14px gutters, 16 to 18px panel padding, 8px between file frames.
        density: Medium. Each file is its own small frame.
        corners: Square panels with slanted edges, round speech bubbles with tails, a pill search.
        borders: 3px cream ink round panels, 2px warm grey round file frames, 3px red round the selected frame.
        shadows: Hard black offsets on captions, buttons, lettering and the selected frame.
        icons:
            2px line icons in cream. Status is a speech bubble with a word, a
            red bubble with a star for Starred, a cream bubble with two heads
            for Shared, a squarer cream bubble with an up arrow for Uploading
            and a black bubble with a checked box for Selected.
        focus: A 3px red outline offset 3px with a cream ring outside it.
        tone: Comic captions, short and punchy, such as 8 files and brand-guide-v3.pdf is selected.
    style282:
        number: 282
        run: 57
        screen: CloudFiles
        name: Tarot night
        idea: A tarot spread laid out on a starry indigo cloth, three framed cards with fine gold line art, corner stars and crescent moons, the selected file drawn as its own card.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/282.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            night: #0e0b1e, the page cloth, fields and the preview ground
            card: #18132e, the three cards and the style sheet
            cardTwo: #211a3d, the current nav and the pressed switch
            selected: #2b2252, the selected row inside a gold line
            gold: #e0c171, line art, corner stars, headings, the primary button with dark text #1a1430, medallions and Starred
            goldLine: #8e7a48, frames and dotted rules, never text
            ink: #f1eadb, text
            muted: #bfb7d2, meta, labels and italics
            moon: #a9c8ff, Shared and focus
            rose: #f3a9c6, Uploading and its moon phase dots
        type:
            One book serif, Baskerville, Libre Baskerville, Garamond, Times New
            Roman. The folder title is 44px small caps tracked 0.1em, card
            headings 18px gold small caps tracked 0.18em between dashes, file
            names 17px, body 16px. Meta, kinds and statuses are italic, 13 to
            14px.
        layout:
            A deep indigo cloth with a scattered star field. A centred header
            has a gold crescent moon with a small star, Brightwork Drive in
            gold small caps, the title Website redesign and an italic
            breadcrumb with star separators. Below lies a spread of three
            cards. Each card has a 14px radius, a dull gold outer line, an
            inner frame 7px in and a small four point gold star at each
            corner. The left card, Drive, lists the five links with My files
            ringed in gold, then a gold storage ring with a moon inside and
            64.2 GB of 100 GB used. The middle card, The files, has a pill
            search, Upload, New folder and a pill List or Grid switch, then
            eight rows split by dotted gold rules. Each row has a round gold
            medallion with the type icon, the name over an italic kind, the
            size, and date and person with italic statuses. The selected row is
            a violet band in a gold line. Uploading adds five moon phase dots
            with three filled. The right card, Details, shows the preview
            inside a sun and moon line drawing, the name on a ruled banner,
            Starred, facts on dotted rules and full width Share, Download and
            Get link. Below 1100px Details moves under the others. Below 740px
            the cards stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 28px between cards, 26px card padding, 12px rows.
        density: Relaxed. Three cards with generous margins.
        corners: 14px cards with a 9px inner frame, pills for controls, round medallions.
        borders: 1px dull gold outer and inner frames, dotted gold rules between rows.
        shadows: A soft long drop under each card, nothing else.
        icons:
            1.3px fine line icons in gold medallions. Status is an italic word
            with a star for Starred, two heads for Shared, an up arrow for
            Uploading and a checked box for Selected.
        focus: A 2px pale moon blue outline offset 3px with a faint halo.
        tone: Hushed and a little mystical in headings, such as The files and Drive, and plain in data.
    style283:
        number: 283
        run: 57
        screen: CloudFiles
        name: Art deco night
        idea: A black lacquer and gold night club facade, a sunburst fan crowning the title, symmetric double ruled frames with stepped corners, and files set in a tall gold ruled register.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/283.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            onyx: #0b0b0d, the page, corner steps and the preview ground
            lacquer: #141418, frames and the style sheet
            panel: #1b1b21, the page inside the preview
            selected: #24211a, the selected row between gold rules
            gold: #d9b45a, rules, fans, headings, the primary button with dark text #120f08, the current nav and Starred
            darkGold: #7d6630, inner rules and fact grid lines, never text
            champagne: #f0e3c0, text and the inner focus ring
            muted: #b9b2a0, meta and labels
            jade: #5cc2a8, Shared
            copper: #e8956b, Uploading and its segments
        type:
            Headings, labels and figures in a geometric sans, Futura, Century
            Gothic, Avenir Next, Josefin Sans, all at 400 weight. The folder
            title is 46px caps tracked 0.22em, frame headings 14px gold caps
            tracked 0.42em, table heads 11px caps tracked 0.26em. Body in Avenir
            Next, Gill Sans, Segoe UI at 15px, file names 16px.
        layout:
            A symmetric facade. A sunburst of fine gold rays and arcs rises
            from behind the centred header, clipped by its section. The header
            has Brightwork Drive in gold, the title Website redesign, a diamond
            rule and a caps breadcrumb with gold diamonds. A centred nav band
            between double gold rules holds the five links, My files as a gold
            block with dark text. Below are two framed columns, a 320px details
            plaque on the left and the register on the right. Each frame has a
            3px double gold border and a small stepped gold square on each
            corner. The plaque shows Details, the preview over fan rays, the
            name, Starred, a two by two grid of facts, full width Share,
            Download and Get link, and a fan shaped storage gauge with six of
            ten blades gold and 64.2 GB of 100 GB used. The register has an
            underlined search, Upload, New folder and a List or Grid switch
            with List gold, then a table captioned Website redesign with 8
            entries, columns Name, Modified and Size, the size right aligned.
            Each name has a gold diamond with the type icon and statuses below
            in spaced caps. The selected row is a warm dark band between gold
            rules with a gold left bar. Uploading shows eight copper segments
            with five filled. Below 1000px the register comes first and the
            plaque follows. Below 700px rows become stacked blocks.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 32px between frames, 28px frame padding, 12px cells.
        density: Medium. A three column register.
        corners: Square frames with a stepped gold square at each corner. No rounding anywhere.
        borders: 3px double gold round frames, double rules under table heads and round the nav, 1px dark rules between rows.
        shadows: None. Depth comes from double rules and inset gold rings on the primary button.
        icons:
            1.5px line icons inside gold diamonds. Status is a spaced caps word
            with a star for Starred, two heads for Shared, an up arrow for
            Uploading and a checked box for Selected.
        focus: A 2px champagne outline offset 3px, then a dark gap and a gold ring.
        tone: Formal and spare, such as Register, Details and 8 entries.

    style284:
        number: 284
        run: 58
        screen: CodeRepository
        name: Arctic
        idea: A calm frost-toned review page in cool blue-grey, with a quiet three-card glance row over the files, the diff and a slim facts column, soft 10px corners and pale ice-blue as the only strong accent.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/284.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            night: #20252d, the page background and the diff code area
            panel: #2a313b, the header band, cards, the side column and the style sheet cards
            raised: #353e4b, the selected tab pill, hover, chips and the disabled merge button
            line: #4a5566, every border and divider
            snow: #e6ecf3, text
            mist: #b0bccb, meta, labels and line numbers
            frost: #8fc6d8, links, the current tab, the primary button and focus
            frostInk: #14202a, text on frost
            aurora: #a9d18e, passed, approved, added counts and added signs
            thaw: #e8c27a, requested changes
            rose: #ef9aa0, failing, removed counts and removed signs
            addTint: #25372f, added line rows
            delTint: #3a2a31, removed line rows
        type:
            One system sans stack, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial,
            base 15px at 1.5. The pull request title is 28px at 600, section titles 17px
            at 600, side labels 12px caps tracked 0.08em in mist, counts with tabular
            numbers. Code is 13px ui-monospace at 1.6.
        layout:
            A centered 1160px column. A panel coloured band holds the Brightwork Code
            mark, the owner and repository name with a Private chip, and Watch 12, Star
            48 and Fork 3 as small outlined buttons. Under it the six tabs sit in one
            rounded segmented pill, the current tab filled with raised and an ice blue
            underline dot. The title with number 214 and the Open chip and merge line
            come next. A glance row of three equal cards follows, checks with a twelve
            segment bar, reviewers, and labels. Then two columns, a wide one with the
            files list with small plus and minus bars and the diff card with the inline
            comment, and a 300px facts column with assignees, labels, milestone, linked
            issue and the merge box. Below 900px everything stacks and the glance cards
            stack below 640px.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px card padding, 16px between cards, 40px between the header and the title block.
        density: Low to medium. Generous whitespace, one idea per card.
        corners: Soft. 10px cards, 999px tab pill and chips, 8px buttons and fields.
        borders: 1px line on every card and row. The diff hunk header and the comment have a 3px frost left edge.
        shadows: None. Separation comes from the panel tint and the thin lines.
        icons:
            Rounded line icons at 1.6px stroke sized at 1.1em. Passed and approved use a
            check circle, failing a crossed square, requested changes a triangle with a
            bang, Open the pull request glyph and the blocked merge a padlock, always
            beside the word.
        focus: A 2px frost outline offset 2px, with a 4px dark gap so it reads on every panel.
        tone: Calm and plain, such as 11 of 12 checks passed and Merging is blocked until all checks pass.
    style285:
        number: 285
        run: 58
        screen: CodeRepository
        name: Vampire
        idea: A dark purple bento board where every tile is labelled like a code comment, the title reads like a keyword, labels are string tokens, and pink, green and cyan carry the syntax colours of the whole page.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/285.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            crypt: #1d1928, the page background and the diff code area
            velvet: #272235, tiles and the style sheet cards
            dusk: #342d48, chips, fields, hunk header and the disabled merge button
            seam: #4d4468, tile borders and dividers
            moon: #f5f2fb, text
            haze: #bbb2d4, meta and line numbers
            pink: #ff79c6, keywords, the title number, the primary button, the current tab and focus
            cyan: #8be9fd, links, owner name and JSX tags
            violet: #c6a8ff, comment style tile labels and attribute names
            green: #5af78e, passed, approved, added lines and function names
            lemon: #f1fa8c, requested changes and strings
            blood: #ff6e6e, failing and removed lines
            addTint: #1f3329, added line rows
            delTint: #3d1f2c, removed line rows
        type:
            System sans, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Arial, for prose at 15px on 1.5,
            and a monospace stack, ui-monospace, Cascadia Code, JetBrains Mono, Menlo,
            Consolas, for every label, token, number and code line. Title 30px at 700
            with the number 214 in pink mono. Tile labels are 13px mono lowercase
            written as // checks in violet.
        layout:
            A 1200px bento grid of twelve columns. A slim top bar shows the owner in
            cyan, a slash and the repository name in pink, a Private token, and Watch
            12, Star 48 and Fork 3 written as small call style chips. Tabs sit beneath
            as a flat row with a 3px pink bar under Pull requests. The first tile spans
            the width and holds the title, the Open chip, the merge sentence with branch
            tokens, and the labels as quoted string tokens. The second row has three
            tiles, checks with a twelve segment donut and 11 of 12 in the middle,
            reviewers, and details with assignees, milestone, linked issue and the
            disabled merge button. The third row has a four column files tile and an
            eight column diff tile with syntax colours and the inline comment. Below
            980px tiles take half or full width, below 640px all stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px gaps between tiles, 24px tile padding, 8px between tokens.
        density: Medium. Many small tiles, each with one job.
        corners: Rounded. 16px tiles, 10px buttons and fields, 999px tokens.
        borders: 1px seam border on every tile. The comment and the hunk header have a 3px pink left edge.
        shadows: A soft 0 8px 24px black shadow under tiles and a faint pink glow under the primary button.
        icons:
            Line icons at 2px stroke sized at 1.1em in the colour of their word. Check
            circle for passed and approved, crossed square for failing, triangle with a
            bang for requested changes, padlock for the blocked merge.
        focus: A 2px pink outline offset 2px with a 6px soft pink glow.
        tone: Playful developer voice in labels, such as // checks and // reviewers, plain sentences in content.
    style286:
        number: 286
        run: 58
        screen: CodeRepository
        name: Retro groove
        idea: A warm brown-black conversation timeline with a three-stripe orange, mustard and aqua band, slab serif headings, chunky pill buttons with hard offset shadows and a ticket stub side column, like a seventies hi-fi brochure set in code.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/286.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            espresso: #1f1a16, the page background and the diff code area
            walnut: #2b241e, timeline cards, the side tickets and the style sheet cards
            cocoa: #3a3028, the masthead, chips, the hunk header and the disabled merge button
            grain: #5c4c3d, borders, the timeline spine and dashed ticket tears
            cream: #f3e6c9, text
            sand: #cdb994, meta, line numbers and side labels
            tangerine: #fe8a3c, the primary button, slab headings, the current tab and focus
            mustard: #f5c046, requested changes and the middle stripe
            aqua: #8ec9b0, links and the third stripe
            olive: #b8cc5a, passed, approved, Open and added lines
            brick: #f47a6c, failing and removed lines
            shadow: #0e0b09, the hard 4px offset shadow under buttons and cards
            addTint: #2c3220, added line rows
            delTint: #3d2420, removed line rows
        type:
            Headings in a slab serif stack, Rockwell, Roboto Slab, Zilla Slab, DejaVu
            Serif, Georgia, title 32px at 700 and section titles 20px. Body in Trebuchet
            MS, Segoe UI, system-ui at 15px on 1.55. Ticket labels 12px caps tracked
            0.14em. Code in Courier New, ui-monospace at 14px.
        layout:
            A cocoa masthead with a round B badge, the owner and repository in slab
            type, a Private stamp and Watch 12, Star 48 and Fork 3 as small pills.
            Directly under it a band of three 6px stripes in tangerine, mustard and aqua
            runs the full width. Tabs follow as rounded top folders, the current one
            tangerine. The title block sits at 1140px. Below, two columns. The left is a
            vertical timeline with a 2px grain spine and round nodes holding icons, with
            events for Sam Ortiz opening the request, the three changed files, the
            checks result with e2e-android named, Jonas Weber approving, and Tomás Ruiz
            requesting changes with the diff card and inline comment nested in his
            event. The right is a 300px stack of ticket stubs with dashed tear lines for
            assignees, labels, milestone, linked issue and the merge stub. Below 900px
            the tickets move under the timeline.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 20px card padding, 24px between timeline events, 48px timeline indent.
        density: Medium low. A story told top to bottom, one event at a time.
        corners: Round and chunky. 14px cards, 999px buttons, tabs and chips, round timeline nodes.
        borders: 2px grain borders on cards and tickets, dashed 2px tear lines between ticket sections, a 2px spine.
        shadows: Hard 4px by 4px offset shadows in near black under cards and buttons, no blur.
        icons:
            Line icons at 2.25px stroke inside 32px round timeline nodes and inline at
            1.1em. Check circle for passed and approved, crossed square for failing,
            triangle with a bang for requested changes, padlock for the blocked merge.
        focus: A 3px tangerine outline offset 3px.
        tone: Friendly and narrative, such as Sam Ortiz opened this pull request and Tomás Ruiz asked for changes.
    style287:
        number: 287
        run: 58
        screen: CodeRepository
        name: Vibrant classic
        idea: A dense, square, all-monospace review workspace on near-black, with a file tree, a dominant syntax-coloured diff and a narrow facts pane butted together by hairlines, where hot pink, lime and orange do the talking.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/287.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            coal: #1b1b18, the page background and the diff pane
            slate: #26261f, the top bar, the file tree and facts panes, the style sheet cards
            ridge: #34342c, the selected file row, chips and the disabled merge button
            rule: #4a4a40, hairlines between panes and rows
            chalk: #f8f8f2, text
            smoke: #b4b4a6, meta, line numbers and pane labels
            hotPink: #ff5c93, keywords, the current tab bar, the pull request number and pane labels markers
            lime: #a6e22e, the primary button, passed, approved, Open and added lines
            orange: #fd971f, requested changes, strings and attribute names
            cyan: #66d9ef, links, JSX tags and focus
            purple: #ae81ff, constants and counts
            red: #ff6b6b, failing and removed lines
            addTint: #25301a, added line rows
            delTint: #3a1f24, removed line rows
        type:
            One monospace stack for everything, ui-monospace, SF Mono, Cascadia Mono,
            DejaVu Sans Mono, Menlo, Consolas. Base 13px at 1.5, the title 20px at 700,
            pane labels 11px caps tracked 0.12em with a pink square marker, counts 12px
            at 700.
        layout:
            Full width, no outer margin. A 44px slate top bar holds the owner and
            repository, a Private tag, watch 12, star 48 and fork 3 as inline counters,
            and the six tabs as flat text tabs with a 2px pink top bar on Pull requests.
            Under it one dense summary strip shows the number 214 in pink, the title,
            Open, Sam Ortiz merging 6 commits into main from feature/push-prefs, the
            checks score and the two review verdicts, separated by hairlines. Then three
            panes butted together with 1px rules. A 260px file tree with folder rows and
            each file with plus and minus counts, the current file highlighted. A wide
            diff pane with a file tab bar, the hunk, syntax colours and the inline
            comment. A 300px facts pane with reviewers, all twelve checks in a compact
            list, labels, assignees, milestone, linked issue and the merge button. Below
            1100px the facts pane drops under the diff, below 760px all three stack.
        spacing: A 4px unit. 8px row padding, 12px pane padding, no gaps between panes.
        density: Dense. Everything visible at once, small type, tight rows.
        corners: Square everywhere, 2px on chips only.
        borders:
            1px rule hairlines between panes and rows. A 2px pink top bar on the current
            tab and a 2px cyan left edge on the comment.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.5px stroke at 1em, square caps. Check circle for passed and
            approved, crossed square for failing, triangle with a bang for requested
            changes, padlock for the blocked merge, always next to the word.
        focus: A 2px cyan outline offset 1px.
        tone: Terse and technical, such as checks 11/12, e2e-android failing and merge blocked.
    style288:
        number: 288
        run: 58
        screen: CodeRepository
        name: Indigo night
        idea: A soft deep-indigo workspace with a left repository sidebar and floating 16px cards, led by a merge readiness panel that gathers the twelve check pills, the two reviewers and the locked merge button, lit only by soft blue and purple.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/288.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            abyss: #12132a, the page background, the sidebar and the diff code area
            deep: #1b1d3c, cards and the style sheet cards
            dusk: #262a55, the current sidebar item, chips, the hunk header and the disabled merge button
            edge: #383c72, card borders and dividers
            starlight: #eceefe, text
            lilac: #b3b8e3, meta, labels and line numbers
            blue: #8fb4ff, links, the primary button and focus
            purple: #b79cff, the current sidebar bar, section icons and the hero glow
            mint: #7ee0b0, passed, approved, Open and added lines
            honey: #ffcf7a, requested changes
            coral: #ff8fa3, failing and removed lines
            addTint: #1b3036, added line rows
            delTint: #3a2140, removed line rows
        type:
            One sans stack, Inter, Segoe UI Variable, Segoe UI, system-ui, Roboto, base
            15px on 1.55. Title 30px at 650, card titles 18px at 600, sidebar items 14px
            at 500, meta 13px. Code 13px ui-monospace on 1.65.
        layout:
            Two columns at full height. A 264px abyss sidebar holds the B mark and
            Brightwork Code, the owner and repository name with a Private chip, three
            small stat tiles for Watch 12, Star 48 and Fork 3, and the six tabs as a
            vertical list with counts, Pull requests current with a dusk fill and a
            purple left bar. The main column, max 1000px, starts with a hero card with a
            soft purple glow at one corner, the number 214, the title, the Open chip and
            merge sentence, and a ruled property row for assignees, labels, milestone
            and linked issue. Next a merge readiness card with three blocks side by
            side, twelve check pills with the failing one hollow and named, the two
            reviewers as avatar rows with verdicts, and the disabled merge button with
            its reason. Then three file cards in a row, each with its path, counts and a
            split bar, and the diff card with the inline comment. Below 1000px the
            sidebar becomes a top block with the tabs as a wrapping row and the
            readiness blocks stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 28px card padding, 24px between cards, 32px main padding.
        density: Low. Big soft cards, plenty of air.
        corners: Very soft. 16px cards, 12px stat tiles and buttons, 999px chips and check pills, round avatars.
        borders: 1px edge borders on cards. The current sidebar item has a 3px purple left bar.
        shadows:
            Large soft shadows, 0 12px 32px at 45 percent black, and a blurred purple
            glow behind the hero corner.
        icons:
            Rounded line icons at 1.75px stroke at 1.15em, section icons in purple.
            Check circle for passed and approved, crossed square for failing, triangle
            with a bang for requested changes, padlock for the blocked merge.
        focus: A 2px blue outline offset 3px.
        tone: Gentle and helpful, such as Merge readiness and Waiting on 1 check.

    style289:
        number: 289
        run: 59
        screen: CodeRepository
        name: Green phosphor
        idea: The whole review is one glowing green-on-black terminal transcript, each part of the screen printed as the output of a command, with inverse-video highlights, ruled output boxes and a blinking block cursor waiting at the end.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/289.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            black: #030803, the page and the style sheet background
            well: #0a1a0d, output boxes, the comment box and fields
            phosphor: #6dff8a, main text, prompts, glow, the inverse bar and focus
            dim: #4cd468, secondary text, line numbers, removed lines and box titles
            trace: #2a7a3c, box rules and the dashed separators, never text
            inverseInk: #031a08, text on the phosphor inverse bar and the primary button
        type:
            One monospace stack, IBM Plex Mono, DejaVu Sans Mono, Liberation Mono,
            ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas, at 15px on 1.6 for everything. The title is
            20px at 700 in caps. Prompts are 15px at 700. Box titles 13px in dim. Every
            glyph glows with a 4px phosphor text shadow.
        layout:
            A single left aligned transcript column, max 1000px, on flat black with a
            faint radial vignette. A full width inverse status line reads Brightwork
            Code, the repository and Private. Then a series of prompts, each followed by
            its output. bw repo view prints Watch 12, Star 48 and Fork 3 and a numbered
            tab menu where Pull requests sits in inverse video. bw pr view 214 prints a
            ruled box with the title, the Open state, the merge sentence and a two
            column key and value list for reviewers, labels, assignees, milestone and
            linked issue. bw pr checks prints all twelve checks as aligned rows with a
            mark and a word and a twelve cell text meter. bw pr diff prints the three
            file totals and the hunk with plus and minus signs and Tomás Ruiz's comment
            boxed inline. bw pr merge prints the block reason and a bracketed disabled
            Merge button. A block cursor blinks on the last prompt. At 375px the same
            column narrows and wide output scrolls inside its own box.
        spacing: A line based rhythm of 24px. One blank line between commands, 16px box padding.
        density: Medium. Text only, aligned in columns, no cards.
        corners: Square everywhere.
        borders:
            1px trace rules around output boxes, dashed trace separators between
            commands, inverse video for the status line and the current tab.
        shadows: No box shadows. Text has a 4px phosphor glow at 55 percent.
        icons:
            Line icons at 2px stroke drawn in phosphor at 1em with square caps, plus the
            word. Check circle for passed and approved, crossed square for failing,
            triangle with a bang for requested changes, padlock for the blocked merge,
            the pull request glyph for Open.
        focus: Inverse video, a phosphor fill with inverseInk text, plus a 2px phosphor outline offset 2px.
        tone: Machine terse in prompts and output, such as 11/12 passed and merge blocked, 1 check failing.
    style290:
        number: 290
        run: 59
        screen: CodeRepository
        name: Amber terminal
        idea: A full-screen amber text-mode application of double-ruled panes with titles set into their borders, an inverse selection bar, a top status line and a bottom function key bar, glowing warmly on black.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/290.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            black: #0c0700, the page, pane interiors and the style sheet
            amber: #ffb000, main text, double rules, the inverse bar and focus
            dim: #d39300, labels, line numbers, removed lines and the key bar captions
            rule: #8a5c00, single inner dividers, never text
            inverseInk: #0c0700, text on the amber inverse bar, pane titles and buttons
        type:
            One monospace stack, Fixedsys, Terminus, DejaVu Sans Mono, Lucida Console,
            ui-monospace, Consolas, at 14px on 1.5. Pane titles 14px at 700 caps tracked
            0.08em in inverse. The title 18px at 700. Function key bar 13px. Amber
            glyphs carry a 5px warm glow.
        layout:
            A full width text-mode screen. A one line inverse status bar shows
            Brightwork Code, the repository, Private and Watch 12, Star 48 and Fork 3.
            Below, a grid of panes with 3px double amber borders, each with its title
            set into the top border as an inverse tag. Row one has three panes, a 240px
            Repository pane listing the six tabs with Pull requests on the inverse
            selection bar and a pointer, a wide Pull request 214 pane with the title,
            Open, the merge sentence and a key and value table for reviewers, labels,
            assignees, milestone and linked issue, and a 300px Checks pane listing all
            twelve checks with a mark and a word and the failing row inverted. Row two
            has a Files pane with three rows of counts and a wide Diff pane with the
            hunk and the boxed comment. A function key bar runs along the bottom with
            keys as inverse numbers and captions, including F8 Merge shown locked and
            disabled. Below 1000px the panes stack in one column and the key bar wraps.
        spacing:
            A character grid. 8px horizontal and 4px vertical cell padding, 12px inside
            panes, 8px between panes.
        density: Dense. A full screen of text, every pane visible at once on a laptop.
        corners: Square everywhere.
        borders:
            3px double amber borders around panes, 1px rule dividers inside them, titles
            cut into the top border.
        shadows: No box shadows. Text has a 5px amber glow at 45 percent.
        icons:
            Line icons at 2px stroke in amber at 1em with square caps, always with the
            word. Check circle for passed and approved, crossed square for failing,
            triangle with a bang for requested changes, padlock for the blocked merge.
        focus: The inverse selection bar, amber fill with black text, plus a 2px amber outline offset 2px.
        tone:
            Utility program voice, short caps titles and terse captions, such as CHECKS
            11/12 and F8 Merge locked.
    style291:
        number: 291
        run: 59
        screen: CodeRepository
        name: CRT scanlines
        idea: The review is broadcast like a teletext page on a curved colour CRT, set in a rounded plastic bezel with scanlines, a soft vignette and a hint of red and cyan fringing, its sections marked by solid colour bands and block mosaic graphics.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/291.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            bezel: #2b2925, the plastic frame around the screen
            bezelEdge: #4a463f, the bezel highlight and the power lamp ring
            tube: #020713, the screen and the style sheet background
            panel: #0a1630, boxed areas inside the screen, the diff and the style sheet cards
            white: #f2f6ff, main text
            cyan: #4ff2ff, the page header, links, the cyan band and focus
            yellow: #ffe94d, the title, requested changes and the yellow band
            magenta: #ff7cf5, labels, line numbers and the magenta band
            green: #5cff8f, passed, approved, Open and added lines
            red: #ff6a6a, failing and removed lines
            blueBand: #1e3cff, the blue band behind white text
            bandInk: #020713, text on the cyan, yellow, green and magenta bands
            scanline: #000000, the 1px dark line every 3px across the screen, drawn at 20 percent opacity
        type:
            A chunky monospace stack, Bedstead, MODE7, Courier New, DejaVu Sans Mono,
            ui-monospace, set bold everywhere so the strokes stay crisp through the
            scanlines. Base 16px on 1.5. The title is double height at 30px. Band labels
            16px caps tracked 0.12em. The page header 14px. Headings carry a 1px red and
            cyan fringe.
        layout:
            The page sits inside a CRT. A dark plastic bezel with 28px padding and a
            power lamp frames a tube with 36px by 56px rounded corners, an inset
            vignette and a scanline overlay. Inside, a teletext layout. A cyan header
            line reads P214, Brightwork Code and the date and time. A block mosaic B
            logo sits beside the owner and repository, Private, and Watch 12, Star 48
            and Fork 3. The six tabs follow as page numbers 100 to 600 with Pull
            requests on a yellow band. Then the double height yellow title with number
            214, the Open marker and the merge sentence. Below, two columns. The left
            has a green CHECKS band with a twelve block mosaic meter and the failing
            check named, then a magenta FILES band with the three files, then a blue
            DIFF band and the boxed hunk with the comment. The right has a yellow
            REVIEWS band, a cyan DETAILS band with assignees, labels, milestone and
            linked issue, and the disabled merge button with its reason. Below 900px the
            columns stack and the bezel thins to 10px.
        spacing: A character grid. 8px band padding, 16px between bands, 32px inside the tube.
        density: Medium. Big chunky text in short rows, like a broadcast page.
        corners: The bezel is 40px round and the tube 36px by 56px. Everything inside is square.
        borders:
            No rules inside the screen. Solid colour bands mark sections. The diff and
            comment sit in panel boxes with a 2px cyan edge.
        shadows:
            A large inset vignette on the tube, a soft outer shadow under the bezel, and
            a faint cyan glow around the tube. Headings carry 1px red and cyan offset
            text shadows.
        icons:
            Line icons at 2.5px stroke at 1em, bold enough to read through scanlines,
            always with the word. Check circle for passed and approved, crossed square
            for failing, triangle with a bang for requested changes, padlock for the
            blocked merge.
        focus: A 3px cyan outline offset 2px with a 6px dark gap.
        tone:
            Broadcast caption voice in caps for bands, plain sentences for content, such
            as CHECKS and 11 of 12 checks passed.
    style292:
        number: 292
        run: 59
        screen: CodeRepository
        name: Pixel CRT game
        idea: The pull request is laid out like an 8-bit adventure screen, with a coin-counter HUD, a menu cursor on the tabs, notched pixel-bordered dialog boxes, a checks health bar of twelve blocks, a reviewer party with pixel portraits and the changed files as inventory slots.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/292.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            night: #100c24, the page and the style sheet background
            panel: #1e1840, dialog boxes and the style sheet cards
            slot: #2c2560, inventory slots, the hunk header, chips and the disabled merge button
            frame: #f2f0ff, pixel borders, main text and focus
            muted: #b9b2e6, secondary text and line numbers
            gold: #ffd23f, counters, the menu cursor, the primary button and requested changes
            hp: #4fe07a, health blocks, passed, approved, Open and added lines
            hurt: #ff6464, the broken health block, failing and removed lines
            sky: #6cb8ff, links and the linked issue
            pink: #ff8ad8, box titles
            ink: #100c24, text on gold, green and sky fills
        type:
            One monospace stack with a pixel font first, Press Start 2P, Lucida Console,
            DejaVu Sans Mono, ui-monospace. Dialog text 15px on 1.6 in normal case so it
            stays readable. The title 24px at 700. Box titles 16px caps tracked 0.1em in
            pink. HUD counters 14px at 700 caps. No smoothing tricks, only crisp shapes.
        layout:
            A 1160px game screen on a night background. A HUD bar runs across the top
            with a pixel B emblem, the owner and repository, a Private lock tag and
            three coin style counters for Watch 12, Star 48 and Fork 3. Under it the six
            tabs sit in a menu box with a gold arrow cursor beside Pull requests. The
            main area is a two column grid of notched pixel boxes. The wide Quest box
            holds the number 214, the title, the Open tag and the merge sentence spoken
            by a pixel portrait of Sam Ortiz. The narrow Party box lists Jonas Weber and
            Tomás Ruiz with pixel portraits and their verdicts. A full width HP box
            shows the twelve checks as health blocks, the failing block cracked with an
            x, and names e2e-android. The Inventory box shows the three files as square
            slots with counts, the Scroll box holds the diff with the comment as a
            speech bubble, and a Stats box lists assignees, labels, milestone and linked
            issue above a locked Merge button. Below 900px every box takes the full
            width.
        spacing: A 4px pixel unit. 20px box padding, 16px between boxes, 8px inside slots.
        density: Medium. Chunky boxes with a few items each.
        corners: Notched pixel corners made by stepping the border, never rounded.
        borders:
            4px frame borders drawn as stepped box shadows so the corners are notched,
            with a 4px dark inner line. Slots have 4px slot borders.
        shadows: A hard 4px drop step in black under boxes and buttons, no blur.
        icons:
            Pixel icons drawn on an 8 by 8 grid with crisp edges at 16px, always with a
            word. A pixel check for passed and approved, a pixel x for failing, a pixel
            triangle with a bang for requested changes, a pixel padlock for the blocked
            merge, a pixel eye, star and fork for the counters.
        focus: A 4px gold outline offset 4px with stepped corners.
        tone:
            Playful game labels for boxes, such as Quest, Party, HP and Inventory, with
            plain words for the content.
    style293:
        number: 293
        run: 59
        screen: CodeRepository
        name: Hacker IDE
        idea: The pull request opens inside a modern dark code editor, with an activity bar, an explorer of repository views and changed files, editor tabs, a diff with change gutters and a minimap, a details panel, a checks terminal and a status bar.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/293.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            editor: #0b0e13, the editor area, the diff and the terminal
            chrome: #151a21, the title bar, activity bar, explorer, details panel and style sheet cards
            tabRest: #1b212a, inactive editor tabs, chips, hover and the disabled merge button
            line: #262e3a, pane dividers and rows
            text: #d6dde8, text
            muted: #8f9bad, meta, line numbers, section headers and inactive tabs
            accent: #4fc1ff, the active tab top bar, the current view, links, the primary button and focus
            statusBar: #1f6feb, the status bar background behind white text
            green: #7ee787, passed, approved, Open, added lines and the add gutter
            red: #ff7b72, failing, removed lines and the remove gutter
            yellow: #e3b341, requested changes and strings
            purple: #d2a8ff, keywords and labels
            addTint: #12261b, added line rows
            delTint: #2d1517, removed line rows
        type:
            Interface text in system-ui, Segoe UI, Ubuntu, Roboto at 13px. The overview
            title 20px at 600. Explorer and panel headers 11px caps tracked 0.08em in
            muted. Code and terminal in JetBrains Mono, Fira Code, Cascadia Code,
            ui-monospace at 13px on 1.6. The status bar is 12px.
        layout:
            A full width editor window. A 36px title bar shows the branch, repository
            and app name with Watch 12, Star 48 and Fork 3 at the right. Under it a grid
            of a 48px activity bar of icon buttons, a 260px explorer, the editor and a
            300px details panel. The explorer has a Repository section with the owner
            and name, Private, and the six tabs as views with counts, Pull requests
            current with an accent bar, and a Changed files tree with folders and the
            three files and their counts. The editor has a tab strip with Pull request
            214 and NotificationPrefs.tsx, the active tab marked by a 2px accent top
            bar. Under the tabs a breadcrumb, an overview block with the title, Open,
            the merge sentence, reviewers and labels, then the diff with old and new
            gutters, a coloured change bar, syntax colours, Tomás Ruiz's comment as an
            inline widget and a 64px minimap at the right. The details panel lists
            assignees, labels, milestone, linked issue and the disabled merge button. A
            bottom panel with Checks and Problems tabs prints the twelve checks as
            terminal lines. A 24px blue status bar shows the branch, the check score and
            the review state. Below 1100px the details panel moves under the editor,
            below 760px everything stacks and the activity bar turns into a row.
        spacing: A 4px unit. 22px tree rows, 35px tabs, 12px panel padding.
        density: Dense. A full workspace with many panes, small type.
        corners: Square panes and tabs, 4px buttons, fields and chips.
        borders:
            1px line dividers between every pane. A 2px accent top bar on the active tab
            and a 2px accent left bar on the current view. 3px gutter bars for added and
            removed lines.
        shadows: One shadow, under the inline comment widget, 0 4px 12px black at 50 percent.
        icons:
            Thin line icons at 1.5px stroke, 24px in the activity bar and 16px
            elsewhere. Check circle for passed and approved, crossed square for failing,
            triangle with a bang for requested changes, padlock for the blocked merge,
            always with the word.
        focus:
            A 1px accent outline offset negative 1px inside lists and tabs, and a 2px
            accent outline offset 2px on buttons and fields.
        tone:
            Tool voice, short and exact, such as CHANGED FILES, 11/12 checks and Merge
            blocked by 1 failing check.

    style294:
        number: 294
        run: 60
        screen: CodeRepository
        name: Dark blueprint
        idea: The pull request drawn as a technical sheet, white and cyan line work on deep blueprint blue, with a parts list for files, a wiring schematic for checks and a title block for the merge facts.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/294.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            blueprint: #0a2a52, the page and style sheet ground under a two level grid
            panel: #0c3263, boxes, tabs, counters and the title block
            tint: #123c72, the current tab
            ink: #f2f7ff, text
            muted: #a9c4e8, captions, labels and line numbers
            line: #7fa6d6, secondary rules and dashed leaders
            whiteLine: #e9f2ff, the sheet frame, box outlines and main rules
            cyan: #74e4ff, the accent, primary button, passed checks, added line markers, links and focus
            redline: #ff9c8f, failing check, changes requested, removed line markers and review notes
            addedRow: #0f4470, added diff line ground
            removedRow: #3a3456, removed diff line ground
        type:
            A narrow technical sans, Bahnschrift, DIN Alternate, Roboto
            Condensed, Arial Narrow, system-ui, for text and headings, and a
            system monospace for every label and the diff. Base 15px at 1.5.
            The pull request title is 30px at 600, the repository name 26px at
            600, labels 11px monospace caps tracked 0.14em, the diff 13px
            monospace at 1.7.
        layout:
            The whole screen sits inside a drawing sheet with a 2px white frame,
            an inner 1px rule 8px inside it and faint zone letters A, B and C
            along the top. The header row holds a square B mark with a dashed
            inner square and the app name, the repository name with the
            owner in white and the name in cyan, a boxed Private tag and three
            joined boxed counters for Watch, Star and Fork. Below it the tabs
            are joined outlined boxes, the current one lighter with a cyan
            underline. The body is a main column and a 320px title block.
            Detail A holds the title, the Open tag, the merge sentence and a
            dimension line reading 6 commits, 3 files and the totals. Inside it
            Detail B draws the twelve checks as nodes wired in series with the
            seventh drawn as a dashed octagon that breaks the wire, then a three
            column numbered list. Detail C lists the two reviewers with round
            initial balloons. A parts list table numbers the three files with
            added and removed counts and a totals row. Section D shows the diff
            with the comment as Note 1, a dashed redline box joined to the line
            by a leader with a small circle. The title block is a ruled table of
            cells for assignee, labels, milestone, linked issue and a hatched
            disabled merge button. Every box carries a caption tab cut into its
            top edge. Below 1000px everything stacks.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px frame padding and gaps, 20px box padding, 16px header gaps.
        density: Medium. Several labelled details are visible at once on the sheet.
        corners: Square everywhere. Only balloons and passed nodes are round.
        borders: 1px white box outlines, a 2px white frame with an inner 1px rule, dashed leaders, and dashed redline borders on anything that blocks the merge.
        shadows: None. Depth comes from line weight and the grid behind.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.5px with square caps and mitred joins. A tick for
            passed, a dashed octagon with a cross for failing, a ringed tick for
            approved, a triangle with a bang for changes requested, a lock on
            the disabled merge, always with the word.
        focus: A 2px cyan outline offset 3px with a faint cyan halo.
        tone: Drafting labels in caps, such as Detail A, Parts list, Section D, Title block and Note 1.
    style295:
        number: 295
        run: 60
        screen: CodeRepository
        name: Ink and red
        idea: A pull request set like the front page of a serious evening paper, warm white serif type on black ink, hairline column rules and one sharp red kept for what blocks the merge.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/295.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            inkBlack: #0e0d0c, the page and style sheet ground
            pressBlack: #171614, the diff excerpt box and fields
            warmWhite: #ede7db, text, thick section rules and the secondary button
            greyInk: #aaa397, meta, captions and labels
            hairline: #3b3833, column rules and row lines
            sharpRed: #ff5245, the one accent for failing, changes requested, the primary button, the current tab bar and the focus ring
            redWash: #2a1311, the failing alert and removed diff lines
            redText: #ff8a80, red words set on the red wash and the needs QA label
        type:
            Three families. A high contrast display serif, Didot, Bodoni 72,
            Iowan Old Style, Georgia, for the masthead, headline and big
            figure. A book serif, Iowan Old Style, Palatino, Georgia, for body
            text at 17px and 1.55 and the italic dek at 24px. A gothic sans,
            Franklin Gothic Medium, Arial Narrow, Arial, for kickers and labels
            at 12 to 13px bold caps tracked 0.16em. The headline is 64px at 700,
            the checks figure 76px, the diff 13px monospace.
        layout:
            A centred newspaper page up to 1240px. An ear line names the suite,
            the edition and the desk. The masthead reads Brightwork Code in
            64px display serif with Code in italic, the repository in italic
            below it, and a dateline row with Private, Watch 12, Star 48 and
            Fork 3, closed by a double rule. The tabs are a centred row of
            gothic caps separated by middots, the current one with a 3px red
            underline. The lead story has a red kicker with the number and Open,
            the title as a huge headline, the merge sentence as an italic dek
            and a ruled byline with author, commits, files and totals. Under it
            two columns split by a hairline. The narrow one holds The checks
            with a giant 11 and of 12 passed, a red washed alert for the failing
            e2e-android check, The review with the two names and verdicts, and
            In this change as a contents list with dotted leaders to the
            counts. The wide one holds The excerpt, the boxed diff, where the
            comment becomes a pull quote with a red rule above and the quote in
            26px italic display serif. A right rail under a thick white rule
            lists assignee, labels, milestone and linked issue, then To press
            with the dashed disabled merge button. Below 1060px the rail moves
            under the story, below 760px the columns stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px column gutters, 12px row padding, 28px between masthead and lead.
        density: Medium. Big headlines and long lines, but every fact is on the page.
        corners: None. Every edge is square.
        borders: Hairline column rules, a 3px or 4px warm white rule over every section, a double rule under the masthead.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            Few, 2px line icons with butt caps. A tick for passed, an octagon
            cross for failing, a ringed tick for approved, a triangle for
            changes requested, each with its word in gothic caps.
        focus: A 2px warm white outline offset 3px with a 5px red ring outside it.
        tone: Headline voice, such as The checks, The review, The excerpt, In this change and To press.
    style296:
        number: 296
        run: 60
        screen: CodeRepository
        name: Dark luxury
        idea: A hushed, symmetrical page of near black and fine gold hairlines, light display serif and widely spaced capitals, where the pull request reads like an invitation card and every figure has room.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/296.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            noir: #0b0a08, the page and style sheet ground
            velvet: #12100d, the card gradient top and the diff panel
            ivory: #efe9dd, text
            taupe: #a39b8d, spaced capital labels and meta
            bronzeLine: #3d3528, quiet dividers and the outer card rule
            gold: #cdae6a, hairline rules, frames, ornaments and the primary button
            champagne: #e6cd92, gold text, figures, approved, links and focus
            ruby: #ec8b80, failing, changes requested and removed counts
            rubyShade: #22110f, removed diff lines
        type:
            A light display serif, Bodoni 72, Didot, Bodoni MT, Georgia, at
            weight 300 for the title at 52px, the repository at 34px, figures
            at 46px and names at 21px. A humanist sans, Optima, Candara, Gill
            Sans, Segoe UI, for body at 16px and 1.65 and for labels at 11px
            caps tracked 0.32em. The diff is 13px monospace at 1.85.
        layout:
            Everything is centred and symmetrical, up to 1160px. The header
            stacks a gold diamond monogram, BRIGHTWORK · CODE in gold spaced
            capitals, the repository in light serif with the name in italic
            champagne, and a row of spaced capital meta for Private, Watch,
            Star and Fork. A gold ornament rule with a small diamond leads to
            the tabs, a centred row of spaced capitals with counts as gold
            superscripts and a thin champagne underline on the current tab.
            The pull request is a centred card with a gold hairline and a
            second bronze rule 6px outside it. It holds Open and Pull request
            nº 214 in spaced capitals, the title, the merge sentence, then three
            equal columns split by hairlines for Checks with a big 11 of 12,
            Reviewers and Labels as outlined gold tags. Below the card two
            columns. The wide one holds Files changed with right aligned serif
            counts and the diff in a quiet panel, where the comment is a gold
            framed remark in italic serif. The narrow column centres assignee,
            labels, milestone and linked issue, an ornament rule and the
            disabled merge button. Below 960px it all stacks.
        spacing: An 8px unit used generously. 48px card padding, 64px between bands, 28px between side facts.
        density: Low. Few items per band with wide margins.
        corners: Square, with rotated diamond monogram and ornaments.
        borders: 1px gold hairlines, a bronze rule 6px outside the card, gold underlines on section headings.
        shadows: None. A faint velvet to noir gradient inside the card.
        icons:
            Thin 1.2px line icons, used sparingly. A ringed tick for approved,
            an octagon cross for failing, a triangle for changes requested, a
            lock on the merge, each with spaced capital words.
        focus: A 1px champagne outline offset 4px inside a soft gold halo.
        tone: Formal and spare, such as Pull request nº 214 and Merging opens once every check has passed.
    style297:
        number: 297
        run: 60
        screen: CodeRepository
        name: Stealth
        idea: A low glare field console in matte black olive, where chamfered panels, stencil labels and a twelve cell status board turn the pull request into a dense, readable set of orders.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/297.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            blackOlive: #121410, the page and style sheet ground
            railBlack: #0e100b, the navigation rail and fields
            olivePanel: #1b1e16, panels and the data plate
            oliveRaised: #22261c, board cells, the current tab and counters
            khakiInk: #d3cfb6, text
            drab: #9c9883, labels, meta and line numbers
            seam: #3a4030, panel edges and dividers
            sand: #c4b47a, stencil titles, the primary button, the current tab edge and focus
            fieldGreen: #a3c46e, passed checks, approved and added lines
            signalAmber: #f0a65a, failing, changes requested and removed lines
            amberShade: #2b2216, the failing cell and removed line ground
        type:
            A stencil face, Stencil Std, Stencil, Impact, Arial Narrow, in caps
            for the repository at 24px tracked 0.06em, panel titles at 13px
            tracked 0.16em and buttons. A narrow sans, Arial Narrow, Roboto
            Condensed, for text at 15px and 1.45 and the title at 28px bold. A
            monospace for data and labels at 11px bold caps tracked 0.12em,
            the diff at 13px.
        layout:
            A 184px dark rail on the left with a sand chamfered B badge, the
            unit name, the six tabs stacked as monospace caps with counts on
            the right, the current tab outlined in sand with a 4px sand left
            edge, and a foot note. The main area starts with a data plate with
            two rivets, the repository, a Private tag and three counters. Below
            sits a 12 column grid of chamfered panels with 14px cut corners,
            each with a stencil title row and a hairline. Objective spans 8 and
            holds the title, number and merge sentence with an Open tag.
            Clearance spans 4 with both reviewers. The status board spans 7
            with a big 11/12, then the twelve checks as a four by three grid of
            cells with a green edge, the failing one amber with a dashed outline
            and the word fail. Manifest spans 5 as a file table. Log spans 8
            with the diff and the comment as an amber Memo box. Orders spans 4
            with assignee, labels, milestone, linked issue and a striped
            disabled Merge locked button. Below 1100px panels go full width,
            below 760px the rail becomes a wrapping top bar.
        spacing: An 8px unit, tight. 10px panel gaps, 14px panel padding, 4px between board cells.
        density: High. Six panels and the full rail on one screen.
        corners: Chamfered 14px on panels and 6px on the badge. Buttons and fields are square.
        borders: 1px seam around every panel, a 4px sand edge on the current tab and fields, 3px coloured left edges on board cells.
        shadows: None. Matte surfaces, low glare.
        icons:
            Heavy 2.2px line icons with square caps. A tick for passed, an
            octagon cross for failing, a ringed tick for approved, a triangle
            for changes, always with a caps word.
        focus: A 2px dashed sand outline offset 2px.
        tone: Terse field labels, such as Objective, Clearance, Status board, Manifest, Log, Orders and Merge locked.
    style298:
        number: 298
        run: 60
        screen: CodeRepository
        name: Carbon fibre
        idea: A pit wall timing screen on woven carbon, with heavy italic condensed type, skewed tabs, a timing tower of checks, sector bars for files and motorsport red for the one thing holding the merge.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/298.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            carbon: #111213, the ground under a 20px woven texture
            weaveLight: #232326, highlight threads in the weave
            panel: #1a1b1e, panels
            panelHead: #232429, panel headers and pit wall cards
            white: #f4f4f5, text, the secondary button and the focus outline
            grey: #a7a9b0, labels, meta and the outline number
            seam: #34363c, panel tops and dividers
            raceRed: #c8160c, the primary button, current tab, failing position and logo
            redLine: #ff4a3d, the header stripe, red panel tops and the focus ring
            pinkRed: #ff8278, failing and removed text on dark red
            greenFlag: #4fdc84, passed checks, the open state, approved and added lines
            amber: #ffc23d, changes requested, the team radio comment and needs QA
        type:
            A condensed sans, Helvetica Neue, Roboto Condensed, Arial Narrow, set
            italic at 800 to 900 in caps for the title at 40px, the repository
            at 26px, panel titles at 14px and buttons. The pull request number
            is a 88px italic outline figure. Body is system-ui at 14px and 1.45.
            Data and the diff use Consolas or a system monospace at 12.5 to
            13px with tabular figures.
        layout:
            The header is woven carbon with a red and white diagonal stripe at
            the right and a 3px red rule below. It holds a skewed red B logo,
            the repository in heavy italic, a Private pill and skewed counters,
            then a row of skewed tabs with the current one red. The body, also
            on carbon, has three columns. The left 240px timing tower lists
            all twelve checks with position numbers in black tabs and PASS or
            FAIL, the seventh row tinted red with a red edge and red position.
            The centre holds the lead panel with the Open flag, the title and
            the outline 214 floated right, a black gauge showing 11/12 and
            twelve skewed segments with the failing one hatched red, and two
            pit wall cards for the reviewers with green and amber left edges.
            Below are Sectors, the three files as S1 to S3 with added and
            removed bars, and Telemetry with the diff, where the comment is a
            Team radio box with an amber edge. The right 280px Race control
            panel lists assignee, skewed labels, milestone and linked issue and
            a striped disabled merge button. Below 1100px race control moves
            under, below 760px all stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px gaps between panels, 14px panel padding, tight 6px timing rows.
        density: High. Three columns with the full timing tower visible.
        corners: None. Tabs, buttons, counters, labels and segments are skewed 12 to 14 degrees instead.
        borders: A 3px seam on panel tops, red on hot panels, 4px coloured edges on pit cards and the failing row.
        shadows: None. Depth comes from the carbon weave between panels.
        icons:
            Bold 2.4px line icons. A tick with PASS, an octagon cross with FAIL,
            a ringed tick for approved, a triangle for changes requested.
        focus: A 3px white outline with a 6px red ring outside it.
        tone: Race words, such as Timing, Sectors, Telemetry, Pit wall, Team radio and Race control.

    style299:
        number: 299
        run: 61
        screen: CodeRepository
        name: Cyberpunk neon
        idea: A night city terminal in magenta and cyan neon on black, with cut corner panels, scanlines, a glitched headline and a hex grid of checks, loud in colour but strict about shape and contrast.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/299.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            void: #07060b, the page and style sheet ground
            panel: #0f0c18, the terminal, shards and file rows
            panelRaised: #171226, raised fills
            ink: #f3eefe, text
            haze: #b3a9cc, labels, meta and line numbers
            grid: #3b2d5c, panel edges and tabs
            magenta: #ff3ddc, the primary button, headings, failing, removed lines and the header glow
            cyan: #2ef2ff, the current tab, passed, approved, added lines, links and focus
            volt: #ffe94d, changes requested, Private and the incoming comment
            magentaShade: #2a0c27, removed line ground
            cyanShade: #06232a, added line ground and passed hexes
        type:
            A wide sans, Eurostile, Microgramma, Bank Gothic, Segoe UI, at 800
            in caps for the title at 46px with a split magenta and cyan shadow
            offset 2px each way, and for section titles at 13px tracked 0.24em.
            Everything else is monospace, ui-monospace, Cascadia Mono, Menlo,
            at 14px and 1.5, labels 12px caps tracked 0.12em, the diff 13px.
        layout:
            A black ticker bar with a magenta rule and glow holds the app name
            as BRIGHTWORK//CODE, uplink stable and three outlined counters. A
            hero band follows with the repository in cyan caps, a volt Private
            tag, outlined tabs with the current one filled cyan and glowing,
            then the glitched title with the number in magenta, a broken neon
            underline in magenta and cyan, and the Open tag with the merge
            sentence. Faint scanlines cover the page. The body has a wide
            column and a 340px stack. The wide column holds the diff as a
            terminal with a prompt line, neon edges on added and removed lines
            and the comment as an incoming message box with a volt border and
            glow, then the three files as rows with a left edge. The stack
            holds three data shards, alternating cut corners. Checks shows
            11/12 and the twelve checks as hexagons, cyan with ticks, the
            failing one solid magenta with an octagon cross, then the failing
            line. Reviewers lists both verdicts. Metadata lists assignee,
            outlined labels, milestone and linked issue and a striped disabled
            merge button. Below 1000px the stack drops under the terminal.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px page gutters, 20px column gap, 16px shard padding.
        density: Medium. A large headline band, then a wide terminal beside a stack of shards.
        corners: Cut corners, 18px clipped on alternate shards, a 9px notch on the primary button, hexagon check cells.
        borders: 1px violet grid lines, 2px neon edges on diff lines and file rows, a magenta rule under the ticker.
        shadows: Neon glows only, magenta under the ticker and primary button, cyan on the current tab and focus, volt on the comment.
        icons:
            2px line icons. A tick for passed and an octagon cross for failing
            inside hexes, a ringed tick for approved, a triangle for changes,
            each with a caps word.
        focus: A 2px cyan outline offset 3px with a cyan glow.
        tone: Terminal slang kept readable, such as uplink stable, incoming and Merge locked.
    style300:
        number: 300
        run: 61
        screen: CodeRepository
        name: Starship bridge
        idea: The pull request as a ship's bridge, with an arched header, a curved main viewscreen for the diff, two bevelled side consoles in orange and blue, and a check gauge that shows which system is down.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/300.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            deepSpace: #060a16, the page and style sheet ground under a navy glow at the top
            console: #0e1630, console bodies, chips and rows
            consoleLight: #152044, console gradient tops and the comment
            bezel: #26355e, bezels, rims and dividers
            viewscreen: #040713, the diff screen, stations and fields
            ink: #e9eefb, text
            steel: #a3b2d3, labels and meta
            bridgeOrange: #ff9f45, headings, the current tab, the primary button, changes requested and the arch rule
            signalBlue: #62b3ff, data, passed, approved, added lines, the open state and focus
            alert: #ff7d88, the failing system and removed lines
            alertShade: #2c1324, the failing row and removed line ground
        type:
            A rounded geometric sans, Avenir Next, Segoe UI, Ubuntu, Trebuchet
            MS, for text at 15px and 1.5. Its condensed cut, Avenir Next
            Condensed, Segoe UI Semibold, Ubuntu Condensed, at 600 for the
            title and repository at 30 to 32px and console titles at 13px caps
            tracked 0.18em in orange. Labels are 11px caps tracked 0.18em, the
            diff 13px monospace.
        layout:
            The header is an arch, a dark navy band whose bottom edge curves
            down in a wide ellipse with a 2px orange rule. It holds a round B
            badge and the app name, pill counters on the right, the repository
            centred with an orange Private pill, and a centred row of pill tabs
            with the current one filled orange. The body has three columns,
            280px, flexible and 280px. The left console sweeps its top right
            corner in an 80px curve and holds Systems, a half ring gauge of
            twelve segments, blue for passed and a dashed red segment with a
            cross for e2e-android, the caption 11 of 12, the failing line and
            all checks in two columns. The centre viewscreen has an elliptical
            top edge, an inner rim and a faint blue glow, with the Open pill,
            the title and number and the merge sentence centred above the file
            bar and the diff. The comment is an orange rimmed Hail bubble. The
            right console mirrors the curve and holds Crew, two rounded reviewer
            cards with ringed initials, then assignee, labels, milestone,
            linked issue and a dashed disabled merge button. A Helm strip runs
            across the bottom with a curved lower edge and three file stations.
            Below 1100px the viewscreen leads, below 700px all stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 20px between consoles, 20px console padding, 28px under the arch.
        density: Medium. A centred viewscreen flanked by two consoles and a helm strip below.
        corners: Curved. Elliptical arch, viewscreen and helm edges, consoles with one sweeping 80px corner, pill tabs and buttons, 14px stations.
        borders: 2px navy bezel rims, a 2px orange rule under the arch and around the comment.
        shadows: Deep drop shadows under consoles, inset rims and a faint blue glow inside the viewscreen.
        icons:
            1.9px rounded line icons. A tick for passed, an octagon cross for
            failing, a ringed tick for approved, a triangle for changes, and
            gauge segments with a cross for the failing check.
        focus: A 3px signal blue outline offset 3px.
        tone: Calm bridge words, such as Systems, Crew, Helm, Station, Hail and Standing by until all checks pass.
    style301:
        number: 301
        run: 61
        screen: CodeRepository
        name: Space station HUD
        idea: A heads up display floating over near black, with hairline cyan rules, corner brackets instead of boxes, thin type with tiny telemetry labels, and a ring of twelve check ticks around the pull request number.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/301.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            void: #03070b, the page and style sheet ground under a faint radial glow
            glass: #07121a, bracketed panels at 85 percent
            ink: #eaf7fb, text
            haze: #8fb4c2, telemetry labels and meta
            trace: #1f4250, hairline rules and dashed dividers
            hudCyan: #5be7ff, brackets, ring ticks, passed, approved, added lines, the primary button and focus
            amber: #ffcf5a, changes requested, the comment and Private
            fault: #ff7070, the failing check and removed lines
        type:
            A light grotesque, Helvetica Neue, Segoe UI, system-ui, at 200 for
            the title at 38px, the repository at 26px and readouts at 22 to
            26px, and at 300 for text at 15px and 1.5. Telemetry labels are
            SF Mono or a system monospace at 10.5px caps tracked 0.2em, the
            diff 12.5px monospace at 1.75.
        layout:
            A top line of three parts over a hairline, a ringed B mark with a
            dashed outer ring and the app name in spaced monospace, the
            repository centred in thin type with an amber Private tag, and
            Watch, Star and Fork as stacked label and number readouts split by
            hairlines. The tabs are centred spaced monospace caps, the current
            one cyan inside square brackets. Panels have no boxes, only four
            16px cyan corner brackets over dark glass. The body has three
            columns, 260px, flexible and 260px. The left holds Telemetry with
            11 / 12, the failing line and a numbered list of all twelve checks
            with ticks or a ringed cross at the right. The centre target panel
            has a ring gauge with twelve tick bars around 214 and a ringed red
            cross at seven o'clock, beside the Open label, the title, the
            merge sentence and a commit trace of six diamonds on a line. Below
            it the Feed panel shows the diff with 1px edge lines, and the
            comment is a bracketed amber Transmission. The right column holds
            Crew for reviewers, Payload with each file and a thin added and
            removed meter, and Docking with details and a dashed disabled
            merge. Below 1100px the centre leads, below 700px all stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between columns, 20px between panels, 18px inside brackets.
        density: Medium. Three columns of readouts around a centred target panel.
        corners: No boxes. Each panel is marked by four 16px corner brackets, with rings and diamonds as markers.
        borders: 1px hairlines only, cyan brackets, dashed trace dividers and square brackets around the current tab.
        shadows: None. A faint radial glow behind the top centre.
        icons:
            Thin 1.3px line icons. A tick for passed, an octagon cross for
            failing, a ringed tick for approved, a triangle for changes. The
            ring uses bars for passed and a ringed cross for failing.
        focus: A 1px cyan outline offset 4px with an outer 1px cyan ring and a faint halo.
        tone: Station telemetry, such as Telemetry, Payload, Feed, Transmission, T+6 commits and Docking clamps hold.
    style302:
        number: 302
        run: 61
        screen: CodeRepository
        name: Night vision
        idea: The pull request seen through a night vision viewfinder, one phosphor green on black with grain, a vignette, corner readouts and a reticle on the title, so every status speaks through its shape and word.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/302.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            black: #000000, the page surround
            scopeBlack: #020902, the viewfinder and style sheet ground
            zone: #061406, zones, fields and the comment
            phosphor: #a6ff9e, text, the primary button and the focus halo
            bloom: #d6ffd0, headings, the failing and changes outlines and the focus outline
            phosphorLow: #6fd06a, labels, removed lines and meta
            phosphorDim: #2c6a2a, the reticle and control outlines
            trace: #1f4d1e, zone borders and dashed dividers
            addedGlow: #0b260b, added line ground
        type:
            One monospace family throughout, OCR A Std, OCR-A, Lucida Console,
            ui-monospace, DejaVu Sans Mono, with a soft green text glow. Base
            14px at 1.55. The title is 34px caps, the repository 22px, the
            checks figure 30px, labels 11 to 12px caps tracked 0.12 to 0.16em,
            the diff 12.5px.
        layout:
            The screen is one viewfinder, a black rounded rectangle with a 28px
            radius, faint green grain behind the content and a dark vignette at
            the edges. An on screen readout row shows a ring with Brightwork
            code live, IR 2 and gain, and the channel PR 214. The header holds
            the repository and a Private note, the tabs as caps with a pointer
            before the current one, and outlined counters at the right. A
            dashed rule leads to the target, a centred block with a framed
            Open PR 214 tag, the title in caps and the merge sentence, behind
            which a reticle draws crosshair lines with a gap round the title,
            tick marks and four corner brackets. Below are three zones, 260px,
            flexible and 260px, each a bordered box with a plus before its
            label. Checks shows 11 of 12 and every check with a tick and ok,
            the failing one boxed in a dashed bright outline with an octagon
            cross and failing. The diff zone shows added lines bright on a
            green ground and removed lines dim and struck, with the comment as
            a bright framed Mark joined by a short line. The right zones hold
            reviewers, files with added and removed counts, details and a
            dashed disabled merge. Below 1100px the diff leads.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 20px between zones, 12px zone padding, 48px around the reticle.
        density: Medium. One centred target, then three zones of readouts.
        corners: A 28px rounded viewfinder, 4px buttons and fields, square zones.
        borders: 1px trace green on zones, dashed dividers, and a dashed bloom outline on whatever fails.
        shadows: A soft green text glow and a dark vignette at the viewfinder edge, with grain behind the content.
        icons:
            1.8px line icons in the one green. A tick for passed, an octagon
            cross for failing, a ringed tick for approved, a triangle for
            changes, always with the word, since colour cannot help.
        focus: A 2px bloom outline offset 3px with a 6px phosphor halo.
        tone: Camera readouts, such as Live, IR 2, Gain, Mark and Locked until all checks pass.
    style303:
        number: 303
        run: 61
        screen: CodeRepository
        name: Sonar
        idea: A submarine sonar console in deep sea green, where a round scope with a sweeping arc plots the twelve checks as contacts, the failing one pinged and labelled, and rounded instrument bezels hold the rest.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/303.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            abyss: #021411, the page, style sheet ground, fields and dials
            console: #06211b, the header strip, tabs and console gradient base
            consoleTop: #0a2c24, console gradient tops and the comment
            bezel: #14453a, instrument rims and chips
            grid: #1a4b3f, dividers and scope rings
            ink: #d2f8e8, text
            kelp: #86c7ad, labels, bearings and meta
            sonarGreen: #3ff0a2, the sweep, contacts, passed, approved, added lines, the current tab, the primary button and focus
            amber: #ffc862, changes requested, the ping comment and Private
            coral: #ff8b7b, the failing contact and removed lines
            coralShade: #2e1716, the failing row and removed line ground
        type:
            A wide humanist sans, Tahoma, Verdana, DejaVu Sans, for headings at
            700, the title at 26px and figures at 26px in sonar green. Verdana
            for text at 13.5px and 1.55 and labels at 10.5px bold caps tracked
            0.14em. Data and the diff use Lucida Sans Typewriter or a system
            monospace at 11.5 to 12.5px.
        layout:
            A pill shaped header strip holds a round badge with a green ring,
            Brightwork Code and the repository, an amber Private label and pill
            counters, with rounded tabs below and the current one filled
            green. The upper band has two instruments. The scope bezel holds a
            round sonar display with three rings, crosshairs, bearings 000 to
            270, a green sweep wedge and a bright sweep line, and twelve
            contacts as green dots, the seventh a coral ringed cross with a
            dashed ping ring and the label 07 e2e-android. Beside it a contact
            list numbers every check with a tick, the failing row tinted
            coral, and under it 11 of 12 checks passed and the failing line.
            The contact report bezel holds the Open pill, the title, the merge
            sentence, two rounded reviewer dials, and a waterfall of the three
            files, each with counts and a dotted green trail scaled to its
            additions. The lower band holds the signal log with the diff,
            where the comment is a Ping bubble with an amber rim and a glowing
            ring marker, and a details bezel with assignee, pill labels,
            milestone, linked issue and a dashed disabled merge. Below 1100px
            the bands stack, below 700px the contact list wraps in two columns.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 20px between instruments, 18px inside bezels, 12px between dials.
        density: Medium. A large scope beside the contact report, then a wide signal log.
        corners: Round. 20px bezels, 14px dials, a pill header, a circular scope and pill chips.
        borders: 2px bezel rims with a 4px dark inner rim, 1px grid lines, a 2px amber rim on the comment.
        shadows: Soft drop shadows under bezels and a glow ring on the ping marker.
        icons:
            1.9px line icons. Dots for passed contacts and a ringed cross for
            the failing one on the scope, and in lists a tick, an octagon cross,
            a ringed tick and a triangle, each with its word.
        focus: A 2px sonar green outline offset 3px with a soft green halo.
        tone: Calm sonar words, such as Scope, Contact report, Waterfall, Signal log, Ping and Holding depth until all checks pass.

    style304:
        number: 304
        run: 62
        screen: OpsMonitor
        name: Dark analytics
        idea: Charts lead on a dark slate canvas, a full-width requests chart over error and latency half charts, each series in its own crisp colour, with a service table and stacked lists below.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/304.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            canvas: #0b1017, the page and style sheet ground
            panel: #121a24, cards and the top bar
            raise: #18222f, the current app tab, the pressed range button and the secondary button
            line: #243243, card borders and table rules
            ink: #e6edf5, text and figures
            muted: #9aa8ba, labels, axes, meta and dashed deploy markers
            requests: #4cc9f0, the requests series and its area, links and the primary button
            errors: #ff7a93, the error series and Firing
            p50: #b19cff, the dashed p50 latency line
            p95: #f2b84b, the p95 latency line, Degraded and Investigating
            healthy: #5ad08e, Healthy and Resolved
            recovered: #7ab8ff, Recovered
            focus: #ffe066, the focus outline
        type:
            One system stack, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
            Arial, at 14px and 1.45, with ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas at 13px
            for service names and versions. The page title is 22px at 650,
            figure values 28px at 650 with tabular numbers, card titles 15px at
            650, figure labels 12px caps tracked 0.04em, axes 11px.
        layout:
            A panel coloured top bar holds a gradient square mark and Brightwork
            Ops, the five suite apps as tabs with Ops current and a requests
            coloured underline, an Environment Production pill and a 1h 6h 24h
            7d segmented range with 24h pressed. The page has a title and the
            description line, then four figure cards in a row, each with a caps
            label, a big value, a 96px sparkline and a note, for requests per
            minute, error rate, api p95 latency and the open incident. A wide
            card holds the requests chart with a fading area, four grid lines,
            dashed vertical deploy markers and a ringed peak point labelled
            9,400 at 14.00, with an hour axis and a note. Error rate and latency
            follow as two half cards, the spike marked with a small triangle.
            Below sits a services table beside a stack of three cards, the
            incident card with an amber border and tinted ground, then alerts
            and deploys as ruled lists. Below 980px everything stacks and the
            figures go two by two, at phone width one per row with the table
            in its own sideways scroll.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px card padding and gaps, 24px page padding.
        density: Medium. Four figures, three charts and the lists over about two screens.
        corners: 10px cards, 8px buttons, fields and range control, full round status pills.
        borders: 1px #243243 on every card, inner rules in #1c2735, no borders inside charts.
        shadows: None. Depth comes from the panel step and the tinted incident card.
        icons:
            16px status shapes in tinted pills beside the word. A ringed tick
            for Healthy, a triangle with a bang for Degraded, a circular arrow
            for Recovered, a bolt for Firing, a plain tick for Resolved and a
            magnifier for Investigating.
        focus: A 2px yellow outline offset 2px.
        tone: Neutral analytic labels, such as Requests per minute, Signal and Production overview.
    style305:
        number: 305
        run: 62
        screen: OpsMonitor
        name: Trading terminal
        idea: A dense black terminal of seven numbered panels with orange title bars, a service ticker tape, function key app tabs and all caps monospace readouts.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/305.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            black: #000000, the page, gaps between panels and the style sheet
            panel: #0c0c0c, panel bodies
            rule: #3a3a3a, panel borders and dotted table rules
            ink: #f2e9da, body text and figures
            muted: #aaa092, labels and axes
            orange: #ff9a1f, panel title bars, the logo block, table headers, request bars and the primary button
            yellow: #ffd23f, times, the peak bar, Degraded, Investigating and p95
            green: #3ddc84, Healthy and Resolved
            cyan: #5cc8ff, Recovered and p50
            red: #ff6161, the error line and Firing
            focus: #ffffff, a white focus outline over an orange halo
        type:
            Monospace for everything, ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas,
            Liberation Mono, at 12px and 1.4. Panel titles 12px bold black on
            orange in caps, quote figures 16px bold, the incident number 18px
            bold yellow. Status words and the alert wire are in caps.
        layout:
            A command bar runs across the top over a 2px orange rule. It holds
            an orange BRIGHTWORK OPS block, the apps as function keys F1
            PROJECTS to F5 OPS with F5 inverted cream, a CMD prompt field
            reading OPS PROD 24H and a PROD 24H readout. A ticker tape follows
            with each service in caps, its status shape and short word, uptime
            and metric, scrolling sideways inside itself on small screens. The
            wall is a 12 column grid with 2px black gaps. Panel 1 is the
            service board table, panel 2 the requests per minute chart as 24
            orange hourly bars with the 14.00 bar yellow and a HI and LO quote
            row, panel 3 the error rate line with base and spike quotes, panel
            4 latency as stepped p50 and p95 lines, panel 5 the incident with a
            yellow border, panel 6 the alert wire as headline rows and panel 7
            the deploy blotter table. A footer line repeats the description.
            Below 1000px panels pair up and at phone width they stack, with
            tables scrolling inside their panels.
        spacing: A 2px gap between panels, 6px panel padding, 4px by 6px table cells.
        density: Very dense. Seven panels and a ticker on one wide screen.
        corners: Square everywhere.
        borders: 1px #3a3a3a panels, dotted row rules, a yellow border on the incident panel, a 2px orange rule under the command bar.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            12px status shapes before caps words, a ringed tick for HEALTHY, a
            triangle for DEGRADED, a circular arrow for RECOVERED, a bolt for
            FIRING, a tick for RESOLVED and a magnifier for INVESTIGATING.
        focus: A 2px white outline with a 4px orange halo.
        tone: Terse terminal caps, such as HI, SPIKE, ALERT WIRE, DEPLOY BLOTTER and 3 FILLS.
    style306:
        number: 306
        run: 62
        screen: OpsMonitor
        name: Mission control
        idea: A deep navy control room wall, a row of large countdown style clocks over a grid of numbered console panels with cyan corner brackets, nominal and caution wording and condensed caps.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/306.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            night: #040a14, the page and the clock faces
            console: #0a1628, panel fill and swatches
            tile: #0e1d33, service tiles
            rule: #29486b, panel borders
            ink: #dbe8f5, text
            muted: #8fa8c4, labels and axes
            cyan: #59d6ff, clock digits, corner brackets, the requests line, p50, Recovered and the primary button
            amber: #ffb020, Caution, the incident panel, p95 and the open incident clock
            green: #4be08a, Nominal, Resolved and the live indicator
            red: #ff6b6b, the error line and Firing
            focus: #ffffff, a white focus outline with a cyan halo
        type:
            Condensed labels in Bahnschrift, DIN Alternate, Roboto Condensed,
            Arial Narrow, system-ui at 14px, and ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo,
            Consolas for clocks and figures. Clocks are 44px mono at 600 with a
            soft glow, the incident number 28px mono bold amber, panel titles
            12px caps tracked 0.2em, status words 13px bold caps tracked 0.12em.
        layout:
            A header bar holds BRIGHTWORK OPS over Production control in
            tracked caps, the apps as caps links with Ops boxed in cyan, and a
            Telemetry live line. The description runs as a tracked caps line.
            A row of four clock boxes follows, Station time 10.00.00, INC-0427
            open T+03.02 in amber, Billing back T+02.06 and Last deploy
            T+00.48, each with a note. Below sits a three column wall of
            console panels, each square with cyan L brackets at the corners and
            a numbered title such as Console 01 Services. Console 01 holds the
            services as a two by two grid of tiles with a 3px status top edge
            and billing full width, Console 02 the requests line on a 12 by 5
            grid with a ringed peak and peak and floor readouts, Console 03 the
            incident with an amber border, then Console 04 error rate, Console
            05 latency and Console 06 the event log, and Console 07 the deploy
            sequence across the full width in three columns. The wall goes to
            two columns below 1100px and one at phone width.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 12px gutters, 16px panel padding, 24px page padding.
        density: Medium dense. Four clocks and seven consoles on one wide wall.
        corners: Square panels with 14px cyan corner brackets, chamfered 8px corners on buttons.
        borders: 1px #29486b on panels and clocks, an amber border on the incident, 3px status top edges on tiles.
        shadows: A faint glow on the clock digits only, and a radial navy glow at the top of the page.
        icons:
            18px status shapes beside caps words, a ringed tick for Nominal, a
            triangle for Caution, a circular arrow for Recovered, a bolt for
            Firing, a tick for Resolved and a magnifier for Investigating.
        focus: A 2px white outline offset 3px with a 6px cyan halo.
        tone: Control room words, such as Console 04, Nominal, Caution, Event log, Deploy sequence and T plus clocks.
    style307:
        number: 307
        run: 62
        screen: OpsMonitor
        name: Radar
        idea: An air traffic radar scope where services are blips on healthy, degraded and outage rings under a sweeping wedge, with flight progress strips, phosphor traces, advisories and departures beside it.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/307.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            scopeBlack: #020a06, the page and style sheet
            scopeFace: #03140b, the scope centre and trace panels
            strip: #0a1f13, service strips
            ring: #1d5a37, rings, borders and rules
            phosphor: #7dffb0, healthy blips, headings, the traffic trace and the primary button
            ink: #d6ffe6, body text
            muted: #6fc796, labels and axes
            amber: #ffc94a, Degraded, the incident box and p95
            sky: #8fd8ff, Recovered and p50
            coral: #ff8a7a, the error trace and Firing
            focus: #ffffff, a dashed white focus outline
        type:
            Monospace throughout, ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas,
            DejaVu Sans Mono, at 14px and 1.5. Strip names 17px bold, the
            incident number 20px bold amber, section titles 13px bold caps
            tracked 0.14em in phosphor, strip labels 11px caps, blip names 15px
            bold inside the scope.
        layout:
            A header holds a small radar mark, BRIGHTWORK OPS, the apps as
            plain links with Ops underlined, and Sector production window 24 h.
            The top area pairs a 560px circular scope with a column of strips.
            The scope has a bezel ring, three rings for healthy, degraded and
            outage labelled along the right axis, cross hairs, degree ticks and
            a static conic sweep wedge. Each service is its status shape used
            as a blip, api, web and notifications on the inner ring,
            sync-worker on the middle ring and billing on the outer ring, each
            named with its word beside it. A caption and a shape key sit under
            the scope. The column holds five flight strips, each with a 10px
            coloured tab, the name, status and uptime with metric in dashed
            cells, then the incident as an amber box. Below run three phosphor
            trace panels for traffic, errors and latency with notes, then
            Advisories for alerts and Departures for deploys as ruled rows.
            Below 1000px the scope sits above the strips, and at phone width
            only blip names show in the scope and strips wrap to two rows.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between scope, strips and traces, 6px between strips.
        density: Medium. The scope dominates, the strips are compact.
        corners: A circular scope, square strips, 8px trace panels, round buttons.
        borders: 1px #1d5a37 rings and panels, dashed dividers inside strips, an amber border on the incident.
        shadows: An 8px bezel ring around the scope and a soft phosphor glow on traces.
        icons:
            The status shapes are the blips themselves, a ringed tick for
            Healthy, a triangle for Degraded and a circular arrow for
            Recovered, and they repeat beside every status word, with a bolt
            for Firing, a tick for Resolved and a magnifier for Investigating.
        focus: A 2px dashed white outline offset 3px.
        tone: Air traffic words kept plain, such as Sector, Service strips, Advisories and Departures.
    style308:
        number: 308
        run: 62
        screen: OpsMonitor
        name: SRE minimal
        idea: A very quiet single column in neutral greys, a plain sentence of the state at the top, hairline lists and tiny grey charts, with colour used only for the open incident.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/308.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            ground: #131416, the page and style sheet
            ink: #dcdcdc, text and the primary button
            soft: #b5b5b5, values and secondary text
            muted: #8f8f8f, labels, times and healthy status
            hairline: #2a2b2e, row rules and chart baselines
            mark: #7d7d7d, chart lines
            incident: #ff8466, the open incident, Degraded, Firing and the error spike only
            focus: #e8e8e8, a thin focus outline
        type:
            One system stack, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
            Arial, at 15px and 1.6. The summary sentence is 34px at 300, the
            incident title 20px at 500, names 15px at 500, labels, times and
            status lines 13px in muted grey.
        layout:
            One left aligned column of about 760px with wide margins. A small
            muted header line reads Brightwork Ops production 24 h with the
            apps as plain links at right. A muted description line leads to a
            large light sentence, One incident open in the incident colour,
            then three services healthy, sync-worker degraded and billing back
            after six minutes. The incident follows with a 2px incident colour
            left line, its number, Investigating and Severity 2 in small
            incident text, the title and the opened time and owner. Services,
            the charts, alerts and deploys follow as quiet sections with small
            muted headings and 64px between them. Lists are hairline rows with
            the name, a right aligned value and a status line below. The charts
            are three small grey line charts side by side with captions, the
            error spike marked by a small incident diamond. At phone width the
            charts stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 12px rows, 64 to 72px between sections, 48px page padding.
        density: Sparse. One narrow column.
        corners: None, 2px on buttons.
        borders: 1px #2a2b2e hairlines between rows, a 2px incident line, an underline field.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            14px status shapes in grey beside lower case words, a ringed tick
            for healthy, a circular arrow for recovered and a tick for
            resolved. Only the triangle for degraded, the bolt for firing and
            the magnifier for investigating take the incident colour.
        focus: A 1px light grey outline offset 4px.
        tone: Lower case and plain, such as healthy, degraded and resolved, led by a summary sentence.

    style309:
        number: 309
        run: 63
        screen: OpsMonitor
        name: Oscilloscope
        idea: The monitor as a bench oscilloscope, phosphor green and yellow traces on a dark graticule with on screen scale readouts, lettered deploy cursors, measurement boxes, knobs and soft keys for the services.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/309.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            bench: #111315, the page behind the instruments
            body: #1c1f22, the instrument body tone and the style sheet
            panel: #25292d, modules, the knob panel and soft keys
            edge: #3a4046, module borders
            silk: #dfe4e8, silkscreen text
            muted: #a4adb6, labels and name plates
            screen: #040806, scope screens and fields
            graticule: #1f3a28, grid divisions, decorative
            phosphor: #5dff8f, the CH1 requests trace and screen readouts
            yellow: #ffe14d, the CH2 error trace, p95, Degraded, the trigger, the primary button and focus
            cyan: #6fe3ff, p50 and Recovered
            red: #ff8080, Firing
        type:
            Silkscreen in Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, system-ui at 14px,
            and screen readouts in ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas.
            Readouts are 12px mono in trace colours, measurement values 15px
            mono, the incident number 20px mono bold yellow, plate and module
            titles 11px bold caps tracked 0.18em.
        layout:
            A slim black bar holds BRIGHTWORK OPS with Production 24 h
            acquisition and the apps as small tabs with Ops raised. The first
            instrument is a rounded body with a name plate, Traffic scope 2
            channel. Its left part is the screen, a 10 by 8 division graticule
            with centre ticks, readouts across the top for CH1 1,250 rpm per
            div, CH2 0.5 percent per div and time 2.4 h per div, the green
            requests trace and the yellow error trace with a trigger arrow at 2
            percent, dashed cursors A, B and C at the deploys, channel markers
            at left and four measurement boxes below for CH1 max, CH1 min, CH2
            mean and CH2 max. Five soft keys under the screen hold the
            services. Its right part is a 240px column with four knobs for the
            scales and trigger, then a Cursors list of the deploys. A second
            instrument, the module bay, holds a latency mini screen, the
            incident module and a trigger log of alerts. Below 1000px the
            column drops under the screen and modules stack, and at phone width
            soft keys stack and on screen text hides behind the readouts.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 20px instrument padding, 12px module padding, 24px between instruments.
        density: Medium. One big screen with its controls, then a bay of three modules.
        corners: 20px instrument bodies, 10px modules, 8px screens, 6px keys and fields.
        borders: 1px #3a4046 on bodies and modules, screens inset in black.
        shadows: Deep drop shadows under instruments, a 2px lip under keys, a glow on traces.
        icons:
            16px status shapes on soft keys and log rows, a ringed tick for
            Healthy, a triangle for Degraded, a circular arrow for Recovered, a
            bolt for Firing, a tick for Resolved and a magnifier for
            Investigating. Knobs and cursor letters are drawn, not icons.
        focus: A 3px yellow outline offset 2px.
        tone: Bench instrument terms, such as CH1, per div, cursors, trigger log and acquisition.
    style310:
        number: 310
        run: 63
        screen: OpsMonitor
        name: Tube amp
        idea: A vintage amplifier faceplate on dark tolex, a row of glowing tubes for the services, analog VU meters for traffic, errors and latency, a chart recorder, a jewel warning lamp for the incident and engraved small caps labels.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/310.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            tolex: #15100c, the textured page behind the amp
            faceplate: #2a2119, the header plate, swatches and the secondary button
            bay: #211a14, section bays
            tag: #1a140f, tube tags, fields and the recorder
            cream: #f3e6c8, engraved text, meter scales and p95
            muted: #cdbb98, secondary labels
            brass: #d6ae62, the logo, bay titles, times and the primary button
            rule: #5a4a38, borders and dashed rules
            amber: #ffbf5e, tube glow, the requests line, Degraded and the incident
            mint: #9be29a, Healthy and Resolved
            sky: #9fd4ff, Recovered and p50
            coral: #ff8a6a, the meter red zone, the error line and Firing
            focus: #ffe7a8, the focus outline
        type:
            Engraved labels in Iowan Old Style, Palatino Linotype, Palatino,
            Georgia as small caps tracked 0.12 to 0.16em, and text in Gill Sans,
            Optima, Trebuchet MS, system-ui at 15px. The logo is 30px italic
            serif bold in brass, the incident number 20px serif bold amber, bay
            titles 16px serif small caps, service names 14px mono bold.
        layout:
            A rounded header faceplate with brass screws holds the italic
            Brightwork logo over Ops production 24 hours, the apps as jacks
            that light amber for Ops, and a glowing pilot lamp marked Power on,
            with the description below. Bays follow on the tolex. Service tubes
            shows five drawn tubes in a row, each glowing warm, the
            sync-worker tube dimmer with flicker marks, and under each a tag
            with the name, status shape and word, uptime and metric. Meters
            shows three VU meters with a cream scale, a coral red zone, a white
            needle at the current value and a gold peak mark, for requests per
            minute, error rate and p95 latency, each with a small caps caption
            and a note. Chart recorder draws the four series over 24 hours on a
            dark gridded strip with a legend. Three bays close the screen, the
            warning lamp with an amber jewel beside the incident facts, alerts
            and deploys. Below 980px tubes go three across and meters stack,
            and at phone width tubes go two across.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 20px bay padding and gaps, 16px between tubes, 24px page padding.
        density: Roomy. Tubes and meters take most of the space.
        corners: 16px faceplate, 12px bays, 10px meter frames, 6px tags, round jacks and pill buttons.
        borders: A 2px dark brass edge on the faceplate, 1px #5a4a38 bays, dashed list rules.
        shadows: A deep faceplate shadow, warm tube, lamp and jack glows, brass screw heads.
        icons:
            16px status shapes on tube tags and lists, a ringed tick for
            Healthy, a triangle for Degraded, a circular arrow for Recovered, a
            bolt for Firing, a tick for Resolved and a magnifier for
            Investigating. Lit and unlit jacks mark the apps.
        focus: A 3px pale gold outline offset 3px.
        tone: Warm hardware words, such as Power on, Service tubes, Meters, Chart recorder and Warning lamp.
    style311:
        number: 311
        run: 63
        screen: OpsMonitor
        name: Modular synth
        idea: A rack of synth modules between metal rails, each service a module with an uptime knob, a status lamp and jacks, a patch bay of coloured cables linking the services, and hourly traffic as a step sequencer.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/311.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            case: #0c0d10, the page behind the rack
            rail: #41454d, rack rails and the style sheet edge
            module: #1b1e25, module faces
            edge: #343a46, module borders and rules
            ink: #eef0f4, silkscreen text and knob pointers
            muted: #a9b0bd, small labels
            sky: #5cc8ff, the api module, p50, Recovered, the primary button and the focus halo
            violet: #c4a3ff, the web module and its cable
            amber: #ffc04d, the sync-worker module, sequencer lights, Degraded and the incident gate
            mint: #6fe0a6, the notifications module, Healthy and Resolved
            pink: #ff8fa8, the billing module and the patch title
            red: #ff7b7b, the error trace and Firing
        type:
            Condensed caps in Roboto Condensed, Arial Narrow, Helvetica Neue,
            Arial, system-ui at 14px, values in ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas.
            The brand is 22px condensed at 800, uptime values 18px mono bold,
            module titles 13px bold caps tracked 0.14em, labels 10 to 11px caps.
        layout:
            Metal rails with oval holes separate four rack rows. Row one holds
            a narrow brand module with BRIGHTWORK and the apps as a lamp list,
            Ops lit, then one module per service, each with a coloured title
            underline, a knob whose arc shows uptime on a 99 to 100 percent
            scale, the uptime value, a status lamp strip with shape and word,
            the metric and In and Out jacks. Billing shows 6 min down and back
            at 07.54. Row two holds the patch bay, five labelled jacks with
            sagging cables from web to api, api to sync-worker, api to billing
            and sync-worker to notifications, listed below, and the gate module
            for the incident on an amber tinted face. Row three holds the
            sequencer, 24 hourly columns of ten amber lights with the 14.00
            peak lit white, and a scope module with error and latency screens.
            Row four holds triggers for alerts and a clock module for deploys.
            Every module has screws top and bottom. At phone width modules go
            full width and service modules pair up.
        spacing: A 4px gap between modules, 20px module padding top and bottom for screws, 12px sides.
        density: Medium dense. Modules pack edge to edge in rack rows.
        corners: 3px module faces, round knobs, jacks, lamps and screws.
        borders: 1px #343a46 modules, a 3px coloured underline under each title.
        shadows: A soft shadow under cables, glowing lamps and lit steps, a metal gradient on rails.
        icons:
            16px status shapes in lamp strips and lists, a ringed tick for
            Healthy, a triangle for Degraded, a circular arrow for Recovered, a
            bolt for Firing, a tick for Resolved and a magnifier for
            Investigating. Knobs, jacks and screws are drawn decoration.
        focus: A 3px white outline offset 2px with a sky halo.
        tone: Synth module names, such as Patch, Gate, Sequencer, Scope, Triggers and Clock.
    style312:
        number: 312
        run: 63
        screen: OpsMonitor
        name: Audio workstation
        idea: A music workstation session, an arrangement of tracks for requests, errors, latency, deploy clips, the incident region and alert markers under a playhead, and a mixer with one channel strip, meter and fader per service.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/312.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            studio: #141518, the page
            panel: #1f2024, the arrangement and mixer frames
            header: #26272c, track headers, channel strips and title rows
            lane: #1a1b1e, track lanes with an hour grid
            rule: #34363c, lane and panel borders
            ink: #ececef, text
            muted: #a3a6ae, labels and the ruler
            teal: #3fc1b0, the requests waveform and the primary button
            violet: #a48bff, the latency track and deploy clips
            amber: #ffb547, the incident region, Degraded and the master bus
            red: #ff7070, the error track and Firing
            green: #6bdc8b, Healthy and Resolved
            sky: #7cc4ff, Recovered and p50
            lcd: #b8f5a0, the time display
            playhead: #ffd84a, the playhead and focus
        type:
            System sans, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial,
            at 13px and 1.4, with ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas for the
            time display, values, clips and scribble strips. The time display
            is 20px mono at 600 in LCD green, the incident number 20px mono
            bold amber, channel values 15px mono, region labels 11px at 600.
        layout:
            A transport bar holds Brightwork Ops session, the apps as folder
            tabs, three transport buttons, an LCD reading 07.48.00 playhead
            billing 5xx and Production last 24 hours. The arrangement panel
            has a 168px header column and a 960px timeline at 40px per hour
            with an hour ruler. Tracks are Requests as a mirrored teal
            waveform region, Error rate with the spike, Latency with p95 solid
            and p50 dashed, Deploys as three staggered clips ending at their
            times, Incident as an amber region from 06.58, and Alerts as
            markers with shapes. A yellow playhead stands at 07.48. Each
            region has a dark label chip. The mixer has five channel strips,
            each with a status button, two meters and a fader on a 99 to 100
            percent scale, uptime, the metric and a coloured scribble strip,
            then a wider amber master bus strip for the incident. Markers and
            clips lists close the screen. The timeline scrolls sideways inside
            its panel on small screens, strips go three then two across.
        spacing: A 4px unit. 6 to 10px padding, 12px between panels, 40px per hour.
        density: Dense. Seven lanes and six strips on one screen.
        corners: 6px panels, 4px regions, clips, buttons and folder tabs.
        borders: 1px #34363c, regions carry a lighter border of their own colour, clips a 3px edge at their time.
        shadows: Only under fader caps.
        icons:
            14px status shapes on channel buttons, markers and lists, a ringed
            tick for Healthy, a triangle for Degraded, a circular arrow for
            Recovered, a bolt for Firing, a tick for Resolved and a magnifier
            for Investigating, plus start, play and flag transport glyphs.
        focus: A 2px yellow outline offset 2px.
        tone: Studio terms, such as Session, Arrangement, Clips, Markers, Mixer and Master bus.
    style313:
        number: 313
        run: 63
        screen: OpsMonitor
        name: Video timeline
        idea: A video editor where services sit in a bin as clips, a program monitor shows the frame at the 07.48 playhead, an inspector holds the incident, and a multi track timeline lays out the 24 hours as video and audio tracks with markers.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/313.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            suite: #16151c, the page
            pane: #211f29, panes
            paneHead: #2a2834, pane titles, track headers and the ruler
            well: #0f0e14, track wells, bin tiles and fields
            rule: #3a3746, borders and rules
            ink: #ecebf3, text
            muted: #aba7bd, labels and timecodes
            video: #5865d8, video clips, the requests filmstrip, the primary button and the focus halo
            audio: #2e8a5a, audio clips under #7ff0b0 waveforms
            playhead: #ff5c7a, the playhead, the timecode readout and the current app underline
            amber: #ffbe55, the incident clip, Degraded and Investigating
            green: #74e0a0, Healthy and Resolved
            sky: #86c8ff, Recovered
            rose: #ff7f8f, the error trace and Firing
        type:
            Segoe UI, system-ui, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial at 13px and
            1.45, with ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas for timecode,
            service names and track tags. The monitor title card is up to 30px
            bold, the incident number 20px mono bold amber, the timecode
            readout 18px mono in the playhead colour, track tags 11px mono bold.
        layout:
            A black bar holds Brightwork Ops, the apps as workspace links with
            a playhead coloured underline on Ops, and Sequence Production last
            24 hours. Three panes follow. The bin shows the services as clip
            tiles, each a 16 by 9 thumbnail with a large status shape and the
            uptime as a duration badge, then the name, word and metric. The
            program monitor shows the frame at the playhead, safe area guides,
            a timecode overlay and a title card reading billing 5xx rate above
            2 percent with the error spike, then playback buttons and a note
            that billing recovered six minutes later. The inspector holds the
            incident as property rows. The full width timeline has a markers
            row with alert flags, a timecode ruler, V3 Incident as an amber
            clip from 06.58, V2 Deploys as three staggered clips, V1 Requests
            as a filmstrip of 24 frames with bar heights, and A1 to A3 as audio
            waveforms for error rate, p95 and p50, with a playhead line at
            07.48. Markers and an edit list close the screen. The monitor moves
            first below 1100px and the timeline scrolls inside itself on phones.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 8px gutters between panes, 6 to 10px pane padding, 44px per hour.
        density: Dense. Three panes over an eight row timeline.
        corners: 4px panes, tiles and buttons, 3px clips and markers.
        borders: 1px #3a3746, clips carry a lighter border of their colour, a dashed safe area in the monitor.
        shadows: None. Wells sit darker than panes.
        icons:
            Large status shapes as bin thumbnails and 14px shapes on markers,
            chips and lists, a ringed tick for Healthy, a triangle for
            Degraded, a circular arrow for Recovered, a bolt for Firing, a tick
            for Resolved and a magnifier for Investigating.
        focus: A 2px white outline offset 2px with a video blue halo.
        tone: Editing words, such as Bin, Program, Inspector, In point, Markers and Edit list.

    style314:
        number: 314
        run: 64
        screen: OpsMonitor
        name: Gaming RGB
        idea: A gamer HUD for the service monitor, with chamfered black panels framed by a cyan to magenta to lime gradient edge, services as a roster of cards with segmented uptime health bars, and terse caps labels.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/314.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            void: #07080d, the page behind a faint 32px cyan grid
            panel: #10121b, inside every chamfered panel and the style sheet
            panelRaised: #171a26, roster cards, readout boxes and list rows
            ink: #eef1ff, text and figures
            muted: #a3abcb, labels, times and axis ticks
            line: #2a2f45, dividers, grid lines and empty health segments
            cyan: #35e0ff, first stop of the RGB edge, the request line and its glow, links
            magenta: #ff5fdc, middle stop of the RGB edge, the error line, panel title diamonds and the focus glow
            lime: #a6ff5c, last stop of the RGB edge, the p50 line and version tags
            healthy: #8dff6a, Healthy and Resolved words, filled circle and square, health segments
            degraded: #ffc23d, Degraded and Investigating, filled triangle, the dashed p95 line and the SEV 2 tag with near black text
            recovered: #5ee6ff, Recovered word and filled diamond
            firing: #ff6b7d, Firing word and filled octagon
        type:
            Bahnschrift, DIN Alternate, Roboto Condensed, Arial Narrow for text,
            and ui-monospace, Cascadia Mono, Menlo, Consolas for every number,
            service name and time. Base 15px at 1.45. The incident ID is 32px
            mono at 800, readout figures 22px mono at 700, panel titles 13px
            caps tracked 0.2em with a small magenta diamond before them, meta
            12px mono.
        layout:
            A dark top bar with a hexagon BW mark filled with the RGB gradient,
            the Brightwork Ops wordmark in tracked caps, the suite apps Canvas,
            Drive, Code and Ops as caps tabs with a magenta underline on Ops,
            and chips for ENV PRODUCTION and WINDOW 24H plus a search button. A
            2px RGB rule sits under the bar. Below, three columns. Left is a
            300px Service roster panel with five cards, each with a 3px status
            left edge, the service name in mono, a filled status shape and caps
            word, a 20 segment health bar where filled segments show uptime
            above 99 percent, and stats such as UPTIME 99.98% and P95 LATENCY
            182 ms. The centre holds a Throughput panel with three readout boxes
            for Peak, Night low and Now, then a large glowing area chart with a
            cyan PEAK 9,400 tag at the afternoon peak, and beneath it two small
            panels for Error rate and Latency. The right 320px column holds the
            Active incident panel with a big INC-0427, a SEV 2 tag, status,
            opened, owner and two buttons, then an Alert feed and Patch notes
            for deploys with lime version tags. Below 1180px the right column
            becomes a row. Below 760px everything stacks in one column.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px page gutter, 16px between panels, 16px panel padding, 10px between roster cards.
        density: Dense HUD. Roster, three charts and the incident column are visible at once on a laptop.
        corners: No radius. Panels have 14px chamfers at top left and bottom right, roster cards a 10px chamfer at top right, the logo is a hexagon.
        borders: Every panel has a 2px RGB gradient edge made by a gradient behind a clipped inner panel. Cards carry a 3px left status edge, lists use 1px line dividers.
        shadows: None for depth. Only the request line glows with a 4px cyan drop shadow.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.8 stroke for navigation. Filled status shapes, a
            circle for Healthy, a triangle for Degraded, a diamond for
            Recovered, an octagon for Firing, a square for Resolved and a
            magnifier for Investigating, always beside the word.
        focus: A 2px white outline offset 3px plus a 5px magenta glow ring. Buttons are never clipped so the ring always shows.
        tone: Terse uppercase HUD labels such as Service roster, Alert feed, Patch notes and PEAK 9,400.
    style315:
        number: 315
        run: 64
        screen: OpsMonitor
        name: Esports broadcast
        idea: The monitor as a live broadcast overlay, with a LIVE bug, a slanted scoreboard where each service is a team with its own colour and its uptime as the score, a big stage chart with a lower third for the incident, and tickers of alerts and deploys.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/315.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            arena: #090c18, the page under a soft navy spotlight gradient at the top
            stage: #11162a, the chart stage, desk cards and the style sheet
            bar: #1a2142, scoreboard blocks, tickers and the title bar
            barRaised: #232b52, the current app tab and the lower third action area
            ink: #ffffff, text, and section tags drawn as white blocks with dark text
            muted: #b0b8db, labels, times and axis ticks
            line: #2d3663, card borders, rules and grid lines
            live: #d6193a, the LIVE bug and the incident key in the lower third, with white text
            highlight: #ffe066, the request line, the peak pin, the primary button, ticker labels and focus
            teamApi: #4da3ff, api team tag and score underline
            teamWeb: #ff9d3c, web team tag and score underline
            teamSync: #2fd8c4, sync-worker team tag, score underline and the p50 line
            teamNotif: #b893ff, notifications team tag, score underline and the p95 line
            teamBilling: #ffd84a, billing team tag and score underline
            healthy: #6ee7a0, Healthy and Resolved with filled circle and square
            degraded: #ffcf4a, Degraded and Investigating with triangle and magnifier
            recovered: #86cfff, Recovered with a filled diamond
            firing: #ff8593, Firing with a filled octagon and the error line
        type:
            Segoe UI, Helvetica Neue, Roboto, Arial, mostly italic at 800 to
            900. Base 15px at 1.45. Scores are 28px italic 900 with tabular
            numbers and a smaller percent sign, the lower third title 20px
            italic 900, section tags 13px italic 900 caps tracked 0.14em, small
            caps meta 12px at 800.
        layout:
            A broadcast top bar made of skewed blocks, a red LIVE bug with a
            white dot, then a navy title block with Brightwork Ops and
            Production last 24 hours, and the suite apps at right with a yellow
            underline on Ops. A white skewed tag reads Scoreboard uptime above a
            row of five parallelogram team blocks skewed 14 degrees with upright
            text. Each block has a team colour three letter tag such as API or
            SYN, the service name, the uptime as a large italic score, and a
            footer with the status word and shape and one fact, and a 4px team
            colour underline. billing shows 6 MIN DOWN as its score. Below sits
            the arena, a wide stage with a Requests per minute tag, a peak
            readout, a yellow area line chart with a 9,400 pin, and across its
            foot a lower third with a red INCIDENT key, a pale caption panel
            holding INC-0427 sync-worker queue backlog with severity, opened,
            owner and Investigating, and an Open incident button. Beside the
            stage a 320px caster desk holds Error rate and Latency cards with
            coloured top edges. At the foot, two ticker rows with yellow Alerts
            and Deploys labels list items in segments. Below 1100px the desk
            moves under the stage, below 760px blocks lose their skew and stack
            and tickers become lists.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px gutter, 16px between stage and desk, 10px between scoreboard blocks, 16px ticker segment padding.
        density: Medium. Five big scores on top, one big stage, two desk cards and two ticker rows.
        corners: None. Blocks are parallelograms skewed 14 degrees and the primary button is a clipped slant.
        borders: A 4px team colour underline per score block, 4px colour tops on desk cards, a 2px highlight rule over each ticker.
        shadows: None. Depth comes from a navy spotlight gradient behind everything.
        icons:
            Filled status shapes beside the word, a circle for Healthy, a
            triangle for Degraded, a diamond for Recovered, an octagon for
            Firing, a square for Resolved and a magnifier for Investigating.
            Teams are three letter codes, deploys use an upload arrow.
        focus: A 3px highlight yellow outline offset 3px. Slanted buttons drop their clip while focused so the ring shows.
        tone: Broadcast captions in italic caps such as LIVE, Scoreboard uptime, INCIDENT and Peak 9,400.
    style316:
        number: 316
        run: 64
        screen: OpsMonitor
        name: Night metro
        idea: The monitor drawn as a night transit map, where each service is a coloured line running across the last 24 hours, deploys and alerts are stations on it, and trouble shows as dashed track and an amber disruption sign.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/316.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            night: #0b1016, the page
            platform: #131a23, panels and the style sheet
            platformRaised: #1b2430, line pills and list rows
            mapWell: #0e141c, the slightly lighter well behind the map
            ink: #f1f5f9, text, the current app pill and the primary button
            muted: #a7b3c4, meta, axis times and the legend
            rail: #2c3746, borders, dashed rules and the hour grid on the map
            lineApi: #4fb3ff, the api line, the header roundel and the request chart
            lineWeb: #ff8a3d, the web line and the p95 line
            lineSync: #3ddc9c, the sync-worker line
            lineNotif: #c792ff, the notifications line and the p50 line
            lineBilling: #ffd23f, the billing line
            healthy: #5ee39a, Healthy and Resolved with circle and square
            degraded: #ffc94d, Degraded and Investigating with triangle and magnifier, and notice times
            recovered: #7cc4ff, Recovered with a diamond, and links
            firing: #ff7b84, Firing octagon stations and the error line
            signAmber: #ffc94d, the disruption band with dark text
        type:
            Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Segoe UI, Arial, signage style. Base 15px
            at 1.5. The incident ID is 28px at 800, the station name 20px at
            700, panel titles 17px at 700, notice times 14px at 700 with tabular
            numbers in amber, map labels 11px at 600.
        layout:
            A near black station sign header with a roundel mark, a ring with
            a bar through it reading OPS, the Brightwork Ops name and Production
            network last 24 hours, and the suite apps as outlined pills with a
            white filled pill for Ops. Below, a full width Service lines panel
            holds the map in a scrollable well. Down the left, five lettered
            bullets A, W, S, N, B with the service name and its status shape,
            word and uptime. Five thick horizontal lines run from 10 yesterday
            to now across an hour grid. Deploys are white circle stations,
            resolved alerts white squares, the firing queue alert a red
            octagon. sync-worker turns to dashed track from the firing alert to
            now, billing has a short break with a dotted white gap and a down 6
            min note. A legend explains clear track, dashed track, break,
            deploy, resolved and firing. Next comes a row of three, an amber
            Service disruption severity 2 sign with INC-0427 and its facts and
            pill buttons, a Service notices board for alerts, and a Timetable
            changes board for deploys, each item with a lettered line pill. A
            final row of three panels holds Requests per minute, Error rate and
            Latency, each with a lettered bullet, a big figure and a thick round
            capped line chart. Below 980px rows stack, below 760px the map
            scrolls sideways inside its well.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px page gutter, 20px panel padding and gaps, 60px between map lines.
        density: Medium. One wide map, then two rows of three panels.
        corners: 14px panels, full pills for buttons, fields, list rows and app tabs, round line bullets.
        borders: 1px rail borders on panels and dashed rules between notices. Map lines are 10px thick with round caps.
        shadows: None. The map sits on a slightly lighter well.
        icons:
            Lettered line bullets A, W, S, N, B. Map stations are a white
            circle for deploys, a white square for resolved and a red octagon
            for firing. Status words pair with a filled circle, triangle,
            diamond, octagon, square or a magnifier.
        focus: A 3px white outline offset 2px with a 6px blue halo.
        tone: Transit signage such as Service lines, Service disruption, Service notices and Timetable changes, with plain facts after.
    style317:
        number: 317
        run: 64
        screen: OpsMonitor
        name: Witch hour
        idea: A deep purple night watch where services stand as potion bottles on a shelf filled to their uptime, charts sit in arched windows under a thin moon, and green glows only where things are well.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/317.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            midnight: #150c21, the page under a faint violet glow at top right
            robe: #20132e, arched windows, cards, bottle tags and the style sheet
            robeRaised: #2a1a3c, the incident card, the current tab and list rows
            ink: #f4edff, text
            mist: #c2b3da, captions, times and axis
            line: #4b3668, borders, rules and the log thread
            shelf: #3a2752, the shelf plank under the bottles
            potionGreen: #7cf0a8, healthy potion, the glowing request line, p50, the primary button, focus, Healthy and Resolved
            violet: #c7a2ff, the moon mark, stars, p95, log beads and the secondary button border
            amber: #ffcb6b, degraded potion, Degraded and Investigating with triangle and magnifier
            moonblue: #8fd3ff, recovered potion, Recovered with a diamond
            rose: #ff94a7, Firing with an octagon, the error line
        type:
            Headings in Palatino Linotype, Book Antiqua, Palatino, Georgia at
            600, body in Gill Sans, Segoe UI, Calibri. Base 16px at 1.5. The
            incident ID is 30px serif, the brand 26px serif with an italic 15px
            subtitle, section titles 21px serif, uptime figures 22px serif with
            old style numbers, captions 14 to 15px italic serif.
        layout:
            A centred 1120px column. The header holds a violet crescent moon
            with a small green star, Brightwork Ops with the italic line The
            night watch over production, last 24 hours, and the suite apps with
            a green underline on Ops. The first section, The shelf of services,
            shows five flask bottles standing on a purple plank. Each flask is
            filled to its uptime on a 99 to 100 percent scale, green for
            healthy, amber for degraded with bubbles, pale blue for recovered
            with a small crack. A string hangs from each bottle to a tag card
            with the service name, status shape and word, the figure and one
            fact. A caption says how the fill is read and that billing shows its
            outage. Next, two columns. The left is an arched window with stars
            and a moon holding Requests per minute as a glowing green area
            chart with an italic 9,400 note. The right holds the incident card
            with a double rule, INC-0427, its facts and two pill buttons, then
            The night log, a thread of alerts with violet beads. Last, three
            small arched windows for Error rate, Latency and Fresh brews, the
            deploys. Below 900px columns stack, below 760px bottles sit left of
            their tags in rows with a plank under each.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px gutters and gaps, 22px card padding, bottles on a 16px grid.
        density: Airy. Five bottles across, one big arched chart, then three small arches.
        corners: Arched tops on chart windows using 260 by 120px elliptical corners with 12px at the foot. 12px cards, 20px pill buttons, 10px fields.
        borders: 1px violet grey lines. The incident card has a double rule made by an inset outline.
        shadows: No drop shadows. The request line glows green and the shelf has a hard 6px dark edge below it.
        icons:
            Flask bottles filled to uptime and a crescent moon mark. Status
            pairs the word with a filled circle, triangle, diamond, octagon,
            square or a magnifier.
        focus: A 2px potion green outline offset 3px with a soft green halo.
        tone: Lightly storybook headings such as The shelf of services, The night log and Fresh brews, with plain facts underneath.
    style318:
        number: 318
        run: 64
        screen: OpsMonitor
        name: Ember
        idea: A calm fireside monitor on near black, where the day's traffic rises as a glowing ember curve, service cards warm from below, and one merged timeline of alerts, deploys and the incident reads like a log by the fire.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/318.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            hearth: #0c0705, the page
            coal: #170e0a, the hero, service cards, chart cards and the style sheet
            coalRaised: #21140e, the incident card and list rows
            ink: #fbeee2, text
            ash: #caa995, meta, axis and labels
            sootLine: #3b261c, borders and grid
            ember: #ff7a3d, glows, the dotted p95 line, the current link underline, the foot of the primary button and the focus halo
            flame: #ffb347, the request line, p50, eyebrows, deploy marks and the focus outline
            deepRed: #b8321a, radial glows only, at low strength behind text
            healthy: #b8e68f, Healthy and Resolved with circle and square
            degraded: #ffc857, Degraded and Investigating with triangle and magnifier
            recovered: #e9c9a0, Recovered with a diamond
            firing: #ff7466, Firing with an octagon and the error line
        type:
            Avenir Next, Avenir, Segoe UI, Helvetica Neue, Arial. Base 16px at
            1.55. The hero figure is 72px at 200, the incident ID 40px at 200,
            service uptimes 32px at 200, section titles 20px at 600, meta 13px.
        layout:
            A single centred 1040px column. A slim header holds a two tone
            flame mark, Brightwork Ops, the suite apps as plain text links at
            right with an ember underline on Ops, and a Production last 24 hours
            pill. The hero is a large 28px rounded card with a deep red bloom
            rising from its lower left. It reads Requests per minute, a huge
            light 9,400 with peak at the afternoon, a calm sentence about the
            quiet night and the current 7,700, then a full width area chart
            whose fill fades from flame to ember to deep red, with a pill
            marking the peak. Below, Services as five rounded cards whose
            bottoms glow warmer for services that need attention, each with the
            name, an outline status shape and word, a light uptime figure and
            one fact. Then two columns, a glowing incident card with INC-0427
            and its facts and buttons, and Since last night, one merged timeline
            newest first of deploys, billing recovered, alerts and the incident
            opening, each with its own shape. Last, two cards for Error rate and
            Latency. Below 960px the two columns stack, below 760px cards go two
            across with billing full width.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px gutter, 48px between blocks, 20 to 36px inside cards.
        density: Roomy. One hero chart, five cards, two blocks and two small charts in a 1040px column.
        corners: Soft. 28px hero and sheet, 20 to 24px cards, 14px buttons and fields, round pills.
        borders: 1px soot lines. The incident card has a deeper red brown border.
        shadows: Warm glows instead of drop shadows. A low orange bloom under the hero and incident, a 6px glow on the request line.
        icons:
            Few. A two tone flame mark. Status as outline circle, triangle and
            diamond on cards, filled square, octagon and diamond in the
            timeline, an arrow on a base for deploys, always with the word.
        focus: A 2px flame outline offset 3px plus a soft ember halo.
        tone: Calm and warm, such as Since last night, Quiet through the night and 7,700 now.

    style319:
        number: 319
        run: 65
        screen: OpsMonitor
        name: Stained glass night
        idea: The whole monitor is one leaded window seen at night, with deep jewel glass panes held in thick black lead, an arched head pane for traffic, five round arched lancets for the services, and pale glowing text on every pane.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/319.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            night: #08070b, the page
            lead: #020203, the window frame, the gaps between panes, roundel rims and list rules
            ink: #f7f1e6, text on every pane
            pale: #d7cdbd, captions, times and axis on every pane
            ruby: #3b0f1d, the incident pane and the sync-worker lancet
            sapphire: #0f1f45, the head pane, the api lancet and the current app
            emerald: #0b3424, the latency pane and the web lancet
            amethyst: #2b1547, the error pane and the notifications lancet
            amberGlass: #3b2608, the alerts pane, the billing lancet and list rows
            slateGlass: #1a1a22, the deploys pane and the style sheet
            gold: #f2d27a, the request line, p95, the primary button and focus
            healthy: #a8f0c0, Healthy and Resolved with circle and square, and p50
            degraded: #ffd98a, Degraded and Investigating with triangle and magnifier
            recovered: #b8daff, Recovered with a diamond
            firing: #ffb5bf, Firing with an octagon and the error line
        type:
            Iowan Old Style, Palatino Linotype, Palatino, Book Antiqua, Georgia.
            Base 16px at 1.5. The incident ID is 32px, the brand 24px small caps
            tracked 0.08em, pane titles 18px at 600 in small caps tracked 0.1em,
            captions 15px italic, figures with lining numbers.
        layout:
            A header with a quatrefoil mark of four jewel discs and a gold
            centre, Brightwork Ops in small caps with an italic subtitle, and
            the suite apps at right where Ops sits on sapphire with a gold
            underline. Below, one window in a 1200px column. A black lead frame
            with a wide elliptical arched top holds every pane with 6px lead
            gaps. The arched sapphire head pane shows Requests per minute with
            an italic caption and a gold area line chart. Under it, five round
            arched lancets in sapphire, emerald, ruby, amethyst and amber, each
            with a leaded roundel holding the filled status shape, the service
            name, the status word in small caps, a figure and one fact. Then a
            row of three panes, ruby for the open incident with INC-0427, its
            facts and two leaded buttons, amethyst for Error rate and emerald
            for Latency. Then a row of two, amber Alerts and slate Deploys, with
            3px lead rules between rows. A grey sill bar sits under the window.
            Each pane carries a faint diagonal sheen. Below 1000px lancets go
            three across, below 760px two across with billing full width, the
            arch flattens and rows stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 6px lead between panes, 20 to 22px pane padding, 56px top padding under the arch.
        density: Medium. One head pane, five lancets, then rows of three and two panes.
        corners: The frame and head pane share one wide elliptical arch, lancets have round arched tops, everything else is square.
        borders: Lead does the work, a 6px black lead around and between panes, 3px lead between list rows and around buttons.
        shadows: None inside. A faint cool glow around the whole window and a sill bar beneath it.
        icons:
            A quatrefoil mark. Status shapes sit in leaded roundels on the
            lancets, circle, triangle and diamond, and beside the word in lists,
            octagon, square and magnifier.
        focus: A 3px gold outline, a black gap and a second thin gold ring, like a leaded border.
        tone: Quiet and formal, small caps headings and italic captions.
    style320:
        number: 320
        run: 65
        screen: OpsMonitor
        name: Observatory
        idea: A night observatory console where the last 24 hours are a round sky chart with traffic as a glowing contour and events as numbered marks on the rim, beside monospaced telescope readouts for each service.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/320.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            nightSky: #04060d, the page with a sparse field of tiny stars
            console: #0a0f1e, panels and the style sheet
            consoleRaised: #111833, list rows
            ink: #e7ecff, text
            muted: #9ea9c9, labels, axis and times
            graticule: #26304d, borders, dashed rings and rules
            instrumentCyan: #7fd4ff, the traffic contour, object names, deploy stars, p50, the current app, buttons and panel corner ticks
            starGold: #ffd27a, the peak star, the incident ID, p95, Degraded and Investigating
            nightRed: #ff8b8b, the error line, firing and spike marks, Firing words and focus
            healthy: #8be0b0, Healthy and Resolved with circle and square
            recovered: #a8ccff, Recovered with a diamond
        type:
            Body in ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas at 14px and 1.55.
            Titles in Futura, Century Gothic, Trebuchet MS at 600 in caps,
            panel titles 13px tracked 0.22em, the sheet title 22px tracked
            0.16em. The incident ID is 24px mono in gold, readings 22px mono,
            axis and dial labels 10 to 11px mono.
        layout:
            A header with a thin telescope mark, BRIGHTWORK OPS in tracked
            geometric caps over a mono line production window 24 h, and the
            suite apps in a bordered segmented strip with Ops filled cyan. A
            two column grid follows. Left is the 24 hour sky panel, a round
            polar chart where time runs clockwise from 10 yesterday at the top,
            dashed rings mark 2.5k to 10k requests per minute, and the traffic
            contour is a translucent cyan shape widest at the afternoon peak
            with a gold peak star. Numbered marks sit on two rims, deploy stars
            inside and alert shapes outside, and a key plus a numbered Rim
            events list explain them. Right is a Service readouts table with
            Object, Status, Uptime and Reading columns in mono, then Incident
            under watch as a definition list with INC-0427 in gold and two
            buttons. A full width row of three strips holds Error rate, Latency
            and an Observation log of alerts and deploys. Panels are near opaque
            with cyan corner ticks at top left and bottom right. Below 1000px the
            columns stack, below 760px the strips stack and the readout table
            scrolls inside its panel.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px gutter and gaps, 18 by 20px panel padding, 10px table cell padding.
        density: Medium dense. A large dial, a five row readout table and three strips.
        corners: 2px panels and controls. The dial and swatches are round.
        borders: 1px graticule borders with cyan corner ticks, dashed rules between rows.
        shadows: None. Panels sit nearly opaque over the star field.
        icons:
            A thin telescope mark. On the dial, four point stars for deploys,
            squares for resolved, an octagon for firing and a triangle for the
            error spike, each numbered. In text, filled circle, triangle,
            diamond, octagon and square, and a magnifier, with the word.
        focus: A 2px night red outline offset 3px with a faint red halo.
        tone: Instrument log terms such as 24 hour sky, Service readouts, Object, Reading and Incident under watch.
    style321:
        number: 321
        run: 65
        screen: OpsMonitor
        name: NOC wall
        idea: A network operations video wall where every block is a square cornered screen split by black bezels, with huge status words, giant figures and thick chart lines that can be read from across the room.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/321.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            bezel: #000000, the page and the 4px gaps between screens
            screen: #13161b, every tile and the style sheet
            screenRaised: #1c2027, the title strip, swatch tiles and list rows
            ink: #ffffff, names, figures and IDs
            muted: #b7bfcb, tile titles, notes and axis
            rule: #2c323c, the neutral band, grid lines and row rules
            signalBlue: #38bdf8, the request line, p50, the current app, the primary button, the deploys band and the focus ring
            healthy: #4ade80, the Healthy band, word and circle, and Resolved with a square
            degraded: #fbbf24, the Degraded band, word and triangle, the incident band, p95 and Investigating
            recovered: #7cb8ff, the Recovered band, word and diamond
            firing: #ff7a7a, Firing with an octagon, the error and alerts bands and the error line
        type:
            Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial at 600 to 800. Base 16px at
            1.35. The incident ID is 60px at 800, service figures scale from 40
            to 52px at 800 with tabular numbers, status words scale from 22 to
            34px at 800 in caps, service names 30px at 800, notes 20px, tile
            titles 18px caps tracked 0.08em.
        layout:
            A full bleed six column wall with 4px black bezels and no outer
            margin. A raised title strip holds BRIGHTWORK OPS, PRODUCTION LAST
            24 H and the suite apps as flat blocks with Ops in signal blue. A
            row of five service screens follows, each with a 10px status band on
            top in green, amber or blue, the name, a huge status shape and word,
            a giant uptime figure and one fact, billing showing 6 MIN DOWN. Then
            a four column Requests per minute screen with a 44px peak figure and
            a 6px line chart, beside a two column incident screen with an amber
            band, a 60px INC-0427, the title, status, opened, owner and large
            buttons. Then Error rate and Latency screens with big figures and
            5px lines, and an Alerts screen with a red band. A full width
            Deploys screen with a blue band lists the three deploys with 32px
            times. Below 1180px services go three across and charts widen,
            below 760px every screen stacks in one column.
        spacing: 4px bezels between every screen, 18 to 20px tile padding, no outer margin beyond one bezel.
        density: Low in items and high in size. Every tile holds one idea at wall scale.
        corners: None anywhere, like display panels.
        borders: A 10px status band across the top of each tile in green, amber, blue or red, and 2px rules inside lists.
        shadows: None. Black bezels separate screens.
        icons:
            Filled status shapes at about 1.3 times the status word, a circle
            for Healthy, a triangle for Degraded, a diamond for Recovered, an
            octagon for Firing, a square for Resolved and a magnifier for
            Investigating. Chart lines are 5 to 6px.
        focus: An inset 4px white ring plus an 8px signal blue inner ring, drawn inside tiles so bezels never hide it.
        tone: Short caps labels for distance, such as INCIDENT SEVERITY 2, PEAK and MS P95.
    style322:
        number: 322
        run: 65
        screen: OpsMonitor
        name: Dark spreadsheet
        idea: The monitor as a dark workbook, with a formula bar, lettered columns and numbered rows holding services, the incident, alerts and deploys as ranges, conditional formatted status cells, floating chart objects and sheet tabs along the foot.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/322.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            app: #18191c, the page, menu bar and tabs
            grid: #1f2125, cells, chart objects and the style sheet
            header: #2a2c31, column letters, row numbers and chart title bars
            cellLine: #383b42, every cell border
            ink: #e8eaed, cell text
            muted: #a8adb5, header rows, axis and the status bar
            selection: #5aa2ff, the selected cell outline and fill handle, function names in the formula, the request line, the primary button and focus
            selectionFill: #22324a, the selected cell background
            healthy: #7ad99a, Healthy and Resolved text with circle and square on a #1d2e24 cell fill
            degraded: #f2c45a, Degraded and Investigating with triangle and magnifier on a #33291a cell fill
            recovered: #90c2ff, Recovered with a diamond on a #1d2a3b cell fill
            firing: #ff8f86, Firing with an octagon on a #3a2121 cell fill, and the error line
        type:
            Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial at 13px and 1.4 for cells,
            ui-monospace, Consolas, Menlo for numbers at 12.5px tabular and for
            the formula at 13px. Range titles 14px at 700, header rows 13px at
            600 muted, column letters 12px at 600.
        layout:
            A menu bar with a green B document tile, Brightwork Ops and
            production last 24 hours read only, and the suite apps at right. A
            toolbar with Refresh, Filter, an Open INC-0427 button and a
            Conditional format status note. A formula bar shows the cell
            reference C5, an italic fx and the formula UPTIME of sync-worker
            over 24h. The work area splits into a scrollable grid and a 380px
            column of chart objects. The grid has letters A to G and rows 1 to
            22. Row 1 is the range title, row 2 the header, rows 3 to 7 the five
            services with Status, Uptime, p95 ms, Queue depth, Down and
            Recovered. C5 is selected with a blue outline and fill handle. Rows
            9 and 10 hold the incident, rows 12 to 15 the alerts with merged
            Condition cells, rows 17 to 20 the deploys, rows 21 and 22 a summary
            of peak, night low, error rate and the spike. Status cells use
            conditional fills plus shape and word. Chart objects have title bars
            with SERIES formulas for requests, error rate and latency. Sheet
            tabs sit along the foot with Overview current and a green underline,
            and a status bar shows the selection. Below 1100px charts move under
            the grid, below 760px the grid scrolls inside its region.
        spacing: A 4px unit. 26px rows, 8px cell padding, 12px around chart objects.
        density: Very dense. Twenty two rows of facts plus three charts on one laptop screen.
        corners: Square cells. 2 to 3px on buttons, chart objects and the document tile.
        borders: 1px cell lines everywhere, 2px under header rows, a 2px blue outline on the selected cell.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            16px line icons in the toolbar. Status cells use a conditional fill
            plus a filled circle, triangle, diamond, octagon or square, or an
            outline magnifier, with the word.
        focus: A 2px selection blue outline offset 1px with a soft blue halo.
        tone: Workbook terms such as ranges, formulas, Count 5 and Min uptime 99.41%.
    style323:
        number: 323
        run: 65
        screen: OpsMonitor
        name: Night paper
        idea: The monitor typeset as a short evening report on warm dark grey paper, a serif reading column with a summary headline, inline sparklines in the prose, a leader dotted service list, numbered figures, and alerts and deploys as margin notes.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/323.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            paper: #29251f, the page and every surface including the style sheet
            paperShade: #322d26, a rare tint kept for hover
            ink: #ebe2d2, text, the request line, p50 and the primary button
            pencil: #bcb09b, captions, times and small caps labels
            rule: #4d463c, hairlines, double rules, dot leaders and the chart grid
            rust: #e6a873, links, the dashed p95 line, the incident label, the secondary button and focus
            healthy: #acd6a2, Healthy and Resolved with outline circle and square
            degraded: #ecc47c, Degraded and Investigating with outline triangle and magnifier
            recovered: #adc9ea, Recovered with an outline diamond
            firing: #f2a89d, Firing with an outline octagon and the error line
        type:
            Charter, Bitstream Charter, Iowan Old Style, Sitka Text, Cambria,
            Georgia. Base 18px at 1.65. The headline is 40px at 400 and 1.15,
            the lead 20px, section labels 15px small caps tracked 0.14em in
            pencil, captions 15px italic, numbers old style.
        layout:
            A 1080px page with a 680px reading column and a 260px margin column
            56px apart. A masthead with Brightwork Ops in small caps, an italic
            Production the last twenty four hours, and the suite apps as small
            text links joined by middots with Ops underlined in rust, all over a
            hairline. The headline reads A steady day, one open incident on
            sync-worker. The lead paragraph gives the traffic range with a small
            inline sparkline and the error spike with a red sparkline, notes the
            billing outage, and names the degraded service and INC-0427. A
            Services section lists each service in italic with a dotted leader
            to its status shape, word and uptime, and a smaller note line for
            p95, queue depth or recovery. The open incident sits between double
            rules with a rust small caps label, the ID at 26px, a sentence of
            facts and Investigating, then Open the incident and Read the
            runbook. Figures holds a wide Figure 1 for requests and two smaller
            Figures 2 and 3 for error rate and latency, each with an italic
            caption. The margin column carries Alerts and Deploys as notes with
            italic times. Below 1000px margin notes drop under the article.
        spacing: An 8px unit. A 680px column, a 56px gutter, a 260px margin column, and 32 to 40px between sections.
        density: Low. One reading column where facts arrive as sentences, a short list and three figures.
        corners: None. Only the swatches are round.
        borders: Hairline rules above sections, a double rule around the incident and dotted leaders in the service list.
        shadows: None. The paper is flat.
        icons:
            Almost none. Small outline status shapes sit inline before the
            word, circle, triangle, diamond, octagon, square and magnifier.
            Sparklines sit in the prose.
        focus: A 2px dotted rust outline offset 4px with a faint warm wash.
        tone: Plain sentences such as A steady day, one open incident on sync-worker, and Read the runbook.

    style324:
        number: 324
        run: 66
        screen: MusicPlayer
        name: Pro streaming
        idea: A polished, generic dark streaming app with a big square cover art block leading the page, clean edge to edge lists, one warm coral accent and a fixed player bar along the bottom.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/324.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            base: #0f1012, the page, the main column and the style sheet
            rail: #16171a, the library sidebar and the queue column
            card: #1f2125, playlist tiles, the lyrics card, hover rows and the player bar
            line: #2e3137, row dividers, the seek track and field borders
            ink: #f3f4f6, titles and body text
            muted: #a9aeb8, artists, durations, counts and labels
            coral: #ff8463, the play button, the seek fill, the liked heart and focus
            onCoral: #1d0a04, the icon and text on coral
            coralSoft: #3a211b, the current lyric line wash and the selected nav item
        type:
            One system stack, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
            Arial. Base 15px at 1.5. The song title is 60px at 800 with
            minus 0.03em tracking, the artist 20px at 600, list titles 15px at
            600, meta 13px with tabular figures, and caps labels 11px at 700
            with 0.12em tracking.
        layout:
            Three columns over a player bar. A 232px rail holds a round coral B
            mark with Brightwork Sound, three nav links with Now playing
            selected on the soft coral tile, a Playlists label over three rows
            with small square art and song counts, and pill links for Albums,
            Artists and Podcasts. The main column opens with a 280px square
            cover of a harbour at night with a row of lights and the words LOW
            TIDE, beside a caps Now playing label, the huge title, the artist,
            From the album Low Tide and a pill reading Liked with a filled
            heart. Below sits a Lyrics card with the current line on the soft
            coral wash behind a small arrow and the next line in muted grey. A
            320px right column lists Up next as numbered rows with title,
            artist and duration. The full width player bar repeats a mini cover
            and title, centres shuffle, previous, a round coral pause button,
            next and repeat above a thin seek line with elapsed and total
            time, and puts a volume line with 70% on the right. Below 1100px
            the queue moves under the main column. Below 760px everything
            stacks with the player bar first and sticky at the top.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px gutters, 16px card padding, about 56px queue rows and an 88px player bar.
        density: Medium. One hero, five queue rows and a short library, nothing crowded.
        corners: 8px cards and cover art, 4px fields, round play button, pills and avatars.
        borders: Almost none. Surfaces step from base to rail to card, with 1px line dividers between queue rows.
        shadows: One deep soft shadow under the cover art, 0 24px 48px black at 50 percent, and nothing else.
        icons:
            Solid transport glyphs and rounded 2px line icons for the nav. The
            liked heart is filled coral and always carries the word Liked. The
            current lyric line has an arrow as well as the wash.
        focus: A 2px coral outline offset 3px, round on round controls.
        tone: Short and familiar, such as Now playing, Up next, Your library and Liked.
    style325:
        number: 325
        run: 66
        screen: MusicPlayer
        name: Spectrum analyser
        idea: The bars and peak caps of a live frequency analyser run the whole layout, so every figure on the page, from progress to volume to song length, is drawn as lime and cyan level bars on black.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/325.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            void: #040605, the page, the analyser well and the style sheet
            well: #0a110c, panels and readout strips
            grid: #1b2b20, graticule lines, unlit segments and panel borders
            phosphor: #e3f4e6, text
            dim: #8fa897, labels, units and axis text
            lime: #b8ff3d, analyser bars, lit progress segments, the lyric marker and focus
            cyan: #46e6ff, peak caps, song length bars, the volume segments and the liked control
            onLime: #0b1400, text on lime
        type:
            One monospace stack, ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas,
            Liberation Mono. Base 14px at 1.5. The title is 40px at 700 in caps
            with 0.02em tracking, readouts 16px at 700 in lime with tabular
            figures, rows 14px, caps labels 12px with 0.14em tracking and axis
            figures 11px.
        layout:
            A test instrument. A ruled header strip reads BRIGHTWORK SOUND in
            lime then Analyser, with CH A+B and Now playing on the right. Under
            it a full width analyser well 260px tall draws 32 lime bars with a
            darker base and a cyan peak cap above each, over faint graticule
            lines, with dB marks down the right edge. The title box sits in the
            top left corner of the well, black with ruled edges, holding Now
            playing, HARBOUR LIGHTS and the artist with the album dimmed. A
            frequency scale from 31 to 16k Hz runs under the well. A transport
            strip follows, with 02 14 in lime, a 48 segment progress bar lit
            to just under half and 04 38, then square buttons each with an icon
            over a short caps word, SHUF, PREV, a lime PAUSE, NEXT, RPT and a
            cyan outlined LIKED with a filled heart. A LEVEL row shows ten
            cyan segments with seven lit and 70%. Three ruled panels close the
            screen. Up next lists numbered rows whose cyan bar length is the
            song length, Src library gives each playlist a lime bar sized by
            song count plus caps links for Albums, Artists and Podcasts, and
            Lyrics shows the current line bold behind a lime chevron with a
            NOW tag and the next line dim. Below 980px the queue takes a full
            row, and below 640px the title box moves under the bars, the
            progress shows 24 segments and everything stacks.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 2px gaps between segments and bars, 16px panel padding and 16px between panels.
        density: High. Readouts, scales and segment meters fill every panel like test gear.
        corners: None. Every bar, segment, button and panel is square.
        borders: 1px grid lines around every panel and behind the analyser. Coloured borders appear only on the liked control and on focus.
        shadows: None, apart from a faint lime glow of 6px at 35 percent under the analyser bars.
        icons:
            Solid square cut transport glyphs above a four letter caps word.
            Liked uses a filled heart and the word LIKED. The current lyric
            line uses a chevron and a NOW tag. Bars always sit beside the
            figure they draw.
        focus: A 2px lime outline offset 2px plus a lime corner tick at the bottom right.
        tone: Instrument labels in caps, such as CH A+B, LEVEL, UP NEXT and SRC LIBRARY.
    style326:
        number: 326
        run: 66
        screen: MusicPlayer
        name: Vinyl lounge
        idea: A walnut turntable plinth fills half the screen with a spinning record drawn in SVG, a brass tonearm in the grooves, brass knobs for volume and a crate of record spines for the queue, all in warm serif type.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/326.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            lounge: #1a110b, the page and the style sheet
            walnut: #2e1c11, the plinth, grained with walnutDark stripes
            walnutDark: #24160d, grain stripes, cards and the crate shelf
            groove: #121010, the record and inset wells
            cream: #f2e6cf, text and the record label
            parchment: #cdb795, artists, times and captions
            brass: #d9ab5f, the tonearm, knobs, engraved labels, the liked heart and rules
            onBrass: #26170a, glyphs and text on brass
            sleeve: #5a3b2a, one of five muted sleeve tints on the crate spines, decorative only
        type:
            One serif stack, Iowan Old Style, Palatino Linotype, Palatino, Book
            Antiqua, Georgia. Base 16px at 1.55. The title is 56px italic at
            400, the current lyric 22px, body 16px, engraved labels 12px at 600
            in caps with 0.2em tracking in brass, and times 14px with oldstyle
            figures.
        layout:
            Two columns on a lounge brown page. On the left a walnut plinth
            with a brass inlay line holds an engraved Brightwork Sound, Side A
            label and 33 rpm, then the turntable drawn in SVG, a black platter
            with fine grooves and a cream label reading Low Tide and SALTMARSH
            TRIO, slowly turning, with a brass tonearm from a round pivot
            resting in the outer grooves and a small pitch slider. A thin brass
            rail shows the elapsed and total time with a cream dot. A dark
            inset strip below holds three round brass buttons for previous, a
            larger pause and next, two slide switches labelled Shuffle Off and
            Repeat Off, and a brass rotary knob ringed by ticks pointing at 70
            with the word Volume. On the right sit the engraved Now spinning,
            the italic title, the artist with from Low Tide, and a pill
            reading Liked with a brass heart. Then a Liner notes card with a
            brass left edge shows the current line large behind a note sign
            and the next line in smaller italic. The crate lists the queue as
            record spines, each with a coloured sleeve edge, an italic brass
            number, title, artist and time. Shelves shows the three playlists
            as brass edged nameplates and underlined links for Albums, Artists
            and Podcasts. Below 980px the columns stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit used generously, 28px plinth padding and 24px between cards.
        density: Low. The turntable takes half the screen and every list stays short.
        corners: 12px plinth and cards, round knobs and buttons, 3px spines, 6px nameplates.
        borders: 1px brass hairlines at half strength on nameplates and the control strip, and a 2px brass inlay inside the plinth edge.
        shadows: A deep 0 18px 40px black under the plinth and small drop shadows under the brass buttons.
        icons:
            Solid glyphs engraved in dark brown on round brass buttons.
            Toggles are slide switches with the words Off or On beside them.
            The liked heart is filled brass beside the word Liked.
        focus: A 2px cream outline offset 3px with a 6px brass glow.
        tone: Lounge words, such as Now spinning, Side A, The crate, Liner notes and Shelves.
    style327:
        number: 327
        run: 66
        screen: MusicPlayer
        name: Club LED
        idea: The screen is a wall of LED modules in a black housing, with the title spelled in round lit dots on a matrix, a strip of colour blocks that pulse to the beat and square light pads for every control.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/327.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            housing: #060507, the page, the gaps between modules and the style sheet
            module: #121015, module faces and unlit pads, with a fine dot texture
            dotOff: #2a1226, unlit title dots, with unlit progress and volume dots in #241f2b
            edge: #2d2733, module borders and unlit pad rims
            ink: #f6eef6, text
            haze: #ad9fb0, labels and meta
            magenta: #ff5bd9, the title matrix, the liked pad, playlist counts and focus
            amber: #ffb22e, the clock matrix, the current lyric and the pause pad
            cyan: #3fe0ff, progress dots, the volume column, queue bullets and durations
            onColour: #140510, text on lit pads
        type:
            A monospace stack, ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas, for all text.
            Base 14px at 1.5. The title and the clock are not type but a 5 by 7
            dot matrix drawn in SVG with a 10px pitch. The current lyric is
            clamp 18 to 26px at 700 in caps with 0.08em tracking, queue titles
            15px at 700 in caps, and labels 12px in caps with 0.2em tracking.
        layout:
            A twelve column wall of modules with 4px black gaps. Module 01
            spans eight columns with Brightwork Sound and a magenta On air lamp,
            then HARBOUR over LIGHTS in magenta dots with every unlit dot still
            visible, then the artist and the album in caps. Module 02, the
            Clock, spells 2 14 in amber dots over of 4 38 and a row of 40 cyan
            dots lit to just under half. A full width strip of twelve colour
            blocks in magenta, amber and cyan pulses gently. The Pads module is
            a three by two grid of square pads, SHUFFLE OFF, PREV, an amber
            lit PAUSE PLAYING, NEXT, REPEAT OFF and a magenta lit LIKED ON. A
            narrow Level module holds a column of ten round cyan dots with
            seven lit from the bottom and 70%. Up next lists the five songs
            with a ringed cyan bullet, caps titles and cyan times on dashed
            rules. Lyrics shows the current line in glowing amber caps on a
            dotted band behind a play arrow, with Next line and the second line
            in small caps beneath. Crates lists the playlists with magenta
            counts and caps chips for Albums, Artists and Podcasts. Below
            1000px every module takes a full row and the level column turns
            sideways. Below 560px the pulse strip shows six blocks.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 4px black gaps between modules, 16px inside a module and 8px between pads.
        density: Medium high. Many small modules, each with one job.
        corners: 4px modules and pads, perfect circles for every LED dot.
        borders: 1px edge around every module and 2px rims on pads, coloured when a pad is lit.
        shadows: Only light. Lit pads and dots glow with 16px of their own colour at 45 percent. No drop shadows.
        icons:
            Solid glyphs above a caps word on each pad. State is written on the
            pad, OFF, PLAYING or ON, and the liked pad adds a filled heart. The
            current lyric gets a play arrow.
        focus: A 2px magenta outline offset 3px with a matching magenta glow.
        tone: Club caps, such as ON AIR, PADS, LEVEL, UP NEXT and CRATES.
    style328:
        number: 328
        run: 66
        screen: MusicPlayer
        name: Concert stage
        idea: The player is a live stage seen from the crowd, with light beams falling from a truss, the song title lit in a spotlight, a crowd silhouette along the front and the queue taped down as a hand set list.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/328.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            backdrop: #0b0912, the page, the stage and the style sheet
            floor: #15121d, the control barrier, the set list card and the passes
            truss: #2f2a3a, the truss bar, borders and dividers
            houseLight: #f7f3ec, titles and body text
            haze: #b8b0c4, artists, times and labels
            spot: #ffcf5a, the spotlight pool, the pause button, the current set list row and focus
            onSpot: #1f1500, text on spot
            beamViolet: #8a5cff, decorative beams only, never behind text
            tape: #d8c48e, gaffer tape on the set list and the strap edge of each pass
        type:
            Titles use a condensed stack, Avenir Next Condensed, Arial Narrow,
            Roboto Condensed, Helvetica Neue, Arial, in caps at 800. Body uses
            Helvetica Neue and Arial at 15px. The title is clamp 52 to 104px
            with 0.92 line height, set list titles 26px, the lyric on screen
            32px at 600, pass names 22px, and caps labels 12px at 700 with
            0.24em tracking.
        layout:
            A stage over a control barrier, with a set list column on the
            right. The stage is about 560px tall, with a hatched truss bar and
            six glowing lamps across the top, five light beams in warm white
            and violet fanning down, a soft amber pool in the centre, then the
            caps line Brightwork Sound, On stage now, the huge condensed title,
            and the artist with Low Tide. A black crowd silhouette with some
            raised hands runs along the bottom edge. The barrier under the
            stage holds round outlined buttons with caps words beneath,
            Shuffle, Prev, a larger spot yellow Pause, Next, Repeat and Liked
            with a filled heart, then a thick progress rail with elapsed and
            total time, and Crowd volume as ten rising bars with seven lit and
            70%. The right column holds a slightly tilted dark card held by two
            tape strips, titled Tonight's set, with Harbour Lights first on a
            spot yellow band with a play arrow and Now, then the five queued
            songs in big condensed caps with numbers and times. A black screen
            band shows Lyrics on screen with the current line large behind a
            play arrow and the next line smaller. Backstage shows the three
            playlists as passes with a tape strap edge and a punched slot,
            plus caps links for Albums, Artists and Podcasts. Below 1060px the
            set list moves under the barrier, and below 560px everything
            stacks.
        spacing: An 8px unit. A tall stage, 20 to 32px section padding and 10px set list rows.
        density: Low on the stage, medium on the set list and the passes.
        corners: Square stage, barrier and set list, 4px passes, round transport buttons.
        borders: The truss bar with lamps across the top, 1px truss rules elsewhere, tape strips instead of a frame on the set list.
        shadows: None on boxes. Light does the work, an amber pool behind the title and beams at 18 to 20 percent.
        icons:
            Solid glyphs inside round outlined buttons with caps words below.
            Liked is a filled heart in a spot ring with the word Liked. The set
            list marks the current song with a play arrow and the word Now.
        focus: A 3px spot outline offset 3px.
        tone: Live show words, such as On stage now, Tonight's set, Lyrics on screen, Backstage and Crowd volume.

    style329:
        number: 329
        run: 67
        screen: MusicPlayer
        name: Hi-fi receiver
        idea: The player is a stack of hi-fi components in brushed dark aluminium, with a blue backlit LCD for the song and lyrics, a machined volume knob ringed by a lit arc, small LED push buttons and a tuner dial whose presets are the queue.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/329.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            rack: #0e0f11, the page, the gaps between components and the style sheet
            plate: #2a2c30, brushed faceplates, striped finely with #26282b and #2d2f33
            plateEdge: #45484e, bevels, button rims and the secondary button border
            engraving: #d6d9de, labels and button words on the plate
            etched: #a9aeb6, secondary labels and units on the plate
            lcd: #071a33, the display, the dial window and text fields
            backlight: #a6dcff, LCD text, lit LCD segments, the volume arc and the dial scale
            backlightDim: #6e9fc9, the next lyric line and unlit segment outlines
            ledAmber: #ffb84a, lit indicator LEDs, preset numbers and markers, and focus
            ledOff: #3b3e43, unlit indicator LEDs
            needle: #ff7a5c, the tuner needle marking the song now playing
        type:
            Two stacks. Engraved labels use Helvetica Neue and Arial, 12px at
            700 in caps with 0.2em tracking, with etched units at 11px and
            0.16em. The LCD uses ui-monospace, Menlo and Consolas, with the
            title at clamp 24 to 36px at 700 in caps, lines at 15px and a soft
            blue glow. Preset titles are 14px at 700.
        layout:
            A rack of three components with 8px gaps. The receiver has a 150px
            left column with Brightwork Sound, Stereo receiver and an amber
            Power on LED, a wide inset LCD in the middle, and a 200px volume
            knob on the right. The LCD reads NOW PLAYING and INPUT LIBRARY in
            small caps, then HARBOUR LIGHTS, the artist and album, a row of 32
            outlined segments with 15 filled, the elapsed and total time, and
            under a dashed rule the current lyric behind a play arrow with the
            next line dimmer. The knob is a machined dark disc with fine
            ridges and an amber dot, ringed by a blue arc lit to 70 percent,
            labelled Volume 70. Under a groove runs a row of small square keys,
            each with an icon cap and a word with an LED, Shuffle Off and
            Repeat Off on the left, Prev, a wider Pause with a lit LED and
            Next in the centre, and Liked On with a lit LED on the right. The
            tuner component shows Presets, Up next with 5 songs beside an
            LCD dial window with a fine blue scale, five amber preset marks
            numbered 1 to 5 and a coral needle before the first, then five
            raised preset buttons with an amber number, title, artist and
            time. The input component lists the playlists with song counts and
            Albums, Artists and Podcasts as raised selector buttons. Below
            980px the knob sits beside the LCD and presets wrap, and below
            620px everything stacks, the keys form a three column grid and the
            dial scrolls sideways inside its window.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 20 to 24px faceplate padding, 8px between components and 10px between keys.
        density: Medium. Each component holds one function, with tiny dense labels like real gear.
        corners: 4px plates, 2px keys and LCD windows, a round knob.
        borders: A light 1px top bevel and dark 1px bottom bevel on every plate and key, and a 2px dark ring around each LCD window.
        shadows: An inset shadow in each LCD window, a hard 0 2px 0 black step under keys and a soft blue glow on LCD text.
        icons:
            Small solid transport glyphs on key caps above engraved words.
            State is a round LED plus the word On or Off, lit amber when on.
            The current lyric has a play arrow.
        focus: A 2px amber outline offset 2px, matching the LEDs.
        tone: Engraved equipment words, such as Power on, Volume, Presets, Input and Shuffle Off.
    style330:
        number: 330
        run: 67
        screen: MusicPlayer
        name: Hard bop sleeve
        idea: The screen is laid out like a 1950s jazz record sleeve, with a huge tight sans title, flat blocks of orange, teal and mustard on near black, controls as coloured slabs and the queue listed as Side B on the back cover.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/330.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            sleeveBlack: #121110, the page, the cover ground and the style sheet
            board: #1d1b19, the back cover panel, plain slabs and list rows
            paperWhite: #f1ebdd, the title and body text, the block beside the artist and the progress fill
            greyPrint: #b1a998, credits, artists and small print
            orange: #e8742c, the artist block, track numbers, the current lyric and the primary button
            teal: #3a9e98, the album bar and the liked slab
            mustard: #e3b23c, the pause slab, the position dot and focus
            printBlack: #111111, text on orange, teal and mustard
            rule: #3a3631, dividers, with dot leaders in #6b645a
        type:
            One stack, Helvetica Neue, Arial Nova, Arial, heavy and tight. Base
            15px at 1.5. The title is clamp 52 to 108px at 900 in caps with
            0.82 line height and minus 0.06em tracking. Block text is 32px at
            900 in caps, back cover headings 28px at 900, the current lyric
            20px at 700 in orange, and credits 11px at 700 in caps with 0.3em
            tracking.
        layout:
            A sleeve and its back cover side by side. The cover sits on a six
            column grid. Small caps credits read Brightwork Sound and Now
            playing, then HARBOUR over LIGHTS fills five columns with three
            descending circles in mustard, orange and teal in the sixth. An
            orange block holds THE SALTMARSH TRIO in black beside a paper white
            block, then a small mustard square sits beside a teal bar reading
            LOW TIDE and From the album. A thick progress rule shows the
            elapsed time in bold, a paper white fill to just under half with a
            large mustard dot and the total in grey. Six slabs butt together in
            a row, each with a heavy icon above a caps word, Shuffle Off,
            Previous, a mustard Pause Playing, Next, Repeat Off and a teal Liked
            On with a filled heart. A Volume line in orange shows 70%. The
            back cover is a board panel with three sections, each with a small
            caps credit over a heavy heading. Up next, Side B lists B1 to B5
            in orange with caps titles, grey artists, dot leaders and bold
            times. Lyrics, Liner notes shows the current line in bold orange
            behind an arrow and the next line in grey. Your library, Also
            available lists the playlists on black rows with grey counts above
            three coloured blocks for Albums, Artists and Podcasts. Below 980px
            the back cover moves under the cover, and below 620px the slabs go
            three by two and the leaders drop.
        spacing: An 8px unit. Blocks butt together with 0 to 4px gaps, 20 to 32px inside blocks and 40px around the sleeve.
        density: Low on the cover, medium on the back cover list.
        corners: None, apart from the round position dot and the three circles.
        borders: None. Edges come from flat colour blocks meeting, with dotted leaders on the back cover only.
        shadows: None. Flat print.
        icons:
            Heavy solid glyphs on each slab above a caps word, with the state
            written underneath as Off, Playing or On. Liked is a filled heart.
            The current lyric gets a bold arrow.
        focus: A 3px mustard outline offset 3px, square.
        tone: Sleeve credits, such as Side B, Liner notes, Also available and From the album.
    style331:
        number: 331
        run: 67
        screen: MusicPlayer
        name: Ambient haze
        idea: A quiet room of soft blurred colour fog behind a single centred column, with light thin type, hairline progress and almost invisible controls, so the song and its words float and nothing asks for attention.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/331.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            nightAir: #0d0e13, the page, the room and the style sheet
            fogViolet: #4b3a6b, a blurred fog bank at the top left, decorative
            fogTeal: #24505a, a blurred fog bank at the right, decorative
            fogRose: #5a3346, a blurred fog bank at the bottom, decorative
            veil: #171820, frosted panels at about 72 percent over the fog
            mistLine: #3a3b48, hairlines, the progress track and field rules
            moon: #eeedf4, the title, the current lyric and primary text
            dusk: #b6b4c6, artists, times, labels and the waiting lyric
            glow: #c9b8ff, the progress dot, the liked heart, the play ring and focus
        type:
            One system stack, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
            mostly at weight 300. Base 16px at 1.6. The title is clamp 40 to
            60px at 200 with 0.01em tracking, the current lyric clamp 20 to
            28px at 300, the waiting lyric up to 20px, and lowercase labels
            13px at 400 with 0.08em tracking.
        layout:
            One centred column in a dark room. Three very large blurred colour
            fogs drift slowly behind everything, violet top left, teal right
            and rose low in the middle, clipped by the room. A faint top line
            reads brightwork sound and now playing in lowercase. After about
            90px of space comes from Low Tide, then Harbour Lights in thin
            large type and the artist. A 1px progress hairline runs between the
            elapsed and total time with a small glowing dot at just under half.
            The controls sit in one quiet row, line icons over small words,
            shuffle off, previous, a 64px thin glow ring with pause, next,
            repeat off and a filled heart over liked. A volume hairline with
            70% follows. Further down a lowercase words label sits over the
            current line in moon behind a small glow dot and the next line
            smaller in dusk. Two frosted panels with 24px corners close the
            page, after this with the five queued songs on hairline rows, and
            your library with the playlists and counts and underlined links
            for Albums, Artists and Podcasts. Below 820px the panels stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit used wide. About 90px above the title, 48 to 72px between groups and 28 to 32px panel padding.
        density: Very low. One column and five quiet rows, nothing competing.
        corners: 24px panels, a round play ring and pill buttons.
        borders: 1px mist line hairlines at most, often none.
        shadows: None. Depth comes from the fog and the frosted panels with a 20px backdrop blur.
        icons:
            Thin line icons at low emphasis with lowercase words beneath.
            Shuffle and repeat say off in words. Liked is a filled glow heart
            over the word liked. The current lyric has a small dot.
        focus: A 2px glow outline offset 4px with a soft 12px glow halo.
        tone: Soft lowercase labels, such as now playing, words, after this and your library.
    style332:
        number: 332
        run: 67
        screen: MusicPlayer
        name: Cassette deck
        idea: The player is a front loading cassette deck, with a tape window of turning reels, a mechanical counter, two amber VU meters with needles, a row of chrome piano keys for transport and the queue typed on the cassette insert card.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/332.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            deck: #151517, the page, the deck body and the style sheet
            ribbed: #1e1e21, body ribs, the insert card and the list row
            bezel: #3a3a3f, window, meter and counter bezels, and rules
            chrome: #c9ccd1, piano keys and toggle caps, as a gradient from #eceef0 to #a6aab0
            keyInk: #111214, legends printed on chrome
            legend: #e6e6ea, panel legends and text
            legendDim: #a8a8b2, units, small print and secondary lines
            meterAmber: #ffc56b, VU faces, the lyric memo, the playing lamp, the progress fill and focus
            peakRed: #ff8a6a, the VU red zone above zero, marked with plus figures
            tapeBrown: #3a2a1e, tape wound on the reels, decorative
        type:
            Three voices. Panel legends use Eurostile, Microgramma, Bank Gothic,
            Arial Narrow in caps, with the title at clamp 24 to 34px at 700 and
            0.12em tracking, and small legends at 11px at 700 with 0.2em. The
            counter and lyric memo use ui-monospace and Menlo, the counter 28px
            at 700. The insert card uses Courier New and Courier at 16px. Body
            text is Helvetica Neue at 14px.
        layout:
            A ribbed deck beside a side column. The deck header reads
            BRIGHTWORK SOUND and Stereo cassette deck, now playing. A tape
            window with an inset shadow shows a dark cassette with a beige
            label handwritten Low Tide, side A, and two white six spoke reels
            turning in brown tape. Beside it two amber backlit VU meters, VU L
            and VU R, with ticks from minus 20 to plus 3, a red zone and white
            needles just below zero. Under them a four wheel mechanical counter
            reads 0214 beside Tape counter and of 4 38, then an Output level
            fader with a chrome cap at 70 percent over a 0 to 10 scale. Below
            sit HARBOUR LIGHTS in wide caps with the artist and album, then a
            black Lyric memo display in amber monospace with the current line
            behind a chevron and the next line dimmer. A row of four touching
            chrome piano keys follows, PREV, PLAY pressed down with a lit
            amber lamp and the word PLAYING, PAUSE and NEXT, then three small
            chrome toggles, Shuffle Off, Repeat Off and Liked On with a heart.
            A thin amber progress bar with the elapsed and total time closes
            the deck. The side column holds the insert card, a spine headed
            Insert, up next and Side A over five typed rows with number, title,
            artist and time, then Tape shelf, your library as three cassette
            spines with a coloured edge and song counts, and chrome keys for
            Albums, Artists and Podcasts. Below 1100px the side column moves
            under the deck, and below 760px the deck stacks.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px deck padding, 16 to 20px between modules and 2px seams between piano keys.
        density: Medium. A full machine face, with the queue on a separate card.
        corners: 6px deck and meter bezels, 12px tape window, 2px keys and fields, 4px insert card.
        borders: 1px bezel rings around the window, meters and counter wheels, a double rule under the insert spine and 2px ribs across the body.
        shadows: Raised chrome keys cast a hard 0 4px 0 black. The pressed key drops to 0 1px 0 and sits 3px lower. The window has an inset shadow.
        icons:
            Classic transport glyphs printed on each key above its word. The
            pressed Play key shows a lit lamp and the word PLAYING. Toggles say
            Off or On, with On in amber. The current lyric has a chevron.
        focus: A 2px amber outline offset 3px on every key, field and card row.
        tone: Hardware legends, such as Tape counter, Output level, Lyric memo, Insert and Tape shelf.
    style333:
        number: 333
        run: 67
        screen: MusicPlayer
        name: Karaoke lyrics
        idea: The lyrics take over the screen, with the current line set huge and wiped in yellow as it is sung, a bouncing ball over the next word, the next line small beneath and every other control shrunk to rounded strips at the edges.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/333.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            stagePlum: #140b22, the page, the lyric stage and the style sheet
            booth: #21143a, the top strip, the control pill, ticket cards and fields
            boothLine: #3d2c63, pill rims, the unplayed track and dividers
            sungYellow: #ffe14d, the sung words, their underline bar, the ball, the pause button and focus
            unsungWhite: #f6f1ff, the rest of the current line and main text
            lilac: #bdb1d8, the next line, artists, times and labels
            pink: #ff7ac6, the liked heart, ticket numbers and the progress fill
            onYellow: #1e1400, text on sung yellow
        type:
            One rounded stack, ui-rounded, SF Pro Rounded, Arial Rounded MT
            Bold, Nunito, system-ui, at heavy weights. Base 15px at 600. The
            current line is clamp 38 to 92px at 900 with 1.3 line height, the
            next line clamp 20 to 30px at 700, the strip title 17px at 800,
            ticket titles 16px at 800, and caps labels 12px at 800 with 0.14em
            tracking.
        layout:
            Lyrics first. A rounded top strip holds a yellow Sing along badge,
            Harbour Lights, the artist and Low Tide, and Brightwork Sound on
            the right. The middle of the screen, at least half its height, is
            the lyric stage, with Lyrics, line 1 of 2 over the current line
            centred and huge. And the harbour lights go is sung, in yellow with
            a soft glow and a thick rounded yellow underline, a yellow ball sits
            over out, and out one by one stays white. The next line follows
            much smaller in lilac after a small caps Next. A long rounded
            control pill holds round previous, a larger yellow pause and next,
            a fat pink progress bar between the elapsed and total time, pills
            for Shuffle Off, Repeat Off and Liked with a pink heart, and a
            volume bar with 70%. Below, Up next to sing shows five rounded
            ticket cards with a pink numbered disc, the time, the title and the
            artist, and Your songbook lists the playlists with counts and pill
            links for Albums, Artists and Podcasts. Below 1100px the control
            pill stacks into rows and the songbook moves under the tickets,
            and below 560px the line drops to 36px and tickets stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 48px around the lyric stage, 12px inside pills and 16px between groups.
        density: Very low in the middle, compact at the edges.
        corners: Fully rounded strip, control pill, buttons and fields, 20px ticket cards and songbook.
        borders: 2px booth line rims on pills, buttons and tickets. The sung words carry a thick rounded yellow underline.
        shadows: Only a soft yellow glow of 24px at 40 percent behind the sung words and the ball.
        icons:
            Chunky solid glyphs in round buttons. A yellow ball marks the next
            word, and sung words are underlined as well as yellow. Liked is a
            filled pink heart with the word Liked. Toggles say Off.
        focus: A 3px yellow outline offset 3px, following the pill shape.
        tone: Friendly and loud, such as Sing along, Up next to sing, Your songbook and Next.

    style334:
        number: 334
        run: 68
        screen: CrmPipeline
        name: Sales graphite
        idea: A sober working CRM in cool graphite, with one summary strip, five even stage columns of clean deal cards and a single teal accent for progress and action.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/334.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #15171a, the page background and the style sheet
            column: #1c1f23, the top bar, summary strip, stage columns and activity panel
            card: #24282d, deal cards, secondary buttons and list rows
            line: #343941, every border, divider and meter track
            ink: #eceef1, text and figures
            muted: #a3aab4, labels, owners, counts and stage totals
            teal: #6fd6c4, the primary button, current tab, target meter and focus
            onTeal: #0c2622, text on teal
            amber: #f3c46f, Stalled text and its warning triangle
            sky: #9ec5ff, next step and closing text with calendar and flag
            green: #8fdca0, Won and Closed text with a check
        type:
            One system stack, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
            Arial, with figures in ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas. Base
            14px at 1.5. The page title is 22px at 650, summary figures 22px
            mono at 600 with tabular numbers, deal names 14px at 600, column
            heads 13px at 650 and meta 12px.
        layout:
            A 56px top bar holds a teal square B mark with Brightwork Sales,
            four underlined tabs with Pipeline current, then search and a teal
            New deal button. Below sits the title Deal pipeline with a round Q4
            chip and an All owners button on the right. One bordered summary
            strip splits into five cells, Pipeline value, Won this quarter with
            of 200,000 and 64 percent beside it and a thin teal meter under it,
            Target, Win rate and Open deals. Five equal stage columns follow,
            each with a 3px top rule that steps from grey to teal to green, a
            head with stage name, count and total in mono. Deal cards show the
            name and value on one line, an initials disc with the owner, and a
            ruled status line with an icon. Recent activity sits below as one
            panel split into three cells. Below 1100px the board goes to three
            columns, below 760px to one, the tabs scroll, search hides and the
            summary goes two by two with the won cell on top.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 12px gaps between columns and cards, 12px card padding, 28px page gutter, 16px on phones.
        density: Medium. Every deal is a card with name, value, owner and one status line.
        corners: 8px panels and columns, 6px cards, buttons and fields, round initials and chip.
        borders: 1px #343941 on every surface, plus the 3px stage top rule on each column.
        shadows: A faint 0 1px 2px black under deal cards only.
        icons:
            Rounded line icons at 1.9 stroke, sized to the text. Calendar for
            the next step, paper plane for sent, warning triangle for stalled,
            flag for closing, check for won, phone and eye in the activity.
        focus: A 2px solid teal outline offset 2px on every control and around the search field.
        tone: Plain CRM words, such as Deal pipeline, New deal, All owners and Recent activity.
    style335:
        number: 335
        run: 68
        screen: CrmPipeline
        name: Neon swimlanes
        idea: The pipeline as five horizontal lanes on near black, each edged by one thin neon line in its own colour, with every value shown as a glowing figure and the deals riding the lane as outlined capsules.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/335.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            void: #09080f, the page and the style sheet
            lane: #100e1a, lane bodies
            capsule: #16131f, deal capsules and fields
            grid: #2a2540, dividers, dashed lane splits and the meter track
            ink: #f1eefb, names and text
            haze: #aca5c4, labels, owners and counts
            cyan: #5ef2ff, the Lead lane, pipeline figure, primary button and focus
            violet: #c2adff, the Qualified lane
            magenta: #ff7ad9, the Proposal lane, win rate and secondary button
            amber: #ffcf6b, the Negotiation lane and open deals figure
            lime: #c4ff6b, the Won lane, won figure and target line
            ember: #ffb36b, Stalled text, its triangle and dashed capsule
        type:
            A geometric stack, Avenir Next, Avenir, Futura, Century Gothic,
            Trebuchet MS, system-ui. Base 15px. Summary figures 44px at 300
            with a glow, lane totals 30px at 300, deal names 15px at 600, lane
            and section labels 12px uppercase at 600 tracked .3em, meta 12px.
        layout:
            A thin top line holds BRIGHTWORK in cyan and Sales, with a magenta
            outline Filter pill and a cyan New deal pill on the right. A tracked
            label Pipeline Q4 leads a row of five large glowing figures, each
            in its own neon colour, with a tracked label beneath, and a thin
            lime target line with a tick at 64 percent under the won figure.
            Five full width lanes stack below. Each lane has a 2px neon left
            edge with a soft inner glow and a neon underline fading out to the
            right. A 220px label cell holds the stage name in its colour, the
            deal count and the lane total as a glowing figure, split from the
            deals by a dashed line. Deals sit in a wrapping row as pill
            capsules outlined at 55 percent of the lane colour, name and owner
            on the left, the glowing value on the right, a status line under a
            hairline. The stalled capsule has a dashed ember outline. Activity
            follows as three items each with a neon left rule. On phones the
            label cell sits above the deals and capsules fill the width.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 10px between lanes, 12px between capsules, 16px lane padding, 28px gutter, 16px on phones.
        density: Low to medium. One lane per stage with plenty of black between.
        corners: Square lanes, pill capsules and buttons, 18px capsules on phones.
        borders: A 2px neon left edge per lane, a fading neon underline, 1px capsule outlines and dashed splits.
        shadows: No drop shadows. A soft colour glow on figures, lane edges and the primary button.
        icons:
            Thin line icons at 1.9 stroke in the text colour. Stalled pairs a
            triangle and the word with a dashed ember outline, so it never
            relies on colour.
        focus: A 2px cyan outline offset 3px with a cyan halo.
        tone: Terse uppercase labels, such as Pipeline, Activity, New deal and Filter.
    style336:
        number: 336
        run: 68
        screen: CrmPipeline
        name: Executive navy
        idea: The pipeline as a formal quarterly board paper in deep navy and gold, with large serif figures between double gold rules, a numbered ledger of stages with leader lines, and notes for the board set apart.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/336.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            navy: #0d1628, the page and the style sheet
            panel: #13203a, the notes panel and fields
            rule: #2c3d5e, single rules between stages and figures
            ink: #ece6d6, ivory text
            muted: #a9b3c7, small caps labels, owners and remarks
            gold: #e2c47a, figures, roman numerals, headings, primary button and focus
            goldRule: #7a6538, double rules, dotted leaders and the secondary border
            onGold: #1a1404, text on gold
            coral: #f2a08f, Stalled and Attention with a triangle
            sage: #a8d5a2, Closed with a check
        type:
            A serif stack, Iowan Old Style, Palatino Linotype, Palatino, Book
            Antiqua, Georgia, with labels in Gill Sans, Optima, Candara, Segoe
            UI. Base 16px. The title is 38px at 400, figures 40px in gold with
            oldstyle numerals, stage names 20px, deal values 19px, section
            heads 13px sans uppercase at 600 tracked .26em, remarks 14px italic.
        layout:
            A centred masthead holds a round gold outline monogram B, the house
            name in tracked caps, the title Quarterly Pipeline Review and an
            italic line Fourth quarter, deal pipeline, with Owners and New deal
            set top right. Five figures sit centred in a band between double
            gold rules and split by thin rules, the won figure with 64 percent
            of target in italic and a thin gold bar. Below, a wide ledger titled
            Pipeline by stage lists five stages with large italic roman numerals
            I to V, the stage name, deal count in italic and the stage total on
            the right. Each deal is a line with a dotted gold leader to its
            value, and an italic line under it with the owner and a remark. A
            320px navy panel with a 3px gold top bar holds Notes for the board
            as a numbered list, the third flagged Attention in coral. Below
            960px the notes drop under the ledger, below 600px figures go two
            by two.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 40px page gutter, 48px between ledger and notes, 18px stage padding, 16px on phones.
        density: Low. A board paper read top to bottom, one line per deal.
        corners: None. Square everywhere except the round monogram.
        borders: Double gold rules round the figures and atop the sheet, single navy rules between stages, dotted gold leaders, a 3px gold bar on the notes.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            Few, fine line icons at 1.6 stroke in gold before italic remarks.
            A coral triangle with the word for stalled, a sage check for closed.
        focus: A 1px gold outline with a navy gap and a second gold ring.
        tone: Formal and measured, such as Quarterly Pipeline Review, Notes for the board and Attention.
    style337:
        number: 337
        run: 68
        screen: CrmPipeline
        name: Dense deal table
        idea: The whole pipeline as one tight 13px table grouped by stage, with group subtotals, a sorted value column, small bracketed status tags and the summary squeezed into a single line of key figures.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/337.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            base: #111418, the page, table body and style sheet
            head: #1a1f26, the header row, summary line, footer and secondary buttons
            zebra: #151a20, even rows
            group: #1d232b, stage group rows
            line: #262d36, every rule and border
            ink: #e3e7ec, text
            muted: #9aa4b1, column heads, dates and counts
            orange: #ff9e64, the sort arrow, percent, primary button and focus
            red: #ff8a80, the STALLED tag, its row edge and triangle
            sky: #7fd4ff, the DEMO and CLOSING tags
            lilac: #cdb6ff, the SENT tag
            green: #8be39b, the WON tag with a check
        type:
            system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Arial, with figures and tags in
            ui-monospace, Cascadia Mono, Menlo, Consolas. Base 13px at 1.4. The
            title is 15px at 650, cells 13px, values 13px mono with tabular
            numbers, column heads 11px uppercase at 600, tags 11px mono at 600.
        layout:
            A small breadcrumb Brightwork, Sales, Pipeline Q4 sits over the
            title Deal pipeline. One bordered mono line lists pipeline 412,000,
            won 128,500 of 200,000 with 64 percent in orange, target, win rate
            31 percent and open 18, split by thin rules. A toolbar holds a
            filter field, Group Stage and Owner All buttons, then Columns and
            an orange Deal button. The table has columns Deal, Owner, Value,
            Status and Date, with Value sorted high to low and an orange down
            arrow. Group rows per stage show a down chevron, the stage, a mono
            count and a right aligned subtotal. Rows are 30px and zebra striped,
            owners carry a boxed mono initials tag, statuses are bracketed mono
            tags with an icon, and the stalled row has a 3px red inset edge. A
            footer row sums the seven shown deals. A 280px Activity panel sits
            right with three ruled rows. Below 980px the panel drops below,
            on phones the table scrolls inside its frame with the deal column
            pinned.
        spacing: A 4px unit. 30px rows, 28px group rows and controls, 10px cell padding, 20px gutter, 16px on phones.
        density: High. Every deal, subtotal and the activity log fit on one screen.
        corners: 3px on the table frame, fields and buttons, square cells.
        borders: 1px #262d36 under every row, round the table and between summary figures.
        shadows: None. A 3px red inset edge marks the stalled row.
        icons:
            14px line icons at 1.9 stroke. Tags sit in square brackets with a
            triangle, calendar, flag, paper plane or check beside the word.
        focus: A 2px orange outline drawn inside the control.
        tone: Terse and technical, with lowercase key figures, Group Stage, Owner All and Columns.
    style338:
        number: 338
        run: 68
        screen: CrmPipeline
        name: Funnel first
        idea: A large stepped funnel in pale sea greens leads the screen, each band naming its stage, count and value, with a round target gauge beside it and the deals laid out in soft rounded stage trays underneath.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/338.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            deep: #0b1514, the page and the style sheet
            surface: #12201f, the funnel panel, cards and activity
            tray: #172927, stage trays, mini figures and secondary buttons
            line: #26403d, the gauge track and field borders
            ink: #e6f2ef, text
            muted: #9db8b2, labels and owners
            foam: #a7f0de, the Lead band
            sea: #86e3d0, the Qualified band, primary button and icons
            lagoon: #66d2be, the Proposal band
            teal: #47bba8, the Negotiation band
            sand: #f6d58a, the Won spout, target gauge, Closed pill and focus
            darkText: #06201b, text on every band and on the primary button
            coral: #ffb08a, the Stalled pill, dashed, with a triangle
        type:
            A rounded stack, ui-rounded, SF Pro Rounded, Nunito, Varela Round,
            Segoe UI, system-ui. Base 15px. Headings 26px at 800, the gauge
            figure 28px at 800, band labels 17px at 800 with values 20px at
            800, card values 20px at 800, labels 12px at 600.
        layout:
            A small header with a rounded B tile, Brightwork Sales over Deal
            pipeline, a Q4 pill and an Add deal pill. A wide rounded panel holds
            Pipeline funnel Q4. On the left five centred bands narrow from full
            width to 44 percent, each a trapezoid with slanted sides, pale
            green to teal, the last a sand spout with rounded bottom corners
            for Won. Each band reads stage, deal count and listed value in dark
            text, and a caption says width shows stage order. On the right a
            ring gauge shows 64 percent beside Won this quarter 128,500 of
            200,000 target, over three small rounded tiles for pipeline value,
            win rate and open deals. Deals by stage follows as five rounded
            trays with a coloured dot matching the band, holding cards with
            name, a large value, owner and a status pill. Latest holds the
            activity. Below 1050px the gauge sits under the funnel and trays go
            two across, on phones one across and bands wrap their text.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 32px panel padding, 14px between trays, 10px between cards, 6px between bands.
        density: Low at the top where the funnel fills the width, medium in the trays below.
        corners: Very round. 28px hero, 22px trays, 16px cards, pill buttons and status pills.
        borders: Almost none. Surfaces step in tone, and a dashed coral outline marks stalled.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            Rounded line icons at 2 stroke. Each pill pairs its word with a
            calendar, paper plane, flag, check or triangle.
        focus: A 3px sand outline offset 3px.
        tone: Friendly and short, such as Pipeline funnel, Deals by stage, Latest and Add deal.

    style339:
        number: 339
        run: 69
        screen: CrmPipeline
        name: Territory map
        idea: The pipeline placed on a dark abstract map of five sales regions, where each deal is a numbered pin whose shape tells its state, with a keyed deal list beside the map as the legend and text version.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/339.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            sea: #08121c, the page and the style sheet
            chartSea: #0b1826, water inside the map
            land: #13243a, region fills, stepped from #112238 to #182e47
            panel: #0f1c2b, the map frame, fields and row hover
            border: #2e4a68, region borders, rules and dashed dividers
            ink: #e3ecf6, text
            muted: #9fb6cf, region names, labels and the compass
            amber: #ffc86b, pins, the target hatch and primary button
            onAmber: #1d1300, pin numbers and button text
            coral: #ff8f7a, Stalled and its triangle pin
            mint: #8de0b5, Won and its ringed pin
            ice: #9cd3ff, the secondary button, note icons and focus
        type:
            A condensed stack, Bahnschrift, DIN Alternate, Roboto Condensed,
            Arial Narrow, Segoe UI. Base 15px. The title is 26px at 700,
            figures 24px at 700 with tabular numbers, region names on the map
            20px uppercase tracked .15em, deal names 15px at 700, meta 13px.
        layout:
            A thin top bar holds a pin icon with Brightwork Sales Territories,
            an All stages outline button and an amber Place deal button. The
            title Q4 pipeline by territory sits over a ruled band of five
            figures split by dashed lines, the won figure with a hatched amber
            bar at 64 percent. Below, a wide map frame takes about two thirds
            of the width. It shows five invented regions, North, Harbour,
            Central, East and South, as dark polygons with dashed contour lines
            and a small compass, and seven numbered pins. Lumen Bakery and
            Saltwater Freight sit in Harbour, Orbit Labs and Northpass in North,
            Kettle and Co in Central, Fernhill Studio in East and Bluewater
            Clinics in South. Under the map sit a shape legend and a note that
            regions are not to scale. The right column, Deals on the map, lists
            pins 1 to 7 with the same pin shape, the deal, region, stage, owner,
            status and value. Field notes holds the activity below. Below 960px
            the list drops under the map.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 20px between map and list, 10px row padding, 24px gutter, 16px on phones.
        density: Medium. The map carries placement and the keyed list carries the detail.
        corners: 6px map frame, 4px buttons and fields, round pins, teardrop swatches.
        borders: 2px region borders, 1px rules under every list row, dashed contours and summary dividers.
        shadows: None. Pins sit on a 3px sea coloured ring so they lift off the land.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.9 stroke in the chrome. On the map pin shape
            carries state, a circle for open, a diamond for a booked date, a
            square for sent, a triangle for stalled and a ringed circle for won.
        focus: A 2px dashed ice outline offset 3px.
        tone: Field and survey words, such as Territories, Place deal, Deals on the map and Field notes.
    style340:
        number: 340
        run: 69
        screen: CrmPipeline
        name: Sales leaderboard
        idea: The pipeline as a friendly sales league on deep indigo, with an owner podium ranked by open value, earned badges and streaks drawn from real deal events, a quarter quest bar toward target and the stages as levels on a quest board.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/340.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            indigo: #15122b, the page and the style sheet
            card: #211c40, panels, levels and moves
            raised: #2c2552, tokens, tiles, podium steps and secondary buttons
            line: #3d3570, the quest bar frame and field borders
            ink: #f4f1ff, text
            muted: #b5addb, labels and owners
            gold: #ffd166, rank 1, the quest bar, primary button and Mara tokens
            silver: #cfd6e6, rank 2 and Sam tokens
            bronze: #f0a875, rank 3 and Lena tokens
            onGold: #211400, text on gold, silver and bronze
            mint: #6ee7b7, Won and the team win
            coral: #ff8fa3, Stalled and Gone quiet with a triangle
            sky: #8ecbff, Booked and Closer badges and focus
        type:
            Display in Impact, Haettenschweiler, Franklin Gothic Bold, Arial
            Black at weight 800 with no synthetic bold, body in Trebuchet MS,
            Segoe UI, system-ui. Base 15px. The title is 36px, the won figure
            40px, podium values 26px, section heads 22px, names 15px at 700,
            caps labels and badges 12px at 700.
        layout:
            A header with a tracked caps line Brightwork Sales Deal pipeline
            over Q4 Sales League with League in gold, and My deals and a gold
            Log a deal button. Two panels follow. Leaderboard open value holds
            a three step podium, Sam Ortiz second, Mara Okafor first and Lena
            Fischer third, each with a hexagon initials avatar in a medal
            colour, the open value, 2 open deals, pill badges and a step with
            its rank number. Badges are Biggest deal and Demo booked for Mara,
            Closer for Sam and a flame 3 opens for Lena. Quarter quest shows
            Won this quarter 128,500, a striped gold bar at 64 percent, 71,500
            to go, level 64 of 100 and three tiles for pipeline value, win rate
            and open deals. Quest board shows five levels L1 to L5 with tokens
            edged in the owner medal colour, Bluewater Clinics marked team win
            in mint. Latest moves holds three cards labelled Booked, Streak 3
            opens and Gone quiet. On phones panels stack and levels go one
            across while the podium keeps three steps.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 20px panel padding, 12px between levels and moves, 28px gutter, 16px on phones.
        density: Medium. Big figures and a podium up top, compact tokens below.
        corners: Chunky. 20px panels, 18px levels, 14px tokens, buttons and fields, hexagon avatars and pill badges.
        borders: Few. A 5px left edge on each token in the owner medal colour, 2px badge rings and a 6px top edge on podium steps.
        shadows: Solid offset shadows with no blur, 0 4px to 0 6px, so buttons and panels look like game pieces.
        icons:
            Line icons at 2 stroke. Trophy, star, hexagon and bolt head the
            sections. A flame marks a streak, a triangle gone quiet, a check won.
        focus: A 3px sky outline offset 3px.
        tone: Playful but plain, such as Sales League, Quarter quest, Log a deal, 71,500 to go and Gone quiet.
    style341:
        number: 341
        run: 69
        screen: CrmPipeline
        name: Rolodex
        idea: The pipeline as a rotary card file on a dark desk, each deal a typed index card with a coloured stage tab, cards filed back to front so their top strips stay readable, and one card pulled forward open in full.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/341.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            desk: #141110, the page and the style sheet
            cardStock: #2a2520, filed cards, summary and notes cards, secondary buttons
            frontCard: #352e27, the pulled card
            rule: #4f443a, card edges and dashed rules
            ink: #efe4d0, typed text
            pencil: #c2b298, labels and owners
            dark: #1e1914, text on every tab and on the primary button
            slateTab: #b9c7d8, Lead
            sageTab: #a9d1b0, Qualified
            manilaTab: #e8c27a, Proposal, the primary button, target bar and focus
            salmonTab: #e6a58f, Negotiation
            oliveTab: #cfe08a, Won and Closed
            stampRed: #ff9c86, the Stalled stamp and triangle
        type:
            A typewriter stack, American Typewriter, Courier Prime, Courier New,
            Courier, with tabs in Avenir Next Condensed, Arial Narrow, Roboto
            Condensed. Base 15px. The title and open card name are 24px at 700,
            values 15px at 700, tabs and divider labels 12px condensed uppercase
            at 700 tracked .12em, meta 13px.
        layout:
            A header with Brightwork Sales in tracked caps, the title Deal card
            file Q4, Find card and a manila New card button, over a dashed rule.
            Three columns follow. A 170px rail of stage dividers shows coloured
            tabs with name and count, Proposal pulled out 10px with a shadow.
            The centre is the drum, two dark rails on its sides, a stack of six
            filed cards and a twin knob drawing below. Cards run back to front
            from Lumen Bakery to Bluewater Clinics, each 14px narrower than the
            card in front, with a stage tab at a stage specific position along
            the top, so every card shows its name, value, owner and status on
            one strip. The front card, Saltwater Freight, is open in full with
            Pulled for follow up, the value, a dotted fact list and a tilted
            double ruled red Stalled stamp. A 300px side column holds a
            Quarter summary card with dotted lines and a manila target bar,
            and a Notes card with the activity. Below 1050px the rail becomes a
            row of top tabs and the side cards sit under the drum.
        spacing: An 8px unit. Cards overlap by 4px and step in 14px per card, 28px between rail, drum and side cards.
        density: Medium. Six filed cards show one strip each and one card is open in full.
        corners: 4px cards with a square corner under the tab, 6px tab tops, 8px divider tabs.
        borders: 1px rule on every card, a 3px top edge in the stage colour, a red rule under side card heads, dotted rules under typed lines, a double ruled stamp.
        shadows: Cards cast a short shadow up onto the card behind, the pulled card casts a deep 10px 24px shadow.
        icons:
            Line icons at 1.9 stroke inline with typed text. Stalled is a
            tilted red stamp with a triangle and the word.
        focus: A 3px manila outline offset 3px.
        tone: Office file words, such as Deal card file, Find card, New card and Pulled for follow up.
    style342:
        number: 342
        run: 69
        screen: CrmPipeline
        name: Boardroom walnut
        idea: The pipeline laid out on a dark walnut boardroom table, each stage a stitched leather folder with a brass name plate, owners on small engraved brass plates, the figures on brass plaques and the activity as minutes on a green leather blotter.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/342.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            walnut: #26170f, the table top, with grain lines in #2d1c13 and #21140d
            sheetWalnut: #1c110b, the style sheet ground
            oxblood: #3b1d1b, open stage folders and the secondary button
            bottleGreen: #1d2c24, the Won folder and the minutes blotter
            stitch: #b08a5a, dashed stitching inside every folder
            ink: #f1e3c8, text on leather and wood
            tan: #d2b994, italic remarks and labels
            brassLight: #e6c983, the top of every brass gradient and focus
            brass: #c9a45c, plaques, name plates and the primary button
            brassDark: #b8924a, the bottom of the brass gradient
            engraved: #2a1a08, text cut into brass
            red: #ffa08c, Stalled with a triangle
            leaf: #b7e0a0, Closed with a check
        type:
            A book serif, Baskerville, Baskerville Old Face, Hoefler Text,
            Garamond, Times New Roman, with plates in Copperplate, Copperplate
            Gothic Light, Trajan Pro, Optima. Base 17px. The header plate is
            24px uppercase at 600 tracked .12em, plaque figures 28px at 600,
            deal names 18px at 600, values 22px, owner plates 11px uppercase,
            remarks 15px italic.
        layout:
            The page is walnut grain drawn with fine repeating lines. A brass
            header plate reads Brightwork Sales over Q4 Pipeline, with a
            stitched oxblood Owners button and a brass New deal button. Five
            brass plaques with two screw dots each show the figures in dark
            engraved text, the won plaque with a dark bar at 64 percent. Five
            leather folders follow, each with a tab at the top left, a dashed
            stitch line inside and a brass name plate with the stage and count.
            Deals are blocks with the name, a large value, a brass owner plate
            and an italic remark, split by thin tan rules, and a Folder total
            line closes each folder. Won is bottle green. A green blotter with
            wooden end strips holds Minutes as a numbered list. Below 1100px
            folders go three across, on phones one across with plaques two by
            two.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 18px between folders, 14px between plaques, 12px inside the stitching, 28px gutter, 16px on phones.
        density: Low to medium. Five folders with generous wood between.
        corners: Folders 4px at the tab corner and 12px elsewhere, 8px stitching, 2px to 4px on brass.
        borders: Dashed 1.5px tan stitching inside folders and the blotter, thin tan rules between deals, wooden ends on the blotter.
        shadows: Deep soft shadows under folders and blotter, an inner shade on leather, a light top bevel and a short drop on brass.
        icons:
            Few small line icons at 1.7 stroke beside italic remarks. A red
            triangle with the word in bold for stalled, a leaf check for closed.
        focus: A 3px light brass outline offset 3px.
        tone: Formal meeting words, such as Q4 Pipeline, Folder total, Minutes and Owners.
    style343:
        number: 343
        run: 69
        screen: CrmPipeline
        name: Signal board
        idea: The pipeline as a black departures board, one terse uppercase row per deal on split flap tiles, each led by a signal lamp whose shape and word give its state, with the key figures spelled out tile by tile above.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/343.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            night: #050607, the page, cell gaps and the style sheet
            board: #0c0e10, board frames
            tile: #16191c, the lower half of every flap tile and row
            tileTop: #1d2125, the upper half of every flap tile
            seam: #000000, the split line across each tile
            line: #2a2f35, board frames and the secondary border
            amber: #ffd23f, figures, values, the header bar, primary button and focus
            onAmber: #1a1400, text on the header bar
            ink: #f2f2ea, deal names and Open lamps
            muted: #a5abb3, column heads, stage and owner
            green: #6ff09a, the Final call play lamp and Landed check lamp
            sky: #7fd0ff, the Booked diamond lamp
            red: #ff7a66, the Stalled triangle lamp and row underline
        type:
            One mono stack, ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas, all caps
            with wide tracking. Base 15px. Figure tiles 22px at 800, the header
            20px at 800 tracked .18em, rows 15px at 800 tracked .08em, column
            heads 11px at 600 tracked .2em, legend 12px.
        layout:
            An amber header bar holds Brightwork Sales, Pipeline Q4 and a dark
            Add deal button. Under it a board strip spells Pipeline, Won Q4,
            Target, Win rate and Open deals one character per flap tile in
            amber, with commas narrow and tile free. The main board, Deals 7 on
            board, is a table with columns Signal, Deal, Stage, Value, Owner
            and Remark. Every cell is a flap tile with a black seam across its
            middle and 2px black gaps between cells. Signals read Open with a
            hollow circle for the two leads, Booked with a diamond for
            Northpass, Sent with a square for Kettle and Co, Stalled with a
            triangle and a red underline for Saltwater Freight, Final call with
            a play shape for Fernhill Studio and Landed with a check for
            Bluewater Clinics. Remarks read Demo 04 Nov, Sent 28 Oct, No reply
            12 days, Closing 07 Nov and Closed 22 Oct. A signal key follows,
            then a Notices board with three rows tagged Call, Opened and Quiet,
            and a Filter board button. On phones each row becomes a block with
            the signal on top, deal and value, stage and owner, then the remark.
        spacing: A 4px unit. 4px between rows, 2px seams between cells, 16px board padding, 24px gutter, 16px on phones.
        density: High and even. Seven deal rows read as one board, every cell one terse value.
        corners: 2px. The board is square.
        borders: 1px frames on boards, 2px black gaps between cells, a 3px red underline on the stalled row.
        shadows: None. The black tile seam gives the flap its depth.
        icons:
            Solid signal lamps lead every row, a hollow circle, diamond,
            square, triangle, play shape or check, each with its word.
        focus: A 3px amber outline offset 2px.
        tone: Departure board shorthand, such as Booked, Final call, Landed, No reply 12 days and Notices.

    style344:
        number: 344
        run: 70
        screen: TeamChat
        name: Chat slate
        idea: A professional three pane chat in blue slate, where a quiet sidebar, a roomy message list and a docked thread panel share one mint accent that only marks where you are and what you can do.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/344.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #171c26, the message list and the style sheet
            side: #1f2633, the sidebar and the thread panel
            surface: #232b39, the composer, cards and the selected message
            raised: #2c3546, hover rows, secondary buttons and the unread badge
            line: #3a4558, every border and divider
            ink: #e6eaf2, text
            muted: #a3adbf, times, group labels and read channels
            accent: #5eead4, Send, the thread link, the current channel bar and focus
            onAccent: #062a26, text and icons on the accent
            accentSoft: #1f3b3d, the current channel row and your own reaction chip
            mention: #fda4af, the mention badge text on #3b2230
            online: #6ee7a8, the online dot
            away: #fcd34d, the away crescent
        type:
            One system stack, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
            Arial. Base 14px at 1.5. Channel title 16px at 650, names 14px at
            650, times and group labels 12px, group labels at 600.
        layout:
            Three columns at 248px, flexible and 300px. The sidebar holds a
            mint square B mark with Brightwork Chat over Mara Okafor, then
            Channels and Direct messages lists. Unread channels are bold with a
            grey count badge, the mention channel carries a rose @1 badge, and
            the current channel sits on a soft teal row with a 3px mint inset
            bar. Each person shows a dot, crescent or ring and the word online,
            away or offline. The middle column has a ruled top bar with the
            channel name, a muted description and a search button, a Today
            divider, then messages with 36px rounded square initials avatars in
            pastel tints, name and time on one line and the text below. Aiko's
            message is selected with a surface fill, reaction chips for thumbs
            up 3 and eyes 1, and a mint 3 replies link. The image shows a
            280px preview card with the filename below. The composer is one
            bordered box holding attach, the field, emoji and a mint send
            square, with three dots and Priya is typing above. The right panel
            shows Thread with a close button, the parent message as a card, the
            reactions spelled out, a ruled 3 replies divider and a Reply in
            thread box. Below 1060px the thread moves under the chat. Below
            720px the sidebar stacks on top and its rows become wrapped
            outlined chips.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 8px by 12px message padding, 16px panel padding, 20px gutters.
        density: Comfortable. Five messages, the composer and the thread fit one laptop screen.
        corners: 8px avatars, messages, cards and composer, 6px buttons and nav rows, round chips and badges.
        borders: 1px #3a4558 between panes and around cards. Panes step in lightness instead of heavy lines.
        shadows: None. The current channel uses an inset mint bar instead.
        icons:
            Rounded line icons at 1.8 stroke, 14px to 18px, for attach, emoji,
            send, search, close and the image. Reactions are drawn thumbs and
            eyes icons beside the count.
        focus: A 2px mint outline offset 2px, drawn around the whole composer when its field has focus.
        tone: Plain workplace labels, such as Channels, Direct messages, Thread and 3 replies.
    style345:
        number: 345
        run: 70
        screen: TeamChat
        name: Threaded minimal
        idea: A chat set like a well kept letter, where there are no avatars, boxes or bubbles, and names, times, indents and one citron underline do all of the work.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/345.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #141311, the only surface, screen and style sheet
            ink: #ece6da, messages, names and the current channel
            muted: #a8a092, times, labels, the thread rule and the composer rule
            faint: #3b3832, section rules and quiet underlines only
            citron: #e3d27a, link underlines, Send, the mention count, the current marker and focus
            focusWash: #25231c, the faint wash behind a focused control
        type:
            A book serif, Iowan Old Style, Palatino Linotype, Palatino,
            Charter, Georgia, for messages at 17px with 1.6 leading and the
            channel title at 40px weight 400. A system sans for metadata. Names
            are 13px bold capitals tracked 0.08em, times 13px tabular, labels
            11px capitals tracked 0.14em.
        layout:
            A centred 1120px page with two columns, a 230px index and the log,
            64px apart, and no panels at all. The index starts with Brightwork
            Chat in serif italic over Signed in as Mara Okafor, then Channels
            and Direct messages as plain text lists. The current channel is
            italic with a citron arrow before it. Unread channels are bold with
            4 unread in small sans, the mention channel adds @ 1 mention in
            citron. People carry the marks filled, half and empty circle with
            the words here, away and offline. The log has the channel title,
            a sans line reading Today, five messages, one thread, then a
            hairline. Each message is a two column row, the time right aligned
            in a 56px gutter, the name in capitals and the text below, at a 62
            character measure. The thread under Aiko's message is indented
            behind a 1px muted left rule with 3 replies in thread and Thumbs up
            3, Eyes 1 in words. The image is an italic line, shared an image,
            with the filename as an underlined link. The composer is Priya is
            typing in italic, then a bare field on one rule with Attach, Emoji
            and Send as small tracked capitals words. Below 800px the index
            becomes inline wrapped runs above the log.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 28px between messages, 64px between index and log, 56px top margin.
        density: Sparse. A 62 character measure and generous leading, like reading prose.
        corners: None anywhere.
        borders: Only rules. A 1px muted left rule for the thread indent and a 1px rule under the composer.
        shadows: None.
        icons: No icons. An arrow marks the current channel, filled, half and empty circles mark presence, always with words.
        focus: A 2px citron underline with the faint warm wash behind the control.
        tone: Quiet and literary, such as shared an image, 3 replies in thread and Priya is typing.
    style346:
        number: 346
        run: 70
        screen: TeamChat
        name: Rounded bubbles
        idea: A friendly messenger on deep plum where every person speaks in their own softly coloured bubble, your own words glow coral on the right, and every shape is a pill or a circle.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/346.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            plum: #1b1530, the page and the style sheet
            card: #261e42, the sidebar and chat cards
            pill: #342a57, channel pills, the composer and chips
            line: #4a3f78, chip rims
            ink: #f4efff, text in bubbles and cards
            muted: #bfb3e0, labels and presence words
            coral: #ff9e7a, your own bubble, Send and the mention badge, with text #3a1206
            sun: #ffd166, the current channel, the thread chip and focus, with text #3a2a00
            mint: #7ef0c0, the new count badge and the online dot
            teal: #154a4a, Priya's bubbles
            berry: #4d2149, Aiko's bubbles
            blue: #1e3462, Jonas's bubbles
        type:
            A rounded stack, ui-rounded, SF Pro Rounded, Nunito, Varela Round,
            then system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto. Base 15px at 1.45. Channel title
            19px at 800, bubble names 13px at 800, sheet title 30px at 900.
        layout:
            Two floating cards with 28px corners on the plum page, a 260px
            sidebar and the chat, 20px apart. The sidebar has a coral circle b
            mark and Brightwork Chat, then channels as full pills, the current
            one sun yellow, unread bold with a mint 4 new pill, the mention
            with a coral @ 1 pill. Direct messages are pills with a small
            round avatar, the name and a dot, crescent or ring with the word.
            The chat card header has a sun yellow rounded square with a hash,
            design-crit and Today. Messages zigzag as bubbles capped at 78
            percent width with round initials avatars at the bottom. Each
            other person has their own tinted bubble with a 6px tail corner.
            Mara's bubble is coral on the right, labelled Mara Okafor (you).
            Aiko's bubble carries reaction pills for thumbs up 3 and eyes 1
            and a sun 3 replies pill. Priya's image sits inside her bubble as a
            rounded preview over Image and the filename. A grey pill of three
            dots with Priya is typing sits above a pill composer with a round
            plus, the field, a round emoji button and a round coral send arrow.
            Below 820px the sidebar stacks on top with wrapped pills.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 14px between bubbles, 10px by 16px bubble padding, 20px card padding.
        density: Relaxed. Bubbles cap at 78 percent so the feed zigzags.
        corners: 28px cards, 22px bubbles with one 6px tail corner, pills and circles everywhere else.
        borders: Almost none. 2px rims on reaction chips and a 2px pill coloured line under the chat header.
        shadows: None. Colour blocks carry the depth.
        icons: Chunky rounded line icons at 2.2 stroke inside 40px circles. Presence is a dot, crescent or ring beside the word.
        focus: A 3px sun yellow outline offset 3px, wrapping the whole composer pill.
        tone: Warm and casual, such as 4 new, Mara Okafor (you) and 3 replies with an arrow.
    style347:
        number: 347
        run: 70
        screen: TeamChat
        name: IRC classic
        idea: A plain terminal chat client, where a topic line, a window list, a log with a fixed time and nick column, a nick list and a status bar do everything in one monospace face.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/347.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            bg: #0c0c0c, the log and the style sheet
            bar: #1d1d2a, the title bar and the status bar
            topic: #00303d, the topic line
            sel: #103a4a, the current window row
            rule: #3a3a3a, pane dividers
            ink: #d0d0d0, message text
            dim: #9a9a9a, times, brackets and event lines
            white: #ffffff, active windows and the inverse focus block
            hi: #5fd7ff, links, the input prompt and section labels
            warn: #ffd75f, reactions, typing and activity
            mention: #ff87af, the mention window
            nick1: #d7afff, Priya's nick
            nick2: #87d787, Mara's nick and the send key
            nick3: #ffaf5f, Aiko's nick
            nick4: #87afff, Jonas's nick
        type:
            One monospace stack, ui-monospace, Cascadia Mono, DejaVu Sans Mono,
            Liberation Mono, Menlo, Consolas, at 14px with 1.5 leading, 13px
            under 720px. Bold only for active and mention windows and section
            heads at 20px.
        layout:
            Full width terminal. A one line title bar reads Brightwork Chat,
            mara on the left and the channel with 5 lines and 1 thread on the
            right. A teal topic line follows, Topic then a derived line about
            the hero options due Monday. Three panes, a 290px window list, the
            log and a 230px nick list, split by 1px rules. Windows are numbered
            1 to 8, channels then queries. The current one is on the sel band,
            mobile-release is bold white with (4 unread), billing-war-room is
            bold pink with [@1 mention]. The log is a grid with a 7ch time in
            brackets, a 16ch right aligned nick in angle brackets in that
            person's colour, then the text. A day change line starts it. Under
            Aiko's line an arrow row holds an underlined thread link with 3
            replies and yellow [+1 x3] and [eyes x1] tags. The image is an
            event line with a star, Priya sent an image and the filename as a
            link. The nick list marks people with plus for online, tilde for
            away and minus for offline plus the word. A status bar shows the
            time, mara, 2 and the channel, and an Act field naming window 3
            with 4 unread and window 4 with @1 mention. Then -- Priya is typing
            in yellow and an input line with the bracketed channel prompt, the
            field and bracketed attach, emoji and send words. Below 720px the
            panes stack, windows wrap inline and each log line wraps with a
            hanging indent.
        spacing: Character cells. 1ch gaps, a 12px pane gutter, one line per message.
        density: Dense. Fixed 7ch time and 16ch nick columns.
        corners: Square everywhere.
        borders: 1px #3a3a3a pane dividers. Bars are solid colour strips.
        shadows: None.
        icons: None. Text marks only, plus, tilde and minus for presence, an arrow for the thread and a star for events.
        focus: Inverse video, a white block with black text.
        tone: Terse client speak, such as Day changed, Act with window numbers, and -- Priya is typing.
    style348:
        number: 348
        run: 70
        screen: TeamChat
        name: BBS ANSI
        idea: A chat that behaves like a dial-up message board, drawn in sixteen colour ANSI with shade block banners, double line boxes, hotkey menus and a message reader that counts MSG 1/5.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/348.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            black: #000000, the page and the label cut outs on box rims
            navy: #000055, side boxes and style sheet boxes
            blue: #0000aa, the message reader box
            dcyan: #00aaaa, message header bars and the current board
            cyan: #55ffff, box rims and info text
            yellow: #ffff55, titles, hotkey letters and the focus block
            white: #ffffff, message text
            grey: #aaaaaa, body text, off-line and the footer bar
            green: #55ff55, the NEW count, ON-LINE and the Send key
            magenta: #ff55ff, mentions and typing
            brown: #aa5500, the hard drop shadow under the title only
        type:
            One monospace stack, Perfect DOS VGA 437, Px437 IBM VGA8, then
            ui-monospace, DejaVu Sans Mono, Liberation Mono, Menlo, Consolas.
            Base 15px at 1.35. The title is 26px bold, tracked 0.12em, yellow
            with a 3px brown drop. Message headers are 15px bold black on
            dark cyan.
        layout:
            A 1200px screen on black. A banner row of light, medium and dark
            shade blocks in blue and cyan, then BRIGHTWORK CHAT in yellow with
            a cyan caller line, then a row of half blocks, clipped by their row.
            Two columns, 350px and the reader, 20px apart. Every region is a
            navy box with a 4px double cyan rim and a yellow label cut into
            the top edge. Message boards lists hotkeys in brackets, G, D, M, B,
            R, the current board on a cyan band marked HERE, mobile-release
            with 4 NEW in green and billing-war-room with @1 FOR YOU in
            magenta. Direct lines lists people with a full block and ON-LINE,
            a half block and AWAY, a dot and OFF-LINE. The reader box is blue
            with a white rim, titled Reading the channel with 5 messages. Each
            message is a framed box whose cyan header bar reads MSG n/5, FROM
            and the name, and the time on the right. Aiko's message adds a
            line with a triangle and 3 REPLIES, read thread, +1 thumbs up x3
            and oo eyes x1. Priya's image is a blocky pixel preview with FILE
            ATTACHED and the filename. Then a magenta typing line and the
            prompt Enter text with the field and three keys, Attach, Emoji
            and a green Send, each with its hotkey letter highlighted. A grey
            footer bar lists the caller, board and keys. Below 780px the
            columns stack.
        spacing: A character grid. 10px between message frames, 20px between boxes.
        density: Busy and full. Every region boxed and a header bar on every message.
        corners: Square.
        borders: 4px double cyan rims with the label cut into the top edge, 1px cyan message frames.
        shadows: Only a hard 3px brown drop under the title text.
        icons: Block glyphs, full block on-line, half block away, dot off-line, triangles for thread and HERE, always with words.
        focus: A solid yellow block with black text.
        tone: Shouty sysop labels, such as 4 NEW, @1 FOR YOU, FILE ATTACHED and Enter text.

    style349:
        number: 349
        run: 71
        screen: TeamChat
        name: Rugged radio
        idea: The chat as a rugged field handset, with a rubber housing, a channel knob and chunky rocker keys around a black screen that logs every message as an RX or TX transmission, and one safety orange for the live channel and Send.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/349.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #111213, behind the handset and the style sheet
            rubber: #232528, the housing and sheet cards
            rubber2: #2e3135, inset panels and key tops
            edge: #4a4e54, moulded rims and key edges
            screen: #0a0b0c, the message screen and fields
            ink: #eceae4, text
            muted: #a9adb3, times, labels and channel numbers
            orange: #ff8a1f, the live channel, Send, TX and focus, with text #1f0e00
            amber: #ffb45c, panel labels, RX and typing
            green: #7fe08a, the MSG count tag and in range bars
            red: #ff7b6b, the CALL mention tag
        type:
            A condensed sans, Roboto Condensed, Arial Narrow, DejaVu Sans
            Condensed, Liberation Sans Narrow, with font stretch condensed,
            plus a monospace, ui-monospace, DejaVu Sans Mono, Menlo, Consolas,
            for readouts. Base 15px. Screen title 24px at 800 in capitals,
            names 13px at 800 capitals tracked 0.06em, message text 16px,
            readouts and tags 11px to 12px mono bold.
        layout:
            The whole app is one handset, a rubber housing with 28px corners,
            a 2px moulded edge, inset highlights and two screw heads in the top
            corners. A top bar holds BRIGHTWORK in orange with CHAT, a mono
            model line naming operator Mara Okafor, and two LEDs with Link up
            and RX. Two columns, 300px of controls and the screen. The control
            column stacks three inset panels with amber mono labels. Channel
            selector shows a drawn knob pointing at channel 2 beside Tuned to
            CH 2, design-crit. Channels are five rocker keys numbered CH 1 to
            CH 5 with a hard ledge below, the current one solid orange with an
            ON AIR tag, mobile-release with a green triangle 4 MSG tag,
            billing-war-room with a red @ 1 CALL tag. Direct lines shows
            signal bars, full for Priya with In range, two of three for Jonas
            with Standby, crossed out for Aiko with Out of range. The screen is
            a black well with an inset shadow, titled CH 2 and design-crit in
            orange over a dashed rule. Each message is a transmission row with
            a 4px left bar, a mono RX or TX and the time, then the name in
            capitals and the text. Mara's row is TX with an orange bar. Aiko's
            row adds keys for Thread, 3 replies in orange and Thumbs up 3 and
            Eyes 1. The image is a small preview with an IMAGE tag and the
            filename. A radio wave icon with Priya is typing ends the screen.
            Under both columns a keypad row holds Attach and Emoji rocker
            keys, the field in a black well and a wide orange Send key. Below
            860px everything stacks and Send spans the row.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 28px housing padding, 20px between panels, 10px between transmissions.
        density: Medium. Large touch keys around a compact log.
        corners: 28px housing, 16px panels and Send, 10px to 12px keys, round screws and LEDs.
        borders: A 2px moulded edge on the housing, 1px edges on keys, a 4px left bar on each transmission.
        shadows: Hard 3px to 5px ledges under keys, an inset well around the screen and a deep drop under the housing.
        icons: Thick 2.4 stroke line icons. Presence as signal bars, full, two of three or crossed out, beside the words.
        focus: A 3px safety orange outline offset 3px.
        tone: Radio talk, such as ON AIR, 4 MSG, 1 CALL, In range, Standby and Out of range.
    style350:
        number: 350
        run: 71
        screen: TeamChat
        name: Dispatch console
        idea: The chat as an emergency dispatch screen, where channels wait in a prioritised call queue, messages land as timestamped log entries in ruled columns, and people are units marked available, away or offline.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/350.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #080d14, the page, fields and the style sheet
            panel: #0f1824, the queue, log and units panes
            head: #16233a, pane headers, the status strip and function keys
            grid: #253850, every rule and the 1px gaps between panes
            ink: #e3ecf7, text
            muted: #9fb1c7, column heads, states and CLEAR
            cyan: #38bdf8, the open line, times, Send and focus, with text #03202f
            p1: #ff7a7a, the P1 mention tag on #3a1218
            p2: #ffc04d, the P2 unread tag, away and the live strip on #33260a
            ok: #4ade80, available
        type:
            A sans, Inter, Segoe UI, system-ui, Roboto, Arial, at 13px with
            tabular numbers, and a monospace, ui-monospace, JetBrains Mono,
            DejaVu Sans Mono, Menlo, Consolas, for times, tags and headers.
            Pane headers 11px mono bold capitals tracked 0.12em, channel names
            14px at 650, message text 14px, the clock 16px mono.
        layout:
            A full width console. A status strip with a 2px cyan rule below
            reads BRIGHTWORK CHAT DISPATCH, Console 2, Operator Mara Okafor,
            Channel design-crit, and a large clock on the right. An amber live
            strip below reads Live, Priya is typing, with a pulse icon. Three
            panes, 300px queue, the log and 230px units, divided by 1px gaps
            that show the grid colour. Call queue lists channels by priority,
            each row with a 4px left bar and a tag, billing-war-room first with
            a red diamond P1 tag and 1 mention for you, then mobile-release
            with an amber triangle P2 tag and 4 unread waiting, then
            design-crit with a solid cyan dot OPEN tag and Active on this
            console, then general and random with outlined dash CLEAR tags and
            Nothing waiting. The log has column heads Time, Unit, Entry and
            Links, and ruled zebra rows with the time in cyan mono, a small
            initials code and the name, the text, and a links column. Aiko's
            row is selected with a cyan inset bar and its links read Thread, 3
            replies, Thumbs up x3 and Eyes x1. The image is a bordered chip,
            IMG and the filename, with Attachment, image in links. Units lists
            people with a full square and AVAILABLE, a half filled square and
            AWAY, an empty square and OFFLINE. Under the panes a New entry row
            holds the field and F1 Attach, F2 Emoji and a cyan F12 Send key.
            Below 1080px units move under, below 720px rows stack with the
            time on the left.
        spacing: A 4px unit. 8px by 12px cells, 1px gaps between panes.
        density: High. Queue, log and units all visible at once, every row ruled.
        corners: 2px on keys, fields and tags. Panes are square.
        borders: 1px grid rules, a 4px left bar coloured by priority and a 2px cyan rule under the strip.
        shadows: None. Selection is an inset 3px cyan bar.
        icons: Shape codes before every state, diamond P1, triangle P2, dot OPEN, dash CLEAR, and full, half or empty squares for units.
        focus: A 2px cyan outline with a 4px deep cyan halo.
        tone: Operational shorthand, such as Call queue, 4 unread waiting, Units, New entry and F12 Send.
    style351:
        number: 351
        run: 71
        screen: TeamChat
        name: Pager LCD
        idea: The chat as a stack of two way pagers, where every message is its own small backlit LCD frame counted MSG 1/5 in a moulded shell, folders replace the sidebar, and pill shaped hardware keys stand in for buttons.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/351.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #0e1013, the desk behind the pagers and the style sheet
            shell: #1d2126, pager housings and sheet cards
            bezel: #05070a, the ring around each LCD
            lcd: #0a1a26, the backlit screen ground
            seg: #a8dcff, lit segments, the selection block and focus
            segDim: #6f9fc0, frame headers, FR and hints
            segOff: #17344a, unlit dashed separators only
            key: #3a4048, rubber keys
            label: #b5bcc6, printed shell labels
            sendKey: #5fbde8, the Send key, with dark text #04192a
        type:
            LCD text in a monospace, Lucida Console, DejaVu Sans Mono,
            ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas, bold 14px capitals tracked 0.06em.
            Message bodies 15px bold in normal case. Frame headers 12px.
            Shell print in system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Arial, 11px at 600 in
            capitals tracked 0.2em.
        layout:
            Every region is a pager, a moulded shell with 22px top and 30px
            bottom corners, a printed label and a small glowing LED, holding a
            backlit LCD with a black inset bezel and faint scan lines. The top
            row has a 280px Folders pager and a wide status pager. Folders
            lists Channels and Direct under dashed headers. The current
            channel is an inverse lit block with a triangle and OPEN,
            mobile-release has an envelope and 4 NEW, billing-war-room an
            exclamation mark and @1, people a filled, half or empty circle
            with ON, AWAY or OFF. The status pager shows the channel name in
            18px, then 5 MSG, battery and signal icons and the clock, a ticker
            line Priya is typing with a block cursor, and a dim line naming
            user Mara Okafor, the folder and 1 thread, with three small pill
            keys below, previous, Read and next. Under it the five messages
            tile as separate pagers in a grid of about 330px columns. Each LCD
            has a header MSG n/5 with the time, FR and the name, then the text.
            Mara's header adds sent. Aiko's frame ends with an inverse Thread
            3 RE block, +1 thumbs x3 and eyes x1. Priya's image is a pixel
            preview with IMG ATTACHED and the underlined filename. A wide
            Reply pager holds a TX prompt field and three hardware pill keys,
            Attach, Emoji and a blue Send, labelled underneath. Below 820px
            all pagers stack in one column.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px between pagers, 10px by 12px inside each LCD.
        density: Low per frame. One message per screen, frames tiled three across.
        corners: 22px top and 30px bottom on shells, 6px on LCDs, full pills on keys.
        borders: A 2px black inset bezel on every LCD and dashed unlit lines inside.
        shadows: A soft 10px drop under shells and 2px to 3px ledges under keys.
        icons: LCD glyphs, a triangle for open, an envelope for new, an exclamation mark for mention, filled, half and empty circles for presence, each beside a word.
        focus: A 2px dashed lit blue outline offset 3px.
        tone: Clipped pager words, such as MSG 2/5, FR, 4 NEW, 3 RE, IMG ATTACHED and TX.
    style352:
        number: 352
        run: 71
        screen: TeamChat
        name: Neon arcade
        idea: The chat as an arcade cabinet, with a glowing marquee, a black bezelled screen where channels are stages and people are players with pixel faces, and a control panel of big round coloured buttons for attach, emoji and send.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/352.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            void: #07040d, the room behind the cabinet and the style sheet
            cabinet: #140b24, cabinet sides and sheet cards
            screen: #05030a, the game screen ground
            trim: #3a1f5c, dashed dividers and card rims
            ink: #f5f0ff, message text
            muted: #b9a8d9, labels and offline
            magenta: #ff4fd8, the marquee tube, the channel title, Send and the mention badge
            cyan: #3ff5ff, section heads, Attach and the thread token
            yellow: #ffe94f, scores, times, the current stage and focus
            lime: #9dff57, the NEW badge, ready and typing
            orange: #ff9a3c, the fourth player colour
        type:
            Labels in a monospace, Press Start 2P, ui-monospace, DejaVu Sans
            Mono, Menlo, Consolas, bold. Message text in system-ui, Segoe UI,
            Roboto, Arial at 16px. Marquee 30px at 900 with a two layer
            glow, names 13px at 800 in each player's colour, times 12px
            yellow, section heads 12px capitals tracked 0.16em in cyan.
        layout:
            A 1120px cabinet. The marquee is a purple box with a 3px magenta
            neon rim and glow, BRIGHTWORK CHAT in glowing pale tube letters
            with WORK in cyan, and a yellow coin slot with Player Mara Okafor
            and Insert coin. The cabinet body frames a black bezel with 26px
            corners around the screen. The screen splits into a 300px side and
            the feed, divided by a dashed trim line. Select stage lists
            channels, the current one in a yellow box with a triangle,
            mobile-release with a lime 4 NEW badge and billing-war-room with a
            magenta @1 YOU badge. Players lists people with an 8 by 8 pixel
            face and a state line, triangle READY online in lime, bars PAUSE
            away in yellow and a cross OUT offline in muted. A HUD row shows
            the channel title in magenta and Stage 2, Msgs 5 and Threads 1 as
            yellow scores. Messages have a 40px pixel face, the name in the
            player colour and a yellow time, then the text. Mara is labelled
            1P. Aiko's message adds tokens with a pixel thumb x3, pixel eyes x1
            and a cyan 3 replies, continue token. The image is a pixel preview
            in a glowing cyan frame with IMG and the filename. Typing is a lime
            caps line. Below the screen a control panel with a cyan top edge
            holds a drawn joystick, the Enter message field and three round
            arcade buttons, cyan Attach, yellow Emoji and magenta Send, each
            glowing with its word below. Below 860px the screen stacks, the
            joystick hides and the buttons spread across.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 22px cabinet padding, 14px bezel, 12px between messages.
        density: Medium. A full feed on one screen and big targets on the panel.
        corners: 18px marquee top, 26px bezel, 16px screen, 4px tokens and badges, round arcade buttons.
        borders: A 3px neon marquee rim, 2px dashed trim dividers on the screen and 2px token rims.
        shadows: Coloured glows of 8px to 18px on neon text, buttons and the current stage, and inset shading under the buttons.
        icons: 8 by 8 pixel art, faces, a thumb and eyes. States use a triangle, bars or a cross beside the word.
        focus: A 3px yellow outline offset 3px with a yellow glow.
        tone: Coin op playful, such as Select stage, Players, 4 NEW, @1 YOU, 1P and continue.
    style353:
        number: 353
        run: 71
        screen: TeamChat
        name: Night market
        idea: The chat as an evening market lane, where channels are stalls under striped awnings, the current stall glows under a string of paper lanterns, and messages hang as warm wooden tags.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/353.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            night: #140a09, the page, fields and the style sheet
            dusk: #1f100d, the lane and neighbour panels
            wood: #2b1712, stall boards and sheet cards
            wood2: #371e17, message tags and wooden keys
            seam: #5a3326, borders, strings and tag holes
            paper: #f6e6cc, text
            muted: #d6b998, times, notes and offline
            lantern: #ff6a4a, lanterns and Send, with text #2a0805
            red: #e0523f, your tag edge and the awning stripes
            mentionPill: #b8321f, the mention pill behind text #fff4ee
            glow: #ffb35c, the current stall, the unread pill, the thread ticket, typing and focus
            jade: #8fd6a8, the green button inside the image preview only
        type:
            A warm serif, Hoefler Text, Iowan Old Style, Constantia, Palatino
            Linotype, Georgia, for the title at 34px weight 600 with a red
            glow, stall names 17px and message names 16px. A humanist sans,
            Avenir Next, Avenir, Segoe UI, system-ui, Roboto, for text at
            15px to 16px and 12px capitals tracked 0.18em for small labels.
        layout:
            A header like a night sky with a dim red radial glow and a curved
            string of eight round red paper lanterns, each with a soft halo,
            clipped by the header. Below, a sign reads Brightwork Chat, the
            night market, over design-crit, with Wandering as Mara Okafor on
            the right. Channels are five stall cards in a row, each with a
            scalloped striped awning on top and a wooden board below. The
            current stall has a red and cream awning, a glowing amber rim and
            You are here with a star. mobile-release shows an amber pill with
            a dot and 4 unread, billing-war-room a deep red pill with @ 1
            mention, the others Quiet tonight. Then two columns, the lane and
            a 270px Neighbours panel. The lane is titled At the design-crit
            stall with five notes hung today. Each message is a wooden tag
            with a string hole on the left, a 3px left edge, the serif name and
            time, then the text, and every other tag steps in 28px. Mara's tag
            has a red edge. Aiko's tag carries dashed paper tickets for thumbs
            up 3 and eyes 1 and an amber 3 replies ticket. The image is a warm
            preview over Image and the filename. Typing is an italic serif
            line with a small lantern. The composer is a counter with an
            attach key, the field, an emoji key and a glowing lantern red
            Send pill. Neighbours shows a lit lantern with Lantern lit,
            online, a half lit lantern with Turned low, away and a dashed
            unlit lantern with Unlit, offline. Below 980px stalls go three
            across and neighbours move under, below 640px stalls go two across.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 12px between stalls, 14px between tags, 20px lane padding.
        density: Relaxed. Alternate tags step in so the lane meanders.
        corners: 14px panels, tags with 4px left and 14px right corners, scalloped awnings, a pill Send.
        borders: A 1px seam on panels and stalls, a 3px left edge on tags and dashed edges on reaction tickets.
        shadows: Warm glows only, around lanterns, the current stall and Send.
        icons: Paper lanterns for presence, lit, half lit or dashed unlit, each with a word. Line icons at 2 stroke for attach, emoji and reactions.
        focus: A 2px amber glow outline offset 3px with a soft 6px amber halo.
        tone: Warm and storybook, such as You are here, Quiet tonight, Neighbours and five notes hung today.

    style354:
        number: 354
        run: 72
        screen: VideoEditor
        name: Pro NLE
        idea: A professional dark grey editing room, four tight panels butted together on a near black frame, tabbed headers, 12px type, and precise yellow timecode as the one voice that speaks loudly.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/354.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            frame: #0f0f10, the near black frame between panels and the page
            panel: #232325, panel bodies, inspector and bin rows
            header: #1c1c1e, tab strips, ruler and track lanes
            trackHead: #2a2a2d, track header cells and transport buttons
            rule: #38383b, row rules and field borders
            ink: #e6e6e6, text
            muted: #a8a8a8, labels, inactive tabs and meta
            timecode: #ffd84d, timecode, active tab rule, Export and focus
            value: #8fb8ff, scrubbable inspector values and media icons
            videoClip: #35557a, video clips
            titleClip: #6a4c93, title clips
            audioClip: #2c6448, audio clips
            clipEdge: #8fb0d8, the light 1px edge that outlines video clips, with lilac and green twins for titles and audio
            playhead: #d63a2f, playhead flag and line
            marker: #5ad1a8, the cut to logo marker flag
        type:
            One system sans stack, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
            Arial, and a mono stack, ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas.
            Base 12px at 1.45. The big timecode is mono 18px at 600 in yellow,
            the duration mono 13px, tab labels 12px at 600, clip labels 11px,
            ruler and bin durations mono 10px to 12px. The title card on the
            monitor is 30px light weight.
        layout:
            A one line menu bar holds a yellow square B, Brightwork Cut, Launch
            teaser with 1080p and 24 fps, then the render readout with an empty
            circle, Render 0% and not started beside a thin bar, and a yellow
            Export button. Below, four panels butt together on a black frame
            with 2px gutters. The left panel is a tabbed bin table with columns
            Name, Duration as full timecode and Type, each row led by a film or
            bars icon. The centre is the program monitor with a dashed safe
            area, the title card, then the yellow current timecode on the left,
            five square transport buttons in the middle and the duration on the
            right. The right panel is Effect controls with grouped rows Motion,
            Opacity and Transition, values in blue mono with a dotted underline.
            The timeline spans the full width with a 112px track header column,
            track ids V2, V1, A1 and A2 with names and an eye or speaker icon, a
            ruler in timecode every 10 seconds, solid clips in steel blue,
            purple and green with a light edge, the selected title clip with a
            white outline and the word selected, a red playhead flag reading 18s
            and a green flag marker labelled cut to logo. Below 1080px the bin
            moves under the monitor. At phone width the bin and inspector hide,
            transport buttons grow to 44px, track headers shrink to the ids and
            every other ruler label hides.
        spacing: A 4px base. Panels touch with 2px black gutters, rows are 24px, track lanes 38px.
        density: High. Bin, monitor, inspector and a full four track timeline share one screen.
        corners: 2px on buttons, clips and the logo. Panels are square.
        borders: 1px black separators, 1px #38383b row rules and a 1px light edge on every clip. No outlines on panels.
        shadows: None. Depth comes from three grey steps.
        icons:
            Thin 1.4 stroke line icons at 14px. Film frame for video, vertical
            bars for audio, eye and speaker on tracks, filled triangle for play.
            The marker is a pentagon flag and the playhead a notched red tag.
        focus: A 2px timecode yellow outline offset 1px on every control.
        tone: Terse professional labels such as Program, Effect controls and 5 items.
    style355:
        number: 355
        run: 72
        screen: VideoEditor
        name: Colour grade suite
        idea: A neutral eighteen percent grey grading room where scopes flank the picture, the inspector becomes a row of round wheels, and the bin is a strip of numbered thumbnails above a thin graticule timeline.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/355.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            roomGrey: #1f1f1f, page and style sheet, kept neutral so colour judgement stays true
            panel: #2a2a2a, scope, viewer and wheel panels
            well: #242424, wheel wells and thumbnail cards
            scopeBlack: #121212, scope screens and the picture surround
            graticule: #4c4c4c, scope grid, wheel rims and lane edges
            ink: #e2e2e2, text
            muted: #ababab, labels, units and notes
            puck: #f0f0f0, wheel pucks, lit ticks, playhead and vectorscope dot
            trace: #bff0b4, the waveform luma trace
            neutralButton: #d4d4d4, Export, play and the selected clip, never a hue
            focusAmber: #f2b33d, focus outline and the marker, the one warm note
        type:
            One system sans stack for interface text and a mono stack for
            numbers. Base 13px at 1.45. Panel heads 11px at 600 in caps tracked
            0.14em with a lighter aside. The timecode is mono 17px at 500, wheel
            values mono 16px, graticule and ruler mono 9px to 10px. The title
            card uses a serif stack, Iowan Old Style, Palatino, Georgia, at up
            to 26px.
        layout:
            A slim header holds a small round hue wheel mark, Brightwork Cut, a
            slash, Launch teaser, a mono pill reading 1080p and 24 fps, then a
            thin render bar with Render 0% and a dashed box saying idle, and a
            light grey Export button. The suite is a three column grid. The left
            panel is a waveform scope on black with a 0 to 100 graticule and a
            pale green trace, low along the floor with a cluster near 90 in the
            middle third. The centre is the viewer with a 6px grey surround,
            then the timecode, three round transport buttons with a light grey
            play, and of plus the duration. The right panel is a vectorscope
            with two rings, crosshairs and six small target squares labelled R,
            Mg, B, Cy, G and Yl, and one white dot at the centre. A full width
            Inspector row shows four wheels, Position as a crosshair wheel with
            a centred puck and X 960 Y 540, Scale and Opacity as full white
            rings reading 100 percent, and Cross dissolve as a ring of 24 ticks
            with 12 lit reading 12 frames, each with a short note. A full width
            Media strip shows five numbered thumbnail cards with an image or
            bars glyph, the file name and duration with V or A. A thin Timeline
            panel last has 18px lanes on a faint graticule, grey clips with a
            grey edge, the selected title clip filled light grey with a diamond,
            an amber marker triangle with a dashed line and a white playhead
            with an up triangle and 18. At phone width only the viewer and the
            timeline remain.
        spacing: An 8px unit with 12px gaps between panels and 14px panel padding.
        density: Medium high. Scopes, picture, four wheels, a thumbnail strip and a thin timeline.
        corners: 8px panels, 6px buttons and cards, round transport buttons and wheels.
        borders: 1px #383838 panel edges and 1px #8a8a8a clip edges. Scopes sit borderless on black.
        shadows: A soft drop shadow under each wheel only, and a 6px grey surround on the picture.
        icons:
            Filled transport glyphs in round buttons. Wheels and rings show
            state by shape, always with the written value beneath. A diamond
            marks the selected clip, a down triangle the marker.
        focus: A 2px amber outline offset 2px, the only warm colour on the screen.
        tone: Technical and calm, such as Waveform luma, Puck centred and 12 of 24 ticks.
    style356:
        number: 356
        run: 72
        screen: VideoEditor
        name: Cinemascope
        idea: The editor framed as a widescreen film, with solid black letterbox bars carrying opening titles and the export, a 2.39 to 1 picture, and the bin and inspector set below as centred end credits with dotted leaders.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/356.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            letterbox: #000000, the top and bottom bars and the picture itself
            auditorium: #0e0c0a, the warm dark between the bars and the style sheet
            seat: #16130f, swatch and control cells
            rule: #3a3226, hairline rules framing the timeline
            leader: #5c5243, dotted credit leaders and the render line
            ivory: #efe6d2, text, the playhead and focus
            parchment: #a89e8a, small caps labels and italic asides
            clip: #8a7b5c, clip bars and outlined buttons
            marqueeGold: #d9b56a, the title, section caps, the selected clip, marker and Export
        type:
            Display is a Didone stack, Didot, Bodoni 72, Bodoni MT, Hoefler
            Text, Georgia. Body is a book serif stack, Iowan Old Style,
            Palatino, Georgia, 15px at 1.6. Labels are system sans in caps,
            widely tracked. The title Launch teaser is 44px caps tracked 0.32em
            in gold, the picture card Didone italic up to 38px, the timecode
            serif italic 18px, credit heads sans 13px caps tracked 0.42em,
            credit roles serif italic and credit values sans 13px tracked
            0.14em.
        layout:
            The page is a film. A solid black top bar centres Brightwork Cut in
            tracked caps with an italic presents, then the gold title, then
            1080p and 24 fps in tracked caps. Between the bars a warm near black
            stage holds a centred picture at 2.39 to 1 on black with a faint
            gold spill beneath, the timecode set like an italic subtitle with of
            and the duration, and three bare transport glyphs with play inside a
            thin gold ring. Below, The Timeline is centred in tracked gold caps
            with an italic aside, and the tracks run as hairline rows. Clips are
            thin 4px bars with italic names sitting above them, the selected
            title bar gold, ringed, and followed by a star and the word
            selected. A gold triangle marker with an italic cut to logo and a
            dotted drop line sits at 84 seconds, and an ivory playhead with an
            up triangle and 18. Then two centred credit columns, Featuring the
            bin with file names and durations joined by dotted leaders, and
            Title card with Position 960 by 540, Scale 100 percent, Opacity 100
            percent and Cross dissolve 12 frames the same way. A solid black
            bottom bar holds a hairline render line with Render 0% and not yet
            begun beside a gold Export in tracked caps. At phone width the bars
            shrink, the credits hide and the track names reduce to their ids.
        spacing: Generous. 40px letterbox bars, 56px between acts, 64px between credit columns.
        density: Low. One wide picture, one thin timeline, two short credit lists.
        corners: None anywhere except the round play ring.
        borders: Hairline rules and dotted leaders only.
        shadows: A faint gold spill below the picture, as if from a projector.
        icons: Very few. Filled transport glyphs, a triangle for the marker, a star for the selection. No icon boxes.
        focus: A 2px ivory outline offset 3px.
        tone: Cinematic and courteous, such as presents, Featuring and not yet begun.
    style357:
        number: 357
        run: 72
        screen: VideoEditor
        name: Film reel
        idea: An editing bench of real film, where every track is a strip of amber celluloid with sprocket holes, audio runs as an optical soundtrack, media sits in labelled film cans and grease pencil marks the selection and the marker.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/357.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            bench: #120c08, page, rack ground and the style sheet
            darkroom: #0d0805, header, rack well and sprocket hole shade
            cueCard: #1d140d, the cue card and swatch cells
            celluloid: #3b2612, film strip base and the gate
            frame: #5a3a1a, picture clips as frames on the strip
            labelTape: #eadcc0, can labels, the header tape and play
            ink: #ecdfca, text
            muted: #b29f86, small typewritten asides
            amber: #f2b25c, section titles, timecode, track ids, Export and focus
            edgeCode: #ffd08c, clip names printed on the strip
            greasePencil: #ffb39e, selection loop, marker cross and handwritten notes
        type:
            Labels and data use a typewriter stack, American Typewriter, Courier
            Prime, Courier New. Section titles use a hand stack, Bradley Hand,
            Segoe Print, Chalkboard SE, Comic Neue, at 22px in amber. Body is
            system sans 14px. The timecode is typewriter 20px bold in amber, the
            picture card typewriter up to 32px, edge codes typewriter 11px bold,
            notes in the hand stack.
        layout:
            The header shows a strip of cream label tape, slightly tilted, split
            by dashed tears into Brightwork Cut, Launch teaser, 1080p and 24
            fps. On the right a tiny film strip of 16 empty frames reads 0%
            rendered and no frames yet, then an amber pill Export with a reel
            icon and a solid lip. The bench is a grid. The Gate takes the left
            with the viewer framed by celluloid and round sprocket holes down
            both sides, then amber timecode, round transport buttons with a
            cream play, and reel length with the duration. The Cue card on the
            right lists Position 960 by 540, Scale 100 percent, Opacity 100
            percent and Cross dissolve 12 frames in typewriter rows with dashed
            rules, and a handwritten note. Cans fill a full row, five round film
            cans with cream tape labels giving name, duration and picture or
            sound. The Splice rack shows each track as an amber film strip with
            sprocket holes along both edges, picture clips as frames divided by
            dark frame lines with a light edge, audio clips with an optical
            soundtrack wave and the name printed as edge code. The selected
            title frame has a dashed grease pencil loop, a cross and the
            handwritten word selected. A grease pencil cross and dashed line
            mark cut to logo, and a cream playhead with a down triangle reads 18
            s. At phone width the cans and cue card hide and track labels reduce
            to ids.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between bench areas, 8px between strips.
        density: Medium. Gate, cue card, five cans and four strips.
        corners: Round cans and transport buttons, 22px pill Export, 2px to 6px on strips and cards.
        borders: Frame lines are 2px dark bars with a 2px #c08a4a edge along each frame, the cue card has dashed rules, tape has dashed tears.
        shadows: Heavy drop shadows under cans and the gate, a 3px solid lip under Export.
        icons: Filled transport glyphs, a reel on Export, a cross for selected and for the marker. Film cans and sprocket holes are drawn with gradients.
        focus: A 3px amber outline offset 3px.
        tone: Workshop talk, such as Cans, Splice rack, reel length and no frames yet.
    style358:
        number: 358
        run: 72
        screen: VideoEditor
        name: Broadcast control
        idea: The editor as a television control room multiviewer, a black wall of tiles each named by an under monitor label with a tally box, the program tile ringed red and marked ON AIR, sources as small monitors with level meters, and the timeline as a rundown strip.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/358.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            wall: #000000, the monitor wall and gaps between tiles
            tile: #08080a, tile faces and the style sheet
            umd: #1b1b1f, under monitor label bars, header cells and list rows
            button: #26262c, transport and secondary buttons
            ink: #f2f2f2, text
            muted: #a9a9b2, field names and track roles
            tallyRed: #ff3b30, program ring, ON AIR dot and the playhead
            exportRed: #d92a20, Export button and playhead tag behind white text
            onAirText: #ff5c52, the ON AIR word
            tallyGreen: #30d158, preview ring, PVW tag and play
            readout: #7dff9a, inspector values
            amber: #ffb000, the clock, the router badge and focus
            cue: #ffcc4d, durations and the cut to logo marker
        type:
            Labels use a condensed stack, Arial Narrow, Roboto Condensed,
            Liberation Sans Narrow, Arial, at 14px, bold and tracked 0.1em in
            under monitor labels. Numbers use a mono stack. The clock is mono
            40px bold in amber, readouts mono 14px in green, durations mono
            12px. The program title card is system sans 600 up to 32px.
        layout:
            A router strip on top shows Brightwork Cut on an amber block, then
            cells SHOW Launch teaser, FMT 1080p and RATE 24 fps. The wall is a
            four column grid of black tiles with 2px gaps. Program spans two by
            two on the left, ringed with a 3px red inset frame, and its label
            bar reads a red disc, PGM, LAUNCH TEASER and a red ON AIR. Four
            source tiles fill the right, SRC 1 to SRC 4, each a small monitor
            with a simple picture or a pair of green level meters, and a label
            bar with a flat dash tally, the file name and an amber duration. The
            third row holds SRC 5 with the logo, a preview tile ringed green
            with an engineering table of POSITION 960 x 540, SCALE 100 percent,
            OPACITY 100 percent and X DISSOLVE 12 FR and a label PVW TITLE CARD
            V2 SELECTED with a hollow green square, and a two column clock tile
            with the amber timecode, TRT and the duration, three flat transport
            buttons with a green play, RENDER with an empty bar and 0% STANDBY
            with a hollow square, and a red EXPORT block. A rundown tile spans
            the full width with track rows, clips as dark blue or dark green
            bars with a bright left edge, the selected title clip outlined green
            with a green PVW tag, an amber diamond CUT TO LOGO with a dotted
            line and a red playhead with a red 18 tag. At phone width only
            program, clock and rundown remain.
        spacing: 2px gaps between tiles, 8px to 14px inside tiles. Nothing else.
        density: High. Eight tiles and a rundown strip fill the wall.
        corners: Square everywhere, except the round ON AIR tally.
        borders: Tally rings are 3px inset frames, red for program and green for preview.
        shadows: None. Light comes only from the tiles.
        icons:
            Tally shapes are the main icons. A filled disc is on air, a hollow
            square is preview or standby, a flat dash is idle. Each sits beside
            a word. Transport uses filled glyphs.
        focus: A 3px amber outline offset 2px.
        tone: Control room shorthand in capitals, such as PGM, PVW, SRC 1, TRT and STANDBY.

    style359:
        number: 359
        run: 73
        screen: VideoEditor
        name: Creator playful
        idea: A bright creator app on deep plum, with chunky rounded cards, fat candy coloured clip pills that each track owns, stickers for the selection and the marker, and big friendly sliders in place of number fields.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/359.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            plum: #1a1433, page and style sheet
            card: #251d47, cards
            raised: #2f2659, clip chips, inspector rows and list rows
            lane: #1d163b, timeline lanes and fields
            ink: #f6f1ff, text
            lilac: #cfc4ec, secondary text and ruler
            bubblegum: #ff7ac6, V2 titles, the logo and the Export start
            sky: #6fd3ff, V1 video and video chips
            lime: #c6f36b, A1 voiceover, audio chips and play
            sunny: #ffd166, A2 music, counts, the marker pin and focus
            peach: #ffb36b, the Export gradient end
            darkOnBright: #2a0d24, text on every bright fill
        type:
            One rounded stack, ui-rounded, SF Pro Rounded, Nunito, Varela Round,
            Quicksand, system-ui. Base 15px at 1.5. The project title is 26px at
            800, card heads 20px at 800, the timecode 24px at 800, the viewer
            title up to 38px at 800, clip pills 13px at 800 and secondary text
            13px to 14px.
        layout:
            A top bar holds a tilted pink rounded square logo with a play shape
            and a sky offset shadow, Brightwork Cut over Launch teaser, two pill
            tags for 1080p and 24 fps, a dashed lime ring with 0% rendered and
            ready when you are beside a short rounded bar, and a big pink to
            peach pill Export with a solid lip. The layout is a two column grid
            of 28px rounded cards with solid offset shadows. The viewer card on
            the left has a rounded picture with a soft plum circle in the
            corner, a big lime round play between two round skip buttons, and
            the timecode with the duration below. On the right, Your clips lists
            five rounded chips with sky video or lime audio icon tiles, then
            Tweak the title shows Position 960 by 540 in a rounded row, chunky
            Scale and Opacity sliders at 100 percent with big white thumbs, and
            a Cross dissolve 12 frames row with a cross icon. A full width
            Timeline card shows each track as a coloured badge with icon, id and
            name, pink V2, sky V1, lime A1 and sunny A2, and clips as fat pills
            in the track colour with dark text. The selected title pill has a
            white ring and a tilted white sticker reading a check and Selected.
            A sunny pin with a flag reads cut to logo with a dashed drop line,
            and a white playhead has a round bubble reading 0 18. At phone width
            the clips and tweak cards hide and badges show only the ids.
        spacing: An 8px unit, generous. 20px card padding and gaps, 8px between lanes.
        density: Low to medium. Big targets, five clip chips, two sliders.
        corners: 28px cards, 18px rows, full pills for clips, tags and buttons.
        borders: None. Shape and colour blocks separate things.
        shadows: Solid offset shadows with no blur, 10px under cards and 5px to 6px under buttons.
        icons:
            Chunky rounded line icons at 2.2 stroke on coloured tiles. Each
            track has its own icon, a T for titles, a camera for video, a
            microphone for voiceover and a note for music. A check marks the
            selection and a flag the marker.
        focus: A 4px sunny yellow outline offset 3px.
        tone: Friendly and casual, such as Your clips, Tweak the title and ready when you are.
    style360:
        number: 360
        run: 73
        screen: VideoEditor
        name: Motion graphics
        idea: A motion design workspace on a blue black grid, where the inspector is a graph editor of glowing neon curves, every property owns a colour and a keyframe shape, and the timeline is a layer stack with diamond keyframes.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/360.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            void: #0a0c16, page ground with a 24px grid, and the style sheet
            grid: #141831, the background grid lines
            panel: #0d1020, panels and the header
            graphBed: #06070f, graph editor bed, viewer surround and fields
            edge: #262b52, panel borders and row rules
            ink: #e4e8ff, text
            muted: #a9b0d6, labels, axis numbers and durations
            opacityMagenta: #ff4fd8, opacity curve and diamonds, selection, Export
            scaleCyan: #3ff0ff, scale curve and squares, timecode, focus
            positionYellow: #f5ff5a, position X curve and circles, the marker
            positionGreen: #5affa0, position Y curve and triangles
            videoLayer: #22305e, video layer bars
            audioLayer: #173a33, audio layer bars
        type:
            Data uses a mono stack, ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas, at
            13px for body and values. Panel heads are system sans 11px at 700 in
            caps tracked 0.16em with a mono aside. The timecode is mono 18px at
            700 in cyan with a soft glow. Layer names are mono 11px, axis labels
            mono 10px.
        layout:
            The page ground is blue black with a visible 24px grid. A header
            holds a magenta curve mark, Brightwork Cut and Launch teaser,
            1920x1080 and 24 fps in mono, a thin render bar with RENDER QUEUE 0%
            and a hollow circle with queued, and a glowing magenta Export.
            Below, a three column workspace of square edged panels. Project
            lists the five files with a MOV or AUD tag, name and duration.
            Composition shows the picture with rule of thirds lines and a cyan
            anchor ring at the centre, then the glowing timecode, the duration
            and three small buttons with a cyan outlined play. Graph editor
            shows a legend, a magenta diamond for Opacity 100 percent, a cyan
            square for Scale 100 percent, a yellow circle for Position X 960, a
            green triangle for Position Y 540, and a hatched swatch for Cross
            dissolve 12 f, then a graph from 14 to 20 seconds where the magenta
            opacity curve eases from 0 to 100 across a shaded 12 frame band and
            holds, the other properties hold as flat lines, solid, dashed and
            dotted, each with its keyframe shape, and a white playhead at 18
            seconds 12 frames. A full width Layers panel stacks the tracks as
            rows with a diamond toggle, id and name, indigo or teal bars, the
            selected title bar in magenta with a glow and two diamond keyframes,
            a yellow down triangle cut to logo marker with a dashed line and a
            white playhead tagged 18s. At phone width the project and graph
            editor hide.
        spacing: A 4px base. 10px between panels, 10px to 12px inside them, 32px layer rows.
        density: High. Project list, composition, graph editor and layer stack in one view.
        corners: 4px panels and buttons, 3px layer bars.
        borders: 1px indigo panel borders over a visible 24px grid.
        shadows: Neon glows only, on curves, the timecode, Export and the selected layer.
        icons:
            Keyframe shapes are the icon set. Diamond for opacity, square for
            scale, circle for position X, triangle for position Y, a hatched
            band for the dissolve, repeated in the legend. Transport uses small
            filled glyphs.
        focus: A 2px cyan outline offset 2px with a soft cyan halo.
        tone: Technical motion terms, such as Composition, Graph editor, Layers and Render queue.
    style361:
        number: 361
        run: 73
        screen: VideoEditor
        name: Animation studio
        idea: A night animation desk where the viewer sits on a round light table disc with pencil construction lines, panels are punched cel sheets with peg holes, and the timeline is turned upright into an exposure sheet read top to bottom.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/361.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            nightDesk: #13161d, page, peg holes and the style sheet
            celSheet: #1d2230, punched cel panels and exposure cells
            sheetHead: #232a3b, exposure sheet column heads
            rule: #3a4258, sheet grid and dividers
            lightTable: #2b2a26, the warm disc behind the viewer
            ink: #e3e6ee, text
            graphite: #a5adbf, labels, units and start times
            holdLine: #8b95ad, hold lines running down a clip
            nonPhotoBlue: #8cc0ff, construction lines, the selection, Export and focus
            guideBlue: #4f7fb8, dashed construction guides in the viewer
            redPencil: #ff8f8f, the playhead row rules
            redPencilText: #ffb0b0, playhead and marker notes
        type:
            Headings and notes use a hand stack, Segoe Print, Bradley Hand,
            Chalkboard SE, Comic Neue, Marker Felt. Body is system sans 14px at
            1.5. The timecode and frame numbers use a mono stack, 20px bold and
            13px at 600. Panel titles are hand 20px bold, cel notes hand 19px,
            the pencil test title hand up to 28px bold.
        layout:
            A header holds a ruled slate with Brightwork Cut in blue hand
            lettering and cells Prod Launch teaser, Fmt 1080p and Rate 24 fps,
            then an empty render bar with Render 0% and not inked yet, and a
            blue Export with a pencil icon. The desk is two columns. Every panel
            is a cel sheet with three peg holes punched at the top, one round
            between two oblong. The left column holds Pencil test, the viewer
            set on an oval warm light table disc, the title card with dashed
            blue construction lines behind it, then the timecode, round flip
            buttons with a blue play and the duration. Under it sit two cels,
            Scene folder listing the five files as small punched sheets with
            duration and picture or sound, and Cel notes with Position 960 by
            540, Scale 100 percent, Opacity 100 percent and Cross dissolve 12
            frames handwritten on ruled lines. The right column is the Exposure
            sheet, the timeline turned upright, a table with columns Sec,
            Action, V2 titles, V1 video, A1 voice and A2 music and one row per 6
            seconds from 0 to 90. A clip writes its name and start in the row
            where it begins, a hold line runs down the rows it covers and a
            short rule reads end and the second where it stops. The selected
            title card is in pale blue with a star and a thicker blue hold line.
            The row at 18 is ruled above and below in red pencil with a play
            arrow and playhead 18 in Action, and Action at 84 reads a cross and
            cut to logo. At phone width the folder and notes hide, the Action
            column drops, the 84 row gets a red cross and a handwritten note
            under the sheet explains the marker and playhead.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between cels, 34px top padding to clear the peg holes, 36px sheet rows.
        density: Medium. A sixteen row exposure sheet beside the viewer, folder and notes.
        corners: Cels are 4px at the top and 10px at the bottom. The light table is an oval disc.
        borders: 1px sheet grid, 2px hold lines, 2px red rules round the playhead row.
        shadows: A soft 20px drop under each cel and a faint warm glow around the disc.
        icons: Few and drawn. Peg holes, a star for the selection, a cross for the marker, a play arrow on the playhead row and a pencil on Export.
        focus: A 2px dashed non photo blue outline offset 3px.
        tone: Studio words, such as Pencil test, Scene folder, Cel notes and not inked yet.
    style362:
        number: 362
        run: 73
        screen: VideoEditor
        name: Documentary muted
        idea: A quiet, desaturated editing page set like a documentary book, with a serif main column for picture and sequence, sources and settings as marginal notes, captions under every figure and the marker written as a footnote.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/362.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            ash: #1b1a18, page, picture surround and the style sheet
            leaf: #22211e, swatch and control cells
            rule: #3a3833, section rules and the marginal rule
            segment: #2e2c29, clip segments
            selected: #3d3a35, the selected clip
            hairline: #6a665e, clip edges, the render line and text button underlines
            ink: #e6e1d8, text, the playhead and the dagger
            caption: #bdb6aa, captions and the dek
            stone: #a8a196, small caps labels, track roles and durations
            paper: #d9d2c4, the Export button, the only filled control
        type:
            A book serif stack, Iowan Old Style, Palatino Linotype, Palatino,
            Georgia, for text at 17px and 1.6. Labels are system sans in small
            caps, 13px tracked 0.2em for sections and 12px tracked 0.14em for
            plate labels. The headline is serif 48px regular, the picture title
            serif up to 34px, captions and clip names serif italic 15px and
            14px, prose 17px at 1.7.
        layout:
            A centred book page about 1120px wide with wide margins. The header
            sets Brightwork Cut as a small caps kicker, Launch teaser as a large
            serif headline, and an italic dek, A sequence in 1080p at 24 frames
            per second. On the right a hairline render line with Rendered 0
            percent and an italic Not started, over a pale paper Export, the
            only filled control. A hairline closes the header. The main column
            holds the picture desaturated on near black with a caption, Plate 1,
            The program at the timecode of the duration, holding on the title
            card, then text buttons Back, Play and Forward with thin chevrons
            and underlines. The sequence follows under a small caps label,
            tracks as hairline rows with the id in sans and the role in italic,
            clips as quiet blocks with a hairline left edge and italic names,
            the selected title card brighter with a 3px ink edge, underlined and
            marked selected. A dagger on the ruler at 84 drops a dotted line, a
            thin ink playhead with a dot reads 18 s, a Plate 2 caption describes
            the figure and a footnote reads the dagger and Marker, cut to logo,
            at 84 seconds. A marginal column behind a hairline holds Sources, a
            numbered list of the five files with durations, and On the title
            card, a prose sentence giving position 960 by 540, scale 100
            percent, opacity 100 percent and a cross dissolve of 12 frames in
            bold. At phone width the margin hides and track roles drop.
        spacing: Book margins. 56px around the page, 48px between sections, 56px gutter to the margin column.
        density: Low. One picture, one sequence and two short marginal notes.
        corners: 2px on Export only. Everything else is square or open.
        borders: Hairline rules, a single marginal rule and underlined text buttons.
        shadows: None.
        icons: Barely any. Thin chevrons and a play triangle beside words, a dagger for the marker and a dot on the playhead.
        focus: A 1px ink outline with a second hairline ring, offset 4px.
        tone: Captioned and literary, such as Plate 1, The sequence, On the title card and Not started.
    style363:
        number: 363
        run: 73
        screen: VideoEditor
        name: Drive-in
        idea: A night at a drive-in, where the viewer is the big screen on its posts under a starry sky, a bulb lit marquee carries the title and Export, the bin is a row of parked cars with number plates, settings read like the snack bar board and tracks become parking lanes.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/363.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            nightSky: #0a0f2c, sky, page and style sheet
            horizon: #1a1f4a, the sky gradient foot
            asphalt: #14151f, the lot under the screen
            lane: #1b1c28, parking lanes
            marqueeBoard: #1a1206, the marquee face behind the bulbs
            ink: #eef0ff, text
            moonlight: #c3c8ec, secondary text, ruler and car posts
            bulbYellow: #ffd36b, marquee title, timecode, title clips, the marker and selection
            neonTeal: #4ff0d2, video clips, transport rings, lot signs and focus
            neonPink: #ff6fa8, audio clips, the ticket booth, Export and the snack bar
            laneLine: #e0c25a, dashed lane and parking bay lines
            screenWhite: #d7dae8, the big screen frame
            plate: #f2ead2, number plates on the cars
        type:
            Marquee lettering uses a condensed display stack, Haettenschweiler,
            Impact, Arial Narrow Bold, Oswald, in caps. Body uses a geometric
            stack, Futura, Century Gothic, Avenir Next, Trebuchet MS, 15px at
            1.5. The marquee title is 46px, the timecode 26px tracked 0.06em in
            bulb yellow, lot signs 20px caps, snack board values 20px, number
            plates mono 11px bold.
        layout:
            The upper band is a starry night sky. On the left a marquee sign
            with a border of round warm bulbs reads Now showing in pink tracked
            caps, Launch teaser in big yellow glowing letters, 1080p and 24 fps
            with a star, and an italic a Brightwork Cut picture. Hanging beneath
            is a ticket booth with a pink top edge, an empty render bar, Render
            0% and reel not rolling, and a wide pink Export in marquee caps. On
            the right stands the big screen, a white framed picture on two posts
            with a cool glow, then the yellow timecode, round teal ringed
            transport buttons with a teal play and running time with the
            duration. The lower band is asphalt. Parked tonight, a teal lot
            sign, heads a row of five parked car silhouettes in dashed yellow
            bays, each with a cream number plate showing the file name and a
            post label with duration and picture or sound. On the right a pink
            neon Snack bar board lists Position 960 by 540, Scale 100 percent,
            Opacity 100 percent and Cross dissolve 12 frames with dotted leaders
            like prices. Parking lanes spans the full width, each track a dark
            lane edged by dashed yellow lines, with the id in yellow marquee
            letters, video clips outlined teal, audio pink, and the selected
            title clip filled bulb yellow with a double border, a glow and a
            star. A yellow diamond road sign reads cut to logo with a solid drop
            line, and a white playhead under a faint projector beam reads 18 s.
            At phone width the marquee stacks over the screen and the cars and
            snack board hide.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 40px page gutters, 28px between ground areas, 46px lanes.
        density: Medium low. One big screen, a marquee, five cars, a menu board and four lanes.
        corners: 14px marquee, 10px booth and board, 8px clip blocks, round transport buttons.
        borders: A ring of bulbs round the marquee, dashed yellow lane lines, 2px neon outlines on clips.
        shadows: Glows only. Warm round the marquee, cool round the screen, neon round Export.
        icons: Car silhouettes for media, filled transport glyphs, a diamond road sign for the marker and a star for the selection.
        focus: A 3px neon teal outline offset 3px.
        tone: Playful night out, such as Now showing, Parked tonight, Snack bar board and reel not rolling.

    style364:
        number: 364
        run: 74
        screen: FinanceBudget
        name: Private wealth
        idea: A discreet private client statement in near black, with fine gold double rules, serif old style figures, a centred monogram and a framed goal arc, so money reads as quiet and well kept.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/364.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #0e1013, the page and the style sheet
            surface: #14171b, kept for hover rows
            gold: #c9a961, every rule, meter fills, the goal arc and the primary button
            goldText: #d9bf85, the brand, section heads, links, Fully drawn and focus
            line: #3a352a, hairlines between rows and meter tracks
            ink: #ece6d8, text and figures
            muted: #a8a193, labels, dates and notes
            within: #b0cba8, Within and money received
            exceeded: #eba496, Exceeded, the owed card balance and overspend hatching
            onGold: #17140c, text on the gold button
        type:
            Headings and figures use Iowan Old Style, Palatino Linotype, Palatino,
            Book Antiqua, Georgia with old style numerals. Labels use system-ui,
            Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial. Base 15px at 1.6. The title is
            40px at 400, centred. Holding figures are 38px serif with a small gold
            euro sign. Section heads are 17px serif small caps tracked .16em in gold
            text. Category names are 18px serif. Labels are 12px sans caps tracked
            .16em.
        layout:
            A centred 1040px statement. The masthead is a three part row, the brand
            in gold small caps on the left, a round gold ringed MO monogram in the
            centre and Mara Okafor with October statement in euros on the right,
            ruled below by a gold line with a dark hairline under it. Four tracked
            caps nav links sit centred below, Overview underlined in gold. The
            centred title Your October position has an italic note under it. A
            Holdings band follows, ruled gold above and below, holding three centred
            columns split by hairlines, Everyday account, Savings, and Credit card
            in rose with a clock and Owed, due 12 November. Below, a wide column
            holds the October allocations table with category, a hairline track with
            a 3px gold fill and a white tick at the limit, spent of limit, and a
            standing word on the right. A narrow column holds The goal in a double
            gold frame with a thin gold semicircle arc at 64 percent, 3,200 of 5,000
            saved, 1,800 remaining and the target date. Recent movements runs full
            width as a ruled list with date, serif payee and the amount with an
            arrow. A gold ruled footer closes the statement. Below 760px holdings
            stack, the table rows become two line blocks with the bar under them and
            the goal moves under the table.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 32px gutter, 56px between bands, 24 to 28px inside holdings.
        density:
            Low. Three holdings, five allocations, five movements and one goal with
            plenty of air.
        corners: None, except the round monogram and round swatches.
        borders:
            Gold 1px rules round the holdings and under the masthead, dark gold
            hairlines between rows, a double frame round the goal.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            Few and thin, 1em outline shapes beside words. A circle check for
            Within, a ruled square for Fully drawn, a triangle for Exceeded by 62,
            up and down arrows for movements and a clock for the due date. The
            overspent track turns into rose dashes past the limit tick.
        focus:
            A 1px gold text outline offset 4px with a second gold ring outside a
            page coloured gap.
        tone:
            Formal and discreet, such as Your October position, Holdings,
            Allocations, Recent movements and Exceeded by 62.
    style365:
        number: 365
        run: 74
        screen: FinanceBudget
        name: Neobank vibrant
        idea: A phone first bank on pure black with one electric volt accent, a giant tabular balance, round action buttons, fat rounded cards and pill meters, where overspend flips a tile to white instead of turning red.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/365.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            black: #000000, the page and the style sheet
            card: #151515, account cards, tiles, the goal and the transaction list
            cardTwo: #222222, raised cards, action circles, chips and fields
            line: #333333, pill tracks and the ring track
            white: #ffffff, text, meters and the inverted over budget tile
            muted: #a3a3a3, labels, decimals and dates
            volt: #d4ff3a, the single accent for the euro sign, Add money, the goal ring, income, money left and focus
            onVolt: #0b0d00, text on volt
        type:
            One system stack, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica
            Neue, Arial, heavy weights. Base 15px. The balance is 88px at 850
            tracked minus .05em with the euro sign and decimals at 44px, the sign in
            volt and decimals in muted. Tile figures are 30px at 850, section titles
            22px at 850, body 15px at 700 and badges 12px at 800.
        layout:
            A 1200px app. The top row has a volt rounded square b mark, the name, a
            pill tab group on the right with Home as a white pill, and an MO disc.
            Below, a 440px left column and a wide right column. The left column
            reads Hey Mara, here's October, then the giant everyday balance with
            Everyday account under it, three 60px round actions Add money in volt,
            Send and Move, two 28px rounded account cards for Savings and Credit
            card with a small chip outline and the figure at the bottom, the card
            one showing a clock and Due 12 Nov, then a goal card with a thick volt
            ring at 64 percent beside Japan trip, 3,200 of 5,000 and the date. The
            right column has October budget with 1,870 spent of 1,930, one segmented
            pill showing each category and a volt end for the 60 left, then a three
            by two grid of 24px tiles, one per category with a badge, the figure
            over the limit and a pill meter, plus a volt All budgets tile with 60
            left. Eating out is a white tile with black text, a black Over by 62
            badge and a black hatched pill. Latest is a rounded list with initials
            discs, the salary disc and amount in volt. Below 1100px the columns
            stack and tiles go two across.
        spacing:
            An 8px unit. 32px gutter, 48px between columns, 12px between cards, 18
            to 24px inside.
        density: Medium low. Big numbers first, then six tiles and a short feed.
        corners:
            Very round. 28px cards, 24px tiles, 20px rows, pills and circles for
            buttons, tabs and meters.
        borders: None. Cards separate from the black by fill alone.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            Bold glyphs in circles for actions and initials discs for payees. Badges
            pair a circle check with money left, a ruled square with Maxed and a
            triangle with Over by 62. A clock marks the due date.
        focus: A 3px volt outline offset 3px.
        tone:
            Casual second person, such as Hey Mara, here's October, 64 left, Maxed,
            Over by 62 and Latest.
    style366:
        number: 366
        run: 74
        screen: FinanceBudget
        name: Ledger night
        idea: The month kept as a bound ledger at night, a two page spread on green black with ruled lines and green column rules, monospace figures in pale ink, red ink in brackets for anything overdrawn or owed, and double underlined totals.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/366.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            desk: #08120d, the page behind the book and the style sheet
            leaf: #0d1c15, ledger pages, fields and rows
            rule: #24402f, the outer edge of the book
            column: #3b6a4f, ruled lines, column rules, double rules and field underlines
            paleInk: #e4ecd3, text, figures, totals and the primary button
            fadedInk: #a7b9a0, dates, folios, column heads and notes
            redInk: #ff9d91, bracketed overspend, owed and money out, the OVER stamp
            greenInk: #9ed9a8, money in, within marks and saved cells
        type:
            Particulars and headings use Georgia, Times New Roman, Cambria in
            italic. Figures, heads and dates use ui-monospace, Cascadia Mono, SF
            Mono, Menlo, Consolas. The title is 30px italic serif, section heads
            20px italic with an 11px mono caps note, particulars 16px italic,
            figures 14px mono tabular and column heads 11px mono caps tracked .1em.
        layout:
            A 1240px book. The title row has Brightwork Money then Ledger in italic,
            a mono caps line with Mara Okafor, October and euros, and mono nav links
            on the right, closed by a double green rule. Below sits one spread of
            two equal leaves split by a double gutter rule, each leaf ruled every
            32px with a folio line on top. The left leaf holds Accounts as a three
            column table, the card balance in red brackets with a clock and due 12
            Nov, then the Budget ledger with columns Category, Allowed, Spent,
            Remains and Mark, a totals row with a rule above and a double underline,
            and an italic note explaining the brackets. Eating out shows (62) in red
            and a tilted red boxed OVER 62 stamp. The right leaf holds the Journal
            with Date, Particulars, Fo., Out and In, payments as red bracketed
            figures in Out and the salary in green in In, with totals for five
            entries. Under it the Sinking fund for the Japan trip is a five by two
            grid of 500 euro cells, six filled green, one two fifths filled, three
            empty, beside Saved, Target, To go and Due. Below 900px the leaves
            stack. At 375px the folio column hides and cells tighten so every column
            fits.
        spacing: A 32px ruled line drives every row. 24px leaf padding and two equal leaves.
        density:
            High and tabular. Three accounts, five budget lines with totals, five
            journal entries with totals and a ten cell fund.
        corners: None.
        borders:
            Green column rules between every column, a 2px rule under heads, double
            rules for the gutter and title, a rule and double underline on totals.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            Very few small outline marks beside words. A circle check with within, a
            ruled square with closed, a triangle inside the tilted red OVER 62 stamp
            and a clock on the due date. Brackets mark negatives.
        focus: A 2px dashed pale ink outline with a slightly lighter green wash.
        tone:
            Bookkeeping words, such as Accounts, Budget ledger, Journal,
            Particulars, Remains, Sinking fund and OVER 62.
    style367:
        number: 367
        run: 74
        screen: FinanceBudget
        name: Market depth
        idea: The budget read as an order book, each category a mirrored depth row with spent growing left and remaining growing right from a central limit column, balances on a ticker strip, savings as a goal ladder and transactions as a trade tape.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/367.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            floor: #090c12, the page and the style sheet
            panel: #0f131b, the three desk panels, fields and rows
            head: #151b26, panel title bars, the ticker strip and the limit column
            grid: #232b3a, 1px gaps between panels and every row line
            ink: #dfe6f2, text and figures
            muted: #93a0b5, column heads, dates and side labels
            spent: #f2b45c, spent figures and spent depth bars
            remaining: #5fcbe3, remaining figures and bars, the primary button and focus
            over: #ff8593, deficit hatching, the OVER tag and the owed balance
            in: #7fe3a9, money in on the tape and filled goal levels
        type:
            One monospace stack, ui-monospace, JetBrains Mono, SF Mono, Menlo,
            Consolas, Liberation Mono. Base 13px. Position figures are 18px at 700,
            ticker figures 15px at 700, depth figures 14px at 700 in their side
            colour, panel heads 11px caps tracked .12em at 700.
        layout:
            A full width trading desk. The top strip holds a BW slash MONEY mark, a
            ticker of cells for Everyday, Savings, Credit card with a clock and DUE
            12 NOV in red, and Oct budget left 60, then MARA OKAFOR, EUR, OCT on the
            right. Below, three panels sit edge to edge with 1px grid gaps, 260px,
            flexible and 330px. The left panel lists Positions and then a Goal
            ladder for the Japan trip, ten stacked levels of 500 from 500 at the
            bottom to 5,000 at the top, six filled green and the seventh two fifths,
            with 3,200 of 5,000 filled and the target under it. The centre panel is
            Budget depth with a header reading spent, limit, remaining. Each
            category is a 52px row with a framed central cell holding the name in
            caps and its limit. To the left an amber translucent bar grows from the
            centre to the share of the limit spent, with the spent figure on its
            end. To the right a cyan bar grows by the share remaining. Rent shows 0
            and a dashed FILLED box. Eating out has a dotted red cap on the spent
            side and a red hatched deficit bar with minus 62 and a boxed OVER tag. A
            spread row shows 1,870 spent, 1,930 total and 60 left, then a key. The
            right panel is the Tape with date, payee, an IN or OUT word with an
            arrow, and amount. Below 1100px the tape drops under, below 760px all
            stack with the book first.
        spacing: A 4px unit. 8 to 12px cell padding, 52px depth rows and 1px gaps between panels.
        density:
            High. Three panels, a ticker, a five row book with totals, a ten level
            ladder and a tape.
        corners: Square, 2px on buttons and fields only.
        borders:
            1px grid lines everywhere, panels split by 1px gaps, and a framed limit
            column in the middle of the book.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            Tiny glyphs beside capital words. A triangle with OVER in a solid box, a
            ruled square with FILLED in a dashed box, arrows with IN and OUT and a
            clock for due.
        focus: A 2px cyan inset outline with a faint cyan inner wash.
        tone:
            Terse trading labels in capitals, such as Positions, Budget depth, Tape,
            OVER, FILLED and 60 left.
    style368:
        number: 368
        run: 74
        screen: FinanceBudget
        name: Vault
        idea: The money app as a steel vault, riveted brushed steel plates, numbered deposit boxes with keyholes and inset readouts for balances, a combination dial for the savings goal and drawer fronts with gauges and indicator lamps for the budget.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/368.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            floor: #121417, the page and the style sheet
            steel: #2a2f35, riveted plates, drawers and the dial face
            steelLow: #22262b, sheet heading plates and the dial hub
            edge: #4a525c, plate edges, rivet rims and bevels
            inset: #0b0d0f, readouts, the log, gauges, fields and stamps
            ink: #e3e7ea, text, readout figures and major dial ticks
            etched: #a9b2bb, labels, box numbers, minor ticks and gauge fill
            amber: #ffb84d, the dial arc and pointer, the Sealed lamp, the primary button and focus
            greenLamp: #8fe0a0, drawers with money left and deposits
            redLamp: #ff8c7a, the over limit drawer and the owed balance
        type:
            Labels use Bahnschrift, DIN Alternate, Roboto Condensed, Arial Narrow,
            system-ui in caps. Readouts use ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas. The plate
            title is 20px at 700 tracked .24em with an embossed text shadow. Box
            readouts are 22px mono, box labels 15px at 700 tracked .12em, the log
            13px mono and section labels 12px tracked .22em.
        layout:
            A 1200px vault. A riveted header plate holds Brightwork Money, Vault, a
            caps line for Mara Okafor, October, EUR, and four inset nav keys,
            Overview outlined in amber. Then three columns, 300px, flexible and
            320px. Deposit boxes stacks three riveted plates, BOX 01 to BOX 03, each
            with a round keyhole and a pressed in dark readout, the card readout in
            red with a clock and Owed, due 12 Nov. The Goal dial plate has Japan
            trip over a large combination dial with 100 ticks, numbers every ten, an
            amber arc to 64, a pointer at 64 and 64 PERCENT in the hub, and a three
            cell inset readout for 3,200 saved, 5,000 target and Open by 1 Apr 27.
            The Access log plate holds an inset list with date, payee, a DEPOSIT or
            WITHDRAWAL tag with an arrow and amount. A wide Budget drawers plate
            follows with five drawer fronts, each with a name, a lamp, a pull
            handle, a segmented inset gauge, spent over limit and a stamped word.
            Totals sit under the drawers. Below 1100px the dial goes first and full
            width. Below 680px everything stacks and drawers go two across.
        spacing:
            A 4px unit. 20px between plates, 14px between boxes, 12px between
            drawers, 20 to 28px plate padding.
        density: Medium. Three boxes, one big dial, a five line log and five drawers.
        corners:
            6px plates, 4px drawers, buttons and readouts, with round rivets,
            keyholes and swatches.
        borders:
            1px steel edge on every plate with a light top bevel and a dark bottom
            bevel. Insets have no border, only an inner shadow.
        shadows:
            Heavy. Plates cast 0 6px 14px black, drawers and buttons sit on a hard
            3px dark ledge and readouts are pressed in.
        icons:
            Hardware as icons, rivets, keyholes, handles and lamps. The lamp shape
            changes with state, a round green lamp for money left, a square amber
            lamp for Sealed and a red triangle for Over 62, each beside a stamped
            word with a circle check, ruled square or triangle.
        focus: A 3px amber outline offset 3px.
        tone:
            Vault words in caps, such as Deposit boxes, Goal dial, Access log,
            Sealed, Over 62 and Open by.

    style369:
        number: 369
        run: 75
        screen: FinanceBudget
        name: Piggy playful
        idea: A friendly rounded money app on deep plum, with a big pink piggy bank that fills like a jar for the savings goal, budgets as little glass jars with faces that fill up, and cheerful words that stay kind when a jar overflows.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/369.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            plumNight: #1c1630, the page and the style sheet
            card: #28203f, cards and pockets
            cardTwo: #352b52, chips, feed rows, empty glass and the secondary button
            line: #4a3f6e, field borders, jar lids and payee discs
            ink: #fbf4ff, text and the jar and piggy outlines
            muted: #c4b8dd, labels, dates and the jar glass outline
            pink: #ff9fcb, the piggy fill, the brand disc and the primary button
            onPink: #3a0c24, text on pink
            mint: #8ff0c8, jars with room to spare, money in and free money
            sun: #ffd66e, Full up jars, coins and the focus ring
            oops: #ff9b8a, the overflowing jar and the owed card balance
        type:
            A rounded stack, ui-rounded, SF Pro Rounded, Nunito, Varela Round, Arial
            Rounded MT Bold, Segoe UI, system-ui. Base 16px at 1.5. The greeting is
            34px at 800, the goal figure 36px at 800, card titles 21px at 800, body
            16px at 700 and tags 13px at 800.
        layout:
            A 1160px page. The top row has a round pink disc with a tiny piggy, the
            name and pill nav on the right, My month ringed in pink. Nice going,
            Mara! leads with a line saying four jars are fine and one got a little
            too full. A wide left column holds Your pockets, three cards with one
            tucked corner for Everyday, Savings and Credit card in coral with a
            clock and Pay by 12 Nov, then the October jars card with five drawn
            glass jars in a row, each filled to its share in mint, sun or coral,
            with eyes and a mouth. Under each jar sit the name, spent of limit and a
            pill tag. Eating out overflows with drips and a frown. A pill below says
            60 is still free. A 380px right column holds the Japan trip piggy, a
            large outlined pig filled pink to 64 percent with coins inside and 64%
            on the fill, then 3,200 of 5,000, Only 1,800 more to go and a Fly day 1
            April 2027 chip, then What happened lately as rounded rows with plus or
            minus discs, the salary disc in mint. Below 1000px the columns stack.
            Below 640px pockets stack and jars go three across.
        spacing:
            An 8px unit. 24px gutters and card padding, 14px between pockets, 12px
            between jars.
        density: Low. Three pockets, five jars, one piggy and five feed rows.
        corners:
            Very round. 32px cards, pockets with one 8px tucked corner, 22px rows,
            pill tags and buttons.
        borders: None on cards. Thick 3 to 5px light outlines on the jar and piggy drawings.
        shadows: Only a soft 4px ledge under buttons.
        icons:
            Drawn jars with faces, a smile for room to spare, a flat mouth for Full
            up and a frown with overflow drips for over. Tags repeat it with a
            circle check, ruled square or triangle beside the word.
        focus: A 3px sunny yellow outline offset 4px with round corners.
        tone:
            Warm and playful, such as Nice going, Mara!, 64 to spare, Full up, Oops,
            62 over and money in, yay.
    style370:
        number: 370
        run: 75
        screen: FinanceBudget
        name: Bullion
        idea: Savings shown as real weight, gold ingots on deep burgundy velvet, balances stamped on trapezoid bars, the goal as a pyramid of ten 500 euro bars filling from the bottom, and budget lines as ingot shaped meters.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/370.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            velvet: #1a0910, the page and the style sheet, with faint plush glows
            plush: #2a1019, panels, fields and rows
            plushTwo: #3a1724, the owed card bar, the partly filled ingot and the secondary button
            seam: #5c2a3a, panel edges and row rules
            ink: #f6e9e0, text
            muted: #d0b3ad, labels, dates and empty bar outlines
            gold: #d8aa3e, ingot bodies, meters, the current nav item and the primary button
            goldHigh: #f4d67e, ingot shine, headings, focus and money in
            goldLow: #a87a22, the ingot shadow edge
            onGold: #2a1600, text stamped on gold
            rose: #ff9fa8, over budget hatching and the owed balance
            paleGold: #e9d58a, the in reserve status
        type:
            Labels use Optima, Candara, Segoe UI, Gill Sans, Trebuchet MS, often in
            caps tracked .2em or more. Figures use Rockwell, Roboto Slab, DejaVu
            Serif, Georgia. The goal figure is 40px slab at 700 in gold high, ingot
            figures 32px slab at 700 on gold, headings 16px caps tracked .24em at
            700, body 17px and status 13px caps tracked .1em.
        layout:
            A 1180px page. The header has a gold coin seal, Brightwork Money in
            tracked gold caps and Mara Okafor with October holdings in euros on the
            right, ruled below by a seam, then caps nav with Overview on a gold
            block. A centred tracked line reads October, what you hold. Three
            trapezoid ingots follow in a row, Everyday account and Savings in
            shining gold with dark stamped text, and the Credit card as a dark plush
            ingot with the figure in rose and a clock with Owed, due 12 Nov. Below,
            a wide October spending panel lists five tiers, each with the name, an
            ingot shaped meter with slanted ends filled in gold, spent of limit and
            a caps status under the meter, Eating out filled with rose diagonal
            hatching. A totals line reads spent 1,870 of 1,930 and 60 still in
            reserve. A 420px Japan trip bars panel shows a pyramid of ten trapezoid
            bars, four, three, two and one, six solid and stamped 500, the seventh
            two fifths gold behind a dashed outline, three dashed empties, then
            3,200 of 5,000, what is left and the target. Deposits and withdrawals
            runs full width below. Below 1000px panels stack, below 680px ingots
            stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px panel padding, 20px between ingots, 32px between panels.
        density: Medium. Three ingots, five tiers, a ten bar pyramid and five movements.
        corners: Trapezoid ingot cuts on balances, meters and swatches. 4px panels and 2px buttons.
        borders: A 1px inset seam round panels and between rows, and a double gold focus ring.
        shadows: Deep, 0 20px 40px black under panels so they sit on the velvet.
        icons:
            Gold bars are the main icon. Status pairs an outline circle check, ruled
            square or triangle with words, and the over meter swaps gold for rose
            hatching. Arrows mark deposits and withdrawals.
        focus: A 3px double pale gold outline offset 4px.
        tone:
            Weighty and proud, such as What you hold, Fine, in reserve, Fully spent
            and Over by 62.
    style371:
        number: 371
        run: 75
        screen: FinanceBudget
        name: Calm budget
        idea: A gentle single column on soft blue grey dark, large unhurried type, budgets explained in reassuring sentences with soft rounded bars, the goal as a gentle path with You are here, and no alarm colours anywhere.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/371.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            dusk: #1d2327, the page and the style sheet
            soft: #252d32, account rows, the goal card, fields and list rows
            softTwo: #2e383e, row dividers and the secondary button
            track: #3a464d, the empty bar track and field borders
            ink: #e9eef0, text
            muted: #aab7bd, labels, figures beside names and explanations
            sage: #a8d5bf, bars with room, headings, money in, the primary button and focus
            onSage: #11291f, text on sage
            sand: #e8c99b, the on plan bar, the due date note and the goal end marker
            lavender: #c9b8e8, the over bar, a soft colour used instead of red
        type:
            Segoe UI Variable Text, Segoe UI, system-ui, -apple-system, Roboto,
            Helvetica Neue, Arial. Base 18px at 1.7. The headline is 40px at 400 and
            1.25, the lede 20px muted, account figures 26px tabular, category names
            20px, explanations 16px and section labels 15px at 600 in sage.
        layout:
            One centred 700px column with wide space. A quiet top row has a sage dot
            with the name in muted text and three plain links, October underlined in
            sage. The headline reads Hello Mara. October is in good shape, and a
            lede says 1,870 of the 1,930 planned was spent, so the month ends 60
            under, and one budget went a little over. Where your money is lists
            three soft rounded rows with the name on the left and a large figure on
            the right, the card row adding a sand clock line saying Due 12 Nov is
            easily covered. How the plan went gives each category a name, spent of
            limit on the right, a 14px round bar and a sentence led by a bold
            phrase, Room left, On plan or A little over. A soft card repeats 60
            under plan. Your goal is a soft card with a gently rising curved path
            from Start to 1 April 2027, filled sage to 64 percent with a ringed dot
            labelled You are here, 64%, then 3,200 of 5,000 and 1,800 to go. Lately
            is a plain divided list. A closing line says That is everything for now.
            At 375px the same column narrows with smaller headings.
        spacing:
            An 8px unit. A 700px column, 64px between sections, 28px between budget
            lines, 20 to 24px inside cards.
        density: Very low. One column, one idea at a time, sentences before numbers.
        corners: Soft. 20 to 24px cards, 16px buttons and rows, round bars and dots.
        borders: Almost none. Thin dividers only between recent items.
        shadows: None. Surfaces lift by tone.
        icons:
            Few and small. A circle check for room left, a ruled square for on plan
            and a triangle for a little over, always before a bold word and a
            sentence. The over bar is lavender, not red.
        focus: A 2px sage outline offset 4px with a wide soft sage halo.
        tone:
            Reassuring and plain, such as October is in good shape, plenty of room
            and That happens, and nothing else needs to change.
    style372:
        number: 372
        run: 75
        screen: FinanceBudget
        name: Monochrome money
        idea: Only white on black, with the numbers doing all the work, a poster size balance, heavy and hairline weights for whole and decimal parts, white rules as the only structure, budget blocks as filled and empty squares, and the over budget row inverted to white.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/372.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            black: #000000, the page, every surface, the style sheet and text on the inverted row
            white: #ffffff, all text, rules, blocks, the goal meter, the inverted over row and focus
        type:
            Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, Liberation Sans, system-ui. Hierarchy
            comes only from size and weight. The everyday balance runs up to 210px
            at 900 tracked minus .06em with decimals at 200. Savings and card
            figures are 56px at 900, budget figures 44px at 900 with the limit at
            22px and 200, the goal percent up to 180px, body 17px at 300 and labels
            12px caps tracked .12em.
        layout:
            A 1280px poster grid of white rules. The top rule holds the name in 900,
            plain nav with October in 900 and underlined, and Mara Okafor, EUR.
            Every band has a 180px label column on the left. The first band is
            Everyday account with 2,184.60 at poster size. The next band splits in
            two by a vertical rule, Savings and Credit card with a clock and Due 12
            Nov. The October budget band lists five rows of name, figure over limit,
            ten blocks where each block is a tenth of the limit, filled white, half
            filled or outlined, and a caps status on the right. Eating out is a
            white row with black text, ten filled black blocks and four dashed
            hatched blocks past the limit. A 3px rule sets off spent 1,870 of 1,930
            and 60 left overall. The last band splits into the goal, 64% huge, a
            bordered white meter and two lines of figures, and Latest with dates,
            payees and heavy amounts, the salary larger and bold. Below 900px status
            drops under the blocks and below 700px every band stacks.
        spacing: An 8px unit. A 180px label column, 12 to 24px inside rows, 32px page gutter.
        density: Medium. Few elements but each figure is huge.
        corners: None anywhere.
        borders:
            1px white rules between every band and row, a 3px rule above totals and
            the style sheet, 1.5px block outlines.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            Hardly any. Small outline circle check, ruled square and triangle before
            capital words. Weight and inversion carry the rest, with dashed hatched
            blocks past the limit.
        focus: A 3px white outline offset 3px with a second thin white ring outside a black gap.
        tone:
            Bare numerals and short labels, such as 64 left, equals limit, plus 62
            over and Latest.
    style373:
        number: 373
        run: 75
        screen: FinanceBudget
        name: Banknote engraving
        idea: The overview printed as a dark green banknote, with the everyday balance as its denomination, an engraved oval frame holding a fern emblem, a guilloche rosette ringed by the savings goal, fine line etched meters and double rules throughout.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/373.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            deepGreen: #08150f, the page and the style sheet
            note: #0f2419, the banknote, mini notes, panels and fields
            noteTwo: #163223, inside the oval frame
            line: #2f5a43, double frames, rules, guilloche back lines and dotted dividers
            engraving: #7fbf98, etched meter lines, the emblem, medallions, remaining status and money in
            ink: #e4f0e1, text and figures
            muted: #a9c6b0, labels, italics and dates
            ochre: #d9bd7c, denomination corners, headings, the goal ring, the primary button and focus
            rust: #f0a58c, the serial line, the owed balance and the exceeded meter and status
            onOchre: #1d1606, text on the ochre button
        type:
            Baskerville, Baskerville Old Face, Hoefler Text, Libre Baskerville,
            Garamond, Times New Roman. Base 16px at 1.55. The denomination is 64px
            at 400 with a 32px ochre euro sign. The note title is 20px caps tracked
            .2em in ochre, section heads 15px caps tracked .3em in ochre with a
            double rule running to the right, body 16px and status 14px italic. The
            serial line is 13px ui-monospace tracked .2em in rust.
        layout:
            A 1180px page. The header has Brightwork Money in widely tracked caps,
            an italic line for Mara Okafor, October, in euros, and caps nav with
            Overview underlined in ochre. The main element is one wide banknote, a
            thin green border with wavy guilloche bands top and bottom, a 6px double
            inner frame and 2,184 in ochre in two corners. Inside are three parts.
            An engraved oval frame of six fine rings around a hatched oval holding a
            fern leaf. The denomination block with Everyday account, Balance this
            October, the large figure, the serial line MO, 31 OCT, EUR, and Held for
            Mara Okafor in italic. A guilloche rosette of two spirograph curves
            ringed by an ochre arc to 64 percent, with Japan trip above and 3,200 of
            5,000 saved and the target date below. Two mini notes follow, each with
            a spirograph medallion, Savings with Held in reserve and Credit card in
            rust with a clock. Then October series lists each category with an
            etched meter of fine horizontal green lines, spent of limit and an
            italic status, Eating out switching to vertical rust lines. Register
            lists the movements. Below 1000px the rosette drops under, below 640px
            the note stacks centred.
        spacing:
            An 8px unit. 28px between the note, mini notes and panels, 24 to 28px
            inside frames.
        density: Medium. One ornate note, two mini notes, five series lines and five register lines.
        corners: None. Ovals and rosettes are the only curves.
        borders:
            Layered. A thin engraving border, a 6px double inner frame, wavy
            guilloche bands, double rules beside headings and dotted dividers.
        shadows: None. Depth comes from fine line work.
        icons:
            Engraving as ornament, spirograph medallions and a fern in an oval
            frame. Status uses an outline circle check, ruled square or triangle
            beside italic words, and the exceeded meter turns from horizontal green
            lines to vertical rust lines.
        focus: A 2px ochre outline offset 3px with a fine green outer ring.
        tone:
            Formal issuing language, such as Balance this October, October series,
            Fully issued, Exceeded by 62 and Register.

    style374:
        number: 374
        run: 76
        screen: SmartHome
        name: Glass hub
        idea: Every room is a frosted dark glass tile floating over slow coloured light, and a room that is doing something glows softly in its own colour while idle rooms stay clear and still.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/374.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #0b0d17, page ground under the light blobs
            glass: #ffffff11, every tile, the top bar and swatch cards
            edge: #ffffff29, 1px tile edges, 30% on buttons and fields
            ink: #eef0fb, text and figures
            mute: #aab0cc, labels, meta and axis text
            warm: #ffcf7a, lights on glow, the alert and evening bars
            mint: #7ff0c8, locked and battery
            lilac: #c9b6ff, motion glow, the active scene and focus halo
            rose: #ffb0a8, heating schedule glow
            sky: #9fd4ff, daytime chart bars
            onWarm: #2a1a00, text on the warm primary button
        type:
            One system stack, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
            Arial. Base 15px at 1.5. Big numbers are thin, the kWh figure 44px
            and room temperatures 40px at weight 250 with the degree sign at
            18px muted. Tile titles 15px at 600, state lines 14px muted, tags
            12px at 650 in caps with 0.04em tracking.
        layout:
            The page ground is near black indigo with three large dim radial
            light blobs, violet top left, teal right and amber bottom, clipped
            by the stage. A full pill glass top bar holds a round B mark, the
            name, Saturday and the time, and a moon line saying Movie scene on.
            Below it a full width glass alert glows amber with a warning bubble,
            the sentence and a cream to amber pill Close now button. A 12 column
            grid follows. The left 8 columns hold five glass room tiles three
            across, each with a round glass icon bubble, a pill state tag top
            right, the room name, a huge thin temperature or a state word, and a
            state line with its own icon. A tile that is doing something glows
            in its colour, amber for lights on, rose for the heating schedule,
            lilac for garden motion, while kitchen and the locked door stay
            clear. The right 4 columns stack Energy today with a thin 44px
            figure, two inner glass chips for solar and battery and a bar chart
            whose evening bars are amber, then Scenes as four tall glass keys
            with Movie lit lilac and marked Active with a check. Below 1060px
            the side column drops under the rooms in two columns, below 760px
            rooms go two across and at phone width one across with scenes two by
            two.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px gaps between tiles, 18 to 20px tile padding, 32px page gutter and 16px on phones.
        density: Airy. Five room tiles, energy and scenes fill one wide screen.
        corners: 22px tiles, full pills for the top bar, tags and buttons, 18px scene keys and round icon bubbles.
        borders:
            1px white at 16 percent on every glass surface, a tinted edge at
            about 50 percent on a glowing tile, 30 percent white on buttons and
            fields.
        shadows:
            An inset 1px white top highlight and 0 12px 32px black at 35 percent
            on glass. Active tiles add a 36px coloured glow, and the alert a
            40px amber glow.
        icons:
            Round line icons at 1.6 stroke, 20px, in 44px glass bubbles. States
            use a bulb for on, a dash circle for off, a flame for the schedule,
            a check for locked and a walking figure for motion, always beside a
            word.
        focus: A 2px white outline offset 3px with a 6px lilac halo, visible on glass and on glow.
        tone: Short and calm, such as Energy today, Scenes, Active and Close now.
    style375:
        number: 375
        run: 76
        screen: SmartHome
        name: Thermostat dial
        idea: One big round thermostat dial for the living room leads the screen, the other rooms sit around it as small ring gauges, and even the day's energy is drawn as a 24 hour clock face.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/375.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #141416, page ground
            body: #1c1c20, room cards, cards and the dial rim
            well: #232328, stat rows, scene discs and fields
            line: #34343b, card borders and dial edge
            ink: #f3f1ee, text and the dial reading
            mute: #aeaab2, labels, meta and dial numerals
            heat: #ff9a5c, lit dial ticks, warm rings, the active scene and primary button
            onHeat: #2b1306, text and icons on heat
            cool: #7cc4ff, cool rings, low hour sectors and focus
            ok: #8fe0a8, locked ring and battery
            warn: #ffc65c, motion ring and the garage alert
        type:
            A rounded stack, ui-rounded, SF Pro Rounded, Nunito, Varela Round,
            then system-ui. Base 15px at 1.5. The dial reading is 88px at 300
            with a 32px raised degree sign, stat figures 22px at 700, room names
            16px at 700, meta 14px muted and chips 12px at 700.
        layout:
            A header row holds a small knob mark with Brightwork Home, the day
            and time, and on the right a pill shaped alert outlined in yellow
            with Garage door open for 2 hours and an orange pill Close now. The
            stage below is a three column grid with a 440px round thermostat
            dial in the centre for the living room. The dial has 81 ticks over a
            270 degree sweep from 10 to 30 degrees, lit orange up to 21.5 with
            an orange marker dot, numerals every 5, and a dark inner face
            showing Living room, 21.5 and lines for 3 lights on at 40 percent
            and TV off. Two room cards sit left and two right, each a pill ended
            card with a 76px ring gauge, blue for kitchen at 20.0, orange for
            bedroom at 19.0 with a heating chip, and green lock and yellow
            walker rings for the front door and the garden. Below, a wide Energy
            today card pairs a 24 hour clock face chart, one radial sector per
            hour with midnight at the top, orange for hours of 0.7 kWh or more
            and blue below, beside three stat rows for used, solar and a battery
            bar. A Scenes card holds four 72px round discs with Movie filled
            orange and marked On now. Below 1080px the dial goes on top with
            rooms two by two, and at phone width everything stacks.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between the dial, the rooms and the cards, 20 to 24px card padding.
        density: Low. One reading dominates and four rooms orbit it.
        corners:
            Everything round. 28px cards, full pills for chips, buttons and
            fields, circles for gauges, discs and swatches.
        borders: 1px #34343b on cards, 1.5px currentColor on chips and the alert.
        shadows: None, except a 6px soft orange ring around the active scene disc.
        icons:
            Round line icons at 2px stroke, 18 to 26px. States pair a word with
            a clock, check, walking figure or dash circle.
        focus: A 3px cool blue outline offset 3px.
        tone: Warm and short, such as On now, Energy today and Close now.
    style376:
        number: 376
        run: 76
        screen: SmartHome
        name: Night light
        idea: A bedside screen in warm low amber on near black, one narrow quiet column with a large clock and old style serif text, dim enough for a dark bedroom yet every word still clears AA.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/376.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #0c0805, page and style sheet ground
            glow: #140d08, faint top glow behind the clock
            rule: #2e1f14, hairline rules between rows
            ink: #dcae80, body text, 9 to 1 on page
            soft: #a8805c, labels, italics and notes, 5.6 to 1
            ember: #f0a560, the clock, active scene, primary button and focus
            onEmber: #1a0d03, text on ember
            emberDeep: #3a2210, the alert band
            alert: #f3b780, alert text on emberDeep
        type:
            Old style serif for text, Iowan Old Style, Palatino Linotype,
            Palatino, Book Antiqua, Georgia, base 17px at 1.6. The clock is
            112px at 400 in ember with old style figures, the bedroom line 24px,
            room names 20px, notes 15px italic. Small labels and buttons use
            system-ui at 12px, 600, caps with 0.18em tracking.
        layout:
            One quiet centred column 680px wide on a near black brown page with
            a faint warm radial glow at the top. A small caps line names
            Brightwork Home and Bedtime view. A huge ember clock shows the time,
            with an italic line Saturday evening, Movie is playing. A ruled
            Bedroom block comes first, saying 19.0 degrees and cooling for
            sleep, with a clock line that heating steps down to 18 at bedtime. A
            deep ember alert band follows with an exclamation mark, the garage
            sentence and an ember pill Close now. Around the house lists the
            other four rooms as rows with dotted leaders from the name to the
            value and an italic note with a thin icon below. Today's energy
            shows three figures split by thin left rules, then a dim curve of
            dots, brighter ember dots for the evening, captioned midnight,
            busiest at seven and now. Scenes are outlined pills with Movie in
            ember and a small on mark. A closing italic hint explains Good
            night. At phone width the clock drops to 84px.
        spacing: An 8px unit with generous 40 to 48px gaps between sections and 14px row padding.
        density: Very low. One fact per line, bedroom first.
        corners: Square rows, a 4px alert band, full pills for buttons and scenes.
        borders: 1px #2e1f14 rules only, and dotted #4a3322 leaders between a room and its value.
        shadows: None. A faint radial glow behind the clock instead.
        icons: Thin 1.3 stroke line icons at 18px, always beside a full sentence.
        focus: A 2px dashed ember outline offset 4px, dashed so it reads apart from the solid rules.
        tone: Hushed sentences, such as Around the house and Heating steps down to 18.
    style377:
        number: 377
        run: 76
        screen: SmartHome
        name: Floor plan
        idea: The home is drawn as a dark blueprint floor plan, each room filled by its state with its own hatch or dot pattern and glyph, framed by a drawing title block, a room schedule and a plotted load graph.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/377.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #0a1a2f, blueprint ground
            grid: #12294a, 24px paper grid
            panel: #0d2038, idle rooms, fields, secondary buttons
            line: #8fb8e8, walls, frame, section heads
            faint: #2a4a74, table rules and dashed scene boxes
            ink: #e3eeff, text, plot line, primary button
            mute: #9fb6d6, labels and axis text
            onLine: #06152a, text on the ink button
            lit: #ffd27a, lights on bands, active scene, focus ring
            heat: #ff9f7a, heating hatch
            move: #c3b2ff, motion dots and rings
            safe: #7fe3b4, locked door
            alarm: #ff8f8f, open garage cross hatch and alert
        type:
            Monospace for everything, ui-monospace, SF Mono, Cascadia Mono,
            Roboto Mono, Menlo, base 14px at 1.5. Headings use a condensed
            stack, Arial Narrow, Roboto Condensed, Helvetica Neue, at 700 in
            caps with 0.12 to 0.14em tracking. Plan room labels 15px at 700
            caps, table text 12px, figures 20px at 600.
        layout:
            A navy blueprint page with a 24px paper grid holds one drawing sheet
            framed by a 2px pale blue border and a thin outer offset line. A
            title bar names Brightwork Home and Level 0 plan view with the day
            and time. A red and maroon striped alert strip reads Alert G1 with
            the garage sentence and an ink coloured Close now. The body splits
            into the plan and a 340px side column. The plan is an SVG floor plan
            with 4px walls, door swing arcs and a dimension line. Each room is
            filled by state with its own pattern and glyph, warm diagonal bands
            and bulbs for the lit living room, a plain fill and dash circle for
            the dark kitchen, a fine hatch and flame for the bedroom schedule, a
            red cross hatch and triangle for the garage with its door drawn
            swung open, and a violet dot field with rings for garden motion
            around the house. The front door sits in the hall with a green lock.
            Room labels sit on dark plates. A key legend under the plan names
            every pattern. The side column holds a title block table, an energy
            block with three ruled figure cells and a plotted step line on a
            grid with the peak circled, and scenes as dashed boxes with Movie
            solid yellow and checked. A full room schedule table with refs R1 to
            G1 spans the bottom. Below 1000px the side column drops under the
            plan, and at phone width the plan keeps a 600px minimum inside its
            own sideways scroll.
        spacing: An 8px unit on a 24px grid. 12 to 16px cell padding.
        density: High. Plan, title block, plot, scenes and a full schedule table in one sheet.
        corners: Square everywhere. No radius.
        borders: A 2px drawing frame with a 1px outer offset line, 1px faint cell rules in #2a4a74 and 4px walls.
        shadows: None. Depth comes from hatch and dot fills only.
        icons:
            Square capped line glyphs at 1.5 stroke in plan rooms and table
            cells. Each state pairs a fill pattern with a glyph and a word.
        focus: A 2px ink outline plus a yellow ring outside a dark gap.
        tone: Drawing office caps with refs, such as R1, G1, Alert G1 and Title block.
    style378:
        number: 378
        run: 76
        screen: SmartHome
        name: Security console
        idea: The home seen as a monitoring desk, a 2 by 2 camera wall with burned in captions leads, an armed status strip runs across the top, and a time stamped event log and zone list carry the rest in dense monospace.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/378.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #08090b, page, camera wall gutter is pure black
            panel: #111317, panels and swatch cells
            panel2: #171a1f, buttons, mode keys, rows
            line: #262a31, every panel border and row rule
            ink: #e6e8eb, text and peak bars
            mute: #9aa1ab, times, labels, low bars
            armed: #5ee0d0, armed strip, active scene, focus and sheet heads
            onArmed: #04201d, text on armed
            alarm: #ff6b6b, REC, open garage outline, primary button
            alarmBg: #2a1012, alert row in the log
            motion: #ffc857, motion box and tags
            ok: #8be08b, locked tags
        type:
            Monospace for data, ui-monospace, SF Mono, JetBrains Mono, Cascadia
            Mono, Menlo, base 13px at 1.45. The armed word is system-ui 20 to
            22px at 800 with 0.16em tracking. Panel heads system-ui 12px at 700
            caps 0.14em, state tags 12px mono bold caps, the clock 22px at 600.
        layout:
            A near black monitoring desk with 12px gutters. A top strip holds
            the brand with a camera icon, a wide teal armed banner with a
            shield, ARMED and Perimeter, 4 cameras online, 1 alert, and a clock
            box. The main area is a 2 by 2 camera wall on black with 4px gaps.
            Each feed is a simple line drawn scene with a black caption band on
            top naming CAM 01 to 04 and a red REC dot with the word, and a
            bottom band with the state. The front door feed shows LOCKED with a
            lock, the garden feed a dashed yellow motion box around a figure
            with MOTION, the garage feed a 3px red outline, the open door, OPEN
            2H and a red Close now, and the living room three lit lamps with the
            room facts. A 360px side column stacks an Event log of time stamped
            rows with icons, the open garage row on a dark red ground, and a
            Zones table with temperature and state. Below sit a Power panel with
            three figures and a bar strip, and a Scene panel of four joined mode
            keys with Movie filled teal and a square mark. Below 1040px the side
            column drops under the wall, and at phone width feeds stack one per
            row.
        spacing: 4px inside the camera wall, 12px between panels, 8 by 12px rows.
        density: Very high. Four feeds, a log, a zone table, power and modes on one screen.
        corners: Square, with 2px on buttons and fields only.
        borders: 1px #262a31 on every panel and row. Feeds use 2 to 3px inset outlines for motion and alarm.
        shadows: None. Captions sit on 72 to 78 percent black bands.
        icons:
            Line icons at 2px stroke, 16px. A lock for locked, a walking figure
            for motion, a triangle for open, a shield for armed and a film frame
            for the scene.
        focus: A 2px teal outline offset 2px.
        tone: Operator shorthand in caps, such as CAM 03, OPEN 2H, REC and Event log.

    style379:
        number: 379
        run: 77
        screen: SmartHome
        name: Home AI
        idea: The home speaks as a calm intelligence, a softly lit orb and one spoken line lead the screen, and the rooms, energy and scenes sit below as quiet notes the assistant is keeping an eye on.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/379.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #07060f, page ground
            deep: #0e0c1c, note panels and swatch cards
            veil: #151229, secondary buttons and fields
            line: #2a2548, panel edges and row rules
            ink: #ecebfa, text and the spoken line
            mute: #a7a3c7, labels and meta
            cyan: #9ee7ff, orb core, speaking status, lights on, focus
            lilac: #c7a8ff, energy curve, motion, active scene
            coral: #ffb3a1, the alert words in the spoken line, heating
            mint: #9df0cf, locked and battery
            onCyan: #061a24, text on the cyan to lilac primary button
        type:
            One system stack, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
            Arial, at light weights. Base 16px at 350. The spoken line is 30px
            at 300 and 1.4, figures 52px at 200, note ledes 19px at 300, meta
            14px muted, labels 12px at 600 caps with 0.22em tracking.
        layout:
            A violet black page with a soft radial haze behind the top. A thin
            caps line shows Brightwork Home and the day and time. The hero is
            centred, a 220px glowing orb with a pale core, cyan to violet body
            and two tilted orbit rings, then a cyan Speaking label with a mic,
            then one spoken sentence greeting the evening, saying Movie is on,
            with the garage sentence in coral and the question Shall I close it.
            A thin cyan waveform line runs under it, then a cyan to lilac pill
            Close now and a dark pill Leave it open. Below, three tall note
            panels with 32px corners sit side by side. Rooms has the lede Five
            places I am watching and five ruled rows with a coloured state icon,
            the room, a muted note and the value or state word. Energy has the
            lede A quiet day until the evening, a huge thin figure, solar and
            battery in cyan and mint, and a lilac filled curve with the peak
            dotted. Scenes has Ask me, or tap one, and four pill rows each with
            a voice hint, Movie edged lilac and marked Running with a check.
            Below 980px the third panel spans two columns, and at phone width
            the orb shrinks to 160px and panels stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit, very open. 56px between the hero and the notes, 24px panel padding.
        density: Low. One sentence leads and three short note panels follow.
        corners: 32px panels and full pills for every button, field and scene.
        borders: 1px #2a2548 on panels and rows, lilac on the active scene.
        shadows: None. Light comes from the orb glow and the radial haze behind it.
        icons: Thin 1.4 stroke line icons at 18px, coloured per state and always with words. A mic marks speaking.
        focus: A 2px cyan outline offset 4px.
        tone: First person and gentle, such as Five places I am watching and Shall I close it.
    style380:
        number: 380
        run: 77
        screen: SmartHome
        name: Cosy linen
        idea: The home dressed like a warm den at night, dark walnut wood behind stitched linen cards, serif headings, a hanging fabric tag for the alert and an energy chart sewn in running stitches.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/380.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            wood: #1d140e, walnut page with a faint grain
            shelf: #2f1f14, the header shelf and sheet top edge
            linen: #2a231d, card cloth with a 4px weave
            linen2: #332a22, patches, scene tabs, secondary buttons
            stitch: #7a6650, dashed stitched borders and the chart baseline
            ink: #f1e6d6, text
            mute: #c6b49e, meta and labels
            terra: #eb9a72, the alert tag, motion and the primary button
            onTerra: #2a1206, text on terra
            mustard: #ebc672, lights on, active scene, peak stitches and focus
            sage: #b3cfa3, locked and battery yarn
            rose: #e8a7a0, heating schedule
        type:
            Serif headings and figures, Charter, Bitstream Charter, Sitka Text,
            Cambria, Georgia. Humanist sans text, Seravek, Gill Sans Nova, Gill
            Sans, Trebuchet MS, Ubuntu, base 16px at 1.55. Title 26px with an
            italic mustard Home, card titles 22px, room temperatures 30px,
            energy figures 34px, state labels 14px at 600.
        layout:
            A dark walnut page with a faint vertical wood grain. A wooden shelf
            bar across the top holds Brightwork Home with an italic mustard Home
            and Saturday evening. Under it a hanging fabric tag cut to a point
            on the left, with a punched hole, carries the garage alert in terra
            on deep rust and a terra Close now. A 12 column grid follows. The
            left 7 columns hold linen room cards two across, the living room
            spanning both, each with a woven texture, a dashed stitch line inset
            7px, a round stitched patch with the room icon, a serif name and
            temperature, and a small dark label with a state icon and word
            beside a muted line. The right 5 columns stack Energy today with
            serif figures, a striped sage yarn battery bar and a bar chart sewn
            in vertical running stitches, mustard for hours over 1 kWh, then
            Scenes as fabric tabs with a round sewn button that fills mustard
            with a check and the words On now for Movie. Below 1000px the right
            column moves under the rooms in two columns, and at phone width
            everything stacks.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between cards, 22 to 24px card padding.
        density: Medium low. Five room cards, energy and scenes.
        corners: 10px cards, 8px buttons and tabs, round patches and scene buttons, and a pointed tag for the alert.
        borders: A 1.5px dashed stitch line in #7a6650 inset inside every card, and a solid stitch colour on buttons.
        shadows:
            A 2px dark ledge plus 0 10px 20px black at 40 percent, like cloth on
            a table. The shelf casts 0 6px 12px.
        icons:
            Rounded 1.7 stroke icons at 20px in stitched round patches. States
            pair a word with a bulb, dash circle, clock, lock or walker.
        focus: A 3px mustard outline offset 3px.
        tone: Homely and spoken, such as Saturday evening, Open for 2 hours now and Seen at half past nine.
    style381:
        number: 381
        run: 77
        screen: SmartHome
        name: Tactile knobs
        idea: The home as a wall of brushed metal faceplates, each room a screwed module with real looking rotary knobs, toggle switches, lit lamps and amber readouts, and scenes are chunky push buttons that stay pressed in.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/381.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #161719, rack ground with fine brushed lines
            plate: #24262a, faceplates, from #2b2e33 at top to #202226
            plate2: #2c2f34, list rows and knob caps
            edge: #0c0d0e, plate edges and button outlines
            hi: #3d4148, top bevel highlight
            ink: #eceae4, text and switch labels
            mute: #aeb0b4, engraved labels and meta
            lcd: #0b0a06, readout windows and the LED matrix
            amber: #ffb84a, readouts, lit ticks, pointers, pressed scene, focus, primary
            onAmber: #2a1700, text on amber
            lamp: #ff6a4d, warning lamp, motion lamp, top matrix cells
            green: #7fe08a, locked lamp and key
        type:
            Condensed labels, Bahnschrift, DIN Alternate, Roboto Condensed,
            Arial Narrow, base 15px. Engraved plate labels 13px at 700 caps with
            0.2em tracking and a dark top text shadow. Readouts use ui-
            monospace, SF Mono, Menlo at 26px, 600 in amber inside black
            windows. Unit labels 12px caps 0.14em.
        layout:
            A brushed dark metal rack with fine horizontal lines holds a 6
            column panel of screwed faceplates, each with two corner screws, a
            top bevel and a raised shadow. A header plate names Brightwork Home
            and Main panel with an amber readout of the day and time. A warning
            plate has a glowing red lamp with a triangle, Garage door open, 2
            hours, and a raised amber Close now. The living room plate holds an
            amber temperature readout, a knurled rotary dimmer at 40 percent
            with lit amber ticks and pointer, a toggle switch up with a round
            amber lamp for 3 lights on, and a toggle down with a dark lamp for
            TV off. The kitchen plate has its readout and a toggle down for
            lights off. The bedroom plate has a thermostat knob at 19 and a
            readout showing the switch to 18. The front door plate has a key
            switch turned to lock with a square green lamp and Locked. The
            garden plate shows the last event time and a triangle red lamp for
            Motion. Scenes are four chunky push buttons, Movie sunk 3px with an
            inner shadow, amber text and a down arrow In. A full width energy
            plate shows readouts for used and solar, a small battery knob at 64
            percent and an LED matrix of 24 columns, each lit cell 0.2 kWh,
            amber with red top cells. Below 1060px plates regroup, and at phone
            width they stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 12px between plates, 20 to 22px plate padding.
        density: Medium. Each room shows its physical controls rather than a summary.
        corners: 6px plates and buttons, 3px readouts, round knobs and screws.
        borders: A 1px near black plate edge with a 1px #3d4148 top bevel highlight.
        shadows:
            Raised plates use 0 3px 6px black, buttons sit on a 3 to 4px dark
            ledge, and a pressed button sinks 3px with an inner shadow.
        icons:
            Line icons at 2px stroke on push buttons. States use lamp shapes, a
            round amber lamp for on, a square green lamp for locked and a
            triangle red lamp for motion, each beside a word.
        focus: A 3px amber outline offset 3px.
        tone: Engraved caps nouns, such as MAIN PANEL, DIM 40%, HEAT SCHEDULE and IN.
    style382:
        number: 382
        run: 77
        screen: SmartHome
        name: Moon phase
        idea: A calm night sky holds the home, a pale moon and scattered stars over a horizon, the day's energy drawn as a tide with high and low marks, and scenes shown as phases of the moon.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/382.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            sky: #060a18, page and lower sky
            sky2: #0b1330, top of the sky gradient
            deep: #0d1530, secondary buttons
            line: #253058, rules, panel and phase card edges
            ink: #e8ecf7, text
            mute: #a3acc8, labels, axis and notes
            moon: #f3ecd2, the moon, lit phases, primary button, active scene edge and focus
            onMoon: #1a1608, text on moon
            tide: #7fb5e6, the energy tide line and motion
            star: #cfd8f5, star dots
            warm: #ffbf94, lights on and the alert
            mint: #9be3c8, locked
            rose: #f5b0c0, bedroom cooling
        type:
            High contrast serif for display, Didot, Bodoni 72, Bodoni MT, Big
            Caslon, Book Antiqua, Georgia. Text in Avenir Next, Avenir, Segoe
            UI, system-ui at 15px and 1.6. The headline is 64px with an italic
            moon coloured Saturday, figures 40px, section titles 28px italic,
            room names 21px, the kicker 12px caps with 0.32em tracking.
        layout:
            A night sky fading from deep blue at the top to near black holds
            about ninety faint star dots in its upper half. The hero pairs a
            kicker line with the home name, day and time, the headline A quiet
            Saturday night and a line saying Movie is on and the bedroom cools
            to 18, with a pale waxing gibbous moon in a soft glow on the right.
            A pill shaped alert outlined in dusky brown has a triangle, the
            garage sentence and a moon coloured Close now. Today's energy tide
            follows with three serif figures and a full width tide line, a
            smooth pale blue curve over a gradient water fill with a faint
            dotted second wave, a horizon rule, hour labels, a filled triangle
            for high and an outlined triangle for low, then a tide table listing
            high, low and now ebbing. Below, Rooms tonight lists the five rooms
            in ruled rows with a coloured icon, serif name, italic note, the
            value and a small caps state word such as Lit, Dark, Cooling, Locked
            and Motion. Scenes show as moon phase cards, new moon for Good
            night, full for Movie with a check and Full now, crescent for Away
            and first quarter for Morning. Below 900px rooms and scenes stack,
            and at phone width the moon moves above the headline at 120px.
        spacing: An 8px unit with wide 40 to 48px gaps between bands and 14px row padding.
        density: Low. Hero, tide, rooms and phases read top to bottom.
        corners: Full pills for the alert and buttons, 24px phase cards and round swatches.
        borders: 1px #253058 rules between rooms and a moon coloured edge on the active phase.
        shadows: None. A soft glow ring around the moon only.
        icons: Thin 1.5 stroke line icons beside rooms, and moon phase discs for scenes, each with a phase name.
        focus: A 2px moon outline offset 4px.
        tone: Quiet and poetic, such as A quiet Saturday night, Today's energy tide, high and ebbing.
    style383:
        number: 383
        run: 77
        screen: SmartHome
        name: Family bright
        idea: A home screen the whole family can use, big candy bright room tiles with thick friendly icons and dark ink on a deep slate page, every touch target at least 64px and every state spelled out in plain words.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/383.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #15182b, deep slate page
            card: #20243d, energy and scene cards
            card2: #2a2f4d, number chips, scene buttons, fields
            line: #3a4068, 3px card borders
            ink: #f6f5ff, text on dark
            mute: #b9bcd9, helper text
            dark: #17142b, text and badges on bright tiles, primary button
            sun: #ffd34d, living room tile, peak bars, sheet heads
            sky: #6fd0ff, kitchen tile, day bars, focus halo
            berry: #ff7fa8, bedroom tile
            lime: #9ef07a, front door tile and battery
            grape: #c6a2ff, garden tile
            tang: #ff9d4d, the alert card
        type:
            A heavy rounded stack, ui-rounded, SF Pro Rounded, Nunito,
            Quicksand, Varela Round, Arial Rounded MT Bold. Base 17px at 600.
            The greeting and tile figures 34px at 900, card titles 24px at 900,
            room names 21px at 900, badges 14px at 800, button text 19px at 800.
        layout:
            A deep slate page. A greeting row has a 64px yellow rounded square
            with B, Hi, family and the home name, day and time. A full width
            tangerine alert card with a 6px darker ledge holds a 64px dark
            circle with a garage icon, The garage door is open in heavy type
            over It has been open for 2 hours, and a dark pill Close now 64px
            tall. Five candy bright room tiles follow in one row, yellow living
            room, sky kitchen, berry bedroom, lime front door and grape garden,
            each with dark ink, a 64px round well with a thick icon, the name, a
            big temperature where there is one, a dark pill badge with its own
            icon and word such as Lights on, Lights off, Bedtime heat, Locked
            and Motion, and a friendly sentence. Below, an Energy today card
            shows a big battery drawing 64 percent full in lime, number chips
            for used, sun and battery, and chunky rounded bars, yellow for the
            evening peak. A Scenes card has four 96px tall buttons with coloured
            round icon wells and a hint line, Movie turned white with On now and
            a star. Below 1100px tiles go three across and the cards stack, and
            at phone width tiles go two across with the living room full width.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px tile gaps, 18 to 24px padding and a 64px minimum touch size.
        density: Low. Five big tiles, then energy and four big scene buttons.
        corners: 28px tiles and cards, 24px scene buttons, 20px fields, full pills for buttons and badges.
        borders: Bright tiles have none. Dark cards use a 3px #3a4068 border.
        shadows: A solid 6px drop ledge under tiles and the alert, like a toy block.
        icons:
            Thick 2.6 stroke rounded icons at 24 to 36px in round wells. Each
            state badge has its own icon and a plain word.
        focus: A 4px white outline offset 4px plus a 10px sky halo.
        tone: Warm and plain, like talking to kids, such as Hi, family, Locked tight and Something moved out there.

    style384:
        number: 384
        run: 78
        screen: FitnessTracker
        name: Athletic neon
        idea: A sports poster in volt yellow on black, where the screen is built from slanted panels and every figure is a heavy italic number, so today reads like a race result.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/384.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            black: #0b0b0a, the page and the style sheet
            panel: #161614, cards and the stats block
            panel2: #20201c, empty tracks, fields and the next session strip
            line: #3a3a33, rules between rows and track outlines
            ink: #f6f6ef, text, week bars, done plan weeks and the secondary button
            muted: #b0b0a2, labels and units
            volt: #d4ff1a, the run hero, ring fill, top zone, today, current plan week, primary button and focus
            onVolt: #0b0b0a, text on volt and on ink
            voltDim: #7d9410, outlines of the quieter zone bars
            rest: #8a8a7e, the Rest word and dash on empty days
        type:
            Figures and headings use Impact, Haettenschweiler, Franklin Gothic
            Heavy, Arial Black, always italic at 900. Text uses Helvetica Neue,
            Arial, system-ui at 15px and 1.45. The run distance is 176px, run
            stats 56px, card titles 26px caps, chart figures 26 to 30px, labels
            12px caps at 800 tracked 0.14em.
        layout:
            A black top bar with a volt slanted BW tile and Move, three slanted
            tabs with Today filled white, and the date in italic caps on the
            right, ruled below in volt. A full width hero has an 8px volt left
            edge. Its left part is a volt panel cut on a slant holding a black
            Done tag with a check, Today 42 min, Evening run and 8.2 km at
            176px. Its right part lists Time 42 min 16 s, Avg pace 5 min 9 s per
            km and Avg heart rate 152 bpm as big italic figures over rules.
            Below, a twelve column grid. Rings takes seven columns with three
            rows, each a caps label, a slanted volt track with a white end tick
            at the goal, and the value over the goal with an open square and the
            amount to go. Heart zones takes five columns as slanted columns with
            minutes on top, zone 3 solid volt and the rest outlined, Z numbers
            and names below and a note on the top zone. This week takes seven
            columns as slanted white columns with today in volt, rest days as a
            grey dash and the word Rest, day names and dates below and the total
            of 23.7 km in the title. A right column stacks Sleep with 7 h 12 m
            in big italic, a slanted deep sleep bar at 22 percent and a key,
            then the Half marathon plan with Week 6 of 12 in volt, twelve
            slanted segments with five white, one volt and six empty, and a next
            strip reading Long run 14 km tomorrow with View plan. Below 980px
            everything stacks and the hero panel loses its slant. At 375px the
            distance drops to 120px and ring tracks move under their labels.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 16px gaps between panels, 24px card padding, a 32px page gutter.
        density: Medium low. One giant result, then five panels with a single chart each.
        corners: None. Bars, tags, tracks, swatches and segments are skewed ten degrees instead.
        borders: An 8px volt bar on the hero edge, a short volt slash on top of each card and 2px rules between rows.
        shadows: None. Flat black panels.
        icons:
            Very few. A square check in the Done tag, an open square for rings
            still to close, and a grey dash with Rest for empty days. Today is
            named Today.
        focus: A 3px volt outline offset 3px, a black gap and a 2px white ring outside it. Slanted buttons drop their slant when focused.
        tone: Short caps labels such as Done, To go, Rest, This week and Long run 14 km.
    style385:
        number: 385
        run: 78
        screen: FitnessTracker
        name: Heart monitor
        idea: The day shown on a bedside style monitor, with stacked signal channels on a fine grid, a live trace for heart rate, the week drawn as a rhythm strip of beats, and the five zone colours leading every reading.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/385.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            bg: #040706, the case around the screen
            screen: #07100d, every channel, the side panel and the style sheet
            grid: #11231c, the fine 8px grid behind signals
            gridMaj: #1a3a2e, the 40px grid and the rhythm baseline
            line: #244236, channel dividers and field borders
            ink: #e6f2ec, text, readings and goal ticks
            muted: #9db8ac, labels, units and rest days
            trace: #43f59b, the heart trace, ring progress, rhythm strip, plan pip and primary button
            z1: #78b6ff, zone 1 Easy and deep sleep
            z2: #43e0a0, zone 2 Aerobic
            z3: #ffd23f, zone 3 Tempo and the average heart rate
            z4: #ff9c45, zone 4 Threshold
            z5: #ff6b7a, zone 5 Max
            onZ: #04120b, text on zone and trace fills
        type:
            Readings use Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial at weight 300
            with tabular numbers, 52px for heart rate, 44px for side parameters
            and 40px for ring values. Channel labels and meta use ui-monospace,
            SF Mono, Cascadia Mono, Menlo, Consolas at 12px, caps at 700 tracked
            0.08em. Body is 14px at 1.45.
        layout:
            One monitor case 1260px wide with an 18px radius and an inset black
            bezel. A status strip across the top holds Brightwork Move, Today
            with the date, a green heartbeat glyph with Last session 42 min 16
            s, and Today, Week and Plan as small mono tabs. Below, a main column
            of channels beside a 300px side panel. Every channel is a row of
            three cells, a 96px mono label cell, a signal cell on a fine green
            grid and a 190px reading cell. The HR channel draws a repeating
            heartbeat trace and reads 152 bpm in zone 3 yellow with a Z3 tag.
            The Zones channel spans the signal and reading cells with one strip
            split into five zone colours, each with its own stripe pattern and Z
            label, and a key of Z number, name and minutes. Move, Exercise and
            Stand channels show a glowing green fill with a ring dot at the
            percent, a dotted remainder, a white goal tick with the percent, and
            a reading of value over goal with open and the amount to go. The
            bottom of the column is the week as a rhythm strip, one beat per day
            with height by distance and the figure above, flat line and rest for
            empty days, day names under it and today marked with a diamond,
            headed with 23.7 km, 4 runs and 3 rest. The side panel stacks the
            Evening run with a Done tag and four parameters, Sleep 7 h 12 min
            with a two part bar for deep sleep, and a green outlined next
            session box with twelve plan pips, Long run 14 km and View plan.
            Below 1000px the side panel moves under the channels in two columns.
            At 375px label and reading share a row above the signal, and the
            rhythm strip scrolls inside its own area.
        spacing: An 8px unit and an 8px signal grid. Channels sit edge to edge with 1px dividers and 12 to 16px inner padding.
        density: High. Every reading is a channel row, all visible at once like a monitor.
        corners: 18px on the monitor case, 8px on the next session box, 3 to 6px on tags and controls.
        borders: 1px dark green dividers between every channel and column.
        shadows: An inset black bezel around the screen and a soft green glow on progress fills.
        icons:
            A heartbeat glyph for the run. Zones carry a Z number, a name and a
            distinct stripe pattern. Rings say open with a hollow circle. Rest
            days are a flat line with the word rest. The average heart rate tag
            has a triangle.
        focus: A 2px white outline offset 2px with a 5px green halo.
        tone: Clinical short labels such as HR, Zones, avg, open, to go and Week rhythm.
    style386:
        number: 386
        run: 78
        screen: FitnessTracker
        name: Track lanes
        idea: Every measure runs as a lane on a night running track, with painted lane numbers at the start, white lane lines, a chequered finish at the goal and a runner chevron marking how far today has got.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/386.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            infield: #0e1612, the page, the board text ground and the style sheet
            stand: #1d2a23, the header and the results board
            track: #3c1b15, every lane group, fields and list rows
            covered: #c8634a, the stripe for the part of a lane already run
            laneLine: #efe5da, lane lines, painted numbers, the finish chequer and today's number tile
            ink: #fbf4ec, text and results
            muted: #e3c4b5, units and rest labels on the track
            infieldMuted: #a9bfb2, labels on the infield and the board
            amber: #ffb84d, the runner chevron, Finished tag, primary button, links and focus
            onAmber: #2a1206, text on amber and on lane line
        type:
            Arial Narrow, Roboto Condensed, Helvetica Neue, Arial for numbers,
            labels and headings, bold. Board figures are 40px, painted lane
            numbers 36px or 26px in small groups, results 26px, section titles
            22px caps tracked 0.06em, lane names 13px caps. Text uses Helvetica
            Neue, Arial, system-ui at 15px.
        layout:
            A dark green stand header with a small track oval mark and
            Brightwork Move, a pill switch of Today, Week and Plan with Today
            filled cream, and the date on the right, ruled below by a 4px cream
            line. The main area has two columns. Every lane group is a dark red
            rubber band with 3px cream lines above and below, square on the
            right and rounded like a track bend on the left. Each lane has a
            painted number cell closed by a 4px start line, the lane name in
            small caps, a thin covered stripe ending in an amber chevron, a
            chequered finish strip at the goal, and the result with its unit on
            the right. The left column holds Today's rings as lanes 1 to 3 and
            This week as lanes 1 to 7, one per day, with today's number on a
            cream tile, rest days as a dashed lane and the word rest, and a 0 to
            10 km scale below. The right column holds the Evening run as a
            results board with a cream frame, a Finished flag tag and four
            figures in a two by two grid, then Heart rate zones as five smaller
            lanes, then the Half marathon plan as two lanes for week 6 of 12 and
            tomorrow's 14 km long run, then Sleep as one lane with a moon number
            showing the deep share. Below 960px the columns stack. At 375px lane
            groups run to the right edge of the screen.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 28px between sections, lanes 58px tall or 46px in small groups, a 32px page gutter.
        density: Medium. Seventeen lanes carry every figure, read left to right like a race.
        corners: Lane groups are square on the right and rounded like a bend on the left. Pills for buttons, nav and tags. 6px on the board.
        borders: 2px cream lane lines between lanes, 3px lines above and below each group, a 4px start line after the lane numbers.
        shadows: None. Painted lines only.
        icons:
            A runner chevron at the end of the covered stripe, a chequered
            finish at the goal, a flag on Finished, a dashed lane and the word
            rest for empty days, a moon for sleep and an arrow for the next
            session.
        focus: A 3px amber outline offset 3px.
        tone: Race words such as Lane, Finished, Finish line is the goal, Longest lane and rest.
    style387:
        number: 387
        run: 78
        screen: FitnessTracker
        name: Boxing gym
        idea: A gritty gym wall at night, with a red digit round timer for the workout, rings counted as rounds of timer lights, heart zones scored in tally marks, and every heading torn from a strip of cream athletic tape.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/387.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            wall: #191817, the speckled concrete page and the style sheet
            panel: #24221f, rounds, scorecard, recovery and plan cards
            housing: #0b0a0a, the timer box and text fields
            chalk: #2a2f2b, the week chalkboard
            tape: #e8dfca, torn tape headings and the secondary button
            onTape: #1e1a14, text on tape
            ink: #f2ede4, text and tally marks
            muted: #b9b1a5, labels, units and done plan weeks
            red: #ff5a4f, the top zone, the current plan week, the primary button and the nav underline
            led: #ff4436, timer digits and lit round lights
            ledOff: #3a1512, unlit digit ghosts and unlit lights
            chalkInk: #e9ece6, chalk figures and bars
            chalkMuted: #b4bcb4, chalk day names and circled rest
            line: #3d3a35, dashed rules and card edges
        type:
            Headings use Rockwell, Rockwell Nova, Roboto Slab, DejaVu Serif,
            Georgia, bold caps tracked 0.08em, 16 to 20px on tape and 36px in
            the style sheet. The timer uses ui-monospace bold at 148px with a
            red glow, other digits 22 to 44px. Text uses Trebuchet MS, Segoe UI,
            system-ui at 15px. The chalkboard uses Segoe Print, Bradley Hand,
            Comic Neue at 14 to 24px.
        layout:
            A speckled concrete page. The header has Brightwork Move on a torn
            tape strip, Today, Week and Plan in slab caps with a red underline
            on Today, and the date on the right. A full width row pairs a steel
            timer box and the rounds card. The timer box has a 10px bezel, two
            bolts, an Evening run tape label and a Final bell done tag with a
            bell, then 42 min 16 s in red digits over unlit ghost digits, then
            distance, average pace and average heart rate in three columns. The
            rounds card shows Move, Exercise and Stand as Round 1 to 3, each
            with its value over goal, a row of round timer lights where one
            light is 50 kcal, 5 min or 1 h, lit for done, half lit for part and
            dark for to go, and a line with percent and amount left. Below, a
            chalkboard in a 12px wood frame shows the week with chalk hatched
            bars, the figure above each, rest days circled, a star on today and
            a chalk total line. Beside it a scorecard table lists zones with
            name, tally marks in groups of five and minutes, the zone 3 row
            tinted red. Last, a Recovery card with 7 h 12 min, a sentence on
            deep sleep and a hatched red deep share bar, and the Half marathon
            plan card with Week 6 of 12, twelve numbered squares with five
            filled, the sixth red and six hollow, and Next session tomorrow Long
            run 14 km with View plan. Each card has its tape heading overhanging
            the top edge. Below 980px everything stacks.
        spacing: An 8px unit. A 32px page gutter and 28 to 36px between pieces so tape headings have room to overhang.
        density: Medium. A big timer, three rounds of lights, a chalkboard, a scorecard and two small cards.
        corners: Mostly square, 3 to 6px on the timer and controls, round lights and torn tape ends.
        borders: A 10px steel bezel on the timer, a 12px wood frame on the chalkboard and 2px dashed rules inside cards.
        shadows: Hard 4 to 10px drop shadows under the timer and buttons and a red glow on lit digits and lights.
        icons:
            A bell for the finished run. Lights are filled for done, half filled
            for part and dark for to go. Tally marks count minutes. Rest days
            are circled in chalk and today has a star.
        focus: A 3px dashed tape coloured outline offset 4px.
        tone: Gym talk such as Today's rounds, Final bell, Zone scorecard, Recovery and rest.
    style388:
        number: 388
        run: 78
        screen: FitnessTracker
        name: Yoga dusk
        idea: A calm single column under a dusk sky, where the three rings become one slowly breathing circle, every figure is told in a soft sentence, and weeks and plans are strung as beads.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/388.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            skyHigh: #16132e, the top of the dusk gradient
            skyMid: #2b1f47, the middle of the gradient and the page fallback
            skyLow: #45284f, the warm horizon lower down
            glass: #1a1530, cards at 72 percent over the sky and empty beads
            track: #3a2f55, unfilled ring tracks
            line: #5b4a72, hairlines, the bead string and field borders
            ink: #fbf1ee, text and figures
            muted: #d9c7d6, labels and gentle meta
            peach: #ffb7a1, the move ring, today, highlights in prose, the current bead and the primary button
            sage: #b5dfc0, the exercise ring and zone 2
            lilac: #cbbcff, the stand ring, zone 1 and done beads
            onPeach: #2a1420, text on peach and on zone pebbles
        type:
            Headings and figures use Iowan Old Style, Palatino Linotype,
            Palatino, Book Antiqua, Georgia at 400, the greeting 40px, the ring
            centre 44px, card titles 26px, prose 19px at 1.6. Text uses Optima,
            Candara, Segoe UI, Gill Sans, system-ui at 16px and 1.65. The date
            and nav are lowercase, the date 13px tracked 0.12em.
        layout:
            A 760px centred column on a vertical gradient from deep indigo
            through plum to a warm horizon. A small header has brightwork move
            in italic serif and lowercase today, week and plan pills. The date
            and the greeting A gentle close to the day sit centred. Then a 380px
            breathing circle with three concentric ring arcs on soft tracks,
            peach outside, sage, lilac inside, a faint halo that slowly grows
            and settles, and 81% of your move goal with breathe with the halo in
            the centre. A three part legend gives a circle, diamond or rounded
            square, the ring name, value over goal and the amount more. Below,
            rounded glass cards. An evening run card tells the run in one serif
            sentence with peach figures, four soft figure tiles, a row of pill
            pebbles sized by zone minutes with zone numbers, and a lowercase
            zone list. A This week card shows seven glowing moons sized by
            distance with the figure and day, rest days as small dashed hollow
            moons with rest, and today named today. Then Sleep and Half marathon
            side by side, sleep as 7 h 12 min with a sentence on deep sleep, the
            plan as week 6 of 12 with twelve beads on a string, five lilac, the
            sixth larger and peach, and a line about tomorrow's long run of 14
            km. Below 680px the pair stacks and figure tiles go two by two.
        spacing: An 8px unit, generous. 28px between cards, 28 to 32px card padding, a 760px column.
        density: Low. One thing at a time down a single column.
        corners: 28px cards, pills for buttons, fields, nav and zone pebbles, round beads and moons.
        borders: Almost none. A faint lilac edge on cards and hairlines in the style sheet.
        shadows: Soft 50px dusk shadows under cards and warm glows around moons and the current bead.
        icons:
            Ring legend shapes, a circle for move, a diamond for exercise and a
            rounded square for stand. Rest days are dashed hollow moons with the
            word rest. A slow halo paces breathing and stops when reduced motion
            is asked for.
        focus: A 2px light outline offset 4px with a wide soft peach glow.
        tone: Lowercase and gentle, such as A gentle close to the day, breathe with the halo and a long run of 14 km.

    style389:
        number: 389
        run: 79
        screen: FitnessTracker
        name: Cycle computer
        idea: The day shown on two pages of a handlebar computer, a moulded housing with hardware buttons around a dark LCD split by hard lines into data fields, each with a tiny caps label, a huge digit and a unit.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/389.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #0c0d0e, the page behind the devices and the style sheet
            housing: #1c1e21, the moulded device body, nav pills and sheet labels
            housingHigh: #2a2d31, the lit top of the housing and the secondary button
            bezel: #060707, the black frame around the screen
            lcd: #0f1612, the screen and every data field
            cellLine: #2c3d33, the 2px lines that split the fields
            ink: #e3f3d2, digits, bars and lit segments
            muted: #9fb79a, field labels, units and rest days
            dim: #3d5446, unlit segments
            amber: #ffb648, the saved alert, the top zone, today, the current page and the primary button
            onAmber: #231503, text on amber
        type:
            Digits and labels use DIN Alternate, Bahnschrift, Roboto Mono, ui-
            monospace, Menlo, Consolas, bold with tabular numbers. The distance
            field is 88px, standard fields 54px, small fields 40px, units 15px
            muted, field labels 11px caps tracked 0.12em. Page text uses Segoe
            UI, Roboto, system-ui at 14px.
        layout:
            A plain header with Brightwork Move, Today and the date, and Today,
            Week and Plan as round pills with Today in amber. Below, two device
            housings side by side, each a 36px rounded moulded body with side
            hardware buttons, a page label and page dots at the top and three
            key labels at the bottom. Page 1 is the Evening run. Its screen has
            a status strip with Run saved, the date and signal bars, an amber
            alert bar with a flag reading Run done 8.2 km saved, then a field
            grid on six columns split by 2px lines. A full width Distance field
            shows 8.2 km at 88px. Then Time, Avg pace, Avg HR and Avg speed in
            half width fields, the speed of 11.6 km per h derived from distance
            and time. Then a full width Time in zone field with five bars,
            minutes on top, zone 3 in amber and Z labels below. Page 2 is Day
            and week. Move, Exercise and Stand each take a third with percent,
            value over goal, a segment gauge and the amount to go. A full width
            Distance this week field draws seven bars with figures, rest days as
            a dashed floor with a dash, two letter day names and a triangle on
            Saturday. Then Sleep 7 h 12 min with deep 1 h 34 min, the Half
            marathon at week 6 of 12 with a twelve segment gauge, and a full
            width Next session field reading 14 km long run tomorrow. Below
            1060px the devices stack. At 375px values shrink to 34px and half
            width fields stay in pairs.
        spacing: An 8px unit. Fields packed with 2px divider lines and 8 to 12px padding, 28px between devices.
        density: High. Every figure gets its own field, the run on page 1 and the day on page 2.
        corners: 36px on the housing, 12px on the screen, square fields, round page dots and pills.
        borders: 2px lines between fields and a 6px black bezel around the screen.
        shadows: A deep drop shadow under the housing, a highlight on its top edge and inset shade on the screen and hardware keys.
        icons:
            A flag in the saved alert, signal bars in the status strip, page
            dots and segment gauges for rings and plan. Rest days are a dashed
            floor with a dash and today carries a triangle.
        focus: A 3px amber outline offset 2px.
        tone: Device labels such as Avg pace, Time in zone, Run done and Next session.
    style390:
        number: 390
        run: 79
        screen: FitnessTracker
        name: Night trail
        idea: A mountain trail at night seen by headlamp, with topographic contour lines in the dark, a warm beam lighting the run, heart zones stacked as altitude bands in a peak, the week drawn as a ridge, and goals marked by painted trail blazes.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/390.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            night: #090e15, the page and the style sheet
            panel: #0f1823, cards, the hero and fields
            topo: #1c2a3b, contour lines in the hero
            line: #2b3d52, card edges, dashed rules and the climb path
            ink: #eef2f5, text and figures
            muted: #a9b7c7, labels, the ridge line, passed weeks and rest days
            beam: #ffe3a0, headlamp light, trail progress, today, zone 3, you are here, the primary button and focus
            blaze: #ff9a52, the move blaze, the next session sign and sheet markers
            onBlaze: #2a1204, text on blaze and beam
            moss: #9fd8a8, the exercise blaze and the Finished tag
            sky: #a9c8ff, the stand blaze and the tent
        type:
            One stack, Avenir Next, Avenir, Nunito Sans, Segoe UI, system-ui.
            The distance is 120px at 700 tracked minus 0.03em, hero stats 34px,
            sleep and goal figures 22 to 36px, the headline 22px at 600, card
            labels 13px caps tracked 0.14em, body 15px at 1.5.
        layout:
            A header with a peak and moon mark, Brightwork Move, Today, Week and
            Plan with an orange underline on Today, and Saturday 31 October
            after dark on the right. A full width hero card on dark slate with
            contour lines drawn on the right and a warm headlamp glow from the
            top left. It holds a headlamp glyph with Evening run in beam caps,
            the line Out and back under the headlamp, 8.2 km at 120px and a
            green Finished tag, and on the right Time, Avg pace and Avg heart
            rate over a rule. Below, a twelve column grid. Trail goals takes
            five columns, each ring a painted blaze, the name, value over goal,
            a dotted trail with a glowing beam fill and a dot at the percent,
            and a line with percent along and the amount to the goal. Heart rate
            zones takes seven columns with a peak cut into five horizontal
            bands, zone 1 at the base and zone 5 at the summit, each as thick as
            its minutes, zone 3 lit in beam colour, beside a list of zones with
            name and minutes. This week's ridge takes seven columns as a ridge
            line through the daily distances with dots and figures, hollow dots
            with rest on empty days, a flag on today and day names. A right
            column stacks Camp sleep with a tent, 7 h 12 min and deep 1 h 34
            min, and the Half marathon plan as a dashed climb of twelve markers,
            filled squares for passed weeks, a lit circle with you are here at
            week 6, hollow squares ahead and race week 12 at the top, then an
            orange arrow sign reading Next tomorrow Long run 14 km with View
            plan. Below 1000px cards stack. At 375px the ridge scrolls inside
            its card.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 20px between cards, 22 to 24px card padding, 36 to 40px in the hero.
        density: Medium. A lit hero, then four cards that each draw one landscape.
        corners: 20px cards, 10px controls, 4px blazes and pills for tags.
        borders: 1px slate edges on cards and dashed rules between trail goals.
        shadows: None under cards. Light comes from the warm beam gradient and small glows on progress.
        icons:
            A headlamp, a peak mark, a tent and a flag. Goals use painted
            blazes, an orange circle for move, a green triangle for exercise and
            a blue square for stand. Passed plan weeks are filled squares,
            future ones hollow and the current one a lit circle. Rest days are
            hollow dots with the word rest.
        focus: A 2px beam coloured outline offset 3px with a soft 6px glow.
        tone: Outdoor and quiet, such as Trail goals, This week's ridge, Camp and you are here.
    style391:
        number: 391
        run: 79
        screen: FitnessTracker
        name: Night swim
        idea: An outdoor pool under night floodlights, seen from above, where the screen is four lanes split by bead lane ropes, numbered from the starting blocks, with a round pace clock for the run and rings filled like water levels.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/391.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            deck: #14191c, the tiled pool deck, page and style sheet
            tile: #20272b, deck tile joints
            water: #05212d, the pool and the sheet basins
            lane: #072a39, alternate lanes and list rows
            floor: #021118, lane floor lines, tube insides, fields and inner panels
            ink: #eefaff, text and figures
            muted: #a3cad6, labels, tube outlines and passed plan weeks
            cyan: #7fe0ff, water levels, zone bars, laps, the Done tag, primary button and focus
            onCyan: #02202a, text on cyan
            coral: #ff8f80, rope beads, the pace hand, the top zone, today and the current week
            ropeWhite: #f2fbff, rope beads and the secondary button edge
            block: #e9eef0, starting blocks, lane numbers, the pool coping and sheet tabs
            onBlock: #0c1418, numbers on blocks
        type:
            One geometric stack, Futura, Century Gothic, URW Gothic, Avenir
            Next, Trebuchet MS, system-ui. Pace in the clock is 34px bold, lane
            figures 28px, block numbers 22px, lane labels 13px caps tracked
            0.16em, body 15px at 1.5.
        layout:
            A tiled deck page with a 48px tile grid. The header has a wave mark,
            Brightwork Move, square Today, Week and Plan tabs with Today in
            white, and the date with lights on. Four white starting blocks
            numbered 1 to 4 sit above the pool. The pool has a 10px light
            coping, floodlight glows at the top and four lanes side by side
            split by bead lane ropes in coral, white and teal, with dark T
            shaped floor lines behind. Lane 1 Rings shows three tall water tubes
            for Move, Exercise and Stand, filled to their percent with a wavy
            surface and a dashed goal line at the top, names, values and goals
            below, and a note on what is left. Lane 2 Evening run has a Done
            tag, a round pace clock with sixty ticks, a coral hand on 9 seconds
            and 5 min 9 s per km in the centre, then four figure tiles. Lane 3
            Zones and laps holds zone bars with zone 3 in coral, then the week
            as seven lap rows with day, bar and km, rest days dotted with rest
            and today in coral. Lane 4 At the wall holds Sleep 7 h 12 min with
            deep sleep, the Half marathon at week 6 of 12 with twelve lap ticks,
            five filled, one coral and six hollow, the next session tomorrow
            Long run 14 km, and View plan. Below 1100px the blocks hide, lanes
            stack and ropes run across, with lane numbers on white tiles before
            each heading.
        spacing: An 8px unit. Lanes with 20px padding, 14px between panels, 10px lane ropes.
        density: Medium. Four lanes side by side, each holding one or two panels.
        corners: 10px panels, 12px water tubes, 4px blocks, pills for buttons, fields and tags.
        borders: A 10px light coping around the pool, bead lane ropes between lanes and 1px teal panel edges.
        shadows: None. Floodlight glows sit in the water at the top.
        icons:
            A wave mark, lane numbers on blocks, a pace clock with a red hand,
            water tubes with a dashed goal line and a check in the Done tag.
            Rest days have a dotted line and the word rest. Passed plan weeks
            are filled, the current one coral and future ones hollow.
        focus: A 3px cyan outline offset 3px.
        tone: Pool words such as water level, At the wall, laps and to the line.
    style392:
        number: 392
        run: 79
        screen: FitnessTracker
        name: Watch face
        idea: The whole day laid out as a round watch face on true black, a large dial with the three rings as outer arcs and subdials for the run, ringed by smaller round complications for zones, week, sleep and plan, so nothing on the screen is square.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/392.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            black: #000000, the page and style sheet, true black
            bezel: #1a1a1c, rings around every face
            face: #0b0b0d, dial and complication faces
            subdial: #151518, subdials, legend pills, nav discs and fields
            track: #2a2a2f, empty ring tracks and future plan weeks
            ink: #f4f4f6, figures and the current nav disc
            muted: #a6a6b0, labels, ticks, rest dots and passed plan weeks
            amber: #ffb02e, the move ring, zone 3, today, the current plan week, primary button and focus
            mint: #5ef0c8, the exercise ring, deep sleep and the Done badge
            violet: #b9a3ff, the stand ring and time asleep
            onAmber: #241600, text on amber and mint
        type:
            One rounded stack, ui-rounded, SF Pro Rounded, Arial Rounded MT
            Bold, Nunito, Varela Round, Segoe UI, system-ui. The dial figure is
            84px at 700, complication figures 34px, subdial figures 26px, labels
            12px caps tracked 0.12em, body 15px.
        layout:
            True black. A header with a two ring mark, Brightwork Move, and
            Today, Week and Plan as 64px round discs with Today filled white.
            Below, a 600px dial on the left and a two by two grid of 250px round
            complications on the right. The dial has three thick outer arcs on
            dark tracks, amber move outside, mint exercise, violet stand inside,
            each ending in a small black circle, diamond or square. Inside sit
            minute ticks, SAT 31 OCT with 31 in amber, 8.2 km evening run at
            84px, a mint DONE badge and three dark subdials for time 42 min 16
            s, bpm 152 and pace 5 min 9 s per km. Under the dial a legend of
            pills with shape, name, value and goal. The complications are Heart
            zones as a numbered donut with zone 3 thicker and 42 min in the
            centre, This week as seven spokes from Sunday at the top, clockwise,
            length by distance, today in amber, rest days as hollow dots and
            23.7 km in the centre, Sleep as a violet arc of 7 h 12 min on a 12
            hour dial with a mint inner arc for deep sleep, and the Half
            marathon as a ring of twelve segments, five grey, the sixth amber
            and thicker, with 6 of 12 in the centre. Each has a caps title and
            one line beneath, the plan line reading Tomorrow long run 14 km.
            Below 1060px the complications move under the dial. At 375px the
            dial fills the width and complications stay two by two.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 40px between the dial and the complications, 28px between complications.
        density: Low to medium. One large dial with three subdials and four round complications.
        corners: Everything is round. Faces, nav, pills, fields, swatches and list rows.
        borders: No lines. An 8px bezel ring and a 1px outer edge around each face.
        shadows: None. True black lets the rings glow on their own.
        icons:
            Ring ends carry a black circle, diamond or square to match the
            legend shapes. Zone segments are numbered and the top zone is
            thicker. Rest days are hollow dots. Passed plan weeks are grey, the
            current one amber and thicker. A check marks DONE.
        focus: A 3px amber outline offset 3px, following the round shape.
        tone: Watch short, such as in zones, km week, asleep, plan week and DONE.
    style393:
        number: 393
        run: 79
        screen: FitnessTracker
        name: Bootcamp
        idea: The day issued as a typed orders sheet on an olive clipboard, with stencilled headings, numbered orders ticked off in boxes, a duty roster for the week, and DONE or OPEN stamped beside every goal in terse capitals.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/393.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            olive: #20231a, the hatched page and the style sheet
            board: #2b2f20, the clipboards
            sheet: #33382a, the paper on each board, fields and list rows
            rule: #565c44, dashed lines between orders
            khaki: #e9e0bd, text, ticked boxes, table rules, the roster header and the primary button
            muted: #c2b994, labels, order numbers, empty boxes and done plan weeks
            drab: #8c936c, the second stripe in hatched log bars
            stamp: #ff8a74, OPEN stamps, the top zone, today's roster header, the current plan week and sheet labels
            go: #c7e08a, DONE stamps
            onKhaki: #1d1f14, text on khaki, muted and stamp fills
        type:
            Headings use Stencil, Stencil Std, Arial Black, Impact at 900 in
            caps tracked 0.12em, with a thin horizontal gap masked through the
            middle like a stencil bridge, 26px on sheets and 44px for big
            figures. Text uses Courier New, Courier, Nimbus Mono PS, ui-
            monospace at 15px and 1.55, orders 16px bold caps, labels 12px caps
            tracked 0.14em.
        layout:
            A diagonally hatched olive page. The header has Brightwork Move in
            stencil, a typed slash line reading daily orders and the date, and a
            boxed Today, Week and Plan switch with Today in khaki, ruled below
            by a 3px khaki line. Each section is a clipboard with a steel clip,
            a hard shadow and a paper sheet inside. Orders of the day has a memo
            block for date, unit and status, then four numbered orders. Orders
            01 to 03 are Move, Exercise and Stand, each a bold caps command, a
            typed status line ending Carry on, a row of tick boxes with X for
            done units, one box per 50 kcal, 5 min or 1 h, and a rotated red
            OPEN stamp. Order 04 is the Evening run with a green DONE stamp.
            Beside it, the After action report with Mission complete, a four
            cell form of distance, time, average pace and average heart rate,
            and an intensity log of hatched bars per zone, zone 3 in stamp red.
            A full width Duty roster table has days as columns, Saturday headed
            in stamp red with a star, and rows for load bars, km with dashed
            REST, and duty with X RUN or STAND DOWN, then the total. Last,
            Lights out with 7 h 12 min and deep sleep, and Campaign half
            marathon with Week 6 of 12, twelve numbered boxes, and Next order
            tomorrow Long run 14 km with View plan. Below 960px everything
            stacks and the roster scrolls inside its sheet. At 375px stamps drop
            under their order.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 28px between boards, 22 to 24px paper padding, 14px per order.
        density: Medium high. Orders, a report form, a roster table and two short notes.
        corners: None. Square boards, boxes, stamps and buttons.
        borders: 2px khaki rules on forms and tables, dashed rules between orders and double stamp borders.
        shadows: Hard 4 to 6px offset shadows under clipboards and the primary button.
        icons:
            Tick boxes filled with an X for done units and empty for to go.
            Stamps read OPEN with an empty square or DONE with a crossed square.
            Rest days read REST with a dash and STAND DOWN. Today has a star.
        focus: A 3px khaki outline, an olive gap and a 2px stamp coloured ring outside.
        tone: Terse orders in capitals such as Carry on, Mission complete, Lights out and Next order.

    style394:
        number: 394
        run: 80
        screen: EmailClient
        name: Mail slate
        idea: A sober, professional three pane mail client in cool slate greys with one teal accent, where rules and steps of lightness do the organising and nothing decorates the work.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/394.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #171c22, the page, the message list and fields
            pane: #1f252d, the top bar, the folder column and the style sheet
            raised: #29313b, the open row and secondary buttons
            line: #343e4b, every rule and border
            ink: #e4e8ee, text
            muted: #9ba7b6, snippets, times and meta
            teal: #4fc1b0, the primary button, the unread dot, the open row bar and focus
            onTeal: #06221e, text on teal
            tealSoft: #1d3936, the current folder
            tealText: #7fd8ca, the current folder label and unread times
            star: #e9c46a, the filled star beside the word Starred
            clients: #8db6ff, the Clients label diamond
            invoices: #f2a970, the Invoices label diamond
            team: #c7a0f2, the Team label diamond
        type:
            One system stack, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
            Arial. Base 14px at 1.45. The open subject is 22px at 650, the list
            heading 16px at 650, the message body 15px at 1.65, unread senders
            and subjects 700, snippets 13px muted, folder group headings 11px
            caps at 650 with wide tracking.
        layout:
            A full width 52px top bar holds a teal square B mark with the name,
            a long search field, a teal Compose button and Mara Okafor with an
            initials disc. Below sit three panes. A 220px folder column lists
            Inbox 12, Starred, Snoozed, Sent, Drafts 2 and Archive with line
            icons, then the three labels each with a small rotated coloured
            square. A 360px list shows six messages as ruled rows with sender
            and time on top, subject, snippet and a meta line for label chips,
            the attachment and the star. The Northpass row is open, raised and
            marked by a teal inset bar on its left. The reader starts with a
            toolbar of Reply in teal, then Reply all, Forward, a divider,
            Snooze and Archive, then the subject, a Clients chip, a sender row
            with a round DW disc and the time, and the short body. Below 1100px
            the reader drops under the list. Below 760px the folders become a
            sideways scrolling strip above the list, and the reader follows.
        spacing: A 4px base, mostly 8 and 16. Rows pad 12 by 16px, the reader gutter is 28px.
        density: Medium. Six messages with snippets fill the list and the reader shows the whole note.
        corners: 6px buttons, fields and folder items, 4px chips, round avatars.
        borders: 1px #343e4b between panes and under every row. No cards.
        shadows: None. The open row has an inset 3px teal bar on its left edge.
        icons:
            16px line icons at 1.7 stroke. Unread is a teal dot plus bold text,
            starred a filled gold star plus the word, a label a rotated square
            plus the name, the attachment a clip plus 1 attachment.
        focus: A 2px teal outline offset 2px on every control and around the whole search field.
        tone: Plain nouns and verbs, such as Inbox, Mailboxes, Reply all and 1 attachment.
    style395:
        number: 395
        run: 80
        screen: EmailClient
        name: Focus inbox
        idea: The inbox leads with only the few messages that need you, set large in a quiet serif inside vast dark space, and lets everything else shrink to one soft line each.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/395.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #111214, the whole page
            well: #17181b, the two focus cards and the style sheet
            hair: #2a2b30, thin rules and card edges
            ink: #ede7dd, headings and the letter
            soft: #b3aca1, snippets, labels and folder links
            faint: #8f897f, times and small notes
            apricot: #f2b48a, the New marker, the open card edge, the Reply button and focus
            onApricot: #2a1608, text on apricot
        type:
            Two stacks. A serif, Iowan Old Style, Palatino Linotype, Palatino,
            Georgia, for the greeting at 60px, card subjects at 30px, the open
            subject at 40px and the letter at 26px with 1.55 leading. A sans,
            ui-sans-serif, Avenir Next, Avenir, Segoe UI, Arial, at 16px for
            everything else, with 13px spaced capitals for small section words.
        layout:
            A single centred column about 1040px wide. A quiet top line holds
            the brand with Mail in apricot and the folders as plain text links,
            Inbox 12 underlined in apricot, then the labels each led by a hash.
            After 96px of space the greeting reads Two things need you, Mara,
            with Mara in apricot, over the line Everything else in your 12 can
            wait until after coffee. Two large rounded cards follow side by
            side for Northpass and Priya Nair, each with a hollow ring and the
            word New, the subject in serif, the quoted snippet and the sender
            and time. The Northpass card has an apricot edge and says open
            below. A section titled Can wait lists the other four messages as
            single ruled lines with sender, subject, small notes and time.
            Far below, the open message sits in two columns, a left column
            with the subject and From, To and Sent pairs, and a right column
            with the letter in large serif and round buttons for Reply,
            Reply all and Forward, then Snooze and Archive as quiet words.
            Below 900px the cards and the reader stack. On a phone everything
            is one column with the list first and the message last.
        spacing: An 8px unit used in big steps. 96px above the greeting, 72 to 120px between sections, 32px inside cards.
        density: Very sparse. Two cards, four one line rows and one letter, nothing else.
        corners: 24px focus cards, fully round buttons, square rows.
        borders: 1px #2a2b30 hairlines. The open card trades its edge for apricot.
        shadows: None at all.
        icons:
            Very few, thin 1.5 stroke at text size. New is a hollow ring plus
            the word New, starred a filled star plus Starred, labels a tag
            outline plus the name, attachments a clip plus Attachment.
        focus: A 2px apricot outline offset 4px, and fields turn their underline apricot.
        tone: One calm human sentence up top, then single words, such as Can wait, Open and New.
    style396:
        number: 396
        run: 80
        screen: EmailClient
        name: Night letters
        idea: Mail as real paper post on a midnight desk under one warm lamp, with messages as envelopes sealed in wax until read and the open message laid out as a letter on dim warm paper.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/396.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            night: #10121c, the room behind everything
            desk: #161926, drawers, secondary buttons and the style sheet
            envelope: #2a2c3a, message envelopes and ribbon tags
            envelopeEdge: #3d4052, envelope borders and the flap lines
            paper: #2b251c, the open letter sheet
            paperEdge: #4a3f2e, the letter border and its header rule
            ink: #f1e7d2, text
            dim: #c2b8a5, subjects, meta and postmarks
            lamp: #f4c374, the glow, the open envelope edge, the Reply button and focus
            onLamp: #2b1a02, text on lamp
            wax: #d9675a, the seal on unread envelopes beside the words
            blueInk: #a9c1ff, the handwritten signature
        type:
            A book serif, Iowan Old Style, Palatino Linotype, Palatino, Book
            Antiqua, Georgia, for everything at a 16px base. The letter subject
            is 30px italic, the letter body 19px at 1.8, senders 18px with
            unread ones at 700, subjects italic. The signature Dana uses a
            script stack, Segoe Script, Apple Chancery, URW Chancery L, cursive,
            at 28px in blue ink.
        layout:
            The top of the page is lit by a soft radial lamp glow from the top
            right, with a small drawn lampshade hanging there. The header holds
            Brightwork in bold and Mail in italic, the folders as small drawer
            fronts each with a round knob, Inbox 12 edged in lamp gold, and the
            labels as notched ribbon tags with a coloured stripe. Below, a left
            column titled The evening post, six letters stacks six envelopes,
            each tilted half a degree the other way from the last, with two
            faint diagonal flap lines, the sender, the subject in italic, an
            optional quoted snippet, state words and a dashed round postmark
            holding the time at the right. The Northpass envelope is ringed in
            lamp gold. The right column, titled Open on the blotter, shows the
            letter on dim warm paper turned slightly, with From, To and Sent
            in its header, the subject in italic, the body, Thanks on its own
            line and Dana in blue script, then a Clients ribbon. Square cornered
            buttons sit under the sheet with Reply in lamp gold. Below 1000px
            the letter moves under the stack, and on a phone the drawers scroll
            sideways.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 14px between envelopes, 48px between the stack and the letter, 48 by 56px inside the letter.
        density: Low to medium. Six envelopes and one letter.
        corners: 4px envelopes, 2px paper, 3px drawers and buttons, round postmarks and seals.
        borders: 1px envelope edge, flap lines drawn as two diagonals, dashed round postmarks.
        shadows: Long soft drop shadows under envelopes and the letter, plus the radial lamp glow.
        icons:
            Few. A red wax seal plus Sealed, unread. An open envelope plus
            Opened. A clip plus Enclosure. A filled gold star plus Starred.
            Ribbon tags carry label names beside a colour stripe.
        focus: A 2px dashed lamp gold outline offset 4px.
        tone: Gently old fashioned, such as The evening post, Open on the blotter and Enclosure.
    style397:
        number: 397
        run: 80
        screen: EmailClient
        name: Sorting office
        idea: A postal sorting room in green enamel and brass, where folders are a wall of pigeonholes filling with slips, messages are tagged dockets on a belt, and the open message is a routing form.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/397.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            enamel: #18201c, the page and the belt floor
            wall: #212b26, the header, the pigeonhole wall and the style sheet
            cubby: #0f1411, the inside of each pigeonhole and fields
            steel: #3c4a43, frames and heavy rules
            slip: #2a332e, dockets and the routing form
            slipEdge: #4d5c54, docket borders and form cell lines
            chalk: #eef0e6, text and label plates
            dust: #aeb8ae, routing codes and meta
            brass: #e2bd4f, folder plates, the form band, the primary button and focus
            onBrass: #231a00, text on brass
            redStamp: #ff8a75, the Unread stamp with its triangle
            mint: #8fdcb4, the Encl. stamp and the Team swatch
            sky: #9cc3ff, the Clients swatch
        type:
            A condensed sans, DIN Condensed, Bahnschrift Condensed, Roboto
            Condensed, Arial Narrow, at a 15px base, with headings, senders,
            plates and buttons in spaced capitals. The open subject is 28px at
            700, senders 18px at 600. A mono stack, ui-monospace, Cascadia
            Mono, Menlo, Consolas, sets the body at 15px with 1.7 leading, the
            routing codes at 12px and the times in small boxes.
        layout:
            A header with a riveted brass name plate, the line Desk of Mara
            Okafor, morning sort, and a boxed field reading Find a slip. Then a
            full width pigeonhole wall in a steel frame, nine deep dark cubbies
            in one row. Each holds a stack of pale slip bars showing how full
            it is and a brass plate with the name and count, Inbox 12 and
            Drafts 2. Inbox has a brass inner frame and a small SORTING arrow.
            The three label cubbies use chalk plates with a coloured square.
            Below, two columns. The left, titled Inbox belt, 6 slips shown of
            12, lists six dockets shaped like luggage tags with a pointed left
            end and a punched hole, each with a code from IN-01 to IN-06, the
            sender in capitals, the time in a small box, the subject, the
            snippet and stamps. The right column is the routing form, a brass
            band reading Docket IN-01, open, four ruled cells for From, Office,
            To and Sent, the subject in capitals, the body in mono, and a
            dashed rule above square buttons with Reply in brass. Below 1100px
            the wall wraps to five per row and the form drops under the belt.
            On a phone the belt and form come first and the wall moves to the
            bottom as a three by three grid.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px gutters, 10px between dockets, 3px steel gaps between pigeonholes.
        density: Medium high. Nine pigeonholes, six stamped dockets and a full form.
        corners: Square everywhere. Dockets have a pointed tag end with a punched hole.
        borders: 2 to 3px steel frames and rules. Label stamps are dashed.
        shadows: Only an inset shadow at the top of each pigeonhole to make it deep.
        icons:
            Square capped 2px icons. Unread is a red bordered stamp with a
            solid triangle, Starred a brass stamp with a filled star, Encl. 1 a
            mint stamp with a clip, labels a dashed stamp with a colour square.
        focus: A 3px brass outline offset 2px. Tag shaped dockets get a brass edge plus a 3px inset brass frame instead.
        tone: Postal shorthand in capitals, such as Belt, Docket, Encl. 1 and Find a slip.
    style398:
        number: 398
        run: 80
        screen: EmailClient
        name: Newswire
        idea: The inbox reads as a wire service feed on a perforated dark paper strip, with every message filed under a timestamp, a priority code and an uppercase slug, and the open message set as wire copy.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/398.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            room: #121316, the page, the desks column and buttons
            strip: #1c1d21, the feed paper and the style sheet
            strip2: #23252a, the item on screen
            perf: #0a0b0d, the sprocket holes
            rule: #3a3c43, dashed and double rules
            type: #ecebe6, text, the ticker band and the primary button
            grey: #a9a8a2, slugs, ledes and labels
            flash: #ff6d5e, the NEW priority block and the WIRE tag
            onFlash: #1d0400, text on flash
            highlight: #f5d547, the current desk, the STARRED box and focus
            onHighlight: #1d1800, text on highlight
        type:
            A mono stack, IBM Plex Mono, SF Mono, ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas,
            at a 14px base for slug lines, copy and labels. Headlines use a
            gothic stack, Franklin Gothic Medium, Arial Narrow, Helvetica Neue,
            Arial, with the masthead 30px caps, the story headline 38px at 700
            and feed headlines 20px, bold when unread. The copy is 16px at 1.75.
            Slug lines are 12px caps.
        layout:
            A cream ticker band runs across the top with a red WIRE tag and the
            three newest items in one line. A masthead reads Brightwork Mail
            Wire over a double rule, with Desk of Mara Okafor, morning file and
            an underlined search led by a slash. Three columns follow. The
            left, DESKS, lists the folders in caps with Inbox 12 on a yellow
            bar led by a caret, then BEATS for the labels. The middle is the
            feed on a slightly lighter strip with a column of round sprocket
            holes down its left edge. Each item has a slug line with the time
            in bold, a priority code, an uppercase slug such as NORTHPASS-DEMO
            and the beat, then the headline as sender and subject, then an
            optional lede led by a dash. Items are split by dashed rules. The
            open item is shaded, ruled in yellow and marked ON SCREEN. The
            right column is the story, a slugbar, the big headline, FROM, TO
            and FILED pairs, the copy behind a grey left rule, an end mark of
            dashes around 30, and a joined strip of buttons each with its key,
            Reply in cream. Below 1100px the story drops under the feed. On a
            phone the feed comes first, then the story, then the desks.
        spacing: A 4px base. 10 to 12px item padding, 20 to 24px column padding, a 44px left gutter for the sprocket strip.
        density: High. Three columns of text with a slug line above every headline.
        corners: Square. Nothing is rounded but the sprocket holes.
        borders: 1px dashed rules between items, 3px double rules under the masthead and above the sheet, a 2px solid rule over the story.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            Typographic only. A filled square plus NEW in a red block, an
            asterisk plus STARRED in a yellow box, plus one ATTACHED, a caret on
            the current desk, and an end mark under the copy.
        focus: A 2px yellow outline offset 2px.
        tone: Wire desk shorthand in capitals, such as DESKS, BEATS, FILED, ROUTINE and YDAY.

    style399:
        number: 399
        run: 81
        screen: EmailClient
        name: Telegraph office
        idea: Mail as a sepia telegraph counter, with folders as brass plaques carrying morse marks, the inbox as a numbered received book, and the open message typed onto a telegram form.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/399.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            umber: #1c150f, the page and fields
            counter: #261d15, the header sign, the ledger and the style sheet
            form: #2f241a, the telegram and the open ledger entry
            groove: #47372a, ruled lines and borders
            cream: #f0e3c9, text
            sepia: #c3ae8c, subjects, box labels and meta
            brass: #d6aa5c, plaques, morse lines, the primary key and the open entry bar
            brassHigh: #f0cd88, the lit plaque top, focus and Starred
            brassLow: #8a6a33, the telegram frame and key edges
            onBrass: #241703, text on brass
            oxblood: #e48a76, the New mark with its filled dot
            wire: #9fc4b8, the Encl. mark
        type:
            A slab stack, Rockwell, Rockwell Nova, Roboto Slab, DejaVu Serif,
            Georgia, at a 15px base for names and headings. The sign is 26px
            caps tracked wide, the telegram subject 24px at 700, senders 16px,
            bold when unread. A typewriter stack, American Typewriter, Courier
            Prime, Courier New, sets subjects, times, marks and the telegram
            body at 17px with 1.8 leading on faint ruled lines.
        layout:
            A sign across the top holds a small drawn brass telegraph key on a
            wooden base, Brightwork Mail in wide caps over Telegraph office,
            Mara Okafor, and a boxed field reading Search the book, all above a
            double rule. Three columns follow. The left, Pigeon rack, stacks
            the folders as small brass toned plaques, each with the name, the
            count for Inbox 12 and Drafts 2, and a line of decorative morse
            marks under it. Inbox is lit in bright brass. Labels follow in the
            same plaques. The middle, Received book, Inbox, is a framed ledger
            with three ruled columns, the entry number, the time and a cell with
            the sender, the subject with its quoted snippet in typewriter, and
            boxed marks. Entry 1 is shaded with a brass bar. The right column
            is a telegram form in a brass frame with an offset outline, a band
            reading TELEGRAM with No. 1, received, Clients, three boxes for
            From, To and Time sent, the subject in slab, the body typed with a
            small STOP after each sentence, a line of decorative morse, and
            pill shaped brass keys with a hard shadow, Reply lit. Below 1100px
            the telegram moves under the book. On a phone the book comes first,
            then the telegram, then the plaques two by two.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between the columns, 10px ledger cells, 18px telegram padding.
        density: Medium. A ruled six entry book beside a full telegram.
        corners: Nearly square at 2 to 3px. Only the brass keys are pill shaped.
        borders: 2px groove frames, 1px ruled cells, a 4px double rule under the sign, a brass frame with an offset outline on the telegram.
        shadows: A hard 3px dark drop under each key so it looks pressable, and gradients on brass.
        icons:
            A drawn brass key in the sign. Marks are typographic in thin boxes,
            a filled dot plus New, a star plus Starred, a plus sign plus Encl.,
            and a dotted box for labels. Morse lines are decoration only.
        focus: A 2px bright brass outline offset 3px plus a soft brass halo.
        tone: Period office words, such as Received book, Pigeon rack, Time sent and STOP.
    style400:
        number: 400
        run: 81
        screen: EmailClient
        name: Mahogany desk
        idea: A private secretary desk in mahogany and green leather, where the open message lies on a gold tooled blotter in a fountain pen serif and the folders are leather index tabs along its right edge.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/400.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            mahogany: #22100d, the page
            wood: #301713, the crest bar, index tabs, blotter corners and the style sheet
            woodHigh: #3d1f19, the open correspondence line
            leather: #17291f, the blotter, the current tab and fields
            leatherEdge: #2b4636, the blotter rim
            gold: #d5ad57, tooling lines, the Reply button, the Unread nib, roundels and focus
            goldSoft: #9c7a35, hairlines and button edges
            onGold: #251804, text on gold
            vellum: #f3e9d6, text
            dust: #cdb9a0, subjects and times on wood
            sage: #b9cfbd, meta on leather and notes
        type:
            Two serif stacks. A high contrast pen serif, Bodoni 72, Didot,
            Bodoni MT, Baskerville, Times New Roman, for the brand at 26px, the
            open subject at 42px and the letter at 22px italic with 1.7
            leading. A book serif, Baskerville, Baskerville Old Face, Hoefler
            Text, Garamond, at a 16px base, senders 17px and bold when unread,
            subjects and times in italic, labels 13px spaced caps.
        layout:
            A wood crest bar holds a gold ringed italic B monogram, Brightwork
            with Mail in gold italic, The desk of Mara Okafor in italic and an
            underlined field reading Search correspondence. Below, three parts
            sit side by side. A 340px left column titled Correspondence, Inbox
            lists six lines between gold hairlines, each with a gold roundel of
            italic initials, the sender, the time in italic, the subject and
            snippet in italic and small notes. The Northpass line is shaded and
            its roundel filled gold. The centre is the green leather blotter,
            with two inset gold tooling lines, triangular wood corners at top
            left and bottom right and a deep shadow. On it sit From Dana
            Whitfield, Northpass, to Mara Okafor with the time, the subject in
            the pen serif, a small gold flourish, the letter in italic, a gold
            framed section mark Clients label and square buttons, Reply filled
            gold. Down the right edge hang leather index tabs, Folios then
            Labels, each tab rounded only on its outer side and the current
            Inbox tab in leather with a gold inner bar. Below 1100px the tabs
            become a row under the desk. On a phone the list comes first, then
            the blotter, then the tabs.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 48 by 56px inside the blotter, 14px per correspondence line, a 32px page gutter.
        density: Low. One elegant list, one letter and a column of tabs.
        corners: Square, with triangular wood blotter corners. Index tabs round only their outer corners at 10px.
        borders: 1px gold hairlines between lines and around buttons. The blotter has two inset gold tooling lines.
        shadows: One deep shadow under the blotter and nothing else.
        icons:
            Fine 1.4 stroke. A pen nib plus Unread, a filled star plus Starred,
            a clip plus Enclosure, and a section mark before every label name.
            Senders show italic initials in gold roundels.
        focus: A 2px gold outline offset 3px with a second fine gold ring outside it.
        tone: Formal and courteous, such as Correspondence, Folios, Enclosure and The desk of Mara Okafor.
    style401:
        number: 401
        run: 81
        screen: EmailClient
        name: Power user
        idea: A dense, keyboard first mail client on near black, with thirty pixel rows, a key hint beside every action and folder, a command field on top and a lime modal status line along the bottom.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/401.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            base: #0d0f14, the page, the list and fields
            panel: #141720, the command bar, the folder column, column headers and the style sheet
            zebra: #11131a, alternate list rows
            line: #252a37, dividers
            key: #1e2230, keycap faces
            keyEdge: #3a4052, keycap borders
            text: #d9dde7, body text
            sub: #8f97ab, snippets and meta
            lime: #c4f23a, the selection bar, the status line, the primary button and focus
            onLime: #142000, text on lime
            sel: #1d2614, the selected row and current folder
            pink: #ff8ad8, the unread dot
            amber: #ffc95c, the starred star
            cyan: #6fd6ff, bracketed label text
        type:
            A sans stack, Inter, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Arial, at a 13px
            base. The open subject is 17px at 650, the body 14px at 1.6, unread
            rows 700 in pure white. A mono stack, JetBrains Mono, SF Mono,
            ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas, sets the app name, times, labels,
            header fields, column heads at 10px caps and keycaps at 11px.
        layout:
            A thin command bar holds bw/mail in lime mono, a wide field led by a
            slash keycap reading search or command with an example query, the
            hints for commands and keys as keycaps, and mara.okafor. Three
            panes fill the window height. A 172px folder column lists folders
            and labels in tight rows, each with a count where needed and a two
            letter key hint such as gi or l1. Inbox has a lime inset bar. The
            list is a sticky headed grid with columns Flags, From, Subject,
            Label and Time, 30px zebra rows, the subject in normal weight
            followed by a muted snippet, labels in brackets. The selected
            Northpass row has a lime bar and a caret. The reader has a toolbar
            of small buttons each with its key, Reply in lime, the subject,
            a mono key and value block for from, to, date, label and state, the
            body and a dashed card of six more shortcuts. A full width lime
            status line at the bottom shows NORMAL, inbox 1/6, 2 unread, hints
            and the sync time. Below 1100px the reader spans under the list and
            the label column hides. On a phone rows become two lines, the list
            comes first, then the reader, then the folders two across.
        spacing: A 4px base. 10px side padding, 30px rows, 26px buttons, 1px gaps in grids.
        density: Very high. Five column rows, key hints, a shortcut card and a status line on one screen.
        corners: 4px buttons and fields, 3px keycaps, square panes.
        borders: 1px #252a37 between panes. Keycaps have a 2px bottom edge.
        shadows: None. Selection is a 2px lime inset bar plus a caret.
        icons:
            No icon set, only text glyphs. A pink dot for unread, an amber star
            for starred, a plus for an attachment, and labels in square
            brackets, each also stated in words for screen readers and in the
            reader state field.
        focus: A 1px lime inset outline plus a 3px translucent lime ring.
        tone: Terse and lowercase for data, such as yday, from, inbox 1/6 and NORMAL.
    style402:
        number: 402
        run: 81
        screen: EmailClient
        name: Zen mail
        idea: One message at a time on sumi black, set in a large quiet serif with ink brush strokes and an enso, a short numbered queue to the side, and a single vermilion seal for the one action that matters.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/402.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            sumi: #121110, the page
            stone: #1a1917, the style sheet
            wash: #2c2a26, dividers and the enso stroke
            paper: #ece4d4, text and the brush stroke
            grey: #a9a193, meta and queue subjects
            mist: #6c665c, underlines only and never text
            seal: #e5664f, the Reply seal, new marks, the current item bar and the focus ring
            onSeal: #1a0703, text on the seal
            moss: #a7c08f, the starred mark
        type:
            A mincho serif stack, Hiragino Mincho ProN, Yu Mincho, Songti SC,
            Noto Serif, Georgia, at a 16px base with 1.8 leading. The subject is
            56px at 400, the letter 24px with 2.0 leading, queue senders 16px
            and bold when unread, small section words 14px with very wide
            tracking. A sans stack, Hiragino Sans, Yu Gothic, Noto Sans,
            system-ui, sets meta and the small marks at 12 to 14px.
        layout:
            Three bands across the width. A 72px band holds Brightwork Mail
            written vertically top to bottom with a small vermilion square
            stamp under it. A 300px queue column, ruled off by one thin line,
            reads Inbox, twelve, then an underlined field reading seek, then a
            numbered list 01 to 06 with the sender, the subject and time on one
            line and a small mark below. The current item has a short
            vermilion brush bar to its left and a vermilion number. The folders
            and labels sit at the very bottom as small plain links. The stage
            fills the rest with wide margins. A large faint enso circle sits
            behind the top right. It reads one of six in spaced letters, then
            the subject very large, From and To with the time in small sans, a
            tapered brush stroke, the letter in large serif and a dash before
            Clients. Actions are a square vermilion seal for Reply, then Reply
            all, Forward, Snooze and Archive as underlined words, and a quiet
            line naming the next message. On a phone the brand runs across the
            top, the queue comes first, then the message.
        spacing: An 8px unit used generously. 96px above the message, 40px around the brush stroke, 64px before actions.
        density: Very sparse. One message fills the stage and the queue is six quiet lines.
        corners: None on panels. The seal has slightly uneven corners from 3 to 7px, and swatches are pebble shaped.
        borders: One 1px wash line between queue and stage. Secondary actions are words with a thin underline.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            No icon set. The brush stroke and enso are decoration. Marks are a
            glyph plus a word, a dot plus new, a six point star plus starred,
            a hollow diamond plus enclosed.
        focus: A 1px paper outline offset 6px with a vermilion ring outside it. Fields turn their underline vermilion.
        tone: Unhurried and lowercase, such as one of six, seek, and Next, when you are ready.
    style403:
        number: 403
        run: 81
        screen: EmailClient
        name: Friendly mail
        idea: A cheerful, chunky mail client on soft plum with rounded everything, a pastel colour for every person and label, and the open message shown as a friendly speech bubble.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/403.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            plum: #19162b, the page and secondary buttons
            card: #25213d, the list panel, the reader and the style sheet
            cardHigh: #2f2a4d, the open row, the current folder and the speech bubble
            edge: #3d3760, borders and ghost chips
            text: #f5f2ff, text
            soft: #bdb6dc, snippets and times
            mint: #7ee0b5, the Reply button, Archive and Team
            peach: #ffb38a, Invoices and the Starred folder tile
            sky: #8cc8ff, Clients and Sent
            lilac: #c9a7ff, the open row ring and sheet heading pills
            sun: #ffd76a, the New sticker, the inbox count and focus
            pink: #ff9ec7, the Write a note button and Drafts
            onPastel: #1b1530, text and icons on every pastel
        type:
            One rounded stack, ui-rounded, SF Pro Rounded, Nunito, Quicksand,
            Varela Round, Segoe UI, system-ui, at a 15px base. The open subject
            is 30px at 800, the list heading 22px at 800, the bubble 17px at
            1.6, unread rows 800, chips 12px at 800.
        layout:
            A light header with a tilted sunny B blob and Brightwork Mail in
            heavy type, a wide pill search reading Find a message, a friend or
            a file, and Hi, Mara! with a round sun avatar. Below, three parts
            with 20px gaps. The left column starts with a big pink Write a note
            button with a solid shadow, then Your mail and Labels as rounded
            rows, each with a pastel icon tile, counts in pills, Inbox current
            with a sun count. The middle is a rounded card titled Inbox with 2
            new ones for you, listing six rows with squircle initial avatars in
            a pastel per sender, the sender, time, subject, snippet and chips.
            The open Northpass row has a lilac ring. The right card shows New
            and Clients chips, the subject, a sender row with a big DW
            squircle, from Northpass, to Mara Okafor and the time, then the
            message in a speech bubble with one sharp corner, chunky pill
            buttons with Reply in mint, and a cheerful line saying one more new
            one remains. Below 1100px the reader spans under the list. On a
            phone the folders become a sideways scrolling row of pills, then
            the list, then the reader.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 20px between panels, 12px row padding, 28 to 32px inside the reader.
        density: Comfortable. Six chunky rows with avatars and chips.
        corners: Very round. 24 to 28px panels, 18px rows, 14 to 18px avatars, pill buttons and chips, and a bubble with one sharp corner.
        borders: 2px edge on fields and secondary buttons. The open row gets a 2px lilac ring.
        shadows: Solid 4 to 6px darker drops under the pink and mint buttons, like toy keys.
        icons:
            Bold 2.2 stroke rounded icons in pastel tiles. New is a sparkle
            plus the word, Starred a filled star plus the word, files a clip
            plus 1 file. Each label pairs a colour with its own icon, a heart
            for Clients, a coin for Invoices and two people for Team.
        focus: A 3px sunny yellow outline offset 3px.
        tone: Warm and chatty, such as Hi, Mara!, Write a note, 2 new ones for you and all caught up.

    style404:
        number: 404
        run: 82
        screen: DatabaseConsole
        name: DB admin
        idea: A professional dark console built from square ruled panes, a tree, a tabbed editor and a dense grid, where a single cyan accent marks only what runs and what is selected.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/404.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #111418, the frame and gaps between panes
            pane: #181c21, the schema tree, results grid, history and style sheet
            head: #20252c, pane headers, the toolbar, grid headers and row numbers
            well: #0c0e11, the editor, the title bar, fields and the status bar
            line: #2c333c, every rule between panes, rows and cells
            ink: #e2e6ea, text
            muted: #9aa4b0, column types, line numbers, meta and pane titles
            accent: #5cc8d6, the Run button, the active tab stripe, function names and focus
            onAccent: #062227, text on the accent
            accentSoft: #163037, the selected tree row and the current grid row
            keyword: #c6a8ff, SQL keywords
            number: #f2c879, numbers, primary key icons and the Read-only label
            ok: #7fd9a0, Succeeded and string literals
            bad: #ff9c94, Failed and the error message, on #2a1719
        type:
            System sans, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial, for
            chrome at 13px and 1.45. Data uses ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo,
            Consolas. Pane titles are 11px bold caps with 0.06em tracking. The
            editor is 13px mono at 1.6, the grid and tree 12px mono. The app
            name is 13px at 600.
        layout:
            A desktop database tool. A 36px title bar holds a cyan B square,
            Brightwork Data, a bordered production-replica chip with a cylinder
            icon and an amber padlock Read-only on the far right. Below sits a
            toolbar with Run in cyan with its shortcut, then Format, Save, a
            divider and Explain. The workspace is three columns. A 240px schema
            tree shows production-replica, then the five tables with chevrons,
            tasks opened and tinted, and its six columns with key icons for id,
            project_id and assignee_id and types right aligned. The centre has
            two file tabs, the active one with a cyan top stripe, a line
            numbered editor with coloured SQL, a green Succeeded bar with 3 rows
            and 38 ms, then a ruled grid with row numbers, typed column headers
            and right aligned amber counts. A 260px History pane lists three
            runs with time, name, duration and a tick or cross line, the failed
            one with a red edged error box. A segmented status bar closes the
            screen. Below 1100px History drops under the grid. Below 720px every
            pane stacks and the grid scrolls inside itself.
        spacing: A 4px unit. 28px pane headers, 5px by 10px grid cells, 8px by 10px history rows.
        density: High. Tree, editor, grid and history are all visible at once.
        corners: 2px on buttons, fields and chips. Panes and the grid are square.
        borders: 1px #2c333c rules between every pane, row and cell. The style sheet starts with a 4px cyan top rule.
        shadows: None. Depth comes from four surface steps.
        icons:
            14px square capped line icons at 1.6 stroke. Cylinder for the
            database, ruled box for tables, a key for key columns, a dash for
            plain columns, tick for Succeeded and cross for Failed, each beside
            its word.
        focus: A 2px cyan outline inset 2px on controls, rows and fields, offset outward on the Run button.
        tone: Terse tool labels, such as Run, Format, Explain, Succeeded and 3 rows.
    style405:
        number: 405
        run: 82
        screen: DatabaseConsole
        name: SQL terminal
        idea: The whole console is one terminal session in a tmux style frame, so the schema, the query, the result table and the history are all plain monospace text drawn with pipes and dashes.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/405.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            bg: #12110f, the page behind the window
            term: #171512, the terminal window and the style sheet
            bar: #2a251f, the status line and the focused list row
            rule: #4a4238, the window border, pane divider and dashed list rules
            ink: #e8e1d2, session output
            dim: #a89f8f, the banner, comments, durations and labels
            prompt: #d4aaff, the prompt arrow
            path: #8fc8ff, the database name in the prompt and sheet subheads
            hi: #f2b45c, the session tab, result header row, focus and primary button
            onHi: #241706, text on hi
            ok: #9ed98b, plus ok lines and the rows count
            bad: #ff948a, x ERROR lines
        type:
            Monospace only, ui-monospace, SF Mono, Cascadia Mono, Menlo,
            Consolas, DejaVu Sans Mono. 14px at 1.5 for the session, 13px below
            600px wide. The sheet title is 18px bold in hi with a hash prefix,
            subheads carry a double hash. The status line is 13px.
        layout:
            One bordered terminal window with a 24px margin. A thin title row
            reads Brightwork Data shell on the left and production-replica
            read-only on the right. The window splits into a wide session pane
            and a 360px side pane with a 1px divider. The session is a single
            pre block. A dim banner, then the prompt production-replica arrow
            with backslash dt listing the five tables as a pipe table with
            5 rows, backslash d tasks listing the six columns with type and key,
            then the query typed over seven continuation prompts, the result
            table with its header row in amber, a green 3 rows ok, Time 38 ms
            and a blinking block cursor. The side pane shows backslash s history
            as three dashed rows of time, plus ok or x ERROR, name and duration,
            the error text on its own red line, a legend sentence, then a boxed
            backslash conninfo with the three status facts. A tmux bar ends the
            window with an amber data session tab, windows psql and history,
            then RO read-only replica, lag 2s and 14 conns. Below 900px the
            panes stack. Wide session lines scroll inside the pane.
        spacing: One text line is the unit. 12px by 16px pane padding, 24px window margin, 12px on phones.
        density: Very high. Everything is text in one scrollback.
        corners: None. Every box is square.
        borders: 1px #4a4238 solid around the window, title row, divider and boxes, dashed between history rows.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            No pictures. Plus for ok, x for ERROR, a greater than sign for the
            focused row and square brackets around button labels.
        focus: A 2px dashed amber outline offset 2px. A focused list row also gets the bar fill and an amber pointer.
        tone: Shell talk in lower case, such as backslash dt, 3 rows, Time 38 ms, lag 2s.
    style406:
        number: 406
        run: 82
        screen: DatabaseConsole
        name: Schema blueprint
        idea: The console is a single engineering drawing on cobalt paper, with the tables drawn as an entity diagram in pale lines, the query and result as lettered notes, history as the revision table and status in the title block.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/406.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            paperDeep: #0a2140, the page and field wells
            paper: #0e2a4f, the drawing sheet and style sheet, with a 24px grid of faint blue lines
            line: #8fb6e6, frames, entity boxes, relation lines and cell rules
            ink: #e1edff, lettering
            muted: #a9c4e8, labels, column types and zone numbers
            pencil: #ffd479, the join line, the project_id row, callouts, Run, keywords and focus
            onPencil: #2a1d00, text on pencil
            redPencil: #ffa394, the failed revision and its error
        type:
            Condensed caps, Arial Narrow, Roboto Condensed, Helvetica Neue
            Condensed, Liberation Sans Narrow, sans serif condensed. Base 14px
            at 1.45. The drawing title is 22px bold caps with 0.16em tracking,
            block titles 12px bold caps at 0.12em, title block labels 10px caps
            at 0.16em. SQL and column names use ui-monospace at 12.5 to 13px.
        layout:
            A drawing sheet with a 2px outer frame, zone numbers 1 to 4 along
            the top and bottom edges, and a 1px inner frame split into a wide
            drawing area and a 340px notes column. The drawing area has the
            spaced caps title Brightwork Data over Schema plan, public,
            production-replica, then an SVG entity diagram. Projects, members,
            invoices and activity are four small boxes in the corners with a
            ruled header and PK id. Tasks sits in the middle as a larger box
            with six dashed column rows and types right aligned. A thick yellow
            line labelled JOIN runs from the project_id row to projects with a
            crow foot on tasks and a double bar on projects. A thin line runs
            from assignee_id to members. Numbered yellow circles mark due_on as
            1 and status as 2, and a dimension line under tasks reads
            6 COLUMNS. A legend follows. The notes column stacks Note A Query
            with the SQL and a yellow Run query button, Note B Result as a ruled
            table with small yellow bars and the caption measured in 38 ms,
            Revisions History as a ruled table with ticks or a red cross, and a
            title block grid of Drawing, Mode in yellow, Lag, Connections and
            Sheet 1 of 1. Below 1000px the notes go under the drawing. On phones
            the diagram scrolls sideways inside its frame.
        spacing: A 24px drawing grid behind everything, 16px on phones. 12px by 14px block padding.
        density: Medium. One diagram, three notes and a title block.
        corners: Square everywhere, including buttons. Callouts are circles.
        borders: 2px sheet frame, 1px inner frame and cell rules, dashed column rules inside the tasks box.
        shadows: None. It is a flat print.
        icons:
            Drafting marks only. Crow foot for the many side, double bar for
            one, numbered callout circles, tick and cross in the revision table.
        focus: A 2px dashed yellow outline offset 3px.
        tone: Drawing office labels, such as Note A, Revisions, Title block, Sheet 1 of 1.
    style407:
        number: 407
        run: 82
        screen: DatabaseConsole
        name: Mainframe
        idea: The console is a block mode terminal screen in seven field colours, with a command line on top, selection letters beside the tables, a message line and a row of PF keys, all in caps inside a dark grey bezel.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/407.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            case: #1b1d20, the page and the bezel
            caseEdge: #2c2f34, the bezel rim and sheet border
            screen: #030506, the screen glass and the style sheet
            blue: #74b6ff, protected text, types and plain table names
            turquoise: #5fe3e0, headings, field labels and PF key numbers
            green: #66f08a, input fields, selection letters, query text and OK
            white: #f4f4f0, data, the message line, keywords and focus
            yellow: #ffe27a, PK and FK marks, the replica name and the RO lock
            pink: #ff9ee0, PF key actions and the secondary button
            red: #ff7a72, the ERR code and error text
        type:
            Monospace only, IBM Plex Mono, ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo,
            Consolas, Courier New. Everything is 15px at 1.55 in capitals, 13px
            on phones. The status line is 14px. A faint blue text glow sits on
            the screen.
        layout:
            A rounded grey bezel with an inner ring holds a black screen. The
            top row has BWDATA01, the centred title BRIGHTWORK DATA QUERY
            CONSOLE and PRODUCTION-REPLICA in yellow. Next is COMMAND with an
            arrow and a green underlined input holding RUN, and SCROLL PAGE on
            the right. The body has a 34ch schema panel and a wide panel. The
            schema panel shows SCHEMA PUBLIC over a dashed teal rule, an S TABLE
            header, then the tables each with a green underscore, TASKS marked
            X in white, and its six columns indented with types in blue and PK
            or FK in yellow. The wide panel stacks the query in green with white
            keywords, RESULT 3 ROWS 38 MS as a two column table, and HISTORY
            TODAY as a table of time, RC, query and ms, with OK in green and
            ERR between asterisks in red beside the red error text. Below sit
            the message BWD0001I QUERY COMPLETE. 3 ROWS. 38 MS., a row of PF
            keys from PF1 HELP to PF12 CANCEL as real buttons, and a ruled OIA
            line with RO READ-ONLY REPLICA, LAG 2S, CONN 14 ACTIVE and a cursor
            position. Below 900px the panels stack, and on phones the title
            wraps to its own line.
        spacing: Character cells. Gaps of 1 to 4ch, one blank line after each panel.
        density: High. Four panels, a message line and seven PF keys on one screen.
        corners: 22px bezel, 10px screen glass, square fields and buttons.
        borders: Green 2px underlines for input fields, dashed teal rules under headings, a thin rule above the OIA line.
        shadows: An inner bezel ring and a faint blue text glow.
        icons:
            None. X selects a table, OK and ERR between asterisks mark results,
            RO in brackets marks the lock.
        focus: A 2px white outline offset 1px with a dark blue fill behind the focused field or key.
        tone: Operator capitals, such as COMMAND, PF5 RUN, QUERY COMPLETE and CONN 14 ACTIVE.
    style408:
        number: 408
        run: 82
        screen: DatabaseConsole
        name: Data lake
        idea: The console reads from the surface down, with each part of the screen a deeper and darker band of water, so status floats at the waterline, tables bob as buoys, results hang as plumb lines and history settles as sediment.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/408.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            sky: #0a2236, the top bar above the waves
            depth0: #11506f, the surface band and the wave strip
            depth1: #0d3d5c, the shallows band
            depth2: #0a2e49, the mid water band
            depth3: #071f36, the deep band
            depth4: #041322, the lake floor, the page and the style sheet
            glass: #0f3552, table buoys and fields
            ink: #eef8ff, text
            muted: #b3d6ea, depth labels, column types and meta
            aqua: #74e4ff, band headings, plumb weights, the primary button and focus
            onAqua: #032434, text on aqua
            sand: #e7c98e, history times and string literals
            ok: #8ce8b4, Done
            bad: #ffa092, Failed and its error
        type:
            Humanist sans, Avenir Next, Avenir, Nunito Sans, Segoe UI. Base 15px
            at 1.55. The app name is 20px at 600, depth figures 22px at 600,
            band headings 13px bold caps at 0.14em, result weights 24px bold.
            SQL and columns use ui-monospace at 13 to 14px.
        layout:
            A top bar with an aqua drop mark, Brightwork Data and Connected to
            production-replica ends in a full width wave strip. Below, five
            full width bands each have a 112px depth rail on the left with a
            dashed edge, reading 0 m Surface, 10 m Shallows, 40 m Mid water,
            120 m Deep and 200 m Lake floor. The surface band shows three round
            pills, a padlock Read-only replica, a wave Lag 2 seconds and linked
            rings 14 active connections. The shallows show tables as round
            buoys, with tasks opened into a glowing card listing its six
            columns down a left aqua line. Mid water holds a 20px rounded query
            panel with lower case SQL and a bar with Cast query, Save and a note
            that the replica is read-only. Deep shows three plumb lines from a
            ruled waterline, each ending in an aqua drop with the count, the
            Billing migration line twice as long, captions under each, and a
            sentence explaining that deeper means more. The floor shows history
            as three stacked sediment strips with sand times, the failed strip
            reddish with a diamond cross icon and the error line. Below 720px
            the depth rail becomes an inline label above each band.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px band padding, 12px to 16px between items.
        density: Low. One idea per band, read top to bottom.
        corners: Round. 20px panels and buoys, full round pills and buttons, drop shaped weights, 16px sediment block.
        borders: Thin translucent pale blue lines, the open table in solid aqua, a dashed depth rail.
        shadows: A soft aqua glow around the open table only.
        icons:
            Rounded line icons at 16px. Padlock, wave and rings for status,
            ring with tick for Done, diamond with cross for Failed, each with
            its word.
        focus: A 3px aqua outline offset 3px, following the round shapes.
        tone: Calm water words, such as Cast query, Soundings, Sediment and Waterline.

    style409:
        number: 409
        run: 83
        screen: DatabaseConsole
        name: Graph network
        idea: The schema is drawn as a node and edge graph, so tables are circles, columns are diamonds, the join is a thick gold edge, result rows are gold nodes sized by their count and history is a chain whose failed link breaks.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/409.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #0c0e19, the page
            canvas: #11142a, the graph canvas with a 22px dot grid in #2a3060
            card: #181c38, the inspector cards, history nodes and style sheet
            node: #1f2550, table node fill
            edge: #5a63a8, edges and outlines
            ink: #eceefe, text
            muted: #aab1da, labels, meta and section titles
            table: #a3adff, table node rings
            focusNode: #ff9fd2, the tasks node ring, the Run button, SQL keywords and focus
            result: #ffd27a, the join edge, result nodes, filter rings and string literals
            onResult: #2a1d00, numbers on result nodes
            column: #7fe0d0, column diamonds on #14322f
            ok: #8fe7a8, Ran
            bad: #ff9a9a, the broken link and its error
        type:
            Rounded sans, ui-rounded, SF Pro Rounded, Nunito, Varela Round,
            Segoe UI. Base 15px at 1.5. The app name is 19px bold, node labels
            15px bold, section titles 13px caps at 0.1em, the sheet title 26px
            at 800. Columns and SQL use ui-monospace at 13px.
        layout:
            A top bar with a three dot graph mark, Brightwork Data, a
            production-replica pill with a gold ring, and three status pills on
            the right. Below, a wide rounded canvas and a 340px inspector. The
            canvas draws tasks as a large pink ringed circle in the middle with
            six column diamonds around it, id key, project_id, title,
            assignee_id, due_on and status, the last two ringed in dashed gold
            and labelled filter. A thick gold curve labelled join on project_id
            links tasks to projects, and three gold result circles branch from
            projects, Billing migration largest with 2, Mobile app 2.0 and
            Website redesign smaller with 1. Assignee_id curves to members.
            Activity and invoices float with dashed rings as not in the query.
            A shape key sits under the graph. The inspector stacks a Query card
            with the SQL and Run and Show path pills, then a Result nodes card
            listing the three rows with sized gold discs and Ran in 38 ms and
            returned 3 rows. Under everything a History chain links three pill
            nodes, two with a green ringed tick and Ran with duration, the last
            joined by a dashed red link, drawn dashed itself with a crossed
            square and the error. Below 1000px the inspector drops under the
            canvas. On phones the graph scrolls sideways and the chain runs
            down.
        spacing: An 8px unit, a 22px dot grid on the canvas, 16px between cards.
        density: Medium. One large graph and two side cards.
        corners: Very round. 24px canvas, 20px cards, 28px style sheet, full round chips, buttons and history nodes.
        borders: 1 to 2.5px coloured rings. Dashed rings mean not used or failed.
        shadows: None. Rings and the dot grid carry the depth.
        icons:
            Shapes are the icons. Circle for a table, dashed circle for unused,
            diamond for a column, gold disc for a result row, ringed tick for
            Ran and crossed square for Broken, always with a word.
        focus: A 3px pink outline offset 3px.
        tone: Friendly graph words, such as Result nodes, Show path and History chain.
    style410:
        number: 410
        run: 83
        screen: DatabaseConsole
        name: Archive vault
        idea: The console is a dark reading room, where tables are labelled cabinet drawers, the open drawer shows its columns as index cards, the query is a typed request slip, results are ledger entries and history is a row of stamped call slips.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/410.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            vault: #14100c, the page
            wood: #2a1e15, the cabinet, the nameplate and the style sheet
            drawer: #35281d, drawer fronts and swatch cells
            drawerEdge: #4a3829, drawer and cabinet edges
            card: #2b2720, index cards, the request slip and call slips
            ledger: #1b201a, the ledger page, with rules in #3b4636
            brass: #dbb86c, label holders, pulls, the title, keywords, Submit and focus
            onBrass: #2a1c06, text on brass
            cream: #f1e6cc, text
            muted: #c4b593, labels, column types and meta
            margin: #e8917f, the ledger margin rule
            ok: #a9d68f, the FILED stamp
            bad: #f19a88, the REJECTED stamp and its reason
        type:
            Old style serif for prose, Iowan Old Style, Palatino Linotype,
            Palatino, Georgia, at 16px and 1.5. Typewriter for slips and cards,
            American Typewriter, Courier Prime, Courier New. The nameplate title
            is 26px small caps in brass, card titles 22px italic, section labels
            13px caps at 0.18em, ledger counts 18px typewriter.
        layout:
            A brass framed nameplate with a double inner rule shows Brightwork
            Data in small caps and Reading room for production-replica. Three
            pieces of furniture follow. On the left a 290px wooden card cabinet
            holds five drawers, each with a brass bordered label holder and a
            round pull. The tasks drawer is pulled out with a ledge below, its
            holder filled with brass, and six tabbed index cards inside, one per
            column with its type. In the middle the request slip, numbered
            0941, has the italic title Overdue tasks by project, a one line
            plain description, the SQL typed on ruled lines, and Submit request
            and Keep on file buttons. On the right a ledger page with a red
            margin line titled Entries returned, Entered in 38 ms, ruled rows
            with tally marks and counts, and a double ruled total of 3 rows
            entered. Below, a call slip log of three cards, each with time and
            name, two stamped FILED with a tick and the duration, the last
            stamped REJECTED in a tilted double box with the reason. A ruled
            brass plaque ends the screen with the three status facts. Below
            1100px the ledger moves under the slip, and on phones everything
            stacks.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 24px gutters between furniture, 10px between drawers, 4px between cards.
        density: Medium. Three pieces of furniture, then the slip log.
        corners: Nearly square, 2 to 6px. Round drawer pulls and tabbed cards.
        borders: 2px brass label holders, double rules on the slip edge and the ledger total, one red margin line.
        shadows: Deep soft black shadows under the cabinet, slip and ledger, and a hard ledge under the open drawer.
        icons:
            Objects instead of icons. Drawer pulls, card tabs, tally marks and
            ink stamps with a tick for FILED or a cross for REJECTED.
        focus: A 3px double brass outline offset 3px.
        tone: Archivist wording, such as Request slip, Submit request, Entries returned and FILED.
    style411:
        number: 411
        run: 83
        screen: DatabaseConsole
        name: Query notebook
        idea: The console is a notebook of numbered cells, so a short prose heading explains the question, the SQL cell carries its own output table, a chart cell draws the answer and the history is a log cell of earlier runs.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/411.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            page: #18161c, the page and the style sheet
            rail: #1f1c24, the table rail and the status bar
            cell: #24212a, cell bodies and secondary buttons
            code: #1a181f, the code area and fields
            output: #2b2732, cell output and inline code
            line: #3a3542, every border
            ink: #ece8f1, text
            muted: #aaa3b5, execution counts, column types and meta
            accent: #ffae6b, the active cell, Run cell, chart bars and keywords
            onAccent: #2d1503, text on the accent
            function: #9dc4ff, function names
            string: #b9e08e, string literals
            ok: #9fe0a8, Done and the idle kernel ring
            bad: #ff9d96, Error, on #33202a
        type:
            Three families. Prose headings in serif, Charter, Bitstream
            Charter, Sitka Text, Cambria, 28px at 600 with 16px prose. Chrome in
            Inter, Segoe UI Variable, Segoe UI, 15px at 1.55. Code in
            ui-monospace, JetBrains Mono, SF Mono, 14px at 1.65, and execution
            counts in 12px mono.
        layout:
            A top bar with an orange pause mark, Brightwork Data, Notebook
            overdue review and a round Kernel idle production-replica pill on
            the right. A toolbar holds Run cell in orange, Run all and a plus
            Cell. A 220px rail lists the tables in mono with tasks opened as a
            disclosure showing its columns and types. The main column, about
            940px wide, stacks cells with a 56px gutter for counts. First a
            borderless md cell with the serif title Overdue tasks by project and
            a sentence. Then cell 5, selected with an orange border and a 4px
            left bar, with a sql pill and ran at 09 41 in its header, the
            highlighted query, and an output table with index 0 to 2, project
            and open_overdue, ending in a green tick Done and 3 rows, 38 ms.
            Cell 6 is a chart cell with horizontal orange bars, labels on the
            left, values at the bar ends and dashed gridlines. A log cell lists
            the three runs with count, time, name and a tick Done or a triangle
            Error, the error shown as a red edged block. A status bar closes
            the screen. The style sheet is itself built from cells. Below 860px
            the rail moves on top, and on phones the counts sit above cells.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 14px between cells, 56px count gutter, 12 to 16px inside cells.
        density: Medium. One column of cells.
        corners: 12px cells, 8px buttons and fields, round kernel and language pills.
        borders: 1px #3a3542 around every cell. The active cell gets an orange border and a 4px inset left bar.
        shadows: None besides the inset left bar.
        icons:
            Few. Play, plus, a tick for Done, a triangle with a bang for Error
            and a ring for the idle kernel, each with its word.
        focus: A 2px orange outline offset 2px.
        tone: Analyst notes in sentence case, such as Run cell, ran at, Done and earlier runs today.
    style412:
        number: 412
        run: 83
        screen: DatabaseConsole
        name: Server room
        idea: The console is two equipment racks, with tables as patch panel ports, the open table cabled to its columns, the query on a console LCD, results as LED meters, history as an event log and connections as lit power sockets.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/412.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            room: #0a0b0d, the page
            frame: #24272c, the rack frames and the sheet border
            rail: #2f3339, mounting rails with dark screw holes
            face: #1a1d22, unit faces and the style sheet
            lcd: #0b1418, displays, log lines and fields
            lcdInk: #bfe9ff, display text
            silk: #e6e8eb, silkscreen labels and text
            muted: #a5abb5, model text, U numbers and units
            green: #4ee08a, OK LEDs, lit meter segments, lit sockets and Run
            onGreen: #04220f, text on green
            amber: #ffc04d, the read-only LED, SQL keywords and focus
            red: #ff7a72, the Fault LED and its error
            blue: #5aa9ff, the patched tasks port, its cable and foreign key columns
            yellow: #f5d547, the key column cable
            grey: #8d949e, plain column cables
        type:
            Industrial condensed sans, DIN Alternate, Bahnschrift, Barlow Semi
            Condensed, Roboto Condensed, Arial Narrow. Base 14px. Unit titles
            12px bold caps at 0.16em, the app name 22px bold caps. LCDs, log and
            values use ui-monospace, with meter values 22px bold.
        layout:
            A dark aisle header reads BRIGHTWORK DATA and Aisle 3, cabinet for
            production-replica. Two racks sit side by side, each a frame with
            rails on both sides marked with U numbers. Rack A holds a patch
            panel unit with five jacks labelled by table, tasks lit blue with a
            cable dropping into a blue bus, then six column strips in three
            columns, each with a coloured cable stripe and type. Under it a
            console unit with a blinking Ready LED shows the SQL on a dark LCD
            with amber keywords, and raised Run and Clear hardware buttons.
            Rack B holds a Result meters unit with an OK LED and three channels,
            each with the project name, a four segment LED meter lit by count
            and the value, then Rows 3, Time 38 ms and Unit open overdue. Next
            an Event log unit with three LCD lines, a round OK LED or square
            Fault LED, time, name and duration or error. Last a power unit with
            sixteen sockets, fourteen lit, and LEDs for Read-only replica with
            an amber triangle, Lag 2 s and 14 active connections. Below 980px
            the racks stack. On phones rails slim down and the ports wrap.
        spacing: Rack units. 6px between units, 24px rails, 12px by 16px unit padding.
        density: High. Two racks of compact units with many small parts.
        corners: Small. 6px racks, 3 to 4px jacks, buttons and displays, round LEDs.
        borders: A light top and dark bottom edge on each unit face, 2px jack rims, 4px coloured cable stripes.
        shadows: A heavy drop under the racks, a 3px hard ledge under buttons, LED glow and an inset shade in each LCD.
        icons:
            LED shapes carry meaning. Round for OK, square for Fault, triangle
            for read-only, always with the word. A blinking round LED means
            ready and stops when reduced motion is set.
        focus: A 2px amber outline offset 2px with a soft amber halo.
        tone: Silkscreened caps, such as Patch panel, Result meters, Event log, Fault and Run.
    style413:
        number: 413
        run: 83
        screen: DatabaseConsole
        name: Lab readout
        idea: The console is an instrument bench of hairline framed readouts, so status shows as large thin measurements, tables as coded reagents, the query as numbered protocol steps, results as filled sample vials and history as a pass or fail run log.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/413.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            bench: #0e1112, the page and the style sheet
            panel: #151a1c, readout cells and swatches
            hair: #343b3f, the 1px grid lines between cells and every rule
            tube: #22292c, empty vial glass and the scale track
            ink: #e9eef0, text
            muted: #a0aaaf, tags, codes, units and crop brackets
            acid: #d4f06a, readings, vial fill, the open table, keywords, Run assay and focus
            onAcid: #1c2600, text on acid
            pass: #8fe0b5, PASS
            fail: #ffa091, FAIL and its error, on #2a1a19
        type:
            Neutral grotesque, Helvetica Neue, Neue Haas Grotesk Text, Arial,
            Liberation Sans, base 14px at 1.5. Readings are 56px at 300 with
            tabular figures, vial values 40px at 300, the mode word 30px.
            Tags and codes use ui-monospace, IBM Plex Mono, at 11px caps with
            0.12em tracking, protocol steps 13.5px mono.
        layout:
            A header with Brightwork Data in bold and assay bench in light,
            and Specimen production-replica in mono on the right. The bench is
            a 12 column grid of cells divided by 1px hairlines, each cell with
            small corner crop brackets top left and bottom right and a mono tag
            row with a code on the left and a unit on the right. Row one has
            three readouts, R1 Mode with a padlock and Read-only replica, R2
            Replica lag as a big acid 2 s over a ten step scale with two lit,
            and R3 Connections as 14 active. Row two has Reagents, a ruled
            table coding the tables T1 to T5 with tasks T2 in acid and its
            columns as .1 to .6, beside Protocol, the SQL as seven numbered
            steps with dotted rules and Run assay and Duplicate buttons. Row
            three has Readings, three vials S-01 to S-03 filled to 2, 1 and 1
            with the value and project, and a summary of 3 rows, 38 ms and
            highest first, beside a Run log table of R-03 to R-01 with time,
            method and a tick PASS with duration or a cross FAIL on a red tinted
            row with the error. Below 1000px the wide cells go full width. On
            phones every cell stacks and the run code column hides.
        spacing: A 12 column grid with 1px gaps. 18px by 20px cell padding.
        density: Medium. Seven readout cells in four rows.
        corners: Square. Corner crop brackets mark each cell instead of rounding.
        borders: Only 1px hairlines in #343b3f, dotted between protocol steps.
        shadows: None.
        icons:
            Drawn instruments. Vials with tick marks, a ten step scale, a
            padlock, a tick for PASS and a cross for FAIL beside the word.
        focus: A 1px acid outline offset 3px with a 4px soft acid halo.
        tone: Clinical lab words, such as Reagents, Protocol, Readings, Run assay and PASS.

    style414:
        number: 414
        run: 84
        screen: TravelPlanner
        name: Night flight
        idea: The trip shown as a seatback screen in a darkened cabin, a deep violet bezel around a glowing moving map, swipeable itinerary tiles and a round icon dock, lit by a lavender and pink mood strip.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/414.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            cabin: #0c0a18, the page, the cabin around the screen and the style sheet
            bezel: #050409, the rounded seatback frame
            screen: #141127, the map ground, dock buttons and secondary buttons
            panel: #1d1936, side panels and list rows
            line: #34305a, hairlines, the map grid and panel edges
            ink: #ece9ff, text and map labels
            muted: #aaa3d6, labels, meta and HUD captions
            mood: #b49cff, the primary button, the logo disc and icon tint
            onMood: #1a0f3d, text on the mood fill
            glow: #ff9ad5, the route arc, city dots, the blossom note and focus
            booked: #8ee6b8, Booked and Done text and icon on a dark green pill
            pending: #ffc98a, Not booked and To do text and icon on a dark amber pill
        type:
            One system stack, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto. Base 15px at 1.5. Big
            figures 44 to 48px at weight 200 with tabular numbers, the trip
            title 36px at 300, section titles 24px at 300, tile titles 19px at
            500, labels 12 to 13px caps tracked 0.1em in muted.
        layout:
            A cabin band with a soft violet ceiling glow and a thin lavender to
            pink light strip across the top. Centred in it a near black bezel
            with a 32px radius holds the whole screen. A top row has a lavender
            B disc with Brightwork Trips, the trip dates on the right and a pill
            Share trip button. Below, a two column grid. The wide left card is
            the moving map, a dark violet chart with a faint grid, an abstract
            coast, three pink city dots for Tokyo, Kyoto and Osaka joined by a
            dotted arc and a small white plane. The title Japan in April and
            Mara Okafor and one guest float on translucent chips over the map,
            and a HUD strip under it shows Route, Length 14 days and Stays
            booked 2 of 3. The right column stacks Budget with a 44px 3,200 and
            a lavender to pink glowing meter, Weather on arrival with a 48px 17
            degrees and a pink blossom line, and Before you fly with the four
            checks as pills. Under the grid, Itinerary is a sideways scrolling
            rail of six tall tiles, each with an icon disc, date, title, detail
            and a status pill. A dock of rounded icon buttons ends the screen,
            Book train filled in lavender. Below 900px the right column drops
            under the map, and at phone width the HUD cells stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 20px bezel padding, 16px between map and panels, 12px between tiles and 40px of cabin around the bezel.
        density: Low to medium. One large map, three side panels and one row of six tiles.
        corners: Very soft. A 32px bezel, a 24px map, 20px panels, 18px tiles and pills for chips and buttons.
        borders: A 1px violet line round every panel and tile, and between HUD cells.
        shadows: A deep black drop under the bezel with a faint lavender halo. The budget meter and the ceiling strip glow.
        icons:
            Rounded line icons at 1.8 stroke inside round tinted discs. Booked
            is a check circle, Not booked a dashed open circle, Done a checked
            box, To do an empty box and Flight a plane, each beside its word in
            a pill.
        focus: A 3px pink outline offset 3px, also round the scrolling tile rail.
        tone: Calm cabin announcements such as Before you fly, Weather on arrival and Itinerary.
    style415:
        number: 415
        run: 84
        screen: TravelPlanner
        name: Departure lounge
        idea: The trip read off an airport departures board, split flap cells in monospace on black, framed by amber wayfinding signs with square pictograms and arrows, and a row of lounge seats showing who is travelling.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/415.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            hall: #101114, the page, the terminal floor and the style sheet
            board: #050505, the departures board ground and fields
            flap: #1c1c1f, split flap cells, cut by a black middle line
            sign: #1f2124, wayfinding sign panels
            line: #34363b, row rules inside signs
            amber: #ffb612, sign text, pictogram squares, times, the primary button and Not booked
            onAmber: #1a1200, glyphs and text on amber
            ink: #f2efe6, flap letters and body text
            muted: #b5b0a3, sub lines and captions
            go: #5fe08a, Booked and Done
            sky: #8fd3ff, Flight rows and the focus ring
        type:
            Signs in Arial Narrow, Roboto Condensed, Helvetica Neue, Arial, bold
            caps. The board in ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas at 17px caps 600
            tracked 0.06em. The board title 34px bold caps, sign titles 20px
            bold caps in amber, column heads 13px caps tracked 0.18em, figures
            46px monospace bold.
        layout:
            A black sign bar across the top with a 4px amber rule below. On the
            left a solid amber square with a black plane and BRIGHTWORK TRIPS in
            amber caps. On the right three wayfinding links, Departures,
            Checklist and Weather, each with an outlined amber arrow box. The
            main area holds the board, black inside a 10px dark grey frame. Its
            head reads Departures over JAPAN IN APRIL with the dates in an amber
            flap cell. A table of six rows has Date, Time, Destination, Detail
            and Status, every cell a split flap tile with a black line through
            its middle. Times show in amber, missing times show dotted flaps.
            Status is a bordered box with a word. The board foot shows a row of
            six lounge seats with two filled amber for Mara Okafor plus 1 guest,
            and the buttons Book train to Kyoto and Find stay in Osaka. Below
            the board four signs sit in a row, each with a 6px amber top bar and
            an amber pictogram square. Route draws a vertical line diagram with
            Tokyo, Kyoto and Osaka as ringed stops and the train time. Checklist
            lists the four items. Budget shows 3,200 euro saved over twenty
            amber segments, thirteen lit. Weather Tokyo shows 17 degrees high
            and a pink blossom line. Below 1000px the signs go two by two and at
            phone width one per row, while the board scrolls sideways inside its
            frame.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 6px gaps between flap cells, 16px between signs and 32px above the board.
        density: Medium high. Every leg is one board row of five cells.
        corners: Square. Signs keep only a 4px lower corner.
        borders: A 10px dark grey board frame, a 6px amber bar on each sign and a 4px amber rule under the sign bar.
        shadows: None, except the 1px black split line drawn through every flap cell.
        icons:
            Black pictograms on solid amber squares and outlined amber arrows.
            Booked is a solid outlined box with a ticked square, Not booked a
            dashed box with a dashed circle, Flight a plane with no box. Done is
            a check and To do a dash.
        focus: A 3px sky blue outline offset 3px.
        tone: Terse airport caps such as Departures, Destination and Book train to Kyoto.
    style416:
        number: 416
        run: 84
        screen: TravelPlanner
        name: Sleeper train
        idea: A night train compartment, walnut panelling and brass trim around a rounded window that holds the route as lit towns along a railway, a printed timetable card with dotted leaders for the itinerary, and small punched ticket cards on a brass rack.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/416.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            night: #120c08, the page edge and the style sheet
            walnut: #2a1a10, the panelled compartment wall with a faint vertical grain
            card: #1e1510, the timetable card, ticket cards and list rows
            line: #4a3424, row rules, double rules and card edges
            brass: #d9b26a, the window frame, rack, corner clips, dates and the primary button
            onBrass: #22160a, text on brass
            cream: #f3e6cc, text and town names
            muted: #c4b08f, italic captions and details
            lamp: #ffd98a, lit towns and focus
            booked: #9fd99a, Booked and punched rows
            unbooked: #f2a27a, Not booked and To do
        type:
            Iowan Old Style, Palatino Linotype, Palatino, Georgia. Base 16px at
            1.5. The timetable title 38px at 400, card titles 22px, stops 18px
            at 600, details 15px italic, labels 15px small caps tracked 0.18em
            in brass, dates with old style tabular numbers.
        layout:
            The whole screen sits on a walnut wall with a faint vertical grain.
            A pill brass edged plate runs across the top with a ringed B crest
            and Brightwork Trips in small caps, and Night service with the dates
            in italic on the right. Below, two columns. On the left a rounded
            window in a thick brass frame shows a night view, stars, a crescent
            moon, dark hills and a brass railway linking three lit towns
            labelled Tokyo, Kyoto and Osaka, with an italic caption under it.
            Under the window a card holds the conductor's weather note, a 52px
            17 degrees beside the text and a pink blossom line. On the right the
            timetable card has brass corner clips. It reads Timetable for over
            Japan in April and the party in italic, then six rows each with the
            date in brass, the stop in bold with a dotted leader, the detail in
            italic below and a small caps status at the right. Two buttons close
            the card. A rounded brass rack bar spans the width, and under it two
            ticket cards. Ticket checks shows each item with a punched round
            hole when done or a dashed square when not. Fare purse shows euro
            3,200 saved of 5,000 with a brass rail and a cream marker at 64
            percent. Below 960px all columns stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 28px between window and timetable, 24px between ticket cards and 12px timetable rows.
        density: Medium. A full timetable of six rows beside one large window.
        corners: A 36px brass window frame round a 26px glass, a 40px pill plate, 6px cards and 4px buttons.
        borders: 1px dark wood edges, double rules under headings, dotted leaders from stop to detail and brass corner clips on the timetable.
        shadows: Warm deep drops under the window, the cards and the brass rack.
        icons:
            Thin 1.5 stroke icons. Booked is a check circle, Not booked a dashed
            circle and Flight a plane. A done check is a punched round hole and
            a To do check a dashed square.
        focus: A 2px lamp yellow outline offset 3px with a faint warm halo.
        tone: Old railway courtesy such as Timetable for, Ticket checks, Fare purse and Conductor's weather note.
    style417:
        number: 417
        run: 84
        screen: TravelPlanner
        name: Passport night
        idea: The trip kept in a dark passport, a data page with the holder, dates and a machine readable line, then a visa page where every itinerary leg is an inked stamp of its own shape and unbooked legs are dashed blanks waiting for ink.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/417.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            desk: #0b0f14, the page and the style sheet
            cover: #13241f, the passport cover band
            leaf: #16232a, passport pages, cards and rows with faint guilloche rings
            line: #2f4a52, field rules, the photo box and page edges
            ink: #eef2ec, text
            muted: #a9b9b4, field labels, the machine line and blank stamp outlines
            gold: #f0cf6a, the emblem, section labels, the flight stamp, the route and the primary button
            stampRed: #ff9484, the Tokyo stamp
            stampTeal: #6fe0d0, the Kyoto stamp
            stampViolet: #c9b0ff, the flight home stamp
            booked: #8be3a6, Booked and Done words
            unbooked: #f6c27a, Not booked and To do words
        type:
            Georgia for page titles at 34px and figures at 40px. Helvetica Neue,
            Arial for labels at 12px caps tracked 0.2em in gold and body at
            15px. Arial Black caps for stamp text at 12 to 15px. ui-monospace
            caps for data fields at 15px and the machine line at 14px tracked
            0.12em.
        layout:
            A dark green cover band on top with a gold ringed star, BRIGHTWORK
            TRIPS in gold spaced caps and Travel document Trip 01 on the right.
            Then two passport spreads, each two pages side by side with a
            shadowed spine. Page 2 is the data page. Trip over Japan in April, a
            photo box with MO and plus 1, and fields Holder, Companions, Valid
            and Route in monospace caps. Funds shows 3,200 of 5,000 euros saved
            with a thin gold bar, then a machine readable line in a dark box.
            Page 3, Visas and entries, holds the itinerary as six stamps in a
            three column grid, each slightly rotated. The flight out is a gold
            double oval, Tokyo a red double circle, Kyoto a teal rounded square,
            the flight home a violet oval. Each stamp holds an icon, date,
            place, detail and a status word under a rule. The train and Osaka
            are dashed grey blanks with Not booked. A legend under the stamps
            explains inked and blank. The second spread holds Page 4 Endorsement
            Route, a sketch with contour lines, a coast and a dashed gold route
            between three ringed points, and Page 5 Conditions of travel with
            the checklist, a weather note with a gold left bar, and the two
            buttons. Below 900px each spread stacks its pages and at phone width
            stamps go two across.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 28 to 32px page padding, 20px between stamp rows and 32px between spreads.
        density: Medium. Two spreads of two pages and six stamps in a three column grid.
        corners: Square pages with a soft spine. Circle, oval and 10px square stamps, 2px fields and buttons.
        borders: Double borders on inked stamps, 2px dashed borders on blanks and dotted rules in the checklist.
        shadows: A spine shadow inside each page where the spread folds and a deep drop under each spread.
        icons:
            Small line icons inside stamps. Booked carries a check under a rule,
            Not booked a dashed circle in a dashed blank, and flights a plane.
            Done is a ticked box and To do a dashed empty box.
        focus: A 2px dashed gold outline offset 4px.
        tone: Official but kind, such as Visas and entries, Conditions of travel and Endorsement.
    style418:
        number: 418
        run: 84
        screen: TravelPlanner
        name: Road trip
        idea: The trip as a car instrument cluster at night, a budget gauge and a checklist gauge with orange needles flanking a cyan navigation screen, warning style lights for the checklist, and the itinerary read out as turn by turn route guidance.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/418.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            road: #06080a, the page and the style sheet
            cluster: #0d1114, the cluster hood, the guidance panel and list rows
            face: #12171b, gauge faces
            rim: #2a3238, gauge rims and the cluster edge
            line: #24303a, row rules and empty gauge arcs
            ink: #eaf2f5, text and figures
            muted: #9fb0b8, labels, ticks and captions
            needle: #ff6a3d, gauge needles, the logo and the primary button
            cyan: #5ee6ff, the nav route, gauge fill, Flight rows and focus
            go: #6ee07a, Booked and Done lights
            caution: #ffbf3c, Not booked, To do and the next to book line
        type:
            Bahnschrift, DIN Alternate, Roboto Condensed, Arial Narrow, Arial.
            Base 16px at 1.45. Gauge figures 30px tabular, the trip title 30px
            at 600, section titles 22px caps at 600, dates 20px at 600 tabular,
            labels 12px caps tracked 0.12em in muted.
        layout:
            A top bar with an orange outlined B and Brightwork Trips in small
            caps on the left, Japan in April centred, and the dates and Mara
            Okafor and one guest on the right. Below sits the cluster, a wide
            hood with an arched top and a 2px rim, shaded dark inside. Three
            parts sit in it. On the left a round Budget gauge, a 240 degree
            scale from 0 to 5,000 with a cyan arc filled to 3,200 and an orange
            needle, reading 3,200 euro saved and 1,800 to go. In the middle a
            cyan navigation screen with Next to book Train to Kyoto 6 Apr in
            caution yellow, a route on a grid from Tokyo to Kyoto to Osaka with
            ringed nodes and an orange position mark, and readouts Trip 14 days,
            Outside Tokyo early April 17 degrees high and Cherry blossom likely.
            On the right a Checklist gauge from 0 to 4 with the needle at 2.
            Under a rule four warning lights show each check with a check circle
            and Done or a caution triangle and To do. Below the cluster, Route
            guidance lists six legs, each with a rounded icon tile, a big date,
            the leg and detail and a status. Two buttons end the panel. Below
            900px the nav screen moves above the gauges and at phone width the
            gauges stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 36px cluster padding, 16px between gauges and screen and 12px guidance rows.
        density: Medium. Two gauges, a nav screen and four lights in the cluster, six guidance rows below.
        corners: An arched hood with a 220 by 140px top radius, a 14px screen, 12px icon tiles, 8px lights and 10px buttons.
        borders: A 2px rim on the hood and gauge faces and 1px rules between guidance rows.
        shadows: Deep inset shade at the top of the hood and a soft cyan halo round gauges and focus.
        icons:
            2px line icons in rounded tiles. Booked and Done are a check circle,
            Not booked and To do a caution triangle and Flight a plane, always
            beside the word.
        focus: A 3px cyan outline offset 3px with a cyan glow.
        tone: Driver prompts such as Next to book, Route guidance and Outside.

    style419:
        number: 419
        run: 85
        screen: TravelPlanner
        name: Night sailing
        idea: The trip on a marine chart plotter run in red night mode, one hue only, a ruled data bar, a chart with crosshair waypoints and a dashed planned route, a waypoint table and physical softkeys on the case, with states told by filled or hollow shapes.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/419.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            cockpit: #0a0303, the page and the style sheet
            case: #1a1312, the plotter housing and softkeys
            screen: #120505, the display ground and the sea
            land: #240a08, land on the chart and the title bar
            line: #5a1f1a, every rule and cell divider
            red: #ff5c4d, the route, waypoint numbers, headings, Not booked and the primary button
            ink: #ffc9c0, text, waypoint crosshairs, Booked and focus
            muted: #d98477, labels, captions and Flight rows
            onRed: #1a0000, text on the red button
        type:
            One monospace stack, ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas,
            Liberation Mono. Base 14px at 1.45, mostly caps. Readouts 20px bold
            tabular, the title 20px bold tracked 0.14em, chart labels 15px bold,
            headings 12px bold tracked 0.14em in red, labels 11px tracked 0.12em
            in muted.
        layout:
            A dark cockpit with a faint red glow at the top. The plotter case is
            a 22px rounded charcoal housing. Inside it the screen sits on the
            left and a column of four softkeys on the right. The screen opens
            with a title bar, a lit red dot with BRIGHTWORK TRIPS NIGHT, JAPAN
            IN APRIL centred and ROUTE PLAN 01 on the right. A data bar of four
            ruled cells follows, Dates 01 to 14 APR 2027, Crew M OKAFOR plus 1,
            Fund 3,200 of 5,000 euro with a small red bar and 64 percent, and WX
            Tokyo 17 degrees HI with blossom likely. The main area splits. The
            chart on the left shows dark land and sea, depth contours, a grid, a
            north arrow, and waypoints 02 Tokyo, 04 Kyoto and 05 Osaka as
            crosshair circles on a solid red route with a dashed inner line and
            a rail label. A caption line gives the weather in full. On the right
            a Waypoints table lists WPT, Date, Leg with detail under it, and
            State. Unbooked rows carry a faint red tint. A ruled row of four pre
            departure checks closes the screen. Softkeys read BOOK TRAIN 03,
            FIND STAY 05, VIEW CHECKS and VIEW ROUTE, the first ringed in red.
            Below 980px the table drops under the chart and below 700px the
            softkeys become a row of four.
        spacing: 4px steps. 8 to 12px cell padding, 14px between screen and keys and 18px case padding.
        density: High. A four cell data bar, a chart, a six row table and four checks on one screen.
        corners: Square inside the screen. A 22px case and 10px softkeys outside it.
        borders: 1px dark red rules split every cell, and a 2px black edge round the screen.
        shadows: A deep inset vignette inside the screen, softkeys on a 3px black ledge.
        icons:
            Nautical shapes in one colour. Booked is a filled diamond, Not
            booked a dashed hollow diamond and Flight an arrowhead. Done is a
            filled square and To do a hollow square. Waypoints are crosshair
            circles.
        focus: A 3px pale red outline offset 2px.
        tone: Instrument caps and short forms such as WPT, CREW, FUND and PRE DEPARTURE CHECKS.
    style420:
        number: 420
        run: 85
        screen: TravelPlanner
        name: Desert stars
        idea: The trip under a desert night sky, a full width starfield that warms to an ember horizon over dune silhouettes, a huge thin title, the route drawn as a three star constellation, the itinerary as a glowing star line, and the weather sitting on the horizon.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/420.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            sky: #0b0d24, the upper night sky behind the hero
            deep: #070818, the zenith at the top of the sky gradient
            panel: #0c0e28, the itinerary glass panel at 82 percent
            ground: #120c16, dunes, the lower band and the page below
            duneCard: #1a1220, style sheet cards, fields and list rows
            ink: #f6efe4, text
            muted: #b9b3d1, captions, labels and Not booked
            star: #fff6d8, stars, nodes, the constellation and focus
            ember: #ffb37a, the horizon glow, dates and the primary button
            onEmber: #2a1206, text on ember
            rose: #f5a8bb, the cherry blossom note and the meter start
            gold: #ffe08a, Booked and Done stars
        type:
            Avenir Next, Segoe UI, Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial. Base 16px
            at 1.6. The title 88px at 200 on two lines, the horizon figure 96px
            at 200 in star white, leg titles 22px at 300, labels 13px caps
            tracked 0.3em, dates 12px caps tracked 0.2em in ember.
        layout:
            A full width night hero. The sky runs from near black at the top
            through indigo to a plum and ember band at the horizon, scattered
            with small stars, and two dune silhouettes close it at the bottom.
            Over it a quiet top row with a star and BRIGHTWORK TRIPS in spaced
            caps and the dates on the right. Then two columns. On the left Mara
            Okafor and one guest in ember caps, Japan in April as a huge thin
            title, and below it the route as a constellation, three haloed stars
            named Tokyo, Kyoto and Osaka in spaced caps joined by fine lines,
            with an italic caption. On the right a 28px rounded glass panel
            holds Itinerary as a vertical star line. Each leg has a node on the
            line, glowing solid when booked, a dashed ring when not, small for
            flights, then the date in ember, the title, the detail and a status
            at the right. Two pill buttons end the panel. On the horizon itself
            sits 17 degrees in a huge glowing figure beside a dark chip with the
            weather sentence and the blossom note. Below the dunes, on the
            ground colour, two quiet blocks under thin rules, Before the journey
            with star bullets and Budget with a 56px thin 3,200 and a rose to
            ember glowing line. Below 900px the columns stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit with very wide gaps. 64px between title and panel and 120px of horizon below the weather.
        density: Low. One title, one constellation, one list, a horizon figure and two quiet blocks.
        corners: A 28px glass panel, and pill buttons, fields and rows.
        borders: A faint star coloured edge on the glass panel and a thin vertical star line through the itinerary.
        shadows: No drop shadows. Stars, nodes, the meter and the horizon figure glow.
        icons:
            Stars as states. Booked and Done are a filled gold star, Not booked
            and To do a dashed hollow star and Flight a thin plane. Booked nodes
            glow and unbooked nodes are dashed rings.
        focus: A 2px star white outline offset 4px with a soft halo.
        tone: Hushed and poetic, such as Before the journey and The route read like a constellation.
    style421:
        number: 421
        run: 85
        screen: TravelPlanner
        name: Neon alley
        idea: The itinerary as a rainy side street of hanging neon signs, each leg a sign with a vertical date blade, booked legs lit in a glowing tube colour and unbooked legs dark with dashed unlit tubes, over a faint brick wall and slanted rain.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/421.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            wall: #0d0b12, the page, the alley wall and the style sheet
            brick: #16121c, lower panels and swatch cards
            signBox: #0a080e, sign faces, blades, fields and list rows
            line: #2a2433, panel edges and row rules
            ink: #f4f1ff, text
            muted: #b4abc8, captions, dates and labels
            pink: #ff5fb0, the Tokyo sign, the route tube, the title glow and the primary button
            cyan: #52f3ff, the flight sign, route nodes and the secondary button
            green: #7dff9a, the Kyoto sign, Booked and Done
            violet: #c4a2ff, the flight home sign
            yellow: #ffe45c, budget digits and focus
            unlit: #6e6680, dashed unlit tubes on unbooked signs
        type:
            Body in Avenir Next Condensed, Arial Narrow, Roboto Condensed at
            16px. Signs and the title in Arial Rounded MT Bold, Trebuchet MS,
            bold. The title 96px with a coloured neon text glow, sign titles
            26px, budget digits 40px monospace bold in yellow, blades 15px bold
            caps set vertically, labels 14px bold caps tracked 0.24em.
        layout:
            A dark wall with a faint brick grid and thin slanted rain lines over
            everything. A top row has Brightwork glowing pink and Trips plain,
            with the dates and the party on the right. The hero title reads
            Japan in cyan neon and in April in pink neon, with one muted line
            explaining that lit signs are booked. Itinerary follows as six signs
            in three columns, the middle column dropped 28px so signs hang at
            different heights. Each sign is a narrow blade with the date set
            vertically joined to a face with the date, an icon and title, the
            detail and a status pill. Lit signs use their tube colour for a 2px
            border and an outer and inner glow, the flight out cyan, Tokyo pink,
            Kyoto green and the flight home violet. The train and Osaka are
            unlit, a dashed grey tube and no glow, with Not booked unlit in a
            dashed pill. A pink pill and a cyan outlined pill follow. A row of
            four brick panels closes the screen. Route is a small neon sign with
            a pink tube joining cyan ringed Tokyo, Kyoto and Osaka. Checklist
            lists the checks with green glowing Done or plain To do. Budget
            shows 3,200 of 5,000 euro in yellow digits over a glowing bar.
            Weather shows a cyan glowing 17 degrees and a pink blossom line.
            Below 1000px signs go two across and panels two by two, and at phone
            width all go single.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 22px between signs, alternate signs dropped 28px and 18px between lower panels.
        density: Medium. Six signs in three columns, then four small panels.
        corners: 14px sign faces joined to 12px blades, and pill status tags and buttons.
        borders: 2px tube borders in each sign colour, dashed for unlit signs, and 1px dark edges on panels.
        shadows: Neon glow in the tube colour outside and inside lit signs and round primary controls. No drop shadows.
        icons:
            2px line icons tinted in the tube colour. Booked is a check circle
            in a solid pill, Not booked a dashed circle in a dashed pill and
            Flight a plane. Done is a check and To do an open circle.
        focus: A 3px yellow outline offset 3px with a yellow glow.
        tone: Streetwise and short, such as Lit signs are booked, dark ones still need you.
    style422:
        number: 422
        run: 85
        screen: TravelPlanner
        name: Hotel noir
        idea: The trip as a dim hotel lobby in black and brass, a wall of deep key boxes where booked legs hold a hanging key, unbooked legs show an empty hook and flights leave a letter, beside a guest register, a weather telegram and a deco framed map, under slanted blind shadows.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/422.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            lobby: #0b0b0c, the page and the style sheet
            panel: #151515, the guest register and swatch cards
            cubby: #1c1b19, key box interiors and list rows
            wood: #241f18, the key box frame
            line: #34312c, register rules and panel edges
            ink: #f1ede4, text, flight letters and focus
            muted: #b3ada1, captions, labels and Not booked
            brass: #c9a45c, number plates, rules, the meter and the primary button
            brassText: #e3c27e, section labels, keys, Booked and Done
            onBrass: #1a1305, text on brass
        type:
            Display in Didot, Bodoni 72, Bodoni MT, Georgia. Body in Georgia at
            16px, often italic. Labels in Futura, Century Gothic, Avenir Next at
            12 to 13px caps tracked 0.3em in brass. The telegram in Courier New
            at 15px caps. The title 96px at 400, box titles 26px.
        layout:
            A dark lobby with a warm glow at the top left and diagonal pale
            bands from window blinds across the whole screen. A marquee of thin
            and double brass rules with BRIGHTWORK TRIPS widely spaced in the
            middle. A centred title block, The front desk presents in italic,
            Japan in April in a large Didone face, and a spaced caps line with
            three cities, fourteen days and the dates. Below, two columns. The
            left is the key wall, a 3 by 2 grid of deep cubbies in a thick dark
            wood frame, each shaded dark inside with a brass number plate 01 to
            06 on its top edge. Inside, a drawn object sits left of the text.
            Booked Tokyo and Kyoto hold a brass key with a tag, the train and
            Osaka show an empty hook over a dashed square, and both flights show
            a white letter. The text gives the date in caps, the title, the
            detail in italic and a status tag. Two square buttons follow. The
            right column stacks the guest register, rows Guest, Party, Stay and
            Account in italic, a thin brass meter and Front desk checks with
            dotted leaders, then a telegram card with a brass left bar reading
            the weather with STOP between phrases, then a deco double framed map
            with diamond markers for Tokyo, Kyoto and Osaka. Below 1060px the
            register column moves under the wall, then boxes go two across and
            one across at phone width.
        spacing: An 8px unit. 44px round the title, 32px between the key wall and the register and a 6px wooden frame between boxes.
        density: Medium. Six key boxes, one register, a telegram and a small framed map.
        corners: Square throughout. Only the brass number plates round by 2px.
        borders: A thick dark wood frame round every box, double brass rules in the marquee, dotted leaders in the checks and a brass bar on the telegram.
        shadows: Deep inset shade at the top of each box, long drops under the key wall and the register, and diagonal light bands from blinds.
        icons:
            Drawn objects tell state. Booked is a brass key on its hook, Not
            booked an empty hook over a dashed square and a flight a white
            letter, each with a word in a tag, dashed for Not booked. Done is a
            check and To do a dash.
        focus: A 2px ink outline offset 3px, ringed again by a thin brass line.
        tone: A discreet concierge, such as The front desk presents, Key boxes and Check out.
    style423:
        number: 423
        run: 85
        screen: TravelPlanner
        name: Arctic expedition
        idea: The trip kept as a polar expedition log, a dark graph paper logbook with an orange margin line where each leg is a dated entry, beside a contoured route sheet with camp triangles, a weather observation table, a taped kit list and a provisions fund drawn as ration blocks.
        page: spec/design/VisualStyles.styles/423.html
        verdict: unrated
        palette:
            polarNight: #0a1118, the page and the style sheet
            logPage: #101b25, the logbook and note cards
            grid: #18283a, graph paper lines on the logbook
            line: #24394c, card edges and dashed table rules
            ink: #e6f1f8, text
            muted: #9fb5c6, labels, captions and flight entries
            ice: #a8dcff, headings, the route, camps, the booked entry rule and the primary button
            onIce: #06202f, text on ice
            frost: #d6f0ff, the focus ring
            signal: #ff9a5c, the margin line, Not booked and To do
            secured: #8fe3c0, Booked and Done
        type:
            Notes in system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto at 15px. Log heads, labels and
            stamps in ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo at 12px bold caps
            tracked 0.12 to 0.16em in ice. The log title 44px at 700, entry
            titles 20px at 700, the fund figure 32px tabular.
        layout:
            A thin header band in monospace caps with a star and BRIGHTWORK
            TRIPS in ice on the left and Expedition log No. 01 on the right.
            Below, two columns. The left is the logbook, a dark page ruled as
            24px graph paper with an orange margin line near its left edge. It
            opens with Field notes for, Japan in April in bold, and Leader Mara
            Okafor, Party 2 with one guest and Window 1 to 14 April 2027. Log
            entries follows, six boxed entries right of the margin, each with a
            diamond bullet on the margin, a monospace head such as Day 1 or Days
            6 to 10 with the date, a title, a note and a status stamp. Booked
            entries have a solid ice left rule and solid diamond, unbooked a
            dashed orange rule and hollow diamond, flights grey. Two buttons
            follow. The right column holds a route sheet tilted slightly with a
            shadow, contour lines, a grid, a north arrow and a dashed ice route
            between three camp triangles for Tokyo, Kyoto and Osaka. Then three
            taped note cards. Conditions observed is a table of Station Tokyo,
            Period Early April, Highs around 17 degrees and a blossom note. Kit
            list shows the four checks. Provisions fund shows 3,200 euro of
            5,000 laid in over five ration blocks of 1,000, three full, one a
            fifth full, one dashed empty. Below 960px the columns stack.
        spacing: An 8px unit on a 24px graph grid. 14px between log entries, 20px between note cards and 28px between columns.
        density: Medium. Six entries in the log and four note cards beside it.
        corners: Nearly square at 2px. The route sheet tilts by 0.6 degrees and tape strips by 3.
        borders: 1px slate edges and a 3px left rule on every entry, solid ice when booked and dashed signal orange when not. Dashed rules in tables.
        shadows: Only under the tilted route sheet. Pale tape strips hold the cards.
        icons:
            Field marks. Booked is a solid flag, Not booked a dashed empty
            square and Flight a plane. Entry bullets are diamonds, hollow when
            unbooked. Camps are triangles. Done is a ticked box and To do an
            empty box.
        focus: A 2px frost outline offset 2px with a soft ice halo.
        tone: Plain expedition speech such as Log entries, Conditions observed, Kit list and Provisions fund.
